window.LORE = [
{"id":"origin-100i","gp":"0j46jjx9QB","t":"100i","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 100i is a light luxury touring spacecraft developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). The first in the [100 series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-100-series), it was created to be an entry-level luxury ship alternative to Origin's more expensive 300 series of ships. With its design focused on maneuverability and fuel efficiency, Origin introduced the eco-friendly Adaptive Intake Refinery (AIR) fuel system with the 100i to reduce emissions and increase the ship's overall range. Variants of the 100i include the [125a](gp:bmNrPP2DZ9) light fighter and the [135c](gp:RLMmvvNXN3) light freighter.","g":["touring","origin jumpworks","100 series","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1358f7df-9153-4164-8e07-29543672d0c4"},
{"id":"origin-125a","gp":"bmNrPP2DZ9","t":"125a","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 125a is a variant of the [100 series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-100-series) developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) that alters the standard [100i](gp:0j46jjx9QB) touring design to focus on combat with the addition of a pair of size one missile racks. The power plant provides an increase in speed. It is most commonly used as a point defense or interceptor ship, but can also fly in support of larger assets like an Origin 890 Jump. The 125a's small size allows it to be stored aboard vessels which might not be able to carry or maintain a larger space superiority fighter.","g":["origin jumpworks","100 series","fighter","light fighter","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cb0b537a-3879-41b1-9f3f-a5968202e47c"},
{"id":"origin-135c","gp":"RLMmvvNXN3","t":"135c","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 135c is a variant of the [100 series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-100-series) developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). While the redesign maintains the base ship's exterior, the overall engine capacity is reduced in exchange for tripling the interior cargo volume with the addition of a dedicated cargo space. The 135c has been marketed towards independent haulers and couriers who prefer to fly a ship with Origin's signature styling.","g":["origin jumpworks","light freight","100 series","freight","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/00abd3dd-ef68-43d1-9670-d701cb33143b"},
{"id":"origin-300i","gp":"0j46jjYgOn","t":"300i","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 300i is the base model of a [line](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-300-series) of luxury touring spacecraft developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). Its high-end amenities and design are targeted towards more affluent customers who prefer a visually attractive spaceship over a utilitarian one. Origin engineers made the basic frame adaptable, which has given rise to a number of role-specific variants. Current 300 variants include the [315p](gp:0j46jjAjK6) exploration craft, the 325a fighter and the [350r](gp:0QxYAAzp25) racing ship.","g":["300 series","origin jumpworks","touring","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a3ee597a-b79b-4181-bf20-b8528940a00a"},
{"id":"origin-315p","gp":"0j46jjAjK6","t":"315p","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 315p is a variant of the [300](gp:0j46jjYgOn) touring spacecraft developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). Added to [the lineup](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-300-series) in 2930, the variant was built with enhanced engines for improved power output and a bespoke communications system designed by [Chimera Communications](gp:R6v8g9jno1). 315p are generally used as vanguards in support of larger exploratory teams or by individual owners who are looking to explore in a craft with Origin's signature style.","g":["300 series","pathfinder","origin jumpworks","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5d2c09e6-73fb-47c2-a0df-5397ff0e7444"},
{"id":"origin-325a","gp":"0QxYAAwjGN","t":"325a","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 325a is a variant of the [300 series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-300-series) of spacecraft developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). Built as a dedicated combat ship, the 325a allows militia, police forces, and private security to arm themselves using the existing civilian maintenance chain. This ship comes standard with additional weapons and a specialized targeting system designed by [WillsOp](gp:bZkaBkrwKd) to allow for a stronger presence in combat scenarios.","g":["300 series","origin jumpworks","luxury","interdiction","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9f315bae-9c45-446f-8d81-75f939494646"},
{"id":"origin-350r","gp":"0QxYAAzp25","t":"350r","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 350r is a variant of the [300 series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-300-series) developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). Designed by Andreas Lang, a limited run of prototypes were initially created and distributed to racing teams to promote the use of [the 300i](gp:0j46jjYgOn) as a high performance platform. Met with unexpected success, Origin began constructing them for a wider customer base, though still in much smaller manufacturer runs than the other 300 series subtypes. The design is easily identifiable compared to other 300i variants because it has twin main thrusters instead of a single drive plume.","g":["300 series","origin jumpworks","racing","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/31ce8771-8870-40b7-a6a3-f3689cf85d5f"},
{"id":"origin-600i-explorer","gp":"0QxYA8xYLj","t":"600i Explorer","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 600i Explorer is a variant of the [600 series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-600-series) of spacecraft developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). The Explorer comes with myriad exploration-focused features, such as advanced scanning capabilities, space for the additional cargo needed on longer expeditions, and vehicle storage for planet-side excursions.","g":["600 series","expedition","origin jumpworks","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/40c28f14-7398-4f96-a2ba-b0bf73231620"},
{"id":"origin-600i-touring","gp":"0Gz5jLWaLg","t":"600i Touring","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 600i Touring is a variant of the [600 series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-600-series) of spacecraft developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). It was designed for leisure travel. In exchange for a reduced cargo capacity, it features luxury living quarters outfitted with furniture from high-end design firm [Tatavo](gp:VpMv8Y7Jq7), along with other passenger-facing amenities.","g":["600 series","touring","origin jumpworks","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/62a67782-963d-44bc-bcd4-1c9f40b2bbee"},
{"id":"origin-85x","gp":"0Gz5jL9vgP","t":"85x","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 85X is a touring vessel manufactured by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). It features performance handling and a wide field of view for its pilot and single passenger. Intended initially as a companion away-craft for the 890 Jump, it has since become available to a wider market as a standalone runabout.","g":["origin jumpworks","touring","transport","personal transport","890 jump","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/973b4072-d906-4bd6-bb91-7a425f2c6450"},
{"id":"origin-890-jump","gp":"RzPoqed1Jr","t":"890 Jump","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The 890 Jump is a luxury civilian spacecraft built by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). With its exterior designed to reference the nautical lines of ocean-borne vessels, the interior is outfitted with luxury accommodations that include multiple bedrooms for passengers and crew. An onboard pool and spa area are among its standard features.","g":["origin jumpworks","touring","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6d932429-5bc3-4ddb-bde7-aa0d01fcefbd"},
{"id":"nine-eight-seven","gp":"RMNWGwE9qA","t":"987","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"987 is a clothing brand headquartered in [Tram](gp:bBzdDMvNEy), [Asura (Ferron III)](gp:0qaPo2JOj1), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Known for its bold, aggressive styling, 987 began as a screenprint shop that made shirts for local musicians to sell at their shows. When the lead singer of [Clover](gp:box5qg83aL) wore one of their shirts during a concert, the brand took off and expanded its catalog to include other types of clothing, including its renowned line of jackets.","g":["clothing manufacturer","asura","ferron iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/61acb002-f883-487e-ab6d-cbd0c04dbc4d"},
{"id":"test-squadron-999","gp":"0qa16drQN1","t":"999th Test Squadron","k":"company","c":["Organizations","Military"],"x":"The 999th Test Squadron (Squadron 999, \"the Wreckless\") is a special unit of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) Navy dedicated to the evaluation of new and experimental spacecraft and vehicles. Originally formed to assist [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) (RSI) with testing the [Zeus](gp:VYLd4WxODo) short-range spacecraft, the 999th was founded by Amecanio [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) test pilot Michelle Saleno, the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to quantum travel beyond the orbit of Jupiter (Sol V). With the 999th's help, RSI overhauled the Zeus' design and released it in SEY 2140. When the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) came into existence in 2380, the 999th was officially incorporated into the new military structure with their 999th designation intact.","g":["ueen squadron","roberts space industries (rsi)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/75c57b5e-7889-4bda-be27-c5d949aee785"},
{"id":"gift-for-baba","gp":"0KnMm3WX5P","t":"A Gift for Baba","k":"culture","c":["Fiction","Human"],"x":"A Gift for Baba is [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) morality tale coined in the late 2300s. There are many versions of the story, but the best known version was adapted into a children's book of the same name by Fatima Reynolds-Malik in 2480. In it, three siblings, all children, travel from Mars (Sol IV) to Europa (Sol 5b) to deliver the perfect gift to their Grandmother, \"Baba.\"","g":["children's literature","human literature"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6d3c4520-18c6-41bd-a58b-2e99abaaea17"},
{"id":"a-tek","gp":"0QlnJar1j5","t":"A-Tek","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"A-Tek is a clothing brand that manufactures athletic clothing and shoes. From its early days as a small boutique on [Green (Ellis III)](gp:RWoNrNeLKP), the company has been known for its lightweight, durable products that are crafted to withstand long periods of use. They are particularly noted for their soft-soled shoes, which are popular among rock climbers.","g":["clothing manufacturer","footwear manufacturer","green","ellis iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f610d533-32d6-4e32-9bc5-667e8c346437"},
{"id":"a1-spirit","gp":"V3G2KOG7WN","t":"A1 Spirit","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The A1 Spirit is a medium bomber manufactured by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N). Based on the Daisy Chain system used in the [A2 Hercules](gp:Vgg7yx8ZpY), the A1 Spirit's Chaplet rig utilizes twin racks with five-bomb payloads that can be quickly deployed during battle. It is additionally equipped with rear-facing manual turrets, front-facing laser cannons, and dual missile racks. The A1 swaps the cargo hold from the [C1 Spirit](gp:01L2MB819w) for a bay that can accommodate a small vehicle for ground-based operations.","g":["bomber","medium bomber","crusader industries","human spacecraft","spirit series"]},
{"id":"a2-hercules","gp":"Vgg7yx8ZpY","t":"A2 Hercules","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The A2 Hercules Starlifter is a transport gunship developed by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N). Heavily armed with remote turrets and front and side ballistic cannons, it is used by the [United Empire of Earth Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) (UEEN) in airborne strikes, bombing runs, search and rescue operations, and air to ground invasions. Its bomb bay can be utilized as a cargo hold for logistics operations.","g":["hercules series","crusader industries","transport gunship","gunship","military transport","transport","military spacecraft","human spacecraft","starlifter series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/30e42c4e-a8ff-4a2b-9520-eb3684077302"},
{"id":"aadya-firmino","gp":"0Nj5o4M9v2","t":"Aadya Firmino","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Exploration"],"x":"Aadya Firmino (SEY 2692 - 2781) was the CEO of Terra Movers Construction and a smuggler best known for her 2716 discovery of the [Tohil system](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9) with her business partner [Oisha Suen](gp:01LrmgveKB). In 2713, seeking adventure after a sheltered childhood, she flew her new [Constellation Andromeda](gp:0QxY3wEXxQ) to [Delamar](gp:0GxoZnAGrg) in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3), where she met pilot and mechanic Oisha Suen. Over the next three years, they ran a smuggling operation in which Firmino made increasingly brazen attempts to steal clientele from other established smugglers in the Nyx system. She and Suen were exiled after a last attempt that destroyed one of [Levski's](gp:0dXQqBMAOp) ports and left three people gravely injured. A few days later, Suen picked up the signal of an anomaly that proved to be a jump point to a previously undiscovered planetary system. Firmino convinced Suen to keep this a secret until they were able to assess the full extent of what they had found. She then took Suen to the Bremen system, plied her with alcohol, and reported the discovery to the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government, claiming that she'd done it on her own. She enjoyed a short period of public adulation until a tell-all interview with Suen was published in the Terra Gazette. The [Department of Transportation and Navigation](gp:VDoPezP7E1) conducted an investigation and reassigned credit for the discovery to both Firmino and Suen. Shortly after this, the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) issued warrants for both smugglers' arrests. While Suen served a reduced sentence in exchange for providing a truthful testimony, Firmino ultimately avoided jail time thanks to her team of lawyers. She attempted to go back to Levski in 2723, but was denied entry. After returning to [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), she joined her father's company, inheriting it and becoming the new CEO when he passed away in 2736.","g":["tohil system","human people"]},
{"id":"aaron-halo-stanton-belt-alpha","gp":"bBzpN9A5w8","t":"Aaron Halo (Stanton Belt Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Aaron Halo (Stanton belt alpha) is a dense asteroid belt in the [Stanton system](gp:RX3lKBA3dq) that falls between the orbits of [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav) and ArcCorp (Stanton III). After [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) purchased Stanton II from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), it attempted to enact mining restrictions in and around the Aaron Halo. However, because the belt was not specifically included in Stanton II's purchase contracts, the company was required to relinquish its claim. Crusader Industries has submitted a legal challenge that has yet to be resolved by the UEE courts. In the meantime, the right to apply for mine claims in the belt has been unilaterally granted to all.","g":["aaron halo","stanton belt alpha","stanton system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0d8d3b15-3c90-4ada-adfd-5438717333fa"},
{"id":"abeni-okon","gp":"Rz2DPeZZnk","t":"Abeni Okon","k":"people","c":["People","Human","History"],"x":"Abeni Okon (SEY 2157 - 2252) was the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) born on a planet other than [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB). Her parents, Kinah and Madu Okon, were early colonists of [Mars (Sol IV)](gp:Regn8D76xw), the first planet successfully [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) by Humans. \n\nOkon was lauded in the media as a symbol of human ingenuity and perseverance, partially due to the failure of the [first Mars terraforming project](gp:bmNrgKnZ6l) in 2125. Though her parents made an effort to keep her safe from the spotlight, she was hounded by media orgs and parasocial strangers. In her late teens she embraced her fame, making appearances at any party and bar willing to pay her fee, engaging in frivolous spending, and making ill-advised investments. The media that once lauded her began to predict her downfall. However, in her late 20s, she withdrew from the public sphere without explanation and started working in community outreach programs. She moved often, and always to areas that needed help. Her final public appearance was in 2232, as the guest of honor at the launching of the colony ship [Artemis](gp:0jGxngnLzm). She died of natural causes in 2252 and is buried on Mars. Her birthday, 18 March, is celebrated as a Human holiday, particularly on Mars.","g":["mars","sol iv","human people","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ecf3c66f-41fc-4378-bbc1-bfd30e116546"},
{"id":"aberdeen-stanton-1b","gp":"0qanJarxqa","t":"Aberdeen (Stanton 1b)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Aberdeen, named for the designer of [Hurston Dynamics'](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) first antimatter warhead, Aberdeen Hurston, is the second moon of [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL). It has a thick, hazy atmosphere composed of sulfurous gas that creates low-visibility conditions on the moon's surface, posing a danger to ground-based travel. Aberdeen is home to a Klescher Rehabilitation Facility, a prison that allows inmates to work off their sentences via mining.","g":["aberdeen","stanton 1b","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","hurston","stanton i","aberdeen hurston","hurston dynamics","uee moon","stanton i moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5484d15b-323e-4d57-922c-078616375f13"},
{"id":"aberdeen-hurston","gp":"VlMMykaZKv","t":"Aberdeen Hurston","k":"people","c":["People","Human","History"],"x":"Aberdeen Hurston (SEY 2821 - 2912) was an engineer who worked at [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) from 2841 until his retirement in 2877. While he was attending university, he began working remotely with the weapons team at Hurston Dynamics on their early forays into antimatter-based missiles. In 2853, after decades of research, the team debuted the company's first antimatter warhead, based on Aberdeen Hurston's design. This secured them a long-term contract with the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The second moon of Hurston was named [Aberdeen](gp:0qanJarxqa) in his honor.","g":["hurston dynamics","human people","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/023be114-c59c-4132-ab4e-cc3a22d10694"},
{"id":"able-baker-challenge","gp":"RPP4LXMeBZ","t":"Able Baker Challenge","k":"history","c":["Illegal Activity","Sports","Human"],"x":"The Able Baker Challenge is an unofficial spacecraft racing event held in the [Baker system](gp:Rz2KGkv13N). It makes use of system-specific obstacles to hamper the pilots' efforts in reaching the finish line. Though the use of weapons is allowed during most legs of the race, shooting to kill is generally discouraged. Even so, the casualty rate of participants can be high. Racers are alerted to the time of the event one Standard Earth Day (SED) before it is set to begin.","g":["baker system","spacecraft racing","human sports","racing"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c54cecfb-3709-4d1e-86f4-9b7cdd6d1cd5"},
{"id":"accelerated-mass-design","gp":"VaZwQNE48v","t":"Accelerated Mass Design","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Accelerated Mass Design is an electronics design and tuning company founded in SEY 2899. They focus mainly on components for consumer spaceflight, such as the UE-9300 expansion card. The company has also partnered with spacecraft manufacturers [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) and [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34) to provide exclusive parts for their products.","g":["electronics design","spacecraft component manufacturer","electronics tuning","human company","uee company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/565d38bd-cf87-485a-846c-3f7a829a0f3e"},
{"id":"acheron","gp":"VJOz3gMM85","t":"Acheron","k":"place","c":["Locations"],"x":"Acheron is one of the major states on the planet [Charon III](gp:RkGGMvDpoz) in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Its environment is made up of mixed deserts and tropical regions. The [Phiyi Tower](gp:01dW3XmX3L), a skyscraper considered a masterpiece of Supermodernist architecture, was erected directly after a devastating SEY 2934 earthquake to symbolize a new, more hopeful era. Acheron and its neighboring state [Dellin](gp:0OaBKD9Kwk) have been engaged in a civil war since 2944.","g":["states","charon iii","phiyi tower","uee states"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6a182c1b-c494-40fd-8815-d05a4b263a01"},
{"id":"aciedo-communications","gp":"0OaBXqLwMq","t":"Aciedo Communications","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Aciedo Communications is a corporation that manufactures and maintains interstellar communications equipment. It was founded in SEY 2480 with the intent to manufacture spacecraft as Aciedo Shipworks. In 2485, the company pivoted to communications drone development and rebranded as Aciedo Communiations. Aciedo is best known for their ubiquitous [CommRelay towers](gp:0OaBMZl17P), first deployed in the 2750s, which transmit communications and navigational data across developed space.","g":["aciedo shipworks","commrelay station","communications","human company","uee company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2a674dc6-780f-4cdc-aa31-81ea05a2539f"},
{"id":"adaliz-dayan","gp":"Vgg7Ml89dN","t":"Adaliz Dayan","k":"people","c":["Exploration","People","Human","History"],"x":"Adaliz Dayan (SEY 2279 - 2317?) was a [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) engineer who is credited with the discovery of the [Banshee system](gp:0Gx4BENmKg). While working for the group terraforming [Hyperion (Fora III)](gp:RegWGPlxqy) in the [Fora system](gp:bo1PDEgGv2), she formed the Immram Association, an organization devoted to exploring the region between terraforming tasks. \n\nDayan disappeared under unusual circumstances while investigating a pocket of radiation. During the search for her ship, it was discovered that the pocket of radiation marked a jump point to the [Banshee system](gp:0Gx4BENmKg). While it is believed she likely jumped there, she has never been located. The system was named Banshee in her honor, inspired by the nickname she earned playing college sataball.","g":["immram association","banshee system","human people","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7820fc11-1387-4016-a91c-aaa67daaf6bc"},
{"id":"adam-corr","gp":"V3qgyvG8ZY","t":"Adam Corr","k":"people","c":["People","Human","History"],"x":"Adam Corr (SEY 2519 - unknown), [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) Army veteran (Sergeant, honorably discharged), participated in the [Battle of Idris IV](gp:ReJajXKelk) and served under [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q). He was later implicated to be one of the two people who allegedly perpetrated a [series of bombings](gp:0Gz5GgEvkj) of the United Planets of Earth by order of Messer in 2546. Corr, an infiltration specialist, bailed demolitions expert and possible accomplice [Cyrus Ishitaka](gp:R4ZGy5XJXe) out of prison in [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5) days before the first bombings struck the city. His whereabouts after this incident remain unknown.","g":["atrocity at jata","battle of idris iv","human people","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/65bd5c9d-4aa1-440f-a22a-165ef1b7013f"},
{"id":"adir-pyro-5c","gp":"0dXpZmg99m","t":"Adir (Pyro 5c)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Adir is the third moon from the gas giant [Pyro V](gp:RAXv9Yeqay), [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Jagged mountains and rocky hills dominate its crater-ridden landscape. Because it lacks a protective atmosphere that would otherwise break apart most approaching celestial objects, its surface sees frequent impacts. The air is permeated with fine particles of dust that are generated during these events.","g":["adir","pyro 5c","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon","pyro system"]},
{"id":"advocacy","gp":"VDoP5pmODk","t":"Advocacy","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"The Advocacy is an inter-system police force formed in SEY 2523, serving the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The Director of the Advocacy reports to the [High-Advocate](gp:RWolAld13P) and oversees all law enforcement throughout the UEE. While local systems and planets do have their own police and security, the Advocacy supersedes their authority and its agents are authorized to exercise more power in pursuit of crimes across systems.","g":["law enforcement","uee advocacy","uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/57d3126b-a3d1-43b4-9d86-0e10772ad056"},
{"id":"aegis-dynamics","gp":"RAdk7jx5Kv","t":"Aegis Dynamics","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Military","Human"],"x":"Aegis Dynamics is a spacecraft manufacturer based on [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5). Because it manufactured a majority of the military ships used by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) during the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo), the company became synonymous with the fascist regime of the time. \n\nAfter the [fall of the Messers](gp:bE3rKa32P7) in SEY 2792, Aegis Dynamics faced massive public backlash for its role in the regime and lost most of its military contracts, which led to massive layoffs and internal restructuring. Relegated to producing parts, the company avoided bankruptcy when civilian sales spiked after they debuted a civilian model of the [Retaliator](gp:0qnN6j2Gq7) bomber. Today, the company is a major manufacturer of both civilian and military ships.","g":["cestulus","davien ii","spacecraft manufacturer","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/449f1583-b061-485d-9dfe-33ba94ba13ee"},
{"id":"aemelia-kiel-3a","gp":"RAX3p8oKpY","t":"Aemelia (Kiel 3a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Aemelia (Kiel 3a) is the moon of [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Before the [anti-Messer revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7) in 2792, the [UEE Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) utilized its wide icy plains as training grounds for land warfare. There are many long, straight scars left by tank treads across Aemelia's landscape that are still visible from the surface of Severus.","g":["aemilia","kiel 3a","severus moon","kiel iii moon","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","kiel system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/92c78b01-7d5f-4e5c-b5ef-02a7bdfecdd3"},
{"id":"aero-terra-I","gp":"RxnzEP5m1Q","t":"Aero (Terra I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Aero is a mesoplanet in the [Terra system](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Orbiting closest to the system's sun, its surface is too dangerous for any [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to venture upon for any great lengths of time under the limits of current technology. Many attempts have been made by corporations and private individuals to establish profitable mining operations on Aero, but none have succeeded.","g":["aero","terra i","terra system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a69ff7b9-b7b9-4cf0-9878-645819029957"},
{"id":"aeroview","gp":"RLMmwmQErL","t":"Aeroview","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Aeroview is a spacecraft hangar manufacturer, presently a wholly-owned subsidiary of [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA). Founded by Arthur Nassir early in 2687, the company first made a name for itself by designing custom hangars for wealthy clients. Since their acquisition by Shubin in the early 29th century, Aeroview has adopted [SELF-LAND's](gp:V7gM8M7Len) modular hangar model for much of their business while retaining their focus on higher-end designs that cater primarily to larger ships.","g":["hangar manufacturer","shubin interstellar","hangars","arthur nassir","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f73f6c6e-8af2-4de3-b118-13b96e4de0f9"},
{"id":"ahmad-harar","gp":"VYLznx8r3e","t":"Ahmad Harar","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Exploration","History"],"x":"Ahmad Harar (SEY 2595 - SEY 2699) was a pilot and Lieutenant in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) best known for discovering the [Kai'pua](gp:V3GBmlQoar)-[Horus](gp:bo1JGZpvwZ) jump point alongside fellow starman [Carl Dyson](gp:R5p2mqLvXN). \n\nIn SEY 2617, Harar was patrolling the Horus system with his gunner Lieutenant Dyson, when they detected a gravitational anomaly that they determined to be a jump point after hours of analysis. Harar convinced Dyson to navigate it instead of reporting it to headquarters, arguing that this was their chance to earn a place in history. However, when they exited the jump point, they found themselves in a [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj)-controlled system and were quickly captured. \n\nHarar and Dyson were held captive and interrogated by the Xi'an government for three full days. They finally convinced their captors that the rest of the UEE military was unaware of the jump point, and were returned to Horus and told to transmit the message that any UEE vessels spotted in Kai'pua would be attacked on sight. Harar was reprimanded for failing to report his discovery to his commander and accepted a demotion. He went on to serve for thirty more years and retired as a Captain in 2647.","g":["human people","kai'pua system","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/047a5d3c-3c29-4579-a791-591ec84f8dbf"},
{"id":"airpra","gp":"bmGyM6NED9","t":"AI Research and Production Restriction Act","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The Artificial Intelligence Research and Production Restriction Act (AIRPRA) is a piece of legislation that places strict rules governing research on true artificial intelligence (AI) in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE). Popularly referred to as \"the AI ban,\" it originated after the disappearance of the Artemis, a long-haul colony ship containing thousands of individuals in cryogenic storage. The AI that had been designed to monitor and pilot the ship was blamed, and politicians latched onto the restriction of AI research as a wedge issue to secure votes. Many countries went on to ban artificial intelligence over the next few decades. When the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) was created in 2380, its architects included AI restrictions in its earliest laws. The [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) and the UEE kept AIRPRA in place during their formations, and it remains the law of the land. \n\n# OVERVIEW\nAIRPRA grants the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) the authority to review and approve or deny all artificial intelligence research, commercial and non commercial. It defines artificial intelligence as \"any software or hardware that can convincingly imitate intelligent Human behavior.\" This broad definition places severe limits on any kind of research that can be done in the AI field, and has effectively banned its production and use throughout the UEE. Specific guidelines include: \n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n• A ban on the reception of government funding for AI research.\n\n• A requirement for Senate approval on privately funded artificial intelligence research.\n\n• If approved, the research must be strictly supervised by the UEE Science and Technology Committee.\n\n• A notice that approval can be revoked at any time.\n\n• A ban on selling any product that displays signs of artificial intelligence.\n\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n\nAny person found in violation of AIRPRA is subject to arrest and may be sentenced to imprisonment for 15 to 20 years. Corporations and research institutions found to be knowingly abetting AI research are subject to a sliding scale of fines and are subject to asset seizure. \n\n# HISTORY\nIn 2043, the Eakara Company launched a line of self-driving cars powered by what they claimed to be the first true AI. This differed from earlier products marketed as AI, which were deep generative models that could mimic the qualities of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) intelligence but did not truly possess it. This new AI, Eakara promised, had the intelligence, good judgment, and fast reaction time of the most seasoned Human drivers. The city of Tokyo was an early investor, and purchased a fleet of cars and buses to bulk up their transportation infrastructure in areas too distant from train stations to be easily reached on foot. \n\nIn 2044, while driving on a road on a high cliff, one of the Eakara buses made a wrong turn and plummeted over the edge to the sea below, resulting in 21 deaths. Fifteen minutes later, another bus followed, this one with 37 passengers aboard. Authorities contacted Eakara and the company's technicians sent out an emergency command to force all self-driving vehicles in Tokyo and its outskirts to immediately stop without finishing their current trips. Vehicles not engaged in active trips stopped as commanded, but those that were transporting passengers at the time ignored the command continued their trips to completion. Although the vast majority did this without incident, three more buses and 18 cars suffered fatal accidents before all vehicles in the fleet ended their trips and finally stopped moving. 113 people in total died. This became known as the \"Lemming Car Incident,\" and resulted in the dissolution of the Eakara Company. The nation of Japan banned the use of AI in self-driving cars, but similar bans would not be enacted elsewhere until deadly incidents caused by cars from other companies occurred in New York in 2044 and Johannesburg in 2047. \n\nWith public distrust in AI high and investors unwilling to back AI-led ventures, researchers began to focus on its application in the sciences rather than day to day life. In 2055, an AI helped to identify a type of bacteria commonly found in the digestive systems of apex carnivores that was utilized to prevent prion diseases. Another AI helped synthesize a cure for rabies. One especially advanced AI was put in charge of calculating the spacecraft trajectories that ensured early missions to Mars were successful. These triumphs helped thaw public opinion and paved the way for AI usage in early terraforming platforms used on Mars. \n\nDesigned to complete quick calculations and enact minute adjustments to the atmosphere, the Mars AI was notable for its ability to provide imaginative solutions to complex issues at a speed much higher than that of a Human and with a significantly lower margin of error. At the time, the team in charge of [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) Mars credited the AI for the ease with which the project appeared to be progressing. However, on 13 September 2125, a miscalculation that was later linked to the AI led to the sudden catastrophic dissipation of the near-complete atmosphere, resulting in the deaths of over 4800 people. This event, deemed the \"[Mars Tragedy](gp:bmNrgKnZ6l)\" in the press, again destroyed positive public opinion about AI and halted most ongoing development. \n\nIn 2201, AI researcher Dr. Carol Zahir secured funding from private sources and began crafting a new type of artificial intelligence that she would name [Janus](gp:VDzOvEdNyd). By far the most advanced AI of its time, Janus could hold conversations, draw conclusions, and make educated guesses at or beyond the level of a Human. In 2228, [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) (RSI) began construction of the [Artemis](gp:0jGxngnLzm), a long-haul colony ship that would rely on quantum travel to reach the potentially habitable planetary system codenamed GJ 667Cc. Zahir reached out to the company and proposed that Janus serve as the nerve center of the ship. Given that it would take over 200 years for the ship to reach its destination, RSI agreed. This would allow all the colonists and crew aboard to remain safely in cryogenic sleep without forcing any one of them to grow old and die while they oversaw the journey. \n\nThe *Artemis* launched in 2232 to great fanfare. Soon after it was determined to be safely on course, its launch crew entered cryosleep, leaving Janus solely in charge. Janus transmitted regular reports to Earth until 2237, when any communications from it abruptly ceased. Mission control repeatedly hailed it, but Janus either refused to or could not respond. RSI and multiple governments launched extensive searches, but the *Artemis* was nowhere to be found. It seemed to have disappeared without a trace. \n\nThe outcry that resulted from the loss of over 5000 people was enormous. Although it was not certain that Janus had anything to do with the disappearance of the *Artemis*, the media vocally blamed it for the catastrophe, citing the Lemming Car Incident and the Mars Tragedy as evidence. Politicians on Earth and Mars latched onto the ban of artificial intelligence as a wedge issue, using it as a springboard to secure votes and take office. As promised in hundreds of campaign speeches, they enacted a wave of bans and halted and confiscated any AI research in their jurisdiction. When the United Nations of Earth eventually formed in 2380, distrust of AI was still high enough that the Artificial Intelligence Research and Production Restriction Act (AIRPRA) became one of the newly-created government's earliest proposed laws. The Senate approved it in a landslide vote.\n\n# CRITICISM\nBecause the definition of AI under AIRPRA is so broad, critics have pointed out that it has been used to stifle research and technology that is only tangentially related to AI, such as more efficient autopilots for spacecraft and companies that sell interactive toys. It has also been argued that the secrecy around AI has allowed the government to conduct dangerous research of its own away from the scrutiny of the public, as revealed with the declassification of Project Overlord in 2943. \n\n[Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) [Laylani Addision](gp:VYLvBm6Po1) promised to loosen restrictions on AI research during her election campaign, stating that \"...the goal of technology should always be to help Humanity, not replace it. AI included,\" in an interview on the popular spectrum show Clean Shot. Her Innovation Initiative, launched soon after she took office in 2951, allows the issuance of special waivers to research institutions pursuing the study of AI. Any institution that receives this waiver is eligible for a limited number of government grants, and must make all advancements resulting from their research both public and free for all to use.","g":["airpra","laws","uee law","ai ban"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/77118db2-0342-486b-93be-45f23eb4f4c2"},
{"id":"ailka-belt-alpha","gp":"0dXXJ6Qano","t":"Ail'ka Belt Alpha (Huichuaihyao y.ath'o se Ail'ka)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Ail'ka belt alpha (Huichuaihyao y.ath'o se Ail'ka) is the first asteroid belt in the [Ail'ka system](gp:01LLZmEygJ), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9), and orbits the system's sun between [Xyeping (Ail'ka I)](gp:02kkXZpnDp) and [K'ya.k'uing (Ail'ka II)](gp:0GxxrPE8oo). Pilots who train in the flight academies on [M.iiy'ong (Ail'ka IV)](gp:0jGGDY1yAW) engage in extensive war-games in the belt. Spacecraft manufacturer [Aopoa](gp:VyvY5jyZwp) utilizes the asteroids as obstacle courses to test the agility of their ships.","g":["ail'ka belt alpha","asteroid belt","ail'ka system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b4104762-0e3a-460b-b2d7-a19700eb5251"},
{"id":"ailka-belt-beta","gp":"VpMvoGWzJO","t":"Ail'ka Belt Beta (Huichuaihyao sy.en'o se Ail'ka)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Ail'ka belt beta is the second asteroid belt from the sun of the [Ail'ka system](gp:01LLZmEygJ). Rich in valuable minerals, it is the system's largest mine, ensuring that all military projects, no matter how large, do not need to rely on imports to obtain raw materials. Rather than stripping resources from the belt as fast as possible, the military only excavates what is actively needed for production.","g":["ail'ka belt beta","ail'ka system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c13ae026-5131-47b1-b072-a8ed5ba65a89"},
{"id":"ailka-system","gp":"01LLZmEygJ","t":"Ail'ka System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The Ail'ka system is an inhabited planetary system within the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Reported by the Xi'an to have been discovered in MXY III.844 (SEY 2538), its existence was kept secret from the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) during the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (UEE), and only declassified in SEY 2793. [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) were not allowed to enter the system until SEY 2915, upon special invitation from military spacecraft manufacturer [Aopoa](gp:VyvY5jyZwp).","g":["xi'an system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9d9d2cc0-14df-4114-93af-8447e256b75d"},
{"id":"akari-kree-treaty","gp":"bE3rKrl5z6","t":"Akari-Kr.ē Treaty","k":"faction","c":["Politics","History","Human","Xi'an"],"x":"The Akari-Kr.ē Treaty is a ratified agreement between [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) and the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that brought about the unofficial end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793 / MXY III.838 - III.1044). It was brokered in SEY 2789 (MXY III.1040) by the [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) of Terra, [Terrence Akari](gp:RL6ZQLwnko), and Xi'an [Emperor Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo). Due to the political instability of the late [Messer Era (SEY 2546 - 2792)](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo), negotiations for this treaty were conducted in secret on the [Tohil system](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9) on undeveloped world [Tohil III](gp:0OD1qEgJdN). The holiday [Armistice Day](gp:RWwZQWZQDA), created in celebration of the war's end, is held annually in the UEE on 29 May. \n\n# HISTORY\n\nIn the latter years of the Messer Era, the UEE and the Xi'an Empire had been on the brink of war for over two centuries, and public sentiment on both sides was strongly in favor of ending the conflict. Planetary systems that bordered the two empires were kept under constant military surveillance, draining funding that was desperately needed in other areas. Major [Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) within the Xi'an Empire had lodged protests against sending their youth to face uncertain fates against a hostile enemy, and, with the threat of [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) attacks becoming a large concern, Humans began to doubt the Messer regime's continued use of the Xi'an as the cause of all the UEE's problems. Additionally, [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) was an unpopular ruler. He had left his father's brutal policies in place instead of undoing them as he had promised his supporters before his SEY 2781 coup, and his habit of swift and deadly retaliation had lost him most of his allies in the Senate and the military. Conditions were ripe for the opening of a road to peace. \n\nSenator Terrance Akari of Terra and Emperor T.uēng se Kr.ē of the Xi'an Empire first began exchanging communications in SEY 2775 (MXY III.1032). The Senator had long held an interest in Xi'an culture, and utilized his political status to pull strings and pass questions along to the Xi'an government when he came up against a cultural concept he didn't understand. To his surprise, the Emperor himself began responding to his missives. Kr.ē recognized the opportunity for what it was: a chance to cultivate a connection to the second highest echelon of Human government. As their correspondence increased over the years, they began to discuss what peace might look like between the UEE and the Xi'an Empire. \n\nIn SEY 2789 (MXY III.1040), they agreed it was time to meet in person and discuss the creation of a possible treaty. After weeks of deliberation on the subject, they chose the Tohil system as the location due to its lack of military presence and position on the border of both empires. While Emperor Kr.ē made his way there with the aid of his government, Akari had to escape the notice of his or risk being arrested and thrown into an [Empire's Light Conversion Center](gp:0KxqnXDpQ2) for collaborating with an alien power. He enlisted the help of Terra's [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) Section Chief Nathan Warrick, who put Akari into contact with a group of smugglers that regularly transported anti-Messer activists between [Bremen](gp:02kd45eyxe) and Tohil through the unclaimed [Nyx](gp:0jGxP6kpG3) system. It was a risky undertaking; Akari was in constant danger of being apprehended by pro-Messer forces, and Emperor Kr.ē was inviting war with the UEE by entering into Tohil in the first place. Their mutual safe arrival on Tohil III created a buoyant mood that Akari identified as a motivating factor in their work on what would become the Akari-Kr.ē Treaty. \n\nOn 11 March, the peace accord was completed, and Emperor Kr.ē signed it on behalf of the Xi'an Empire. He departed for the Xi'an capital planet Ka'ua (Hyoton IV) soon after, where he would secure the approval of the [Imperial](gp:R6v8OZOrP5) House's [Council of Three](gp:Rw1DPO8v8q). Akari made his way to Earth (Sol III) and spread word about the treaty's existence amongst his most trusted staff members and fellow pro-peace Senators. On 29 May, while Linton Messer XI and his sister [Fiona](gp:R56nLjJog7) were on vacation in the [Goss system](gp:RxnYdDZj96), Akari triggered an emergency session of the Senate and called for an immediate vote on the treaty. Without the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) there to rally any opposition, the deal was narrowly approved. \n\n# MAIN PRINCIPLES\n1 - **Non-aggression agreement:** The Xi'an Empire and the UEE agreed to not threaten or use force against one another's territory or independence, and to acknowledge one another's right to self-defense if subject to armed attack. \n\n2 - **Border Security:** Each side promised to respect one another's territory and to not cross their respective borders without permission. \n\n3 - **The Perry Line:** The Xi'an Empire and the UEE agreed to withdraw their military forces from the Perry Line. \nPolitical refugees. The Xi'an Empire agreed that they would accept Human refugees from the UEE, and Terra agreed to provide resources to aid in their care.\n\n4 - **Status of Terra:** If leadership in the UEE rejected the terms of the treaty, the peace agreement would stand between Terra and the Xi'an Empire. \n\n5 - **Duration of terms:** The terms of the agreement were to remain in place indefinitely unless any terms were broken or in the event of a change in structure of the UEE or Xi'an governments.\n\n# IMPACT\nHistorians credit Linton Messer XI's refusal to ratify the Akari-Kr.ē Treaty as the moment the Messers fully lost their grip on the UEE. Although the Imperator declined to sign the accord when it arrived at his desk, the Xi'an Empire withdrew its military forces from the Perry Line as promised, demonstrating the hollowness of the Messer regime's assertion that they were the only thing standing between the people and a Xi'an invasion. This, coupled with the regime's inability to arrest Akari, who had gone into hiding, fueled public perception of Linton Messer XI as an incompetent ruler. People who had previously felt that standing against the Imperator would be too risky took the plunge and joined up, swelling the ranks of the anti-Messer movement. This influx of funding and connections would later enable the resistance group [Tide](gp:RXlXOpwG6k) to obtain footage of the [Massacre of Garron II](gp:01dWeqnMr1) and finally [end the Messer dictatorship](gp:bE3rKa32P7). On 5 July SEY 2793 (III.1044.08), the Perry Line Pact was ratified and signed by the new UEE government and the Xi'an Empire, officially bringing an end to the cold war.","g":["treaties","terrence akari","xi'an-human cold war","armistice day","terra","terra iii","xi'an empire","t.uēng se kr.ē","xi'an history","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d146e0fc-7f5d-491c-90c3-4821b5715a14"},
{"id":"akiro-cluster-pyro-cluster-alpha","gp":"0dXpZY2Eed","t":"Akiro Cluster (Pyro Cluster Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Akiro cluster (pyro cluster alpha) is a dense asteroid cluster on the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Situated in the L3 Lagrange point of [Pyro I](gp:RMNjxnZp3n), the asteroids periodically move closer to the planet or farther away from it as they travel around their sun. Most were stripped of their most valuable minerals by Pyrotechnic Amalgamated and other companies, but some small mining outfits have been known to search the cluster for undiscovered troves.","g":["akiro cluster","pyro cluster alpha","asteroid cluster","pyro system"]},
{"id":"alberto-vara","gp":"VgEgojrAQ3","t":"Alberto Vara","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Alberto Vara (2891 - present) is an Aron Award-winning astroengineer and founder of Infinity Custom, a full ship customization studio and garage. After graduating from the [Martian Institute of Space and Technology (MIST)](gp:RL67MAJreO) in 2914, he began his career at [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) as a junior engineer. Vara's engine work on the [M50](gp:V7gMWO7Yo3) earned him his first [Aron Award](gp:bBz5BKzjWJ) in 2921. He was promoted to chief engineer in 2925, a position he held until he left to found his own company in 2932. A few years after his departure, a design sketch depicting an open-canopy racer was discovered in Origin's archives. Vara collaborated with Origin to bring this concept to life, and the [X1](gp:VDoPD9Ejz1) racer debuted in 2947.","g":["infinity customs","x1","human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/55607c6b-daf1-4283-8158-546a8f0ed515"},
{"id":"alejo-brothers","gp":"R5p37Wrz8m","t":"Alejo Brothers","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Alejo Brothers is a clothing brand that specializes in producing outdoor gear and survivalist equipment. Known for its rugged, practical designs, it often partners with weapon manufacturers to produce shirts decorated with company logos. The brand came under fire in SEY 2949 for its use of xenophobic messages in an advertising campaign. After a period of public pressure, they pulled the ad but did not issue an apology, leading some activists to boycott.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/76d14d5a-5ff8-448c-b2b2-94de8557056e"},
{"id":"altruxiatoxin","gp":"bZkE1L4zLM","t":"Altruciatoxin","k":"culture","c":["Illegal Activity","Science and Technology"],"x":"Altruciatoxin is an illegal drug under [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) law. Derived from the pollen of the [revenant tree](gp:0Oa5AMlQAw), it is also known as dust, candy, or round off and most often sold in the form of a fine powder. It causes sensory enhancement, muscular relaxation, and lethargy in its users. A user will dab the substance on their tongue and absorb it through the mucus membranes. Those who wish to experience a reduced high may purchase it in a crystalline form and smoke it instead. Though uncommon, usage of the drug can induce a violent and rarely deadly allergic reaction, especially in those who are already sensitive to pollen.","g":["illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a659fe1a-9131-4509-a8b7-e8ee0351d2ad"},
{"id":"amandeep-vakario","gp":"R4jPNKq9vY","t":"Amandeep Vakario","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Amandeep Vakario (SEY 2884 - present) is a self-proclaimed spirituality leader, motivational speaker, and self-help coach. He is best known for his 2942 book *Enlightened Negotiating* and for his individual work with high-profile clients. \n\nBorn on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), he attended a series of meditation seminars in 2903, where he experienced a \"spiritual revelation\" while laying in a sensory deprivation tank. This experience led him to self-publish his first book, *Finding the Hidden You*, which saw enough success that Vakario began a self-produced [spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q)-based spiritual advice show. *Costless Visualization* amassed a large following, eventually enough to land a guest spot on the show [Something Every Tuesday](gp:V3GJNlQakW) in 2936. After this, his popularity skyrocketed, and he retired from his show in favor of taking on individual celebrity clients such as [Ellroy Cass](gp:RegZ7z96Gy) and [Magnus Tobin](gp:RkGZqr8yNQ). \n\nAt Tobin's request, Amandeep wrote and performed the inspirational quote series *Moments of Clarity*, which are played in the Commons of New Babbage, [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1).","g":["human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4be9f0cd-e1ef-41d4-86ca-bd595ddf0823"},
{"id":"amioshi-plague","gp":"bZkLlDElQq","t":"Amioshi Plague","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The amioshi plague is a lichen that is invasive on multiple planets throughout known space. Originally from [Kampos (Ellis IV)](gp:RAXxrxr7M5), it naturally grows in the cracks of rocks, where it anchors its rhizines to absorb nutrients and water. It needs little to no light to survive, and can often be found in caves, forests, and other shaded areas. When it is ready to reproduce, it sends up hooded growths that open to disperse countless spores.","g":["lichens","kampos","ellis iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/039a8aeb-238c-4c46-85b4-359f8eab6636"},
{"id":"amon-and-reese-co","gp":"RkZ949Ey5L","t":"Amon & Reese Co","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Amon & Reese Co. (A&R) is a Human manufacturer that produces energy-based weapons and spacecraft engines for the military and civilian markets. Founded in the early 2500s, the company has held a longstanding contract with the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) to provide handheld and shipboard weapons to the military. Though it supplied many of the weapons utilized by government forces during the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (SEY 2546 - 2792), A&R's continuous charity work for veterans and their families has helped keep the company's reputation neutral after the [fall of the Messers](gp:bE3rKa32P7).","g":["amon & reese","spacecraft engine manufacturer","weapons manufacturer","idris iv","locke"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a19ce8f0-c2c4-43c7-a430-30a60ae5e150"},
{"id":"angeli-croshaw-ii","gp":"0QlxqwG14Q","t":"Angeli (Croshaw II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Angeli is the second planet in the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and was the first planet settled by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) outside the Sol system. Its position in the system's green band enabled a rapid colonization phase in spite of the planet's tectonic instability. Angeli is a major destination for culinary connoisseurs, producing a variety of unique food and spirits influenced by an eclectic mix of cultures from Earth (Sol III). As a recognized planet, Angeli holds three seats in the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ).","g":["angeli","croshaw ii","habitable","habitable planet","croshaw system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/88a53d70-ee4a-4742-9e5e-a419789cee24"},
{"id":"angeli-on-air","gp":"0dQ4n4oJ1m","t":"Angeli on Air","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"Angeli on Air was a [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) network founded on [Angeli (Croshaw II)](gp:0QlxqwG14Q) in 2459. It focused on broadcasting shows created by people born on Angeli, usually ones with a community or cultural focus. AoA was the original home for popular news debate program [*Showdown!*](gp:RwZBw4Lrxz), adapted for Spectrum in 2521. Facing financial difficulties, the company was purchased and subsumed by [SSN/CAtv](gp:0QxYwPK88l) in 2524.","g":["spectrum","showdown!","ssn/catv","croshaw ii","angeli","spectrum network","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/915f7186-373d-414b-bfe7-f1ce5838be3b"},
{"id":"anthony-tanaka","gp":"RwZBdpj2rz","t":"Anthony Tanaka","k":"people","c":["People","Human","History"],"x":"Anthony Tanaka (SEY 2745 - 2757) was a child laborer who became a martyr to the [anti-Messer movement](gp:bE3rKa32P7) when he was murdered by an [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) agent for refusing to continue work. \n\nHe was born in Newcastle, [Borea (Magnus II)](gp:R9vGaQPXJN), and was forced to begin work at a munitions factory by local authorities when he was 7 years old. On 3 December 2757, Tanaka, exhausted after a sixteen-hour shift, refused to take over for a co-worker who had gone into anaphylactic shock. An Advocacy agent employed as one of the company's security enforcers executed him on the factory floor for his defiance. \n\nFootage of the murder was smuggled out of the factory, and became a symbol of resistance to the growing members of the anti-Messer movement. [Remembrance Day](gp:VJXGx2wyon) was established in honor of him.","g":["borea","magnus ii","anti-messer revolution","human people","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/32fffcf7-5e99-41e6-a544-da39838ba36b"},
{"id":"anthony-tanaka-remembrance-day","gp":"VJXGx2wyon","t":"Anthony Tanaka Remembrance Day","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"Anthony Tanaka Remembrance Day is a holiday in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), observed annually on December Third. It is held in honor of [Anthony Tanaka](gp:RwZBdpj2rz), a child laborer who was publicly executed by an [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) agent on 3 December 2757 for refusing to obey an order to continue working. Footage of his murder was captured and smuggled out of the factory by members of the anti-Messer movement, where it became a symbol of resistance against the cruelty of the Messer government. In 2793, after the events of the [Anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7), [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y) signed a declaration from the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) that recognized the anniversary of Tanaka's death as a holiday. Traditionally, observers light candles in honor of Tanaka while they observe a moment of silence.","g":["anthony tanaka","anti-messer revolution","uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9f21d078-7af1-490f-98ca-5b7ae3f8e6b1"},
{"id":"anti-messer-revolution","gp":"bE3rKa32P7","t":"Anti-Messer Revolution","k":"history","c":["Politics","History","Human"],"x":"The Anti-Messer Revolution was a complex series of events spanning decades that culminated in the end of the fascist [Messer regime](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo), the death of [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq), and the disappearance of [Fiona Messer](gp:R56nLjJog7) in SEY 2792. The [Akari-Kr.ē Treaty](gp:bE3rKrl5z6), which signaled the upcoming end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War (2530 - 2793)](gp:RXlLjDewkZ), played a significant role in sparking dissent against the Messer government. The [Massacre of Garron II](gp:01dWeqnMr1), broadcast over the [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) by the activist group [Tide](gp:RXlXOpwG6k), fanned that dissent into a flame and open revolts against the Messers began. After twenty-two days of civil unrest, the Messers were removed from power, and Imperator [Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y) took office.","g":["linton messer xi","fiona messer","massacre of garron ii","tide (activist group)","revolutions","messer era","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d7fd42d3-3771-47af-91c3-827eb9dc66bc"},
{"id":"anti-ship-mines","gp":"ReJa8GYYjM","t":"Anti-Ship Mines","k":"culture","c":["Weapons","Science and Technology"],"x":"Anti-ship mines, also called proximity mines, are explosives that can be placed at fixed points in space. They are designed to explode when spacecraft come within a particular range, inflicting heat and projectile damage on anything nearby. Mines are used by the military for purposes of area denial and are often abandoned if unused during a conflict, making former battlefields dangerous to traverse. Anti-ship mines were used extensively in former Perry Line systems during the Xi'an-Human Cold War (SEY 2530 - 2793). Many were abandoned, and remain active and dangerous in spite of cleanup efforts.","g":["explosive weapons","proximity mines"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/978c2c77-a555-4105-a6af-ae2f8edbad25"},
{"id":"antimatter-processing-plant","gp":"V3qgy3L7ra","t":"Antimatter Processing Plant","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"An antimatter processing plant or refinery is a factory constructed to purify and convert antimatter precursors into usable antimatter. Antimatter precursors are mined from a variety of sources and shipped to refineries for processing. The processed antimatter is used for starship drives and antimatter warheads. The process can be extremely dangerous for workers. Hurston in the Stanton System and the penal planet Quarterdeck are home to a significant number of antimatter processing plants.","g":["antimatter"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bd87eca5-7a21-4a73-a1e2-7255bbc12545"},
{"id":"antimatter-warhead","gp":"bE3rKalNkJ","t":"Antimatter Warhead","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Weapons"],"x":"Antimatter warheads are high yield explosive weapons armed with an antimatter payload rather than fission or fusion devices. Because they are among the most destructive weapons available to the [United Empire of Earth's (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) armed forces, their deployment and availability are closely monitored by the UEE government. [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ), headquartered on [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL), is one of their main manufacturers.","g":["antimatter","antimatter warheads","warheads","explosive weapons","hurston dynamics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0a79d2f5-20ec-4300-992a-f1ecd3c7ad49"},
{"id":"antoine-lebec","gp":"0ODddzO7Dq","t":"Antoine Lebec","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Exploration","History"],"x":"Antoine Lebec (SEY 2258 - 2307?) was a navjumper most notable for his discovery of the [Nul system](gp:VgEnlpqyJ9) in 2290. \n\nBorn on [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB), he was inspired to become an explorer after [Nick Croshaw](gp:VyvYkAr7YW) discovered the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp) in 2271. He completed pilot training in 2277, but wasn't able to afford his own spacecraft until 2282, when he won a land and mineral rights lottery to a plot on [Angeli (Croshaw II)](gp:0QlxqwG14Q) that sat on a natural vein of copper. This source of revenue enabled him to purchase a ship and become a full time navjumper. \n\nWhen he discovered the Nul jump point, he reported that he had found \"nul\" during his initial visit there, thus giving the system its name. He disappeared while investigating the outskirts of Nul in 2307. Historians speculate that he may have perished while attempting to navigate the Nul-Caliban jump point that would later be discovered by Ashleigh Gonn.","g":["nul system","earth","sol iii","human people","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ace4ae75-061b-48dc-90ec-db52691ea925"},
{"id":"anvil-aerospace","gp":"0qnN6Od6YD","t":"Anvil Aerospace","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Military","Human"],"x":"Anvil Aerospace is a spacecraft manufacturing corporation headquartered on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). Founded in SEY 2772 by spacecraft designer J. Harris Arnnold, it produces both military and civilian crafts. Anvil's earliest ship, the Osprey, was directly inspired by the work of the renowned ship designer Leonard Casse, who perished in a mid-air collision in SEY 2615. Casse's signature curves and circles are incorporated into the silhouettes of most Anvil ships. The [F7 Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) and the [F8 Lightning](gp:bZwQ7r6nkE) are among the Anvil spacecraft currently produced for all branches of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military.","g":["terra","terra iii","spacecraft manufacturer","vehicle manufacturer","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b46ae51c-d339-4126-b1e5-1921bb66609e"},
{"id":"aopoa","gp":"VyvY5jyZwp","t":"Aopoa","k":"company","c":["Xi'an","Commerce"],"x":"Aopoa is a [Xi'an House](gp:box9JmxvWL) and spacecraft manufacturer. They hold a monopoly granted by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government to exclusively manufacture light craft, such as the [Khartu-al (Kal'tuāl)](gp:0rqz5L28ad) and the San'tok.yāi. One of a growing number of Xi'an corporations that market their products to [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), Aopoa has sponsored multiple marketing events highlighting the exchange between Human and Xi'an cultures. In SEY 2910, they partnered with [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) to market their products to Humans. Their logo incorporates the crest of the Imperial [House Kr.ē](gp:R6v8OZOrP5).","g":["ka'ua","hyoton iv","spacecraft manufacturer","xi'an house","vehicle manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/90ce09da-d341-4c06-8973-c051819e33ed"},
{"id":"apocalypse-arms","gp":"V7gM1wXdWk","t":"Apocalypse Arms","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Apocalypse Arms is a handheld and shipboard weapons manufacturer headquartered on [Lo (Corel III)](gp:VarAoYEQYd). The company released its first branded munitions in SEY 2913, after founder Dalton Colabello discovered a cache of unused designs from deceased [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792) engineer Juliet Maupin. Everything that Apocalypse Arms sells is explicitly based on Messer Era weaponry.","g":["weapons manufacturer","juliet maupin","dalton colabello","corel iii","lo","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c8f73acd-1076-459c-a97d-f1ee93e4bdf8"},
{"id":"apollo-medivac","gp":"RwZBLzvn4N","t":"Apollo Medivac","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The Apollo Medivac is a variant of the [Apollo](gp:RPPxoQoLKZ) spacecraft developed by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). A limited edition, the Apollo Medivac is a hardened version of the standard medical ship that adds additional armor and missile racks for combat search and rescue operations. The Medivac model is typically used for rescue operations where combat may be ongoing, including in support of major United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN) operations.","g":["apollo series","roberts space industries (rsi)","support spacecraft","medical support","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a2a6faef-c5b5-42f1-8053-e64ce5fcbe58"},
{"id":"apollo-triage","gp":"RPPxoQoLKZ","t":"Apollo Triage","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Apollo Triage is an armored medical spacecraft sold by [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) for use as a dedicated hospital ship when a ground-based facility is not available. It combines the ambulance capabilities of a spacecraft like the [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed)[Cutlass Red](gp:0QxYEyzo99) with the more advanced medical technology found at medstations, and is used both to perform rescue operations and provide comprehensive patient care during transport. RSI also produces an [Apollo Medivac](gp:RwZBLzvn4N) variant with additional armor and missile racks for protection in combat.","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","apollo series","support spacecraft","medical support","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/36e40fa3-ce1e-4dea-b2b0-14ef284d7dea"},
{"id":"arccorp","gp":"0dQ47zYd6O","t":"ArcCorp (Company)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"ArcCorp is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) business conglomerate that oversees a diverse set of industries, including manufacturing, mining, [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), and space exploration. Founded in 2687 as a deep-space exploration consortium, ArcCorp shifted to mining in the early 2700s and fusion engine manufacture in the 2810s. Their fusion engine is the standard engine for 100+ meter spacecraft. After purchasing Stanton III from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) in 2865, ArcCorp developed the planet to support business and property interests. By utilizing [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) urban development theory, the planet became the most industrialized planet in the UEE.","g":["spacecraft component manufacturer","terraforming company","mining company","arccorp (corporation)","arccorp (planet)","stanton iii","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e62deb75-46da-43ca-aa20-2c8400f7fce2"},
{"id":"arccorp-stanton-iii","gp":"bBzpNY6ANd","t":"ArcCorp (Stanton III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"ArcCorp is the third planet from the sun of the Stanton system, and is one of four planets in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) owned by a corporation. When the megacorporation [ArcCorp](gp:0dQ47zYd6O) purchased the world in 2865, leadership chose to partition off the land and lease it to other organizations and individuals for further development instead of conducting all work solo. ArcCorp is the most populous planet in the [Stanton system](gp:RX3lKBA3dq). Its largest port, [Area18](gp:bEz3N7zL66), is the planet's main hub for commercial activity and interplanetary traffic.","g":["arccorp (planet)","stanton iii","stanton system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ffad47b9-0855-46a2-b344-93f073c1d29e"},
{"id":"archangel-station","gp":"VJXkOPNeE4","t":"Archangel Station","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"Archangel Station is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) space station in the [Chronos system](gp:RvlQZKy95l), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). It was initially constructed by the UEE in the 29th century as the marshaling and scientific nerve center for [Project Archangel](gp:RLMmAnr4gj), also known as Synthworld. Shipping traffic through Archangel Station has varied radically as support for the project has waxed and waned. The platform remains the home port of the 18th Battle Group.","g":["project archangel","space station","uee space station","research station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ea8a241d-939d-4374-9f59-225772dd06d5"},
{"id":"area18","gp":"bEz3N7zL66","t":"Area18","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Area18 is the main commercial port of [ArcCorp (Stanton III)](gp:bBzpNY6ANd) and serves as a nexus for traffic in the region surrounding the planet. Riker Memorial Spaceport, the main spaceport on ArcCorp, is located in Area18, and is connected to the Central Plaza via the Cityflight Transit shuttle service. As one of the zones on ArcCorp cleared for interplanetary commerce, Area18 is heavily trafficked by offworld traders and visitors. Privately-owned security firm BlacJac Security, first hired to keep the peace on the company's behalf in 2906, have recently been criticized by local news media for excessive use of force.","g":["cities","uee city","arccorp (planet)","stanton iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e93a4952-e823-4733-b5f0-17d1cfd68e1c"},
{"id":"aremis-vega-ii","gp":"RkGGjdOwQz","t":"Aremis (Vega II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Aremis is a terrestrial planet in the Vega system, [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It is famed for its set of rings, which are sharply defined by two shepherd moons that orbit the planet on the ring's inner and outer sides. After being minimally [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), it was initially settled only by the military to house [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q), [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), and [Marine](gp:V7d5ZYEr1a) bases. Vega II's population expanded in SEY 2737 when refugees fleeing the Vanduul flooded the system after the [Fall of Virgil](gp:box5moyeoZ). Over the next two centuries, the population steadily rose and the planet was on track for recognition as of 2945. The [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) formally recognized Aremis in late 2945, one month after the planet was attacked by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) in the [Battle of Vega II](gp:0Gz5mkprmg).\n\nToday, while it is still not fully recovered from the attack, Aremis has both a strong military presence and a growing population of native-born civilians and descendants of refugees. The city of [New Corvo](gp:RWwZqmP1w4) has developed into a center for commerce and experimental cuisine.","g":["aremis","vega ii","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/209eaf72-fd62-4459-8487-9b436d51728d"},
{"id":"arena-commander","gp":"VyvY5LQXd6","t":"Arena Commander","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"Arena Commander is a spaceflight simulator released in 2943 by Original Systems. In the game, players fly realistic versions of real spacecraft and engage in dogfights with similarly realistic recreations of modern ships of Xi'an, Banu, and even Vanduul origin. The lead designer of Arena Commander, Tristan Blair, was inspired to create the game after he and his friends survived a Vanduul attack thanks to the quick thinking of their commercial pilot.","g":["spaceflight simulator","original systems","games"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/51d6a517-672b-40e6-8eb4-1c9db8d93b4b"},
{"id":"ares","gp":"RPD64YANnr","t":"Ares","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Ares Star Fighter is a heavy single-seat fighter manufactured by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N). Debuting in 2949, it was designed from the ground up as a civilian ship to provide security against hostile large spacecraft or capital-class vessels. The Ares' chassis is fitted with a modular weapon mount specifically designed for use with the custom made [Behring](gp:0n9vZ4GpQn) SF7 series. The laser-equipped Ion variant is adapted for spearheading attacks, and the Inferno variant is equipped with a ballistic weapon that allows for overwhelming gunfire, fitting it into a disabling role during battle.","g":["ares ion","ares inferno","crusader industries","fighter","heavy fighter","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b6ea7c47-f06d-4c22-850f-4418b62bbc81"},
{"id":"argo-astronautics","gp":"0KnA1vvJEM","t":"Argo Astronautics","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Argo Astronautics is an industrial design and manufacturing concern located in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Best known for their [Multi-Purpose Utility Vehicle](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/mpuv) (MPUV) line of spacecraft, the company got its start designing terrestrial mag-lev train cars and has, over several centuries, become primarily associated with industrial spacecraft. \n\n# HISTORY\nThe company was founded as AR-Go Technologies in SEY 2243 by Alana Redmond, an assistant engineer of mag-lev trains. Having grown up alongside the multiple continent-spanning Trans-America rail line, Redmond had a lifelong interest in trains. In her spare time, she invented a tool to automatically repair weak points in the mag-lev tracks. After encouragement from her parents to patent and market the tool, Redmond filed articles of incorporation and accepted investments from interested parties. The commercial release of the tool was an immediate success, and over the next few decades, AR-Go focused on improving rail travel. The company's innovations included the design of a faster cargo latch and lock, new passenger management systems, and a unique vibratory recharger. \n\nShortly after acquiring Todairo Manufacture and rebranding as Argo Transportation, the company was awarded a contract to design and manufacture the entire rail transportation system for the newly-founded city of [Port Renatus](gp:RWwZWj9vOZ) on [Mars](gp:Regn8D76xw) (Sol IV). Personally planned by Redmond, the design was a success, and the company went on to produce train networks on other worlds, including the Prime Transit Metrorail on [Terra](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) (Terra III) and the Municipal Transit Line on [Angeli](gp:0QlxqwG14Q) (Croshaw II). \n\nSeeking to further improve their services and networks, Argo invested some profits from these projects into building a team of designers tasked with identifying and correcting common delay issues in rail cargo. The team found that waiting for unloaders at spaceports led to significant periods of inactivity. In response to these findings, Argo purchased Telluman Shipworks with the intention of building their own loader spacecraft. The result was the [Argo Orbital Utility Craft](gp:0rqz57XoZY) (OUC). \n\nThe OUC was capable of unloading stock cargo containers from Argo railways and moving their contents to orbital stations much quicker and more economically than traditional heavy lift transports. This proved attractive to multiple industries, who purchased the OUC and adapted it to a wide variety of uses. In 2619, Argo began offering a new model of the OUC to the public under the MPUV brand name. The sales of this ship were profitable enough that the company shifted its focus from rail work to industrial spacecraft. \n\nIn 2665, the company renamed itself Argo Astronautics in recognition of its new focus as an industrial spacecraft developer. Over the next few centuries, the company diversified its portfolio first by offering other models of the MPUV, including people carriers, recovery pods, and repair modules, and then by developing additional job-specific industrial ships. While the MPUV is still its bestselling product, Argo also produces shuttlecraft, low-atmosphere skippers, and reentry pods, among other things.","g":["spacecraft manufacturer","mars","sol iv","port renatus"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3612fcab-844b-4821-b34c-a27ef56ed85a"},
{"id":"arial-stanton-1a","gp":"VlMNJMYzy4","t":"Arial (Stanton 1a)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Arial is the first moon of [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL), and is named for [Arial Hurston](gp:0qnN5w4kmW), the creator of the [Life/Labor-style contract](gp:RLMmBD2z5d) utilized by [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) for their employees. It has a thin nitrogen-methane atmosphere and a rocky, dry landscape. Colonies of the invasive slime-mold prota have been found on Arial's surface.","g":["arial","stanton 1a","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","hurston","stanton i","arial hurston","hurston dynamics","uee moon","stanton i moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4fb79fd9-3537-4653-86e6-e2a0d901468c"},
{"id":"arial-hurston","gp":"0qnN5w4kmW","t":"Arial Hurston","k":"people","c":["People","Human","History"],"x":"Arial Hurston (SEY 2466 - 2537) was the third CEO of [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ). During his time as CEO, his cost-cutting measures pushed Hurston Dynamics into two decades of record profits. Among those measures was the still controversial [Life/Labor-style employee contract](gp:RLMmBD2z5d) that many labor advocates criticize as so binding that they are almost the equivalent of legitimized slavery. Arial, the first moon of Hurston, was named in honor of him.","g":["hurston dynamics","life/labor-style employee contract","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bde1a4e7-0ea6-4bc4-8158-314d2fa63d18"},
{"id":"ariel-sol-7b","gp":"bBzJMjj9PJ","t":"Ariel (Sol 7b)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Ariel (Sol 7b) is a moon of [Uranus (Sol VII)](gp:0rxOX3eKQ2), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Scientists speculate that the many scarps, canyons, and ridges carved into the moon's surface were created in the distant past by liquid forms of ammonia, methane, or carbon dioxide. The UEE operates multiple permanent research stations on Ariel dedicated to the study of Uranus' weather.","g":["ariel","sol 7b","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0b90bc7f-7b93-4f27-834f-7f3c825aacb6"},
{"id":"arma-mod","gp":"RWwZQEAnke","t":"ArmaMod","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"ArmaMod is a personal weapon attachment manufacturer located in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Its stocks, grips, barrels, and under-barrels are made to fit a wide variety of weapon brands. Though they are not endorsed as official mods by the original manufacturers, ArmaMod has found success on the low to mid-range market.","g":["weapon component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/76de3e84-975c-406d-bbb9-98ec9ab0c444"},
{"id":"armistead-perry","gp":"Rw1KpEJDvp","t":"Armistead Perry","k":"people","c":["People","History"],"x":"Armistead Perry was a General of the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) Navy from 2531 to 2546, and of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) Navy from 2546 to 2589. She is best known as the architect of the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO). Born into a military family, Perry completed her [Equivalency](gp:Vgg7YGdQDY) at age 16 and was the valedictorian at the UPE Navy Officer Academy and Flight Training Center. She entered the UPE [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) in 2488 as a Lieutenant and was deployed to the [Corel system](gp:R9vQnko7Y2), where she patrolled the [Geddon](gp:bo1yaaL4wN)-Corel jump point and intercepted smugglers from the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). She quickly rose through the ranks, making Colonel by 2503. In 2531, after losing a leg in a clash with a major smuggling ring, Perry was promoted to General and transferred to the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP) based on her decades of experience along the UPE's borders. She played a key role in establishing a major military presence in the [Yā'mon](gp:VarxDJ5yLo) system after its 2531 discovery, and in 2542 proposed the creation of a buffer zone between the the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) and the UPE to add an extra line of defense to its borders. After months of deliberation, the [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) agreed and selected eight planetary systems to create this zone, naming it in honor of General Perry.","g":["perry line","uee navy","human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a6c44950-f31f-435e-8ac0-a38ca6b50a6e"},
{"id":"armistice-day","gp":"RWwZQWZQDA","t":"Armistice Day","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"Armistice Day is a holiday celebrated annually on 29 May in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It was established in SEY 2792 to recognize the 2789 signing of the the [Akari-Kr.ē Treaty,](gp:bE3rKrl5z6) which brought about an unofficial resolution to the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (2530 - 2793) and contributed to [the events](gp:bE3rKa32P7) that ended the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792). Many [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) businesses close during Armistice Day. The holiday is especially popular on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), the home of Senator [Terrence Akari](gp:RL6ZQLwnko), who authored the treaty in secret with a then-young [Emperor T.uēng se Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo).","g":["terrence akari","xi'an-human cold war","akari-kr.ē treaty","messer era","t.uēng se kr.ē","uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bd3d9b58-967e-4f90-a21e-6900d754fd0d"},
{"id":"armitage-orion-iii","gp":"RL6KLK4ylo","t":"Armitage (Orion III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Vanduul"],"x":"Armitage is the third planet from the sun in the [Orion system](gp:VlMpwMky6d). It was a [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and settled planet which became the site of [first contact](gp:RWwZDmxaXP) between [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) in 2681, when a Vanduul raiding party razed the settlement of [Dell Township](gp:RkZ9mGOpD4). Before the Orion system was [lost to the Vanduul](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) in 2712, Armitage was a fast-developing colony world of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["armitage","orion iii","habitable planet","habitable","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/be2f8a61-c636-4bb3-94b5-92504fa7bb97"},
{"id":"armitage-weapons-manufacturer","gp":"V8gJ1vK78X","t":"Armitage (Weapons Manufacturer)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Armitage is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) weapons manufacturer founded in 2717 by a group of survivors from the [Battle of Orion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) (2712). Named for the once Human-inhabited planet in the fallen system, Armitage produces weapons that are simple to use by people without training. The company has remained committed to philanthropic causes; twenty-five percent of proceeds from their sales go towards helping families displaced by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO).","g":["weapons manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3335bb72-0c1a-435c-b91b-f376f160ef4c"},
{"id":"aron-award","gp":"bBz5BKzjWJ","t":"Aron Award","k":"history","c":["Culture","Human"],"x":"The Aron Awards, popularly known as the Arons, are awards for outstanding works in design, given by the Interplanetary Association of Artisans and Designers (IAAD). They are recognized as one of the most prestigious design awards in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Each year since 2779, one outstanding product and one outstanding designer are chosen for the award by a committee made up of designers from multiple disciplines. Some past winners have included [Alberto Vara](gp:VgEgojrAQ3) (2921) for his work on [Origin Jumpworks'](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) [M50](gp:V7gMWO7Yo3), and [microTech's](gp:bE3rBB4j7J) [mobiGlas](gp:01dW3alkmB) (2818).","g":["design awards","awards and honors"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4dd6a1d9-6185-4c17-8656-f7fadc36c823"},
{"id":"arrastra","gp":"0n1Oyp7ml7","t":"Arrastra","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Arrastra is a mining spacecraft manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) (RSI). Designed for deep space, large scale operations, it comes with remote-controlled industrial mining turrets, a tractor beam, and an on-board ore refinery to help limit the need for third party involvement between harvesting and selling resources. The ship's bay can support two small vehicles, and its living quarters can house a crew of up to five.","g":["mining","heavy mining","roberts space industries (rsi)","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/87df634d-3c0c-414e-ad29-4b1e1b0e1f24"},
{"id":"arrow","gp":"box5ODOk6L","t":"Arrow","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Arrow is a light fighter manufactured by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN). A dedicated single-seat interceptor, it was built for speed and maneuverability in dogfighting, intending to directly counter the Vanduul Blade light fighter, which had begun to effectively combat the heavier [Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) and [Sabre](gp:0NwpeQOqY4) space superiority ships. The Arrow was introduced as a civilian model in 2949.","g":["light fighter","anvil aerospace","fighter","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/08be1d2d-24f7-4166-9831-8047e8aa9ad3"},
{"id":"artemis","gp":"0jGxngnLzm","t":"Artemis","k":"history","c":["Spacecraft","History","Human"],"x":"*Artemis* was a long-haul colony spacecraft that launched from Earth (Sol III) in 2232 and disappeared in 2237. Built before the discovery of [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) and after the discovery of quantum travel, its mission was to travel to the potentially habitable planetary system GJ 667Cc and establish a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) colony through conventional quantum drive engines. Travel was estimated to take over a century. The 5000 people on board, all volunteers, were to remain in stasis while the prototype artificial intelligence nicknamed [Janus](gp:VDzOvEdNyd) piloted the ship and managed life support. In 2237, fourteen years before the ship was scheduled to fall out of contact with Earth, its daily status updates abruptly ceased. It has not been seen since. \n\nWhen news of the ship's disappearance was released, many speculated that Janus was responsible for the loss of the vessel. Evidence corroborating this claim has never been found.","g":["the artemis","human spacecraft","human history","human vessel"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4894ef7e-db6d-4645-8fa7-9a89ccd6c0f4"},
{"id":"artificial-gravity","gp":"0rxB6vkMqd","t":"Artificial Gravity","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Artificial gravity refers to the use of technology to replicate the effects of a gravitational force. Common amongst spacefaring civilizations, it is vital aboard spacecraft and space stations to combat the muscle and bone atrophy that can result from long-term exposure to low gravity environments. Early technology relied on rotation to create gravity, whereas modern technology relies on spinning superconductors to generate powerful fields in limited areas. The Localized Artificial Gravity (LAG) system common throughout the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) utilizes gravplating panels connected to a particle generator via a system of conduits to generate gravity on demand. In the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9), artificial gravity technology is especially advanced, and is so commonplace that it is used for mundane activities such as holding up tables and chairs.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8ed47d9b-7725-4851-8c63-60f8caf94bde"},
{"id":"ascension-astro","gp":"R4ZG162l4w","t":"Ascension Astro","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Ascension Astro is a Human spacecraft equipment company that develops and manufactures aftermarket stealth components. The company was founded in 2901 by a group of friends who had developed a new technique to reduce the infrared and electromagnetic signature of standard ship thrusters. Over time, Ascension Astro has changed focus from selling only high-end boutique thruster modifications to mass producing thruster and shield generator units.","g":["spacecraft component manufacturer","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4354cd7d-1925-4bb6-8957-4bc61ef77953"},
{"id":"ashana-nul-v","gp":"bZkd47KMB6","t":"Ashana (Nul V)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ashana is the fifth planet from the sun of the unclaimed [Nul system](gp:VgEnlpqyJ9). A cold desert world, the majority of its surface is covered in shifting sand dunes interspersed with glaciers. In 2571, the [UEES Olympus](gp:0Gxk9rGkej) was pursuing a group of anti-[Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) activists to their makeshift base on Ashana when it drifted too close and was caught by the planet's gravitational pull. The carrier crashed and was subsequently abandoned. People who had been hiding out in caves on Ashana moved into the wrecked *Olympus* and turned it into a [settlement](gp:Regrl72egM) of the same name.","g":["ashana","nul v","nul system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b89b881-c63e-41ac-aee2-44277c7e27dd"},
{"id":"asiatica","gp":"RxNx1lONPa","t":"Asiatica","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"Asiatica is the largest state on the planet [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB). It was created in the nascency [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO), the first single-world [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) government. Populous and prosperous, Asiatica is a center of commerce and transportation. The [Human Overpopulation Era](gp:RxNxLk4yNz) left much of Asiatica's landscape demolished in favor of superstructures and skyscrapers. However, after Humans expanded into [Croshaw](gp:0qanKAEJwp) in the 2300s SEY, a movement to restore the gardens and parks lost during that time has had a positive effect on the environment.","g":["sol iii","earth","states","uee states"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7b8944d3-91f2-4104-8355-29da22eba3dc"},
{"id":"assan-kieren","gp":"RWwZQK774P","t":"Assan Kieren","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Assan Kieren (2584 - 2639?) was a Human politician representing Terra (Terra III) who publicly opposed the United Empire of Earth's pro-military agenda and then disappeared under still-unexplained circumstances. He was elected a governor of Terra in 2633. In 2638, Kieren achieved notoriety across the UEE when he called for Terra to hold a vote of sovereignty that would allow it to separate from the UEE. The UEE's propaganda machine under the Messers responded by working to discredit Kieren, and his referendum failed. The ensuing controversy ended Kieren's political career. He disappeared the following November.","g":["messer era","governors","uee senator","terra iii","terra"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a061c60e-1f2e-4633-9dca-90552dab356e"},
{"id":"asd","gp":"RkZ957WBpn","t":"Associated Science & Development","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Associated Science & Development (ASD) is a high-end Human spacecraft weapons manufacturer headquartered on Persei (Rhetor II). Among their common products are energy weapons, distortion cannons, rail guns, and shredders. The company's reputation suffered a blow after their EE6 Electron Cannon suffered a catastrophic malfunction that resulted in several deaths during its public unveiling.","g":["asd","weapons manufacturer","persei","rhetor ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9d7f87bf-c431-4db9-8468-63537c022898"},
{"id":"astravin-university-at-cestulus","gp":"box52XYpDL","t":"Astravin University at Cestulus","k":"place","c":["Education","Human","Locations"],"x":"Astravin University at Cestulus (AUC) is a public research university in [Jata](gp:Rz2PmWxpMM) on [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5) and the flagship campus of the Astravin University system. Founded in SEY 2520, AUC survived Cestulus' difficult colonial period and expanded during the planet's economic reversal in the 27th century. It is the largest university in the [Davien system](gp:Rz2g71YlkY) and features an oshi fish as its mascot.","g":["auc","cestulus","davien ii","higher education","uee higher education","uee education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3036c75f-ff26-4761-ad87-dd71730655bf"},
{"id":"astrid-messer-vii","gp":"0KnA1D5nQM","t":"Astrid Messer VII","k":"people","c":["People","Human","History"],"x":"Astrid Messer VII (SEY 2661 - 2701) was one of two [Imperators](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) from 2697 to 2701. She seized power from her aunt [Illyana Messer VI](gp:bZwQBNmWrL) after the latter died of a sudden stroke. Agents loyal to Illyana smuggled her youngest son and named successor, [Samuel](gp:RkZ9W2L2NB), away from [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) before Astrid could have him assassinated. As Imperator, Astrid devoted military resources to locating Samuel, expanded censorship, and ordered mass arrests of journalists who spoke against the conflict. She was assassinated by Samuel's agents in 2701, which led to his ascension to Imperator.","g":["uee imperator","messer era","messer dynasty","human people","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/981bad52-fcec-44db-b007-506bf8abfdd1"},
{"id":"asura-ferron-iii","gp":"0qaPo2JOj1","t":"Asura (Ferron III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Asura is the third planet from the sun in the [Ferron system](gp:Vy2Qo1dB18) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). [Terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) shortly after the system's discovery in 2460, the early settlers of Asura generated a great deal of wealth from the planet's rich mineral deposits. Asura became one of the richest planets in the UEE, with a thriving economy immediately evident by the grand, ornate architectural style common in its cities. However, in the early 29th century, its mineral resources were fully depleted, and within a decade, the economy was in shambles. Though the population has fallen considerably since the mining crash, it is still represented by two [Senators](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ).","g":["asura","ferron iii","ferron system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/75f5baa9-584f-4c40-8a21-41404f21e7d7"},
{"id":"atchivo","gp":"0qaPOdoMra","t":"Atchivo","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Atchivo is a settlement on [Goss I](gp:RegqZ3ze8y), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), located deep within the planet's largest agricultural zone. A major shipping center with a busy spaceport, it is surrounded by enormous commercial and storage facilities. Most of the produce on Goss I marked for export to Cassel (Goss II) passes through customs on Atchivo before being hauled off the planet.","g":["goss i","towns","uee towns"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c89450a2-5353-4f71-905c-870f8acae0f9"},
{"id":"atlas-platform","gp":"R9vdJKjy8M","t":"Atlas Platform","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Atlas Platform was a mobile missile platform developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military. First introduced in 2808 as the first in a potential line of anti-air and anti-space vehicles to be used in ground-based engagements. Its sturdy frame and adaptable chassis proved successful in combat, and Anvil accepted a long-term contract with the UEE to develop military vehicles. After it was retired in 2821, the frame of the Atlas was used as the basis for the [Ballista](gp:V8gJyXMDrM) missile platform in 2822, and again for the [Spartan](gp:0QlyWlqqyJ) armored personnel carrier in 2951.","g":["anvil aerospace","military vehicle","human vehicle","tank","mobile missile platform"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b564c555-8033-4e31-bf35-9bc2b1a519bd"},
{"id":"atrocity-at-jata","gp":"0Gz5GgEvkj","t":"Atrocity at Jata","k":"history","c":["History","Illegal Activity","Human"],"x":"The atrocity at [Jata](gp:Rz2PmWxpMM) was the first in a series of bombings that took place in the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) in SEY 2546. While only the initial attacks took place in [Jata](gp:Rz2PmWxpMM), [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5), the name became synonymous with bombings that were shown to have used the same technology on other worlds. After multiple attacks and almost five thousand civilian deaths with no perpetrator identified by the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk), then-High General [Ivar Messer](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) used the attacks to stoke public fervor to support the creation of the office of [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr), to which he was shortly elected. The architect of the bombings was never conclusively found. Evidence uncovered in 2806 by historian Sydney Kamarck posits that Messer himself may have arranged the bombings with two former acquaintances from the UPE Army.","g":["ivar messer i","adam corr","cyrus ishitaka","sydney kamarck","prime citizen","human history","terrorist attack"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/16556779-9dd9-4d27-90d4-09e743c29fc9"},
{"id":"atuvo","gp":"0n12epw8Zd","t":"Atuvo","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Atuvo is a Human manufacturer and retailer of upscale kitchenware, houseware, appliances, and furniture headquartered on Mars (Sol IV), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Founded in 2872 by noted chef Chu Thụy Du, it started as a small shop in [Port Renatus](gp:RWwZWj9vOZ). It soon gained a reputation for producing quality goods, enough so that after a year of major profits in 2881, Atuvo expanded to three other locations. The success of its Foodspace System, a series of kitchen technologies designed to save space while serving all possible food preparation needs, caught the attention of [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw), who partnered with Atuvo to supply their [Constellation Phoenix](gp:VyvYqezlqW) with tables, chairs, and appliances.","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","home goods retail","commercial and industrial goods manufacturer","furniture manufacture","mars","sol iv","constellation phoenix"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f0275a52-64aa-4236-8a89-7ab4c6ba8b34"},
{"id":"aurora-cl","gp":"R6v8nwGPNq","t":"Aurora CL","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Aurora Clipper (CL) is a light freighter variant of the [Aurora series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/aurora-series) of single-crew spacecraft developed by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). It was designed as a starter spacecraft for entry-level merchants and traders, with an expanded cargo capacity over that of its base model. In order to keep the price-point down, RSI removed the Aurora CL's armor capabilities and equipped it with a smaller power plant.","g":["light freight","roberts space industries (rsi)","freight","aurora series","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/59b98f5e-22cd-475b-b222-1140d7c9c30c"},
{"id":"aurora-es","gp":"0rqzmOo9Nq","t":"Aurora ES","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Aurora Essential (ES) is a light single-crew spacecraft manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). It is marketed as an entry-level spacecraft with a lower price point making it one of the more common vehicles found in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Several [Aurora](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/aurora-series) variants have been produced: the [LX luxury version](gp:R6v8nwKka4), the [MR combat](gp:bZwQGo6D36) variant, the [LN fighter](gp:R56nGJnEz9), and the [CL cargo](gp:R6v8nwGPNq) ship.","g":["aurora series","roberts space industries (rsi)","pathfinder","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9efb9dce-09a1-43b1-bc19-4f15a51d18d3"},
{"id":"aurora-ln","gp":"R56nGJnEz9","t":"Aurora LN","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"Aurora Legionnaire (LN) is a fighter variant of the [Aurora series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/aurora-series) of single-crew spacecraft developed by Roberts Space Industries (RSI). Like the [Aurora MR](gp:bZwQGo6D36), it closely retains the original specifications of the [Aurora ES](gp:0rqzmOo9Nq), but features upgraded hardpoints and more robust shield capabilities.","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","fighter","light fighter","aurora series","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fccc1c81-d11f-40e2-9717-91a63bb5381e"},
{"id":"aurora-lx","gp":"R6v8nwKka4","t":"Aurora LX","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Aurora LX is a luxury variant of the [Aurora series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/aurora-series) of single-crew spacecraft developed by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). Among other modifications, its interior was upgraded with premium materials to be more comfortable than the base model with additional decorative trim on the hull. Ship reviewer Jax McCleary once compared the LX to \"eating a Whamburger soaked in champagne.\"","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","pathfinder","aurora series","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cc6f372f-1c08-4e96-a2ca-f6b542dd9187"},
{"id":"aurora-mr","gp":"bZwQGo6D36","t":"Aurora MR","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Aurora Marque (MR) is a variant of the [Aurora series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/aurora-series) of single-crew spacecraft developed by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). It closely retains the mass and maneuverability of the base model while adding additional weaponry and cooling system capacity.","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","fighter","light fighter","aurora series","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ecde709c-e4dd-4ec8-9eae-3df54b0511f9"},
{"id":"automated-hydrogen-fuel-harvesting-platforms","gp":"V3qg1w71yj","t":"Automated Hydrogen Fuel Harvesting Platforms","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Automated hydrogen fuel harvesting platforms are space stations set in stable orbit around hydrogen-rich gas giants that harvest and process hydrogen into spacecraft fuel. While they are fully automated, they are not self-repairing. Well-maintained platforms are visited by repair crews multiple times per Standard Earth Year. Platforms that have fallen into disrepair are sometimes abandoned.","g":["hydrogen fuel","automated hydrogen fuel harvesting platform","spacecraft fuel"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/26c81383-188c-414a-9657-0e823ed2d444"},
{"id":"avenger","gp":"ReJanvr73r","t":"Avenger","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The Avenger is a multi-role fighter sold by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). It was initially designed as a [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) carrier-borne spacecraft in the mid-28th century SEY. As more focused interceptors and space superiority spacecraft were developed in the mid-29th century, the Avenger found a second life as a law-enforcement utility spacecraft until it too was replaced by more current designs. Today, the ship is flown by civilian pilots thanks to ease of use, reliability, and Aegis releasing multiple variants. Avenger variants include the [Titan](gp:V7gMyBEKv3) cargo ship, [Stalker](gp:0qnN6jyoa5) bounty hunter and [Warlock](gp:V3qgyY8AyW) EMP platform.","g":["aegis dynamics","avenger series","fighter","human spacecraft","light fighter"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4b7e3559-5b08-4071-8349-6b08d96abcbc"},
{"id":"aydo","gp":"01L5KoNx28","t":"Aydo","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Aydo is a major city on [Green (Ellis III)](gp:RWoNrNeLKP) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A coastal city, it sits atop a sheer wall of cliffs overlooking the ocean. In the past, gaps in these cliffs were used as tracks in one of the legs of the race that ultimately gave birth to the first [Murray Cup](gp:bE3r71yZ87). While most of these gaps have since been closed off, some of them have been preserved and can be closely viewed during MCR Museum tours. Murray Tower, a 5-star hotel and restaurant located in Aydo, boasts a spectacular view of the city, the cliffs, and the ocean, and is often booked years in advance. Aydo's population is said to double during the Murray Cup.","g":["green","ellis iii","uee city","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/10144402-99e8-4c88-8465-8ba2ba2f3df3"},
{"id":"azure-sky-aero","gp":"0qajMeyPvk","t":"Azure Sky Aero","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Azure Sky Aero is a tech company that manufactures EVA suits, EVA packs, and other wearable equipment. Particularly notable for their Better Built (BB) line of propulsion devices, the company began as a machining studio that produced and sold custom parts to spacecraft corporations. They began experimenting with EVA tech in SEY 2911, eventually releasing the BB-1 under their own name in 2914.","g":["clothing manufacturer","electronic consumer goods manufacturer","human company"],"img":"https://static.robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/upload/c8fe7ea2-238a-4ea2-a893-63228abc76cf"},
{"id":"b0otycall","gp":"R6d3NaGl7n","t":"B0otycall","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*B0otyCall* is an underground [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) broadcast that covers events pertaining to the criminal underworld of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It is hosted by an anonymous person who goes by the pseudonym Jester. It first appeared in 2941, when Jester successfully hijacked the Spectrum signal and aired information on a planned [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) sting on the independent settlement Levski in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). Soon, Jester began to regularly intercept the signal in whichever system he happened to be, offering his sardonic opinion on recent events, sharing tips about areas to avoid, and describing his own, often violent, exploits. Episodes of *B0otyCall* air irregularly and are sometimes interrupted.","g":["pirate show"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4dc719f2-6035-486e-8328-58f9b6b61555"},
{"id":"b3","gp":"R4jjEaMeGw","t":"B3","k":"culture","c":["Food and Beverages","Human"],"x":"B3 is a strong brandy distilled in the Rhetor system from blue bilva, a fruit indigenous to Reisse Rhetor III). In 2733, a group of students at the [University of Mentor](gp:RWozpy2kwa) on Mentor (Rhetor IV) used a bushel of [blue bilva](gp:VlMMykdrNM) as the basis for an experimental homemade spirit. The concoction, which retained a sweet flavor profile along with a powerful alcoholic punch, was a hit at their next party. Blue bilva brandy continued as a student-made spirit enjoyed by locals until 2872, when the drink was smuggled to the University of Rhetor on Reisse and it underwent a surge in popularity. Following this increase in demand, three University of Mentor students started the Blue Bilva Brandy company in 2875, with B3 as their flagship beverage.","g":["alcohol","beverage","human beverage"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4c5fed4b-f62b-4600-b147-34f5a4dbcea8"},
{"id":"bacchus-i","gp":"0jGyn86pXm","t":"Bacchus I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Bacchus I is the first planet from the suns of the [Bacchus system](gp:bBzaExgj1o), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A massive and dense super-Earth, it has both high gravity and a wide circumference. It is close enough to its suns that parts of its crust liquify into lava during the day and solidify during the night. The planet's hot and smoggy atmosphere creates a high-pressure environment, making the already dangerous surface impossible to land on without specialized equipment.","g":["bacchus system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/06d5364b-4c00-4eae-9626-f03e549dbc52"},
{"id":"bacchus-ii","gp":"Var6oAn18Z","t":"Bacchus II","k":"place","c":["Planets","Banu"],"x":"Bacchus II is the second planet from the suns of the [Bacchus system](gp:bBzaExgj1o), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A temperate terrestrial world blanketed by vast oceans, it is dotted with thousands of populated islands and archipelagos and is host to a wide variety of climates and biodiversity. Travel between the islands is common, and water vessels are a popular mode of transportation. [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) archaeologists have discovered evidence on Bacchus II that suggests it is the original homeworld of the Banu people, though the Banu themselves have not confirmed or validated this.","g":["bacchus system","habitable","habitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0fc11e9b-5a37-474d-a5e0-ce57990254af"},
{"id":"bacchus-iii","gp":"0jGynn8Ben","t":"Bacchus III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Bacchus III is the third planet from the suns of the [Bacchus system](gp:bBzaExgj1o), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A gas giant with a green and brown atmosphere, it is dotted with swirling clouds that mark the location of violent storms, some of which have raged for hundreds of years. The largest and oldest of these storms was nicknamed \"Jerry's Eye\" by [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) astronomers in honor of the first [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) ever [encountered](gp:VY4Wnv7ZgW) by Humanity.","g":["bacchus system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/74bc02e1-d480-4b75-bd86-102ddeb0f5f5"},
{"id":"bacchus-system","gp":"bBzaExgj1o","t":"Bacchus System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Banu"],"x":"The Bacchus system is a planetary system in the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) that consists of a super-Earth, a terrestrial planet, a gas giant, and a binary star system made up of a type G and a type K main sequence star. Believed to be the home system of the Banu people, it is the traditional location of [the Gathering](gp:V7gM7yNAeK), an irregularly-held convocation of Banu leadership that convenes to make decisions that will affect all [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) people. Myriad well-trafficked trade lanes cross the system, linking [Bacchus II](gp:Var6oAn18Z) and the [Nuso flotilla](gp:R9vEnnAY2M) to the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) via the Garron-Bacchus jump point.","g":["banu system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b4277b44-c97a-451a-94f1-658aa57f3708"},
{"id":"badger-bad","gp":"R6v817Xa4e","t":"Badger Bad","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Badger Bad is a Human weapons and ammunition manufacturer specializing in missiles and handheld rockets. It was founded in 2932 by former employees of Talon Weapon Systems who were seeking to break their former employer's hold on the missile market. Though they have yet to completely disrupt Talon's sales, Badger Bad's missiles have seen high sales numbers in the civilian market.","g":["munitions manufacturer","weapons manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a4ef9401-d53f-4e5a-bd00-6306af7df736"},
{"id":"baker-i","gp":"Vy2dg37KDa","t":"Baker I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Baker I is the first planet from the binary stars in the [Baker system](gp:Rz2KGkv13N), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Due to its proximity to the suns, its surface has been eroded to the point that its iron core is partially exposed. Astrophysicists estimate that it will collide with one of the system's stars in approximately 150 million years.","g":["baker ii","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","baker system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f7805899-a5c8-4c7f-9a49-8f3fc6ef11b0"},
{"id":"baker-ii","gp":"bEzdJwPmzQ","t":"Baker II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Baker II is a smog planet in the [Baker system](gp:Rz2KGkv13N), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The second planet from the suns, its position in the green band would normally make it a prime candidate for colonization. However, the high-pressure, poisonous atmosphere has so far prevented any attempts at [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). Spacecraft that have attempted to land on Baker II have been heavily damaged by the toxic air.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","baker system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a196f6a1-8cbb-4479-8712-7e90bd2bef5b"},
{"id":"baker-iii","gp":"V8W73LXErr","t":"Baker III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Baker III is an ice giant in the [Baker system](gp:Rz2KGkv13N), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The third planet from the suns, its atmosphere is white with deep veins of blue. Baker III's circumference is actively expanding and therefore has been deemed as a hazard by the [UEE Department of Transportation and Navigation](gp:VDoPezP7E1).","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","baker system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c06e88c2-2e16-46b3-b533-c49c1d3161cc"},
{"id":"baker-iv","gp":"RPD8Xr8Xjq","t":"Baker IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Baker IV is the fourth planet from the suns of the [Baker system](gp:Rz2KGkv13N), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A terrestrial, coreless planet, it has no magnetic field, but many valuable mineral deposits. [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA) maintains an outpost there named GIO. The planet is lightly populated by the overseers and workers of Shubin's mining operations.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","baker system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/336f6360-2628-4274-80dc-c6e4b5971af4"},
{"id":"baker-system","gp":"Rz2KGkv13N","t":"Baker System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Baker system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Discovered in 2522, It consists of two K-type main sequence stars and four uninhabited worlds. The only major [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) settlements in the system are [Xenia](gp:0ODJ2DE6rZ), a [Covalex](gp:V3qgXNEGQW) shipping hub, and [GIO](gp:RMN8kv8AeA), a [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA) mining outpost. Cargo ships transporting goods between the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) and the UEE often use Xenia as a pit stop. On an irregular basis, Baker hosts an unofficial racing event known as the [Able Baker Challenge](gp:RPP4LXMeBZ).","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/48623669-058b-4b5f-bc9c-5afa95095992"},
{"id":"ballista","gp":"V8gJyXMDrM","t":"Ballista","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Military","Human"],"x":"The Ballista is a mobile missile platform developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military. It was designed for terrestrial anti-air and anti-space operations and is built around a large missile launcher and reloading mechanism. While it is primarily utilized for the military, it is also sold to civilian operators, such as homesteaders and other frontier operators who have cause to defend assets from airstrikes. The Dunestalker and Snowblind variants are adapted for use in desert and tundra environments.","g":["mobile missile platform","anvil aerospace","tank","ballista dunestalker","ballista snowblind","military vehicle","human vehicle","atlas platform"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2a0bb01b-6cda-4449-aa53-0bbb44fd47d3"},
{"id":"banded-fessle","gp":"bZwvaaLll6","t":"Banded Fessle","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"# Banded Fessle\nThe banded fessle is a carnivorous saltwater fish indigenous to the warmer areas of the Animas Sea on Terra (Terra III), Terra System, United Empire of Earth (UEE). A popular aquarium fish, banded fessles in captivity have been bred to encourage docility and to accentuate their deep blue vertical stripes.\n \n \n# Description\nBanded fessles are identifiable by their ovular heads, protruding mouths, and deep blue and white stripes. These stripes help them camouflage themselves among the seaweed and coral of their natural environment. They have squat, triangular dorsal fins, lowslung pectoral fins, and broad, strong tails. Their mouths are lined with two rows of small, sharp teeth which they use for grasping and consuming prey. Over a ten-year life cycle, a banded fessle can grow to between 40 and 50 cm long.\n \n \n# Behavior and Ecology\nBanded fessles are ambush hunters, preying mainly on smaller fish, macroinvertebrates, and zooplankton. They play an important role in their ecosystem, keeping worms and other creatures from over-grazing on vegetation and disrupting delicate coral reefs. When hunting, a banded fessle floats motionless among local environmental features until a prey animal passes about 5 cm from its hiding spot. It then strikes before its prey is aware of its presence. At around three years of age, a banded fessle will begin to seek out a mate. Banded fessles form lifelong pairs. Each fish will protect the other from threats, assist in hunting, share larger prey, and fend off potential suitors. A banded fessle that has lost its mate sometimes refuses to seek another.\n \nWhen they are ready to spawn, the pair seek out an appropriate spawning medium, usually a strong seaweed frond or sheltered coral surface. The female then lays a line of eggs and the male fertilizes them. They repeat this process until they have laid up to a thousand eggs. The parents guard their offspring until they learn to hunt on their own. About 1 percent survive to adulthood.\n \nIn general, banded fessles seldom venture more than 12 meters deep, although they have been recorded at depths of 15 meters when pursuing prey.\n \n \n# Aquarium Fish\nPrized for their pairing behavior and their vibrant, contrasting colors, banded fessles are one of the more popular aquarium fish in the UEE. They number among the marine life that can be raised in tanks alongside fish indigenous to Earth (Sol III). Ideally, they should be kept in warm saltwater, about 24 to 25 degrees Celsius. Because they can grow to be up to 50 cm long, they should only be kept in very large tanks (750 liters or more per fish).\n \nThe banded fessle is not territorial, but as a carnivore, it can pose a danger to other fish in a shared tank. It is recommended that generous portions of food be provided to fessles so they do not get hungry and turn on their tank mates.","g":["animas sea","terra","pets","fish","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/817cdd78-0af9-49c7-a093-fa14c2fd21e5"},
{"id":"banshee-i","gp":"R5pA751ZyX","t":"Banshee I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Banshee I is a rocky mesoplanet in the [Banshee system](gp:0Gx4BENmKg), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Long-distance scans have indicated that Banshee I contains many pockets of valuable mineral resources. However, its proximity to the system's star, a pulsar that emits regular bursts of deadly radiation, have made exploration of the planet difficult.","g":["banshee system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f5421449-7318-4877-81fb-4860b6b9544d"},
{"id":"banshee-ii","gp":"VarjBAK2am","t":"Banshee II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Banshee II is a terrestrial planet in the [Banshee system](gp:0Gx4BENmKg), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The second planet out from the system's sun, much of the planet's surface has been worn away due to solar radiation, partially exposing the iron core. Additionally, large sections of the surface were removed during the [Messer Era (2546 - 2792)](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) for unknown purposes.","g":["banshee system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6d238cd8-ed09-47f2-a28a-1e6d2599a790"},
{"id":"banshee-iv","gp":"VgE3k1DGWx","t":"Banshee IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Banshee IV is an ice giant with a marbled blue and white atmosphere in the [Banshee system](gp:0Gx4BENmKg), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the fourth and final planet from the sun. There is a vast gap of empty space between Banshee IV and [Lorona (Banshee III)](gp:bZkDByjyPO). Astrophysicists speculate that it once may have housed one or more planets that have since gone rogue.","g":["banshee system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1e651a1a-d5b3-4d5d-9a6a-a7f9efd5d31f"},
{"id":"banshee-system","gp":"0Gx4BENmKg","t":"Banshee System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Banshee system, discovered by [Adaliz Dayan](gp:Vgg7Ml89dN) in SEY 2317, is an unusual planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), consisting of a pulsar, a mesoplanet, two terrestrial planets, and one ice giant. Its star is not luminous enough for life to develop on the surfaces of any of its planets. However, the third planet from the sun, [Lorona](gp:bZkDByjyPO), supports an underground settlement populous enough to hold a seat in the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ). From the 24th to the 26th century, travel to the system was severely restricted by the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) until the landmark Minto vs UPE court case that nullified the government's travel ban and ruled that full systems could not be declared off limits.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5717d037-451e-447e-be5f-7f7285aa6531"},
{"id":"banu","gp":"0NwpYPpNZ4","t":"Banu","k":"species","c":["Banu","Civilizations"],"x":"The Banu are a spacefaring civilization, and the first extrasolar one to ever make contact with [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2). They are capable of quantum travel, traversing [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY), and [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) planets. Because the Banu do not keep historical records and inhabit multiple celestial bodies in disparate planetary systems, their world of origin is unknown. They are capable of comfortably breathing in a variety of atmospheres and can adapt to a wide range of environments not suitable for Humans, Tevarin, or Xi'an. Banu are trained from childhood in a single skill by members of their [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron), a group of non-blood related Banu who live and work together. They maintain open trade relations with all known spacefaring civilizations.","g":["banu protectorate","extant civilizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c86ce135-94b0-4c03-ae5a-644d13525e01"},
{"id":"banu-cuisine","gp":"0GxyNLZzaP","t":"Banu Cuisine","k":"culture","c":["Food and Beverages","Banu"],"x":"# BANU CUISINE\nBanu Cuisine refers to the common methods by which [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) prepare their food for consumption. Because of the scarcity of records on Banu history due to their cultural practice of not documenting the events of the past, little is known about the origins of their food preparation methods. In addition, their vast trade network, love of experimentation, sensitive palates, and ability to digest almost anything have led Banu to integrate ingredients and cooking techniques from other cultures into their cuisine over time. There are nevertheless distinct traits that are typical of Banu cooking. Most crucial are the melding of many flavors and textures in a dish, the importance placed on utilizing the entirety of each ingredient in a meal, and the taboo on food waste. \n# CUSTOMS\nTypically, Banu have one big meal that is eaten alongside other members of their [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron), and then snack throughout the day. The meal is expected to be a show of abundance, with more food than can be eaten in one sitting. Using their hands, each Banu will take food from the display and place it on plates for ease of mixing constituent parts of the meal to personal taste. The meal is then eaten while sitting partially reclined. \n\nAt the end of a meal, the remaining food is left out, and Banu will come back to it during their work shifts to pick up snacks and maintain their energy. Any food left at the end of the day is then added to the *onjussuæ*, or \"all-flavor\" stew, a dish that is featured at almost every big meal and is normally eaten as an appetizer. It isn't unusual for a Souli to keep a simmering pot of *onjussuæ* that is rarely emptied all the way, and is replenished with liquid and ingredients as needed. If properly maintained, *onjussuæ* can be perpetually cooked for decades. \n\nServing utensils are not common; food that cannot be grasped is scooped with personal plates or cups that individual Banu are expected to bring to the table. These plates often have handles attached and are wide, round, and slightly bowled so that flavors can mingle at the bottom. Banu take pride in using beautifully decorated plates and cups.  \n\n# THE NINE TASTES\nBanu have a very sensitive palate and can detect a wide range of flavors. When filling their plates at the family meal, they seek a balance of what they refer to as *biki ndzotayu*, or the Nine Tastes: salty, savory, sweet, pungent (acidic/spicy), bitter, hot, cold, soft, and crunchy. The more tastes included in a single bite of a dish, the better it is. One example of this is *ofasa*, a popular fried treat and staple of Banu food markets. The outside is hot and crunchy, the inside is soft and cool, the *ibifissa* meat is sweet and salty, and the *angafede* is bitter and pungent. Having all nine flavors in one bite is seen as efficient and is highly prized. \n# FOOD WASTE TABOO\nBanu do not have a notion of food waste. Whereas [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) will peel an orange before consuming it, Banu will eat the entire thing, savoring the bitter rind as a part of the experience. A [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) will discard the hard shell of a *klom.e'a*, but a Banu diner will leave it on, enjoying the mouthfeel of crunchy chitin breaking apart against soft, sweet flesh. It is seen as extremely inefficient and wasteful not to use the entirety of all ingredients. If any part of an ingredient doesn't work in a particular meal, it is saved for later and used elsewhere. \n# FOOD AND EATING SOULIS\nThere is a prevailing cultural attitude that things made by expert artisans are superior to anything that can be made by a hobbyist, and this includes meals. Outside of the maintenance of the pot of *onjussuæ*, there is a strong preference among Soulis to procure ready-made or easily reheatable meals and snacks from Food Soulis, which specialize in making a handful of dishes designed to produce maximum flavor efficiency and very little waste. These meals are either delivered or picked up at large markets.\n\nSome Soulis have been known to [indenture](gp:bZwQBk42OL) Banu from recently-dissolved Food Soulis to keep everyone fed. Larger Soulis will typically form partnerships with Food Soulis to keep all their members fed, whereas small Soulis will have their members procure food on a rotating basis and contribute to the pantry. It is considered a caring gesture for Banu to pick up a treat for their fellow Souli members and add it to the pantry. [Essosouli](gp:R6v8kxEPBD) are expected to provide their members with especially nice food from time to time, particularly if it has been sourced from distant locations.  \n\nDining out is very popular among Banu. Eating Soulis operate public dining halls where they prepare and serve freshly-made food, generally buffet-style. Members of Soulis that have signed long-term contracts with Eating Soilis are among their most common guests, but most will welcome individual paying customers as well. Just as Banu bring their own plates to their meals at home, they are expected to do this at Eating Soulis. Those who come to an Eating Souli without a plate can often purchase one from a nearby Dishware Souli. Rarely, an Eating Souli will keep emergency plates in stock, but having to use one is seen as uncouth.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9430c921-0b00-471a-b250-d78b2493d0d3"},
{"id":"banu-flotilla","gp":"0qnN5GrMAa","t":"Banu Flotilla","k":"culture","c":["Banu"],"x":"A Banu flotilla is a loosely allied collection of [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4)-owned space stations and ships. Usually, Banu flotillas operate as vibrant marketplaces, acting as centers of trade for travelers. Most Banu planetary systems host one or more flotillas. Generally located in [Banu space](gp:Vgg795z2a3), they are subject only to whatever system of law has been agreed upon by members of the flotilla, if any.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/23dc838f-22a3-493a-b050-d537f363e535"},
{"id":"banu-friendship-museum","gp":"V7gMm55QDA","t":"Banu Friendship Museum","k":"culture","c":["Culture","Banu"],"x":"The Banu Friendship Museum was established in 2838 on a former United Empire of Earth (UEE) Navy base around Davien IV to commemorate Humanity's long relationship with the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). The museum features a variety of exhibits and artifacts on the history of the alliance between the UEE and the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). It oversees millions of visitors per year.","g":["davien iv","davien system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a5ddc2ab-3654-4907-9663-2c2c9d88e622"},
{"id":"banu-indenture","gp":"bZwQBk42OL","t":"Banu Indenture","k":"culture","c":["Banu","Culture"],"x":"Indenture is a [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) practice in which another being is purchased for a limited-term service contract. Most Indentured Banu are children who have been put on the market to be sold to an appropriate [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron), where they will be taken on as an Apprentice and trained in a new skill in exchange for room and board. Upon adulthood, a successful Indentured Apprentice will be granted full membership in their Souli. Adults in the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) may sell themselves into Indenture to pay off a debt, learn a new skill, or for a variety of other reasons. Prisoners can also be sold to Indenture Soulis for a profit.","g":["banu sociopolitics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6a077262-7fc1-4626-88dc-370e700a9bcb"},
{"id":"banu-language","gp":"RPPxJdLBJj","t":"Banu Language","k":"culture","c":["Culture","Banu"],"x":"Banu language refers to a family of languages originating with and spoken by the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). Though all Banu share the same writing system, they speak many dialects, some of which are not mutually intelligible. Xenolinguists believe that this is partially due to their lack of both a central homeworld and a centralized government. The Banu have no formal name for their languages; instead, one who speaks Banu would say they \"speak like Banu-folk\" (*yufu zuBanu*, or *yufu zo uBanu*).","g":["banu protectorate","language"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3c107dd7-4385-4a72-bf31-6d8881a0e7e4"},
{"id":"banu-protectorate","gp":"Vgg795z2a3","t":"Banu Protectorate","k":"place","c":["Government","Banu"],"x":"The Banu Protectorate (BP) is an allied coalition of planet-states and city-states, some based in [Banu flotillas](gp:0qnN5GrMAa), that make up [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4)-controlled territory. A governmental body called the Protectorate or the Protectorate Council, made up of hundreds of individual Banu, maintains connections between Banu systems and manages high-level administrative tasks. [Essosouli](gp:R6v8kxEPBD) from across Banu space can be called to convene in the [Bacchus system](gp:bBzaExgj1o) and join the Protectorate in debating issues that affect the Banu as a whole in an event known as [the Gathering](gp:V7gM7yNAeK)(eTseyæ Yæ). The BP maintains friendly trade relations with most known spacefaring civilizations. \n\n# HISTORY\nBecause Banu do not keep historical records, it is unclear when in their history they formed the Protectorate. The earliest known iteration of the BP was encountered in MXY III.364 (SEY 1924) in the Trise system, upon Banu-Xi'an First Contact. At that time, the Banu had already settled in multiple planetary systems, and were utilizing the Protectorate Council and the Gathering as a method of large-scale management. The BP has continued to operate in the same manner since that time. Given the current consensus among xeno-anthropologists that the Banu people are originally from the ocean world [Bacchus II](gp:Var6oAn18Z), it is speculated that the earliest form of the BP emerged based on alliances between the small island-nations that make up the majority of land on the planet. \n\n# GOVERNMENT\nEach planet-state and city-state within the BP is governed by one or more political and bureaucratic [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) that plan the tasks needed to keep their locales operating smoothly, and then execute them by forming contracts with Soulis that perform said tasks. These include energy production and distribution, water service, sewage processing, road maintenance, garbage collection, and many others. Compensated for their work via a complex system involving bartering combined with monetary payment, these Soulis hold a great deal of power, and are known to withdraw their services if they encounter unfavorable conditions. Conversely, if they gain a reputation for operating in bad faith, they may face retaliation from other Soulis. Although there are some truly independent groups of Banu that operate in their own unique manners, this method of governance is the most common one used in the BP.\n\nSimilar to the Soulis that operate planet-states, the Protectorate Council takes care of the tasks necessary to keep Banu society functional from the top down. These include the distribution of shared currency, the management of inter-civilization trade, the negotiation of treaties, and other ministerial activity. Banu who want a seat on the Protectorate must purchase it directly from their predecessors. In some cases they are handpicked for purchase of the seat, usually from among the non-Protectorate affiliated Essosouli who attend the Gathering. The most successful members of the Protectorate are those who know how to balance the pursuit of their own agenda with the necessity of working with others to achieve a common goal. \n\nThe Gathering is the most important political event in the BP. Generally held on an as-needed basis, it tends to occur two or three times per Standard Earth Year, although sometimes multiple years can pass between meetings. Issues that will affect the entirety of the BP are presented and debated at Gatherings, such as the valuation of their shared currency, the renegotiation of trade agreements, the reassessment of laws and customs, the state of the BP's borders, and others. Grievances between Soulis are also aired and resolved in the interest of preventing armed conflict from breaking out between the planets and city-states.","g":["banu sociopolitics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/13094d69-9c10-4f0a-91f6-3348ff8826e0"},
{"id":"banu-religion","gp":"RXlXGygBPD","t":"Banu Religion","k":"culture","c":["Banu","Culture"],"x":"Banu Religion is made up of a wide variety of beliefs concerning rituals and the cultivation of good luck. Generally, the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) focus less on the soul or the afterlife and more on a feeling that if something exists beyond the physical world that it should be on your side and working in your favor. It is therefore not uncommon for Banu to adopt gods from religions they encounter during the course of their lives. Cassa, the Patron of Luck, and Taernin, the Great Traveler, feature strong followings.","g":["religion"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a2448a9c-42f5-4988-8fae-9fd009bc3eea"},
{"id":"banu-human-first-contact","gp":"VY4Wnv7ZgW","t":"Banu-Human First Contact","k":"history","c":["Exploration","Banu","Politics","Human"],"x":"Humans and [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) first made contact in 2438, when navjumper Vernon Tar encountered a Banu fugitive in the outskirts of the [Davien system](gp:Rz2g71YlkY). After mistakenly opening fire on the Banu vessel, Tar relayed his coordinates to the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO). A delegation party led by General [Neal Socolovich](gp:VJX7vxG2BG) were immediately dispatched to the system to reverse any possible diplomatic fallout and attempt to open communication. Two weeks later, representatives of the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) arrived in Davien and made formal contact with Socolovich. In October of 2438, [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) signed their first [Interstellar Peace and Trade Accord](gp:RzPoJ1aP4z) with an alien civilization.","g":["first contact","vernon tar","davien system","neal socolovich"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f20bf4e3-15a5-41b5-ada8-2115a4997bec"},
{"id":"banu-human-interstellar-peace-treaty","gp":"RzPoJ1aP4z","t":"Banu-Human Interstellar Peace Treaty","k":"faction","c":["Banu","Politics"],"x":"The Banu-Human Interstellar Peace Treaty (the Interstellar Peace and Trade Accord) is the first interspecies treaty in Human history. First negotiated by General [Neal Socolovich](gp:VJX7vxG2BG), It was signed between the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) and the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) in 2438 and began the social and commercial alliance between [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) and Humans that has been enjoyed by both species for over 500 years. Due to the nature of contracts in Banu culture, once per Banu generation, the treaty must be renegotiated with Banu leadership.","g":["interstellar peace and trade accord","treaties","neal socolovich"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0a58fe74-3bc4-4426-a49c-42b9759ed744"},
{"id":"bareton","gp":"0rxPE3LxDg","t":"Bareton","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Bareton is one of very few cities located on [Noble (Ellis V)](gp:V8W545NrKo) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Founded after the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) voted to preserve Noble's environment, it was constructed as a series of enormous platforms connected by transparent walkways. A massive old-growth forest sits in the partial shade underneath Bareton, and can be observed from any of the benches and viewing areas dotted around the city. Most import and export traffic on Noble passes through Bareton, making it a noisy and busy place in spite of its scenic surroundings.","g":["neo taurii","kampos","ellis iv","uee city","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d711e758-520a-4361-8a74-a1960c044aab"},
{"id":"basilisk","gp":"R9BwxzG9KZ","t":"Basilisk","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Basilisk is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) personal and spacecraft armor manufacturer headquartered on Cascom (Castra II). Founded in the first half of the 2500s to research new armor composites, Basilisk received the bulk of its initial funding from the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) until the end of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) in 2792. In the aftermath, their budget was significantly reduced during the governmental reorganization, so they opened their products to the civilian market.","g":["cascom","spacecraft component manufacturer","armor manufacturer","castra ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5964f5c1-d758-4d45-9e28-0e157d0f60fe"},
{"id":"battle-of-centauri","gp":"VlM1yqjoNv","t":"Battle of Centauri","k":"history","c":["Military","History","Human","Tevarin"],"x":"The Battle of Centauri was an armed military engagement between the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) and the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) and was the final battle of the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv). On 24 June 2610 SEY, the Tevarin Warlord [Corath'Thal](gp:RkGxWGQ2Qp) and his forces entered the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5) with the Centauri-Elysium [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) as their goal, around which the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) had placed a blockade. Instead of charging for the jump point, Corath'Thal's fleet diverted for [Yar](gp:R6dd5pyOZ5) and [Saisei](gp:Vy22NQJ1q6), forcing the UEE Navy to break its formation and defend the populace leaving a small contingent of ships behind to protect the jump point. Captain Alexandra Dunlevy of the UEE Navy's 42nd Squadron, believing that this strategy would fail, convinced her commanding officer Admiral Tibault Fraser of the UEES *Countenance* to pretend to retreat under fire from the approaching Tevarin forces. As Corath'Thal's fleet broke formation to enter the jump point, the 42nd Squadron ambushed them and took out their shields, giving the UEEN the opportunity to destroy a majority of the Tevarin ships. While Corath'Thal and his remaining forces did manage to break the line and enter the [Elysium system](gp:RvlQrKZxPO), they lacked the numbers to retake it. Instead, they chose to immolate themselves in the atmosphere of their former homeworld, bringing the Second Tevarin War to an end.","g":["centauri system","battles","second tevarin war"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e8ec601b-9838-408d-a891-148532656bc9"},
{"id":"battle-of-idris-iv","gp":"ReJajXKelk","t":"Battle of Idris IV","k":"history","c":["Military","History","Tevarin","Human"],"x":"The Battle of Idris IV was a major engagement during the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541-2546) between Human forces of the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) and the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X). It took place on 1 October 2544 on and above Idris IV. Before the battle, the UPE had been losing ground, resulting in the planet being overtaken by Tevarin forces. The tactics of a young [Ivar Messer](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) ensured UPE victory at Idris IV and turned the tide of the war. This battle was key in beginning Messer's rise to power. A monument to the battle has been established on Idris IV.","g":["idris iv","battles","first tevarin war","ivar messer i","united planets of earth"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6e3136ed-b8d0-4b10-ad69-bfbc03010973"},
{"id":"battle-of-koren-pass","gp":"01dWmOD45G","t":"Battle of Koren Pass","k":"history","c":["Military","History","Human","Tevarin"],"x":"The Battle of Koren Pass was a military engagement between the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) in 2605. It took place on Crion (Caliban II), when a group of [UEE Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) soldiers traveling in [Nova](gp:01L8gLYXaY) tanks were besieged by a Tevarin strike team. The battle lasted sixteen straight hours, without rest. It ended with a UEE victory when rescue forces arrived and forced a Tevarin retreat.","g":["second tevarin war","battles","crion","caliban ii","nova (tank)","united empire of earth"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/225dd058-eceb-4ff6-ae38-4cd1baf431c2"},
{"id":"battle-of-orion","gp":"RMXyYxqw8K","t":"Battle of Orion","k":"history","c":["Military","History","Human","Vanduul"],"x":"The Battle of Orion was a massed engagement between the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) that began on 16 February 2712 SEY, when thousands of Vanduul accompanied by a [Kingship](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm) poured into [Orion](gp:VlMpwMky6d) from a previously unknown jump point to the system later coded VS-09 \"[Vulture](gp:01Lx6KLKO8).\" The battle marked the first time UEE forces encountered a Kingship. On 18 February, the UEE was forced to cede the Orion system to the invading Vanduul forces. This was the first major defeat for the UEE since the temporary loss of the [Idris system](gp:bZkrMGnLdM) in 2542. It is considered by military historians to be a turning point in the ongoing conflict between the UEE and the Vanduul.","g":["orion system","kingship","battles","vanduul clans","vanduul invasions","united empire of earth"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8de0daa6-fc30-4eed-8e0e-83adc55b1979"},
{"id":"battle-of-vega-ii","gp":"0Gz5mkprmg","t":"Battle of Vega II","k":"history","c":["Military","Human","Vanduul"],"x":"The Battle of Vega II was fought on 5 October 2945 SEY between the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO). It was sparked when a large Vanduul Clan led by a [Kingship](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm) jumped to the Vega system and attacked the planet Aremis (Vega II). After a desperate battle against overwhelming forces, the [UEE Navy's](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) 2nd Fleet commanded by [Admiral Ernst Bishop](gp:ReJaavPB3k) managed to turn the tide with the destruction of the kingship that drove the Vanduul survivors out of the system. The attack elevated concern about the Vanduul threat and led to a military action to reclaim UEE systems lost to the Vanduul. This marked the first time in history that Human forces destroyed a Vanduul Kingship.","g":["aremis","vega ii","ernst bishop","kingship","battles","vanduul clans","united empire of earth","vanduul invasions"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/87be4f8a-7b64-43c5-967e-5c21abdf17af"},
{"id":"behesht-mines","gp":"VpMez1B2qM","t":"Behesht Mines","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Behesht Mines was a mining group that operated from 2237 until 2796. Founded in the early days of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-led space exploration, before the discovery of [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) in 2271, it was one of the first corporations to gain a foothold in the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp). During the time it operated, the company came under fire multiple times for unsafe policies and disregard for environmental protection. Behesht went bankrupt during the [collapse](gp:bE3rKa32P7) of the [Messer regime](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) and sold off or abandoned its holdings. It is best known for causing the fire that still burns on [Nul II](gp:VlM1y7lvWA) in the unclaimed [Nul system](gp:VgEnlpqyJ9).","g":["mining company","nul system","vann","croshaw iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4b1d0068-8ee2-41a5-ba26-75d2b71dcee4"},
{"id":"behring","gp":"0n9vZ4GpQn","t":"Behring Applied Technology","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Military","Human"],"x":"Behring Applied Technology is a weapons consortium based on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). Founded in SEY 2554, Behring is comprised of dozens of smaller research and development firms to build a variety of items, weapons, and vehicles, usually for defense purposes. Their laboratories contributed to the standardization of laser weaponry, along with other innovations in computers, shield generators, missiles, personal weapons, spacecraft weapons, and ordnance. Multiple divisions of Behring are located in the [Kilian](gp:0ODD4mY9aP) system in order to work on classified projects for the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military.","g":["behring","terra","terra iii","weapons manufacturer","spacecraft component manufacturer","munitions manufacturer","macarthur","kilian v","weapon component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/eea8f89f-86c0-4402-8ab8-cec845fbcb19"},
{"id":"bengal","gp":"RwZBLqLQdp","t":"Bengal","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The Bengal is a fleet carrier spacecraft developed in SEY 2871 by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) for the [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). Bengal-class carriers carry a full complement of fighters, bombers and support ships and typically form the nucleus of a UEEN battle fleet or task force group. They are roughly 1000 meters long and can support several thousand crew on-board.","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","carrier","capital ship","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5bf35241-66a1-4bb0-a371-498f803c11c6"},
{"id":"bethor","gp":"RMXyYx3lWx","t":"Bethor","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Tevarin"],"x":"Bethor is a research station built in 2536 for privately-funded scientists studying the atmosphere of [Taranis III](gp:VYLqxAqQvo). After their research was completed, the station was abandoned, and squatters began to seek shelter there. The original station's layout has been expanded piece by piece over the centuries by the various settlers who have made their home there. Currently, it is home to a mixed population of [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) and [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2).","g":["taranis iii","research station","sealed settlement","tevarin settlement","independent settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/827c5634-1906-4d3a-8e49-aa973bfabfcc"},
{"id":"bevic-group","gp":"RAXX71OBdB","t":"Bevic Group","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"The Bevic Group is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) food and drink conglomerate headquartered in [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Founded in SEY 2078 by siblings Bartholomew and Vevrai Bevic after receiving a substantial inheritance from their grandparents, the first product it sold was the canned beverage Get Up Coffee, which became very popular among college students. The company's first acquisition was the Sunshine and Daisies Milk Company in 2093, which allowed Bevic to control their own dairy supply. After their merger with instant dinner manufacturer Page-Callier in 2122, the company expanded its scope to include food as well as beverages. Since then, it was purchased and merged with multiple companies, and has expanded to become one of the largest food and drink manufacturers in the UEE.","g":["beverage company","food company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cc9da3ba-fd1a-481c-8d4a-9e23d3988614"},
{"id":"big-bennys","gp":"V3GPzWZXNA","t":"Big Benny's","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Food and Beverages","Human"],"x":"Big Benny's is a food brand owned by Terra Mills that produces kacho, a heavily spiced combination of noodles and broth. Founder Benicio Lewis Jr. first began selling kacho inspired by his father's recipe from a food stall on [Lo (Corel III)](gp:VarAoYEQYd) after encouragement from friends. He named the stall Big Benny's after his father. His cheap and satisfying fare found early popularity, and soon Lewis opened franchises. When [Terra Mills](gp:0Gz5Z39z1a) offered to purchase the brand, he accepted, leading to its spread across the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Some of the bestselling Big Benny's flavors include Fhaal Fire, Ginger Give-Spice, and Lo Classic.","g":["fast food","food company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a54a3e55-6bd8-44ff-8e35-a483e1993f5d"},
{"id":"bioticorp-limited","gp":"RWoe2K4X8a","t":"BiotiCorp Limited","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"BiotiCorp Limited is a medical research and technology company that manufactures diagnostic and surgical systems, medical scanners, and surgical robots. Best known for the Calliope reconstruction device, the company was founded in SEY 2915 by Dr. Diyo Nikolas and Dr. Ted Santos after their work identified a connection between the genetic gravitational compression that occurs during quantum travel and increased fatality rates for transporting patients while in surgery. Their first product was a software suite for surgical robots designed to combat this problem.","g":["medical research","medical goods manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4c7bb7a1-3b09-4b93-8e6a-d0c66a5c5ee1"},
{"id":"blackwater","gp":"R4ZGmKnA9O","t":"Blackwater","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"The Blackwater district was a geographic region on Crion (Caliban II). It became increasingly settled in the 2860s as the population of Crion grew. During this time, Blackwater was home to a burgeoning grey market that connected traders with the workers and militia working on the project. The [United Empire of Earth Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) 89th Logistic Support Squadron, or [Squadron 89 (the Lost Squad)](gp:0Gz5BNmPqo) operated from makeshift airstrips in the Blackwater district during the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) in 2884.","g":["crion","caliban ii","squadron 89","fall of caliban","vanduul territory","lost squad"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8d002fd9-052b-4557-bce9-c4eadbf4fd77"},
{"id":"blade","gp":"RegdeBENkw","t":"Blade","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Vanduul"],"x":"The \"Blade\" is the official [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) designation for a standard light fighter operated by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO). In many observed raids, the Blade forms a significant portion of the Vanduul order of battle. They are commonly encountered serving as advance scouts, escort fighters for bombers, and as interceptors. Blade units acting as independent skirmisher squadrons have also been engaged. [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer [Esperia](gp:0OaBKL7wlv) has partnered with the UEEN to produce replica Blade spacecraft for aggressor training operations and for sale on the civilian market.","g":["light fighter","vanduul blade","vanduul spacecraft","fighter","esperia"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ad63a2ff-6548-443a-9135-dc709e5fd107"},
{"id":"bloom-pyro-iii","gp":"0KxjqgQdNY","t":"Bloom (Pyro III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Bloom (Pyro III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Cold but naturally habitable, it became the epicenter of mining endeavors in Pyro. [Pyrotechnic Amalgamated](gp:VpM4anYBn1) and other corporations constructed multiple staging sites, employees barracks, and processing centers that were in use until the cost of their maintenance could no longer be offset by mining profits. Abandoned when the last active corporations in Pyro ceased operations there in the late 26th century, they were claimed by squatters, outlaws, and former miners who lacked the means to return to the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE).","g":["bloom","pyro iii","habitable","habitable planet","unclaimed planet","pyro system"]},
{"id":"blue-bilva","gp":"VlMMykdrNM","t":"Blue Bilva","k":"life","c":["Food and Beverages","Plants"],"x":"The blue bilva (or blubee) is a rich, sugary, and aromatic tree fruit that originated on Reisse (Rhetor III). Fibrous in its natural state, the vivid turquoise flesh of the fruit clings to a large black stone that is so hard it must be cracked through mechanical means. Some artisans on Reisse use powered tools to carve the stone into intricate sculptures that they sell to new students for good luck. Blue bilva forms the base of the locally popular brandy [B3](gp:R4jjEaMeGw).","g":["blubee","fruit","trees","reisse","rhetor iii","food"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6107fd72-384d-4771-8587-35b2dd3b6a93"},
{"id":"blue-triangle-inc","gp":"VgEB2ermrZ","t":"Blue Triangle Inc","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Blue Triangle Inc is a manufacturer of computers, cryptokeys, radars, and analytic systems. Former hackers Jade Sui-Sellars and Pradiana4 founded the company after they were acquitted of exploiting a security vulnerability in the [Central Core Bank](gp:RvlaGZkMx8) (CCB). They were arrested by the Advocacy after they brought the vulnerability to the bank's attention by sending them a demonstration of how it could be used to siphon funds from high-balance accounts. Once cleared of all charges, they were awarded an undisclosed sum from the CCB, which they used to found the company. Blue Triangle is known for hiring engineers and programmers who began their careers as black hat hackers.","g":["computer manufacturer","electronic consumer goods manufacturer","spacecraft component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2d638807-ce9c-4404-9ab8-767fc75b9273"},
{"id":"bombora-ellis-x","gp":"01L5KopKpr","t":"Bombora (Ellis X)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Bombora (Ellis X) is a gas giant with a stormy atmosphere in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Hydrogen and helium are abundant on Bombora, but due to its turbulent winds, harvesting resources from it is a challenging affair. It was nicknamed bombora after a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) term for a dangerous stretch of water.","g":["bombora","ellis x","ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e646257b-d1b0-4136-9f23-917a6d6fb355"},
{"id":"borea-magnus-ii","gp":"R9vGaQPXJN","t":"Borea (Magnus II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Locations"],"x":"Borea is the second planet from the sun in the [Magnus system](gp:RWolrNa1Ge), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). [Terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) began on the planet shortly after the system was discovered in 2499. Until 2631, it was the center of shipbuilding operations for the [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), and enjoyed a thriving economy. Newcastle, the capital, was renowned for the quality of ship components produced by its artisans and businesses. However, when the shipbuilding industry shuttered after the Navy's move to Kilian, the planet's fortunes sharply degraded. Many buildings were abandoned as the population sought jobs on other worlds. In recent decades, commercial spacecraft industries such as [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed) have purchased the old warehouses and shipyards in Odyssa that were abandoned by the UEEN, bringing much-needed jobs with them. For the first time since the mid-27th century, its population is rising.","g":["borea","magnus ii","magnus system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bc9f4266-31b6-4373-86ee-cb4d96e23686"},
{"id":"boreal-stalker","gp":"Rz22pdkZaN","t":"Boreal Stalker","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"The boreal stalker is an apex predator found on [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1) and created by the company [microTech](gp:bE3rBB4j7J) to help round out their planet's ecosystem. After the error in the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) process that led to a climate far colder than had been intended, many of the plants and animals the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government used to stock the planet died. After purchasing the planet from the UEE, microTech opted to artificially engineer plants and animals to fill empty ecological niches, including the boreal stalker.","g":["microtech (planet)","stanton iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4080c327-5ad9-4785-824b-d97f6f5a8bb6"},
{"id":"boro","gp":"Rxn2Noljlz","t":"Boro","k":"place","c":["Settlements"],"x":"Boro was a city on [Crion (Caliban II)](gp:bEzvPwYZ96), [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). The capital of Crion, it was the home of the main chambers of the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) and was the main population center of the planet. Particularly popular among long-haul traders and explorers, it was described in SEY 2599 by travel writer Shasta Wagner as having \"a cosmopolitan appearance, but a strong frontier spirit.\" Political activism in Boro increased alongside [Vanduul raids](gp:Rw1gdnOKBp) in the decades leading up to the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE), as residents believed the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) government was intentionally withholding much-needed military aid. Boro was destroyed when the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) finally invaded en masse in 2884.","g":["crion","caliban ii","abandoned city","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e75b1a1b-1988-4699-a9b2-3aabde722ef9"},
{"id":"branaugh-belt-alpha","gp":"bBzKmQ2r3N","t":"Branaugh Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Branaugh belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the Branaugh system. Residents of the system operate various independent mines on the asteroids to keep their settlements supplied with goods to trade. In addition to the mines, some [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) who prefer to live in isolation outside of the community on [Branaugh II](gp:RL6524Kx6L) reside on the larger asteroids. Each year, several spacecraft are reported missing while traveling the belt. Although the ships' disappearances have never been directly linked to the asteroid inhabitants, locals use caution while flying in the area.","g":["asteroid belt","branaugh system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a0ab21ec-61f0-49ad-83c0-d34c89a48c68"},
{"id":"branaugh-i","gp":"RX3jG2lzdK","t":"Branaugh I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Branaugh I is a terrestrial planet in the [Branaugh system](gp:VJX9mlar4n). Mostly covered in lava rock from ancient volcanic eruptions, the planet has a black surface interspersed with cracks of gray and brown. Because of its dark color, it reflects very little light and is difficult to see with the naked eye unless it is viewed in transit across its sun. It completes its orbit around Branaugh in around 22 Standard Earth Days.","g":["branaugh system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d01102b0-dd1c-4a9e-86db-e09592938e2e"},
{"id":"branaugh-ii","gp":"RL6524Kx6L","t":"Branaugh II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Branaugh II is the second planet from the sun of the [Branaugh system](gp:VJX9mlar4n). Uncommonly among terrestrial worlds of its size, it has a wide set of rings that are visible from its surface. Surveyors initially thought the beautiful rings might attract people to Branaugh II, but upon further inspection, concluded that the stormy planet was not a good candidate for [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). In the early 2900s, a small group of [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) who no longer wished to live in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) repurposed the outposts and structures that the surveyors left behind as dwellings. As more settlers arrived, the settlement expanded into a town. Today, Branaugh II is home to a large community of Tevarin in spite of the planet's unfriendly atmosphere.","g":["branaugh system","habitable planet","habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c8ef5da4-3384-4652-8830-8b4844acace1"},
{"id":"branaugh-iii","gp":"bo1Lk62ppZ","t":"Branaugh III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Branaugh III is a gas giant in the [Branaugh system](gp:VJX9mlar4n). Due to the presence of ammonia crystals, it is pale yellow in color with bands of light-yellow green and grayish-blue. Violent storms erupt on Branaugh III when water vapor trapped in the upper atmosphere undergoes cooling, then rapidly breaks through the layers of hydrogen and helium that comprise most of the planet's atmosphere. In 2911, the largest storm ever recorded on Branaugh III encircled the entire planet.","g":["branaugh system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ac8d8132-706d-495d-ba39-6751a75d7c9b"},
{"id":"branaugh-system","gp":"VJX9mlar4n","t":"Branaugh System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Branaugh system is an [unclaimed](gp:VgExMejDPx) planetary system that consists of a K-type main sequence star, two terrestrial planets, one gas giant, and an asteroid belt. Although it was officially discovered by mining surveyor [Desmond Fell](gp:RX3dlQ5KON) in SEY 2877, he was not the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to visit the system. During Fell's initial surveys, he located the crashed ship and the body of explorer [Theresa Branaugh](gp:VpMeGzBPyz), who had gone missing four years prior. The UEE ultimately chose not to claim the system after the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) Subcommittee on Expansion delivered an analysis that showed that the potential resources gleaned from the system would barely offset the cost of development. Since then, an enclave of [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) expatriates has developed on [Branaugh II](gp:RL6524Kx6L), despite its unfriendly atmosphere.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dfc3471e-55c2-41f2-a88d-058564d66d02"},
{"id":"bremen-i","gp":"0jGqXn9peW","t":"Bremen I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Bremen I is the first planet from the sun of the [Bremen system](gp:02kd45eyxe), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A protoplanet, it has a differentiated interior, but somewhat misshapen surface. A superstition originating on [Rytif (Bremen II)](gp:R5pA7q691W) credits Bremen I with granting pilots good luck when they tip the wings of their spacecraft towards the planet.","g":["bremen system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/42ef5039-2f52-4d8d-be0f-1a24ba07128d"},
{"id":"bremen-iii","gp":"0rxoJ314k9","t":"Bremen III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Bremen III is the third planet from the sun of the [Bremen system](gp:02kd45eyxe), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A coreless planet, its undifferentiated interior was once rich in natural resources. Extensive mining activity since its discovery in 2441 has depleted Bremen III of nearly all its large valuable mineral deposits. Many smaller veins remain, but all the major mining companies previously located on Bremen III pulled out when the price of continuing their operations outweighed potential profits.","g":["bremen system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3970c866-abf9-4391-9bdf-f12cfb8ef99a"},
{"id":"bremen-iv","gp":"Rz2KO3x8pA","t":"Bremen IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Bremen is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Bremen system](gp:02kd45eyxe), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). An ice giant, it is largely made up of hydrogen; however, violent weather conditions on the planet create inhospitable conditions for harvesting gas. The people of [Rytif (Bremen II)](gp:R5pA7q691W) consider Bremen IV to be the guardian of the system, thanks to an incident in 2591 when a dangerously large comet on a trajectory towards Rytif instead was caught in Bremen IV's gravity, saving Rytif from a potentially deadly impact.","g":["bremen system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6075ae2c-db57-4868-984e-465a592c980d"},
{"id":"bremen-system","gp":"02kd45eyxe","t":"Bremen System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Bremen system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), consisting of a K-type main sequence star, one protoplanet, two terrestrial planets, and one ice giant. Discovered by explorer Bao Yun in SEY 2441 during the [Human Colonial Expansion Era (2380 - 2530)](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm), the system saw slow development until the [Second Tevarin War (2603 - 2610)](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv). The demand for military rations caused a population boom as much of [Rytif (Bremen II)](gp:R5pA7q691W) was turned into a center of food production. After the war, immigration to the system sharply fell, and the population eventually returned to its pre-war level. Bremen came to prominence again in 2792, when it was revealed that [anti-Messer revolutionaries](gp:bE3rKa32P7) had been using the system as a base of operations.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6d5a7b8b-9cd7-4333-b068-a2df36e04271"},
{"id":"bruder-chronos-i","gp":"V3G5LAPkLm","t":"Bruder (Chronos I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Bruder is the first planet from the sun in the [Chronos system](gp:RvlQZKy95l), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A mesoplanet, it orbits close enough to the system's sun that landing on the surface without adequate thermal shielding is dangerous. While long-distance scans indicate that valuable resources exist in Bruder's crust, the temperature is too high to justify long-term mining operations.","g":["bruder","chronos i","chronos system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1afc1363-d21a-41cd-9823-3969cb3b2fcb"},
{"id":"buccaneer","gp":"VyvYXd1X7a","t":"Buccaneer","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Buccaneer is a civilian medium fighter sold by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). It was initially designed as an affordable option for frontier militia squadrons conscious of limited repair and maintenance opportunities. The Buccaneer is offered alongside Drake's [Cutlass](gp:R6v8krK71n)/[Caterpillar](gp:VY4WmNG9v6) system and has become a popular design among explorers and pirates.","g":["drake interplanetary","interdiction","human spacecraft","fighter","medium fighter"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/26cd1834-e5bf-4d87-9b05-dba53d8e6afd"},
{"id":"buloi-sataball-arena","gp":"V3GEAj34wa","t":"Buloi Sataball Arena","k":"place","c":["Locations"],"x":"The Buloi Sataball Arena is a space station and staball stadium located in the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Founded by the Buloi Sataball Souli, it hosts hundreds of games each year. A crystal-clear hull on one side of the station shows spectacular views of [Yulin II's](gp:bo1yMW5Z5A) prismatic atmosphere during games, creating the illusion of an open-air building in the depths of space.","g":["sataball","space station","banu space station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/063c08b9-ea52-4946-8027-b66c259f0628"},
{"id":"buloi-satabo","gp":"0n1ypnOxO7","t":"Buloi Satabo","k":"people","c":["People","Banu"],"x":"Buloi Satabo is the [Essosouli](gp:R6v8kxEPBD) of the Buloi Sataball [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron) and its [namesake arena](gp:V3GEAj34wa), located in the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). They re-founded the Souli in the late 2920s after the sudden death of the previous Essosouli and immediately contracted with a Construction Soili to create the arena. A huge fan of sataball, Buloi attended every game held at their stadium until their streak was broken 2941, when an influx of shoddily-made counterfeit tickets forced the Essosouli to temporarily devote their time to rooting out the tickets' source.","g":["buloi sataball arena","banu people","essosouli"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9984c44d-4367-4b16-a514-d6244ceb214a"},
{"id":"buoy","gp":"VY4Wn9LNXD","t":"Buoy","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A buoy is an object positioned at a stationary point in space. Buoys are most frequently used to mark specific points of interest in space either to warn spacecraft of a particular danger, like an asteroid field, or to support navigation towards difficult-to-detect spaces like shipping lanes or jump points. Buoys are also used to transmit communications and to provide early warning to military and police organizations.","g":["navigation"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a55852b8-bbe2-4fcc-bf0e-b3d3680d152e"},
{"id":"c1-spirit","gp":"01L2MB819w","t":"C1 Spirit","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The C1 Spirit is a medium hauler manufactured by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) that supports a crew of up to two people. Designed for mid-range cargo delivery and courier jobs, the Spirit comes with a 64 SCU hold and an industrial-grade tractor rig. In addition, it has four forward-facing guns and two missile racks, providing its pilot with protection during trips through dangerous areas of space.","g":["freight","medium freight","crusader industries","human spacecraft","spirit series"]},
{"id":"c2-hercules","gp":"0QxYEKvorl","t":"C2 Hercules","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The C2 Hercules Starlifter is an armed transport spacecraft developed by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N). Built with a military-grade frame, the C2 Hercules includes turrets and ballistic canons, as well as a large shielding system. Its hold can be transformed into a dedicated cargo space large enough to store other spacecraft and ground vehicles. Private organizations such as touring or entertainment companies utilize the C2 Hercules as passenger transports.","g":["hercules series","crusader industries","passenger transport","transport gunship","transport","human spacecraft","starlifter series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8b1696a4-763a-4b3f-aeb3-076f5904967a"},
{"id":"c8-pisces","gp":"RkG2n2J57L","t":"C8 Pisces","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The C8 Pisces is a scouting spacecraft manufactured by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) as a landing craft for the [Carrack](gp:R4ZGyLQaBl). It is not available for standalone purchase. While it can be utilized as a reconnaissance, exploration, or landing ship by a single pilot, it is capable of transporting two additional passengers. The cargo hold can be used to transport cargo and supplies from the surface of a planet to a Carrack in orbit. An expedition version of the ship, the C8X, is equipped with additional firepower and can be purchased as a standalone.","g":["carrack","human spacecraft","pathfinder"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/36e40443-82b5-4981-b9b1-3ca49031988a"},
{"id":"caldera","gp":"VY4Wn9rgae","t":"Caldera","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Caldera is a personal armor company located in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that sells high-tech spacesuits and exploration gear designed to withstand harsh environmental conditions. Most of their products are built with internal communications devices and scanners for use in remote or unexplored locations. While their suits are not combat armor, they do come with defensive capabilities.","g":["armor manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bd87649f-75c8-4dc1-8958-408d0eacea0e"},
{"id":"caliban-2a","gp":"Rxnyko3XLQ","t":"Caliban 2a","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Caliban 2a is the sole moon of [Crion (Caliban II)](gp:bEzvPwYZ96), located in the [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m) in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Its yellowish surface is covered in unusual craters which were the subject of a long-term study to determine their origin before the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) overtook the Caliban system [in SEY 2884](gp:0Gz5DNryvE).","g":["caliban system","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","vanduul moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/10f14667-f07f-4dd1-ab0f-9a974cdfc952"},
{"id":"caliban-3a","gp":"0qayAQX5OA","t":"Caliban 3a","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Caliban 3a is the first moon from the surface of [Caliban III](gp:VgEljZZ8PN), Caliban system, located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Large and lumpy in appearance, astronomers speculate that it is the leftover nucleus of a planet that failed to coalesce into a planet. The [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) have been observed extracting water ice from its deepest craters.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","vanduul moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b52c9309-fab6-409a-91e2-2537d1d87401"},
{"id":"caliban-3b","gp":"0rxymg8qPq","t":"Caliban 3b","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Caliban 3b is the second moon from the surface of [Caliban III](gp:VgEljZZ8PN), [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Much smaller than its companion moon, it is porous, ovoid, and low in mass. It was most likely captured from the nearby Caliban belt alpha sometime before it was discovered by Humans in SEY 2341.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","vanduul moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/26150c94-cc62-42df-9e13-2b8bbf23d0eb"},
{"id":"caliban-4a","gp":"RL63AA7lJ3","t":"Caliban 4a","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Caliban 4a is the first moon from the gas giant [Caliban IV](gp:0GxavvKo2P), [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Iron-rich and very dense, studies conducted on the moon have shown that it is likely older than any other celestial body in the system. Astronomers hypothesize that it is the former core of a rogue planet that was captured by the gravity of Caliban IV on its way through the system.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","vanduul moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0e7ce8f9-0948-4a64-b864-53484521c51a"},
{"id":"caliban-4b","gp":"RWo8WW6OMw","t":"Caliban 4b","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Caliban 4b is the second moon from the gas giant [Caliban IV](gp:0GxavvKo2P), [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Enveloped by a weak magnetosphere, it is encircled by a pair of auroral belts that generate shimmering red light shows when the moon's magnetic field interacts with that of Caliban IV.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","vanduul moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8f5c96c6-6ccc-4a8d-b2bc-635bdba42e76"},
{"id":"caliban-4c","gp":"VgEljjNNyn","t":"Caliban 4c","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Caliban 4c is the third moon from the gas giant [Caliban IV](gp:0GxavvKo2P), [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Small and dark, its reddish-brown surface is dusted with iron oxide. The abundant presence of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere causes any iron in the dust to oxidize and appear rusty. Bright white streaks of silicate crisscross the crust.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","vanduul moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d04e4eed-e368-4335-a91a-6838742c23a0"},
{"id":"caliban-4d","gp":"VgEljjBLow","t":"Caliban 4d","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Caliban 4d is the fourth moon from the gas giant [Caliban IV](gp:0GxavvKo2P), [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Composed of silicate rock, it has a water-ice crust with a very smooth surface that completely covers a moon-wide ocean of liquid salt water. The ice is laced with dark cracks thousands of kilometers long.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","vanduul moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6cf88dbc-69cd-49be-8f6d-32ba69b15beb"},
{"id":"caliban-4e","gp":"RX3MQQoxOZ","t":"Caliban 4e","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Caliban 4e is the fifth moon from the gas giant [Caliban IV](gp:0GxavvKo2P), [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Frigidly cold, it has a surface that is coated in mostly frozen nitrogen mixed with some water ice. It is geologically active, and is covered with cryovolcanoes that spew plumes of nitrogen ice.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","vanduul moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8a20802a-20fc-4409-8a6e-c432a36c315d"},
{"id":"caliban-4f","gp":"VlMyvv7Yn7","t":"Caliban 4f","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Caliban 4f is the sixth moon from the gas giant [Caliban IV](gp:0GxavvKo2P), [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Rich in carbon, it is dark in color, and reflects very little light from its distant sun. Copious tholins caused by millenia of ultraviolet radiation cast a reddish tint on its otherwise black surface.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","vanduul moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/962276b2-a3a0-48e2-96d4-1ad0ea3e2b7d"},
{"id":"caliban-belt-alpha","gp":"V7dE88dGXK","t":"Caliban Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Caliban belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). When the Caliban system was possessed by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE), the belt was a hub for miners, haulers, and salvagers, and was dotted with rest stops in service of travelers. When the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) seized control of the system [in SEY 2884](gp:0Gz5DNryvE), evacuees abandoned all equipment and space stations. It is believed that the resources left behind have been harvested by the Vanduul.","g":["asteroid belt","caliban system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c78878ca-3618-49a2-8eb7-d84a2519d12c"},
{"id":"caliban-i","gp":"VlMyvGyPGA","t":"Caliban I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Caliban I is the first planet from the sun of the [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m) in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). A small coreless world, it was rich in valuable resources that [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) extracted to aid in the development of [Crion (Caliban II)](gp:bEzvPwYZ96). Now completely strip-mined, it is ignored by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) who [overtook](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) the Caliban system in SEY 2884.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3712795e-adea-4d9f-833e-618f1f019bc6"},
{"id":"caliban-iii","gp":"VgEljZZ8PN","t":"Caliban III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Caliban III is the third planet from the sun of the [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m) in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). When it was first discovered in SEY 2341, it was deemed a non-viable [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) candidate and left alone in favor of settling [Crion (Caliban II)](gp:bEzvPwYZ96). However, by the mid-29th century, there were enough advances in technology that development was approved and terraforming started. All activity came to a halt in 2884, when the Vanduul [invaded](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) the Caliban system and wrested it from the possession of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE). Derelict machinery damaged in the fighting and abandoned in orbit routinely plummets to its surface.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/62932061-7b46-41de-bc49-9a279bd34f95"},
{"id":"caliban-iv","gp":"0GxavvKo2P","t":"Caliban IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Caliban IV is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m) in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). A gas giant, its atmosphere is banded with voluminous clouds of silicate and iron that give the world its gray-green color. It is orbited by the wreckage of automated hydrogen harvesting platforms that were abandoned when [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) fled the system during the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) invasion in SEY 2884.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b775df5c-bbeb-48c9-9596-c5ed1f0c4dec"},
{"id":"caliban-system","gp":"0jGyPQ1r5m","t":"Caliban System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Caliban system is a planetary system in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), formerly of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE). Officially purchased from hauler Ashley Ghan in SEY 2341, a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-made shelter was found on [Caliban 4f](gp:VlMyvv7Yn7) during the surveying process, indicating that someone had discovered the system before Ghan and had chosen to keep it a secret. The system was rapidly developed, and enjoyed steady growth until 2739, when [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) raiding parties first appeared in the system. Years of struggle against the invading forces [culminated in 2884](gp:0Gz5DNryvE), when an enormous Vanduul [Clan](gp:R9vzjxmEBx) invaded the system without warning. After two days of fighting and an evacuation effort led by the [89th Logistic Support Squadron](gp:0Gz5BNmPqo), the UEE was forced to cede the system to the Vanduul.","g":["vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/aac93b49-9fe0-46e3-8a81-f67c88e3eb35"},
{"id":"caliban-v","gp":"0rxymm6YZ3","t":"Caliban V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Caliban V is the outermost planet from the sun of the [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m) in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). A protoplanet with a craggy surface, it was considered of little value to the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) and was therefore largely ignored. After the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) took the system [in SEY 2884](gp:0Gz5DNryvE), they began strip-mining operations, leading to speculation that it must hold resources the Vanduul consider desirable.","g":["caliban system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9e5bab43-381f-40b4-9b3b-39c39ba4e590"},
{"id":"calliope-stanton-4a","gp":"Rz2PaqwwPM","t":"Calliope (Stanton 4a)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Calliope is a cold, windy moon of [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1), named after the mythical muse of epic poetry and eloquence from ancient Earth (Sol III). Due to the high winds and extreme cold, weather suits worn by visitors to the planet are known to fail, particularly on the moon's dark side. [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA) operates a number of processing facilities on Calliope.","g":["calliope","stanton 4a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","microtech moon","stanton iv moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/08c4ef34-a0d0-49c4-931a-93dc839fef9e"},
{"id":"callisto-sol-5d","gp":"bEzYGPE4L8","t":"Callisto (Sol 5d)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Callisto (Sol 5d) is a moon of [Jupiter (Sol V)](gp:Vy2OMo22wz), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Of all the celestial bodies in the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), Callisto's surface is the most heavily cratered. Because it has never been geologically active, it is home to multiple sealed settlements and a handful of specialized resorts that cater to people who suffer from seismophobia.","g":["callisto","sol 5d","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8132812e-b1fe-49bb-890c-aced3721926d"},
{"id":"candle-road","gp":"0KnAmEqQQ2","t":"Candle Road","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Candle Road was a Human settlement on Crion (Caliban II) and was the de facto headquarters of the [Crion Security Legion](gp:VY4WM8e2N1). Initially established in 2510 as a military airfield, it did not rise to prominence until the mid-29th century when it became a major support facility for efforts to [terraform](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) Caliban III. Candle Road was destroyed by aerial bombardment in 2884 during the final phase of the [Vanduul invasion of the Caliban System](gp:0Gz5DNryvE).","g":["crion security legion","lost squad","vanduul territory","fall of caliban","caliban ii","crion"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/df24bdc5-5a80-4ed2-82cb-e96d429b6616"},
{"id":"cano-belt-alpha","gp":"RkGvWnWJ64","t":"Cano Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Cano belt alpha is an asteroid belt that orbits the sun in the [Cano system](gp:Rxn9DYKdnd) between [Cano III](gp:RL6KBQ9Kzj) and [Pox (Cano IV)](gp:RWoy1A9eWm), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). While it was mined extensively in the past, activity has slowed since the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) was applied to [Carteyna (Cano II)](gp:RX34BrgYND) in the late 2800s.","g":["asteroid belt","cano system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/df427652-845e-46cd-8a0f-fc3534ada389"},
{"id":"cano-i","gp":"Rz2KO3aJWk","t":"Cano I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Cano I is a mesoplanet in the [Cano system](gp:Rxn9DYKdnd), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is tidally locked to its sun. Abundant lava flows have caused crystalline structures to form along the solar terminator. While the formations cannot be easily visited due to Cano I's proximity to its star, they are large enough to be seen from space.","g":["cano system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a558b0b6-8a77-46c0-9fdc-e55290b65f22"},
{"id":"cano-iii","gp":"RL6KBQ9Kzj","t":"Cano III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Cano III is a smog planet in the [Cano system](gp:Rxn9DYKdnd), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). While it is located within the system's green band, its dense, thick atmosphere has made [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) impossible. [Geohacking](gp:R9Bwj1BZAN) corporations that once operated on [Carteyna (Cano II)](gp:RX34BrgYND) have been granted permission from the UEE government to use Cano III as a testbed for new technology.","g":["cano system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e63ae1ea-7bbc-453c-9a6c-c8d7b12ececb"},
{"id":"cano-system","gp":"Rxn9DYKdnd","t":"Cano System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Cano system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), discovered in SEY 2463 by Tabatha Caster and Jamel Normond during [Project Far Star](gp:0qnNAD6YKa). It consists of a G-type main sequence star, a mesoplanet, two terrestrial planets, an asteroid belt, and a gas giant. Though none of the planets in the system have been successfully [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), [Carteyna (Cano II)](gp:RX34BrgYND) supports a small population of [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) in sealed arcologies under the northern ice cap.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/673b9337-94f5-474b-b1c7-1f267ca53a32"},
{"id":"carl-dyson","gp":"R5p2mqLvXN","t":"Carl Dyson","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Carl Dyson (SEY 2593 - SEY 2701) was a gunner and Lieutenant in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) and musician best known for discovering the [Kai'pua](gp:V3GBmlQoar)-[Horus](gp:bo1JGZpvwZ) jump point alongside fellow starman [Ahmad Harar](gp:VYLznx8r3e). In SEY 2617, he and his pilot Lieutenant Harar were patrolling the Horus system when they detected a gravitational anomaly. After a long period of analysis, their ship's computer determined that this was likely to be a jump point. Dyson wanted to alert his commanding officer, but Harar convinced him to navigate the jump point before doing so, thus ensuring that they would earn a place in history. On the other side, however, their ship was immediately disabled and the two starmen were captured by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military. They spent three days being interrogated, and eventually managed to convince their captors that the UEE Navy knew nothing about the jump point. Dyson and Harar were returned to the Horus system with a message: any UEE vessels spotted in Kai'pua in the future would be shot on sight. Dyson was reprimanded for failing to report his discovery to his superiors. Instead of accepting a demotion, Dyson requested and was granted an honorable discharge. He then emigrated to Earth (Sol III) to pursue his lifelong dream of becoming a musician. His most notable album, \"Twilight on the Firing Line,\" earned two [Elira Awards](gp:bmNrm67NY9).","g":["human people","kai'pua system"]},
{"id":"carrack","gp":"R4ZGyLQaBl","t":"Carrack","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Carrack is a long-term exploration spacecraft developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Navy (UEEN). Once only used by the military, it is now sold on the civilian market. The Carrack is capable of making planetfall in hostile environments and deploying smaller exploration vehicles in support of its mission. It is equipped with specialized sensors for pathfinding, medical and repair facilities, and reinforced fuel tanks for long-duration flight. Each Carrack comes with a [C8 Pisces](gp:RkG2n2J57L) snub scout ship.","g":["expedition","anvil aerospace","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fd956c67-84d6-47b8-9fd3-4e3145a4c3ec"},
{"id":"carteyna-cano-ii","gp":"RX34BrgYND","t":"Carteyna (Cano II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Carteyna is the second planet from the star of the [Cano system](gp:Rxn9DYKdnd), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). An ocean world discovered in 2463, Carteyna has resisted [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) attempts. Its residents inhabit sealed arcologies surrounded by geothermal waters underneath the planet's northern ice cap. The [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) was invoked to prevent further terraforming attempts when microscopic organisms exhibiting signs of intelligence were discovered in the ocean. While immigration is prohibited, the descendants of Carteyna's original settlers have been allowed to stay in Carteyna City.","g":["carteyna","cano ii","cano system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/575fa51b-d973-47c4-b7a6-ec5453eab1ef"},
{"id":"carteyna-city","gp":"0GxEKdlzBE","t":"Carteyna City","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Carteyna City is the only city on [Carteyna (Cano II)](gp:RX34BrgYND), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Located in an underwater arcology below the planet's polar ice cap, Carteyna City is a wonder of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) engineering, and is able to draw energy from geothermal vents located fathoms down. Many of its inhabitants are either active researchers engaged in observing the nascent sentient life developing among Carteyna's microorganisms, or are descendants of the planet's original settlers.","g":["carteyna","cano ii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/45d5c9fa-ad18-4eb0-8dd5-0c93dda58324"},
{"id":"cascom-castra-ii","gp":"0dXKkL9a9o","t":"Cascom (Castra II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Cascom is an inhabited planet in the [Castra system](gp:R4jxkAd8El), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It was originally [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) as a military-only planet in the late 2500s, and operated as a [UEE naval](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) base until 2789, when it was opened for civilian settlement. Cascom remained lightly populated until the 2830s, when a successful promotional campaign offering incentives attracted a new influx of immigrants. Its capital, [Sherman](gp:R4jxLALWgJ), is home to many retirees brought there by the city's views and low-priced real estate.","g":["cascom","castra ii","habitable","habitable planet","human planet","castra system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/97d56e19-1b0e-4fe5-8d6e-d486d9af94ee"},
{"id":"cassa-the-patron-of-luck","gp":"02kg3POv8e","t":"Cassa, the Patron of Luck","k":"culture","c":["Culture","Banu"],"x":"Cassa, the Patron of Luck, is the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) god of fortune, prosperity, money, and merchants. Although its origins are unknown, it is one of the most common deities in the [Banu pantheon](gp:RXlXGygBPD) for its governance over success in business. Religious [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) that represent Cassa travel from Souli to Souli, collecting offerings and prayer commissions from Banu seeking good fortune in trade. Because it is so commonly seen on altars throughout the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3), xenoanthropologists speculate that it may be one of the oldest Banu gods still worshiped.","g":["cassa","the patron of luck","religion","banu religion","gods","banu gods"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0d9ae63c-7a82-4bdd-9162-9efb37a56b8e"},
{"id":"casse-aerospace","gp":"RPPx3G1MMX","t":"Casse Aerospace","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Casse Aerospace was a spacecraft manufacturer that operated from 2599 to 2623. Founded by noted ship designer and former [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) engineer [Leonard Casse](gp:RX3Krj1EKN), it released its first ship in 2604, the limited-run Cosmo Sloop. Due to the ongoing [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) (2603 - 2610), the leisure craft's sales were lower than projected, and Casse made the decision to pivot his designs from civilian to military. The 2607 [Hurricane](gp:bmNrpdn4gQ) fighter saw success in the latter years of the war. After the conflict ended, the company accepted a contract from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government to create a long-range patrol ship, but all work ceased when Casse passed away in 2615 after an in-air collision. The board sold the company to an investment firm in 2620, and closed its doors. In 2784, [J. Harris Arnold](gp:Vy2ZqLy458) of [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) purchased Casse Aerospace's portfolio in response to a copyright infringement lawsuit for allegedly stealing elements of Casse's designs. Today, Anvil utilizes Casse's signature elements of curved wings and an open circle signet in many of its ships.","g":["spacecraft manufacturer","leonard casse","hurricane"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8618016e-3775-4dd7-9ecd-4eff24b0b0b6"},
{"id":"cassel-goss-ii","gp":"RPDy6gqX7Z","t":"Cassel (Goss II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Cassel (Goss II) is the second planet from the binary suns of the [Goss system](gp:RxnYdDZj96) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). An ocean world with many islands and small continents, Cassel was colonized in the early 2500s. The natural beauty of turquoise, gold, and deep orange bands in the sky alongside the planet's coastlines and forests have made it a major tourist destination. Exports from Cassel are strictly regulated. The planet is currently recognized and has one seat in the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ).","g":["cassel","goss ii","goss system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c9eee105-31a8-4930-8b16-f4186984c68c"},
{"id":"castor-corel-iv","gp":"VYLJxEXrvW","t":"Castor (Corel IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Castor (Corel IV) is a terrestrial, desert planet that sits at the far outer edge of the [Corel system's](gp:R9vQnko7Y2) green band, in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). In 2651, [Corsen Messer V](gp:0OaB8O6awO) ordered several companies to [terraform](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) the planet, so it could serve as an example of the capacity of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) technology. Though it was technically terraformed, the atmosphere is thin and the climate is almost intolerably cold. A handful of settlements dot Castor, primarily centered around deep ice-mining operations.","g":["castor","corel iv","corel system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/17d5d16c-cb3d-4a62-9abf-6576e31dc632"},
{"id":"castra-i","gp":"RxnBYoGWKQ","t":"Castra I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Castra I is a coreless planet in the [Castra system](gp:R4jxkAd8El), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)). Too close to the sun to be [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) for [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) habitation, the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) used Castra I for target practice and weapons testing throughout the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (SEY 2546 - 2792), leaving it covered in craters. The swathes of glass left on the surface after centuries of weapon impacts will sometimes catch the light and make the planet appear to glitter.","g":["castra system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/330061e9-2a9f-4ad7-98ea-97840fcfb0da"},
{"id":"castra-system","gp":"R4jxkAd8El","t":"Castra System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"Castra is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Discovered in SEY 2544, it was originally designated as a military staging area due to its [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) connection with the [Oya system](gp:0KxGow1ly4) in the former [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO). At the end of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792), the system was opened up to non-military settlement and has since become a center of trade and tourism. The second planet from its sun, [Cascom (Castra II)](gp:0dXKkL9a9o), is expected to apply for representation in the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) in the near future.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/42a94060-9c05-4af2-8307-474f8fae3adb"},
{"id":"caterpillar","gp":"VY4WmNG9v6","t":"Caterpillar","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Caterpillar is a multi-crew utility spacecraft and armored freighter manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). Designed for storage, it can be adapted to suit the needs of multiple types of cargo. It can also can be used for combat roles, such as a raiding command center or a q-ship. Drake sells the Caterpillar as the flagship of its spacecraft system, which includes the [Cutlass](gp:R6v8krK71n), [Dragonfly](gp:VlNPm8MOor), and [Buccaneer](gp:VyvYXd1X7a).","g":["drake interplanetary","freight","transport","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ddea21bd-fb52-4c93-8a16-a8b2470d6947"},
{"id":"cathcart-belt-alpha","gp":"0rxZX6Mxkg","t":"Cathcart Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Cathcart belt alpha is a wide asteroid belt in the [Cathcart system](gp:RL6524vWO3). Located in the system's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), it lacks any celestial bodies large enough to support the kind of atmosphere that would give rise to life. Astrophysicists believe that these asteroids grew from what little matter was left in Cathcart after the formation of its massive star.","g":["asteroid belt","cathcart system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bb8861b1-5b87-4304-b97d-e7b48a2f300f"},
{"id":"cathcart-system","gp":"RL6524vWO3","t":"Cathcart System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Cathcart system is an unclaimed planetary system that consists of a class A main sequence star and an asteroid belt. Discovered in SEY 2438 by [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) fugitive Adelaide Lorris, who named the system after the Marshal who had been pursuing her, it was not claimed by the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) due to its lack of planets. Instead, the military utilized it as a junkyard for outdated and damaged spacecraft and space stations. It wasn't long before outlaws and drifters began to claim the abandoned vessels, lashed the salvaged hulls together, and retrofitted them with atmospheric systems. By the 2700s, this mass of interconnected ships became the system's largest settlement, a sprawling network of repurposed space junk nicknamed \"[Spider](gp:VaZwengjJv).\"","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b5d19d9f-e9fc-466c-bb23-1b5e61f5fd94"},
{"id":"CBD","gp":"0qajMeBdLa","t":"CBD","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"CBD (Custom Built Duds) is a clothing brand known for its aggressive, anti-conformist style. Originally a spectrum site for fans of do-it-yourself, punk-style fashion, it launched its own line of clothing in SEY 2777. Its earliest designs featured military elements described by the designers as a direct insult to the [Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo)-backed government. CBD still includes this in their modern work.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4f2a64a4-96f3-4354-b1b3-092171fbb39b"},
{"id":"ccs-conversion","gp":"VyvYM3mpX8","t":"CC's Conversions","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"CC's Conversions is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) personal armor customization and resale company. In addition to creating bespoke pieces, CC's purchases discounted stock from other vendors and converts it into limited edition sets. They do not repeat runs once they are completely sold.","g":["armor customizer","armor reseller"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/31065dc3-63f1-4e0d-99f3-ae18f36be098"},
{"id":"celebration-week","gp":"bEzE5gm18v","t":"Celebration Week","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"Celebration Week is a holiday period in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) that commemorates when all people in the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) gained the rights to self-determine their romantic relationships and gender identities. It arose from two holidays that were held on [Vann (Croshaw III)](gp:bZkk4l4j2D) in the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp) to recognize when these hard-won rights became local law. After many decades, the holidays were eventually combined into a week-long celebration that was held on both Vann and the much more temperate [Angeli (Croshaw II)](gp:0QlxqwG14Q). It became such a popular event that it started attracting tourists to Angeli in particular from other parts of the UNE, boosting economic growth and thus inspiring other planets to host their own festivals. In SEY 2450, Celebration Week was made an official holiday throughout the UNE.","g":["uee holiday","vann","croshaw iii","angeli","croshaw ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5c8ae1f4-9c80-432c-a5e0-72d76f11a2c4"},
{"id":"cellin-stanton-2a","gp":"Rw1Z9yz1jJ","t":"Cellin (Stanton 2a)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Cellin is a volcanically active moon thronged with geysers that orbits [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav), and is the planet's closest natural satellite. Its tenuous atmosphere contains trace amounts of oxygen, but not enough to support respiration. In spite of the toxic air, many residences and outposts have been established on Cellin since Phillip Xu constructed the first permanent homestead in 2906. The moon was named after the character Cellin from the popular [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) children's story [A Gift for Baba](gp:0KnMm3WX5P).","g":["cellin","stanton 2b","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","crusader","stanton ii","crusader industries","uee moon","stanton ii moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/446521ee-4350-4cc0-9839-ac15b05e4302"},
{"id":"centauri-belt-alpha","gp":"0KxxorB7d2","t":"Centauri Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Centauri belt alpha is an [asteroid belt](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/asteroid-belt) in the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), that orbits the [system's](gp:VaZwNWg372) sun between [Centauri IV](gp:0qaakPppn1) and [Centauri V](gp:VgEElDmGQY). A dense belt with enough mass to form a planet, the heavy metals and other resources that can be found there are extracted to support various industries on [Saisei (Centauri III)](gp:Vy22NQJ1q6). Due to the abundance of resources, major mining conglomerates, independent businesses, and sole prospectors are able to work alongside one another with little competition.","g":["asteroid belt","centauri system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/36564527-f5cf-4bff-8e2f-6da448b000cb"},
{"id":"centauri-i","gp":"01LL854AyJ","t":"Centauri I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Centauri I is a protoplanet in the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that orbits very close to its sun. Surveyor Kelly Alden captured an image of Centauri I in 2639 through her ship's camera, capturing the protoplanet in the path of a blue-white prominence that seems to reach out and grasp it. A copy of the photograph hangs in the Centauri Museum of Fine Art.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","centauri system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7aecd01d-b452-43f1-87ab-5137301b9181"},
{"id":"centauri-iv","gp":"0qaakPppn1","t":"Centauri IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Centauri IV is the fourth planet from the sun in the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A coreless world, it lacks an electromagnetic field, and experiences no volcanic activity. Its surface is heavily scarred from crater impacts, likely from the nearby asteroid belt. Although it exists outside Centauri's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), multiple [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) companies have considered attempting to install an atmosphere on Centauri IV to facilitate easier access to the planet's mineral deposits.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","centauri system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/51277e05-8dea-49b7-b464-f32282827dbc"},
{"id":"centauri-system","gp":"0Qllvmr5v5","t":"Centauri System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Centauri system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), made up of an A-type main sequence star, a protoplanet, three terrestrial planets, an asteroid belt, and a super-Jupiter gas giant. Discovered in SEY 2365, two of its planets have been [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) for [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) habitation. [Yar (Centauri II)](gp:R6dd5pyOZ5) is a largely desert world, sparsely populated and beset by dust storms. [Saisei (Centauri III)](gp:Vy22NQJ1q6) is a carefully constructed, highly populated world built to harmonize with the natural environment.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/58a4cdf5-3f9d-45e6-8bef-b0bc0d77cced"},
{"id":"centauri-v","gp":"VgEElDmGQY","t":"Centauri V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Centauri V is a red and yellow super-Jupiter in the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Enormous, violent storms that almost encircle the entire planet occasionally develop near the equator, while its north and south poles are encircled by systems of permanent cyclones. Spacecraft sometimes utilize the upper atmosphere of Centauri V for refueling, barring the presence of any extreme weather.","g":["centauri system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/539020e3-573c-41d7-93d3-e3272d3462e8"},
{"id":"centennial-bloom","gp":"0n9vL8gKYz","t":"Centennial Bloom (Pui'arai.ly'ii)","k":"life","c":["Plants","Xi'an"],"x":"# Centennial Bloom\nThe centennial bloom (*pui'arai.ly'ii*) is a plant indigenous to Ko'li (Ē'aluth III) that flowers once every 100 [Modern Xi'an Years](gp:R4ZQ89gBQx) (MXY). Many centennial blooms are tended on [R.aip'uāng (Kai'pua II)](gp:Rw1rnY1AYJ), the center of [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe) in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Like the centennial bloom's reproduction cycle, R.aip'uāng's rotation period completes once every 100 MXY.\n# Description and Lifecycle \nStanding half a meter tall at its highest, the centennial bloom is a small tree that varies in coloration depending on its particular cultivar. The most common variety has a sturdy, woody trunk with dark-brown and light-brown horizontal banding and dark-green elliptic leaves. Its light-pink flowers are bilaterally symmetrical and have stamens about twice as long as the flower itself. During the short time it blooms, it gives off an earthy scent. Flies and other carrion-eating bugs are its main pollinators on its world of origin, Ko'li. The flower blooms for around 40 hours before it starts to wither, putting all its energy into reproduction.\n\nThe centennial bloom grows a small, dark-purple berry that's eaten by local wildlife and propagated in the surrounding areas. Its native desert climate dries out the seeds in preparation for the rainy season. It takes a seed one full [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) year to sprout. During that year, it must only be watered sporadically and must never be allowed to remain wet for more than 20 hours or the seed is in danger of rotting. Centennial blooms on R.aip'uāng grown in more temperate areas are kept dry through constant, careful attention and specialized equipment that mimics the day/night cycle on Ko'li. Lovers of the centennial bloom often keep theirs in a sealed arcology that automatically regulates the environment to suit the plant's needs. Over the past decade, it has increased in popularity as a shipboard plant\n# Importance to Li'tova\nLi'tova is a spiritual practice centered around the understanding of time. One of the main facets scholars contemplate is the way actions ripple backwards and forwards across time. Acknowledging the seen and unseen ramifications of one's deeds is one of the core principles in the Li'tova code of ethics. Other aspects include the exploration of time as a dimension, the perception of time on an individual level through metabolic manipulation under meditation, and the measurement of time on a collective level. The centennial bloom's 100-year flowering cycle appeared to the explorers who discovered it on Ko'li to be a poetic manifestation of Li'tova itself. The plant was extracted from Ko'li en masse before its [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and exported to R.aip'uāng to be raised and contemplated.\n# End of the Cold War\nAt the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) in 2793 (III.1053), [Emperor Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo) invited the new [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y) for a tour of R.aip'uāng. Though the existence of the [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) was public knowledge, [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) had long been barred from entering the Ē'aluth system. The Emperor personally clipped a branch from a centennial bloom and handed it to Toi. The offer of the centennial bloom and the subsequent opening of the system to all Humans were gestures of peace, made in the hope that the previous age of strife and misunderstanding between the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the Xi'an Empire would be replaced with one of cultural exchange and harmony.","g":["centennial bloom","ko'li","ē'aluth iii","r.aip'uāng","kai'pua ii","flowers"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f9f20091-d587-41ef-8209-500de0403590"},
{"id":"centermass","gp":"0rqzXEkLXY","t":"CenterMass","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"CenterMass is a spacecraft weapons and armor retailer with franchise stores in multiple locations across the United Empire of Earth (UEE). Founded as a weapons-only store, they added armor to their inventory in SEY 2939. They also keep mechanics on staff for installation, modification, and repair of any items purchased at a CenterMass store.","g":["armor retailer","weapons retailer","armor repair","weapon repair","spacecraft component repair"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ffff2f6f-d75b-4d83-96d0-dfc300c4ee21"},
{"id":"central-core-bank","gp":"RvlaGZkMx8","t":"Central Core Bank","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"The Central Core Bank is the bank that maintains the reserves necessary to financially back the United Earth Credit (UEC), the official currency of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). It was founded in SEY 2528 by experts from various financial markets, who were brought in by the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) to create and administer monetary policy, conduct foreign exchange operations, and monitor the banking sector. The Central Core Bank is one of the largest financial organizations in the UEE, and still oversees the regulation of the UEC.","g":["financial institutions","banks"]},
{"id":"central","gp":"R56nmzpqPg","t":"Central Headquarters and Shared Services Center","k":"place","c":["Commerce","Locations","Human"],"x":"The Central Headquarters and Shared Services Center (aka Central Tower) is the name of the main headquarters of [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) located in the capital city of [Lorville](gp:Rw1ZlJNE36). It also has the distinction of being the largest building on [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL). The CEO's office, a showroom for the products of Hurston Dynamics, and the command center of the planet's surveillance force can all be found within the walls of Central Tower.","g":["hurston dynamics","hurston","stanton i"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/45336d95-6ed8-4b94-9b8f-b8f1b28bc8a4"},
{"id":"centralist-party","gp":"01dWmzB3aG","t":"Centralist Party","k":"faction","c":["Politics","Human"],"x":"The Centralist party is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) political party; one of the three largest political parties in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Members of the Centralist party typically favor government regulation and spending, lower taxes, and increased privacy laws, and vote against military spending. They also take a hard-line stance against moving the capital of the UEE away from Earth. The most recent Centralist [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the UEE was Mikkel Sheriden, who served from 2931 to 2941.","g":["uee political party"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b3645dad-844b-49ff-9848-c9d9f230b9f2"},
{"id":"centurion","gp":"VlMlnYZQJA","t":"Centurion","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Military","Human"],"x":"The Centurion is a short-range anti-aircraft ground vehicle manufactured by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). Like the [Ballista](gp:V8gJyXMDrM) and the [Spartan](gp:0QlyWlqqyJ), it is built on the [Atlas Platform](gp:R9vdJKjy8M). Intended to work in tandem with longer-range vehicles, the Centurion was designed as a mobile perimeter defense system able to operate in a variety of environments. It comes with a turret with a gunner's seat and a remote turret controlled by the driver, and features a thick armored hull.","g":["anvil aerospace","military vehicle","human vehicle","tank","atlas platform"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9c0105be-0f05-48a3-9da2-3bfc6301ecdc"},
{"id":"ceprozin","gp":"02k3Ne7Y5z","t":"Ceprozin","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Ceprozin is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug invented by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke) in 2938 at the Hickes Research Outpost on the moon [Cellin (Stanton 2a)](gp:Rw1Z9yz1jJ) in the [Stanton system](gp:RX3lKBA3dq), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A product of decades of research and development, Ceprozin provides pain relief and curbs inflammation without any of the side effects common with other NSAIDs, such as stomach and kidney problems. It is widely used during cybernetic replacement surgeries.","g":["medication","pain reliever","rayari inc"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/90895da8-971b-4278-9ed1-e9bc18993c08"},
{"id":"cestulus-davien-ii","gp":"0QlKaQ76a5","t":"Cestulus (Davien II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Cestulus is the second planet in the [Davien system](gp:Rz2g71YlkY), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Despite being initially considered a poor candidate for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), Cestulus became a major shipping hub after first contact with the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) in SEY 2438. The city of Jata was the site of a series of bombings in 2546. The bombings, known as the [Atrocity at Jata](gp:0Gz5GgEvkj), were one of the catalysts that led the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) to adopt [Ivar Messer's](gp:RXlXYPWk8q)[Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr) plan. After the end of the [Messer Era (2546 - 2792)](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo), historian [Sydney Kamarck](gp:VaZwNWd7lm) uncovered evidence that linked the attack to Messer allies [Adam Corr](gp:V3qgyvG8ZY) and [Cyrus Ishitaka](gp:R4ZGy5XJXe), allegedly to facilitate Messer's political ascent.","g":["cestulus","davien ii","davien system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b225c248-0867-4f70-85ab-d50bfa5eb2c7"},
{"id":"char","gp":"RvgpG6aLQv","t":"Char","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Illegal Activity","Human"],"x":"Char is a former surveying station on [Cole (Nul III)](gp:RMNKLQkw2B) in the Nul system. Constructed in SEY 2493 by Behesht Mines, the facility was abandoned in 2614 after the costs of operating it exceeded the profits the company earned from mining the planet's resources. In the mid-2600s, people looking to conduct business outside of legal oversight began to use the station as a meeting place. Over the years, it has grown into a thriving marketplace that offers an eclectic variety of goods, some of which are illegal in certain jurisdictions.","g":["nul iii","black market","research station","sealed settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/004f6799-e91b-426a-ba83-8893f2abd4a0"},
{"id":"charon-sol-9a","gp":"0Gx3l4Wle8","t":"Charon (Sol 9a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Charon (Sol 9a) is a moon of [Pluto (Sol IX)](gp:0qa1Zo37jk), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The largest of the dwarf planet's five natural satellites, Pluto and Charon are mutually tidally locked to one another and orbit a common barycenter that lies outside Pluto's surface. The two bodies are thought by astrophysicists to have collided in their formation before settling into their current orbit.","g":["charon","sol 9a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dbce695d-bfd4-49ca-be4d-4eef405ede4d"},
{"id":"charon-2a","gp":"V8WWGg9z7r","t":"Charon 2a","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Charon 2a is the innermost moon of [Charon II](gp:02kk9BXyEe), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Unusually for a moon of its small size, it has a thin atmosphere generated by high volcanic and seismic activity. An independent band of mercenaries attempted to establish a base on Charon 2a in the late 2800s, but were forced to abandon it after it was destroyed in a powerful series of earthquakes.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable moon","charon system","charon ii moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7fec3ddc-5325-47c1-9e1e-2cedbb3e7ab3"},
{"id":"charon-2b","gp":"VpMMLvek9O","t":"Charon 2b","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Charon 2b is the outermost moon of [Charon II](gp:VarrdBl87w), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Though it is desolate today, systems of channels and caves on its surface suggest that liquid water once flowed there. The majority of caves on Charon 2b have yet to be fully charted.","g":["charon system","charon ii moon","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e52b458a-d207-44d0-9d7e-74e87cbf2cf3"},
{"id":"charon-i","gp":"RAXXpdkA6A","t":"Charon I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Charon I is the first planet from the sun in the [Charon system](gp:VarrdBl87w), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). At some point in the distant past, the planet was likely knocked from its orbit by a rogue body. Its surface is sublimating as it falls towards the sun, giving the planet the appearance of an unusually massive comet.","g":["charon system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/526416b5-913f-4a3a-b7c0-1aab245160da"},
{"id":"charon-ii","gp":"02kk9BXyEe","t":"Charon II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Charon II is a smog planet in the Charon system, [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Positioned just inside the green band, its surface temperature and high-pressure atmosphere make landing on the planet dangerous. Carbon dioxide and carbon monoxide are the two most prevalent gasses on the planet, causing a runaway greenhouse effect.","g":["charon system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/17092166-88cf-4bb5-883b-9d18ae572beb"},
{"id":"charon-iii","gp":"RkGGMvDpoz","t":"Charon III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Charon III (formerly Haros) is an inhabited planet in the [Charon system](gp:VarrdBl87w), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). During the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (SEY 2546 - 2792), the planet was used as a site for vast prisons and re-education camps. After the [fall of the Messers](gp:bE3rKa32P7) in 2792, the populace stormed the detention facilities and freed the prisoners. Once the extent of the deplorable conditions and practices came to light, it inspired a vote to renounce Haros' recognition by the UEE. Today, Charon III remains an unrecognized planet. Two of its states, [Dellin](gp:0OaBKD9Kwk) and [Acheron](gp:VJOz3gMM85), began armed conflict with one another following the election of [Tarquin Klast](gp:0dQ4mGDJYd) as Dellin's governor in 2944. The UEE military has been monitoring the civil war, but has avoided direct interference.","g":["charon system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ae9c6899-4c9a-4035-a5dd-38a960cec7fe"},
{"id":"charon-iv","gp":"VgEEq1w5dw","t":"Charon IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Charon IV is an ice giant in the [Charon system](gp:VarrdBl87w), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Its atmosphere, composed mainly of methane and ammonia, is icy blue, giving the planet an almost white appearance when viewed from orbit. When Max Keaton discovered the Charon system in 2538, the sight of the gas giant's pale skies inspired him to name the system after Charon, ferryman of the dead.","g":["charon system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3f3287ef-0043-4eb0-9a99-a695813e464d"},
{"id":"charon-system","gp":"VarrdBl87w","t":"Charon System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Charon system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Discovered in SEY 2538, it was used as a prison system during the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792), with [most prisons](gp:0KxqnXDpQ2) concentrated in the state of [Dellin](gp:0OaBKD9Kwk) on [Haros (Charon III)](gp:RkGGMvDpoz). After the assassination of [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) in 2792, the non-incarcerated population of Charon III stormed the prisons seeking to free political dissidents being held there. Once the public gained access to the site, the many atrocities performed by the administrators of the prison on behalf of the Messer government were confirmed. These revelations pushed the planet's senators to renounce their recognition from the UEE. To this day, the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) of Charon III has not sought re-recognition from the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ).","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b518fff5-20a6-4931-8c78-678262b824b4"},
{"id":"charon-v","gp":"ReggdWQonM","t":"Charon V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Charon V is a dwarf planet in the [Charon system](gp:VarrdBl87w), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Numerous planetary surveys done since the system was discovered have confirmed that there are not enough precious mineral resources to justify the installation of permanent mining operations here. Some independent miners operate outposts on Charon V, away from possible business interference from large conglomerates.","g":["charon system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1775e738-a433-4da1-8771-fc6884c07497"},
{"id":"checkmate-station","gp":"RPDeA41EZX","t":"Checkmate Station","k":"place","c":["Locations"],"x":"Checkmate Station, formerly designated PYAM-FARSTAT-2-4, is a space station that orbits the star of the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N) in the L4 Lagrange point of [Monox (Pyro II)](gp:0jGdgLEjqJ). Originally constructed as a resupply satellite for workers on Monox, it was abandoned when [Pyrotechnic Amalgamated](gp:VpM4anYBn1) went out of business in 2563. Various outlaw gangs have laid claim to it, sometimes changing the station's name to reflect who controls it. Currently, the [Rough & Ready](gp:RMNjxwk8pB) gang are in charge, and are responsible for its current moniker. The group allows travelers through Pyro to stop at Checkmate Station to refuel their ships, purchase supplies, and indulge in entertainment.","g":["PYAM-FARSTAT-2-4","space station","pyro system","rough & ready","independent space station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b60caddf-b2b1-45d8-be61-a21dd3f90c96"},
{"id":"chemline-solutions","gp":"RX3DP9Adn8","t":"Chemline Solutions","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Chemline Solutions (CS) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer and distributor of industrial chemicals. It was founded in SEY 2889 by Victor Zahid, a businessman, and his twin sister Adorai Zahid, a geological engineer, after Adorai's company Edo Inc. cancelled her project to develop a new kind of resource extraction technology. While Adorai worked to complete her research, CS supplied chemicals to various companies in order to build up the company's reputation. In 2904, CS activated their first gas mining facility on the moon of [Odin I](gp:VlNP3xpMx4), [Gainey](gp:Rw1G2JG4K9). Though CS was successful in harvesting gas from deep inside Gainey, it caused dangerous seismic events. Adorai sued Victor for rights to her technology when he fired her for her continued dissent against a plan to build another extraction facility on a populated world. The highly-publicized legal battle severely impacted the company's reputation. No longer able to maintain the Gainey facility, CS closed it in 2919 and sealed it in 2923.","g":["commercial and industrial goods manufacturer","chemical manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dff3ade8-beaf-489c-a499-5f819a1a95e5"},
{"id":"chibanzoo","gp":"Rxnnywv2AM","t":"Chibanzoo","k":"life","c":["Food and Beverages","Plants"],"x":"The chibanzoo is a berry that grows in clusters on the chibanzoo plant, and is indigenous to [Cassel (Goss II)](gp:RPDy6gqX7Z). Wild chibanzoo are often more tart than the commercially grown variety, which is known for its sour and very sweet flavor. In the center of each berry is a cluster of small, highly bitter black seeds that [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) usually discard while eating. [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) and [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) prefer to consume the seeds alongside the flesh of the fruit. Chibanzoo berries are used as ingredients for desserts such as ice cream, and as the main ingredient of [Chibanzoo Cream](gp:RvllyMyBNA) liqueur.","g":["fruit","bushes","cassel","goss ii","food"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/afb59680-a7ed-4775-a9a6-0b9fae2c9095"},
{"id":"chibanzoo-cream","gp":"RvllyMyBNA","t":"Chibanzoo Cream","k":"culture","c":["Food and Beverages","Human"],"x":"Chibanzoo Cream is a brand of liqueur manufactured on Cassel (Goss II). It was first brewed by the original settlers of the planet from the local [chibanzoo](gp:Rxnnywv2AM) berries. The earliest version of the liqueur was more tart than sweet, and was generally mixed with sugar syrup and cold soda water. As the chibanzoo has become more sugary over centuries of commercial use, the liqueur has grown to have a sweeter profile that still maintains its sour edge. While it can be consumed as a standalone beverage, it is most often used as a cocktail ingredient.","g":["alcohol","beverage","human beverage"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/400e3a1c-b771-441c-b87d-b0dcf83167c0"},
{"id":"chibanzoo-plant","gp":"0QlnWyd84v","t":"Chibanzoo Plant","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The chibanzoo is a type of plant that bears a fruit of the same name. Originally from [Cassel (Goss II)](gp:RPDy6gqX7Z), it thrives in warm, breezy environments and grows best if deeply watered, but can be cultivated in a wide variety of climates. Each berry it produces has a thin, semi-translucent skin that shows the bright red flesh underneath it, and is sweet, extremely tart, and has a tannic mouth-drying effect when eaten.","g":["chibanzoo","cassel","goss ii","fruiting plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7255e728-a311-4bb5-8e8f-5b971ef3f3fe"},
{"id":"chimera-communications","gp":"R6v8g9jno1","t":"Chimera Communications","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Chimera Communications is a Human manufacturer of communications and scanning systems, mainly for specialized mining and exploration spacecraft. They maintain a dedicated research and development department focused on increasing the durability of their products. The company experienced a period of rapid growth after forming an exclusive partnership with Origin Jumpworks to outfit their 300 series of spacecraft with radar and scanning systems.","g":["communications","scanner manufacturer","radar manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1958f536-5705-4434-8d0e-df9ecaaf07fa"},
{"id":"chronos-system","gp":"RvlQZKy95l","t":"Chronos System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Chronos system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE), and is made up of a mesoplanet, a rocky planet, and a G-type star. With only two planets, both uninhabited and unable to be [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), the system would likely have not risen to prominence if it weren't chosen to be the home of [Project Archangel](gp:RLMmAnr4gj), the UEE's long-term scientific endeavor to create a fully artificial planet. Commonly known as Synthworld, [Chronos III](gp:bZkyrEPLra) has been under construction for over seven decades.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dd33f9ac-bfad-41f0-a0d6-066123842ed3"},
{"id":"chuaichuai-rila-i","gp":"Rw1xWXQxdX","t":"Chuai'chuai (R.il'a I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Chuai'chuai (R.il'a I) is the first celestial body from the sun of the [R.il'a system](gp:Rw1xWXME1B), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A protoplanet, it is oblate in shape and resembles an egg pockmarked with craters. Since it had little to offer in the way of resources, the Xi'an military used it as a landmark during training exercises that required close proximity to the system's sun. Now that R.il'a has turned towards industrial use, shield manufacturers are known to test advanced barriers against stellar radiation from the surface of the Chuai'chuai.","g":["chuaichuai","r.il'a i","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"chauton-taal-vi","gp":"RAXvm855pn","t":"Chuaiton (T.āl VI)","k":"place","c":["Plants","Xi'an"],"x":"Chuaiton (T.āl VI) is the sixth planet from the sun of the [T.āl system](gp:R4j2mdjZE5), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Uninhabitable but rich in resources, its mineral deposits have historically helped to support all of the system's industries. In the early 30th century, its mining operations began to report sharply dwindling takes, leading to an economic slowdown that came dangerously close to causing a system-wide recession. Multiple industries in T.āl now rely largely on imports to continue functioning.","g":["chuaiton","t.āl vi","t.āl system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"church-of-the-journey","gp":"V8WGP6zjXe","t":"Church of the Journey","k":"culture","c":["Culture","Human"],"x":"The Church of the Journey is a system of beliefs that rose to prominence among [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) in the late 29th century. In 2876 its founder, Vita Perry, developed a meditation technique to be undertaken before, during, and after long journeys. The technique was meant to enhance its practitioner's appreciation of their path through life via understanding how a journey had changed them, delight in a journey begun, acceptance of a journey ended, and anticipation of the next journey. By the late 2890s, a code of morals centered around passing through the universe with as little impact upon it as possible developed alongside the meditation practice. Followers of this code are known as Journeymen.","g":["religion","human religion"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/27d548be-be51-4506-96f1-890b3a64ecd3"},
{"id":"citizen-day","gp":"bmGYMYp9Xy","t":"Citizen Day","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"Citizen Day is a holiday observed annually in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) on October tenth. It was established to recognize the achievements of [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) who have attained [Citizenship](gp:RLMmop8rkr) through civic responsibility, military service, altruistic work, or other positive and impactful contributions to their communities. It is also the day in which new Citizens are formally recognized. The recognition ceremony takes place at the Citizen Day Conference (also known as CitizenCon), an event held in a new city in the UEE every year. \n\nIt was seen primarily as a bank holiday until 2734, when [Galor Messer IX](gp:VyvYAGKxAz) used xenophobic propaganda to turn it into a tool boost military recruitment and held lavish celebrations in honor of Citizens' sacrifices for the betterment of the UEE. In the second half of the 28th century, anti-Messer activists on Terra used the holiday to recruit others to their cause. After [the Messers fell](gp:bE3rKa32P7), the new [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y) held the first Citizen Day Conference in New York City, Earth (Sol III) on 10 October 2793.","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f10d919a-e30e-4911-ae28-351bb6826063"},
{"id":"citizens-for-prosperity","gp":"RegEXoEDnw","t":"Citizens for Prosperity","k":"company","c":["Organizations","Human"],"x":"Citizens for Prosperity (formerly Citizens for Pyro) is a civilian non-profit organization that hopes to expand the non-outlaw population of [Pyro](gp:0ODxJM917N) and the systems connected with it until they have stable enough communities for the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) to finally claim the systems as its own. Madge \"Dash\" Hartford originally established the organization in SEY 2950 with the goal of eradicating all criminals from the Pyro after her best friend Kyuwa Endicott was caught in the crossfire between rival gangs and killed. After leading multiple missions into Pyro to hunt down outlaws, Hartford concluded that the only way to truly make the system safe  would be to increase the viability of non-criminal settlements and attract commercial interests to the area. Over time, and with the backing of commercial enterprises, she believes that civilian interests will grow powerful enough to overpower Pyro's criminal element. Since then, Citizens for Prosperity has been recruiting new members and raising funds to establish a major settlement on [Bloom (Pyro III)](gp:0KxjqgQdNY). In 2954, the organization officially expanded its mission to include systems other than Pyro.","g":["non-profit organization"]},
{"id":"city-lights","gp":"01LjekGnv1","t":"City Lights","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"City Lights is a casual clothing brand that is sold throughout the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Focused on affordability, it produces simple pieces with clean lines that are easy to construct and can be paired with a wide variety of outfits. The company was founded under the philosophy that anything they design should be as timeless as possible and within reach of anyone regardless of social class.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/edb1394b-3e75-422d-9b1e-e5b8f94b8af6"},
{"id":"cdf","gp":"0QxYZvMl8o","t":"Civilian Defense Force","k":"faction","c":["Organizations","Human"],"x":"The Civilian Defense Force (CDF) is a civilian militia connected to the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk). Founded in 2947, it was created with the enactment of the [Militia Mobilization Initiative](gp:RkZ96m89Jm) as a way for law enforcement to enlist the public to help with larger scale threats in the system. The CDF program is currently run under Advocacy supervision, so local law must petition the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) for authorization.","g":["militia","uee advocacy","civilian defense force (cdf)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/474f6310-2617-43c8-89cf-ff03887afbbf"},
{"id":"clark-defense-systems","gp":"0QxYZvWY7N","t":"Clark Defense Systems","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Military","Human"],"x":"Clark Defense Systems (CDS) is a Human personal armor manufacturer headquartered on Cascom (Castra II), United Empire of Earth (UEE). Many of their products were inspired by equipment utilized by the UEE military. In 2945, CDS was awarded a government contract to research next generation light armor. They also produce jetpacks.","g":["cds","jetpack manufactuerer","armor manufacturer","castra ii","cascom"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/233dc914-01d3-40a2-94b0-7cb7e0aa1064"},
{"id":"clarkson-energies","gp":"0NwpL13BWJ","t":"Clarkson Energies","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Clarkson Energies is a Human manufacturer of weapon batteries and power plants. Not strictly partnered with any one producer of weapons, their aim is to create products that can be used with a wide variety of brands.","g":["weapon component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2d84f786-fc2f-4ce8-b648-7ff5388185c6"},
{"id":"claw-salamanders","gp":"RL64awp5oL","t":"Claw Salamanders","k":"faction","c":["Illegal Activity","Organizations","Human"],"x":"The Claw Salamanders are an independent faction and outlaw group based in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). Known for their custom-made armor suited for cold environments and helmets that conceal their faces and modulate their voices, they can generally be found living in deep freeze environments. The group's origin is not known, but evidence suggests that it may have been started by out-of-work miners who lost their contracts when the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) government elected not to claim the Nyx system in the late-26th century SEY. The Claw Salamanders largely keep to themselves unless they are in need of resources, but will attack those who intrude on what they consider to be their territory.","g":["outlaw factions","human outlaw factions","nyx outlaw factions"],"img":"https://static.robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/upload/33404ef1-b023-4c06-b430-836e567a7eb6"},
{"id":"clio-stanton-4b","gp":"01Ld63ezDB","t":"Clio (Stanton 4b)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Clio is the second-closest moon to [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1), and is a popular destination for tourists due to its liquid oceans and pink and teal sky. It was named for the ancient Earth (Sol III) muse of history in order to remind those on microTech that their work is built on the labor of their predecessors. Rayari Inc. has established research outposts on Clio dedicated to the study of the moon's environment.","g":["clio","stanton 4b","microtech moon","stanton iv moon","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0ef66d67-5ce0-40b7-b38b-4a77a15a16d4"},
{"id":"clover","gp":"box5qg83aL","t":"Clover","k":"culture","c":["Music","Human"],"x":"Clover was a [Human](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/category/human) music group active in the 2920s and 30s. Known for their aggressive metal arrangements, their most successful single \"Moonlight\" reached number one on multiple music charts in 2931. While they never achieved another mainstream success, Clover had a dedicated cult following. The band broke up when the lead guitarist died of a sudden heart attack during a live performance in 2939.","g":["metal (music genre)","asura","ferron iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e9320bfa-0a80-481d-a743-4e89a83acf8a"},
{"id":"code-blue-apparel","gp":"RX3oBdJ3JZ","t":"Code Blue Apparel","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Code Blue Apparel is a workwear clothing brand known for its durable products. Initially founded as a medical-wear manufacturer, its first products were simple scrubs with the company's logo sewn over the front pocket. These saw early success not just among emergency room workers, but those in adjacent fields, such as veterinarians. The company expanded into other fields within five standard years.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1887a5d6-3bb5-4bd8-8e8c-0324bd39e7ff"},
{"id":"cole-nul-iii","gp":"RMNKLQkw2B","t":"Cole (Nul III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Cole (Nul III) is the third planet from the sun of the unclaimed [Nul system](gp:VgEnlpqyJ9). Located on the inner edge of the system's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), it has a relatively temperate climate that has made it a potential target for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) companies. However, its thick atmosphere of ammonia and sulfur has resisted all terraforming attempts, and the planet remains uninhabitable. It is nevertheless occupied by a busy, unregulated market that operates out of an old [surveying facility](gp:RvgpG6aLQv) abandoned by [Behesht Mines](gp:VpMez1B2qM) in 2614.","g":["cole","nul iii","nul system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/91cb8a2a-bc16-47ab-971c-217eac717118"},
{"id":"cole-carlson-and-taylor","gp":"RWwZnvLBoa","t":"Cole, Carlson & Taylor Inc.","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Military","Human"],"x":"Cole, Carlson & Taylor Inc. (CCT), is a manufacturer of ammunition for handheld and spacecraft weapons. The company focuses its efforts on producing simple, dependable products. Though they don't have a standing contract with the United Empire of Earth (UEE), the bulk of their sales come from the military and the Advocacy. As such, they rarely advertise.","g":["uee advocacy","cole, carlson, and taylor (cct)","munitions manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b195e23-491c-4d01-bd84-842a576d9d22"},
{"id":"comm-relay-station","gp":"0OaBMZl17P","t":"Comm Relay Station","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Human"],"x":"A comm relay is a type of prefabricated communications relay tower that collects data from a network of comm arrays positioned through an area of open space. Generally operated by communication companies such as the [Aciedo](gp:0OaBXqLwMq) corporation, these relays are found throughout the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and are both an important historical aspect of Humanity's outward expansion and a still-necessary part of general [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) data transfer.","g":["commrelay station","aciedo communications","communications","space station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fbfc1e94-1ff2-4a4d-8c98-e1f122daee03"},
{"id":"common-laws","gp":"R6dwElxNo1","t":"Common Laws","k":"faction","c":["Government"],"x":"The Common Laws are a set of baseline rights, privileges, and standards that apply to all who reside within the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) regardless of the representation status of their location. These laws include fundamental personal freedoms, safety standards, health services, basic education, a system to allow interplanetary trade and travel, jump point discovery and exploration, and an allowance for the existence of a security force to protect from external threats and internal crime. The laws were established in SEY 2525 after the passage of the Common Laws Initiative, sponsored by Senator Nomi Row of [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5).","g":["laws","human law","uee law"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/05c6be77-d491-4ca4-9f0f-4f9f817e006a"},
{"id":"condi-hillard","gp":"RX3dlOezZM","t":"Condi Hillard","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Condi Hillard (2659 - 2712) was a security contractor for Orion Defense Protection (ODP), best known for being the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to have defeated a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) in ship-to-ship combat. After she completed her [Equivalency](gp:Vgg7YGdQDY), she obtained an old [Gladius](gp:0j46NP5eB3) from a scrapyard, repaired it, and found work in the [Orion system](gp:VlMpwMky6d) with ODP. In the aftermath of the Vanduul attack on [Armitage (Orion III)](gp:RL6KLK4ylo) in 2681, ODP increased patrol shifts for all its pilots, including Hillard. The Vanduul struck two weeks later, and Hillard downed a [Scythe](gp:0qakL3mmmq) and led her team to destroy the rest of the Vanduul ships before they could strike at a nearby outpost. Hillard was commended for her actions, and the United Empire of Earth [Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) Squadron 36 utilized her strategies to develop an early technique to down Vanduul fighters. She died in action in 2712 defending Armitage during the [Battle of Orion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K).","g":["battle of orion"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/32def8e7-8093-447f-ae5b-77b495ad462f"},
{"id":"connors-beard-moss","gp":"V7dkoA8oZ2","t":"Connor's Beard Moss","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"Connor's beard moss is a type of moss that was first discovered in Connor's Land and Load, a space station in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP). Very fragile, if it is removed from its environment it must be provided with a piece of rock, concrete, or metal to grow on and kept in a sealed biosphere that replicates its natural conditions. Ideally, the temperature should be maintained at a constant 23 degrees Celsius and the moss must be continuously provided with a thin layer of water condensation.","g":["connor's land and load","moss"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/78df7141-4938-4beb-86bb-373b15a778a7"},
{"id":"consolidated-outland","gp":"0KnAYqez34","t":"Consolidated Outland","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Consolidated Outland is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) spacecraft development and manufacturing company based on [Rytif (Bremen II)](gp:R5pA7q691W). The company was founded by trillionaire [Silas Koerner](gp:V8gJMXjE8o) in an express effort to disrupt modern spacecraft manufacturing and design conventions. Its first spacecraft, the [Mustang](gp:bZwQJN6WYB), is a low-cost/high-utility ship design of Koerner's own imagining. Koerner followed the successful launch with a different effort to produce a modular colonization ship, the [Pioneer](gp:R6v8glgLWn), launched in late SEY 2947. All aspects of ship production, from initial design to final specs, are overseen by Koerner.","g":["spacecraft manufacturer","rytif","bremen ii","silas koerner"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/36a17b33-dcb6-471f-9730-aa86a8ec659e"},
{"id":"constellation-andromeda","gp":"0QxY3wEXxQ","t":"Constellation Andromeda","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Constellation Andromeda is a multi-crew spacecraft manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). The Constellation's iconic silhouette was crafted by RSI designers to give the craft a memorable appearance. Each Constellation comes pre-packaged with a [Kruger Intergalactic](gp:0Gz5BWEOEg)[P-52 Merlin](gp:RXlXBj5rrk) snub craft. As the baseline model for the ship line, it enjoys popularity among traveling merchants for its modular storage bay, and among smugglers for its weapons loadout.","g":["constellation series","roberts space industries (rsi)","freight","medium freight","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/629eedd1-2899-42f1-be9c-a2e8a97dd4a6"},
{"id":"constellation-aquila","gp":"RzPoZZO24A","t":"Constellation Aquila","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Constellation Aquila is an expedition variant of the [Constellation](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/constellation-series) line of multi-crew spacecraft manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). Intended for exploration, the cockpit of the Aquila was designed to increase the pilot's field of view, and advanced sensors were added to aid the crew in unfamiliar territory. Each Aquila is packaged with an [Ursa Rover](gp:RAdjOOm67M) and a [P-52 Merlin](gp:RXlXBj5rrk).","g":["constellation series","roberts space industries (rsi)","expedition","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7e7ddda7-0438-4cf4-bc6a-19569101df03"},
{"id":"constellation-phoenix","gp":"VyvYqezlqW","t":"Constellation Phoenix","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Constellation Phoenix is a luxury touring variant of the [Constellation](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/constellation-series) line of multi-crew spacecraft manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). The interior of the Phoenix includes high-end customizations created by multiple design firms, such as a primary operator seat by [Gallo & Frost](gp:VDzoZ3jggz), a dining table by Atuvo, and wood interiors by Emil Quast, among other amenities. Each Phoenix comes with a Lynx Rover and a [Kruger Intergalactic](gp:0Gz5BWEOEg)[P-72 Archimedes](gp:RMXyBO9elE) snub craft. A limited-edition version of the Phoenix, the Phoenix Emerald, features bright green livery in honor of [Stella Fortuna](gp:0qn8vv3Aw1).","g":["constellation phoenix emerald","constellation series","roberts space industries (rsi)","touring","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8b28926b-18bd-415a-b8de-122eafb62682"},
{"id":"constellation-taurus","gp":"Vgg7jYmpQn","t":"Constellation Taurus","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Constellation Taurus is a mid-range variant of the [Constellation](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/constellation-series) line of multi-crew spacecraft manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). Adapted to meet the needs of haulers, it was designed with a modular interior, a cargo release system for quick unloading, and a security hold reinforced with tech plating.","g":["constellation series","roberts space industries (rsi)","freight","medium freight","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/832f7400-7772-4b8b-ae4f-d9c242d163df"},
{"id":"coramor","gp":"RWozkYYxla","t":"Coramor","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"Coramor is a holiday celebrated annually in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) on 11 February. It traces its origins to SEY 2486 when Yuri Ilyin disappeared trying to reunite with his lover Corazon Tan, who had become trapped behind the recently-collapsed [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) to the [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). During his search, Yuri would send emotional daily comms to Cora's parents updating them on his search, the last of which was unintelligible except for \"...anything for Cora… amor...\" Yuri was never seen again after sending that final message. The story of Yuri and Cora was popularized in a late 25th century vid titled *Coramor*, a portmanteau derived from Yuri's final comm. Inspired by the tragic tale of love, people began to exchange romantic messages on 11 February, the date of his disappearance. Today, Coramor traditions include the exchange of gifts and comms between lovers, travel to romantic destinations, and the sending of comms into space in hopes of attracting new love. Some celebrants will use the day to send comm messages to lost loved ones. The colors pink and black, the same as the livery of Yuri's ship in *Coramor*, are associated with the holiday.","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0b13af98-476f-4b68-b5c5-c6ebbd3d83bf"},
{"id":"corbyn-salehi","gp":"RL65p7Qpdr","t":"Corbyn Salehi","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Corbyn Salehi (2829 - 2922) was [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) from 2871 to 2881. Elected on a platform that promised an open government and an end to corruption, Salehi authorized the declassification of thousands of records, supported [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) investigations on government officials accused of misconduct, and widened the definition of a protected planet under the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP). His most long-lasting achievement was the foundation of [Project Archangel](gp:RLMmAnr4gj), also known as [Synthworld](gp:bZkyrEPLra). After ending his term as Imperator, Salehi served as the director of the project. He died in 2922 due to complications from his artificial pancreas.","g":["uee imperator"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b59b7953-8160-454d-aefb-a7d94e3b1c6b"},
{"id":"corel-i","gp":"VpMdYJNvyk","t":"Corel I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Corel I is a terrestrial planet that orbits closely to the sun of the [Corel system](gp:R9vQnko7Y2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Parts of the planet's iron core are visible through several deep, enormous holes in the crust and mantle. It is hypothesized that in the distant past, the planet was hit by a series of celestial objects that devastated the surface.","g":["corel system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ee59ad04-7110-4805-8dd4-01b69d1be2e7"},
{"id":"corel-ii","gp":"0QlmM1krnN","t":"Corel II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Corel II is a coreless, terrestrial planet located in the [Corel system](gp:R9vQnko7Y2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The second planet from its sun, it has no magnetic field and an undifferentiated interior. UEE surveys of the planet have shown that it is rich in valuable mineral resources. An ongoing legal dispute between dozens of companies who claim to own exclusive mining rights to Corel II prevented anyone from mining here for decades, but in the near future, the statute of limitations on these various contracts will revert back to the UEE and it is expected that claims will be open to the public.","g":["corel system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6540fba8-3b7a-403b-ad15-4cf805f0114f"},
{"id":"corel-system","gp":"R9vQnko7Y2","t":"Corel System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"Corel is a planetary system on the border between the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) that was discovered in SEY 2449. As an important center of trade between the two civilizations, it is home to many [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). It is made up of four terrestrial planets, one gas giant, one protoplanet, and one G-type star. While its third planet [Lo (Corel III)](gp:VarAoYEQYd) has representation in the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ), its neighboring planet, [Castor (Corel IV)](gp:VYLJxEXrvW), does not.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c17a09df-7bd7-4f33-a924-1bdb2bfb53b5"},
{"id":"corel-v","gp":"VDz2vJ9yex","t":"Corel V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Corel V is a gas giant in the [Corel system](gp:R9vQnko7Y2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A brown and red gas giant with a stormy atmosphere, it is primarily composed of hydrogen and helium, with a solid rocky core. It is a popular spot for young pilots in Corel to learn how to slingshot their ships off planets with high gravity to achieve a burst in speed.","g":["corel system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/60592f85-0c13-45b6-b8f7-47041ead57d7"},
{"id":"corel-vi","gp":"R6dpZo84md","t":"Corel VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Corel VI is a protoplanet located in the outskirts of the [Corel system](gp:R9vQnko7Y2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). In contrast to its sister planets, Corel VI's 12 degree orbital inclination puts it far off from the system's elliptical plane. Outlaw groups attempted to utilize the protoplanet as a base of operations due to its remote location more than once in the past, but each time they were routed by local police forces.","g":["corel system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1f02ba93-fa13-4557-809f-cb60a54275f3"},
{"id":"corin-kilian-ix","gp":"V8WWyl5zGo","t":"Corin (Kilian IX)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"# CORIN (KILIAN IX)\n\nCorin (Kilian IX) is a mesoplanet in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), owned by the [UEE Marines](gp:V7d5ZYEr1a). Located far outside the system's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), surface conditions on the planet are very dangerous for anyone without protective gear. The Marines maintain an extensive underground base here, used as their headquarters and primary training ground. The exact nature of their training is classified, but many believe that the planet's inhospitable environment factors heavily into it. A full Marine battle group patrols the area around Corin at all times to prevent unauthorized access.\n\n# HISTORY\n\nCorin was discovered in SEY 2463 in the initial survey of the Kilian system. As Human territory expanded from Kilian to Ellis, from Ellis to Magnus, then from Magnus to Terra, Kilian's connection to these systems caused its strategic value to rise. Multiple branches of the military were among the first colonizers of Kilian, starting with a forward operating base from the UEE Navy on MacArthur (Kilian V). In 2560, the newly independent UEE Marines chose Corin, an inhospitable, frozen dwarf planet, to use as a base for extreme condition training operations. \n\nCorin's position beyond Kilian's frost line made it impossible to terraform. The Marines instead established a sealed colony as their initial base and soon expanded underground with factories, water processing plants, and waste recycling facilities staffed and run by Marines and high-level clearance contractors. Additionally, budget reports from 2611 revealed that arcologies for raising livestock and growing produce were added to Corin's surface. In 2633, construction appeared to be complete and all imports to the planet ceased.\n\n# UEE MARINE HEADQUARTERS\nToday, Corin remains entirely within the purview of the Marines. The planet is surrounded by a no-fly zone and is patrolled at all times. Ships that have not been cleared to pass through Corin space are subject to shoot-to-kill orders. Non-military ships that have been cleared to land by High Command are only allowed to land on Corin's surface with the stipulation that they do not enter the underground base. Because the base is self-sufficient, this happens very rarely. \n\nAll Marines selected for service from the Army or Navy go through six months of rigorous training on Corin. While the majority of a recruit's training takes place underground, wargames and other training exercises are conducted on Corin's harsh surface to prepare each recruit for the rigors of fighting in potentially deadly environments.","g":["corin","kilian ix","kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet","uee marines"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3af79c59-a867-4578-8f74-a3a121317665"},
{"id":"correction-facilities-leoetothleayingipuo","gp":"0QlOdyez39","t":"Correction Facilities (Le'oeto.thl'e'ayingipuo)","k":"faction","c":["Xi'an","Government"],"x":"Correction facilities (le'oeto.thl'e'ayingipuo) are prisons in which [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) who have been judged to be guilty of a serious offense are imprisoned and compelled to perform labor. The labor varies; in some locations, the prisoners mine for valuable resources, in others, the prisoners might work with volatile chemicals. One of the largest labor prisons is located on the former [Perry Line](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) system Yengchuai (La'uo II). There, prisoners work off their sentences in mining and production facilities.","g":["correction facilities","le'oeto.thl'e'ayingipuo ","xi'an prisons"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/70a2e560-bbc0-4cf6-aa97-a3436059a432"},
{"id":"corsair","gp":"R5p8GDyla3","t":"Corsair","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Corsair is a multi-crew expedition spacecraft manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). Capable of supporting a crew of up to four people, it is outfitted with living quarters that include a full kitchen and washroom facilities. Each Corsair comes with a cargo bay that can accommodate a ground exploration vehicle or up to 72 SCU of cargo, and is equipped with cannon mounts on the bow, a manual turret, wing-mounted cannons, missiles, and an aft-facing remote turret. The Corsair also features a perpendicular cockpit configuration in which the co-pilot is seated below the pilot.","g":["expedition","drake interplanetary","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4eaa8f4e-f2e0-45ab-abb5-0069ec6031ee"},
{"id":"corsen-messer-v","gp":"0OaB8O6awO","t":"Corsen Messer V","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Corsen Messer V (2609-2662) was the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) from 2643 to 2662. Born youngest son of [Deacon Messer II](gp:0j46m4BYge), his older sister, [Livia III](gp:01dWwaQkrL), became Imperator in 2628. He ascended to the office in 2643, when his sister retired from public life two years after her husband Daniel Scota and their son [Marius](gp:RxNxAgrXZz) were killed in a shuttle crash in Moscow, Earth (Sol III). During his reign, he widened the range of crimes eligible for capital punishment, raised taxes throughout the UEE, suspended the right to a trial for political crimes, increased censorship, founded the Monumentalist architectural movement, and opened more political prisons on Charon III. He and his elder son [Gammon](gp:0rxrqgDP12) were assassinated via poisoning in 2662. Though the culprit was never uncovered, historical consensus places the blame on his youngest daughter, [Illyana VI](gp:bZwQBNmWrL).","g":["uee imperator","messer dynasty","messer era"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bee9e4ca-b764-417e-96e7-d19933c27c3b"},
{"id":"corsito-virgil-1b","gp":"RWoewELgz2","t":"Corsito (Virgil 1b)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Corsito (Virgil 1b) is the second moon from [Cyrene (Virgil I)](gp:VlMBNGnxK5), [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). In contrast to its sister moon [Jai (Virgil 1a)](gp:0GxYzeAA9g), it has a dark, slightly blue surface and reflects about half as much light. An enormous crater with a large ring of bright carbon dioxide ice on its floor lies in its northern hemisphere, creating a single bright point of light.","g":["corsito","virgil 1b","virgil system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/270e5c40-c72c-4fbf-9c31-eb645466db78"},
{"id":"cosmo-sloop","gp":"VlMJWLNxG4","t":"Cosmo Sloop","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Cosmo Sloop was a limited-run luxury leisure spacecraft manufactured by [Casse Aerospace](gp:RPPx3G1MMX). Launched in 2604, it was the company's debut ship, personally designed by founder and lead engineer [Leonard Casse](gp:RX3Krj1EKN). Its controls were set up with ease-of-use in mind, so that even newly-minted pilots could fly it without facing a high learning curve. Additionally, the hull featured the open circle signet and curved wings that became a hallmark of Casse's future designs, and later, those of [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). The Cosmo Sloop was retired the same year it debuted after a period of poor sales partially caused by the then-ongoing [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) (2603 - 2610).","g":["casse aerospace","leonard casse","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6f3227a0-3bec-46c9-98b7-2cdc43ef359e"},
{"id":"council-of-three","gp":"Rw1DPO8v8q","t":"Council of Three","k":"faction","c":["Xi'an","Government"],"x":"A Council of Three (kyoLyon) is the ruling body of a [Xi'an House](gp:box9JmxvWL), composed of three elders. Three is seen by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) as the ideal number to balance important decisions, ensuring that multiple points of view are heard and wisdom prevails. All aspects of the governance of a House are overseen by its Council, such as the expenditure of fiscal assets, the distribution of food and clothing, and the arrangement of breeding partners to continue the family Line, among others. \n\nThe Imperial House's Council of Three differs in that it is required by law to be made up of those who are not blood-related to the current Emperor. Instead, it consists of an advanced practitioner of [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe) from R.aip'uāng (Kai'pua III), and one representative each from the civil (yi'p.ūt'ung) and military (yi'p.ūh'yath) branches of the [Imperial Bureaucracy (Pō't.ōngp.ū)](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ). Members of the Council do not retain ties to their Houses of birth, either having chosen to remain with the Bureaucracy after completion of their required 30 years of service, or having dedicated their lives to the study of Li'tova. As the second highest ruling body in the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9), this Council of Three advises the Emperor, directs the governance of the Service, interprets and applies Li'tova, and controls the movement of the military.","g":["xi'an government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/033eda0f-0e70-4b35-bc17-f61e0fbfbc0d"},
{"id":"cousin-crows-custom-craft","gp":"R5ppgyMJpY","t":"Cousin Crow's Custom Craft","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Cousin Crow's Custom Craft is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) company founded by Nampo \"Cousin Crow\" Vasko in 2924 that specializes in customizing spacecraft. Many of the [Genesis](gp:0NwprWlxpX) ships sold on [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav) are converted into branded [starliners](gp:RWwZ7OAjXw) for the corporations that purchase them at the flagship location of Cousin Crow's Custom Crafts in Orison. Cousin Crow's operated only on [Lo (Corel III)](gp:VarAoYEQYd) until 2949, when [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed) released the Privateer, a variant of the [Kraken](gp:0n11yZd6k9) that was converted by Cousin Crow's into a traveling marketplace. Thanks to the publicity garnered from this release, the company made record profits.","g":["lo","corel iii","spacecraft modification company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/aa741440-1dc9-4a0d-9596-23c7744ec927"},
{"id":"covalex-shipping","gp":"V3qgXNEGQW","t":"Covalex Shipping","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Covalex Shipping is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) cargo transportation company founded by goods conveyor Hanso Mallory near the end of the [Messer Era (2546 - 2792)](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo). Initially a smuggling operation, Covalex gained legitimacy when it became an official vendor of [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) goods across all borders and military lines, and attained popularity when it smuggled arms to anti-Messer activists. Currently, it operates as the largest hauling company in the UEE.","g":["shipping company","hauling company","hanso mallory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0074ad93-4dd6-417c-96c7-9f1384e96b79"},
{"id":"crion-caliban-ii","gp":"bEzvPwYZ96","t":"Crion (Caliban II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Crion (Caliban II) is the second planet from the sun of the [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m) in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Located in the green band, it was [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) shortly after it was discovered in SEY 2341 and turned into a thriving, populous colony. In 2884, the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) invaded the Caliban system [en masse](gp:0Gz5DNryvE), laying waste to all the settlements and killing anyone who could not evacuate. The once cosmopolitan Crion is now a wasteland in the process of being consumed by Vanduul [Harvesters](gp:0n1MYzOkG7).","g":["crion","caliban ii","caliban system","habitable","habitable planet","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/208c8fd6-5829-4b90-a7bd-314e1d671239"},
{"id":"crion-security-legion","gp":"VY4WM8e2N1","t":"Crion Security Legion","k":"faction","c":["Organizations","Human"],"x":"The Crion Security Legion was a privately-owned security group that was based out of Crion (Caliban II). It was one of many groups stationed in the Caliban system to supplement the thinly-spread patrols of the [89th Squadron](gp:0Gz5BNmPqo). During the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE), members of the Crion Security Legion assisted in the mass evacuation of the system's inhabitants.","g":["crion","caliban ii","fall of caliban","private security"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/aad81d64-2d0c-4c9e-9eff-88e37480c591"},
{"id":"croshaw-i","gp":"V8WgNMJ62G","t":"Croshaw I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Croshaw I is a terrestrial planet with a thick, high pressure-atmosphere that closely orbits the star of the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp). After its discovery in 2271, some prospectors attempted to establish harvesters on the planet's surface in an effort to gain easy access to industrial-strength acids. However, the vivid yellow and orange atmosphere proved too corrosive for even the most advanced technology at the time to effectively harvest.","g":["croshaw system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/38bc8c6e-1af1-4688-99a7-d37618986d03"},
{"id":"croshaw-iv","gp":"RPDDZz2Lwm","t":"Croshaw IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Croshaw IV is an uninhabitable super-Earth in the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and is the furthest planet from the [system's](gp:VaZwNWg372) sun. Geological evidence suggests that it once had an atmosphere partially made of water vapor, but due to an unknown event, the atmosphere dissipated. The impact of a large meteoroid is considered the most likely cause; however, a crater large enough to support this hypothesis has yet to be discovered.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","croshaw system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bf6c5361-0e67-448f-a162-1205fe493a0d"},
{"id":"crowshaw-system","gp":"0qanKAEJwp","t":"Croshaw System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Croshaw system is a [planetary system](gp:VaZwNWg372) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Discovered in SEY 2271 by [Nick Croshaw](gp:VyvYkAr7YW), it was the first planetary system explored and colonized by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) outside of their home system [Sol](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5). Private companies initially tried to lay claim to the system's planets, but failed when the cost of transporting materials and maintaining operations proved too high. In response, the leadership of [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) called a World Summit in 2281, at which they passed the [Freeman Act](gp:RWooPaXwE2), a cooperative piece of legislation between all Earth governments that created a lottery system to grant potential colonists land and mineral rights. The success of the Freeman Act ultimately led Human leadership to form a new unified government in 2380 called the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO).","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/74ec41ed-493f-42a8-bd19-37f74ec9cb49"},
{"id":"crucible","gp":"bE3rK9OZAv","t":"Crucible","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Crucible is a repair spacecraft developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN), intended to provide field repairs of a variety of ship classes. It includes a rotating bridge that can overlook a large workspace and a series of remote manipulator arms that allow the crew to either repair smaller spacecraft or to dock alongside larger damaged ships. Its repair bay can be pressurized and also detached for remote use. Crucibles are operated by the UEEN and a variety of private enterprises.","g":["repair","heavy repair","anvil aerospace","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8f6cef5e-b22a-4a41-ba4f-37ecb4aeae74"},
{"id":"crusader-stanton-ii","gp":"VarZxj1Qav","t":"Crusader (Stanton II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Crusader (Stanton II) is a low mass gas giant in the [Stanton system](gp:RX3lKBA3dq), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The world was purchased by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) from the UEE in 2865 and is now the company's headquarters. Rare among gas giants, Crusader's upper atmosphere is breathable by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and supports an active indigenous biosphere. The company settled Crusader via a complex network of floating platforms that had been constructed by the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) in 2855 as repair drydocks for its capital ships.","g":["crusader","stanton ii","crusader industries","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3d8c278b-3c5c-4171-a6ca-2d8c698e86b9"},
{"id":"crusader-industries","gp":"0OaBkLLG1N","t":"Crusader Industries","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human","Military"],"x":"Crusader Industries is a spacecraft and spacecraft component manufacturer located in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). One of four corporations in the UEE to own a planet, Crusader Industries designs and constructs its spacecraft in the upper atmosphere of [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav), while the corporation and its employee-inhabitants reside on a latticework of floating colony platforms. A producer of large commercial vessels, among its more popular products is the [Genesis](gp:0NwprWlxpX)[starliner](gp:RWwZ7OAjXw), a luxury transport operated by civilian passenger lines across the galaxy. Crusader also produces a number of military support ships, including the [M2 Hercules](gp:0Gz5Dk8aGa) military transport and the [Mercury](gp:RkZ9m2DO1N) blockade runner.","g":["spacecraft manufacturer","crusader","stanton ii","spacecraft component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c5ed3add-3ff0-498e-9a7e-da34cc06c06f"},
{"id":"crusader-security","gp":"bmNrmYB8MP","t":"Crusader Security","k":"faction","c":["Organizations","Human"],"x":"Crusader Security is [Crusader Industries'](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) private security force responsible for maintaining law, order, and adherence to company policy in and around [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav).","g":["crusader industries","private security","crusader","stanton ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/81a6a2a7-986a-48bd-9afe-0ca2733e7da6"},
{"id":"cry-astro","gp":"VpGEmxgqaA","t":"Cry-Astro","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Cry-Astro is a franchised chain of Human fuel and repair stations with locations across the United Empire of Earth. A recent entrant to the fuel station market, it has gained market share by presenting itself as a cheaper, hands-on alternative to its competitors. Its recent marketing campaign, featuring absurdist humor and purposefully poorly constructed images, has attracted a wave of younger clientele. Cry-Astro stations are also noted for their large selection of food.","g":["spacecraft refuel","spacecraft repair","food retail"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/912fa7d4-b6bf-4237-a163-3f51352d8891"},
{"id":"cryopod","gp":"0GxY74adqg","t":"Cryopod","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A cryopod is a type of enclosed machine or medical device that is used to put people in a state of suspended animation. Once enclosed within the cryopod, the subject is injected with a chemical that induces deep sleep. The device then performs a series of precisely timed temperature drops to create and maintain a coma-like state. Personal cryopods can be controlled from within and programmed to awaken an occupant at a later date. Hospitals utilize specialized medical cryopods to sedate grievously injured or ill patients over the long to aid in the healing process. Cryopods are also favored by some law enforcement organizations and bounty hunters for safer criminal transport.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4219482a-8d9d-45ca-8ef0-01d2528cc2a0"},
{"id":"curelife","gp":"0KxkeN9Oe3","t":"CureLife","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"CureLife is a company that manufactures health products such as portable MedPens, the ParaMed Medical Device, medical beds, and other medical equipment. Formed by a group of doctors, it was the first company to offer MedPens to the general public. The company frequently collaborates with the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military to keep medics supplied with lifesaving equipment and to develop more efficient ways to address field wounds in dangerous situations.","g":["medical research","medical goods manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fc966061-7a78-43d2-9f5e-2889f1117746"},
{"id":"cutlass-black","gp":"R6v8krK71n","t":"Cutlass Black","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Cutlass Black is a space superiority fighter manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). It was initially developed in the mid-29th century SEY as a bid for a military contract with the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). When the bid failed, Drake opted to market the Cutlass Black as a low-cost, easy-to-repair spacecraft to civilians. Other Cutlass variants include the [Cutlass Blue](gp:RxNxZ9aZoz) for law enforcement and bounty hunters and the [Cutlass Red](gp:0QxYEyzo99) medical transport.","g":["drake interplanetary","medium fighter","medium freight","freight","fighter","cutlass series","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fa9d4436-bde2-4076-a0b4-aaa9cf8f99b4"},
{"id":"cutlass-blue","gp":"RxNxZ9aZoz","t":"Cutlass Blue","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Cutlass Blue is a variant of the Cutlass fighter developed by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). Seen as an attempt by Drake to address the criminal reputation of the [Cutlass series](gp:R6v8krK71n), the Blue adapts the original design for use as a police interceptor and a medium range patrol ship. Changes include exchanging cargo space for additional missiles, the addition of a more powerful engine and the installation of holding cells in the rear of the spacecraft. Due to its low price point and repairability, many law enforcement agencies have adopted the Cutlass Blue as their standard ship.","g":["drake interplanetary","interdiction","cutlass series","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/747c3767-4f93-42f2-b148-dd44979ab47a"},
{"id":"cutlass-red","gp":"0QxYEyzo99","t":"Cutlass Red","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Cutlass Red is a variant of the [Cutlass fighter](gp:R6v8krK71n) developed by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). The Red is a combined search and rescue vehicle and medical transport, replacing the standard Cutlass' cargo bay with an autodoc and other medical devices. Standard equipment on the variant includes a Nav-E7 Echo Transponder, enhanced scanners, and a Secure Plus docking collar to support mercy missions. Cutlass Reds often operate in support of larger hospital ships or space stations.","g":["drake interplanetary","cutlass series","medical support","transport","support spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d453d770-d89d-4fc8-beca-12bd689ebf54"},
{"id":"cutlass-steel","gp":"Rw1yW19YLB","t":"Cutlass Steel","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Cutlass Steel is a combination gunship and dropship manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). Designed for transport during combat situations, the Steel modifies the cargo area of the base [Cutlass](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/cutlass-series) model to make room for 18 jump seats and personal weapons lockers. Its doors are equipped with mounted guns, meant to be operated by crew, and a co-pilot-controlled rear turret covers the ship's aft. Other Cutlass variants include the [Cutlass Red](gp:0QxYEyzo99) medical transport, the [Cutlass Blue](gp:RxNxZ9aZoz) prisoner transport, and the [Cutlass Black](gp:R6v8krK71n) armed freighter.","g":["cutlass series","gunship","dropship","drake interplanetary","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e6fa801f-f698-4731-8e79-74f737d50004"},
{"id":"cutter","gp":"VDzA9d5g79","t":"Cutter","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Cutter is a light cargo spacecraft introduced in 2920 and manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). The most recent model debuted at the [Intergalactic Aerospace Expo](gp:R4jpEgezde) in 2952. A single-seat ship with a large cargo hold and minimal living quarters, it was designed as an entry-level vessel for independent haulers, and can be used as transportation as well as cargo transport. The Cutter comes equipped with two laser repeater hardpoints and two dual missile racks.","g":["drake interplanetary","freight","light freight","cutter series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/07cba17d-f68a-4494-bdf5-7c505bf5f81b"},
{"id":"cutter-rambler","gp":"0Gx9Ge7Kkd","t":"Cutter Rambler","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Cutter Rambler is a small expedition spacecraft manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). A variant of the [Cutter](gp:VDzA9d5g79) cargo ship, it swaps some cargo space for expanded living quarters and an additional fuel tank to support long journeys. Drake Interplanetary markets the Rambler as a starter ship for explorers.","g":["cutter series","expedition","drake interplanetary","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/36f9cb75-31a2-49fa-8a12-62692bad4000"},
{"id":"cutter-scout","gp":"V7dDyeLMBK","t":"Cutter Scout","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Cutter Scout is a small reconnaissance and intelligence spacecraft manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). Designed for a single pilot, the Scout is a part of Drake's [Cutter](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/cutter-series) line of starter ships. When compared to the base model, it has a different weapons loadout and enhanced scanning components.","g":["cutter series","reconnaissance","intelligence","drake interplanetary","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1eacb215-2539-4a28-bfcd-18a90dce8b90"},
{"id":"cyclone","gp":"V3GdnGmmzZ","t":"Cyclone","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Cyclone is a light-armored ground vehicle developed by [Tumbril Land Systems](gp:VarkpZnxjd). It can be adapted for multiple roles and forms the backbone of many ground operations that require harsh terrain be traversed. Variants include the Cyclone AA anti-aircraft vehicle, Cyclone RC racing buggy, the Cyclone RN scout and the Cyclone TR turreted model.","g":["tumbril land systems","expedition","all-terrain vehicle (atv)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c2b32a42-ac0a-4cba-a3c9-7fb0283055c4"},
{"id":"cyrene-virgil-i","gp":"VlMBNGnxK5","t":"Cyrene (Virgil I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Virgil I, nicknamed Cyrene, is the first planet from the sun of the [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). The only [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) candidate when the system was discovered, it was quickly turned into a beautiful and warm world with exceptionally fertile soil. It was on track to receive recognition from the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) until SEY 2732, when the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) invaded the neighboring [Tiber system](gp:RMNLm97EDj) and Cyrene was transformed into a military stronghold. When [Tiber fell](gp:0OaBY5pGrq) in 2736, the Vanduul immediately flooded into the system and launched an attack on Cyrene, dropping countless bombs and destroying nearly all life on the planet. Today, the atmosphere is poisonous, and the once warm environment is deep in nuclear winter.","g":["cyrene","virgil i","habitable","habitable planet","virgil system","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5bf7a395-12d2-4255-9689-2b466320d61b"},
{"id":"cyrus-ishitaka","gp":"R4ZGy5XJXe","t":"Cyrus Ishitaka","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Cyrus Ishitaka (SEY 2521 - 2546) was a [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) Army veteran (Corporal, honorably discharged) squadmate of [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) who participated in the [Battle of Idris IV](gp:ReJajXKelk). Little is known about his private life outside of multiple arrests for narcotic possession and distribution. He was later implicated to be one of the two people who allegedly perpetrated a series of bombings of the United Planets of Earth by order of Messer in 2546. Ishitaka, a demolitions expert in the Army, was present on four of the five planets that bombed and found dead less than a week after the final attack. The autopsy found traces of a chemical used in the bombings under his fingernails.","g":["atrocity at jata","battle of idris iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/59f00801-766c-4588-b4f7-d0d250a004d7"},
{"id":"daedalus-cluster-croshaw-cluster-beta","gp":"bmGGyP9DkQ","t":"Daedalus Cluster (Croshaw Cluster Beta)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Daedalus cluster (Croshaw cluster beta) is an [asteroid cluster](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/asteroid-cluster) that shares an orbit with the [Icarus cluster (Croshaw cluster alpha)](gp:0n11yrOBDB) in the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Dense and initially resource rich, the cluster has supported generations of miners in Croshaw since the late 2200s. Though not as productive as it once was, prospectors in the system are still able to locate and extract untapped veins of minerals.","g":["daedalus cluster","asteroid cluster","croshaw system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8fec2f13-0c11-4c4f-a8de-5e5e15089eb0"},
{"id":"dahunsil-kosoko","gp":"0KxyMa6y82","t":"Dahunsil Kosoko","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Exploration"],"x":"Dahunsil Kosoko (2512 - 2581)  was an explorer and navjumper best known for his 2539 discovery of the [Gurzil system](gp:0Kxydrxd45). Born on [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5), he joined a navjumping crew in 2529 when he answered a local job posting. In 2538, he suffered a starship crash that required eight months of inpatient care and resulted in the loss of one of his legs. The insurance payout from the crash left him with enough money to purchase a new ship, which he did the day he was discharged from the medstation where he'd been recuperating. He headed to the then-Nivelin system and began scanning. Three weeks later, he picked up minute traces of a strange signal, which upon close investigation, proved to be a jump point to a previously-unknown planetary system. Kosoko reported his discovery to the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN)  government and requested that the system be named Odara, after his aunt. It was renamed Gurzil and added to the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) in 2542, when the R.il'a-Odara jump point was discovered. Kosoko remained a navjumper until his death in 2581 due to a malfunction in his ship's air recycling system.","g":["cestulus","davien ii","gurzil system","human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c874d8ea-aeee-42dd-8d86-84fb3d40a5bd"},
{"id":"dalton-colabello","gp":"VlMJJp9B9M","t":"Dalton Colabello","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Dalton Colabello (b.2858) is the founder and CEO of [Apocalypse Arms](gp:V7gM1wXdWk). Born on [Borea (Magnus III)](gp:R9vGaQPXJN) to a low-income family, Colabello joined his uncle's contracting company upon attaining his [Equivalency](gp:Vgg7YGdQDY). He broke off and founded his own construction business in 2884, eventually becoming a millionaire in 2887 when he renovated a series of warehouses on behalf of [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). In 2911, his antique weapon collecting hobby led him to a crate of ship weapon prototypes found on [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5) with unknown origins. Captivated by their unique design and potential power, he began a long investigation that eventually led him to the great-granddaughter of [Juliet Maupin](gp:VarxxjKJe5), a former [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) engineer who had developed the armaments under contract from the [Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) regime. Colabello purchased the original design documents and production rights from the family and used Maupin's work as the basis for a debut line of weapons for his new company Apocalypse Arms, founded in 2913.","g":["apocalypse arms","borea","magnus iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6f5b2299-ba74-493d-b1aa-5d4cf60f810b"},
{"id":"daniel-penselin","gp":"RX3lK73waM","t":"Daniel Penselin","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Dr. Daniel Penselin (2445 - 2496) was a physicist whose work improved the fuel economy of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)[quantum drives](gp:RX3DOkJdxJ). In 2491, Penselin published a paper outlining a working hypothesis for the creation of more efficient quantum drives that would allow for an approximate 20 percent reduction in fuel use. Penselin's research funding ran dry soon after this due to budget cutbacks in the astroengineering department of Astravin University. When he could not secure financial backing elsewhere, Penselin modified the drive of his own spacecraft, the *Lilienthal*, and launched it for a test run in 2496. The ship crashed into [the moon](gp:V8WkA3d7LG) of [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5) after a catastrophic system failure. Based on the ship's logs and an analysis of its flight path, however, it was proven that the *Lilienthal* did indeed consume far less fuel during quantum travel. After modifications were made to his research to combat the safety issue, Penselin's work was made standard in all quantum drives, and the moon upon which he died was named in his honor.","g":["quantum drive"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b668b8fa-c888-4de1-b128-2f2e88c207ff"},
{"id":"daniela-argen","gp":"RvlxLvYKKv","t":"Daniela Argen","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Daniela Argen (2762 - 2838)  was a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) of [Locke (Idris IV)](gp:RAX8yYv9jm) from 2801 to 2827. First elected under a platform of revitalizing the economy, she spearheaded a series of tax breaks for first-time business owners and instituted a hiring program that decreased Locke's overall unemployment rate. In 2815, she presented a proposal to the UEE Senate outlining a detailed plan to construct a maximum security prison and an antimatter processing plant on [Kellog VI](gp:R6dAQZgGQe). She argued that the heavy guard presence would serve as an early warning system against [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) incursions through the then-newly discovered jump points to Virgil and [Vector](gp:VgEE5KQeWY) without costing additional military resources, and the plant would generate revenue and provide the UEE with a steady stream of antimatter. Her plan was approved. During her third term, Argen was arrested by the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) on charges of accepting bribes, and was forced to resign. After a trial, she was fined for her actions and went on to become a private business consultant. In 2838, she was found dead in a hotel room on [Asura (Ferron III)](gp:0qaPo2JOj1), having suffered multiple stab wounds. Her murder remains unsolved.","g":["uee senator","universalist party","locke","idris iv","quarterdeck"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e5d56d39-3f85-423a-9144-91d34cabe809"},
{"id":"davien-i","gp":"R9vGmDAkrz","t":"Davien I","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Davien I is the first planet from the sun in the [Davien system](gp:Rz2g71YlkY), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). While it bears a striking visual similarity to Earth's moon, it is larger, denser, and undifferentiated. Its lack of mineral resources has left it largely untouched by miners or developers.","g":["davien system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cb3702b1-20e7-497b-9104-4cb05c69e7dc"},
{"id":"davien-iii","gp":"R4jY58AoMW","t":"Davien III","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Davien III is a smog planet in the [Davien system](gp:Rz2g71YlkY), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Though it orbits further from the sun than Davien's only inhabited planet, [Cestulus](gp:0QlKaQ76a5), its thick, acidic atmosphere has made the planet much hotter. Landing on Davien III is technically possible, but the corrosive air is highly damaging to most spacecraft.","g":["davien system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dd378136-5a90-4fb7-bf10-3b69348d13b2"},
{"id":"davien-iv","gp":"V8WkAloQyx","t":"Davien IV","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Davien IV is an ice giant in the [Davien system](gp:Rz2g71YlkY), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)\n and is the furthest planet from the sun. It was chosen as the parent body for the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4)[Friendship Museum](gp:V7gMm55QDA) due to its picturesque blue and white atmosphere and proximity to the Davien-Cathcart [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY).","g":["davien system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8bba4b78-640a-456f-b142-21a527c9d396"},
{"id":"davien-system","gp":"Rz2g71YlkY","t":"Davien System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Davien system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Discovered in SEY 2430, it was the system in which [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) first encountered intelligent extraterrestrial life: the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). People and businesses flocked to Davien after this, in spite of the thin atmosphere present in the system's only inhabitable planet, [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5). The 2546 [Atrocity at Jata](gp:0Gz5GgEvkj) on Cestulus was a political flashpoint in the leadup to [Ivar Messer I's](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) ascension to [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr) and ultimately [Imperator](gp:VgEQXQrrKN).","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b9fa2a07-40bb-4e38-9897-e7eb058ee40b"},
{"id":"day-of-the-vara","gp":"RkGQqpJwGp","t":"Day of the Vara","k":"history","c":["Culture","Holidays","Human"],"x":"# Day of the Vara\nDay of the Vara is a holiday celebrated in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) annually on October 27th. The holiday involves public festivals adorned with decorations in black and green and private gatherings convened to remember and honor the dead. Celebrants dress up as people who have passed away or in other costumes and swap scary stories, especially pertaining to mysterious incidents in space. It is seen by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) as a day that gives equal weight to the joy of life and the macabre.\n\n# The Vara\nThe holiday first originated around 27 October 2557 after the disappearance of the *Vara*, an exploration vessel orbiting the second planet in the then-recently discovered Hades system. Communications from the *Vara* to the Rhetor system stopped early in the morning, after captain Tisiphone Heptane sent her initial impressions of the ruined alien cities. Systems on board ceased transmitting ship status reports a few hours later. Though search and rescue teams were dispatched the next day, the *Vara* and her crew were nowhere to be found. No wreckage or remains were ever located.\n\n# Origin and Development\nIn the years following this disappearance, rumors spread among haulers and travelers that something malevolent lurked in the Hades system. People began to avoid flying through it on the anniversary of the Vara's demise because on that day, the ship and her crew would supposedly return from the dead and haunt the system. Stories would vary about what would happen to those who encountered the ship but all of them touched on fears surrounding space travel: sometimes the undead crew would secretly board passing vessels to sabotage vital systems; other stories had them haunt the living until they went insane and vented their own ship; in some, scavengers would happen across an abandoned spacecraft, only for the frozen bodies aboard to come alive at the worst possible moment. Horror stories like these remain a major part of Day of the Vara.\n\nOne of the lighter tales that became popular involved a protagonist who disguised themselves as a *Vara* crew member, which inspired others to dress as the deceased to protect themselves from bad luck in space travel. Members of [Terra's (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) counterculture picked up on the superstition and threw the first official Day of the Vara event on 27 October 2593. Many attendees dressed as [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q), who had died in 2592, ostensibly to ward off evil. Songs celebrating Messer's demise that circulated among the crows that night indicated otherwise. [Deacon Messer II](gp:0j46m4BYge) and the UEE government spun the footage as support for the government and encouraged more Day of the Vara celebrations in 2594, describing it as a way to \"fondly remember those who have been lost.\" The campaign was successful; today, the holiday is primarily seen as a day to dress up as and honor those who have passed. It was officially established as an annual holiday in 2595.\n\n# Celebration and Traditions\nIn addition to wearing costumes, remembering dead loved ones, and swapping scary stories, revelers practice traditions adapted from various other festivals that celebrate the dead, such as indulging in food and drink like spirit cakes and iced wine, lighting candles, and staying up until the first morning light. Those celebrating on space stations rely on the artificial day/night cycle to signal festivity's end. Many long-term spacers consider it bad luck to skip the holiday, lest they attract unfavorable attention from the dead. Holos of dead loved ones are often brought out and adorned with green and black ribbons, a reference to colors of the *Vara* crew's uniforms. A hauler on a job might set up a holo of a dead celebrity and adjust the colors for lack of better options. Those on long haul journeys or on explorer vessels still avoid travel to the Hades system in late October.","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d1c4aa02-0671-47f6-8127-059b71f93e02"},
{"id":"daymar-stanton-2b","gp":"VpMGDvX48N","t":"Daymar (Stanton 2b)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Daymar is [Crusader's (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav) second closest natural satellite, and was named after Daymar, one of the siblings in the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) tale [A Gift for Baba](gp:0KnMm3WX5P). Due to the character's tendency to get lost, early explorers of the moon also named the canyon Daymar's Run after him for its twists and turns. Underground race [Daymar Rally](gp:bZkkq3WWk8) is held on Daymar every Standard Earth Year (SEY). In 2862, the Javelin-class destroyer UEES *Flyssa* crashed on Daymar after an illegal mining spacecraft it was pursuing unexpectedly exploded. All 65 souls on board were lost.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable moon","crusader","stanton ii","crusader industries","daymar","stanton 2b","uee moon","stanton ii moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8454968c-0f69-4a2f-ad5f-5a40455b431d"},
{"id":"daymar-rally","gp":"bZkkq3WWk8","t":"Daymar Rally","k":"history","c":["Sports"],"x":"The Daymar Rally is an annual unsanctioned race that takes place on Daymar every Standard Earth Year (SEY) on [Daymar (Stanton 2b)](gp:VpMGDvX48N), the second moon of [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav). In each race, participants  must pilot ground vehicles to multiple checkpoints and complete set tasks there before they are allowed to cross the finish line. Live fire is allowed after the drivers reach the first checkpoint, which has resulted in multiple injuries and deaths since the first race was held in 2922. Due to the dangerous nature of the race, [Crusader Security](gp:bmNrmYB8MP) strongly discourages people from participating.","g":["daymar","stanton 2b","stanton system","vehicle racing"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a6350cec-7353-407a-8d8b-1c22f21b2e90"},
{"id":"deacon-messer-ii","gp":"0j46m4BYge","t":"Deacon Messer II","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Deacon Messer II (2567-2661) was [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) from 2592 to 2628. The only son of [Ivar I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) and Delia Hassan, Deacon oversaw the [Second Tevarin War (2603-2610)](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv), increased military spending, expanded the powers of the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk), increased minimum sentences for criminals, approved funding increases on exploration and [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) efforts, increased taxes on the wealthy, and decreased taxes on the poor and middle class. He voluntarily stepped down as Imperator in favor of his daughter [Livia III](gp:01dWwaQkrL) in 2628. Deacon took on the role of advisor to the Imperator until the death of Livia's son and his grandson, [Marius IV](gp:RxNxAgrXZz), in 2641. Alongside Livia, he retired from public life entirely in 2643, severing ties with son [Corsen V](gp:0OaB8O6awO). He remained close with his grandchildren throughout his life. A year after his 2661 death, his granddaughter [Illyana VI](gp:bZwQBNmWrL) allegedly had her father Corsen and brother [Gammon](gp:0rxrqgDP12) assassinated.","g":["messer era","uee imperator","messer dynasty","second tevarin war"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2b76b11b-bad6-4df3-ad4b-b16b34fc88ab"},
{"id":"decari","gp":"0qaj3Ygr5q","t":"Decari","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The decari is a type of fungus that produces a large, edible spore pod. It anchors itself to rocks and soil using long, filament-like rhizoids that are capable of regrowing the decari's main body if it is destroyed. When it is ready to reproduce, it creates a fruiting structure that resembles a rock. Eventually, the lightweight pod is released and it blows across the ground, scattering spores as it tumbles. The pods themselves are also capable of becoming new decari.","g":["fungi"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a9ea064b-dab1-4207-9ae8-4754e6f3f5a8"},
{"id":"dssags","gp":"V7gMqgGrln","t":"Deep Space Scanning & AstroGraphical Station","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Human"],"x":"Deep Space Scanning & AstroGraphical Stations (DSSAGS) are dedicated space platforms used by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government to aid in the search for [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY). These turnkey facilities constantly require a minimal crew who collect data and transmit it to the Imperial Cartography Center, where it is interpreted by scientists trained in reading space for signs of jump tunnels. They are located in most inhabited planetary systems across the UEE.","g":["dssags","imperial cartography center (icc)","orbital platform"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dd183d6d-903d-4009-becd-4216411f82e7"},
{"id":"defender","gp":"V3qgm9vdxm","t":"Defender","k":"vehicle","c":["Banu","Spacecraft"],"x":"The Defender is a [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) combat spacecraft that can generally be found escorting their trading caravans. A point defense interceptor, it is equipped with four tachyon cannons and delivers excellent performance in terms of speed and maneuverability. The Banu typically operate as two-person spacecraft. Like many Banu designs, the exact origin of the ship is unknown but the Defender has clearly evolved with a mix of technology acquired from multiple sources, including the Xi'an. Defenders occasionally become available to Human civilians.","g":["light fighter","fighter","banu spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c09f3bd1-10c1-47af-8f30-ffe2e22ce180"},
{"id":"degnous-root","gp":"RX3oJEgrkP","t":"Degnous Root","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"Degnous root is a type of macroalgae that has medical applications when processed. Discovered along the shallow coastlines of [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv) in [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), it was found to contain complex amino acids and was initially used as a dietary supplement. The degnous root has soft flesh that is dark in color and orange and yellow air bladders that vary in size. It thrives in shallow, warm seawater.","g":["algae","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c53dd2e7-b81b-404c-b496-dc848130f2b0"},
{"id":"deimos-sol-4b","gp":"RAXM4zoEvA","t":"Deimos (Sol 4b)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Deimos (Sol 4b) is the second and farthest moon from the surface of [Mars (Sol IV)](gp:Regn8D76xw), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). At only 6.2 kilometers in diameter, it bears a strong resemblance to an asteroid. One leading theory proposes that it originated as a part of a larger asteroid that was hit by another object and shattered.","g":["deimos","sol 4b","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bae9bd8e-8e31-40a2-92e5-fc276d1ef51c"},
{"id":"delamar","gp":"0GxoZnAGrg","t":"Delamar","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"Delamar is an inhabited asteroid located in the [Glaciem ring (Nyx belt alpha)](gp:0Kx8gwkXMP) of the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). In SEY 2655, a group of political dissenters against the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) moved into an abandoned mining facility on Delamar and formed an independent community they named People's Alliance. They called their new settlement [Levski](gp:0dXQqBMAOp) after 19th century revolutionary Vasil Levski from [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB). Delamar is the most densely populated and heavily trafficked location within Nyx, and serves as a hub for many of the miners who continue to work the asteroids within the Glaciem ring for resources.","g":["nyx system","not habitable","asteroid"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ad2e1314-5c45-43fc-8381-5d47ed45e18b"},
{"id":"dell-township","gp":"RkZ9mGOpD4","t":"Dell Township","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Dell Township was the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) settlement on Armitage (Orion III). It was founded shortly after the system was discovered in 2650 as a center for water purification. Over 600 inhabitants of the township were killed in 2681, when the then-unknown [Vanduul raided the planet for supplies](gp:RWwZDmxaXP).","g":["armitage","orion iii","vanduul-human first contact","vanduul territory","towns"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/71a0e23b-21ca-445e-9ff7-c08956ed557f"},
{"id":"dellin","gp":"0OaBKD9Kwk","t":"Dellin","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"Dellin is one of the largest states on [Charon III](gp:RkGGMvDpoz), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Recent economic forecasts list the majority of Dellin's inhabitants as living below the poverty line, but just above minimum requirements from the UEE Common Laws. This may have been one of the key factors in the election of [Tarquin Klast](gp:0dQ4mGDJYd) as the governor, who has introduced controversial legislation that political news outlets claim removes many of the checks and balances that prevent the creation of a dictatorship. In 2944, there was a failed attack designed to oust Klast from power orchestrated by [Acheron](gp:VJOz3gMM85), another state on Charon III. Since then, the two states have been at war. The UEE has declared the planet a conflict zone and monitors the situation.","g":["states","charon iii","tarquin klast"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2532574b-ffb9-4413-9a79-8900642a2e41"},
{"id":"dtn","gp":"VDoPezP7E1","t":"Department of Transportation and Navigation (DTN)","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"The Department of Transportation and Navigation (DTN) is a branch of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government that regulates intersystem travel. Management of space traffic lanes, shipping routes, quantum travel points, and [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) fall under the auspices of the DTN. The Traffic Safety Board (TSB), a subset of the DTN, establishes rules and regulations for flight safety.","g":["traffic safety board (tsb)","uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3a5ac702-cd34-4349-861c-aaf97f134e0f"},
{"id":"derion","gp":"VDzlBAdmA3","t":"Derion","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Derion is a clothing brand that creates high-end business wear. Headquartered on [Mars](gp:Regn8D76xw) (Sol IV) in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE), it was founded by a group of tailors from [Earth](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) (Sol III) who settled in [Port Renatus](gp:RWwZWj9vOZ) during the first wave of immigration after Mars was fully [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). The muted colors, classic cuts, and fine fabrics they personally wove led Derion to become the definition of high-end formal and business wear.","g":["clothing manufacturer","mars","sol iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5b340694-86cd-4fc3-93e5-4473a18be96b"},
{"id":"desmond-fell","gp":"RX3dlQ5KON","t":"Desmond Fell","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Desmond Fell (2846 - 2933) was an explorer, surveyor, and navjumper who is best known for his rediscovery of the [Branaugh system](gp:VJX9mlar4n) in 2877. A graduate of the [University of Lo, New Junction (ULON)](gp:VgEngjy9y3), Fell obtained a dual degree in geotechnology and political discourse to help fulfill his lifelong dream of discovering a planetary system. He was hired as a surveyor for the LFR Mineral Group after graduation, and was ultimately able to purchase an Aurora with his earnings in 2876. During a visit to the [Chronos system](gp:RvlQZKy95l) to view [Synthworld (Chronos III)](gp:bZkyrEPLra), Fell detected an anomaly that led him to an unrecorded [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY). On the other side, Fell found not only a new system, but the body of explorer [Theresa Branaugh](gp:VpMeGzBPyz), who had been missing for four years. Fell reported the existence of the system to the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and named it in honor of Branaugh.","g":["branaugh system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e4f37989-1712-4f44-a579-6d0547948e6a"},
{"id":"developing-system","gp":"V7gMqAvgv2","t":"Developing System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"A Developing system is a planetary system under the protection of [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP). While under this designation, the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) act as stewards and protectors for the system to allow the planets that harbor sentient or potentially sentient life to develop without outside interference. In order to be granted this protected status, the beings in this system must not have yet achieved space flight. Contact with the system's inhabitants, along with [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and mining of any kind, is prohibited.","g":["fair chance act","uee legal definition"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/50ef3b1e-c354-4f15-82d1-2cd5b8bcd0d2"},
{"id":"devil-may-care-productions","gp":"VY4Wm4pAmo","t":"Devil May Care Productions","k":"company","c":["Entertainment","Commerce","Human"],"x":"Devil May Care Productions is a Human entertainment production company founded in 2943 by writers Jaina Tatman and Hadrian Weir to produce Lost Squad. After the success of Lost Squad, the company has begun development on two other unannounced projects. Its offices are located on Terra (Terra III).","g":["production company","lost squad (show)","jania tatman","hadrian weir","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e1f0c75b-eec8-40cf-a127-8c7a1e98ba3d"},
{"id":"dione-sol-6d","gp":"RxnjXkpENz","t":"Dione (Sol 6d)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Dione (Sol 6d) is a moon of [Saturn (Sol VI)](gp:0jGpvn8AOW), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Marked with numerous impact craters and chasmata, it is theorized that Dione went through a period of heavy meteor strikes in the distant past that turned the moon 180 degrees on its axis. After the [Battle of Orion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) resulted in the loss of that system to the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) in SEY 2712, a conspiracy theory alleging that the Vanduul had performed this bombardment emerged on spectrum.","g":["dione","sol 6d","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7c345152-7272-4876-84b0-d8937c75694b"},
{"id":"dmc","gp":"0Gx3BAlr1d","t":"DMC","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"DMC (Denim Manufacture Corporation) is a clothing brand known for its durable pants and outerwear. Famed for its high-quality, reinforced stitching and use of rivets, the company incorporates industrial materials into its fabrics to ensure that they can withstand long periods of constant usage. The company uses a variety of materials other than denim, and is especially known for its line of leather duster coats.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/53c5b55d-c96f-4649-854e-ee1cb9b771ec"},
{"id":"dolivine","gp":"RMNNLQOdaA","t":"Dolivine","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Dolivine is a semi-clear green-colored mineral that is sold as a decorative gemstone. Due to its density and natural resistance to weathering, it is also used as a cutting tool or for other industrial purposes. It came to prominence as a gemstone after [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Illyana Messer VI](gp:bZwQBNmWrL) wore a 45 carat dolivine brooch to her niece [Astrid's](gp:0KnA1D5nQM) wedding in 2690. In its natural state, dolivine most often occurs as dark green bands in rocks.","g":["geology","minerals"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d8509001-f4f3-463e-8f25-c64b49c8f742"},
{"id":"donono","gp":"V8Wq6pLlgr","t":"DoNoNo","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"DoNoNo is a fast fashion clothing brand known for its line of flashy, colorful clubwear. Founded initially as a lingerie company, it expanded into cocktail dresses and shirts when one of its bestselling corsets became popular among nightclub goers as a statement piece. Risqué elements such as mesh, high slits, or leather straps adapted from fetishwear commonly feature in DoNoNo's designs.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/49a4e6f2-5742-426e-9040-fdd8c0fa13f3"},
{"id":"doomsday","gp":"RxNxZ9NxZy","t":"Doomsday","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Doomsday is a Human personal armor manufacturer headquartered in Haven on Tyrol V, United Empire of Earth (UEE). They produce stylized armor and clothing meant to intimidate and terrify opponents on the battlefield. One of their bestselling helmets, the Butcher, was designed to resemble the sun-bleached skull of large, horned animal.","g":["armor manufacturer","haven","tyrol v"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/295f1605-3bd2-4b91-8fae-237ff8671ecd"},
{"id":"doplencyethorphine-dopple","gp":"R9vlWQDAmZ","t":"Doplencyethorphine (Dopple)","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Doplencyethorphine (dopple) is a dissociative drug that creates a feeling of separation from one's surroundings. When medically prescribed and taken in small quantities, doplencyethorphine can be used to treat mood disorders and can help manage anger issues. The street version of the drug, called dopple, is most commonly available in the form of a small jelly cube that is placed under the tongue and allowed to dissolve. Users experience a disconnection from reality, a detachment from emotions, and a sense of serenity. Side effects can include memory loss, panic attacks, paranoia, and psychotic episodes.","g":["doplencyethorphine","dopple","dissociative drug","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ed862e12-e71e-4f41-a031-9fe1bc661332"},
{"id":"dracaena-pura","gp":"01LoDoJ598","t":"Dracaena Pura","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The dracaena pura is a genetically modified plant created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke). to extract pollutants from water. In 2930, Rayari debuted the dracaena pura as a part of their new line of plants meant to aid in [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) a planet. It distributes the toxins it can't safely convert to energy throughout its leaves, growing taller as it does so. Some specimens of the plant have reached nearly 10 meters in height.","g":["rayari inc","trees"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/24c6730d-4768-4257-b720-930b1bbb8ea9"},
{"id":"dragonfly","gp":"VlNPm8MOor","t":"Dragonfly","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Dragonfly is a personal open-canopy space and ground vehicle sold by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). Built to be stored aboard larger spacecraft, it is part of Drake's cooperative web of ships alongside the [Cutlass](gp:R6v8krK71n) and [Caterpillar](gp:VY4WmNG9v6). Dragonflies are used as both ground-based transports and as snub craft supporting operations in space. They are not capable of planetary reentry themselves. Its color variants are Yellowjacket and Black.","g":["drake interplanetary","racing","personal transport","transport","dragonfly yellowjacket","dragonfly black","human vehicle"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/824fd0d1-8baa-4ec9-bc55-56f74d3f2d1e"},
{"id":"drake-interplanetary","gp":"RLMm9KeZed","t":"Drake Interplanetary","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Drake Interplanetary is a spacecraft manufacturer headquartered on [Borea (Magnus II)](gp:R9vGaQPXJN). The fifth largest spacecraft producer in [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE), Drake was founded in SEY 2845 by Jan Dredge to produce the [Cutlass](gp:R6v8krK71n) medium fighter for militia use. Drake has cultivated its image since then to appeal to those seeking less conventional designs. Spacecraft produced by Drake include the [Cutlass](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/cutlass-series) line, the [Caterpillar](gp:VY4WmNG9v6) freighter, the [Dragonfly](gp:VlNPm8MOor) ultralight, the [Buccaneer](gp:VyvYXd1X7a) fighter, the [Herald](gp:VpGEmdYJPA) information runner and the [Vulture](gp:RPDAMBAOr4) salvage ship.","g":["jan dredge","spacecraft manufacturer","borea","magnus ii","vehicle manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8f52bcf4-0e6c-42b0-9d74-981c5262c2f3"},
{"id":"driller","gp":"V3GPzWDO1A","t":"Driller","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Vanduul"],"x":"\"Driller\" is the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Navy military designation for a type of escort and troop carrier operated by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO). A capital ship, it has most often been observed accompanying large-sized [Vanduul Clans](gp:R9vzjxmEBx) during major raids. Declassified military reports indicate that Drillers have multiple turrets and front-facing ship to ship guns that are capable of immense firepower.","g":["escort carrier","carrier","vanduul system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4f83dad0-51e3-4caa-b997-f5833850ecfb"},
{"id":"drop-kings","gp":"RPDeLyzavq","t":"Drop Kings","k":"faction","c":["Illegal Activity","Organizations"],"x":"The Drop Kings are a major criminal syndicate that is active in multiple systems across the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Founded in the SEY 2640s by a group of anti-[Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) activists who fled their homes under threat of retaliation from the Messer government, their earliest recorded crimes were in the [Fora system](gp:bo1PDEgGv2), where they ran blackmarket goods manufactured on [Hyperion (Fora III)](gp:RegWGPlxqy) to [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) via a route through the [Taranis system](gp:RkG1nnXYE4). When they began smuggling goods and people to and from [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) space in the 2690s, they quickly rose to prominence and expanded their network to more systems. \n\nIn the 2740s, they entered the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N) and clashed with the fellow smuggling group the [Headhunters](gp:bZkOavLgjB). Beginning in 2781, the Drop Kings abruptly stopped this conflict and began to focus on smuggling goods across the borders of the UEE, leading historians to speculate that they were involved in transporting [anti-Messer refugees](gp:bE3rKa32P7) to Banu and Xi'an territories. They returned to business as usual in 2799 and launched an attack on [Ruin Station](gp:RX3AzPdnw8), ousting the Headhunters from power and becoming the de-facto rulers of the Pyro system. Control of Pyro passed back and forth between the Drop Kings and the Headhunters until 2912, when the Drop Kings became involved in a feud with the Terra-based Rangda syndicate. Since then, they have dialed back their activities in Pyro but are known to maintain operations in the Fora, [Castra](gp:R4jxkAd8El), and [Elysium](gp:RvlQrKZxPO) systems.","g":["human outlaw factions","pyro outlaw faction","fora outlaw faction","castra outlaw faction","elysium outlaw faction","outlaw factions"],"img":"https://static.robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/upload/87c05f16-b03b-44d3-a58c-fa1cffec04d0"},
{"id":"dyna-lei","gp":"bo1LkZwmX7","t":"Dyna Lei","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Dyna Lei (2833 - 2941) was a fashion designer and businesswoman most noted for founding the brand Dyna Lei. Born in 2833 to a family of textile workers, she began working as apprentice tailor for the clothing brand LaVenti at the age of 16 based on the strength of her portfolio. Three years later, she began to sell clothing of her own design over Spectrum. She used the profits from her sales to open a small fashion boutique in [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv) on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). When one of her gowns was worn by musician Aris Achrekar to the [Elira Awards](gp:bmNrm67NY9) in 2857, Lei's business vastly expanded. Active as a designer until her death in 2941, one of the last pieces she produced was a gown inspired by the coloration of [Kiel IV](gp:V3GOdOLnkp), worn by [Senator](hhttps://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/VaZn8OqaNZ-senate) [Janna Thurville](gp:Var8a27eW2) to the Green Gala for the [Imperial Arts Foundation](gp:RX3Nr11PPk) in 2939.","g":["fashion design"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/52d70c3e-4505-4a04-b057-640d809fab29"},
{"id":"etam","gp":"bo1BDPjodd","t":"E'tam","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Illegal Activity"],"x":"E'tam is a recreational drug that is used by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) to slow body function and sharpen awareness, allowing the user to enter a deep meditative space. Derived from the leaves of the e'tam plant, which are then fermented and sun dried, e'tam is placed in the mouth and the drug is slowly absorbed through the mucus membrane. It is most commonly used by dedicated followers of [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe). In [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), e'tam acts as a stimulant that can cause hyper awareness, increased cognitive function, emotional dysregulation, and hyper focus so strong that users may neglect to eat, sleep, or take care of basic bodily functions. The sale of e'tam is illegal in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE).","g":["stimulant","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/109f76fb-1edc-4572-9294-8a21790ee3aa"},
{"id":"e1-spirit","gp":"RkGDJanKGm","t":"E1 Spirit","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The E1 Spirit is a medium transport spacecraft manufactured by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N). Designed for luxury travel, the six seats in the passenger cabin each have a table and a viewing screen, and are situated next to large portholes that offer panoramic views of the E1's surroundings. The ship's weapon package comes with a twin remote turret, four hard-points, and dual missile racks. Accommodations for up to two crew members can be found behind the cockpit.","g":["transport","passenger transport","crusader industries","human spacecraft","spirit series"]},
{"id":"earth-sol-iii","gp":"Rw1KpMJLZB","t":"Earth (Sol III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Earth (Sol III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The homeworld of [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), it is the home of the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) and the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl), the capital of the UEE, and the focal point of commerce and culture. Corporations and governments stripped Earth of most of its resources before Humans began living on other planets, causing pollution, overcrowding, famine, and widespread death. Parts of Earth have recovered thanks to centuries of careful government management, but the population depends on imports to thrive.","g":["earth","sol iii","habitable","habitable planet","sol system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0cede813-4787-4415-95c6-49687b3cc43c"},
{"id":"eclipse","gp":"0NwpZZm6Gr","t":"Eclipse","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The Eclipse is a strategic bomber developed in SEY 2930 by [Aegis Dynamics]([Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv)) and utilized by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Navy ([UEEN](gp:RPDvKOpdP4)). It was designed to use advanced stealth technology to deliver a payload of torpedoes without triggering electronic early warning systems. Eclipse bombers have been used in raids against enemy capital ships and deployed against stationary ground installations. In 2947, as part of the Militia Mobilization Initiative, a civilian variant of the frame was made available to the general public.","g":["aegis dynamics","stealth bomber","bomber","stealth","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/119f5306-30ad-4f11-ae82-02f4d406f3c0"},
{"id":"eda-terra-3a","gp":"VgEQPE8vBw","t":"Eda (Terra 3a)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Eda (Terra 3a) is the only natural satellite of [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Because it is nearly identical in size to the moon of [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB), its presence in Terra's skies was seen as a sign by early settlers that Terra was meant for [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) habitation. Its close orbit around Terra, however, causes more extreme tides than those found on Earth.","g":["eda","terra 3a","terra moon","terra iii moon","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e33a4969-7ee5-40a9-b69b-f5bd4cbd9805"},
{"id":"eclibre-belt-nexus-belt-alpha","gp":"0qaqyE8yEa","t":"Elcibre Belt (Nexus Belt Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Nexus belt alpha is the sole asteroid belt of the [Nexus system](gp:RWoj8pnGma), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). In the 26th and 27th centuries, it served as a productive center of mining for the [Hathor Group](gp:R6v8Dg8o6a). Most notably, Dean Kellar hid in the Elcibre belt where he abandoned his ship and stole another one during his [famous flight](gp:RxNxDYYJNd) from the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) in 2931.","g":["elcibre belt","nexus belt alpha","asteroid belt","nexus system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6bd04b3b-0560-4a30-a0ac-25ac048699e2"},
{"id":"element-authority","gp":"RXlXm2LpyZ","t":"Element Authority","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Element Authority is a Human personal weapons, EVA suit, and armor retailer with locations throughout the United Empire of Earth (UEE). The company's goal is to serve as a one-stop shop for any personal defense needs. To differentiate itself from its competitors, Element Authority employs Human sales associates as opposed to automatic, computer-operated kiosks in its stores.","g":["weapons retailer","armor retailer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e74367aa-8c06-41bf-bc68-557989646148"},
{"id":"eli-price","gp":"bo1wkzJE41","t":"Eli Price","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Exploration"],"x":"Eli Price (SEY 2560 - 2663) was a Lieutenant in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)\nNavy and a lawyer, most notable for being the official discoverer of the [Oya](gp:0KxGow1ly4)-[Castra](gp:R4jxkAd8El) jump point in 2587. While tracking down a group of outlaws who had been attacking cargo ships in the Castra system, Price staked out a drop point they had been using for their stolen goods. According to his journals, Price watched a ship appear out of thin air and collect the goods. He secretly tracked the ship until it vanished into what he was sure was a previously undiscovered jump point. After successfully navigating to the system, he overheard comm chatter between the outlaws, and found out that they were a group of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) separatists that were raiding ships only when they needed supplies. Though conflicted, he reported what he had found to his superiors. The [Navy](hhttps://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/RPDvKOpdP4-uee-navy) responded by dispatching strike teams to secure the outlaws. When they attempted to flee, the military destroyed their ships. In 2590, Price wrote in his journals that he had been dealing with a constant sense of guilt after his actions directly led to the deaths of so many. He left the military in 2591 and was accepted to law school, and after graduating in 2594, spent the rest of his career as a defense attorney.","g":["oya system","human people"]},
{"id":"elio-harman-aerospace","gp":"Vgg7yZjdGn","t":"Elio-Harman Aerospace","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Elio-Harman Aerospace is a defunct Human spacecraft manufacturer founded in 2456. Elio-Harman's most famous design was the [Stiletto](gp:R4ZG3A66v5) interceptor, one of the first frontline military spacecraft operated by the military. The company went bankrupt in 2568 and its assets were divided among multiple creditors.","g":["spacecraft manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ffe2f7e0-e621-4949-8d4f-94ff31235d74"},
{"id":"elira-awards","gp":"bmNrm67NY9","t":"Elira Awards","k":"culture","c":["Music","Entertainment","Human"],"x":"An Elira Award is an award that recognizes achievement in music. Held since SEY 2803, Elira Awards are presented in a variety of categories annually at a presentation held in [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv), [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). The Elira is one of the most prestigious [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) awards for musicians and the presentation is popular viewing via [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) broadcast. The Elira Awards ceremony includes performances from major musical artists.","g":["music awards","awards and honors","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/86c13c02-c6f5-4753-a6e3-81853601ddf1"},
{"id":"ellis-5a","gp":"0dXKPK7zBJ","t":"Ellis 5a","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Ellis 5a is the first moon of the planet [Noble (Ellis V)](gp:V8W545NrKo), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). To the naked eye, it appears to be softly pink. In 2845, the prominent jewelry company Apgar's debuted a line of pink pearl necklaces inspired by Ellis 5a, made of pearls harvested from oysters cultured on [Green (Ellis III)](gp:RWoNrNeLKP). The clasp of each necklace was created from gold and silver harvested on Ellis 5a.","g":["ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e9b60446-6572-4108-95bf-0e3e1120cc55"},
{"id":"ellis-5b","gp":"V3G5M5oWEr","t":"Ellis 5b","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Ellis 5b is the second moon of [Noble (Ellis V)](gp:V8W545NrKo), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is tidally locked to the planet. Nearly three times larger than its sister moon [Ellis 5a](gp:0dXKPK7zBJ), the light reflected off its pristine white surface is sometimes bright enough that Ellis 5a becomes difficult to see at night. Its opposite side is covered in scars from crater impacts.","g":["ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b96f83b-fdb4-4003-bab2-d3e2a727f3f9"},
{"id":"ellis-belt-alpha","gp":"02k585XkQe","t":"Ellis Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Ellis belt alpha is the only asteroid belt in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Best known as the location of one of the racetracks in the [Murray Cup](gp:bE3r71yZ87), the belt first began to be used as an obstacle course for spacecraft by off-duty workers on the [Green (Ellis III)](gp:RWoNrNeLKP) and [Noble (Ellis V)](gp:V8W545NrKo) [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) projects. These early races became a tradition for inhabitants of the Ellis system, and were later incorporated into the modern day Murray Cup. Today, it is outfitted with many permanent installations used during the races.","g":["ellis system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bbd1aafa-d286-484b-ab90-63c1ec6a7ed1"},
{"id":"ellis-i","gp":"0qaP2PxJw1","t":"Ellis I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ellis I is a protoplanet in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Its scorched surface is dotted with lakes of bubbling lava. Exploration attempts of Ellis I have so far been impossible  due to the protoplanet's proximity to the sun. In 2799, Dab Demirjian became the first person to successfully land a piloted spacecraft on Ellis I by using specialized shielding he developed himself; however, the shielding failed after seven minutes, and Demirijan perished when his ship melted under the sun's unrelenting radiation.","g":["ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/432c1d8f-5107-477e-a21b-19bfb44bdfde"},
{"id":"ellis-ii","gp":"0dXKPKX1j8","t":"Ellis II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ellis II is a terrestrial planet with a thick, high-pressure atmosphere located in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Underneath the swirling clouds that hide its surface is an enormous, planet-wide desert marked with ever-shifting swirls and ridges created by frequent, violent wind storms. If rain is generated in these storms, it burns away before it can hit the ground. Snow made up of evaporated metal has been observed capping some of the planet's mountains.","g":["ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e7025228-abd5-4841-bb7e-2a64c4ce4434"},
{"id":"ellis-system","gp":"RxnBEBWBjQ","t":"Ellis System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Ellis system is a planetary system located in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that consists of thirteen planets, one asteroid belt, and one F-type main sequence star. Most famously home to annual spacecraft race the [Murray Cup](gp:bE3r71yZ87), its three habitable planets are all centers of tourism or scientific interest in their own right. Ellis is also a main thoroughfare for commercial travel and the long-haul transportation of resources to and from the [Sol](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5) and [Terra](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4) systems. Lines to land at the many rest stop stations orbiting the planet [Walleye (Ellis IX)](gp:0n1Ppn9Kr9) can be hours long during Murray Cup season.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/33006fac-f96d-4ca1-a640-3fbfcd6df794"},
{"id":"ellis-vi","gp":"RvlQEQovWr","t":"Ellis VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ellis VI is a terrestrial planet that sits just outside the [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy) of the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Since 2931, it has been used by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) as an experimental [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) site for the development of technology that will allow planets far from their system's sun to someday support Human-friendly atmospheres. Long-term researchers live at Encole Station, a small science lab that sits in geostationary orbit around the planet.","g":["ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e453c62c-aa8b-41a1-a355-beea1d1ea271"},
{"id":"ellis-vii","gp":"bo1PEPNNn2","t":"Ellis VII","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ellis VII is a terrestrial smog planet orbited by two narrow rings of rock and ice in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Although it is located beyond the system's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), the surface of Ellis VII is hot, caused by its dense, dark, and high-pressure atmosphere. Spacecraft entering local orbit are advised to stay in the exosphere in order to avoid corrosion.","g":["ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d29869d1-b350-4549-b387-4dbd988757cf"},
{"id":"ellis-viii","gp":"0GxEdE5qmE","t":"Ellis VIII","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ellis VIII is a planet in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Cold and desolate, the rolling plains of Ellis VIII are coated in thick layers of nitrogen and water ice supplied by a system of active cryovolcanoes. Off-gassing from this ice has produced a thin atmosphere. Many tourists in the system seek out drinking water collected from Ellis VIII, citing its unique mineral content as evidence of superior flavor.","g":["ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ad5478c9-8c12-4c25-b016-fd04d58cfc6d"},
{"id":"ellis-xi","gp":"bZkyPrr5vD","t":"Ellis XI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ellis XI was a planet in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that was famously destroyed in 2943 when its moon collided with it. The moon was completely broken up in the impact, and the planet itself splintered, creating an extremely dense debris field. Astrophysicists speculate that the planet will continue to break up, and will ultimately become the system's second asteroid belt.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","ellis system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9c3e67d0-4ba4-42d9-a4f0-3931d1d255ae"},
{"id":"ellroy-cass","gp":"RegZ7z96Gy","t":"Ellroy Cass","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Ellroy Cass (b. 2919) is a Human artist, actor, dancer, musician, and general celebrity known for his large-scale works that often incorporate sound, visuals, and live performance. The death of actor Jared Yildiz in 2944 after an overdose of Neon he reportedly obtained aboard Cass' [Constellation Phoenix](gp:VyvYqezlqW) marked an escalation in a series of personal struggles in the public eye. Already under scrutiny for a recent stint in a rehabilitation facility, the increased media attention led Cass to a public meltdown in which he attempted to set fire to his vacation home on [Tangaroa (Helios II)](gp:RX3rnQ3XqM). He is a fixture of the tabloid press for his large, frequent parties, substance abuse issues, over-the-top art pieces, lavish purchases, bombastic behavior, and various artistic endeavors.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a682ea96-018a-4567-9d3b-ab4d46b2a114"},
{"id":"elysian-bloom","gp":"VlMnJnLrv5","t":"Elysian Bloom","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"The elysian bloom is a carnivorous plant that was created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke). Designed to alleviate pest problems for farmers on newly [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) worlds, it uses the sticky resins it exudes to attract and trap insects and other small animals. Rayari is currently conducting a long-term study on the elysian bloom's ability to survive in the desert at their research facility in [Reza's Landing](gp:Vgg7jB2YE9), [Vosca (Elysium III)](gp:R9vQWkLNNM).","g":["rayari inc","carnivorous plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/903d4c59-bff8-459c-919b-b807d558dff6"},
{"id":"elysium-i","gp":"bZkyYEAvx8","t":"Elysium I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Elysium I is the closest planet to the sun of the [Elysium system](gp:RvlQrKZxPO), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Tidally locked to its star, the gas giant completes an orbit every six Standard Earth Days (SED). Its highly-diffuse, superheated atmosphere contains clouds of silicates. Astrophysicists speculate that Elysium I formed beyond the frost line of its system, and later migrated inward.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","elysium system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7e8d838e-3c78-4a85-9f4a-ba16effefb28"},
{"id":"elysium-ii","gp":"0ODA5E1ElN","t":"Elysium II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Elysium II is an uninhabited planet in the [Elysium system](gp:RvlQrKZxPO), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Second from its sun, it sits inside the system's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy) and has a fragile atmosphere of carbon dioxide. Thousands of impact craters litter its surface. The largest of these is speculated to have been caused by a collision with a comet around 5 kilometers in diameter.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","elysium system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/929e08d2-398c-4253-820a-c25f458c5033"},
{"id":"elysium-system","gp":"RvlQrKZxPO","t":"Elysium System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human","Tevarin"],"x":"The Elysium system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) made up of an F-type main sequence star, one gas giant, three terrestrial planets, and a dwarf planet. The ancestral home of the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X), Elysium was annexed by the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) government at the end of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM). Tevarin [Warlord Corath'Thal](gp:RkGxWGQ2Qp) launched a campaign against the UEE to take back the system in 2603, sparking the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv). Ultimately, the campaign was not successful, and Elysium remained in possession of the UEE.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a8699b5a-176c-4102-9eca-c675c6c5d980"},
{"id":"elysium-v","gp":"0GxE7eJpng","t":"Elysium V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Elysium V is a dwarf planet that orbits farthest from the sun of the [Elysium system](gp:RvlQrKZxPO), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Although its surface is barren, the crust is rich in water ice, most densely at the poles. Highly reflective patches of frozen brine can be observed twinkling from the bottom of two deep craters along the planet's equator.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","elysium system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5e718789-d085-428e-905a-f681ac7957d6"},
{"id":"emancipation-day","gp":"VDoXz5Kgrx","t":"Emancipation Day","k":"history","c":["Human","Holidays"],"x":"Emancipation Day is a holiday celebrated in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) annually on May 2nd that commemorates the end of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (SEY 2546 - 2792). On this day [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq), the last member of the Messer family to rule the UEE as [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl), was deposed in the aftermath of the [Massacre of Garron II](gp:01dWeqnMr1). When the news of Messer's toppling reached the populace in 2792, there was spontaneous celebration in the streets throughout the UEE. Festivities reoccurred annually, and it was finally established as an official holiday in 2795 under Imperator [Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y). Emancipation Day is especially popular on Earth (Sol III) and [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa).","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7b80ba38-33c3-42e4-81db-38216e003c86"},
{"id":"ecn","gp":"R9vlYMoLnM","t":"Emergency Communication Network (ECN)","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"The Emergency Communication Network, popularly called the ECN, is a government-operated system of communication satellites and space stations in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Designed to facilitate stable communication in a state of emergency, each station has multiple backup power sources and transmitters, ensuring that urgent messages make it to their destinations. They also broadcast over numerous frequencies to avoid jamming. This separation of broadcast spectrums makes the system much more stable in an emergency.","g":["emergency communication network","ecn","communications"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ef034c45-5d2b-4a98-af6a-8a029c8b7073"},
{"id":"emil-quast","gp":"R4jdlJl6oe","t":"Emil Quast","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Emil Quast (b.2888 - present) is an architect and interior designer notable for his work on the Flowhouse, a public assembly building on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) with an organic, curving silhouette. Self-taught, he began his career in Jele City, [Vann (Croshaw  III)](gp:bZkk4l4j2D), where he made waves for his use of wood accents on the walls of his close friend Jiemba Kahlon's art gallery. Jele City's governor hired him to redesign her office, the first in a series of public works that eventually led him to relocate to [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv), Terra. [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) hired Quast to help design the interior of the [Constellation Phoenix](gp:VyvYqezlqW), which debuted to high acclaim in 2944.","g":["constellation phoenix"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2eeffac9-2989-41ac-a700-2e50801cea8f"},
{"id":"emperor-taunuasao-taoyusao","gp":"VYLyPxQnpp","t":"Emperor (Tao'nuasao / Tao'yusao)","k":"faction","c":["Xi'an","Government"],"x":"The Emperor (Tao'nuasao) is the sovereign monarch of the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). It is the duty of the Emperor to make decisions that affect all Xi'an while adhering to the tenets of [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe) and Xi'an law while considering the advice of the [Council of Three](gp:Rw1DPO8v8q). The Emperor also acts as the head of the [Imperial Bureaucracy (Pō't.ōngp.ū)](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ) and ceremonially \"adopts\" all Service members into the Imperial [House](gp:box9JmxvWL) until their Service has ended, symbolizing the unity of the Xi'an people for the collective good. An inherited position, the Emperorship is passed down from mother to daughter in the regnant Xi'an House, or, in uncommon cases, from mother to son. While male Xi'an can become Emperor in their own right, they cannot pass on the position to their descendants. Upon the death or abdication of a male Emperor (Tao'yusao) who has no female relatives, another House is chosen by the Council of Three to take his and his Line's place, and a new Imperial Age begins.","g":["xi'an emperor","tao'nuasao","tao'yusao","xi'an government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9bbaedea-e027-465b-aced-0910370c3789"},
{"id":"emperor-bloom","gp":"R56EXX3QWN","t":"Emperor Bloom","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"###### Emperor Bloom\nThe Emperor Bloom is a member of the genus Plena, of the Tuserac family of plants. It is one of many varieties of flowering plants indigenous to Terra (Terra III) with a solitary flower featuring a conical spiral of petals over the pistil. Its vibrant color, strong scent, and long blooming season have earned it a prominent place in Terran culture.\n \nFound primarily in the tropical regions of Terra, the Emperor Bloom Reserve in the state of Vastac attracts thousands of sightseers every year.\n \n###### Description and Life Cycle\nThe mature plant features a single, thick stem with simple, basal, elliptical leaves. When the plant begins preparing to flower, it develops a dark brown husk coated in brown fuzz that averages 15 cm in length. One by one, the Emperor Bloom drops its leaves as its energy is redirected into incubating the blossom. Finally, the husk turns a deep purple and unfurls into a spectacular, three-tiered flower in showy shades of violet.\n \nIt blooms during the temperate dry season, when average temperatures reach 25 C. The outer petals of the flower drop off when temperatures begin to average above 32 C. The conical spiral of petals in the center harden and darken as the plant develops its seeds. At the height of the dry season, the pods burst open and hundreds of fluffy seeds are picked up by the late-dry winds and propagated to germinate at the beginning of the wet season.\n \n###### Discovery\nIn 2559, a group of early planetary surveyors came across a field of these flowers on the outskirts of what would later become Prime. Specimens were collected and brought back to the settlement, where they were cultivated over centuries to maximize flower size, scent, and brightness of color. Today's domestic Emperor Bloom is larger in size than its wild cousins and has a longer flowering time.\n \n###### Cultural Significance\nThe Emperor Bloom has become an unofficial symbol for Terra's natural beauty. It's celebrated on Terra with the Twilight Festival, which is held every year in Vastac at the start of blooming season. The morning of the festival, ships both airborne and aquatic cross the Zaffre Bay from Prime to reach the vast Emperor Bloom reserve. Temporary viewing areas are made available to attendees so they can enjoy the flowers without accidentally trampling them. Food, music, and games are featured at the festival, along with an outdoor market where attendees can purchase their own Emperor Blooms. Just after sunset, the elected chairman of the festival simultaneously illuminates hundreds of lights that have been staked among the flowers.","g":["terra","terra iii","flowers","vastac","twilight festival"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f75aa449-dc2d-442c-a086-fa4986f3f80f"},
{"id":"emperor-chulee-se-rua","gp":"0QleWjn559","t":"Emperor Ch.ul'ē se Ru'a","k":"people","c":["People","Xi'an"],"x":"Tao'nuasao Ch.ul'ē se Ru'a was the second to last [Emperor](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) of the [First Imperial Age](gp:VDoPeW55W4). As the only daughter of the previous Emperor, there was extensive pressure on her from her House's [Council of Three](gp:Rw1DPO8v8q) to produce as many heirs as possible in order to assure the continuance of the [Ru'a](gp:V3qgaLK82W) line. In MXY I.14568 (SEY 1021 BCE) she successfully gave birth to her son [Se'ang](gp:RWo5gEXjnP), but failed to conceive additional children in spite of repeated attempts. A lifelong lover of animals, she authorized the construction of the nature preserve on [Ko'li (Ē'aluth III)](gp:Vy29gQ3x4Y), and personally oversaw the creation of multiple specialized habitats for animals that had originated on the original Xi'an homeworld, RyiXy'an (Hyoton III). Ch.ul'ē died in a landslide after being caught in an unexpected storm during a visit to [Xi (R.il'a V)](gp:RkGDJnlB2p) at the young age of 162.","g":["ch.ul'ē se ru'a","xi'an emperor","house ru'a","first imperial age","xi'an people"]},
{"id":"emperor-lii-se-kree","gp":"0Qlgxrv6xv","t":"Emperor Lii\" se Kr.ē","k":"people","c":["People"],"x":"Tao'nuasao Lii\" se Kr.ē was the [Emperor](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) of the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) from  MXY III.715 to III.926 (SEY 2372 - 2643), and is the second to last Emperor of the Third Imperial Age. Aunt of the current Emperor [T.uēng se Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo), she was known for ordering the fast buildup of [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military resources along the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO). She held a staunch anti-[Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) stance based on the events surrounding [Xi'an-Human First Contact](gp:R4ZQpYEEvx), and refused to share intelligence about the expanse of the Xi'an Empire after the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) made repeated overtures threatening military action.","g":["lii\" se kr.ē","xi'an emperor","house kr.ē","third imperial age","xi'an people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/294d8b99-a22c-4b2d-b477-60ca50abb10b"},
{"id":"emperor-seang-se-rua","gp":"RWo5gEXjnP","t":"Emperor Se'ang se Ru'a","k":"people","c":["People","Xi'an"],"x":"Tao'yusao Se'ang se Ru'a was the final [Emperor](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) of the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9)\n belonging to the Imperial Line [Ru'a](gp:V3qgaLK82W), the ruling House of the [First Imperial Age](gp:VDoPeW55W4) (MXY I.0 - I.14680 / SEY 19668 - 878 BCE). He was the only son of his mother Tao'nuasao Ch.ul'ē se Ru'a, who died at an unexpectedly young age without further issue, leaving Se'ang the only Ru'a qualified to inherit the crown. Faced with an unprecedented situation, Se'ang worked together with Ru'a's [Council of Three](gp:Rw1DPO8v8q) to devise a method to choose the next Imperial House. Ultimately, the method they devised selected [House Xy.ō](gp:RXlXBrm5o1) as the successor to the throne, and Se'ang voluntarily stepped down to allow Y.ah'a se Xy.ō to ascend as the first Emperor of the [Second Imperial Age](gp:RAdjOk77n7) (MXY II.0 - II.1824 / SEY 878 BCE - SEY 1457 CE). He retired to [R.aip'uāng (Kai'pua II)](gp:Rw1rnY1AYJ) and spent his remaining decades studying Li'tova.","g":["se'ang se ru'a","xi'an emperor","house ru'a","first imperial age","xi'an people"]},
{"id":"emperor-kree","gp":"VaZwmlmPQo","t":"Emperor T.uēng se Kr.ē","k":"people","c":["Xi'an","People"],"x":"Tao'yusao T.uēng se Kr.ē  ([Emperor](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) T.uēng Kr.ē) is the current Emperor of the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Crowned in 2643, Emperor Kr.ē was one of the architects behind the first [resolution](gp:bE3rKrl5z6) to end the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ), along with [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Senator Terrence Akari. He is the last member of the [Kr.ē family](gp:R6v8OZOrP5) who can lawfully assume the title Emperor. A new family will be chosen as the next Imperial House upon his death, and the [Third Imperial Age](gp:R4ZejoYNEY) will end.","g":["t.uēng se kr.ē","akari-kr.ē treaty","third imperial age","xi'an emperor"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/48d68a3a-c91f-4988-ae7f-3f0da3b26c9d"},
{"id":"emperor-yaha-se-xyoo","gp":"0ODxZEPdoZ","t":"Emperor Y.ah'a se Xy.ō","k":"people","c":["People","Xi'an"],"x":"Tao'nuasao Y.ah'a se Xy.ō was the first [Emperor](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) of the [Second Imperial Age](gp:RAdjOk77n7). A food microbiologist, she joined her House's [Council of Three](gp:Rw1DPO8v8q) when she discovered a type of bacteria that enabled quick fermentation of grains and legumes, thus staving off a potential famine on Ka'ua (Hyoton IV). When Xy.ō was selected to succeed [Ru'a](gp:V3qgaLK82W) as the next Imperial House, she was chosen to be Emperor due to her auspicious position as the youngest of three daughters. She partnered with the last Ru'a Emperor [Se'ang](gp:RWo5gEXjnP) to lead the terraformation of [R.aip'uāng (Kai'pua II)](gp:Rw1rnY1AYJ) in honor of the Ru'a family's many millennia of service. During her time on the throne, she championed scientific endeavors that led to an expansion in knowledge of food preservation techniques, and increased the influence of Houses involved in the field of biology.","g":["y.ah'a se xy.ō","xi'an emperor","house xy.ō","second imperial age","xi'an people"]},
{"id":"empire-report","gp":"RwZBqM4K9J","t":"Empire Report","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*Empire Report* is a daily Spectrum news program produced and broadcast by [SSN/CAtv](gp:0QxYwPK88l). Billed as companion to [*SSN/CAtv Nightly News*](gp:bZwQ6AxomO), the two shows coordinate to avoid covering the same topics on a given day. *Empire Report* is typically scheduled for a regular daily time slot although its sets and personnel have been used to broadcast breaking news as needed. Its current hosts are Beck Russum & Alan Nuevo.","g":["news organization","news show","spectrum show","ssn/catv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8be6d562-edd9-4ab7-bea8-e648e4f74b6a"},
{"id":"empires-light-conversion-centers","gp":"0KxqnXDpQ2","t":"Empire's Light Conversion Centers","k":"place","c":["Human","History","Government"],"x":"# Empire's Light Conversion Centers\nThe Empire's Light Conversion Centers of the Charon system were a large network of prisons constructed on Charon III by the [Messers](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/messer-dynasty), starting with [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Livia Messer III](gp:01dWwaQkrL). These maximum-security facilities were reputed to be the most secure in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and were used to house political dissidents opposed to the [Messer regime](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo). Following the [fall of the Messers](gp:bE3rKa32P7) in 2792, the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) of Charon III ordered that the prisons be torn down and published evidence of previously unproven atrocities committed against the prisoners by the former government. In the subsequent public uproar, Charon III voted to renounce its UEE recognition.\n\n# Foundation\nShortly after Livia Messer III ascended to Imperator in 2628, she presented a proposal to the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) to build a special maximum-security prison under the sole jurisdiction of the Imperator in the sparsely populated state of [Dellin](gp:0OaBKD9Kwk) on Charon III. The project would kickstart the struggling economy with new jobs and an influx of government funds. The Senate granted near-unanimous approval.\n\nThe first prison, completed in 2630, injected enough money into the economy that the population of Charon III sharply rose. By the time Imperator [Corsen Messer V](gp:0OaB8O6awO) ascended in 2643, the once-rural colony in Dellin had become an urbanized center of commerce based around Livia's prison. Corsen ordered the construction of more facilities in Dellin and its neighboring state [Acheron](gp:VJOz3gMM85) after a meeting with the Governors Council of Charon III in 2644. The largest of these, Orville, became the central processing center for all new prisoners. The collective of facilities was named the Empire's Light Conversion Centers (ELCC). During this time, Charon III's economy boomed. In 2670, Corsen sent a decree to the Senate ordering the recognition of Charon III. A former Representative of Dellin, Gwen Czukay, was sworn in as the planet's first Senator and the world was officially recognized under its new name, Haros.\n\n# Life in the Prisons\nThe largest group of prisoners were political dissidents. These included deserters from the military, [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) sympathizers, former members of the press, protestors, social organizers, violent agitators, and even politicians. Anyone who acted or spoke against the edicts of the Messer government was in danger of being imprisoned on Haros. Convictions weren't necessary; being arrested for a political crime was enough to put someone in Orville, ostensibly to await a fair trial. Many died there, waiting for hearings that were never granted. Contact was not allowed with the outside world.\n\nPrisoners were put to work producing components for the UEE military or low-cost goods to be used by public welfare programs. Their meals were bland but nutritionally complete, and medical care was available to those who took ill so that they could continue to work until they died of old age or exhaustion. When [Astrid Messer VII](gp:0KnA1D5nQM) ascended to Imperator in 2697, standards of living in the ELCCs, already poor, plummeted. Funds meant for prisoner welfare were redirected to military resources. Malnutrition, dehydration, exhaustion, and disease became the leading causes of death.\n\nUnder [Samuel Messer VIII](gp:RkZ9W2L2NB), who ousted Astrid from power in 2701, a new decree set interment limits so that old-age prisoners would be killed to make room for new ones. The dead were interred in mass graves in the Dellin desert.\n\nRumors about the deplorable conditions in the ELCCs began to spread among the people of Haros, though no hard evidence could be found. Any workers suspected of leaking information were themselves at risk of imprisonment and all civilian protesters were incarcerated or killed, eventually quelling any kind of organized protest against the prisons. In 2751, the military began testing bioweapons on segments of Orville's populace. Bodies buried in the desert leached chemicals and radiation into the already poor soil, fueling a new collective action among the populace of Haros. Though any dissent was brutally suppressed, protests increased in frequency for the following few decades.\n\n# Liberation\nWhen news of Imperator [Linton Messer XI's](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) death in 2792 reached the populace of Haros, they stormed the prisons, liberating those inside. They arrested or killed any guards who hadn't fled and broke into offices previously sealed off to the public, recovering centuries of documentation on acts of torture, murder, and other atrocities conducted by those who ran and guarded the prisons. First-hand accounts from the formerly incarcerated were compiled and sent to media organizations across the UEE. Senator Constance Whittlefield of Haros was arrested on charges of fraud. In 2795, the planet voted to renounce their recognition of the UEE and revert to their former designation of Charon III.\n\nEven after the Messers were permanently ousted from power and a new, progressive government reformed under Imperator [Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y), Charon III refused to rejoin the UEE, citing their forced participation in crimes against Humanity as reason enough to permanently remain independent. The government then razed the prisons to the ground. Anti-UEE sentiment, common on Charon III, continues to be especially strong in Dellin.","g":["charon iii","messer era","uee prisons","human history","messer era prisons of charon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4689158b-ae69-4ef2-899c-8e68179f6f16"},
{"id":"endeavor","gp":"RXlXZ6Pw9N","t":"Endeavor","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Endeavor is a research spacecraft platform developed by [MISC](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) with a modular back end designed to be adapted to multiple roles. A capital-class spacecraft, can be built to include research labs, spacecraft docking bays, biodomes, hospital facilities, and additional fuel storage. The front end can be detached from the rest of the vessel and autonomously piloted. Popular configurations include the Discovery-class science ship, Hope-class hospital ship and Olympic-class agricultural research ship.","g":["heavy science","misc","human spacecraft","capital ship"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/032e2618-877c-4186-b0bb-85958ab89d21"},
{"id":"energy-shield","gp":"V8WaX7BnDD","t":"Energy Shield","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"An energy shield is a barrier that protects an area from energy attacks. Normally invisible to the naked eye, it is projected from a shield generator through a series of emitters that absorbs and dissipates incoming blasts from energy weapons. If a shield is struck too many times, it can overload and fail. Energy shields are able to slow projectile weaponry, thus reducing potential damage, but cannot prevent an impact from landing. Utilizing similar technology, energy shields can also be used to prevent the escape of gas from an environment. In this context, they are known as air shields.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f56e5571-b6e0-4b82-bc65-897cc7700210"},
{"id":"ent","gp":"V3qgoDwMJ2","t":"Entertainment Nine Transmission (ENT)","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"Entertainment Nine Transmission (ENT) is a Spectrum broadcast network that focuses on live and scripted entertainment programming intended to appeal to Humans between the ages of 18 and 34. The network was acquired by [ArcCorp](gp:0dQ47zYd6O) in 2873 but has not been otherwise rebranded. In 2908, ENT acquired the assets of short-lived competitor RealCom, including the Spectrum program *Fake Outs*.","g":["spectrum","realcom","spectrum network","arccorp (corporation)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/44fc2d56-997f-4a87-9721-2517c7c2745b"},
{"id":"environment-suits","gp":"01LxzZ6418","t":"Environment Suits","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Environment suits, also called exploration suits, are a type of body armor designed to withstand extreme environments, such as those with life-threatening heat and cold. Many are built with advanced sensors that automatically adjust internal conditions so that the wearer's body temperature remains stable. To maintain this level of protection, they are fully sealed and must utilize their own oxygen supply. Advanced forms of these types of suits can be worn in corrosive atmospheres.","g":["environment suit","exploration suit","body armor"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a63c812d-ed06-428f-8a07-0ee3160017c9"},
{"id":"epheet-virgil-1c","gp":"R9vlBkO17z","t":"Epheet (Virgil 1c)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Epheet (Virgil 1c) is the third moon from [Cyrene (Virgil I)](gp:VlMBNGnxK5), [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). The smallest of the three moons, it was nicknamed \"little brother\" for appearing to follow the other two moons across the sky. During the [Fall of Virgil](gp:box5moyeoZ), it was damaged by debris and stray bombs, and is covered in impact craters and wreckage from fallen ships.","g":["epheet","virgil 1c","virgil system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/397bac33-4305-4724-b616-75e29130440d"},
{"id":"equivalency","gp":"Vgg7YGdQDY","t":"Equivalency","k":"culture","c":["Education","Human"],"x":"# EQUIVALENCY\n\nAn Equivalency is a certification awarded to people in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) upon completion of their secondary education. It can be earned through the completion of an upper or full secondary UEE-certified education program or through passing a group of subject tests issued by the UEE government. All [civilians](gp:Vgg7rq5J73) in the UEE must earn their Equivalency in order to pursue post-secondary education, enter the armed services, or earn full [Citizenship](gp:RLMmop8rkr). \n\n# OVERVIEW\nAs outlined by the Common Laws, all people born in the UEE have the right to an education. Between ages 13 to 14, the majority of students in the UEE begin their secondary education at public schools overseen by teachers employed by a planet's [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3). Classroom size and teaching style vary from planet to planet, but all students are required to complete a standardized exam that has been standardized according to UEE educational requirements. Most students are awarded their Equivalency between ages 17 and 18.    \n\nPeople in the UEE who don't have access to planet or colony-provided secondary education are able to complete their secondary education programs through the same educational programs that are provided to public school students via [Glas](gp:01dW3alkmB) or computer system. Rural students often complete their education through [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q)-guided learning programs. Without a teacher to set the pace, provide lectures, or to address questions, self-guided students are free to achieve Equivalency whenever they have completed their program. \n\nPrivate and military academies also offer courses in secondary education. The teacher- to- student ratio in these academies is generally smaller than that of public schools, and the education is more personalized. However, these courses are not government provided. All students must pay tuition, either out of pocket or through grants and scholarships. \n\n# HISTORY\n\nDuring the [Human Colonial Expansion Era](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm) (2380 - 2530), secondary education was required by law for all children born within the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO). As more planets were discovered and colonized, the law became difficult to enforce. Children born to the first settlers of early colony worlds who could not be sent back to more developed parts of the UNE for their education were homeschooled, if they were schooled at all. To address this gap in education, in 2464 the UNE released a standardized set of computer-based learning modules called the Educational Equivalency Curriculum (EEC). These modules replaced in-person education on worlds where teachers and schools were not yet available. Those who successfully completed the program were awarded an Educational Equivalency Degree (EED), or Equivalency, which certified that the holder had completed all secondary-level education requirements under UNE law.\n\nThe Equivalency was intended to be a temporary replacement for in-person education until colony worlds established stable local governments. However, as intersystem expansion continued, more and more [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) completed their secondary education via EEC. When the Common Laws were established in 2526, the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) designated the EEC as the standardized secondary education curriculum. The provision of a formalized education and offering Equivalency exams became the responsibility of all local governments. \n\nDuring the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792), the EEC was edited multiple times to indoctrinate the populace into pro-Messer ideology. Xenology and sociology modules were increasingly seeded with anti-alien, pro-Human thought. The history module was especially edited; key events in [Ivar Messer's](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) rise to power were presented as the plans of aliens seeking to destabilize the government. Events directly perpetrated by the Messers or their agents that could not be blamed on aliens, such as military action against Human-led protests, were not taught at all. \n\nFollowing the [fall](gp:bE3rKa32P7) of [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) in 2792, all EEC modules were recalled by the new government and were completely revised. Secondary school was suspended until a new version of the EEC with a detailed history on the Messer Era was released in 2794. \n\nThe EEC is updated and revised once every ten years.","g":["secondary education","uee education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8d25e65e-47f4-4df6-8e02-cac4dd55439d"},
{"id":"ergo-nemo-iii","gp":"VlMYrYzwre","t":"Ergo (Nemo III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Ergo (Nemo III) is an inhabited ocean planet in the [Nemo system](gp:R6d454E3Pw), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Although today there is no indigenous life on the planet, the vast quantities of oil under its oceans suggests that at one point it supported an ecosystem of animals and plants. Paleontologists theorize that a mass extinction event took place roughly 300 million SEY ago. Because of the relative lack of land, the majority of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) settlements on the planet are situated on artificial islands and floating platforms. Oil and tourism are the main industries on Ergo. One of its main attractions is the [planet's moon](gp:RX3jvjEBZq), nicknamed the \"Space Whale\" for its supposed resemblance to a whale, a large aquatic animal native to Earth (Sol III).","g":["ergo","nemo iii","nemo system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6a22755e-07ca-44a6-84e9-4d7eecb4d988"},
{"id":"eri-city","gp":"VgEvqvgd9w","t":"Eri City","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Eri City is the capital of [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN), [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Once a center of military power during the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793), the infrastructure abandoned by the armed forces when they left Kiel after tensions cooled are now being utilized by major aerospace corporations such as [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). Some buildings have been torn down and replaced with city parks, and others have been converted to civilian apartments. One major renovation project was the expansive convention hall built near the city's center that has been home to the Intergalactic Aerospace Expo since 2916. A culture of fine dining developed after Severus was recognized in 2937, and the city has become a top destination for gourmet food enthusiasts.","g":["severus","kiel iii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/afc0a70a-b0c9-441d-bcdf-ed8aacb960db"},
{"id":"eria-quint","gp":"V7gMqNgeOa","t":"Eria Quint","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Eria Quint (2901-present) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) journalist, debate show anchor, and political analyst. She is the current host of the Spectrum news debate program [Showdown!](gp:RwZBw4Lrxz) Before she took over in 2935, she was a political reporter for the *Terra Gazette*.","g":["showdown!"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d5fc8b5d-e56f-4cc8-af72-44d6d1c0f132"},
{"id":"erin-toi","gp":"R4ZG3NxM7Y","t":"Erin Toi","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Erin Toi (SEY 2746 – 2873) was a politician and author elected as a [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) for [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) and the first Imperator of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) to serve after the end of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792). During her time in office, she oversaw the creation and implementation of the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP), the war crimes tribunals of former Messer agents, the [Perry Line Pact](gp:0Gx9GdvqAQ), the restoration of the [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) system, and other major revisions to the UEE government. She left office in 2801.","g":["uee imperator","messer era","fair chance act","perry line pact"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8121caed-3af3-4ccb-a11b-ac6e603effa6"},
{"id":"ermer-family-farms","gp":"bEzzvoGw9J","t":"Ermer Family Farms","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Ermer Family Farms is a commercial dairy owned and operated by the Ermer family, based on Keene (Kilian VII). Founded in 2923, the dairy first rose to prominence at the [Najita](gp:VgEElmgYm3) Dessert Fest 2931, where it debuted one of its most popular varieties, lunes ice cream. The company soon expanded their dairy to include an ice cream manufacturing facility and began to offer their ice creams across the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Lunes, chibanzoo, chocolate, and coffee are among Ermer Family Farms' bestselling flavors.","g":["food company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/13c5e7d0-e16b-41d5-bcb2-659effb48aa6"},
{"id":"erna-virgil-3a","gp":"0qaBnw7AjA","t":"Erna (Virgil 3a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Erna (Virgil 3a) is the first moon from [Virgil III](gp:V8WagLl2Nx), [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Partially coated in water ice, the parts of its surface that are uncovered are rife with deep craters and long, steep, and deep chasmata. Some of its cliffs reveal dark layers alternating with lighter layers, suggesting that in the past Erna was geologically active.","g":["erna","virgil 3a","virgil system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/def4bb49-a8c8-489f-9036-c74d20c725ac"},
{"id":"ernst-bishop","gp":"ReJaavPB3k","t":"Ernst Bishop","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Ernst Bishop (SEY 2880 - present) is an Admiral in the [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), currently serving as the commander of the 65th Battle Group, 2nd Fleet since 9 February 2939. He previously served as commander of the 6th Battle Group. He was confirmed by the UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) as an Admiral in 2930, after being nominated for the position by [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) Mikkel Sheriden. Bishop commanded the 65th Battle Group during the [Battle of Vega II](gp:0Gz5mkprmg).","g":["uee navy"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/03056700-dd50-42d1-b7ad-97c269be6423"},
{"id":"errol-navis","gp":"bZkAvg8BPE","t":"Errol Navis","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Exploration"],"x":"Errol Navis (2822 - 2931) was an accountant and amateur explorer best known for his 2861 discovery of the [Oso system](gp:bZkAMEarPd). Born on [Carteyna (Cano II)](gp:RX34BrgYND) to two geoengineers, he became an accountant at [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA) in 2843 after completing a mathematics degree. Later attributed to a childhood spent in a series of confined, environmentally-controlled bases, Navis described himself as harboring a strong desire to live in a world with open skies and a breathable atmosphere. When Shubin denied his transfer request to [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), Navis purchased a small ship, which he used to take himself and his young daughter Oso on weekend trips to exotic locations. During one of these trips, his scanners picked up an anomaly in the outskirts of the [Castra system](gp:R4jxkAd8El) that turned out to be a jump point to an undiscovered system. He used the reward money from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government to buy a home on Terra and start a business as an accounting consultant.","g":["carteyna","cano ii","oso system","human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fdd66ca3-2f6f-4a11-ad6c-da5e82f22c48"},
{"id":"escar-limited","gp":"Vy2j7Z1MNz","t":"Escar Limited","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Escar Limited is a casualwear clothing brand that is known for creating comfortable shirts and pants. A direct competitor to [City Lights](gp:01LjekGnv1), Escar Limited was founded by former employees of the rival company who wanted to incorporate more creativity into their designs. Their pieces typically utilize mixes of textiles and complicated seams to create visual interest.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d6859447-8e16-4f52-9c08-cc0f84532206"},
{"id":"esperia","gp":"0OaBKL7wlv","t":"Esperia","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Esperia is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) spacecraft manufacturer that adapts, reproduces, and sells existing spacecraft designs. The company was founded in 2873 by Jovi and Theo Ingstrom, brothers interested in preserving spacecraft-building history. Esperia's current lineup of spacecraft reproductions includes copies of the [Vanduul Blade](gp:RegdeBENkw), [Glaive](gp:bo1dozJpB2), and [Scythe](gp:0qakL3mmmq) and an updated model of the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X)[Prowler](gp:02BQOJQQP7) dropship. The [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) makes use of Esperia's replica spacecraft for testing and for aggressor training their combat pilots.","g":["spacecraft manufacturer","battle of orion","jovi ingstrom","theo ingstrom","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f3d12e41-6a2a-4cb2-910a-92dd8e1f6917"},
{"id":"essosouli","gp":"R6v8kxEPBD","t":"Essosouli","k":"culture","c":["Banu"],"x":"An Essosouli is someone who has achieved the highest social and political rank within their [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron). Essosouli are often the most skilled artisans in their Souli, or the ones who have accumulated the most wealth over time. The position of Essosouli can be attained through a variety of means, not limited to popular election, appointment by another Essosouli, assassination of another Essosouli, or bribery of an Essosouli. Upon Divestment, Essosouli retire and their Souli either re-organizes or disbands.","g":["souli","banu sociopolitics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/de9b4198-cd14-49ff-8894-de80c8261b2d"},
{"id":"etos-osiris-i","gp":"RAXPPX7g77","t":"Etos (Osiris I)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"Etos is the first planet from the sun of the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Osiris system](gp:0qaJeqWBZD). Located on the innermost edge of the green band, it has a natural oxygen-nitrogen atmosphere and is inhabited by countless species, one of which, the [Phare's Ape](gp:RX3Krj8Mzq), shows strong evidence of sapience. Nearly all the animals on Etos live underground, in an extensive cave system that reaches down to the planet's mantle. While travel to the planet is prohibited, research teams are occasionally dispatched there to observe life in the caves.","g":["etos","osiris i","osiris system","habitable","habitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b11e6c7a-5a22-4ebf-a69b-178e94ef5d65"},
{"id":"europa-5b","gp":"0jGNWPN8Ln","t":"Europa (Sol 5b)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Europa (Sol 5b) is a moon of [Jupiter (Sol V)](gp:Vy2OMo22wz), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Coated with a sheet of water ice that hides a brackish ocean, its surface is crisscrossed with vast cracks that appear when tidal heating induces too much stress upon it. In SEY 2431, single-celled organisms were discovered living under the ice. Multiple institutes of higher learning maintain permanent bases on Europa that they use to study these creatures.","g":["europa","sol 5b","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","uee moon","sol system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/70b98ade-a228-4e72-b41d-cbb1c8cc8109"},
{"id":"euterpe-stanton-4c","gp":"02kBNLWB33","t":"Euterpe (Stanton 4c)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Euterpe is the third and smallest moon of [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1), named for the ancient Earth (Sol III) muse of music. Largely covered by ice sheets and frozen oceans of water, the landscape of the moon is dotted with pillars of rock formations that researchers theorize are ancient cores of extinct volcanoes. Geological evidence suggests that Euterpe was once temperate.","g":["euterpe","stanton 4c","microtech moon","stanton iv moon","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8169573c-6826-459b-a28c-d71c04fe1e19"},
{"id":"evalight","gp":"VYL3Bd1WJm","t":"EvaLight","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"EvaLight is a clothing brand that incorporates technology into its designs. Utilizing creative cuts, mixed colors, shiny fabrics, and light-up elements to give its pieces a futuristic feel, the company advertises itself as anti-establishment, often producing pieces that directly lampoon high fashion. Despite its messaging, EvaLight is not popular among those who consider themselves true members of the counterculture.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e7b76240-3462-40cc-bf15-5051867068f6"},
{"id":"everline-structures-incorporated","gp":"0jGGy3m6oK","t":"Everline Structures Incorporated","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Everline Structures Incorporated is a [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of [Housing Exchange (HEX)](gp:bmN4vB4rzQ) stations, affordable housing with commercial spaces that are built into hollowed-out asteroids. Although the company offers an extended contract to perform maintenance on their products for ten Standard Earth Years, most businesses and individuals that purchase HEXes opt out of the extra cost and abandon the stations when they become too expensive to repair. Stations that have been discarded by their owners are common throughout the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), especially in areas once used for mining purposes. Abandoned HEX stations are often repurposed as by squatters housing or utilized as bases for those who wish to conduct business outside of [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) law.","g":["housing manufacture","prefabricated housing"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8d225069-635e-4528-aee6-10f456eb0c52"},
{"id":"everus-harbor","gp":"VgEEe9Zpjk","t":"Everus Harbor","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"Everus Harbor is a space station that orbits the planet [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL) above the city of [Lorville](gp:Rw1ZlJNE36). Owned and operated by [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ), it is the primary port of call for all large-scale incoming and outgoing cargo from Lorville. Private traders are known to buy and sell commodities on Everus Harbor.","g":["space station","stanton system","hurston dynamics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5eb42276-9e2a-460f-b4ab-dfb44ff384ee"},
{"id":"expanse","gp":"RMNqLEBxe8","t":"Expanse","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Expanse is a refinery spacecraft manufactured by [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/misc) (MISC). The engineering team at MISC developed the Expanse as a complementary vessel to the [Prospector](gp:0QxYA5BPGj) mining ship. Outfitted with a suite of reactors, the Expanse can process and refine a wide variety of raw materials. Each Expanse is built with cargo pod mounts, allowing it to easily collect ore pods that have been filled by other ships.","g":["refinery","mining","misc","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/92da61da-8135-4fea-b2a5-d071a496a98e"},
{"id":"F7A-Hornet","gp":"RXlXgwDlDk","t":"F7A Hornet","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The F7A Hornet is a single-seat space fighter developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). It is the Navy's current baseline space superiority fighter and is deployed across the Empire aboard all spacecraft carriers. Hornets are used for a variety of missions including combat air patrol, interception, ground attack, reconnaissance in force, escort and strike operations. Anvil also builds a line of civilian Hornet spacecraft adapted from the same frame, the [F7C Hornet](gp:VggevxyPA9).","g":["anvil aerospace","medium fighter","hornet","fighter","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a1056678-b4ab-4562-adeb-ef772435dd00"},
{"id":"f7c-hornet","gp":"VggevxyPA9","t":"F7C Hornet","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The F7C Hornet is a civilian variant of the [F7A Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) space superiority fighter by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). Introduced in 2923 after the F7A had a distinguished period of service in the United Empire of Earth Navy, the F7C was the first ship released by Anvil for civilian use. To keep the ship compliant with UEE military secrecy laws, Anvil replaced 60% of the existing internal hardware systems of the F7A, but made no changes to the frame. Anvil saw a significant spike in sales after the F7C's debut, leading the company to plan further civilian additions to its ship catalog.","g":["anvil aerospace","human spacecraft","fighter","medium fighter","hornet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ae0d6bea-6c28-4d3d-bbfe-20bea4a9e6d0"},
{"id":"f7c-hornet-wildfire","gp":"R6v8K4rp3e","t":"F7C Hornet Wildfire","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The F7C Hornet Wildfire is a limited-edition medium fighter developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the civilian market. [*Arena Commander*](gp:VyvY5LQXd6) creators Original Systems partnered with Anvil to design the Wildfire in honor of pilot Aria Reilly for her distinguished service with United Empire of Earth Navy Squadron 42. The Wildfire's custom livery is not available for any other ship in Anvil's catalog.","g":["hornet","anvil aerospace","original systems","fighter","medium fighter","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c6f608a2-0f6c-4a3d-8dc5-43c33651f6aa"},
{"id":"f7c-m-super-hornet","gp":"VlNP5d1ow4","t":"F7C-M Super Hornet","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The F7C-M Super Hornet is a civilian variant of the [F7A Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) space superiority fighter developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). Designed to mirror the military F7A Hornet as closely as possible using equipment and materials available on the civilian market, the F7C-M's overall modularity is reduced by the return of a military-style turret amidship. Super Hornets are produced in lower numbers than the standard model. They are popular among mercenaries and bounty hunters.","g":["super hornet","hornet","medium fighter","anvil aerospace","fighter","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ba57c9e1-b042-49ed-bffd-1fae9d52a64f"},
{"id":"f7c-m-super-hornet-heartseeker","gp":"R4ZGapk41Y","t":"F7C-M Super Hornet Heartseeker","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The F7C-M Super Hornet Heartseeker is a limited-edition medium fighter developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the civilian market. Based on the [Super Hornet's](gp:VlNP5d1ow4) frame, the Heartseeker is outfitted with near military-spec components along with four laser cannons designed by [Behring](gp:0n9vZ4GpQn). Anvil markets the Heartseeker as the ideal ship for combat enthusiasts.","g":["hornet","super hornet","fighter","medium fighter","anvil aerospace","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7596c874-c1fe-44a0-8c76-327aa29525eb"},
{"id":"f7c-r-hornet-tracker","gp":"0NwpYZZ5jg","t":"F7C-R Hornet Tracker","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The F7C-R Hornet Tracker is a civilian variant of the [F7A Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) space superiority fighter developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). It has been modified from the standard civilian model Hornet with the addition of an advanced scanner suite. Trackers can serve in a variety of roles, such as command and control assets for militia and mercenary units and as fighter escorts on anti-piracy missions. Explorers use the improved computer capacities for charting and scanning purposes.","g":["pathfinder","hornet","anvil aerospace","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bebeb67c-cd24-4945-ad61-21bca93da83f"},
{"id":"f7c-s-hornet-ghost","gp":"VlNP5dG8q7","t":"F7C-S Hornet Ghost","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The F7C-S Hornet Ghost is a civilian variant of the [F7A Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) space superiority fighter developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). Built with Void armor, low-draw weapons, and low-emissions drives, the Hornet Ghost is the stealth fighter of the civilianized Hornet lineup. It trades some offensive capacity for the technology to diminish its signature from standard sensors, but can still be used as a dogfighter. Ghosts are utilized by mercenaries charged with strike operations and by data runners who will need to fight if identified.","g":["stealth fighter","hornet","anvil aerospace","fighter","stealth","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7b8ebaaf-9a0e-4c82-bea7-785fba4cb736"},
{"id":"f8a-lightning","gp":"bZwQ7r6nkE","t":"F8A Lightning","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The F8A Lightning is a next-generation, single-seat, triple-thruster space superiority heavy fighter developed for the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN) by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). Built as a successor to the[ F7A Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) currently utilized by the UEE military, the F8 was specifically designed as a match for the latest Vanduul fighters. It is more maneuverable and heavily armed than its predecessor. Use of the Lightning is restricted to elite UEEN squadrons, though it is expected to see widespread adoption over the next decade.","g":["anvil aerospace","fighter","heavy fighter","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/07841eb5-c02a-49b6-a422-2fc5449f8580"},
{"id":"f8c-lightning","gp":"0Gz5LW2ekd","t":"F8C Lightning","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The F8C Lightning is a civilian variation of the [F8A Lightning](gp:bZwQ7r6nkE) space superiority fighter developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). It closely mimics the military specs of the original F8A, and has been used in lines of defense against Vanduul invaders. It was made available in extremely limited numbers to the civilian market by Anvil to celebrate the debut of the F8A in the United Empire of Earth Navy.","g":["anvil aerospace","fighter","heavy fighter","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ddd08bc2-dd7e-42a8-ac9f-00d33d5c4b36"},
{"id":"fair-chance-act","gp":"RXlXmnaYGP","t":"Fair Chance Act","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The Fair Chance Act is a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) law passed by the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) in 2795, in the wake of the [Massacre of Garron II](gp:01dWeqnMr1) (2792). Sponsored by [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y), it created a new status for planetary systems, Developing system, and added several protections to said systems in order to foster the development of potentially new civilizations. One or more planets in a given system must harbor sentient or potentially sentient life in order to be declared [Developing](gp:V7gMqAvgv2). Contact with the system's inhabitants, [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), and mining are prohibited in order to shield the inhabitants from any interference under the assumption that once they grow to the point of space travel, they can be officially contacted.","g":["erin toi","laws","massacre of garron ii","uee law"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/007efd7f-9183-4e76-9059-144ce254fb74"},
{"id":"fairo-pyro-5d","gp":"RL6e8GzD5r","t":"Fairo (Pyro 5d)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Fairo is the fourth moon from the gas giant [Pyro V](gp:RAXv9Yeqay), [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). A hotbed of seismic activity, Fairo experiences frequent earthquakes that disturb its deep oceans of brackish water. The moon has an unusual ecosystem that thrives both on the surface and under the sea, supported by the carbon dioxide and nitrogen in Fairo's dense atmosphere","g":["fairo","pyro 5d","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon","pyro system"]},
{"id":"fall-of-caliban","gp":"0Gz5DNryvE","t":"Fall of Caliban","k":"history","c":["History","Military","Human","Vanduul"],"x":"# FALL OF CALIBAN\n\nOn 7 July 2884 SEY, a [Vanduul Clan](gp:R9vzjxmEBx) led by a [Kingship](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm) launched a surprise attack on the moderately-populated planet [Crion (Caliban II)](gp:bEzvPwYZ96). The [89th UEE Navy Logistic Support Squadron](gp:0Gz5BNmPqo) were the only military forces in system at the time of the attack. They managed to hold off the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) for two days, allowing much of the planet's population to escape at the cost of nearly the entire squadron. [Naval](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) reinforcements arrived on the third day to engage the full Vanduul fleet, but they were unable to hold out against the onslaught. On 23 July 2884, after heavy casualties, Crion and the rest of the [Caliban system](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m) were lost to the Vanduul. In honor of their sacrifice, the 89th Squadron was retired, earning them the nickname \"the Lost Squad.\" This battle marked the last time a [Kingship](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm) was spotted by [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) forces until the [Battle of Vega II](gp:0Gz5mkprmg) in 2945.\n\n# PRELUDE TO BATTLE\nSmall [Vanduul raiding parties](gp:Rw1gdnOKBp) first began attacking Caliban in 2739, during the latter years of the [Messer era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo). While the initial raid sparked fear in the system's inhabitants, causing a brief population drain, subsequent skirmishes were largely casualty-free. As raids continued to occur at a steady rate of between two and five per year, the UEE installed a small [naval](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) presence in Caliban along with system-wide perimeter sensors. The people of Crion saw this response as inadequate; political activism spiked among the populace, but the [Messers](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/messer-dynasty) sent no more aid.\n\nDuring the [fall](gp:bE3rKa32P7) of the Messer regime in 2792, the military presence in Caliban was pulled away from the system to repress mass civilian uprisings elsewhere. A medium-sized Vanduul Clan launched a raid on the largely undefended system, which claimed over one hundred lives. The newly formed post-Messer UEE government ordered the 31st Battle Group to Caliban to fend off the invasion. Their efforts were successful in stopping the raid from spiraling into something much deadlier.\n\nSubsequent Vanduul raids dropped down to previously established levels of roughly five per year, finally peaking in 2859 when a single large Clan clashed with the 31st Battle Group in the system's asteroid belt. This was the last Vanduul raid until 2884. In 2870, the 31st was assigned elsewhere, leaving the 89th Logistics Support Squadron behind as Caliban's only protection.\n\n# THE ATTACK\nAt 04:43 Earth Standard time (UST), 7 July 2884, a Vanduul Clan led by a Kingship slipped past the system-wide sensor beacons. Two pilots of the 89th, on patrol near [Caliban IV](gp:0GxavvKo2P), spotted the Clan. Both of them fired off a distress signal, but their messages were cut off before they could be completed. \n\nNot comprehending the scope of the threat they faced, the bulk of the 89th mobilized against the invading Clan. Four ships were lost to advancing scouts before the Kingship was in sight. At the sight of it, Commander Sylvie Randall made two snap decisions; first, to send out comm drones requesting reinforcements, knowing that it might take up to two days for reinforcements to arrive; second, to retreat back to Crion to organize and defend civilian convoys. It was this decision that allowed over three million inhabitants to escape with their lives.\n\nBy the time the 2nd UEE Naval Fleet arrived, 49 SE Hours later, there was nothing left to do but rescue any remaining people and abandon the system. The 89th Squadron, along with the Caliban system, were lost. It is estimated that over five and a half million people died, though no official numbers have ever been released.\n\n# AFTERMATH, ANALYSIS, AND IMPACT\nNo attempts were immediately made to reclaim Caliban. Though the Kingship responsible for the bulk of casualties in battle returned to Vanduul space soon after its victory, UEE forces held off on moving in until casualties could be assessed. The UEE announced in 2891 that there were no active plans to retake Caliban until the Vanduul threat could be fully neutralized. In 2945, military strategists began to discuss possible future campaigns into the system to rout the Vanduul encampments. \n\nHistorians believe that the decades of Vanduul absence in Caliban, combined with a thinly-spread military, poor system-wide sensor maintenance, and an incomplete understanding of Vanduul intentions were what led to the invaders' decisive victory. Though the Tiber, Virgil, and Orion systems had already been abandoned to the Vanduul, military strategists did not foresee an attack of that strength on Caliban. The 89th Squadron was there in full force, but one squadron was not enough to stand against the firepower of a Kingship. In honor of their sacrifice, Squadron 89, redubbed the Lost Squadron, was officially retired from the UEE Navy.\n\nVanduul [Harvesters](gp:0n1MYzOkG7) are actively consuming what is left of the Caliban system. Crion, once a thriving, lush world, is now devastated. There are no known Human inhabitants in the system.","g":["vanduul invasions","battles","lost squad","squadron 89","human history","vanduul history","caliban system"],"img":"https://static.robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/upload/67be6e7d-4ecb-4c32-a2fe-6a80a24d2247"},
{"id":"fall-of-virgil","gp":"box5moyeoZ","t":"Fall of Virgil","k":"history","c":["History","Military","Human","Vanduul"],"x":"The Fall of Virgil refers to the 2 January 2737 SEY invasion of the [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY) by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) directly after the conclusion of the [Siege of Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq). [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) forces, depleted after four years of battle, were unable to mount a suitable defense against the invading Vanduul, who pursued them once [Tiber](gp:RMNLm97EDj) fell. Although the system was lost, the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) was able to cover the retreat of over one million refugees. \n\n# BUILDUP\nBefore 2681 and the events of [Vanduul-Human First Contact](gp:RWwZDmxaXP), the Virgil system was on an upward trajectory. As the launchpoint of [Project Far Star](gp:0qnNAD6YKa), it was both a hub for explorers and a symbol of the UEE's continual outward expansion. [Cyrene (Virgil I)](gp:VlMBNGnxK5) was growing to be an economic powerhouse, having both a thriving resort industry due to its beautiful, lush landscapes and a robust agricultural system fed by highly fertile soil. However, when the Vanduul began launching regular raids in Virgil, the system's growth slowed. Project Far Star and talks of [Senatorial](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) recognition for Cyrene were put on hold pending resolution of the worsening Vanduul-Human conflict. \n\nAfter the [Orion system fell](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) to the Vanduul in 2712, the military forces stationed there retreated into the Tiber system, where they set up a line of defense in anticipation of a forthcoming assault. With the mounting threat to its neighboring systems, Virgil's already faltering tourism industry collapsed, and the system was soon transformed into a military outpost.\n\nAt the start of the Siege of Tiber in 2732, the population of Cyrene dropped to a few million people as all those with the means to do so fled. Countless others who did not have the resources to escape on their own applied to the government to help them relocate, but the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) Galor [Messer IX](gp:VyvYAGKxAz) refused to grant any aid, stating that Cyrene could not afford to lose more workers. Many turned to smugglers to help them flee, but some remained behind, believing that the might of the UEE would eventually prevail. Their faith appeared on the verge of paying off in November 2736, when the UEE conducted a bombing run on [Tiber II](gp:R5pxGYd9w7) and destroyed all Vanduul encampments there, enabling them to retake the planet, the [Tiber belt alpha](gp:VDza9J272q), and the Vector-Tiber jump point. Two [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) Battle Groups departed the system for repairs, and two more remained to pick off the few remaining Vanduul. It seemed that the UEE was on the verge of victory. \n\nOn 29 December 2736, the tide abruptly turned. A [Kingship](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm) accompanied by an enormous [Vanduul Clan](gp:R9vzjxmEBx) entered Tiber through the Orion-Tiber jump point and opened fire on the 81st Battle Group. Within half a day, three quarters of their ships were destroyed. Admiral Mira Triolo ordered them to retreat into Virgil while she remained behind with the 6th Battle Group to hold the line. \n\n# THE INVASION\nWhen the remains of the 81st entered Virgil it set off a panic. Millions of people who remained in the system clamored to be evacuated ahead of a potential Vanduul invasion. Citing the actions of the Vanduul in the aftermath of the Battle of Orion, the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) of Cyrene issued a statement assuring the public that a secondary invasion was unlikely to occur, and that they had sent a message to the Imperator requesting immediate military assistance. This helped calm things enough to avoid the threat of riots while the Council, with the help of the 81st, was able to organize an evacuation effort that succeeded in transporting over one million evacuees through the [Vega](gp:0jGGODZ6O6) and [Oberon](gp:VYLdlgMqop) jump points over three standard days.\n\nOn 2 January 2737 the 6th Battle Group in Tiber fell. Within hours, the Kingship and its accompanying Clan entered the Virgil system headed straight for Cyrene, making landfall at the city of Kastak and launching an all-out assault on the planet. The remnants of the 81st could offer little resistance, but elected to do all they could to hold off the Vanduul while the last transports fled the system under the protection of Squadron 214. When the final transport made it through the Vega jump point, Squadron 214 turned back to attempt to rescue more people. They were able to complete two more runs before they were unable to continue.\n\nThe Vanduul continued their assault against Cyrene and the rest of the system unabated until no other life remained. The surface of Cyrene was reduced to nothing, casting a cloud of radioactive ash into the atmosphere that created nuclear winter. Hundreds of thousands of [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) that were unable to escape perished. Those who had not died during the initial Vanduul onslaught soon starved or succumbed to radiation poisoning. \n\n# AFTERMATH, ANALYSIS, AND IMPACT\nThe military aid that the Governors Council of Cyrene had requested did not arrive until well over a week later. By that point, the Virgil system was completely overrun. Instead of entering the system and ousting the Vanduul, the military created a defensive line around the jump point to Virgil in anticipation of another assault. As with the loss of the Orion system, the attack did not immediately occur, and the Vanduul began to harvest Virgil's resources. Multiple scouting missions came back with reports that Cyrene was irrecoverable. In 2743, the UEE announced that they would not retake the system.\n\nSuddenly finding themselves on the front line, residents of the neighboring Vega system took what happened in Virgil as a cautionary tale and began to flee in droves, severely impacting the system's economy. Evacuees from Virgil, most of whom had little in their possession but their clothing, suffered food shortages as they awaited resettlement. Some were able to relocate to other systems, but the majority stayed near the military bases on [Aremis (Vega II)](gp:RkGGjdOwQz) and took any jobs that they could. Historians believe that this may have prevented the system's economy from entering a true depression, though it did not avert a recession. Today, over a quarter of people born in the Vega system can trace their lineage back to former residents of Cyrene. \n\nThe destruction of the Virgil system deeply affected the UEE. While Orion's loss had been significant, it was a young colony and had not undergone significant development, and Tiber was a sparsely-populated mining system with only small settlements. Virgil had over 300 years of history and was a major system with a world on the verge of recognition. As the heart of Project Far Star, it was also a symbol of the UEE's continual expansion. The UEE Navy's defeat at Tiber and subsequent failure to protect Virgil shook the people's confidence in the military and in the UEE at large. Historians cite the Fall of Virgil one of the many motivating factors that eventually led to the [anti-Messer revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7) in 2792.","g":["united empire of earth","battles","vanduul invasions","vanduul clans"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4b587cd7-faa6-480b-b49e-6be743d97bb4"},
{"id":"feratomine-freeze","gp":"RkGBl8J3A4","t":"Feratomine (Freeze)","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Feratomine (Freeze) is a tranquilizer and prescription drug that causes heavy sedation in the user while also stimulating nerve endings in the muscles. When used for medical purposes, it helps to rebuild damaged muscle tissue and is most often used to treat deep tissue injury. It can also be used as a sedative, and was briefly sold as an orally-consumed weight-loss supplement. The street version of the drug, freeze, is an aerosol that was first derived from the supplement. When inhaled, it creates a bluish shimmer inside the mouth, induces feelings of peace and euphoria, and lowers inhibitions.","g":["feratomine","freeze","tranquilizer","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/db2b5611-6c60-4a1b-9b59-9a25f62fb326"},
{"id":"feroh","gp":"VlMjQ1ZdLd","t":"Feroh","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Feroh is a high-end clothing brand that primarily produces footwear. Known for its elegant designs, shoes made by this company have become synonymous with luxury, and are often worn by celebrities during red carpet events. A typical Feroh shoe has a simple silhouette with one notable accent and is made with top-quality materials.","g":["clothing manufacturer","footwear manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f3054009-f13d-4ecf-bbf9-a1f269b2ecbf"},
{"id":"ferron-i","gp":"RvlQZEQdWY","t":"Ferron I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ferron I is a small mesoplanet that orbits closest to the sun of the [Ferron system](gp:Vy2Qo1dB18), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). While it appears to be spheroid to the naked eye, recent measurements of its surface confirm that it is misshapen enough to possibly fit the definition of a protoplanet.","g":["ferron system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2f3b2317-57dd-494c-bbb3-b44f71373f4b"},
{"id":"ferron-ii","gp":"0jG8nE55zm","t":"Ferron II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ferron II is a coreless, uninhabited planet in the [Ferron system](gp:Vy2Qo1dB18), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Second from the system's sun, its relative position makes it only a tenuous candidate for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). Ever since its neighbor [Asura (Ferron III)](gp:0qaPo2JOj1) ran dry of resources, many small mining consortiums set up operations there, hoping to discover resources that major companies consider too unprofitable to harvest. The [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) of Asura has held multiple debates over the past decade on whether to fund a private company to terraform Ferron II on their behalf.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","ferron system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/efd613d7-b625-4550-b95b-0a22966997f7"},
{"id":"ferron-iv","gp":"VYLJxPzow6","t":"Ferron IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ferron IV is a dense gas giant that is located farthest from the sun of the [Ferron system](gp:Vy2Qo1dB18), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Because it has an especially active electrical field, ships with sensitive avionics are advised not to fly too close to it, lest it cause their systems to malfunction. Bands of outlaws have been known to lurk just outside the danger zone, waiting to prey on malfunctioning ships.","g":["ferron system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b70eb93-a945-4d03-8d89-35e4da518237"},
{"id":"ferron-system","gp":"Vy2Qo1dB18","t":"Ferron System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Ferron system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that consists of one mesoplanet, one coreless planet, one terrestrial planet, one gas giant, and an F-type star. Discovered by Pali Laumet in SEY 2460, it was one of the wealthiest systems in the UEE until 2791, when [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) accused its populace of harboring political dissidents. Wealthy [Citizens](gp:RLMmop8rkr) and Messer loyalists fled, taking large amounts of funds with them. Then, in 2832, [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA) announced profit losses for the first time ever, signaling that most of Ferron's mineral resources were depleted. More businesses pulled out, triggering further economic devastation.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e3fdf123-d33a-4688-8e4c-094ba5a46287"},
{"id":"fiona-messer","gp":"R56nLjJog7","t":"Fiona Messer","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Fiona Messer (2768-unknown) was the younger sister of Linton Messer XI, and after his death, became the last surviving member of the Messer dynasty of [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) [Imperators](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl). After working with [her brother](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) to usurp power from their father [Ulysses](gp:bBp6YZPOGO), she engaged in seditious activities with elements inside the UEE to remove Linton from power and inherit his position. The intelligence she shared with the resistance group Tide helped spark the [anti-Messer revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7). After the footage of the Massacre of Garron II leaked onto the Spectrum and the uprising began, Fiona noted in her personal log that it was spreading too quickly to control. Historians speculate she went on the run to avoid capture and the execution that awaited her brother. Her whereabouts after this point remain unknown.","g":["messer era","tide (activist group)","anti-messer revolution","messer dynasty"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1f808eb6-f436-495c-80b3-ac1d0665eb1e"},
{"id":"fiore","gp":"0NjQBKLdL2","t":"Fiore","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Fiore is a business wear clothing brand that uses historic fashion as inspiration for its designs. Founded by art history student Fiore Ouwerx after the sudden death of their grandparents, they were inspired to create their first piece when sorting through their grandmother's belongings which would go on to inspire the keystone garment in their debut show during [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv) Fashion Week in SEY 2897.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a251f198-9734-4920-b6ff-e15f39bbd52f"},
{"id":"fire-rats","gp":"bZkOav4oEO","t":"Fire Rats","k":"people","c":["Organizations","Illegal Activity"],"x":"The Fire Rats are a criminal organization and religious cult based in the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). It originated in 2563, when a group of former [Pyrotechnic Amalgamated](gp:VpM4anYBn1) workers found themselves abandoned on [Bloom (Pyro III)](gp:0KxjqgQdNY) after their employer declared bankruptcy. Forced to eke out a living or perish, they took up residence in their former barracks. It is rumored that when resources began to run low, a large cargo ship that had been hit by a powerful stellar flare crashed near their settlement, granting them a bounty of supplies. This is believed to be the origin of their reverence for Pyro's star and its especially violent stellar activity. Today, the Fire Rats are known for shipjacking, and for sporting scars from repeated, intentional exposure to stellar flares.","g":["outlaw factions","human outlaw factions","pyro outlaw faction","religion","human religion"]},
{"id":"fire-team-five","gp":"0QxYE6oQN3","t":"Fire Team Five","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*Fire Team Five* is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) Spectrum show that ran for eleven seasons from 2913 to 2924. It followed a group of mercenaries operating on the edge of human space. Episodes typically began with the group accepting a deceptively rewarding mission that would force them to choose between their morals and their credit balances. *Fire Time Five* was a leading example of the 2910s frontier fad, which saw a high volume of popular culture offering a romanticized view of the [Human Colonial Expansion Era](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm) (2380-2530).","g":["spectrum show","tedge 8"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/235857de-aa10-4760-b16d-225603570cc0"},
{"id":"firestorm-kinetics","gp":"0QxYED5aql","t":"FireStorm Kinetics","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons"],"x":"FireStorm Kinetics is a Human spacecraft weapons manufacturer headquartered on Cascom (Castra II). Originally an exclusive contractor for the military, FireStorm built rockets for capital ships and torpedoes for military bombers. They have since expanded to the civilian market, and have added missiles and rocket pods to their production line.","g":["weapons manufacturer","cascom","castra ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6db70ad8-466d-4875-acdf-b36235ec641d"},
{"id":"first-contact-day","gp":"01Lvo8ZWxX","t":"First Contact Day","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"First Contact Day is a holiday celebrated by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) to commemorate the moment they first made contact with civilizations outside their own. On 12 June 2438, explorer Vernon Tar encountered a [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) pilot in the Davien system. Though he initially believed the Banu's ship was another Human attempting to survey the same area of space, he soon realized his mistake and sent his coordinates to the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO). In response, a diplomatic team led by General Neal Socolovich arrived to smooth out the situation. The [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) made formal contact two weeks later, and signed the [Interstellar Peace and Trade Accord](gp:RzPoJ1aP4z) in October 2438. Humans celebrate the holiday by cooking or purchasing meals from alien cultures, holding parties or small gatherings, and shopping at Banu, [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X), and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj)-owned businesses.","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/44ce8c32-9660-4a86-ab2a-1b77b2b9805f"},
{"id":"first-imperial-age","gp":"VDoPeW55W4","t":"First Imperial Age","k":"history","c":["Xi'an","History"],"x":"The First [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) Age was the longest dynasty [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) history. Spanning almost fifteen thousand Xi'an years, it began with the crowning of the first Emperor Ru'a in MXY I.0 (19668 BCE), several years after the [loss of the Xi'an homeworld](gp:VyvYA5qmqX) RyiXy'an (Hyoton III) in 19770 BCE. During this era, the Xi'an discovered [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY), established the [Civil Service (Pō't.ōngp.ū)](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ), codified the tenets of [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe) into common law, and first [terraformed](gp:R6dWOrLEM4) worlds outside their home planetary system. The Age came to an end in I.14680 (878 BCE), when Emperor Se'ang se Ru'a, the final heir of his house, stepped down to make way for Y.ah'a se Xy.ō, the oldest daughter of [her House](gp:RXlXBrm5o1) and the first Emperor of the [Second Age](gp:RAdjOk77n7).","g":["house ru'a","xi'an service","li'tova","eras"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/14e78f30-a9c6-4e40-9f3e-3f7ad44504a1"},
{"id":"first-jump-day","gp":"VpMxKQpX6O","t":"First Jump Day","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"First Jump Day is a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) holiday celebrated on 10 April that recognizes the day [Nick Croshaw](gp:VyvYkAr7YW) became the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to discover a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY). In the mid-23rd century, spacecraft in the Sol system began to vanish without explanation in a region nicknamed the Neso Triangle. The mystery attracted multiple scientists and explorers interested in pinning down the reason behind the disappearances. After ten years studying the area, astrophysicist Nick Croshaw discovered and successfully navigated a [jump tunnel](gp:bBp6Bx33wm) via a personally-modified [quantum drive](gp:RX3DOkJdxJ) and discovered a new planetary system. The system was named Croshaw in his honor. The holiday was established in 2380 after the formation of the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) government. Many commemorate the day by traversing a jump or by searching for new jump points.","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/77e01ccb-17e0-401d-9094-879218dd214f"},
{"id":"first-sister-kilian-i","gp":"VlMMagKEzd","t":"First Sister (Kilian I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"The First Sister is the first planet of the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A massive hot Jupiter streaked with green and yellow, it shares an orbit with two small protoplanets that sit in the L4 and L5 Lagrange points of the First Sister-Kilian system. Collectively, these three celestial bodies are known as the \"Three sisters.\"","g":["first sister","kilian i","kilian system","three sisters"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/19c8486a-6401-4fa4-a207-f794c23b1a67"},
{"id":"first-tevarin-war","gp":"bZwQm3meJM","t":"First Tevarin War","k":"history","c":["History","Military","Human","Tevarin"],"x":"The First Tevarin War was an intersystem conflict between the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) and the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN). The Tevarin declared war with [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) in 2541, shortly after first contact. The motivations behind the war were complex; it was both a bid for the Tevarin to claim UPE-controlled territory to assuage their overpopulation problem and a consequence of the high cultural value the Tevarin as a people placed on combat. The war was responsible for countless advances in spacecraft technology. [Ivar Messer](gp:RXlXYPWk8q), then an officer in the [UPE Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q), was propelled to power following the [Battle of Idris IV](gp:ReJajXKelk), a key conflict in the [First Tevarin War](gp:ReJajXKelk). The Tevarin were defeated in 2546.","g":["wars","united planets of earth","ivar messer i"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7fbd2f17-c178-4e7c-b45b-4356f35a845f"},
{"id":"fizzz","gp":"RMNNA1BL88","t":"Fizzz","k":"culture","c":["Food and Beverages","Human"],"x":"Fizzz is a carbonated soft drink manufactured by the [Bevic Group](gp:RAXX71OBdB), a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) company that manufactures a wide variety of branded food and beverages. It debuted in 2777, after a team at the Bevic Group made a research breakthrough in adapting the flavor of the soursop fruit into beverage form. Initial sales of the soda were so high that a black market sprung up around the purchasing and reselling of cases of Fizzz until the Bevic Group was able to increase production and resolve its supply chain issues in 2779. Fizzz mainly featured fruit flavors until 2893, when they added a cola flavor to the lineup. Other popular flavors include muscat, peach, and triple berry.","g":["soft drink","beverage","human beverage","bevic group"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/81576199-b33a-4aac-9609-25df4f65ccf4"},
{"id":"flareweed","gp":"RMNWkvB2ZY","t":"Flareweed","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"Flareweed is a type of grass that grows in dry, hot environments. During extreme heat waves, the plant can retract its blades until the temperature reaches a more tolerable level. Individual flareweed plants grow alongside one another and their roots form an interwoven clump that appears to be a solid mass on first glance. The roots and the leaves can be processed and used as a component in water filtration systems.","g":["grasses"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ba470bd1-8783-49c4-bdbc-2b5b347cc7c6"},
{"id":"flashfire-systems","gp":"0OaB28xezv","t":"Flashfire Systems","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Flashfire Systems is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) engineering firm and weapon mount manufacturer headquartered on Angeli (Croshaw II). Founded in 2904 as a laser weapons manufacturer, Flashfire nearly went bankrupt after their line of standard lasers failed to gain traction in the market. Flashfire redirected its manufacturing efforts to universally usable weapon mounts after the company was purchased by Garvin Snarm.","g":["weapon component manufacturer","gavin snarm","angeli","croshaw ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a81a6a19-4271-4b86-9079-e5a7786591a4"},
{"id":"flatcat","gp":"0Gx6qvGraj","t":"Flatcat","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"A flatcat is a small carnivorous animal indigenous to [Kampos (Ellis IV)](gp:RAXxrxr7M5). Because it evolved on a high-gravity world, the flatcat has a wide, squat body and stocky, muscular legs. A social animal, it lives in groups of between two and forty individuals in its natural habitat. During dawn and dusk when they are most active, flatcats hunt together, sometimes taking down prey much larger than themselves. Their resemblance to the domestic cat endeared them to the people of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) and sparked a trend for pet flatcats in the early 30th century SEY that proved short-lived when their natural strength and tendency to scent-mark surfaces showed that they were not suited for indoor living. However, the animal still has some enthusiasts, and there are multiple breeding programs on Kampos dedicated to creating a true domestic flatcat.","g":["kampos","ellis iv","pets"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3f239a7d-2376-4824-826c-9396e211fcf0"},
{"id":"flight-of-fancy","gp":"VpMYDYgozO","t":"Flight-of-Fancy","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The flight-of-fancy is a genetically modified plant that was created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke) to decrease symptoms caused by airborne allergens. The fine, light pollen produced in its bright orange flowers is an antihistamine, and is easily spread via wind distribution. Thanks to this and the large broad leaves that provide ample shade when the plant reaches maturity, the flight-of-fancy is usually planted in [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) cities, or in new settlements on recently [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) worlds.","g":["rayari inc","herbaceous plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/78fbb3ac-b3f3-4a6f-9cf2-f87e41e05a4b"},
{"id":"flo-pets","gp":"V8gJOo3ZGO","t":"Flo-Pets","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"Flo-Pets are a bioluminescent freshwater slug indigenous to Xis (Kellog II). Despite being protected by the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP), [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) smugglers began eluding United Empire of Earth military forces to travel to the surface to capture Flo-Pets around 2918, intending to develop them as an easily-bred compact protein source. When they proved inedible for Humans, they were instead marketed as novelty pets, which led to a brief fad that further fueled smuggling operations. Flo-pets adapt to new environments easily and discarded pets have gone on to establish populations on many Human-inhabited worlds.","g":["xis","kellog ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6ea8de52-55dc-4e9d-b16d-557b5d1c6915"},
{"id":"fora-belt-alpha","gp":"0ODA5rLEWe","t":"Fora Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Fora belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the [Fora system](gp:bo1PDEgGv2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Smugglers in Fora typically use the belt as a drop point for contraband, which is then picked up and smuggled into the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Pirates have also been known to utilize some of the asteroids as staging areas for ambushes on haulers entering or leaving the system. The UEE has issued a travel alert advising visitors to Fora to give the area a wide berth.","g":["asteroid belt","fora system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0bf0fbc8-0b5b-484f-a20f-5fe4f13c8a81"},
{"id":"fora-i","gp":"VlM8eE8W7e","t":"Fora I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Fora I is a mesoplanet in the [Fora system](gp:bo1PDEgGv2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A hot, dry planet that closely orbits its sun, temperatures on its surface are dangerously high for most spacecraft. A ridge runs along the equator of Fora I, forming a complex system of peaks. Scientists are uncertain what caused the ridge to form, but one hypothesis suggests that the mesoplanet once had a ring system that eventually raised the ridge via collisional accretion.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","fora system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ec2f0b68-4a98-48a0-a124-d53a611f6abe"},
{"id":"fora-ii","gp":"RxnB5EqL2M","t":"Fora II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Fora II is a coreless terrestrial planet located in the [Fora system](gp:bo1PDEgGv2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). After the [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) of Hyperion (Fora III) failed, several companies attempted to terraform this planet, in spite of its location outside the system's green band. All attempts failed, forcing those who hoped to turn the system into a trading hub to finally abandon their plans.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","fora system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ab65c0f2-abd7-407d-897b-09f236d9e91d"},
{"id":"fora-iv","gp":"Rz2QNEdGNA","t":"Fora IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Fora IV is a gas giant in the [Fora system](gp:bo1PDEgGv2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The fourth planet from the sun, Fora IV completes its orbit roughly once every 1600 Standard Earth Days (SED). Its pale yellow and green-banded atmosphere surrounds a mantle made of metallic hydrogen and helium.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","fora system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b49fc02-9da0-475a-a65f-5ddc0b115447"},
{"id":"fora-system","gp":"bo1PDEgGv2","t":"Fora System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Fora system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is made up of a K-type main sequence star, a mesoplanet, two terrestrial planets, a gas giant, and an ice giant. After a jump point to the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) system Yulin from the Banshee system was discovered in SEY 2463, developers were hopeful that Fora could become a major trade hub. However, a [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) error created a perpetual dust storm on [Fora III](gp:RegWGPlxqy), the system's only potentially habitable planet. Today, the sparsely-populated system is a favorite outpost for pirates and smugglers.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4daf3eda-b154-4fb7-866f-2caf2bad760c"},
{"id":"fora-v","gp":"VJXn6rmDY8","t":"Fora V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Fora V is an ice giant in the [Fora system](gp:bo1PDEgGv2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Its thick ammonia and water atmosphere is pale blue with bands of darker blue. Lacking a solid surface, its core is composed of iron and nickel, and it has a mantle rich in ammonia, methane, and water. Deep within the planet, there are regular showers of diamond crystals.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","fora system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/16163eca-9a15-47b6-a428-a462cfdd7614"},
{"id":"fortified-armor","gp":"bZwQjMOy1d","t":"Fortified Armor","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Fortified Armor is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of low-end personal armor and clothing. The company focuses on creating strictly utilitarian products that emphasize affordability over high quality. Many of their goods are built to mimic the look of high-end pieces from other companies.","g":["armor manufacturer","clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d525db75-2320-4941-95f7-e0258ea54e2e"},
{"id":"fortress-palm","gp":"RxnYvY1aZd","t":"Fortress Palm","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The fortress palm is a genetically modified fruit-bearing tree with fan-shaped, palmate leaves. Created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke) in 2930, the fortress palm was designed to provide nutrient-dense fruit for the inhabitants of newly-[terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) worlds. Additionally, it was made to be as resistant to pests as possible, with a thorny trunk detrimental to climbing and leaves that contain pain-causing alkaloids. Its fruit must be harvested via machinery or while wearing protective gear.","g":["rayari inc","fruiting plant","trees"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fc4d5c3a-00fa-4945-863c-ef5512c1bed4"},
{"id":"fountation-festival","gp":"RAXKmZQAMy","t":"Foundation Festival","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"The Foundation Festival is a civic program that takes place annually in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) for the duration of the month of July. Proposed in SEY 2861 by [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) Gayatri Deomana, the holiday endeavors to strengthen community participation by encouraging Citizens and civilians to volunteer with local and imperial organizations. Independent charitable organizations often reach volunteer capacity during the holiday, so the UEE government offers short-term volunteer opportunities such as mentorship programs and cleanup events. [Civilians](gp:Vgg7rq5J73) can submit repeated Foundation Festival volunteer work as one of many qualifications to receive [Citizenship](gp:RLMmop8rkr).","g":["uee holiday"]},
{"id":"freelancer","gp":"RvgzWy7o6v","t":"Freelancer","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Freelancer is a multi-role transport spacecraft developed by [MISC](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) and was the first vessel to be constructed as part of a unique lend-lease agreement with the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government. The ship's hull is sold in several variants that have been adapted for various  alternate roles like the [Freelancer DUR](gp:0Gz5jxlM4a) exploration ship, the [Freelancer MAX](gp:RWwZqoXZW6) enhanced cargo ship and the [Freelancer MIS](gp:bE3r7yYoN7) missile launcher.","g":["misc","freight","medium freight","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/78ad60dd-d39b-484c-a1f1-d731cf7da901"},
{"id":"freelancer-dur","gp":"0Gz5jxlM4a","t":"Freelancer DUR","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Freelancer DUR is a variant of the [Freelancer](gp:RvgzWy7o6v) freighter developed by [MISC](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). Adapted for exploration, the DUR trades some of the base Freelancer's cargo capacity in exchange for a number of adaptations intended to increase overall range and durability. These include a dedicated scanner suite, an improved jump drive, and a larger fuel supply.","g":["expedition","misc","freelancer","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/da6d3bd6-c0d5-4bd7-82d7-5f7e8097e66d"},
{"id":"freelancer-max","gp":"RWwZqoXZW6","t":"Freelancer MAX","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Freelancer MAX is a variant of the [Freelancer](gp:RvgzWy7o6v) freighter developed by [MISC](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). Unusually for spacecraft variants, the MAX is a total rebuild of the standard Freelancer hull rather than a redesign. Thanks to these changes, it can carry twice as much internal cargo as its parent model in exchange for sacrificing some speed and maneuverability.","g":["medium freight","misc","human spacecraft","freight","freelancer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1dcd7d38-6bbf-49a7-98a5-3a82176b8e4e"},
{"id":"freelancer-mis","gp":"bE3r7yYoN7","t":"Freelancer MIS","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human","Military"],"x":"The Freelancer MIS is a limited-edition variant of the [Freelancer](gp:RvgzWy7o6v) freighter developed by [MISC](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). The design replaces much of the standard Freelancer's cargo capacity with high-capacity missile magazines. The original request for the update came from the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN) who looked to convert the readily available commercial ship into an effective carrier-based missile boat. While some are in active military service, others have been made available in small numbers on the civilian market.","g":["gunship","misc","freelancer","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e833ab21-2aa0-4e3c-91ae-eec5fecc377a"},
{"id":"freeman-act","gp":"RWooPaXwE2","t":"Freeman Act","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The Freeman Act is a piece of legislation passed cooperatively by all governments on Earth (Sol III) in 2281 that created a lottery system to grant land and mineral rights to potential colonists of the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp). Revenue generated from the lottery was used to fund ongoing [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) efforts. Winners of the lottery were granted one-way tickets to the system, eligible for use once the terraformation of [Croshaw II](gp:0QlxqwG14Q) was completed. The success of this program convinced the governments of Earth to form a new one-world government called the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) in 2380.","g":["laws","human law","uee law"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a31c30c2-a2e4-4fdc-8fd2-5ad5b92bed42"},
{"id":"front-row","gp":"VgEWp1Ox2N","t":"Front Row","k":"place","c":["Settlements"],"x":"Front Row is a settlement on the surface of [Lanisto (Tyrol 1a)](gp:R4jwKdNQPJ), the moon of [Tyrol I](gp:0GxQnP34YP) in the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N). In 2848, a series of interconnected research stations funded by multiple private institutes were constructed below the surface in old lava tunnels as a part of a project to observe the evolution of the white dwarf's potential nova. The study lost its funding in 2901, and the facility was abandoned. Shortly thereafter it was claimed by smugglers and drifters. Aware that when the star eventually goes nova they will be the first to perish, the settlement's few permanent residents have nicknamed it \"Front Row.\"","g":["lanisto","tyrol 1a","sealed settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5421a535-46b9-43dd-805b-4e8359369672"},
{"id":"fuego-pyro-5e","gp":"0rx4rG8W49","t":"Fuego (Pyro 5e)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Fuego is the fifth moon from the gas giant [Pyro V](gp:RAXv9Yeqay), [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Relatively temperate but still cold, it has a mostly carbon dioxide atmosphere with small percentages of nitrogen, sulfur dioxide, and oxygen. High amounts of iron-sulfide in its soil gives its surface a yellow and black appearance. Infamous smuggler group Headhunters often utilized Fuego as a stash point for goods during their nascent years in the early 2600s.","g":["fuego","pyro 5e","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon","pyro system"]},
{"id":"fujin-city","gp":"RxNxAeyOq6","t":"Fujin City","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Fujin City (風神都) is the capital city of [Saisei (Centauri III)], [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Considered by environmentalists to be an achievement in urban and geodevelopment, it is one of the most verdant cities in the UEE. Traditional Japanese architecture and modern building styles blend with carefully constructed gardens and parks to create a balanced environment. A center of commerce and industry, all businesses in the city must comply with strict environmental regulations. Most traffic entering and leaving Saisei passes through Fujin. The [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) of Saisei has implemented a population cap in order to curb overpopulation and preserve the environment.","g":["saisei","centauri iii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2fc16563-46f5-469c-909a-94df8ddd0137"},
{"id":"fujin-technical-college","gp":"VlNPAZByq7","t":"Fujin Technical College","k":"place","c":["Education","Human","Locations"],"x":"Fujin Technical College (FTC) is an institute of higher education located in [Fujin City](gp:RxNxAeyOq6) on [Saisei (Centauri III)](gp:Vy22NQJ1q6). FTC offers a variety of training courses, and is most notable for its Certification in Arts and Design. The school itself was designed to blend seamlessly with [Fujin City's](gp:RxNxAeyOq6) natural environment.","g":["fujin city","higher education","centauri iii","saisei","uee higher education","uee education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/884042c3-b513-44c8-afd3-f290c39a101e"},
{"id":"fulcrum-mining-associates","gp":"0OaB8LgXlZ","t":"Fulcrum Mining Associates","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Fulcrum Mining Associates was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) mining concern that operated from 2448 through its sale to [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA) in 2554. The company was one of the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) off-world mining concerns. In 2554, Fulcrum reached out to Shubin with a bid to sell off unwanted corporate assets in the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5). Shubin opted to purchase Fulcrum outright instead and by 2585 had fully retired the company's branding.","g":["shubin interstellar","mining company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a5a093dd-061b-487e-8833-8b481dc6c822"},
{"id":"fury","gp":"RkGOyEBkJB","t":"Fury","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Fury is a snub fighter manufactured by [Mirai](gp:Vy2B1o6gn6), a subsidiary of [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/misc) (MISC). Developed with an infusion of [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) and [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) technology, the Fury utilizes an agility-enhancing gimballed thruster array more commonly encountered in Xi'an fighters. It was designed with a focus on maneuverability, speed, and firepower, and has a minimal silhouette, making it a challenging target to damage during combat.","g":["fighter","snub fighter","snub","mirai","human spacecraft","fury series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/87ed50b4-5bcf-4fdc-b5b2-1cea2bf3d73d"},
{"id":"fury-lx","gp":"0qa1y2z1Jp","t":"Fury LX","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Fury LX is a snub racer manufactured by [Mirai](gp:Vy2B1o6gn6), a subsidiary of [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/misc) (MISC). A variant of the [Fury](gp:RkGOyEBkJB) snub fighter, the LX swaps the weapons of the base model for additional maneuvering thrusters, increasing the ship's speed and agility. Its frame was updated to enhance the ship's movement in atmosphere, which has led to its usage in major racing events.","g":["racing","snub racer","snub","human spacecraft","fury series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5c4a9cb7-89f7-4ac6-a705-6333436d3cae"},
{"id":"fury-mx","gp":"VYLYlP3AK1","t":"Fury MX","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Fury MX is a snub bomber manufactured by [Mirai](gp:Vy2B1o6gn6), a subsidiary of [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/misc) (MISC). A variant of the [Fury](gp:RkGOyEBkJB) snub fighter, it was redesigned to hold more missiles when compared to the base model, and was given a retractable blast shield to protect the pilot during close-range bombing runs. Because this limits visibility, the MX is equipped with sensors that aid navigation.","g":["fury","snub","mirai","human spacecraft","fury series","fighter","snub fighter"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f800424e-10f9-481a-8036-bf9574fae0ea"},
{"id":"gainey-odin-1a","gp":"Rw1G2JG4K9","t":"Gainey (Odin 1a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Gainey (Odin 1a) is the former moon of [Odin I](gp:VlNP3xpMx4), [Odin system](gp:RX3jMavYGk), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). After Odin I was destroyed, it slipped into a stable orbit around the system's sun close to its parent planet's remains. It has a breathable atmosphere, and was the home of many fracking operations and gas refinement plants until tectonic instability forced the companies to leave.","g":["gainey","odin 1a","odin system","habitable","habitable moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/86aa4a0e-c036-4671-9eb2-885861c04fb1"},
{"id":"gal-dougan","gp":"box5WYgM2A","t":"Gal Dougan","k":"people","c":["Music","People","Human"],"x":"Gal Dougan (SEY 2868 - unknown) was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) folk singer. She began her career as a miner in her family's business, but is famous throughout Human settled space for both her distinct music and the mysterious circumstances surrounding her disappearance. Known for her elegant orchestrations, blue-collar poetic lyrics, and a unique singing style that is commonly referred to in music publications as \"that Gal Dougan sound,\" her original compositions over four albums tend to deal with the joys and sorrows of work, love, and family through a gritty lens, the result of her turbulent upbringing as part of a hardscrabble mining family. She disappeared after a concert in 2931. Her whereabouts remain unknown.","g":["borea","magnus ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/89744663-68e9-457d-bc99-95a564520996"},
{"id":"galactic-tour-galactic-gear","gp":"0rxqDJrxp3","t":"Galactic Tour (Galactic Gear)","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*Galactic Tour* (formerly *Galactic Gear*) is a [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) show hosted by [Jax McCleary](gp:RL6MjgGJJ3) that reviews spacecraft after putting them through outlandish tests. Debuting in 2931 as *Galactic Gear*, the show featured McCleary and a rotating cast of friends and guest stars who accompanied McCleary in his test flights. Voyager Direct purchased the show in 2945 and renamed and relaunched it as *Galactic Tour* in 2946 A new host, Rahul Menon, took over after McCleary left in 2947. Since it first aired, *Galactic Tour* has been popular with audiences for the unusual methods it uses to evaluate spacecraft and for its frank and often comedic commentary.","g":["galactic tour","galactic gear","spectrum show","reviews","jax mccleary"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/33dd1351-429e-42ee-bfa2-1185d0409aa9"},
{"id":"Galaxy","gp":"V3GZEvLj52","t":"Galaxy","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Galaxy is a large multi-role spacecraft developed by [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) (RSI). Released in 2952, it was scheduled to be unveiled the same year at the [Intergalactic Aerospace Expo](gp:R4jpEgezde), but the show floor prototype was stolen. [Jax McCleary](gp:RL6MjgGJJ3) of the popular [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) show [Whitley's Guide](gp:V8WgdOP8px) discovered the prototype on Ruin Station while livestreaming his escape from the Pyro system, where he had been traveling with a group of outlaws. The Galaxy is a ship designed for easy customization, with a mid-ship space constructed to house different modules. Cargo, medical, and refinery modules debuted alongside the ship, with plans from the company to produce more at a later date. The base model includes three turrets and two missile hard-points, a hangar, and quarters for a crew of six.","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","multi-role spacecraft","modular spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/14565620-0e0b-4aa5-8cc3-0f5f0fdb162c"},
{"id":"gallenson-tactical-systems","gp":"bBp6YN8EjB","t":"Gallenson Tactical Systems","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Gallenson Tactical Systems is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) personal and spacecraft weapons manufacturer headquartered on Earth (Sol III). Founded as a gun shop, it entered manufacturing when the owners purchased a small foundry in 2763. Gallenson produces lower-tech weapons out of heavy materials built to endure the stress of repeated use.","g":["weapons manufacturer","earth","sol iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0ea959b9-1d37-43a8-b9b8-8a2628d0f9b5"},
{"id":"gallo-and-frost","gp":"VDzoZ3jggz","t":"Gallo and Frost","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Gallo & Frost is a company that creates luxury furniture, including premium seating for spacecraft and ground vehicles. Founded by Timo Gallo and Helen Frost in 2902, the company requires its designers to partner with artisans and material suppliers local to the areas in which its products are made. In 2943, Gallo & Frost accepted a contract from [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) to provide the then-upcoming 2945 edition of the [Constellation Phoenix](gp:VyvYqezlqW) with its primary operator seat.","g":["furniture manufacture","constellation phoenix"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/de4c0c8a-1b4f-446c-8ee2-255c394285b0"},
{"id":"galor-messer-ix","gp":"VyvYAGKxAz","t":"Galor Messer IX","k":"people","c":["People","Human","History"],"x":"Galor Messer IX (SEY 2666 - 2751), [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) from 2715 - 2751, was the older brother of [Samuel VIII](gp:RkZ9W2L2NB). Under his rule, he changed the name of the UEE currency system to Imperials, remade government buildings in the Meta-Baroque style, and named his nephew [Ulysses](gp:bBp6YZPOGO) as successor. \n\nAs a child, he contracted an illness with a poor prognosis, and was not expected to live past his 20th birthday. His mother [Illyana VI](gp:bZwQBNmWrL) disinherited him in favor of his younger brother. After Samuel was stabbed to death in bed, Galor ascended to the title of Imperator. He died in office in 2751 at age 85, after a prolonged battle with a degenerative bone illness.","g":["messer era","messer dynasty","uee imperator","human people","human history"],"img":"https://static.robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/upload/c4f918cf-632c-447c-a2e9-6a2046f2b517"},
{"id":"gammon-messer","gp":"0rxrqgDP12","t":"Gammon Messer","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Gammon Messer (2629 - 2662) was the eldest child of [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Corsen Messer V](gp:0OaB8O6awO) and actress Inaya Satti. He spent his childhood on Earth (Sol III) with his sister [Illyana](gp:bZwQBNmWrL) and his cousin [Marius](gp:RxNxAgrXZz). Third in line from ascension at the time of his birth, he was raised without expectation that he become Imperator. He spent his youth pursuing hobbies and was rumored to have indulged heavily in vice. After Marius was killed in a 2641 shuttle explosion and Corsen became Imperator two years later in 2643, Gammon was suddenly first in line for succession. He was forced to attend military school at the behest of his father, and formally entered the [UEE Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) at age 18. In 2654, he married Colonel Yemi Duas in a lavish ceremony in New York City on Earth, which his sister Illyana did not attend. His only daughter [Astrid](gp:0KnA1D5nQM) was born in 2661. Before his assassination alongside his father in 2662, Gammon was credited with creating more intense prisoner conditions and devising particularly violent forms of information extraction, many believed to have been derived while accompanying Corsen on his multiple visits to the [political prisons on Charon III](gp:0KxqnXDpQ2).","g":["messer dynasty","messer era"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b0d3793-0d81-4fe9-8d31-9483088e30a8"},
{"id":"ganymede-sol-5c","gp":"VlMjgvz1WL","t":"Ganymede (Sol 5c)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Ganymede (Sol 5c) is a moon of [Jupiter (Sol V)](gp:Vy2OMo22wz), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The largest moon in the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), its diameter is greater than that of the planet [Mercury (Sol I)](gp:V3G8yDedAN). Before Ganymede's subsurface ocean was explored in the 25th century SEY, it was popularly speculated that the moon may have had extraterrestrial life. No forms of life in the past or present have thus far been observed.","g":["ganymede","sol 5c","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cf9568ae-88f7-421b-9c43-175866cbf8ca"},
{"id":"garrity-arms","gp":"bE3rLKwr9J","t":"Garrity Arms","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Garrity Arms was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) weapon design and manufacturing company that operated from 2280 to 2516. Founded on Earth (Sol III), it relocated to Mars (Sol IV) in 2299, where it developed the first Human-designed off-world weapon, the Tedge 8 handgun. Garrity Arms' weapons were primarily used during the [Human Colonial Expansion Era (2380-2530)](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm). Although the company went out of business in 2516, some of its brands are owned and utilized by other weapons manufacturers today.","g":["weapons manufacturer","mars","sol iv","tedge 8","human colonial expansion era"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ad81e1f9-1659-4a3f-bf68-5a7549380e5b"},
{"id":"garrity-defense","gp":"RkZ9WAYJNn","t":"Garrity Defense","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Garrity Defense is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) retailer of personal armor systems and flight wear. While the store offers a wide range of options, their primary demographic skews to individual civilian users rather than military or industrial entities. Garrity Defense storefronts are a favorite stop for explorers, athletes and daredevils, and are the de facto body armor provider for professional Sataball players and high-endurance racing teams.","g":["armor retailer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/584e2493-0c88-47e4-9632-c6049c9be5c3"},
{"id":"garron-i","gp":"VDzJz87Ql9","t":"Garron I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Garron I is the first planet from the sun of the [Garron system](gp:0GxexoWn2P), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). A terrestrial planet, its proximity to its star has led to the formation of vast seas of lava. As it rotates on its axis, cycling through day and night, the dark side of the surface cools slightly and short-lived islands of rock form that melt when they are once again exposed to light and heat.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","garron system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/19c865be-d37b-4e6d-b7d8-b8f2d49bcfa8"},
{"id":"garron-ii","gp":"VlMGMLM1lL","t":"Garron II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Garron II is the second planet from the sun of the [Garron system](gp:0GxexoWn2P), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Originally a lush, biodiverse world populated by countless animal and plant species and a burgeoning civilization, it was subjected to [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) at the orders of [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) and the majority of its life was destroyed, including its intelligent inhabitants. Footage of this event, known as the [Massacre of Garron II](gp:01dWeqnMr1), was broadcast throughout the UEE, inspiring [an uprising](gp:bE3rKa32P7) that led to the fall of the Messer dynasty and the reorganization of the UEE government. The [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) passed the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) in SEY 2795 to ensure what happened to Garron II would not happen elsewhere and funded a long-term program to attempt to restore Garron II's original biosphere. This process remains ongoing.","g":["habitable planet","habitable","garron system","fair chance act","massacre of garron ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a95c2522-dded-464a-82cd-cdcdbd4f940d"},
{"id":"garron-iii","gp":"VlMGMLlnPd","t":"Garron III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Garron III is the third planet from the sun of the [Garron system](gp:0GxexoWn2P), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). A super-Earth, it was initially left untouched in favor of its temperate neighbor, [Garron II](gp:VlMGMLM1lL). After the events of the [anti-Messer revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7) and the passing of the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP), the UEE conducted exhaustive studies to confirm that the planet was completely uninhabited. It was then cleared for mining in order to fund the restoration of Garron II's devastated biosphere.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","garron system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4bb8fe55-61f9-4052-8c4e-104cdec9714e"},
{"id":"garron-iv","gp":"RL6E6Dn49j","t":"Garron IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Garron IV is the fourth and final planet from the sun of the [Garron system](gp:0GxexoWn2P), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). A cold, barren, and rocky, it is largely undeveloped save for a memorial entitled The Sentinel that was erected by the UEE in memory of the lost civilization on [Garron II](gp:VlMGMLM1lL). It also serves as a sign of the government's commitment to protecting developing life in all known and yet-to-be-known systems.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","garron system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ae17f6b7-8288-4481-a3e9-5efd2e09714a"},
{"id":"garron-system","gp":"0GxexoWn2P","t":"Garron System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Garron system is a [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) that consists of a G-type main sequence star, three terrestrial planets, and one super-Earth. Discovered in SEY 2784 by Imperial Pathfinders, the Garron system was found to have a planet that was home to intelligent life. This news made waves across the UEE and initially, Imperator [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) proclaimed that the civilization would be contacted and uplifted. A team of scientists led by noted xenoanthropologist and linguist Dr. Michael Shiherlis was assigned to work from a nearby observation station to devise a means of contact. \n\nHowever, after it became apparent that there were abundant valuable resources on Garron II, Linton dismantled the team and showed interest in mining the planet. Shiherlis broke protocol and released vast amounts of information to the public in the hopes of embarrassing the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) to inaction. Instead, Linton incarcerated Shiherlis for his opposition and began to [terraform](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) Garron II. The anti-Messer organization Tide obtained footage of the resulting devastation and released it over [spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q). This sparked outrage among the public and kicked off [the events](gp:bE3rKa32P7) that led to the toppling of the [Messer dynasty](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/messer-dynasty) and Shiherlis' release from prison. In 2795, after the re-organization of the UEE government, the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) passed the Fair Chance Act to foster the development of potentially new civilizations and protect them from potential harm.","g":["uee system","fair chance act"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dac4ecdb-6c84-4b00-a2e5-9405b4be06e5"},
{"id":"gatac-manufacture-aotoangatak","gp":"bo13Earlar","t":"Gatac Manufacture (Ao't.o'a'Ng.at'ak)","k":"company","c":["Xi'an","Commerce"],"x":"Gatac Manufacture (Ao't.o'a'Ng.at'ak) is a commercial and industrial spacecraft manufacturer located on Tethle'a (Hyoton II). The company has a reputation in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) for producing cutting-edge and reliable cargo ships. After the SEY 2947 [Human-Xi'an Trade Initiative (HuXa)](gp:01LvKoLvZ8) went into effect, the company began funding research to create spacecraft adapted to the needs of both [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) and [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2). It released its first [Xi'an-Human ship](gp:VpMxKQx7E1) in 2951.","g":["gatac manufacture","ao't.o'a'ng.at'ak","house ng.at'ak","spacecraft manufacturer","vehicle manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/20b34777-0682-46f2-afb9-3d8f6bfd88ce"},
{"id":"gavin-e-hurston","gp":"RzPoAdZpEl","t":"Gavin E Hurston","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"\"Colonel\" Gavin E. Hurston (2867-present) is the current CEO of [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ). He succeeded his mother, Magda Hurston, who made the decision to purchase Stanton I from the United Empire of Earth (UEE). He has continued the policies of his predecessors, strip-mining the planet for resources and using Life/Labor-style contracts in place of employment.","g":["hurston dynamics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2011cf57-8533-40c1-bdaa-31c0170385a7"},
{"id":"geddon-system","gp":"bo1yaaL4wN","t":"Geddon System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Banu"],"x":"The Geddon system is a planetary system located in the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) that consists of an O-type main sequence star and one terrestrial planet. Directly connected to the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) via the Geddon-Corel jump point, it is frequently trafficked by haulers moving cargo between the two civilizations. [Takto (Geddon I)](gp:0jGynn5Nnn), the system's only planet, is a highly-respected center of manufacturing.","g":["banu system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4dbe1c35-07c8-4099-9efc-9875abd4ec2a"},
{"id":"gedinasho","gp":"RMXyG1z79B","t":"Gedinasho","k":"culture","c":["Fiction"],"x":"Gedinasho is a fictional hero character created by artist/writer Fief. Her adventures exploring unknown areas of space were chronicled in a comic that ran from 2432 to 2445. Numerous [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) series and movie adaptations were made of the comic throughout the 25th century. The asteroid belt of the [Charon system](gp:VarrdBl87w) was named after her.","g":["gediansho belt","gediansho","characters","fief"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d6deebc7-c6bc-4cb9-b3a6-cf6341435c23"},
{"id":"gedinasho-belt-charon-belt-alpha","gp":"0n11M2dYdJ","t":"Gedinasho Belt (Charon Belt Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Gedinasho belt (Charon belt alpha) is an asteroid belt in the [Charon system](gp:VarrdBl87w), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that orbits the system's sun between [Charon III](gp:RkGGMvDpoz) and [Charon IV](gp:VgEEq1w5dw). It was named after [Gedinasho](gp:RMXyG1z79B), a fictional hero character created by artist/writer Fief whose comics were adapted to vid multiple times in the 25th century. Merchant marine Max Keaton, who discovered the system, had been a fan of Gedinasho since childhood.","g":["gedinasho belt","charon belt alpha","charon system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3f88b253-1487-4ec4-83e8-0482a3318820"},
{"id":"gemini","gp":"RzPoOAZDxZ","t":"Gemini","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Gemini is a manufacturer of personal weaponry located in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The company began as a producer of kinetic weapons and only began offering laser-based systems following their acquisition of energy weapon start-up Octa in the late 2930s SEY. Current models include the LH86 pistol, R97 shotgun, C54 SMG, F55 LMG, A03 sniper rifle, H29 HMG and S71 assault rifle.","g":["octa","weapons manufacturer","arccorp (planet)","stanton iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/91d96bb8-af48-4ba2-88b5-656011c06126"},
{"id":"gemma","gp":"V7gM71L7mk","t":"Gemma","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human","Tevarin"],"x":"Gemma is the capital city of [Jalan (Elysium IV)](gp:VarAXY2zy2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), but formerly part of the Tevarin Empire. It was overtaken by the UEE after the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) surrendered to [Human-led](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) forces at the end of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546). Historically, it was a Tevarin stronghold and capital city, selected for its protective geographical features. The UEE has attempted to preserve its historic cultural buildings, but many were lost during the Tevarin wars, the subsequent [Purge](gp:R6dWB877Nn), and the assimilation of Tevarin culture that followed.","g":["jalan","elysium iv","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5dfeb67d-9e0e-4b7e-9dc7-3476ba7aea2a"},
{"id":"gen-terra-iv","gp":"RMNMv8ekn8","t":"Gen (Terra IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Gen is the fourth planet from the sun in the [Terra system](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and the second most populous. [Terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) on Gen was completed roughly a century after Terra (Terra III) was settled. Many military and administrative bodies from the UEE established headquarters on Gen, taking advantage of the system's seven jump points and the planet's proximity to Terra. Gen's population is thus largely made up of government workers. [Representatives](gp:0KnAzj9B1o) of Gen have made multiple bids for [Senatorial](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) representation, but no attempt has yet succeeded.","g":["gen","terra iv","terra system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fcb72bf6-f81c-4161-8d8c-4caddd0aed92"},
{"id":"genesis-belt-alpha","gp":"bZkZ9rlzKO","t":"Genesis Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Genesis belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the developing [Genesis system](gp:Rw1moXkwBB). Located between the second and third planets from its sun, its proximity to the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected world [Genesis II](gp:V7dp6XEX52) has made it off limits from potential industrial development. However, some of the larger asteroids have deposits of ice that are mined under strict government supervision as water supplies for many of the observation stations that orbit Genesis II.","g":["asteroid belt","genesis system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/aa568b1e-2ed9-4bcb-ac6a-656c47887fd6"},
{"id":"genesis-i","gp":"0qal7oJL8k","t":"Genesis I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Genesis I is a mesoplanet in the developing [Genesis system](gp:Rw1moXkwBB). Because it lacks a protective atmosphere, its surface is pockmarked with thousands of craters caused by meteorite bombardment, and its core is partially exposed. In 2933, the observation station Lalahon located in the planet's polar region was destroyed in a meteor strike. There were no casualties thanks to an early detection and evacuation, but the institute funding the station elected not to rebuild after it was unable to secure additional grant money from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["genesis system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9fc65ae8-7047-4acd-b30b-9158c01e4a17"},
{"id":"genesis-ii","gp":"V7dp6XEX52","t":"Genesis II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Genesis II is a terrestrial planet in the developing [Genesis system](gp:Rw1moXkwBB). Situated in the temperate green band around its star, it has oceans of liquid water interspersed with thickly forested continents. It was declared a protected planet under the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) the same year it was discovered in 2812 due to the presence of multiple sentient species on its surface and in its seas. In 2942, cephalopod-like, ocean-dwelling creatures were observed exploring one of the landmasses. This sparked a violent confrontation with the dominant land-based species. As the conflict continues, scientists and academics have begun to question the morality of noninterference in the war as required by the FCA.","g":["genesis system","habitable planet","habitable","unclaimed planet","developing planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5eacc3cc-4ffc-458b-a24b-5f16797f777d"},
{"id":"genesis-iii","gp":"0ODP9QpqMr","t":"Genesis III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Genesis III is an ice giant in the developing [Genesis system](gp:Rw1moXkwBB). Located beyond the frost line, it has an upper atmosphere of hydrogen and helium, and a mantle composed of volatile chemical compounds such as ammonia, methane, and water in a supercritical fluid state. Ranging in color from pale blue to almost white, it starkly stands out against the surrounding blackness of space.","g":["genesis system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7817f7c5-a88b-4d10-8ce0-c147e32048d9"},
{"id":"genesis-system","gp":"Rw1moXkwBB","t":"Genesis System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Genesis system is a [developing planetary system](gp:V7gMqAvgv2) that consists of a G-type main sequence star, a mesoplanet, a terrestrial planet, an ice giant, and an asteroid belt. Discovered in SEY 2812, it was immediately evident that the second planet from the sun was lush with vegetation. Many [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) companies put in early bids with the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government, but were ultimately barred from developing the system when the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) was invoked after multiple intelligent species were detected on [Genesis II's](gp:V7dp6XEX52) surface. The system's other two planets are situated on either side of the [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), and are poor candidates for terraformation.","g":["developing system","unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8f340148-5db0-409e-a6e2-df96875acab1"},
{"id":"geohacking","gp":"R9Bwj1BZAN","t":"Geohacking","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Geohacking is a colloquialism that refers to the practice of altering the environment of an already habitable planet. Geohacking is different from [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) in that it is done upon planets and moons that already have established atmospheres and environments. It can also refer to modifications done on a smaller scale, and primarily to alter a world's weather system. The [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) utilizes the planets of the Th.us'ūng system for its ongoing research into geohacking and terraforming technologies.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/364cc592-11ef-4462-8848-b4e30b4b041d"},
{"id":"ghata-veras","gp":"bBzPN2lLG9","t":"Ghata Veras","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Ghata Veras (2887 - present) is the [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) of [Lo (Corel III)](gp:VarAoYEQYd), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). After serving in the [UEE Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) for fifteen years, Veras earned his [Citizenship](gp:RLMmop8rkr) and ran for a seat on the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) of Lo under a campaign promise to decrease taxes on middle and lower income individuals. He took office in 2920, and while on the Council, joined a committee that successfully pushed through a 3% decrease on income tax planet-wide. In 2941, he was elected as Senator of Lo on the [Centralist](gp:01dWmzB3aG) party ticket. Since taking office, he has continued to fight for lower taxes, and has helped craft several consumer-protection laws that decrease the amount of data that can be harvested and sold without notice. Ghata spearheaded a campaign in 2943 to decommission the maximum security prison QuarterDeck located on [Kellog VI](gp:R6dAQZgGQe), citing a history of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-rights violations. Although the proposal was ultimately unsuccessful, political commentators expect Ghata to try again under a more favorable political climate.","g":["uee senator","lo","corel iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/20b3bf02-b978-4a47-a393-a4ebe171e4be"},
{"id":"giant-yar-moth","gp":"bBzkEK1Azo","t":"Giant Yar Moth","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"The giant Yar moth is a flying arthropod indigenous to [Yar (Centauri II)](gp:R6dd5pyOZ5). Typically, it has a wingspan of about 20 centimeters, making it one of the largest moths on Yar. It survives in the harsh Red Desert by drinking the nectar of desert flowers and juices from vegetation and primarily flying in the early morning or evening. It is one of the most common pollinators of plants that grow in the Red Desert, particularly the [kavische](gp:bZkyPrB42d) cactus.","g":["yar","centauri ii","arthropods"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/53084a03-0ec5-4623-aaf4-536769873407"},
{"id":"giboshi-bane","gp":"0KxpypYnao","t":"Giboshi Bane","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The giboshi bane is a genetically modified bush that was created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke) in 2930. Its deep green leaves were designed to excrete an oil that can be safely rubbed on skin and used as an insect repellent. As an unintentional side effect of the genetic modification process, the plant's trunk exudes a scent similar to the fruit of the [oza](gp:RPDDZz4Zam) tree.","g":["rayari inc","bushes"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6e60c06d-0fac-4ae6-a278-c3d2348a379d"},
{"id":"gideons-belt-virgil-belt-alpha","gp":"RvlBgKOve3","t":"Gideon's Belt (Virgil Belt Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"Gideon's belt (Virgil belt alpha) is the only asteroid belt in the [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). While the system was part of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE), deposits of iron, titanium, and other metals in the belt supported a modest mining industry that kept [Cyrene (Virgil I)](gp:VlMBNGnxK5) supplied with the raw materials needed to construct its settlements. Vanduul ships have been observed harvesting resources from the asteroids.","g":["gideon's belt","virgil belt alpha","asteroid belt","virgil system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d1899375-aa06-4b30-a338-1c0bd24662a5"},
{"id":"gio","gp":"RMN8kv8AeA","t":"GIO","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"GIO (Geological Investigation Outpost) is a mining outpost owned and operated by [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA) on [Baker IV](gp:RPD8Xr8Xjq), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). GIO mostly consists of a vast network of interconnected mining tunnels deep underground, marked on the planet's surface by a group of utilitarian buildings. In 2945, Shubin held the Shubin Mine Rescue Challenge in GIO, an event in which participants competed to win prizes in categories such as angle vertical rescue, firefighting, and zero-G accident rescue.","g":["shubin interstellar","baker iv","outpost"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/868a2e79-3669-44cb-a742-c7e91fcf3888"},
{"id":"glaciem-ring-nyx-belt-alpha","gp":"0Kx8gwkXMP","t":"Glaciem Ring (Nyx Belt Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Glaciem ring (Nyx belt alpha) is a dense asteroid belt located between the second and third planets in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). Outlaw raids in Nyx are believed to operate out of bases established within the depths of the belt. The largest settlement in the Glaciem ring, [Levski](gp:0dXQqBMAOp), is located on the asteroid [Delamar](gp:0GxoZnAGrg).","g":["glaciem ring","nyx belt alpha","nyx system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cbf9221a-6fb6-48b1-a219-21fdaeaa5aa3"},
{"id":"gladiator","gp":"RWwZQYNy4a","t":"Gladiator","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Gladiator is a two-seat light bomber developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). It was designed as a combination fighter-bomber companion to Anvil's [F7A Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) line of spacecraft, offering the UEEN the ability to significantly increase the overall offensive power of smaller escort carriers and support ships.The Gladiator has been a key part of the UEEN's skirmisher forces since the 2930s SEY and was recently made available to the civilian market for private enterprises and militia groups.","g":["bomber","anvil aerospace","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/83bf8b36-cb11-42db-bd3f-3b51085ce936"},
{"id":"gladius-valiant","gp":"bo1exWa8W7","t":"Gladius Valiant","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Gladius Valiant is a special edition of the [Gladius](gp:0j46NP5eB3) light fighter developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). Created as a part of the Masters of Flight ship series in conjunction with the flight-sim [Arena Commander](gp:VyvY5LQXd6), the Valiant pays homage to famed pilot [Condi Hillard](gp:RX3dlOezZM), best known for being the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to defeat a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) in ship-to-ship combat. The Valiant is equipped with a loadout designed for dogfighting, and features custom edition livery honoring Hillard's ship.","g":["gladius","aegis dynamics","fighter","light fighter","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0e79e88c-5e4b-4a00-87d1-8944f4c8861b"},
{"id":"glaive","gp":"bo1dozJpB2","t":"Glaive","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Vanduul"],"x":"The \"Glaive\" is the official [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) designation for a fighter spacecraft operated by [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) forces. The Glaive is notable for its double bladed wings, in contrast to the [Scythe's](gp:0qakL3mmmq) single bladed wing, as well as the inclusion of a missile rack and a neutron gun. Glaives appear with a much lower frequency than Scythes. Owing to their proficiency in battle, there is some indication that they are typically flown by veteran Vanduul pilots, though this has yet to be proven. Human manufacturer [Esperia](gp:0OaBKL7wlv) has produced limited numbers of a Glaive replica spacecraft for civilian sale.","g":["vanduul glaive","vanduul spacecraft","fighter","medium fighter","esperia"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1dcd6775-e86e-4984-bbea-7cd24f50454f"},
{"id":"gliese-belt-alpha","gp":"VpMyYYJZMA","t":"Gliese Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Gliese belt alpha is the first asteroid belt from the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Packed with valuable ores and minerals, it is an active mining site and is home to countless [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) engaged in mining, shipping, processing, or protecting resources. Some disputes over mining rights have broken out between Soulis, leading towards an upsurge in the presence of security and mercenary Soulis.","g":["asteroid belt","gliese system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/77394252-c7e2-424b-b304-07b6a20871d5"},
{"id":"gliese-belt-beta","gp":"V7dEXXqoLn","t":"Gliese Belt Beta","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Gliese belt beta is the second belt from the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Located between [Nogo (Gliese IV)](gp:R4jEkkOAkW) and [Gliese V](gp:0NjkMMBx8w), it is packed with ancient outposts and abandoned rigs, left there from an earlier period in which resources were abundant. It is a popular salvaging site and is home to myriad [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) in that field.","g":["asteroid belt","gliese system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/01e6b4c5-e845-4d5d-9aeb-26dbbbad76a5"},
{"id":"gliese-cluster-gamma","gp":"01LNoo33GG","t":"Gliese Cluster Gamma","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Gliese cluster gamma is the farthest asteroid cluster from the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Only sparsely populated with asteroids, it sees little traffic in comparison with the alpha and beta belts. Some smaller [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) have made a go of mining the cluster, despite its remote position and hazardous mining conditions.","g":["asteroid cluster","gliese system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/31459072-99c3-43a6-9d95-c683434c5140"},
{"id":"gliese-i","gp":"RX3MrrJzOZ","t":"Gliese I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Gliese I is the first planet from the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa) [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). An iron planet with a superheated ferromagnetic core that is partially exposed to vacuum, its intensely hot conditions make landing on its surface nearly impossible without specialized technology. The planet sees some traffic from [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) who say that being near the core helps ease pain associated with cybernetic limbs. There is no evidence that this is true, but there are numerous merchants on [Nogo (Gliese IV)](gp:R4jEkkOAkW) that advertise transportation services to and from Gliese I based on the popularity of this claim.","g":["gliese system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0beabea7-4464-42f5-832f-9a30a1b64d17"},
{"id":"gliese-ii","gp":"0QlXMMp2ko","t":"Gliese II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Gliese II is the second planet from the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A smog planet, it has a dense, high-pressure atmosphere of carbon dioxide and nitrogen. Surface conditions on Gliese II can be hazardous to many spacecraft if they remain there for too long. Uniquely amongst the other planets in the system, Gliese II rotates in a retrograde direction.","g":["gliese system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3d639233-cfca-4be3-bb61-a83d1655d30b"},
{"id":"gliese-iii","gp":"VDzavvNeY8","t":"Gliese III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Gliese III is the third planet from the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A terrestrial world with an unbreathable atmosphere, it is dotted with various [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) engaged in a wide variety of trades, from farming to mining to manufacturing. Each Souli is located within a sealed settlement to create conditions that are just safe enough to ensure maximum work efficiency. Territories regularly change hands as Soulis fold and form.","g":["gliese system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/aa661511-d35e-464a-920c-be62db31d922"},
{"id":"gliese-system","gp":"V7dEXXD4wa","t":"Gliese System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Banu"],"x":"The Gliese system is a planetary system in the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) that consists of a type-A main sequence star,  three terrestrial planets, one smog planet, one gas giant, one protoplanet, an asteroid cluster, and two asteroid belts. A bustling hub of commerce and cultural exchange, its resource-rich planets and asteroid belts have made it a center of trade between the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) and other civilizations. Most Banu in the system reside in the sprawling [Lyris flotilla](gp:bo1yaak7LL), located near the habitable planet [Nogo (Gliese IV)](gp:R4jEkkOAkW). The Protectorate has allowed [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to set up a colony there, but no Banu live alongside them.","g":["banu system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f06398d6-2bec-4cb0-a91b-594510b62f00"},
{"id":"gliese-v","gp":"0NjkMMBx8w","t":"Gliese V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Gliese V is the fifth planet from the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Clouds of water vapor float in the upper reaches of its hydrogen-methane atmosphere, creating bands of white, light grey, and dark grey. [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-owned corporation [Terragra](gp:0Gz5Z39z1a) uses Gliese V as the source for their line of bottled water.","g":["gliese system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fbd7da9e-72ca-4b9c-90de-3400af75c84b"},
{"id":"gliese-vi","gp":"RX3MrrQ9yK","t":"Gliese VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Gliese VI is the sixth and final planet from the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A protoplanet, it is oblate in shape and has no atmosphere. An unknown [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron) built a statue of [Cassa](gp:02kg3POv8e), the Patron of Luck here in roughly SEY 2200 CE, according to carbon dating. New trade Soulis departing from the Gliese system leave luck offerings here before starting their first journeys.","g":["gliese system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1c35919c-7a0b-4e32-88f8-1f87e172e17d"},
{"id":"glow","gp":"V3GP35nLK2","t":"Glow","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Glow is a street drug derived from the empathogen–entactogen neonazacyclicdienorthoamphetamine, more commonly known as neon. Sold in the form of brightly-colored capsules, when it is taken orally it can leave a glowing residue on the tongue. It was formulated by unknown makers to have a more potent effect on the nervous system than neon, which in turn creates more euphoric feelings and fewer hallucinations in its users. Once the effect wears off, however, some users experience days of suicidal depression as their brain chemistry normalizes.","g":["empathogen-entactogen","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b919e4bd-59cb-40aa-a641-749479ce76a8"},
{"id":"gold-horizon","gp":"bmNrApJp3P","t":"Gold Horizon","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Gold Horizon was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) orbital platform manufacturing company that went defunct in 2655. Established as a prospecting corporation in 2546, the company transitioned to manufacturing prefabricated mining stations, and then to terraforming support stations, which made up the bulk of its business. [Imperator Corsen Messer V](gp:0OaB8O6awO) nationalized all terraforming support concerns in 2654, halting the company's main line of profit. Gold Horizon officially ceased business in 2655, but some of their old stations can still be found around the universe.","g":["orbital platform manufacturer","messer era","corsen messer v"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dfcb510e-af94-4a37-b9f8-adee5f9bb1dc"},
{"id":"golden-lion","gp":"bBp6BYoLK8","t":"Golden Lion","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Golden Lion is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) ballistic munitions manufacturer. The name derives from their flagship product, a line of gold-colored hollow point shells. In addition to their hollow point rounds, Golden Lion produces ammunition in a wide range of calibers. Their products are popular among ballistic weapons enthusiasts.","g":["munitions manufacturer"]},
{"id":"golden-medmon","gp":"0n11yZQQKv","t":"Golden Medmon","k":"life","c":["Food and Beverages","Plants"],"x":"The golden medmon is a fruit indigenous to Jalan (Elysium IV), cultivated by [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) over hundreds of years for its nutritious seeds and hydrating flesh. In its natural state, the fruit is very firm and astringent. While Tevarin prefer to eat it raw, [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) prefer to let the fruit soften once it has been harvested. After the fruit wrinkles and darkens, the flesh loses much of its moisture and gains a very sweet flavor along with a creamy consistency reminiscent of caramel.","g":["fruit","trees","food"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8f1011a3-9b6e-496f-bb6a-8625859f9994"},
{"id":"golem-tek","gp":"Rvgp44NEKO","t":"Golem-Tek","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Golem-Tek is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) retailer of industrial armor, EVA equipment, and flight wear. Founded in 2941, they market their stores to blue-collar workers, and tend to be located in heavy industrial areas. The company expanded into selling body armor and environment protection suits aimed at miners and salvage crews in 2944, with licensing agreements to offer products from [Basilisk](gp:R9BwxzG9KZ) and Virgil Ltd.","g":["armor retailer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5f107012-58c2-4e64-a717-d3237bef44f5"},
{"id":"gonn-oberon-i","gp":"VJXAYN81Q5","t":"Gonn (Oberon I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Gonn is the first planet from the neutron star of the unclaimed [Oberon system](gp:VYLdlgMqop). A super-Earth that was once the core of a brown dwarf, this planet is rich in carbon and has long been rumored to hide vast deposits of diamonds that have yet to be discovered. Because the extreme environmental conditions make it difficult for automated facilities to operate, most miners that operate on Gonn are independent. According to local legend, one of the earliest miners on the planet used to chase away rivals while yelling, in a [Cathcart](gp:RL6524vWO3) regional dialect, \"Chinewa bedda get gonn,\" thus giving Oberon I its name.","g":["gonn","oberon i","oberon system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f833cb58-e34b-4aa6-a71f-c258496aa40c"},
{"id":"gorgon-defender-industries","gp":"RWwZDn5xwp","t":"Gorgon Defender Industries","k":"company","c":["Military","Commerce","Human"],"x":"Gorgon Defender Industries is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) spacecraft shield systems manufacturer. Gorgon was founded by survivors of [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) (2884) interested in selling high-quality defensive systems to civilians. In 2942, Gorgon signed their first military contract with the United Empire of Earth to produce shield modules for combat spacecraft.","g":["spacecraft shield manufacturer","spacecraft component manufacturer","fall of caliban","vann","croshaw iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/52e9a6a9-3c13-4c68-9c7c-c0c40695f4f0"},
{"id":"goss-i","gp":"RegqZ3ze8y","t":"Goss I","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Goss I is the first planet from the suns of the [Goss system](gp:RxnYdDZj96), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The system's breadbasket, much of the planet consists of farmland dedicated to supplying itself and its sister planets with food. Instead of an ocean, it is covered in springs, lakes, rivers, seas and other bodies of water. The largest of these, the Salann Sea, is so salty that it is uninhabitable to all but a few species.","g":["goss system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/39ebeac9-b379-4cdc-bdf7-0bdc655a16fc"},
{"id":"goss-iii","gp":"VlMnJ8v4J5","t":"Goss III","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human","Military"],"x":"Goss III is a terrestrial super-Earth located in the [Goss system](gp:RxnYdDZj96), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The furthest world from its systems suns, Goss III is temperate and heavily forested with multiple tropical and subtropical biomes. It is largely undeveloped save for [Port Fairfax](gp:0jG8wK5LDJ), a mid-sized [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) base and a large military hospital complex. Many soldiers injured in the ongoing conflict between the [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) are treated here.","g":["goss system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9f268c6c-5c84-40b1-acd0-e53e17a15104"},
{"id":"goss-system","gp":"RxnYdDZj96","t":"Goss System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Goss system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that consists of two K-type main sequence stars, two rocky planets, and one super-Earth. All three of its planets are habitable, and have skies streaked with bands of turquoise, orange, and gold due the system's proximity to the nearby [Olympus Pool](gp:bmGxJA35Wl); a dense, highly-reflective cloud of cosmic dust. These unique skies combined with beautiful coastlines and warm seas have made its second planet [Cassel (Goss II)](gp:RPDy6gqX7Z) a major tourist destination. Thanks to the revenue generated from tourism and the abundance of food and resources found on [Goss I](gp:RegqZ3ze8y), the system is largely self-sufficient.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d9629452-0eb7-4757-9198-4b919bcd4aef"},
{"id":"grand-flabellum","gp":"bo1aJaAJ32","t":"Grand Flabellum","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The grand flabellum is a genetically modified plant created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke). In 2930, it debuted as part of their new line of plants designed to aid in the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) process. Before a planet establishes adequate plant cover, harsh winds pose a danger to settlements. The grand flabellum has a wide leaf structure and deep root system that help it act as an erosion break.","g":["rayari inc","herbaceous plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/73c5096a-cc77-4c3c-bf7a-ea28ea2ac6a4"},
{"id":"green-ellis-iii","gp":"RWoNrNeLKP","t":"Green (Ellis III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Green (Ellis III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A warm oceanic world dotted with high-end resorts and small cities, Green is home to the most popular spacecraft race in the UEE, the [Murray Cup](gp:bE3r71yZ87). Each year, its resorts fill with racing fans eager to be close to the action. In the off-season, Green's economy relies on a steady flow of tourists who visit the planet to take advantage of its mild climate and immaculate beaches.","g":["green","ellis iii","ellis system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/09e53778-210e-4c93-a922-ccb7f4fded6e"},
{"id":"green-band","gp":"ReJaAjgOwy","t":"Green Band","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Also known as the habitable zone, Goldilocks zone, or circumstellar habitable zone, the green band of a planetary system is the area in which it is possible for liquid water to exist on the surface of a planet given sufficient atmospheric pressure, either naturally or through artificial intervention. This area varies from star to star, and is calculated based on stellar luminosity, among other factors.","g":["terraforming"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d2ed52e2-77f7-4476-86b7-ad755e7b204e"},
{"id":"green-imperial-housing-exchange-grim-hex","gp":"0jGGDvYm93","t":"Green Imperial Housing Exchange (Grim HEX)","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"The Green Imperial Housing Exchange, also known as Grim HEX, is a housing exchange located in the ring of [Yela (Stanton 2c)](gp:bo1xJPgMNL) that was closed in 2938 and subsequently fell under the control of criminals. Completed in 2903, the exchange was constructed inside an asteroid to provide affordable housing for workers and supervisors tied to nearby mining operations. Profits from rent easily covered the cost of maintenance until 2933, when most of the mines in the ring of Yela began to decline. Many of the inhabitants left when their jobs ended, cutting off the station's main source of revenue, and it fell into disrepair. After it was officially shut down in 2938, squatters, smugglers, transients, and others moved in, and a black market established itself there away from the jurisdiction of authorities on [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav). The first recorded usage of the nickname Grim HEX was from a police interrogation of a local criminal in 2938.","g":["green imperial housing exchange","grim hex","stanton system","sealed settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/60901c57-d5ca-4613-89ce-090a5d07d0e3"},
{"id":"greycat-industrial","gp":"02BQlmgoDy","t":"Greycat Industrial","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Greycat Industrial is a manufacturing company that produces armor, industrial equipment, and utility vehicles. Founded on Mars in SEY 2337, Greycat is one of the oldest still-operating corporations in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Early in its history, Greycat's first successful product was advanced armor plating created to protect mine workers, followed by the Pyro RYT Multi-Tool. Today, Greycat's best-known product is the [Personal Transport Vehicle](gp:bBp6YmmjGJ) (PTV), sometimes referred to informally as the Greycat.","g":["armor manufacturer","mining equipment manufacturer","ground transportation manufacturer","commercial and industrial goods manufacturer","vehicle manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f989bb19-9578-44e8-a2ab-b0ab89087df1"},
{"id":"grindstone-boots","gp":"01LjekE1nr","t":"Grindstone Boots","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Grindstone Boots is a workwear clothing brand that primarily produces footwear. Tough and long-lasting, the company has a longstanding reputation among blue-collar workers for making products that can stand up to the abuses common in industrial environments. Grindstone often incorporates recycled materials into its products.","g":["clothing manufacturer","footwear manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f662d494-542d-412d-8510-9a42c26c6e13"},
{"id":"gnp","gp":"VDoP3jlA69","t":"Groupe Nouveau Paradigme (GNP)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Groupe Nouveau Paradigme (GNP) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) spacecraft component manufacturer that sells sensors, engines, and software. An unusually structured company, GNP was founded via an alliance between the governments of the Helios, Odin, Charon, and Baker systems in order to utilize facilities abandoned by the defunct FarSeer corporation. As a public company, GNP redirects all of its profits into further development and builds out facilities in the four aligned systems. Today, GNP produces the Tonnerre line of freighter power plants and the V601-11 RADAR used by the military for current-generation [Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk)  spacecraft.","g":["groupe nouveau paradigme","gnp","spacecraft component manufacturer","farseer corporation"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/243c776a-aaee-4cd3-b337-44998944e338"},
{"id":"gurzil-belt-alpha","gp":"RX36nZAw28","t":"Gurzil Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Gurzil belt alpha is a protoplanetary disk that orbits the sun of the developing [Gurzil system](gp:0Kxydrxd45). Still in its infancy, it is a swirling mass of dust, asteroids, and planetessimals. During the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793), many spacecraft from both sides of the conflict were lost in the Gurzil belt, officially due to poor visibility. Salvage companies under contract from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government are engaged in long-term cleanup operations to remove wrecks and anti-ship mines that were abandoned in the system after the territory was ceded to the UEE under the terms of the 2789 [Akari-Kr.ē](gp:bE3rKrl5z6) Treaty.","g":["developing system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/146742d0-4b6d-4c6a-8a8d-d4f506185dea"},
{"id":"gurzil-system","gp":"0Kxydrxd45","t":"Gurzil System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Gurzil system is a developing planetary system that consists of a K-type main sequence star and a vast protoplanetary disk. First discovered in 2539 by [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) explorer Dahunsil Kosoko after he spent three weeks scanning the Hadrian system, it was discovered again in 2542 by [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) explorer Nē\" se Ruoth via a jump point from the R.il'a system, a stronghold of the Xi'an military. The [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) government responded by incorporating the then-Odara system into the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) and changing its name to Gurzil, after an ancient Human deity of war. Following the [fall](gp:bE3rKa32P7) of the [Messers](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/messer-dynasty) and dissolution of the Perry Line, Gurzil was placed under UEE control. The Senate debated placing the system under the protection of the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) but ultimately decided against it. Today, it is inhabited mainly by miners, salvagers, and scientists engaged in the long-term study of early planetary system development.","g":["developing system","perry line"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/17205028-402a-458c-8a49-efbae62ba9e3"},
{"id":"gyson-inc","gp":"0dX8odAZ1L","t":"Gyson Inc.","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Gyson Inc. is a discount clothing, industrial goods, and armor brand known for offering low-cost products. The company has come under fire for quality control issues multiple times since it entered the market, but it continues to weather any periods of backlash due to its extensive catalog and rock-bottom prices.","g":["clothing manufacturer","gyson inc"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/382ee307-7042-4b76-820b-b2c831e997f7"},
{"id":"hauu-thusuung-v","gp":"bmGwynMYrl","t":"H.au'u (Th.us'ūng V)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"H.au'u (Th.us'ūng V) is the fifth world from the sun of the [Th.us'ūng system](gp:V8WeExnJge), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A dwarf planet with very low gravity, it lacks a substantial atmosphere, and conditions on its surface are nearly identical to being in the vacuum of space. It is believed that the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government utilizes the planet to conduct experiments here that are considered too hazardous to be done elsewhere in the system.","g":["h.au'u","th.us'uung v","th.us'uung system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f88e9075-2e76-4299-ae80-2cf38d6d316d"},
{"id":"habidash","gp":"RL6XB7WpPv","t":"Habidash","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Habidash is a clothing brand that produces outdoor-oriented clothing designed to withstand extreme environments. Known for creating garments that have flowing fabrics, the company's products typically sell well among residents of newly-terraformed worlds or those who travel through or reside in unclaimed systems. Its pieces take inspiration from historic garments worn by the people of [Earth](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) (Sol III).","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d57b7db2-4a6a-424e-ab4a-167cfdcdda47"},
{"id":"hades-extinction-event","gp":"V8gJZNZlKG","t":"Hades Extinction Event","k":"history","c":["Archaeology"],"x":"The [Hadesian](gp:RPPxMqdkpE) extinction event marks when the earliest known inhabitants of the Hades system disappeared. Current research estimates that the extinction event occurred at roughly 300000 BCE, but ongoing study of the archaeological record of the lost civilization continues to refine science's understanding of what happened. There are multiple theories of what specifically caused the extinction event. One of the more widely accepted hypotheses is that the Hadesians were wiped out by a devastating interplanetary war. Detractors point to a lack of evidence for technology that could have caused destruction on such a large scale.","g":["hades system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/65760910-2daf-4445-9168-07b6f410e621"},
{"id":"hades-i","gp":"Rw1GnEjB4B","t":"Hades I","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"Hades I is the first planet from the sun of the [Hades system](gp:RAX3mnkp8v). Located just on the inner edge of the system's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), ruins on its surface suggest that the lost civilization of Hades may once have operated colonies there in spite of its high temperature. It is dotted with impact craters that seem to have been caused by weapons. Some scholars believe that Hades I once had an atmosphere, but it was blasted away during the war that ultimately destroyed the [Hadesians](gp:RPPxMqdkpE). Research to settle this question is ongoing.","g":["hades system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/34465283-3a5f-401e-abd5-12ec40ce2a32"},
{"id":"hades-ii","gp":"VYLAnPpr5D","t":"Hades II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Hades II is the second planet from the sun of the [Hades system](gp:RAX3mnkp8v). Once inhabited by the lost [Hadesian](gp:RPPxMqdkpE) civilization, ruins of ancient cities can be found on the planet under layers of volcanic ash. The lack of moisture and air underneath the ash layers has kept the objects that lay within them almost perfectly preserved. They are of special interest to archaeologists because they represent the best remains of the destroyed Hadesian culture. Any ruins left exposed to the violent atmosphere of the dead planet have been eradicated over time.","g":["hades system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/49e9f180-61ca-4b65-8324-6e7263272f4f"},
{"id":"hades-iii","gp":"bBzKmr811J","t":"Hades III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Hades III is a smog planet in the [Hades system](gp:RAX3mnkp8v). Its high-pressure, toxic atmosphere covers a landscape riddled with impact craters and the scant remains of abandoned cities. Due to dangerous conditions, researchers have only been able to make a few expeditions to explore and document these ruins. Planetary scans show that while nearly all of these sites have been eroded away, many more ruins lie buried beneath the surface.","g":["hades system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2386f9a3-cd23-40d3-93b0-616c619d877a"},
{"id":"hades-iv","gp":"VDzqmrGdw8","t":"Hades IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Hades IV is a former planet in the [Hades system](gp:RAX3mnkp8v). Once a sizable terrestrial world, it is split into two large pieces. The leading theory as to the cause of the planet's bifurcation is that it was likely impacted by a weapon of mass destruction during the ancient war that eradicated all life from the system. It's unclear if the world was ever inhabited, but its destruction indicates that it was strategically important to the [Hadesians](gp:RPPxMqdkpE). Any structures that may have existed on its surface were obliterated when the planet was destroyed.","g":["hades system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/14fc4f50-a2ed-4f8d-b997-f1c586dfa6f5"},
{"id":"hades-system","gp":"RAX3mnkp8v","t":"Hades System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"# HADES SYSTEM\nThe Hades system is a planetary system that consists of an F-type main sequence star, a mesoplanet, two terrestrial planets, and one broken terrestrial planet. First visited by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) in SEY 2531, it was immediately obvious that the system had once been home to a previously unknown [spacefaring civilization](gp:RPPxMqdkpE) that vanished after an interplanetary war. Although officially [unclaimed](gp:VgExMejDPx), the Hades is loosely protected by a mixture of private security firms guarding academic expeditions and sparse [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) personnel protecting the trafficked shipping lane that runs through the system. \n\n# PLANETARY SYSTEM\nHades, the system's star, is an F-type main sequence star roughly five billion years old. The closest planetary body to Hades is [Hades I](gp:Rw1GnEjB4B), a mesoplanet covered with impact craters. Two of its three terrestrial planets, [Hades II](gp:VYLAnPpr5D) and [Hades III](gp:bBzKmr811J), are in the temperate zone of the system's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy). [Hades IV](gp:VDzqmrGdw8), a terrestrial planet that was cracked in half by what historians believe was an ancient weapon, is located in the green band's frigid outer edge. There is evidence that at one point, most of the planets in the system were inhabited, including the dangerously hot Hades I.\n\n# DISCOVERY\nIn 2515, the scanners of the tramp freighter *Merry Crow* picked up an anomaly in the [Nexus system](gp:RWoj8pnGma). After an investigation, the crew found that it was a previously undocumented [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY). At the time, they were in possession of several hundred freight units of stolen fusion drives, which they were smuggling to the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ). The crew voted to keep the jump point's location to themselves and continue on their route rather than risk arrest by reporting the discovery. Although they planned to return to the jump point and navigate it to determine whether it connected to a known system or a new system, which would net them a much larger payout, circumstances prevented this. In 2529, the ship's navigator Jake Tapps became the only survivor of this crew when a deal went bad and the others were killed in a firefight. Tapps sold the logbooks of the *Merry Crow* to the Dynamo Corporation in 2531. \n\nAfter navigating the jump point, the Dynamo Corporation realized they had discovered a new planetary system and dispatched a team to survey their find. Initial scans revealed remnants of a previously-unknown ancient civilization on most of its planets. One worker commented that the desolate ruins looked like cities of the dead, and the company began to call the system Hades after an ancient Human god of death and the underworld. At first, leadership of the company wanted to proceed with [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) in spite of these ruins, but when it was confirmed that Hades II and Hades III could not be terraformed under the limits of then-current technology, they elected to turn the system over to the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) government and the collect substantial reward money it offered for their discovery. \n\n# HISTORY\nThe UPE claimed the new system in light of its historical significance. Early expeditions were extensive, and [xenoarchaeologists](gp:0QlOdMyvPo) excavated and documented a great deal of information. However, the advent of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) in 2541 led to the UPE retracting their protection of the system in favor of directing military resources to the ongoing conflict. When Imperator [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) took power in 2546, the newly formed [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government continued to leave the system unprotected, leaving it vulnerable to grave robbers. Researchers had to hire private security for protection against these outlaws, which slowed down any new expeditions to a trickle. \n\nIn 2647, the xenoarchaeological faculty of [Astravin University at Cestulus (AUC)](gp:box52XYpDL) published a joint paper outlining their theory that an interplanetary war wiped out the Hadesian civilization. Imperator [Corsen Messer V](gp:0OaB8O6awO) grew interested in the possibility that ancient weapons of mass destruction might still be in Hades, and ordered the UEE Marines to conduct a thorough search. Many building sites and artifacts were destroyed as a side effect of this unregulated hunt, erasing untold amounts of possible sources of information about the Hadesians and their way of life. \n\nIt wasn't until the [fall of the Messers](gp:bE3rKa32P7) in 2792 that Humans began to consider claiming Hades again. Hundreds of academic institutions across the UEE signed a petition asking the government to take responsibility for the invaluable system and bring it under their protection. However, the UEE's ongoing conflict with the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) took priority over the safety of an archaeological site, and the system remains unclaimed to this day despite ongoing petitions. \n\n# HADESIAN CIVILIZATION\nMost historians and archaeologists believe that the Hadesian civilization existed until sometime between 300,000 and 290,000 BCE. At that point, the Hadesians had colonized at least three of the four planets in the system. Hades II and Hades III were the most densely populated, and Hades I was home to a handful of settlements. It is not certain whether the civilization originated on Hades II or Hades III. Both planets have atmospheres that may once have supported life, evidence of ancient oceans and riverbeds, and are covered in the ruins of demolished cities. Fragments of writing recovered in the system are written in an identical language that has yet to be deciphered, suggesting that the planets were closely culturally related, and that there was trade and travel between them. \n\nThere is strong evidence that a devastating interplanetary war wiped out the once thriving civilization. The surface of each planet is covered in impact craters and the soil is contaminated by heavy metals and radioactivity. It is likely that the atmospheres of Hades II and Hades III were poisoned either through fallout from the conflict or via sabotage. If Hades I had an atmosphere at some point, as analysis of its surface has suggested, it was annihilated during the war. In these conditions, it is very unlikely that any form of life could survive. Additionally, the bifurcation of Hades IV implies that the Hadesians were in possession of a weapon capable of destroying entire planets, which may have been the ultimate instrument of their extinction. \n\nMuch of the artifacts of this civilization were lost thanks to the consequences of this war. Structures and goods that were not destroyed during the fighting were worn down by erosion, and any organic remains decayed into dust. On Hades II in some areas, a deep layer of ash lies on top of preserved buildings, offering the closest picture of daily life in the Hades system at the time of their disappearance. \n\n# HADES CRYPTID\nSince the system was open for travel, multiple people have reportedly seen a creature aboard their ships. It was first sighted in 2602 by navjumper Eli Thorn. According to Thorn, he caught something out of the corner of his eye as he was climbing down a ladder to middeck. He described it as a bipedal body with exposed musculature that was covered in blue veins. When he tried to get a direct look at it, the ship suddenly rocked, and it vanished. \n\nMany such sightings have been reported since Thorn first shared his account, with several people claiming they believe the creature is one of the long lost Hadesians themselves or possibly a ghost of a deceased Hadesian. Descriptions vary; some say the creature has multiple, tentacle-like appendages, while others say it has two arms. Some report that the encounter filled them with a sense of dread, and others feel a sense of urgency, like the creature is trying to communicate with them. All agree that when they try to look directly at it, it disappears.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3bd841f2-4d6b-45c5-ae57-cb5bc185118c"},
{"id":"hadesians","gp":"RPPxMqdkpE","t":"Hadesians","k":"culture","c":["Civilizations","Archaeology"],"x":"Hadesian is the colloquial name for the indigenous inhabitants from the Hades system that achieved interplanetary space flight. They suffered a mass extinction at an undetermined point before the system's discovery in 2515. Precise dating has proven difficult, due to the harsh conditions on the surface of each previously-inhabited planet and the adverse effect of radiation from an unknown weapon or device.","g":["hades system","hades extinction event","extinct civilizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/938afbfb-8c16-4263-b7d2-9c9d44686e7b"},
{"id":"hadrian-belt-alpha","gp":"VYLx6AQA8v","t":"Hadrian Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Hadrian belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the [Hadrian system](gp:RX3r6jlZok), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that orbits between the system's second and third planets. Although it is abundant in resources, no corporation has elected to mine it due to the presence of undetonated anti-ship mines that remain from the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (2530 - 2793). In 2936, independent miner Yubyeol Greene was killed in an explosion when her ship accidentally grazed an active mine.","g":["asteroid belt","hadrian system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9d685d26-2570-467f-a70a-78d7229a1229"},
{"id":"hadrian-i","gp":"V3GLJOJB4A","t":"Hadrian I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Hadrian I is a gas dwarf in the [Hadrian system](gp:RX3r6jlZok), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The closest planet to its sun, it has a rocky core and a thick, stormy hydrogen-helium atmosphere with tan and brown-black bands. Astrophysicists believe that Hadrian I became the system's innermost planet when its sun entered its red giant phase, destroying any other bodies close to it.","g":["hadrian system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/769024c7-89d7-4d47-93a6-92772f7086b5"},
{"id":"hadrian-ii","gp":"RxnYvGyz3g","t":"Hadrian II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Hadrian II is a planet in the [Hadrian system](gp:RX3r6jlZok), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Relatively calm for a gas giant, its placid, bright blue atmosphere is orbited by hundreds of fuel refineries and gas mining operations. It was the main center of commerce in Hadrian until the 29th century, when it was eclipsed by industries related to trade with the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9).","g":["hadrian system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/73985162-37e0-44ef-9b04-5857dfeb02b8"},
{"id":"hadrian-iii","gp":"0qaoJqLda7","t":"Hadrian III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Hadrian III is an ice giant in the [Hadrian system](gp:RX3r6jlZok), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Located in the outer reaches of the system, it has no well-defined solid surface, and instead harbors an ammonia, water, and methane mantle. Its pale green, nearly white atmosphere is broken up by an enormous, permanent dark storm cloud that circles the equator. Inhabitants of Hadrian have nicknamed it \"the Watcher\" due to its resemblance to a Human eye.","g":["hadrian system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b8619be0-07b0-4e85-a036-a2e0f244dc2d"},
{"id":"hadrian-system","gp":"RX3r6jlZok","t":"Hadrian System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Hadrian system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that consists of a red giant, a gas giant, a gas dwarf, an asteroid belt, and an ice giant. Originally named Nivelin, it renamed Hadrian in SEY 2542 after an ancient human defensive wall and turned into a military staging ground due to its jump point connection with the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) system [Gurzil](gp:0Kxydrxd45). For the next two centuries, Hadrian was fortified with mines and outposts in preparation of a Xi'an attack that never came. Although it was demilitarized and reopened to civilians in 2793 at the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (2530 - 2793), many mines remain in the system's asteroid belt. Today, the military structures that have been declared safe have been converted into pit stops for those traveling between the UEE and the Xi'an Empire.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3daf8f8f-3f9f-422a-a38b-17d20cd7af0e"},
{"id":"haldor-lily","gp":"bo1aJavXGr","t":"Haldor Lily","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The haldor lily is a genetically modified plant created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke) to aid in the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) process. Designed for strength and durability, the haldor lily can be planted on worlds that suffer torrential storms without drowning or breaking. In addition, the tough leaves are difficult for most insects and other small herbivorous animals to consume, ensuring that in most circumstances the lily will be able to safely thrive.","g":["rayari inc","herbaceous plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/203f70e8-0d43-44d6-b540-766c8a0346ff"},
{"id":"hammer-propulsion","gp":"RvgpAn6Pwl","t":"Hammer Propulsion","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Hammer Propulsion is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of thrusters and powerplants for high-performance vehicles and maneuverable fighters. Key Hammer thruster types include the light grade HE-series, medium grade HM-series and heavy HL-series. The HM series was developed in cooperation with Origin specifically to propel the M50 and 350R racing ships. Additionally, Hammer provides the main thrusters for manufacturers [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv), [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw), and [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v).","g":["spacecraft component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/75048f67-0cc7-4ce4-ab57-6da88b29ada6"},
{"id":"hammerhead","gp":"ReJaMyZAw6","t":"Hammerhead","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Hammerhead is an armored gunship manufactured by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) and used by the [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) as a fleet screen and patrol spacecraft. It entered UEEN service in SEY 2773 and saw extensive use during the latter years of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792). With the fall of the [Messers](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/messer-dynasty), Aegis tried to distance their fleet from the corrupt regime and began to release a civilian model of the Hammerhead at the start of the 29th century.","g":["heavy gunship","aegis dynamics","gunship","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1444bc7c-eaa4-476f-8a2e-24f3baa042db"},
{"id":"harbinger","gp":"Vgg7Jj5Dge","t":"Harbinger","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Vanguard Harbinger is a variant of the Vanguard deep space fighter developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). Aegis removed the standard Vanguard [Warden](gp:0QxYDWPE7l)'s escape pod for the Harbinger,  allowing the addition of a bomb bay. The United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN) uses the Harbinger as a dedicated fighter-bomber. The Warden, Harbinger and [Sentinel](gp:VY4Wog4K8e) variants of the Vanguard can operate together as escort, bomber and support ship for long range operations with a reduced overhead for support and maintenance.","g":["vanguard","bomber","aegis dynamics","fighter","military spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d77acf80-41b0-479a-b3c4-60414970d0fa"},
{"id":"hardin-tactical","gp":"bmNrgWqZ8K","t":"Hardin Tactical","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Hardin Tactical is [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) personal armor manufacturer. Their stylishly-designed armor is popular among high-end consumers in cities and other centers of culture, though it has a somewhat negative reputation among security professionals who feel that the products sacrifice protection for aesthetics. Despite multiple bids, the company has not yet been able to break into industrial markets.","g":["hardin technical","armor manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1068f6e3-9430-4a15-9c07-620f38c83916"},
{"id":"hardpoint-guys","gp":"R6v8OWN844","t":"Hardpoint Guys","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Hardpoint Guys is an aftermarket spacecraft component retailer based in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The company typically presents itself as a friendly local ship shop and has standardized storefronts around the UEE that stock spacecraft upgrades such as thrusters, power plants, shield generators, scanners, weaponry, and tuning equipment. Their stores are oriented for average spacecraft owners rather than enthusiasts or high-end power users.","g":["spacecraft component retailer","spacecraft modification company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ea5c93a1-cd24-4736-bcf2-52481b1f6804"},
{"id":"harvester","gp":"0n1MYzOkG7","t":"Harvester","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Vanduul"],"x":"The \"Harvester\" is the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) designation for the specialized machinery utilized by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) to strip-mine conquered worlds. In general, Harvesters are several stories tall and typically transported on a carrier before being deployed onto the surface of a planet, asteroid, or other body from orbit. It then digs into the ground and begins to take in resources, automatically moving as it completes strip mining an area. Once a Harvester is full, they have been known to send out self-propelled pods full of processed materials to an orbiting ship, return to space themselves to be redeployed, or can possibly convert themselves into manufacturing centers. Harvesters on Tomb (Tiber II) have been observed using the resources they mine to manufacture additional Harvesters. The mechanism by which this is done is not yet understood or has not been revealed to the public.","g":["vanduul harvester","mining","heavy mining","salvage","heavy salvage"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fd7a8e61-4b9c-4914-83c3-6a8be2522124"},
{"id":"hathor-group","gp":"R6v8Dg8o6a","t":"Hathor Group","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"The Hathor Group was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) inter-planetary mining concern that employed harsh, environmentally catastrophic techniques that left otherwise inhabitable planets desolate in the company's wake. It purchased the [Nexus system](gp:RWoj8pnGma) from the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) in SEY 2468, strip mining the surface of [Lago (Nexus IV)](gp:0dXE5egx98) and ignoring burgeoning criminal activity in the system. Following a run of bad investments and failed claims, the company invested the last of their funds into mining the recently discovered Stanton System in 2853. However, due to some unforeseen difficulties, they were forced to cease operations and the Hathor Group was formally dissolved in 2864.","g":["mining company","human colonial expansion era","messer era","nexus system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/09f4bc6e-1cb7-4061-9089-e56269dd75d1"},
{"id":"haven","gp":"V3G6l5aNLa","t":"Haven","k":"place","c":["Settlements"],"x":"Haven is a settlement on [Tyrol V](gp:0GxQ6EB3JE) in the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N). Built into the side of a deep canyon to shelter from the heat of the suns, Haven started as a collection of tunnels that were used as temporary hide-outs by outlaws with nowhere else to run. As more people desperate enough to disregard the looming risk of the nova have made their way to the system, Haven has grown into an interconnected warren of caves both natural and artificial. An underground river flows through the deepest part of Haven, providing a fresh supply of liquid water to its inhabitants.","g":["tyrol v","sealed settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7f41bc45-ccb2-4be2-b48c-5a6feb7a6b2a"},
{"id":"hawk","gp":"ReJaOMrp6X","t":"Hawk","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The Hawk is a light fighter developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN). Initially developed as a dogfighter and ground attack vehicle in 2937, it saw only limited operations while in UEEN service. In response to this, Anvil developed a civilian model aimed at the bounty hunter market in 2940. The new model added a selection of EMP weaponry and a containment pod capable of carrying a passenger or prisoner.","g":["light fighter","anvil aerospace","fighter","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/318cc947-0685-439a-8212-33a534d7a243"},
{"id":"hawksworths","gp":"RX3JyO55dJ","t":"Hawksworth's","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Hawksworth's is a footwear brand that specializes in manufacturing business attire for professional environments. Known for its long-standing commitment to classic styles and colors, it is best known for its line of low-ankle Vivant shoes, which have been the brand's signature style since its founding in the late 26th century SEY.","g":["hawksworths"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/19e7c113-fac3-4699-b5d4-9ab0bd768665"},
{"id":"hawthorne-development-ltd","gp":"VDzM7KvdPz","t":"Hawthorne Development Ltd.","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Hawthorne Development Ltd. is a tech brand that manufactures high-end EVA suits. From conception to realization, the brand handles all aspects of their products in-house instead of sourcing materials, systems, and technologies from other suppliers. The brand has made its versatile and durable textiles as much a part of its identity as its life support systems, and sometimes partners with the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) to craft military-grade flight suits.","g":["hawthorne development ltd","electronic consumer goods manufacturer","clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/720eaa3c-d1ee-4fdf-894e-28861640328e"},
{"id":"headhunters","gp":"bZkOavLgjB","t":"Headhunters","k":"people","c":["Organizations","Illegal Activity"],"x":"The Headhunters are a major criminal organization based in the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N) that specializes in smuggling, theft, and protection. Originally from the Virgil system, the gang first rose to prominence as smugglers in the 2610s, when they established a fast shipping route from Virgil to [Terra](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4) through [Nyx](gp:0jGxP6kpG3) and Pyro that proved to be difficult for authorities to detect. By the 2620s, they fully relocated to Ruin Station, where they could more easily avoid encounters with the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk). It was during this era that they adopted the Human skull into their symbolism, and began including motifs of it in tattoos, personal decor, and graffiti. A location marked with a Headhunter skull warned other criminals that the area was under their control. Much of Pyro stayed under their influence until the criminal syndicate the Drop Kings challenged their authority in the 2740s in an effort to expand their smuggling network, resulting in a series of conflicts that caused control of Ruin Station to pass back and forth between the gangs for several decades. The Drop Kings ultimately withdrew when they clashed with another criminal syndicate in 2912. Since then, the gangs are officially on neutral terms, though they maintain a sense of rivalry.","g":["outlaw factions","human outlaw factions","pyro outlaw faction"]},
{"id":"hedeby-gunworks","gp":"VY4WByAzXv","t":"Hedeby Gunworks","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Hedeby Gunworks is a personal weapons manufacturer located in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The company was founded by inventor Altruis Hedeby in SEY 2921 as a single shop to market armaments had developed himself. Hedeby sought to utilize his experience with [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) technology to introduce new design and manufacturing techniques to the UEE market. The Salvo pistol, which introduced a variety of new cooling techniques, was their earliest successful product. The company continues to adapt traditional weapons with unconventional new design techniques.","g":["weapons manufacturer","altruis hedeby","asura","ferron iii","human company"],"img":"https://static.robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/upload/b78dbc97-3a62-4229-bdfb-4afcdb7a285d"},
{"id":"helios-i","gp":"R5pqNGoZM9","t":"Helios I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Helios I is a terrestrial rocky planet in the [Helios system](gp:0KxpdzWBK4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The closest planet to its sun, temperatures on Helios I are dangerously high. In 2937, the scientific survey station *OB Tarasque* crashed onto the planet's surface. Its lack of adequate shielding put all the survivors in danger of dying by heat exposure. As quickly as possible, members of a local garrison modified their fighters to withstand the extreme conditions and were able to rescue six survivors before it was too late.","g":["helios system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7597741e-5dfb-4375-920b-93e9f66cb425"},
{"id":"helios-iii","gp":"0KxpdzoxDP","t":"Helios III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Helios III is the third planet from the sun of the [Helios system](gp:0KxpdzWBK4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Massive and hydrogen-rich, it is the main source for hydrogen collection in Helios and is the hub for the system's gas processing and refinement operations. Its atmosphere is uniformly tan in color, lacking the distinctive bands often found on other gas giants of similar size.","g":["helios system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/65d66585-7302-4d32-a3d7-9de96dc29df0"},
{"id":"helios-iv","gp":"RxnYekOYZy","t":"Helios IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Helios IV is the outermost planet from the sun of the [Helios system](gp:0KxpdzWBK4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Although it is covered in thick sheets of ice and lacks a substantial atmosphere, the UEE military operates a network of outposts on Helios IV, located deep underground. The purpose of these facilities has never been publicly stated. Locals speculate that they are used for black-ops training or secret research, but no evidence to support these claims has ever been found.","g":["helios system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8fc266fe-39ee-44f6-aba1-88650ded30a1"},
{"id":"helios-system","gp":"0KxpdzWBK4","t":"Helios System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Helios system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), consisting of a peculiar main sequence B-type star, three terrestrial planets, and a gas giant. It was discovered in 2529 by a group of outlaws known as the Daybreak Marauders, who used it as a launching point for their frequent raids on convoys in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ). That same year, it was officially annexed by the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) when [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) agents Avon Dorville and Gia Trask tracked the Daybreak Marauders to their hidden jump point in the Taranis system. The system's most populated planet, [Tangaroa (Helios II)](gp:RX3rnQ3XqM), has a brackish water ocean that gives rise to waves hundreds of meters high.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4a20336e-579a-4470-8795-c6e38bfa9c0a"},
{"id":"henge-cluster-terra-cluster-alpha","gp":"RPDmr866oE","t":"Henge Cluster (Terra Cluster Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Henge cluster (Terra cluster alpha) is an asteroid field located between the [third](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) and [fourth](gp:RMNMv8ekn8) planets from the sun in the [Terra system](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). High in metallic asteroids, much of the cluster has already been claimed by various major mining corporations. While independent mining is allowed, the high density of claims in the area has resulted in heavy regulations.","g":["henge cluster","terra cluster alpha","asteroid cluster","terra system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c30e40c6-611a-49be-8710-a546fc9977a9"},
{"id":"herald","gp":"VpGEmdYJPA","t":"Herald","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Herald is a data runner spacecraft sold by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). It is an unusually specialized design for Drake, focusing entirely on the process of securely storing, transmitting, and moving data as quickly as possible. The Herald is built with an armored computer core and an STA-M6A1 high power broadcast array that allows for long range transmission. They are used by a variety of corporations and by independent contractors who specialize in data running missions.","g":["drake interplanetary","medium data","data (role)","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/043bc6c9-4359-4cb2-92d0-25a76a2e9747"},
{"id":"herschel-belt-sol-belt-alpha","gp":"R4jo9gv6Dq","t":"Herschel Belt (Sol Belt Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Herschel belt (Sol belt alpha) is an asteroid belt in the Sol system, [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Located between the orbits of [Mars (Sol IV)](gp:Regn8D76xw) and [Jupiter (Sol V)](gp:Vy2OMo22wz), it is where Humans first began to experiment with asteroid mining. Pure water ice harvested from the belt helped ease the water crisis during the [Human Overpopulation Era](gp:RxNxLk4yNz) in the 21st and 22nd centuries SEY.","g":["herschel belt","sol belt alpha","asteroid belt","sol system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bdb15054-0296-43a9-9e28-d9d59f44ba9a"},
{"id":"high-command","gp":"RegxqX26ok","t":"High Command","k":"faction","c":["Government","Military","Human"],"x":"The High Command is a governmental body in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), made up of three representatives from each branch of their military. These representatives, [Legatus Navium](gp:V7dPXLWYL3), [Legatus Exercitus](gp:0QlKMOJELo), and [Legatus Marinuum](gp:RWolAvP7qp), replaced the [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) position of High General. Aside from overseeing the management of the military, they brief the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) and the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) on military matters and facilitate the Imperator's orders. High Command was created in SEY 2793 after the [Anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7), to prevent any future Imperators from using the military as an oppressive force.","g":["uee high command","human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9d53a7a8-cfaf-458e-ba01-489e7e5061a8"},
{"id":"high-advocate","gp":"RWolAld13P","t":"High-Advocate","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"The High-Advocate is the leader of the judiciary and law enforcement branch in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Laws that have passed through the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) and have been approved by the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) are interpreted and enforced by the High-Advocate, then funneled to local governments for adoption. Originally created as an elected office in 2523, the position was dissolved by [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) in 2546. It was re-established in 2793, after the events of the [Anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7) deposed Imperator [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq), ending over 200 years of despotic rule. The High-Advocate is nominated by the newly-elected Imperator but must be approved by the Directors Council, a committee composed of the heads of the various law enforcement and judicial departments that fall under the High Advocate's control. This structure was set up after the end of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) to prevent future Imperators from treating the Advocacy and other departments as a private security force.","g":["uee high-advocate","human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b38747c8-00ce-4710-8257-87ad25f5d70b"},
{"id":"high-secretary","gp":"RkG2n2MWYn","t":"High-Secretary","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"The High-Secretary is the chief executive of infrastructure in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and oversees matters such as transportation, power, communications, sewage, and agriculture. Structural legislation that has been debated and refined by the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) is passed first to the High-Secretary before it is passed to the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) for final approval. The position was originally created at the formation of the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) in 2523 as part of the three-member [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) that would run the government. [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) retired the office when he became [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr) in 2546. After the events of the [Anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7) in 2792, the office of High-Secretary was re-established as one appointed by the duly-elected Imperator, subject to final approval from the Senate.","g":["uee high-secretary","human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8858a743-a8b9-4cfd-a7a4-2e45c0782f0a"},
{"id":"hilago-boots","gp":"VDzM7KZojz","t":"Hilago Boots","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Hilago Boots is a footwear brand that creates shoes and accessories. Originally a direct-to-consumer business, it got started after founder Rock Hilago found success selling handmade leather goods at local craft fairs in [Stalford](gp:VY4Wj6Yrj1), [Rytif (Bremen II)](gp:R5pA7q691W). An amateur costumer, he was particularly interested in historic fashion from [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB), and used it as a template for his designs. Today, Hilago is known for its sturdy boots and leather goods that continue to draw inspiration from Earth's history.","g":["footwear manufacturer","stalford","rytif","bremen ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1638b187-5b0c-4f83-ac85-110ce47851fe"},
{"id":"historical-truth-act-of-2941","gp":"0OaB8KmBKq","t":"Historical Truth Act of 2941","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The Historical Truth Act is an information law passed in 2941 by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) that declassified thousands of documents created during the [Messer Era (2546 - 2792)](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo). It defines records created by the Messers and those associated with them as subject to disclosure, outlines the declassification procedures, and describes the circumstances under which exemptions to the law are allowed. Created to expose the Messers' abuse of government power to the public, it unsealed military records, confirmed the existence of previously classified spacecraft, unearthed secret projects, and revealed the fates of many people who had disappeared under mysterious circumstances.","g":["laws","uee law"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4ba4faa0-e08a-4451-9f6f-54f823d919e4"},
{"id":"hitbox","gp":"Rz2My4N8jA","t":"Hitbox","k":"culture","c":["Publications","Human"],"x":"# HITBOX\n\n*Hitbox* is a gaming magazine managed by C&K Publishing that releases a new issue every Standard Earth Month. Launched in December 2935, each issue of *Hitbox* features previews of upcoming games, news and statistics related to the games industry, reviews of new releases, and at least one interview with a game developer. This standard format is only broken in the December issue, which dives into a detailed retrospective on the best and worst games of the past year. After a rocky start, it has consistently been one of the top selling gaming magazines produced by Humans since reaching the mass market in 2939.\n\n# HISTORY\n\nRoommates Velma Bhatti, Amahle Mhlongo, and Augustin Fontenot began a [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) site called Collision Detection in 2929 containing short reviews of digital games they had recently played. Enthusiasts who first bonded with one another over their shared love of games, Mhlongo had recently obtained her [Equivalency](gp:Vgg7YGdQDY) and was unsure of what to do next, and Bhatti and Fontenot were working restaurant jobs while they saved money to buy a [Constellation Taurus](gp:Vgg7jYmpQn). Initially, their reviews were posted on an irregular schedule, based on when one of the three could afford to purchase a new game. Their posts became more frequent in late 2929 when Mhlongo got a job at retailer Baers and was able to temporarily borrow games as a part of her store's employee check-out program. Views began to climb due to the site's more regular publication schedule and the shared sense of humor the friends included in each of their articles.\n\nIn 2931, the site was receiving enough views that Mhlongo suggested reaching out to advertisers to cover their ballooning hosting costs. Fontenot and Bhatti were reluctant to do so, as they did not want to be tied to maintaining a hobby site when they eventually saved enough to purchase their own spacecraft. However, as their bills continued to grow higher, they conceded that they could no longer afford to cover the costs on their own and they partnered with their first advertisers. They were soon able to cover their server bills with some money left over. The site continued to grow, eventually becoming profitable enough thanks to increased viewership and advertising revenue for all three to quit their jobs and dedicate themselves to reviewing full time in 2932.\n\nPublishing company C&K reached out to the trio in 2934 with an offer to publish Collision Detection as a physical magazine. The contract would provide the site founders with an influx of credits, enough for Fontenot and Bhatti to finally purchase their first ship. They eagerly signed, and Mhlongo threw herself into developing the format of the magazine while Fontenot and Bhatti focused on keeping the site maintained, updating it remotely from their ship as they fulfilled their dream of traveling. C&K took on the bulk of production planning, and after almost a year of preparation, the first issue was released in December 2935 under the new name *Hitbox*, which had tested well with focus groups. The site was renamed as well. \n\nInitial sales were disappointing. The first six issues struggled with confusing page layouts, and a screenshot of the game Canine Coiffure, long used by Bhatti as filler to be replaced before her articles were published, was mistakenly used for multiple unrelated games and sent to print until it was excised from the production pipeline. Even after the issues were resolved, it seemed that *Hitbox* was not destined to be a hit. However, sales picked up throughout 2937 thanks to a strategy devised by Bhatti. As she and Fontenot journeyed through the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), they would drop free bundles of the magazine with games and electronics retailers along with the contact information of C&K Publishing. By 2939, *Hitbox* could be purchased at most places where games were sold.\n\nMhlongo remains at *Hitbox* as Editor-in-Chief, and Fontenot and Bhatti contribute reviews and special articles to the magazine and the site multiple times per year. The two married in 2943.\n\n# CONTROVERSY\n\nIn 2941, the magazine was mailed a copy of a lost game titled Meet Me in Elysium, ostensibly made by a reclusive team of [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) who published their work under pseudonyms. Features Editor Gavin Joy wrote an in-depth article on the game with interviews from the developers that was published in the March 2941 issue of the magazine. The game was revealed to be an elaborate hoax concocted by [Borea (Magnus III)](gp:R9vGaQPXJN) radio hosts Burke and Banyon for the holiday [Triggerfish](gp:0rxrqgzgP6). *Hitbox* published a written apology signed by all its editors in the April issue, promising to exert more due diligence in the future. Joy resigned.","g":["hitbox magazine","entertainment publication","magazine"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6b86078c-779b-48bd-b9f7-b01223f0e60a"},
{"id":"hoplite","gp":"VpGEjz6qL1","t":"Hoplite","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Vanguard Hoplite is a variant of the Vanguard deep space fighter developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). The design replaces the standard escape pod located amid-ship with weapons racks and cradles to support a squad of armored soldiers. The [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) utilizes the Hoplite for boarding and air to ground operations.","g":["dropship","vanguard","aegis dynamics","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/713d913b-86e3-4b65-af0a-49e3fcb1b153"},
{"id":"horus-belt-alpha","gp":"R5plEOr6g3","t":"Horus Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Horus belt alpha is the first asteroid belt from the sun of the [Horus system](gp:bo1JGZpvwZ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It is the most active center of mining operations in the system, providing [Serling (Horus I)](gp:Vy28DwK2a8) with materials that cannot be extracted planetside without threatening the delicate balance of its environment. In 2911, a small mining outpost set up on one of the belt's larger asteroids had a defective filter installed during construction which led to the presence of a constant pall of dust that caused long-term respiratory problems in its inhabitants. A court case following this incident against the filter's manufacturer forced an industry-wide overhaul in regulations compliance.","g":["asteroid belt","horus system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2e792018-06a8-43ac-acfe-b8cdccf89318"},
{"id":"horus-belt-beta","gp":"RWo69XO6oZ","t":"Horus Belt Beta","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Horus belt beta is the second asteroid belt from the sun of the [Horus system](gp:bo1JGZpvwZ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). In contrast to its [neighboring belt](gp:R5plEOr6g3), it sees little commercial traffic aside from passing trade ships despite being located closer to the system's only inhabited planet [Serling (Horus I)](gp:Vy28DwK2a8). [Marie Sante](gp:RX36PWwe4K), who discovered the Horus system, kept a personal base on the largest asteroid in the Horus belt beta that she utilized when exploring the system's outer reaches. Left abandoned after her 2545 disappearance, the base was re-discovered in 2977 and was declared a cultural heritage site.","g":["asteroid belt","horus system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2f53f27a-c582-4467-b5cf-df5f619a261d"},
{"id":"horus-ii","gp":"RAXPkgLxgm","t":"Horus II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Horus II is the second planet from the sun of the [Horus system](gp:bo1JGZpvwZ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Although it is located in the habitable zone, it lacks any natural bodies of water and does not have an atmosphere that can support life. After the 2947 signing of the [Human-Xi'an Trade Initiative (HuXa)](gp:01LvKoLvZ8), some of the old military bases on Horus II leftover from the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) were transformed into cargo exchange stations for traders passing through the R.il'a and Kai'pua jump points. There is growing public interest in the potential terraformation of Horus II as trade between the UEE and the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) continues to increase.","g":["horus system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1d9cb4c2-84a2-44c8-b127-5770829313c1"},
{"id":"horus-iii","gp":"RMN2w7LDyn","t":"Horus III","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Horus III is a super-Jupiter on the [Horus system](gp:bo1JGZpvwZ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the most distant planet from its sun. More massive than most other gas giants, it has a high-density atmosphere that compresses the planet, lowering its overall circumference in comparison to low-mass gas giants. Many rest stops and refueling stations orbit Horus III in support of travelers and traders that pass through Horus between the UEE and the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9).","g":["horus system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b282e797-4483-41f0-b617-01b0d9b8aa3c"},
{"id":"horus-system","gp":"bo1JGZpvwZ","t":"Horus System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Horus system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that consists of an M-type main sequence star, two terrestrial planets, a super-Jupiter, and two asteroid belts. In 2528, navjumper [Marie Sante](gp:RX36PWwe4K) reported her discovery of the Horus system to the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN), alongside detailed documentation describing its celestial bodies. It was incorporated into the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) when Sante discovered a jump point to the Xi'an-owned R.il'a system in 2542, after which the UPE closed Horus to non-military personnel. When the Perry Line was dissolved in 2793, the UEE government re-opened the system and oversaw the colonization of the tidally-locked planet [Serling (Horus I)](gp:Vy28DwK2a8). Horus' connection to the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9), once a hindrance to its development, is now the main driver of its economic growth.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/78687a80-8925-4dd3-aae5-6b4ad499fd77"},
{"id":"hosanna-tree","gp":"bo1jYEvMdA","t":"Hosanna Tree","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The hosanna tree is a genetically modified plant derived from the flowering dogwood and the taverbark pine. Created by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) for the platform-based city of [Orison](gp:V7dgN8Pkrm) on [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav), the trees were designed with strong roots and flexible branches to tolerate high winds and given leaves that could thrive in a low-humidity environment. The tree's delicately-scented pink flowers have become a symbol of Orison and are often featured in promotional images of the city.","g":["crusader industries","trees","crusader","stanton ii","orison"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ebb428cd-91c2-482d-b070-ff47047cf42c"},
{"id":"house-chii","gp":"0qnNZOo3lk","t":"House Chii","k":"history","c":["History","Xi'an"],"x":"Chii was one of the four major [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj)[Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) that fought in the [Great Divide ](gp:VyvYA5qmqX)(20044 - 19770 BCE). Allied to House [Uai'i](gp:RMXyBdkAQA), it joined the war after hostilities between [Ru'a](gp:V3qgaLK82W) and Uai'i became deadly. Though it was the largest House to survive the destruction of the Xi'an homeworld's atmosphere in 19770 BCE, it was unable to gain significant power in the government restructuring that followed. Leadership of Chii attempted to seize power from [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) House Ru'a only thirteen years after the end of the Great Divide. As punishment for their actions, they were exterminated.","g":["the great divide","house uai'i","house ru'a","house kl.ō","xi'an house"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d49f8752-ceed-461b-91dd-67a89d8b481a"},
{"id":"house-kloo","gp":"V8gJ62qO81","t":"House Kl.ō","k":"history","c":["Xi'an","History"],"x":"Kl.ō was one of the four major [Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) involved in the [Great Divide](gp:VyvYA5qmqX)(20044 - 19770 BCE). When the last daughter of Kl.ō attempted to defect to [House Uai'i](gp:RMXyBdkAQA), a move that would have ended her family line, a war broke out between the Houses. In the final year of the war, the Kl.ō forces were severely depleted; defeat appeared inevitable. Facing the possibility of their House's extinction, some members of House Kl.ō attempted to assassinate the leadership of houses Uai'i, [Ru'a](gp:V3qgaLK82W), and [Chii](gp:0qnNZOo3lk) by poisoning the air directly above peace talks on RyiXy'an (Hyoton III). Their act of sabotage accidentally started a chain reaction throughout RyiXy'an's network of antique weather manipulation satellites that contaminated the entire planet's atmosphere, resulting in the death of millions and rendering the Xi'an homeworld uninhabitable. As penance for their actions, House Kl.ō voluntarily chose not to continue their family line. They died out roughly 100 years after the end of the Great Divide.","g":["the great divide","xi'an house"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/526c0ce5-ad1e-4f7d-826f-c4572ffd9ab5"},
{"id":"house-kree","gp":"R6v8OZOrP5","t":"House Kr.ē","k":"culture","c":["Xi'an"],"x":"House Kr.ē is the current [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp)[House](gp:box9JmxvWL). They first came to prominence during the [Spirit Wars (II.961 - II.1735 / SEY 351-1342)](gp:0dQ4DYJ9W8), gaining the attention of Imperial House [Xy.ō](gp:RXlXBrm5o1) for collecting volumes of strategically valuable intelligence on the [Kr'thak](gp:RxNxDYkqzz). Kr.ē was Imperially sanctioned as the prime intelligence house in II.1138 (SEY 578). As one of the largest surviving houses after the end of the Spirit Wars, Kr.ē was instrumental in reconstruction efforts. They were selected as the Third Imperial House in III.0 (SEY 1457). The infant U.e'o se Kr.ē became House Kr.ē's first Emperor. The current Emperor, [T.uēng se Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo), is the last member of his line.","g":["third imperial age","xi'an imperial house","xi'an house"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dc7876c5-4e34-4d3e-906a-7bcad465ed6d"},
{"id":"house-ngatak","gp":"RWolrAj1vm","t":"House Ng.at'ak","k":"culture","c":["Xi'an"],"x":"Ng.at'ak (also known as Gatac) is one of the major [Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). During the [Great Divide (20044 - 19770 BCE)](gp:VyvYA5qmqX), Ng.at'ak, a vassal of [House Ru'a](gp:V3qgaLK82W), built and maintained vehicles and spacecraft that formed the backbone of Ru'a's logistics operations. Three of Ng.at'ak's elders perished alongside the leadership of Ru'a when [House Kl.ō](gp:V8gJ62qO81) unintentionally poisoned the atmosphere of the Xi'an homeworld RyiXy'an (Hyoton III). When Ru'a was made the first [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) House in the aftermath of the tragedy, newly elevated Emperor Ya.l'ē se Ru'a rewarded Ng.at'ak for their service by granting them exclusive rights to build industrial spacecraft for the SaoXy'an in perpetuity. Today, Ng.at'ak owns and operates [Gatac Manufacture (Ao't.o'a'Ng.at'ak)](gp:bo13Earlar) and maintains close familial ties with the current Imperial House.","g":["xi'an house"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9d6f3fce-6f22-4312-a93b-121da0dd79ff"},
{"id":"house-rua","gp":"V3qgaLK82W","t":"House Ru'a","k":"history","c":["Xi'an","History"],"x":"Ru'a was the first [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) House in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). It was one of the four major [Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) involved in the [Great Divide](gp:VyvYA5qmqX) (20044 - 19770 BCE), allied to the [Kl.ō](gp:V8gJ62qO81) house against Houses [Uai'i](gp:RMXyBdkAQA) and [Chii](gp:0qnNZOo3lk). Alliances fractured over the years until all four Houses fought for themselves to achieve supreme power. As the Chii emerged as the likeliest victors, the leadership of Ru'a and Uai'i elected to attempt peace talks with the Chii on the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) homeworld RyiXy'an (Hyoton III), hoping to negotiate a ceasefire. However, all leaders of Ru'a and some of Uai'i and Chii were wiped out when the struggling House [Kl.ō](gp:V8gJ62qO81) sabotaged RyiXy'an's network of antique weather manipulation satellites above the talks, inadvertently setting off a chain reaction that poisoned the atmosphere of the entire planet. All Xi'an were forced to flee their homeworld. \n\nA surviving daughter of Ru'a, Ya.l'ē, was named the first Emperor of the new unified government in recompense for her family's near-annihilation. She encoded the mores of [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe) into Xi'an law. The House ruled until Se'ang, the final Ru'a Emperor and the last member of his line, stepped down in 878 BCE (I.14680), beginning the [Second Imperial Age](gp:RAdjOk77n7).","g":["the great divide","xi'an imperial house","first imperial age","xi'an house"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9b9bd68c-48f2-4cbe-abbb-316d7a62374a"},
{"id":"house-uaii","gp":"RMXyBdkAQA","t":"House Uai'i","k":"history","c":["Xi'an","History"],"x":"Uai'i is one of the major [Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an.)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) Credited with creating the first single-occupant spacecraft capable of exiting and re-entering the atmosphere, Uai'i came to power in 26038 BCE. Before this point they were a minor but prosperous House, having written culinary treatise *Three Leaves of Flavor* around 29500 BCE. The attempted defection of the only daughter of House [Kl.ō](gp:V8gJ62qO81) to [Uai'i](gp:RMXyBdkAQA) incited the [Great Divide](gp:VyvYA5qmqX)(20044 - 19770 BCE), the Xi'an civil war that rendered the Xi'an homeword, RyiXy'an (Hyoton III), uninhabitable.","g":["the great divide","xi'an house"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/593a60b8-6b0e-47af-bf64-6e1cabe7ce82"},
{"id":"house-xyo","gp":"RXlXBrm5o1","t":"House Xy.ō","k":"history","c":["Xi'an","History"],"x":"Xy.ō was the second [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) House (Yii'uaTao\") in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Selected by other major [Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) in II.0 (878 BCE), the new Emperor Y.ah'a se Xy.ō and the rest of her House commemorated the terraforming of R.aip'uāng (Kai'pua III) to be a spiritual center of [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe) in honor of the Ru'a Line's millennia of service. The final Emperor Xy.ō and her entire family were exterminated by the [Kr'thak](gp:RxNxDYkqzz) in II.1706 (SEY 1305), during the Spirit Wars (II.961 - II.1735; SEY 351 - 1342). Their destruction led to [the Dark](gp:VyvYXnM2Pl) (II.1706 - II.1824; SEY 1305 - 1457), a period of [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) history beset by anarchy and cultural decline.","g":["second imperial age","spirit wars","xi'an empire","xi'an imperial house"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a85a004c-45fc-4a6f-ad9f-269aa283b613"},
{"id":"housing-exchanges-hex","gp":"bmN4vB4rzQ","t":"Housing Exchanges (HEX)","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Housing Exchanges (HEX) are a common name for prefabricated facilities established inside hollowed asteroids and other frontier locations. They are simple, interconnected living spaces built to sustain workers and passing travelers at locations where constructing bespoke housing would be either too difficult or unnecessary. The first HEXs were manufactured by Everline Structures Incorporated and have since been imitated by other corporations.","g":["everline structures incorporated","prefabricated housing"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/38a01b32-02ea-4d9c-bad0-f732d96ee296"},
{"id":"hoverquad","gp":"0rxOylJ8WB","t":"HoverQuad","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation"],"x":"The HoverQuad is a grav-lev vehicle manufactured by [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34). Designed to fit in the bed of the Nomad, it was developed with a focus on exploration. Each [HoverQuad](gp:RegxW5ywdj) is equipped with four grav-lev pads that enable its singular rider to traverse sudden changes in the landscape with minimal turbulence, which allows the vehicle to maintain its speed over rough terrain.","g":["expedition","racing","consolidated outland","human vehicle"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dcd028e5-626f-448f-9820-882b568e4caa"},
{"id":"huanam-thusuung-iv","gp":"01LrNAvwpG","t":"Hua'nam (Th.us'ūng IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Hua'nam (Th.us'ūng IV) is a gas giant in the [Th.us'ūng system](gp:V8WeExnJge), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9), and is the fourth planet from its sun. A pressurized research station constructed, owned, and operated by the Xi'an government is located inside Hua'nam's stormy hydrogen-helium atmosphere, at depths currently unreachable via [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) technological means. The [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government has not publicly shared the methods they utilized to construct this station.","g":["hua'nam","th.us'uung iv","th.us'uung system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cc275b3e-2a67-4602-84fd-ebf8791f10e5"},
{"id":"huichuaihyao-syeno-se-lauo","gp":"RWo5gxkmKa","t":"Huichuaihyao sy.en'o se La'uo (La'uo belt beta)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Huichuaihyao sy.en'o se La'uo (La'uo belt beta) is an asteroid belt in the [La'uo system](gp:R6demJ8Xmq), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Located between [Kyu'ām (La'uo III)](gp:RX35G91XA1) and [S.ap'uāng (La'uo IV)](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/bBz3m21j78-sapuaang-lauo-iv ), it hosts a large concentration of asteroids that are coated in highly prized, very pure water ice. The [nyayu'a](gp:bZkaBD5alD) who reside on the system utilize ice harvested from these asteroids as a source of fresh water. Some Xi'an mining consortiums have entered into agreements with the *nyayu'a* to conduct operations here in exchange for peacefully ceding a small percentage of their cargo if they are boarded.","g":["huichuaihyao sy.en'o se la'uo","la'uo belt beta","asteroid belt","la'uo system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2a5653df-caef-4d0c-ba06-083dcb99506e"},
{"id":"huichuaihyao-yatho-se-lauo","gp":"VYL5n9woex","t":"Huichuaihyao y.ath'o se La'uo (La'uo belt alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Huichuaihyao y.ath'o se La'uo (La'uo belt alpha) is an asteroid belt in the [La'uo system](gp:R6demJ8Xmq), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). In the space between [Yengchuai (La'uo II)](gp:R6demaZlkD) and [Kyu'ām (La'uo III)](gp:RX35G91XA1), a large planetesimal abundant in metals and minerals once orbited La'uo's star during the time the system was first forming. However, it failed to gather enough material to coalesce into a full planet and eventually broke apart to form this asteroid belt.","g":["la'uo belt alpha","huichuaihyao y.ath'o se la'uo","asteroid belt","la'uo system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a716c468-acfd-4bd8-a053-8d8740f27d37"},
{"id":"huichuaihyao-yatho-se-thusuung","gp":"Rz2rykvJXk","t":"Huichuaihyao y.ath'o se Th.us'ūng","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Huichuaihyao y.ath'o se Th.usūng (Th.us'ūng belt alpha) is an asteroid belt in the [Th.us'ūng system](gp:V8WeExnJge), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Rich in valuable mineral resources, Kathryn Segovia cited its presence as a primary motivating factor in her decision to sell the location of the Th.us'ūng-[Baker](gp:Rz2KGkv13N) jump point to [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) organization Gaia Planet Services. However, the company's plans to mine the belt were halted before when they inadvertently made first contact with the Xi'an Empire.","g":["huichuaihyaho y.ath'o se th.us'uung","th.us'uung belt alpha","asteroid belt","th.us'uung system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/547a6571-e10d-4e5e-a0a2-8e1886ddc874"},
{"id":"huichuaihyao-yatho-se-yaamon-yaamon-belt-alpha","gp":"RAXPyzK6Lm","t":"Huichuaihyao y.ath'o se Yā'mon (Yā'mon Belt Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The huichuaihyao y.ath'o se Yā'mon (Yā'mon belt alpha) is an asteroid belt in the [Yā'mon system](gp:VarxDJ5yLo), [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Used as a supplier of minerals for the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military, it was under heavy guard for the duration of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793). [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) scouts on observation missions were sometimes captured and held as political hostages until they could be exchanged for Xi'an prisoners kept in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). After the end of the Cold War, the belt was opened to commercial mining, and is one of the main resources of materials for the ongoing terraforming projects on [Yethlūl y.ath'o (Yā'mon II)](gp:bo1JQK12rr) and [Yethlūl s.yen'o (Yā'mon III)](gp:V8WPNjrEjW).","g":["huichuaihyao y.ath'o se yaa'mon","yaa'mon belt alpha","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/722bc223-e1c8-4cd3-86ed-2af12821164c"},
{"id":"eealuth-belt-alpha","gp":"VYLzwJQxgW","t":"Huichuaihyao y.ath'o se Ē'aluth","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Huichuaihyao y.ath'o se Ē'aluth (Ē'aluth Belt Alpha) is an asteroid belt in the [Ē'aluth system](gp:Rw1xW1lzxN), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). The government allows a tightly-capped quantity of water ice to be extracted from the belt under close supervision, solely to support those who reside full time in Ē'aluth as protectors and supervisors of the nature preserve on [Ko'li (Ē'aluth III)](gp:Vy29gQ3x4Y). After the water is brought to the various space stations scattered throughout the system, it is inoculated with minerals and microorganisms and aged to suit it to the Xi'an flavor palette.","g":["ē'aluth belt alpha","asteroid belt","xi'an asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/67b72722-e8d5-44e5-ad03-3d7209ef0f71"},
{"id":"hulla","gp":"V3qgkBE71Z","t":"Hull A","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Hull A is a freighter developed by [MISC](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). The smallest and most affordable of the Hull series, the Hull A has limited defensive and maneuvering capabilities compared with similarly sized craft, but has commensurate carrying capacity. Many corporations have utilized the Hull A as a solution for the short range transport of goods from larger freighters to planetary surfaces.","g":["medium freight","misc","freight","human spacecraft","hull series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6be3c3ad-b2dd-4e99-afe6-b1ffcb0d169b"},
{"id":"hullb","gp":"VyvYkrKkop","t":"Hull B","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Hull B is a freighter developed by [Musashi Industrial & Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) as part of the Hull series of spacecraft. Designed to handle a larger cargo payload than the [Hull A](gp:V3qgkBE71Z), the B model's monotasking focus on hauling means that while it is not as versatile as some other haulers in its class like MISC's own [Freelancer-line](gp:RvgzWy7o6v), it is quite capable in its area of expertise. It is often utilized by corporations for space-terrestrial transfer.","g":["heavy freight","misc","freight","human spacecraft","hull series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5b3e0aa5-8b1e-4200-b751-77d45f3f3890"},
{"id":"hullc","gp":"VlNP94zqg5","t":"Hull C","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Hull C is a modular bulk freighter produced by [Musashi Industrial & Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). It is capable of transporting large quantities of goods attached to the frame in standard cargo containers. The Hull C is the standard-bearer of the Hull line and is marketed as an adaptable solution to corporations requiring a fleet of smaller transports, as well as smaller businesses and organizations.","g":["heavy freight","misc","human spacecraft","freight","hull series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/82613168-eb95-453d-a189-5790500c0316"},
{"id":"hulld","gp":"0n9vrwLDkv","t":"Hull D","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The Hull D is a modular bulk freighter produced by [Musashi Industrial & Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). The Hull D is the second largest freighter in the Hull line and is capable of transporting large quantities of goods attached to the frame in standard cargo containers. The Hull D is typically operated by mid-sized corporations or larger organizations and frequently serves as the flagship for mercantile groups. [The United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) armed forces use a modified version of the Hull D in logistics operations, the ship forming an important part of the supply chain refueling and rearming soldiers on the front lines.","g":["heavy freight","misc","freight","human spacecraft","hull series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/002bce31-71a7-4020-a060-444439d0542a"},
{"id":"hull-e","gp":"RkZ96wLznN","t":"Hull E","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Hull E is a modular bulk freighter produced by [Musashi Industrial & Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). It is the largest freighter in the Hull line, and is capable of transporting a higher quantity of cargo than any other dedicated transport MISC produces. Due to high operating costs and the massive volume of goods required to outfit the ship to capacity, Hull E are typically utilized by larger corporations. Because their maneuverability is low, MISC recommends to its owners that they travel with escort craft.","g":["heavy freight","misc","freight","human spacecraft","hull series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/48882a93-2a0f-47eb-bdae-b682761490e7"},
{"id":"human-colonial-expansion-era","gp":"0dQ4BjlQQm","t":"Human Colonial Expansion Era","k":"history","c":["History","Exploration","Human"],"x":"The Human Colonial Expansion Era (2380 - 2530) was a period marked by rapid discovery of jump points and planetary systems and outward expansion from the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) home system Sol. Historians believe that a drop in the price of spacecraft made exploration vessels more freely available to civilians, which led to an upward spike in the discovery of [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY). In 2380, the formation of the first pan-Human government, the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO), allowed mass proliferation of resources formerly available to a few. [Bremen](gp:02kd45eyxe) and [Oretani](gp:bo1eNYWqqN) were among the many systems discovered during this time. The rate of colonization fell after Humans made [first contact](gp:R4ZQpYEEvx) with the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) in 2530.","g":["eras","united empire of earth"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6b2455e2-6308-4a9b-a4a7-867156b45c85"},
{"id":"human-overpopulation-era","gp":"RxNxLk4yNz","t":"Human Overpopulation Era","k":"history","c":["History","Human"],"x":"In the 21st and 22nd centuries (SEY 2038 - 2157), population levels on [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) began to rise beyond sustainable capacity. Pollution, dwindling resources, and famine affected all nations of the world, leading to overcrowding in the few unspoiled places left on the planet. Natural wonders previously under protection from their governments were bulldozed over in favor of creating settlements or potential arable land. Countless animal and plant species became extinct. The successful terraforming of [Mars (Sol IV)](gp:Regn8D76xw) in 2157 provided a much-needed outlet for the populace, ending the Overpopulation Era and opening the path to the stars.","g":["eras"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/53613aea-0d8f-4877-a13c-4072051bc248"},
{"id":"human-xian-trade-initiative-huxa","gp":"01LvKoLvZ8","t":"Human-Xi'an Trade Initiative (HuXa)","k":"faction","c":["Human","Xi'an","Government","Commerce"],"x":"The Human-Xi'an Trade Initiative (HuXa) is a 2947 trade agreement between the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Spearheaded by [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Kelos Costigan](gp:VJOzBxdJ28)(b:2855 - present), it loosened restrictions on the export and import of goods between the two empires and established incentives for [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj)[Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) to engage in business with [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) companies. Negotiations for the 10,000 page HuXa were conducted in secret between Xi'an and Human government officials on a one-to-one basis to prevent the private sector from speculation. In the runup to the vote, mercenary Maurice Vano attempted to assassinate Costigan. Though it was never confirmed if the attack was motivated by opposition to the HuXa, it inadvertently boosted public opinion on it. The Senate ratified the HuXa by a narrow margin after weeks of debate. Since its passing, multiple Houses such as [Aopoa](gp:VyvY5jyZwp) and [Ng.at'ak](gp:RWolrAj1vm) have debuted goods aimed at the Human market.","g":["uee law","xi'an law","laws"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/09aa48c6-ae9b-4120-ade9-79160484859f"},
{"id":"humans","gp":"0Nwpnr6wa2","t":"Humans","k":"species","c":["Civilizations","Human"],"x":"Humans are a spacefaring civilization originating on Earth (Sol III). They are capable of spaceflight, quantum travel, traversing [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY), and [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) planets. Since achieving piloted spaceflight in SEY 1961, they have settled in over thirty planetary systems and established diplomatic relationships with the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj), though they experienced a prolonged [period of military tension](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) with the Xi'an from 2530 - 2793. After the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) (2603 - 2610), the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) were assimilated into the Human government, the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Their current leader is [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Laylani Addison](gp:VYLvBm6Po1).","g":["human people","united empire of earth","extant civilizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bbae0ec9-3d69-4bf8-a9d0-51f9b813ebc2"},
{"id":"hurricane","gp":"bmNrpdn4gQ","t":"Hurricane","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Hurricane is a strike fighter manufactured by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). Originally launched in SEY 2607 by the now defunct [Casse Aerospace](gp:RPPx3G1MMX), the Hurricane is a turret fighter, combining the speed and maneuverability of an interceptor with a single manual turret operated by a second crew member. The first model of the Hurricane was used by the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN) during the Second Tevarin War where it saw limited combat. In 2871, the UEEN requested that Anvil Aerospace update the design for service against the Vanduul. New models were deployed in 2878.","g":["casse aerospace","heavy fighter","anvil aerospace","fighter","military spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b80c52ba-c5ba-4d40-a481-3cdb30bc753e"},
{"id":"hurston-stanton-i","gp":"0Qlx4dQnxL","t":"Hurston (Stanton I)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Hurston is a hot, arid planet that orbits closest to the sun in the Stanton system. Discovered in 2851, it was sold by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government to the company [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) in 2865. Unrestricted industry and mining, especially of antimatter precursor, have heavily polluted the atmosphere of the planet since the company took possession. Inhabitants are kept up to date on atmospheric conditions by a public air quality index. [Lorville](gp:Rw1ZlJNE36), the oldest and most populous city on Hurston, is home to Hurston Dynamics' [headquarters](gp:R56nmzpqPg), a towering structure nicknamed \"Central\" that casts a permanent shadow on the buildings below.","g":["hurston","stanton i","uninhabitable planet","habitable","hurston dynamics","stanton system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/af39fe34-588a-4735-b4bc-5b859a7857d1"},
{"id":"hurston-dynamics","gp":"RxNxAZpWlQ","t":"Hurston Dynamics","k":"company","c":["Military","Weapons","Commerce","Human"],"x":"Hurston Dynamics is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) weapons manufacturer and materials processor based on [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL). They are the largest producer of standard munitions warheads for military contracts in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), as well as the third-largest [refiner of antimatter precursor](gp:V3qgy3L7ra). [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) owns the planet upon which it is headquartered. The company has frequently been criticized for its controversial employee contracts and its disregard for Hurston's ecology.","g":["weapons manufacturer","munitions manufacturer","materials processor"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8f1dc261-1caf-4430-9201-2072928d2345"},
{"id":"hydrogen-fuel","gp":"V7gMKP2Pwr","t":"Hydrogen Fuel","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Hydrogen fuel is a colorless, odorless fuel derived from hydrogen that is primarily used to power conventional spacecraft engines during non quantum flight. It is mostly collected by spacecraft during flight via a fuel scoop, but it can also be purchased at refueling stations.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/705c9e7d-e8e2-45d1-8220-362b07b87045"},
{"id":"hydrogen-fuel-refinery","gp":"0OaB2wd5Zw","t":"Hydrogen Fuel Refinery","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A hydrogen fuel refinery is an industrial process plant where hydrogen is refined into [hydrogen fuel](gp:V7gMKP2Pwr). Hydrogen refineries are mostly located on orbital platforms around hydrogen-rich gas giants.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c89e1765-6888-4dd9-b77d-8fc31fe57b1a"},
{"id":"hyoton-system","gp":"RkGDYnpq4L","t":"Hyoton System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The Hyoton system is a planetary system in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that consists of an F-type main sequence star, four terrestrial planets, and a super-Earth. The birthplace of the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) people, it is the center of political power in the Xi'an Empire. [Ka'ua (Hyoton IV)](gp:0qa4Zow7pk), the present capital, is seat of the Emperor, and the jungle world [Tethle'a (Hyoton II)](gp:0GxpmKaqzg) is the home of some of its most powerful [Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL). The former Xi'an capital and homeworld of the Xi'an, [RyiXy'an (Hyoton III)](gp:bBz9mEDyqO), was abandoned in the last days of the [Great Divide](gp:VyvYA5qmqX) when an assassination attempt perpetrated by [House Kl.ō](gp:V8gJ62qO81) inadvertently set off a chain reaction that rendered the atmosphere toxic.","g":["xi'an system"]},
{"id":"hyperclay","gp":"RkZ9W2BkDz","t":"HyperClay","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Found on [Hyperion (Fora III)](gp:RegWGPlxqy), HyperClay is a fine, red-colored dust-like particle that was released into the atmosphere when the planet was [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). It is readily picked up by wind and sticks easily to most surfaces, and can also cause respiratory issues if inhaled. HyperClay storms are a perpetual problem for residents of Hyperion.","g":["hyperion","fora iii","geology"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ff184177-86f4-4a44-9cc8-e1843cf58984"},
{"id":"hyperion-fora-iii","gp":"RegWGPlxqy","t":"Hyperion (Fora III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Hyperion (Fora III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Fora system](gp:bo1PDEgGv2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the system's only populated world. In 2316, the Aether Worldbuilding Corporation started terraforming operations on Fora III, but abandoned the project in 2319 when the company unexpectedly folded. When a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) was discovered in Fora's neighboring system [Banshee](gp:0Gx4BENmKg) to the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) system Yulin in 2463, there was a rush to terraform the planet. However, an accident during the terraforming process vaporized part of the mantle, creating a fine red powder that dispersed into the atmosphere and plunged Hyperion into a perpetual, planet-wide dust storm. The project was abandoned. Today, Hyperion is used as a de facto home base for many pirates and smugglers.","g":["hyperion","fora iii","habitable planet","habitable","fora system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6b3f7fee-312f-45d4-b1e6-1067891e8d77"},
{"id":"iapetus-sol-6e","gp":"Rz2j1Z5NeY","t":"Iapetus (Sol 6e)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Iapetus (Sol 6e) is a moon of [Saturn (Sol VI)](gp:0jGpvn8AOW), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Tidally locked to Saturn, the leading hemisphere of the moon is much darker than that of the trailing hemisphere, giving it a striking two-tone coloration. Dust that has fallen from Saturn's rings over time sits in a 12 centimeter layer on the surface of the moon's leading hemisphere, giving it its dark appearance.","g":["iapetus","sol 6e","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c96d2ac0-280e-476a-8a6d-8fcca3b517cf"},
{"id":"icarus-cluster-croshaw-cluster-alpha","gp":"0n11yrOBDB","t":"Icarus Cluster (Croshaw Cluster Alpha)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Icarus cluster (Croshaw cluster alpha) is an [asteroid cluster](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/asteroid-cluster) that orbits the [system's](gp:VaZwNWg372) sun beyond the orbit of [Croshaw IV](gp:RPDDZz2Lwm). Soon after [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) began to colonize Croshaw in the late 2200s, independent miners established themselves in the cluster and began to harvest its resources. It remains one of the oldest active mining fields in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["icarus cluster","asteroid cluster","croshaw system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4ccd1050-b425-4e8e-aad2-672f5fa36245"},
{"id":"icc-stellar-surveyors","gp":"V8gJvaZ2YW","t":"ICC Stellar Surveyors","k":"faction","c":["Exploration","Government","Human"],"x":"The Stellar Surveyors are a group of people who work under the auspices of the [Imperial Cartography Center (ICC)](gp:VyvY7nE1k6) to examine and explore newly discovered worlds and other locations. Their work is essential to the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government in establishing maps and boundaries and in the discovery of any potential resources. Most Stellar Surveyors are invited to work for the ICC based on their skill and experience in the public and private sectors. The official motto of the group is \"Charting the Way Ahead.\"","g":["uee government","imperial cartography center (icc)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/866abdde-d26d-4af6-8a09-cb00dff4910f"},
{"id":"ice-mining","gp":"VlNPQXzlLe","t":"Ice Mining","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Ice mining is a process by which ice is collected from asteroids and other celestial bodies beyond a planetary system's frost line. Mined water ice is generally used to provide water to spacecraft or to locations that suffer from a lack of water. Ice of other kinds, such as carbon dioxide or ammonia, can be commercially sold or used for research purposes.","g":["mining"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0402e719-fabb-4c8e-9119-5498b578e61f"},
{"id":"idris-i","gp":"VYLx8gMQ7x","t":"Idris I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Idris I is a terrestrial planet in the [Idris system](gp:bZkrMGnLdM), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Closest in orbit to its system's sun, heat and radiation have eroded the planet's crust and mantle down to its solid iron core. Its surface is covered in extensive mare-like plains and heavy cratering. The largest of these craters has a diameter of roughly 1600 kilometers, and is surrounded on all sides by a concentric mountainous ring.","g":["idris system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bf67c7f2-4412-416f-ba97-d326e4eaebcc"},
{"id":"idris-ii","gp":"bZkrM6DJ9E","t":"Idris II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Idris II is the second planet from the sun of the [Idris system](gp:bZkrMGnLdM), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It has a dense, volatile, high-pressure atmosphere that consists mainly of carbon dioxide. A layer of highly-reflective clouds of sulfuric acid envelops the planet, preventing its surface from being viewed by the naked eye. While there is evidence of extensive geologic activity in the past, volcanic eruptions are now infrequent.","g":["idris system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6ad3b973-34bd-4d3d-888e-246782102d5d"},
{"id":"idris-iii","gp":"01Lo67kNZG","t":"Idris III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Idris III is an ocean planet in the [Idris system](gp:bZkrMGnLdM), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Although its location suggests it would be a good candidate for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), it is covered in oceans of hot, high-density fluid made up of a mix of water with ammonia and other volatiles that make it far from ideal. Research probes sent to investigate the planet have often fallen victim to its dangerous seas.","g":["idris system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/369c8bab-4e00-4396-841b-89c74c989d66"},
{"id":"idris-system","gp":"bZkrMGnLdM","t":"Idris System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Idris system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), made up of an F-type main sequence star, four terrestrial planets, and a protoplanet. Discovered in SEY 2493, the system experienced significant economic expansion when the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) declared it a Recommended Growth Center in 2533. Because it shares a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) with the [Elysium system](gp:RvlQrKZxPO), it was the site of multiple battles in the [First](gp:bZwQm3meJM) and [Second](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) Tevarin wars. The [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) surprise invasion of Idris in 2542 was the first in a series of events that helped propel [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) to power.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5b54bec5-b54c-44fc-af2f-f1e06aa096af"},
{"id":"idris-v","gp":"VgEXoYwn9Z","t":"Idris V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Idris V is a protoplanet in the [Idris system](gp:bZkrMGnLdM), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Once dense with valuable minerals, the UEE government and various companies systematically strip-mined Idris V throughout the 26th and 27th centuries. Its resources were significantly depleted. Pits and furrows left by mining equipment scar its surface, and its abandoned mining facilities are sporadically occupied by squatters and criminals.","g":["idris system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1d6836ea-44f8-4d7e-a8a7-749848b7e81f"},
{"id":"idris-m","gp":"RWwZ1lGjo2","t":"Idris-M","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The Idris-M is a frigate manufactured by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). It lends its name to the standard line of frigates in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). Idrises are larger than traditional corvettes, but smaller than destroyers and destroyer escorts. They can be found in most active battle group formations in the UEE military. In addition to typical capital weaponry, Idris-class ships maintain a flight deck and a small spacecraft detachment. Several variants, including the Idris-P and the Idris-K, have been made available to the general public.","g":["idris","aegis dynamics","frigate","capital ship","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ec275d3f-516e-4824-b470-36e66e5c164a"},
{"id":"ignis-pyro-5a","gp":"VgENxYYAzk","t":"Ignis (Pyro 5a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Ignis is the innermost moon of the gas giant [Pyro V](gp:RAXv9Yeqay), [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). The canyons and dry riverbeds on its surface suggest that liquid water once flowed there in the distant past. Its frigid average temperature and deadly atmosphere of sulfur dioxide creates an unfriendly environment for those who lack proper protective equipment. Nonetheless, the moon sometimes sees visitors seeking to resupply their air reserves thanks to the small amount of oxygen in the atmosphere.","g":["ignis","pyro 5a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon","pyro system"]},
{"id":"illyana-messer-vi","gp":"bZwQBNmWrL","t":"Illyana Messer VI","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Illyana Messer VI (2631-2697) was [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) from 2662 to 2697 after the assassination of her father, [Corsen Messer V](gp:0OaB8O6awO) and brother [Gammon](gp:0rxrqgDP12). Under her rule, the UEE lessened some of its propaganda practices, allowing news organizations to criticize aspects of the government without retribution. Near the end of her life, she named her youngest son [Samuel](gp:RkZ9W2L2NB) as her successor over his brother [Galor](gp:VyvYAGKxAz) in order to avoid a power struggle between her children. In spite of this precaution, her niece [Astrid](gp:0KnA1D5nQM) seized the throne upon Illyana's death in 2697, sparking a four year stretch of armed conflicts between family loyalists.","g":["uee imperator","messer era","messer dynasty"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6d6f8a1f-5de4-4a99-aef8-3c910dbdd7eb"},
{"id":"illyana-sharrad","gp":"0rxdJWnwyq","t":"Illyana Sharrad","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Illyana Sharrad (2897 - present) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) politician and the High-Secretary of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) from 2942 to 2950. Appointed by [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Kelos Costigan](gp:VJOzBxdJ28), she first took office in 2942 after a two decade career as a civil infrastructure consultant. It was her work exposing a major corruption scheme centered around private firms bidding for public works projects that first drew the attention of the Imperator's office. As High-Secretary, she has advocated for increased funding for infrastructure repair and improvement, worked to close loopholes in Imperial Grant Policy, and helped to oust multiple officials for corruption. She announced her intention to run for Imperator in late 2949 and succeeded in becoming one of five final candidates in the April 2950 Secondary Vote. A member of the [Universalist](gp:VDo6qOgLx9) party, her platform included the Jump Start plan to increase infrastructure spending for achievable local projects in an effort to create employment opportunities, freezing and re-evaluating [Synthworld](gp:RLMmAnr4gj) funding, and the Active Engagement program to increase civic engagement. Anonymous attack ads criticizing her budget plan released just before the Secondary Vote pulled some Universalist support from her in favor of fellow party member [Titus Costigan](gp:VDz7Be7E33).","g":["uee high-secretary"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b1fe84a4-e714-49b9-a54d-d1ffa337b285"},
{"id":"imperators-day","gp":"VgEQXQrrKN","t":"Imperator's Day","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"Imperator's Day is a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) holiday commemorating the unification of all [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) under one government, celebrated annually on July twelfth. It was established as a holiday in 2380 under the name Council Day to recognize the initial council that led the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO). When the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) was founded in 2523, it became Tribunal Day, and in 2546 after [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) established the UEE, it took on its current name. There have been recent petitions to change the name of the holiday again to reflect the diminished political importance of the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) role in the modern governance of the UEE.","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/69e6106b-d244-4b80-8c78-3ff9c7e2f87d"},
{"id":"imperial-arts-foundation","gp":"RX3Nr11PPk","t":"Imperial Arts Foundation","k":"company","c":["Human","Art","Organizations"],"x":"# IMPERIAL ARTS FOUNDATION\nThe Imperial Arts Foundation (IAF) is a nonprofit charitable organization located on [Green (Ellis III)](gp:RWoNrNeLKP) that provides funding and resources to artists and arts programs in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It was founded in 2811 by Marana River (2788-2887). Every year, the IAF awards grants and fellowships to artists who work with a wide variety of forms, including music, sculpture, dance, performance, digital media, and writing.\n\n# BACKGROUND\nAfter graduating from Aydo Polytechnic with a degree in sculpture, heiress Marana River was able to work comfortably as an artist thanks to her family's wealth. Many of her friends, however, struggled to make art and support themselves at the same time. This difference in circumstances pushed River to research how she could provide artists like her friends with enough money to concentrate on their work without worrying about paying rent or obtaining basic necessities.\n\nEnlisting the help of her parents, River secured initial funding to hold a gala, to which she invited local businesses, government officials, celebrities, and wealthy friends. The gala was a success; in its first year, the organization raised roughly 3 million UEC. With these funds, River registered her new charity under the name Green Foundation for the Arts and hired her first employees. She continued to hold other fundraiser events alongside her annual gala, and after six years of fundraising, established an endowment of 400 million UEC. The charity awarded grants only to new artists on Green for eleven years. When it opened a second branch on [Aremis (Vega II)](gp:RkGGjdOwQz) in 2829, it was renamed the Imperial Arts Foundation and amended its mission to support new artists in all parts of the UEE.\n\n# EVENTS\nThe IAF sponsors two major events every year: the Green Gala and the Folk Arts and Music Fair. The Green Gala, held at the Green Museum of Art, is a red-carpet, invite-only event used to generate funds for the IAF. Celebrities and philanthropists attend alongside IAF grant recipients selected by an independent committee of arts peers. Each gala is assigned a theme to set the tone for attendees' formal dress. The Folk Arts and Music Fair, held on multiple planets on a rotating basis, is an arts festival showcasing traditional and non-traditional arts unique to each planet in the UEE. The first fair, held on [Saisei (Centauri III)](gp:Vy22NQJ1q6) in 2847, honored traditional Saisei instrument craft.\n\n# AWARDS\nIn addition to grants, the IAF gives out awards to artists who demonstrate outstanding potential. Those early in their careers are given the River's Promise Award and a monetary prize. The Eminence Award is given to artists who have benefited from IAF grants and have gone on to achieve prominence in their chosen discipline. Lastly, supporters who have donated to the IAF, without whom the charity would be unable to continue its mission, are recognized with a Patron of the Arts Award.","g":["non-profit organization"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a9c722a1-9264-4aaf-9390-b36e18217e68"},
{"id":"imperial-cartography-center","gp":"VyvY7nE1k6","t":"Imperial Cartography Center","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"The Imperial Cartography Center (ICC) is a public institute in the United Empire of Earth (UEE) responsible for locating jump points and keeping current stellar cartography information up to date. It was founded by [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) in 2546 as a branch of the Government Cartography Agency (GCA). The ICC is instrumental in providing the most current star charts and jump point entrances.","g":["imperial cartography center (icc)","uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0c442ad2-c653-49dd-b5b0-43ba924b8200"},
{"id":"inb-new-corvo","gp":"0QxYAEaojL","t":"INB New Corvo","k":"place","c":["Locations","Military","Human"],"x":"The Imperial Naval Base (INB) at New Corvo is a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military facility on Aremis (Vega II). All [Naval](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) personnel moving in and out of the Vega system are required to check in at the base. Because of its proximity to a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) system, INB New Corvo also serves as a training school on Vanduul tactics.","g":["ueen base","uee navy"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/75d9e426-7b66-446b-85eb-cbefa6697043"},
{"id":"ins-aniene","gp":"VlNPQMPnrA","t":"INS Aniene","k":"place","c":["Military","Locations"],"x":"INS Aniene was a [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) installation in the [Tiber system](gp:RMNLm97EDj). It was originally established as one of two fleet support bases in the system with large-scale drydock and collier facilities capable of outfitting multiple capital ships simultaneously. During the [Siege of Tiber (SEY 2732 - 2736)](gp:0OaBY5pGrq), Aniene became a major command and control point for the 31st Battle Group during its initial defense of the system. On 29 December 2736, the base was completely destroyed by a massed [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) attack.","g":["space station","ueen station","siege of tiber","uee navy","uee space station","ueen base"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ea29619b-bccc-4425-ad0e-1c4ef77eb7c7"},
{"id":"ins-dunleavy","gp":"Vy2jgd8Zk8","t":"INS Dunleavy","k":"place","c":["Locations","Military"],"x":"The Imperial Naval Station (INS) Dunleavy is a [Naval](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) base located in the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Found near the Sol-[Davien](gp:Rz2g71YlkY) jump point, it is the main operational center of the Sol fleet, and is the system's first line of defense against potential invaders. The station is outfitted with extensive training facilities, and is renowned for the war games it regularly hosts.","g":["space station","ueen station","uee navy","sol system","uee space station","ueen base"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bf5dc936-e5ec-4eee-97b7-4c1d0b65358e"},
{"id":"ins-flavus","gp":"RkZ9WG9L7n","t":"INS Flavus","k":"place","c":["Military","Locations"],"x":"INS Flavus is a former [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) installation in the [Tiber system](gp:RMNLm97EDj). Flavus was originally established as one of two fleet support bases in the system with a focus on supply chain management. Flavus acted as a military depot and a contact point for civilian freighters moving goods and personnel to Tiber. During the [Siege of Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq) (SEY 2732 - 2736), Flavus was designated as the secondary command and control point following the destruction of [INS Aniene](gp:VlNPQMPnrA). Surviving elements of the 81st Battle Group massed at Flavus in anticipation of a push to retake the system. When the decision to retreat from the system was made the station was instead abandoned.","g":["ueen station","space station","siege of tiber","uee navy","uee space station","ueen base"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e6fc8c71-951d-4ed1-8d9e-ac1b20175cb6"},
{"id":"ins-hephaestus","gp":"VYLx8g5p8v","t":"INS Hephaestus","k":"place","c":["Locations","Military"],"x":"INS Hephaestus is a military outpost that orbits [Tangaroa (Helios II)](gp:RX3rnQ3XqM) in the [Helios system](gp:0KxpdzWBK4), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Operated by the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), the station acts as a general launching area for system security and as a waystation for fleets moving through the system. Battle Groups frequently utilize the station as an operational headquarters for war gaming scenarios and training exercises.","g":["space station","helios system","uee navy","ueen base","uee space station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cd06c5aa-caa0-49d1-be8f-e57c7034f7df"},
{"id":"ins-jericho","gp":"RkGG7Yp5pL","t":"INS Jericho","k":"place","c":["Locations","Military"],"x":"The INS Jericho is a [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Navy (UEEN) station in the [Stanton system](gp:RX3lKBA3dq). Completed in SEY 2871, it was named after leader of Squadron 214 Commander Amare Jericho, who sacrificed his life battling [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) forces up to the last minutes of the [UEEN](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) pullout [from Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq) in 2736. The station is outfitted as a refuel and resupply station for UEEN vessels, and serves as a center for logistical support.","g":["space station","stanton system","uee navy","ueen base","uee space station","ueen station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f14c1b48-4308-4e91-bf3f-d769de81f02f"},
{"id":"integrity-and-honor","gp":"VpGE8vMX9N","t":"Integrity and Honor","k":"culture","c":["Military","Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*Integrity and Honor* is a 45 minute-long United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN) recruiting film released in 2935. It was intended to spur naval enlistment and to improve the public's understanding and opinion of the military's role in the conflict with the Vanduul. It was filmed aboard the *UEES Integrity* during a 2932-33 leg patrol, with additional scenes staged aboard the cruiser after the completion of its tour and others generated from archival gun camera footage.","g":["propaganda","vids","uees integrity"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/680c2d45-ec7d-4ae4-9a9d-d6f834be41c4"},
{"id":"interdimension-software","gp":"R9Bw9vjxv7","t":"InterDimension Software","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"InterDimension Software is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) entertainment software company best known for the [*Star Marine*](gp:bE3rke4j28) franchise. InterDimension was founded in 2941 by level builder James Romanov and tech designer James Vandyke. The company has been responsible for several high-profile game releases such as the kid-friendly *Admiral Cool* franchise and the popular *Star Marine* combat simulator. Its corporate headquarters is located on microTech (Stanton IV) in Stanton System, [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["game developer","james romanov","james vandyke","microtech (planet)","stanton iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1d86caf9-a3c7-426a-863f-0245d5f457e7"},
{"id":"intergalactic-aerospace-expo","gp":"R4jpEgezde","t":"Intergalactic Aerospace Expo","k":"history","c":["Commerce","Spacecraft"],"x":"The Intergalactic Aerospace Expo (IAE) is an annual spacecraft exposition that is held in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Founded in 2670 by spacecraft enthusiast Audrey Timmerman, it was initially held on [Castor (Corel IV)](gp:VYLJxEXrvW) until 2847, when the board of directors voted to rotate the location of the IAE each year. This continued until the board voted to permanently host the event on [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN) in the [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ) in 2913. Spacecraft manufacturers such as [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed), [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34), and [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) use the expo to debut new ships and run sales. It is usually held over 10 Standard Earth Days. Starting in 2948, the IAE began hosting satellite events to allow more people to attend with several being hosted in the [Stanton system](gp:RX3lKBA3dq). Since its premiere in 2950, the spectrum show *[Whitley's Guide](gp:V8WgdOP8px)* runs a special series of episodes on the IAE each year hosted by [Jax McCleary](gp:RL6MjgGJJ3).","g":["exhibition","iae"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3d73a288-c995-40db-8e26-0177a4b32fe7"},
{"id":"intergalactic-research-concepts","gp":"RxNxD9lO56","t":"Intergalactic Research Concepts","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Intergalactic Research Concepts (IRC) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of spacecraft-mounted energy weapons. Their specialty is developing cutting-edge weaponry, such as plasma and tachyon cannons, and adapting them for mass production. Products include the ZW Helicon Plasma cannon range and the X series tachyon cannons.","g":["weapons manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/91f727ba-152b-4bc0-ae3c-95d138ad414b"},
{"id":"interspace-communication-technology","gp":"0NjXvAKgJ4","t":"Interspace Communication Technology","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Interspace communication technology refers to devices that enable the rapid transmission of data across great distances. Composed of an intricately connected web of space stations and satellite-based relay towers, the network facilitates quick information transfer by sending burst packets of data from station to station. During the [Human Colonial Expansion Era](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm) from SEY 2380 to 2530, these relay stations were key in accelerating the growth of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) settlements located outside the Sol system. With a quick, reliable communication network on hand, colonists were reassured that they would be able to stay in touch with their loved ones and request aid if needed without waiting months between messages. The network also facilitated travel and trade, and allowed the central government to supervise even long-distance colonies.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3e7cc7bf-5d72-4a4d-8d28-6e344ce2e269"},
{"id":"interstellar-transport-guild","gp":"V3G8yAEDBp","t":"Interstellar Transport Guild","k":"company","c":["Organizations"],"x":"The Interstellar Transport Guild (ITG) is a professional union of cargo haulers that acts as an intermediary between contractors and companies. Founded in SEY 2391, the ITG was created to combat the harsh conditions, unrealistic schedules, and lack of benefits common to the growing fleet of haulers that were key to supporting the [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and settlement of newly discovered planets. Among their most notable achievements are securing the right to self-defense while hauling and the enforcement delivery timelines that allow haulers to take breaks.","g":["unions"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/55077061-c576-4a81-87d5-caa218d510f0"},
{"id":"invictus-launch-week","gp":"0KnDxLpvkM","t":"Invictus Launch Week","k":"history","c":["Human","Military","Holidays"],"x":"Invictus Launch Week (Fleet Week) is an event held the last week of May that marks the beginning of the new recruiting year and graduation of the latest class of officers and pilots of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4).  It originated in SEY 2542 during the [First Tevarin War (2541-2546)](gp:bZwQm3meJM), when the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN)[Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL), in need of new soldiers in the face of [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) invasion, sent transports from planetary system to planetary system to pick up volunteers and transport them to UPE Naval base Invictus on Mars (Sol IV). It was established as a yearly event under [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) in 2581. Today, although Invictus base no longer exists, the event is still celebrated by the UEE Navy under the same name.","g":["fleet week","uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f4ac06dc-bf5b-4e79-ba9f-8b590516cc67"},
{"id":"inacio-stanos-melo","gp":"0qnNMa3Mgq","t":"Inácio Santos Melo","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Inácio Santos Melo (2513-2615) was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) journalist and the host of [*Showdown!*](gp:RwZBw4Lrxz) from 2546 to 2588. Born on [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5) in 2513, Melo's first job was as a political aid, leading to a brief career in campaign management, until he became a political correspondent for the [*United Times/Tribune*](gp:RAdjeJe5Y7). He was hired to replace show creator [Upsana Dixit](gp:0Gx2n4G7na) in 2546 as the host of *Showdown!* His confrontational style with the guests on the program led to a boost in ratings and became a part of the show's standard methodology even after Melo's retirement in 2588.","g":["showdown!","cestulus","davien ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/26ac3635-5b05-4bbe-8d54-5b341cc06eeb"},
{"id":"io-sol-5a","gp":"VJXq2NLeZP","t":"Io (Sol 5a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Io (Sol 5a) is a moon of [Jupiter](gp:Vy2OMo22wz) (Sol V), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Due to tidal heating and the presence of a subsurface ocean of molten and solid rock, Io is the most geologically active object in the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5). Armor manufacturer Caldera utilizes the surface of Io as a testbed for its newest environmental suits.","g":["io","sol 5a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/76537170-8f30-4538-b288-10878c922d6e"},
{"id":"ironclad","gp":"RxnOyokowd","t":"Ironclad","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Ironclad is a heavy freight spacecraft manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). Developed as a vessel that can traverse dangerous routes, the Ironclad's hull is covered with specialized, thick armor plating that can withstand assaults from multiple types of weapons. Missile launchers and turrets give it the ability to fend off attackers, and a trio of tractor beams allow it to remotely load and unload cargo without risking the lives of its crew. In the event of an emergency, the detachable command module can be used as an escape pod.","g":["freight","heavy freight","drake interplanetary","human spacecraft","ironclad series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e0efa2ca-415f-42ab-b8f6-e1d2c34fe70d"},
{"id":"ironclad-assault","gp":"bmGOynQJ38","t":"Ironclad Assault","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Ironclad Assault is a combined arms platform spacecraft manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). A variant of the [Ironclad](gp:RxnOyokowd) freighter, it has been given a fortified ramp to support the fast deployment of ground-based assault platforms and squads of infantry. Quad turrets have been added to provide air support, along with a full-service garage capable of the fabrication of components, refueling, and rearming.","g":["ironclad","drake interplanetary","human spacecraft","combined arms platform","ironclad series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0a815ab8-2ae0-412a-8d5d-3770717085ed"},
{"id":"ita-stanton-1d","gp":"bZkwADDA5d","t":"Ita (Stanton 1d)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Ita is the outermost moon of [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL). Its dusty terrain is dotted with tall rock formations and craters from old meteor impacts. Leadership of [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) chose to name the moon after Chief Warrant Officer [Ita Hurston](gp:0qnNMY2dO1) (2512 - 2542) of the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) Advanced Special Operations unit, who was killed in action during the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM).","g":["ita","stanton 1d","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","hurston","stanton i","ita hurston","hurston dynamics","uee moon","stanton i moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1c3cc2db-b427-4f0d-adea-079d6d2fab01"},
{"id":"ita-hurston","gp":"0qnNMY2dO1","t":"Ita Hurston","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Chief Warrant Officer Ita Hurston (2512-2542) was a [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN)Advanced Special Operations soldier who died in the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541-2546). The fourth moon of Hurston (Stanton I), [Ita](gp:bZkwADDA5d), was named in her honor.","g":["first tevarin war","hurston dynamics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/db940de1-0e3c-48b7-9c4d-f956a60721bb"},
{"id":"ivar-messer-i","gp":"RXlXYPWk8q","t":"Ivar Messer I","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Ivar Messer (2516-2592) was the first [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). He was a Captain in the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN)[Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) 112th Infantry Battalion when he distinguished himself in the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541-2546) during Operation Nemesis and in the [Battle of Idris IV](gp:ReJajXKelk), when he took command after the death of his captain and led his troops to victory. The government capitalized off his image as a brave and charismatic officer in an advertising campaign to recruit soldiers. After the war, he utilized this to gain political influence, securing a position in the [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) as High-General. He then leveraged public fervor against the [Atrocity at Jata](gp:0Gz5GgEvkj) to create the new governmental position of [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr). During an emergency election held 15 December 2546, he was elected to the office he helped enact. He went on to completely restructure the government: first dissolving the Tribunal, then renaming the UPE the United Empire of Earth, and then declaring himself Imperator in early 2547. He continued to enact sweeping changes, accruing power and further entrenching his position. Ivar married Corporate CTO Delia Hassan in 2571 and had one son, [Deacon](gp:0j46m4BYge), shortly after, who would ascend to Imperator after his father's death in 2592.","g":["prime citizen","uee imperator","first tevarin war","upe high-general","messer era","battle of idris iv","tribunal","messer dynasty"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/93405fd1-c1c2-402c-aee1-827120d5fb40"},
{"id":"j-harris-arnold","gp":"Vy2ZqLy458","t":"J Harris Arnold","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"# J HARRIS ARNOLD\n\nJude \"J\" Harris Arnold (2742 - 2853) was the lead designer and founder of [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). Born in 2742, he was the only son of Pax Harris and Ndilimeke Arnold, real estate moguls on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). He graduated from the Astronautics Laboratory within the [Martian Institute of Space Technology (MIST)](gp:RL67MAJreO), where he was first exposed to the works of deceased spacecraft designer Leonard Casse, whose portfolio strongly influenced Arnold's future designs. In 2772, he founded Anvil Aerospace, which went on to become one of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military's premier shipbuilders. Arnold insisted on personally approving every part of his vehicles' designs while he served as CEO. His policies of profit-sharing with his workers and fostering the talents of promising employees at Anvil led to the launch of many successful careers, and made him a popular figure in the often cutthroat spacecraft manufacturing industry. He died of old age in 2853. \n\n# CAREER\n\nArnold began his career as a junior designer at [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) in 2763, where he would eventually be assigned to assist on Project Monitor, developing the vehicle which would become the [Hammerhead](gp:ReJaMyZAw6). A design of his was selected to be made into one of six prototypes, but it was not ultimately delivered to the [UEE Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) after it failed early flight tests. Arnold became demoralized with his job after a lack of feedback from his supervisors, especially after repeated rejections of new designs following his failed prototype. In his spare time, he began to sketch ideas for ships based on the creations of his favorite designer, Leonard Casse. \n\nIt became apparent to Arnold by 2770 that he had no path forward at Aegis. He decided to quit his position and accepted a seed loan from his parents to start his own ship manufacturing company, which he planned to operate based on the flat organization style that was used at Casse Aerospace. Under this style of management, everyone's opinions would be given equal weight no matter their status, with all final decisions left to Arnold. Although this would cause a long development process, Arnold felt that worker satisfaction would lead to a stronger final product.\n\nIn 2772, construction on his new shipbuilding facility in Nova Kyiv, Terra was complete. Arnold named the new company Anvil Aerospace in reference to former MIST professor Robert Calvin's famous assertion from his book *Mechanisms of Empire* that military spending \"...fuels the furnaces of expansion and strikes the anvils of innovation.\" Within the first year, Arnold and his team had created a prototype fighter called the Osprey. As an homage to Casse, Arnold included signature elements from Casse's ships such as curved wings and the open circle signet in his own designs.\n\nUsing connections he had made during his time at Aegis, Arnold showed the prototype to a small gathering of Navy officials. The ship proved to be a hit and the Navy placed Anvil's first ever order. As word spread of the new manufacturer's successful entry into the military market, it caught the eye of the holding firm that owned the rights to the Casse Aerospace portfolio, which sued Arnold for copyright infringement. Facing a potentially devastating lawsuit, Arnold chose to settle the case by purchasing all of Casse Aerospace's portfolio for an undisclosed sum. Arnold released a public statement that Anvil would continue to utilize Casse's signature elements in their ships as an ode to a talented designer who died far too young. \n\nAfter the events of the [anti-Messer revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7) in 2792, the UEE stripped Aegis Dynamics of most of its contracts due to its strong association with the [Messer regime](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo). As a part of the UEE Navy's defensive restructure focused on protecting and serving the civilian population, Anvil Aerospace was approached by Vice Admiral Galen Whishaw of the UEEN Research & Development Division, who offered Anvil a direct contract to develop a brand new ship. The result was the [U4A-3 Terrapin](gp:RWwZQYmBAe), a design that Arnold had been working on with lead engineer Allegra Wilsing. The successful deployment of that ship in 2796 helped to make Arnold and his company an indispensable part of the UEE's defense. Over the next few decades, Arnold personally supervised the development of all Anvil's military ships, most notably the [F7A Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk), which replaced the Aegis [Avenger](gp:ReJanvr73r) as the UEE's standard front-line fighter.\n\n# LATER LIFE\n\nIn semi-retirement by the early 2840s, Arnold nevertheless still required that all parts of a ship's development be approved by him. On a trip to [MacArthur (Kilian V)](gp:Rz22dGBlnz) in 2850, he is reported to have been evaluating changes made to Anvil's many projects on his [mobiGlas](gp:01dW3alkmB) in between meetings with UEEN leadership. He served as a guest lecturer at MIST in 2851 and was invited to return the following year, but he declined, citing a desire to return \"home\" to the Anvil offices in Nova Kyiv. He died at his desk in 2853.","g":["jude harris arnold","anvil aerospace","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4295aa93-7074-43e0-af98-36743979aa1b"},
{"id":"jai-virgil-1a","gp":"0GxYzeAA9g","t":"Jai (Virgil 1a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Jai (Virgil 1a) is the first moon from [Cyrene (Virgil I)](gp:VlMBNGnxK5), [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Composed of silicate and carbon, its pale and largely unmarred surface strongly reflects the light of its sun. During the rare cloudless nights that Jai is full, it shines so brightly that very few stars can be seen from the surface of Cyrene.","g":["jai","virgil 1a","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","virgil system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/28680f18-c959-4fee-a7bc-facf076839c3"},
{"id":"jalan-elysium-iv","gp":"VarAXY2zy2","t":"Jalan (Elysium IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human","Tevarin"],"x":"Jalan is the most populous planet in the [Elysium system](gp:RvlQrKZxPO), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE), and is the home planet of [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X). Originally called Kaleeth, it was annexed by the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) at the end of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) and colonized by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), displacing many Tevarin. [Warlord Corath'Thal](gp:RkGxWGQ2Qp) launched the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) to retake the lost planet, but his efforts ultimately failed. In SEY 2610, it was recognized by the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) and renamed Jalan. The oldest known Tevarin structures that survived both Tevarin wars and the [Purge](gp:R6dWB877Nn) can be found here; most notably, the Rijoran Temple in Gemma. In 2946, one of its current Senators, [Suj Kossi](gp:RMNgraDJAA), became the first Tevarin elected to the Senate.","g":["jalan","elysium iv","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/39dc5604-b16f-4f99-8239-a0c96234ba20"},
{"id":"janis-rezaian","gp":"VaZwBAGOBv","t":"Janis Rezaian","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Janis Rezaian (2469-2550) was High-Secretary of the United Planets of Earth from 2539 to 2546. Along with High-Advocate [Mauricio Tusk](gp:VY4WBM6OZ1), she publicly criticized High-General [Ivar Messer](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) for his unwillingness to negotiate with his colleagues on the [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL). When Messer obtained the office of [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr), he dismantled the Tribunal. Rezaian ran for Senator of Vann (Croshaw III) in 2548, but lost to her opponent. She died of natural causes at age 81.","g":["upe high-secretary","tribunal","vann","croshaw iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/43a0c5cb-c423-4494-a092-b4f141dc7445"},
{"id":"janna-thurville","gp":"Var8a27eW2","t":"Janna Thurville","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Janna Thurville (b. 2895) is the Senator of [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN), [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The oldest daughter of former [Governor](gp:RkZ9A5KjBL) of Severus [Joona Tzur](gp:RkGaY322MQ) and concert pianist Xin Yi Tzur, she was elected as one of the first [Senators](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) of Severus alongside [Centralist](gp:01dWmzB3aG) Hideo Uto when it was recognized in 2937. A member of the [Transitionalist](gp:0OaylwDmvv) party, she supports the decentralization of governmental power and its delegation to the UEE's most economically successful planets. She advocates for increased spending on education and the arts, and is opposed to excessive military spending.","g":["uee senator","transitionalist party","severus","kiel iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/be8b5a39-e80a-4b54-b76c-20a4e89f0eba"},
{"id":"janus","gp":"VDzOvEdNyd","t":"Janus","k":"history","c":["Science and Technology","History","Human"],"x":"Janus was an artificial intelligence (AI) program designed to monitor and pilot the long-haul colony spacecraft [*Artemis*](gp:0jGxngnLzm), launched in SEY 2232. Prominent AI researcher Dr. Carol Zahir began work on the program that would become Janus in 2201. Zahir spent the rest of her career growing her team of researchers and bringing Janus to life. Though she ultimately succeeded in creating the most complex artificial intelligence yet developed, she passed away two years before its completion. The Janus AI was lost alongside its ship when the *Artemis* fell out of contact with Earth (Sol III) in 2237 and disappeared. Rumors that Janus purposely caused the disappearance of the *Artemis* circulated in [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) news after the ship vanished, though there was no evidence to support this claim. Many cite this negative speculation as one of the reasons [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) have done little research on artificial intelligence since the early 23rd century.","g":["artificial intelligence","the artemis","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/51d2611e-798a-497d-9228-109567a1ba4b"},
{"id":"jarl-virgil-3b","gp":"0NjXwdNkre","t":"Jarl (Virgil 3b)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Jarl (Virgil 3b) is the second moon from [Virgil III](gp:V8WagLl2Nx), [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Instead of a water cycle, it has a methane cycle, fed by the vast fields of methane ice that coat its surface. Gaseous methane directly sublimates off the ice and creates clouds high in the atmosphere, where snow forms before falling back down onto Jarl.","g":["jarl","virgil 3b","virgil system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f7385fa3-de45-4587-b9cb-4becfab7ca51"},
{"id":"jata","gp":"Rz2PmWxpMM","t":"Jata","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Jata is the most populous city of [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5). Because the planet's atmosphere is thin, Jata is largely located under enormous, complex biodomes kept habitable by a system of air production facilities that help supplement the oxygen supply. It became the [United Nations of Earth's (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) main center for trade with the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) after [Banu-Human First Contact](gp:VY4Wnv7ZgW) in SEY 2438. The city has remained a hub of commerce and shipping, partially due to the presence of major spacecraft manufacturer [Aegis Dynamics'](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) main headquarters. Jata has often been the setting of political upheavals, such as the 2529 [Unified Currency Riots](gp:0QlvpyjLvJ) and the 2546 [Atrocity at Jata](gp:0Gz5GgEvkj), the first in a series of terrorist bombings that led to the implementation of [Ivar Messer I's](gp:RXlXYPWk8q)[Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr) plan.","g":["cestulus","davien ii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bb1626e7-dcc9-448a-b09d-2634e5bc2951"},
{"id":"javelin","gp":"0OaBgMK9DO","t":"Javelin","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Javelin is a destroyer created by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) for the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). Designed as a modular spacecraft, the UEEN can make major conversions to the Javelin for different roles rather than constructing individual specialized capital ships. Javelins are used as convoy escorts, fleet support, orbital fire suppression, reconnaissance in force, and fast interception missions. Surplus Javelins have been sold on the civilian market.","g":["destroyer","aegis dynamics","capital ship","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/179f8a1d-9943-4d12-8086-5fd79a63843f"},
{"id":"jax-mccleary","gp":"RL6MjgGJJ3","t":"Jax McCleary","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Jax McCleary (b.2887 - present) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) journalist, pilot, and [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) personality best known for hosting the shows [Galactic Tour](gp:0rxqDJrxp3) and [Whitley's Guide](gp:V8WgdOP8px). Before becoming a show host, McCleary worked as the sports anchor for the local news program in Aydo on Green (Ellis III), gaining a reputation as a bombastic, tongue-in-cheek commentator on spacecraft races with deep insight on the inner workings and handling of the ships. McCleary left his position in 2931 to launch *Galactic Gear*, a show that examines and reviews spacecraft through often outlandish means. The show was sold in 2945 to [Voyager Direct](gp:V7dgpKQ7rL) after years of ratings success and was relaunched and rebranded as *Galactic Tour* in 2946. McCleary left the show shortly after, and returned to racing commentary until accepting a contract to host *Whitley's Guide* in 2950.","g":["galactic gear","galactic tour","whitley's guide"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8d2bffa1-b10e-402b-84dd-988f3c7c20dd"},
{"id":"jele-city","gp":"0KxKBKXmg3","t":"Jele City","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Jele City is the capital of [Vann (Croshaw III)](gp:bZkk4l4j2D). Since its founding early in Vann's [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) process, the city was designed to offer maximum protection from the cold weather. Most of the vibrantly-painted homes are built in rows very close to one another in order to cut down on wind chill, with narrow passageways between them. Due to its location near the equator, the temperature changes very little throughout the year.","g":["vann","croshaw iii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/41d78467-fa14-40fc-914d-b070bba4c551"},
{"id":"joker-engineering","gp":"ReJa3WXqmE","t":"Joker Engineering","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Joker Engineering is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of novelty spacecraft weapons and components. Founded by eccentric engineer Barlowe Elias, the company's key interest is designing alternative weapons with unlikely applications that defy the usual missile-or-gun classification. Their unusual products are sometimes utilized by criminals because of their unconventional warfare applications, particularly the Beacon Bomb, an explosive shell that emits a simulated distress call.","g":["weapons manufacturer","barlowe elias","arccorp (planet)","stanton iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3a3fa5a1-3f68-4ca0-bd73-bcda24e44333"},
{"id":"joona-tzur","gp":"RkGaY322MQ","t":"Joona Tzur","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Joona Tzur (b. 2852) is the former Governor of [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN), [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Elected in 2903, he established a program to revitalize Severus' economy by selling the planet's abandoned military infrastructure to corporations in search of low-cost real estate. The strategy paid off when numerous aerospace corporations took Tzur up on his offer. Tzur reinvested the money into the creation of green spaces and other public places, creating more jobs for the residents and improving the previously blighted landscape. In 2913, thanks to Tzur's overtures, the board of the [Intergalactic Aerospace Expo](gp:R4jpEgezde) elected to make a permanent home on Severus. Tzur completed his term as Governor in 2915.","g":["uee governor","severus","kiel iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1d3a85ca-15f3-4198-b7a4-4b65a4504dd0"},
{"id":"joule-consortium","gp":"R9BW9XLNv9","t":"Joule Consortium","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Joule Consortium is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of energy-related products, including energy weapon munitions. Although the company advertises itself as a medical supply company, their flagship product is a high-end laser cell used in personal and spacecraft weaponry. Joule has invested in other energy-related concerns in the hopes of expanding the market for their laser cells.","g":["munitions manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d75a947a-9f84-4669-99ec-af534c5e3dda"},
{"id":"judecca-ellis-xii","gp":"RWoNrAd8lA","t":"Judecca (Ellis XII)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Judecca (Ellis XII) is a terrestrial ice planet located in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Covered in kilometers of water ice, Judecca is profoundly cold, and has a tenuous atmosphere made of hydrogen and oxygen. The planet is occasionally used for ice-mining expeditions. It was nicknamed Judecca after a frozen lake depicted in an ancient Human story that eternally imprisons traitors.","g":["judecca","ellis xii","ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/36a62e7d-279b-48c6-87bf-67d9e3bd182f"},
{"id":"juliet-maupin","gp":"VarxxjKJe5","t":"Juliet Maupin","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Juliet Maupin (2747 - 2862) was a weapons and scanner engineer. She began her career at [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) as a machinist in 2766, eventually transferring to the ships team on [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5) in 2772. There, she worked her way up to lead engineer and led the team responsible for the 2783 revamp of the [Retaliator](gp:0qnN6j2Gq7) bomber. Following that success, she was enlisted by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military to produce a new line of powerful and advanced weapons for the [Messer government](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo). Maupin fled with her family to the [Corel system](gp:R9vQnko7Y2) after the events of the [anti-Messer revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7) for fear of being associated with the former regime. A crate of Maupin's prototypes that never made it to the Kilian system for testing was discovered in a Cestulus warehouse in 2911 by [Dalton Colabello](gp:VlMJJp9B9M), who went on to use them as the basis for the debut line of weapons for his new company [Apocalypse Arms](gp:V7gM1wXdWk).","g":["apocalypse arms","cestulus","davien ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/022e3f03-7a3a-4d6b-8be4-edd596d9e1e5"},
{"id":"jump-point","gp":"0rqzJPaMpY","t":"Jump Point","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A jump point is a point in space that marks the opening of a [traversable wormhole (jump tunnel)](gp:bBp6Bx33wm) that tunnels through interspace and opens to another location, often a different solar system. In their natural state, jump points are nearly invisible to the naked eye. Their discovery has allowed civilizations to cross vast distances in the universe. Known, stabilized jump points are marked off with large structures and usually patrolled to ensure that they have been legally and safely traversed.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/04972f32-c5e4-4476-b6e2-f7831cf191ab"},
{"id":"jump-tunnel","gp":"bBp6Bx33wm","t":"Jump Tunnel","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A jump tunnel (traversable wormhole) is a naturally-occurring topological feature in spacetime that effectively allows for superliminal travel through interspace across vast distances. Jump tunnels allow spacefaring civilizations to easily and quickly travel to other planetary systems that would normally only be accessible after years, sometimes decades of quantum travel. Though jump tunnels can be stabilized and often have incredibly long lives, they are known to collapse without warning.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9d6113d9-e223-472f-ab17-5ccdb25a292c"},
{"id":"jumping-lime-yar-fruit","gp":"R6dZA4XGO5","t":"Jumping Lime (Yar Fruit)","k":"life","c":["Food and Beverages","Plants"],"x":"# JUMPING LIME (YAR FRUIT)\n\nThe jumping lime, also called the Yar lime or the Yar fruit, is a sweet, sour, astringent fruit that grows from a cactus that naturally mutated on [Yar (Centauri II)](gp:R6dd5pyOZ5) some time after the planet's [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). Discovered in 2450, the fruit was named for the ease with which it falls off its parent plant and clings to clothing and skin. It was domesticated as a crop plant in the early 26th Century. Wild specimens can still be found in Yar's Red Desert, but they are not as sweet as the domesticated variety.\n\n# CULTIVATION\n\nThe jumping cactus (cylindropuntia acerbus), the plant from which the jumping lime grows, is a mutation of the Earth (Sol III)-native plant jumping cholla (cylindropuntia fulgida). A tree-like plant, it has branches that grow near the base of the trunk, each one covered in small, hair-like spines with tiny hooks on the end. It grows to heights of roughly three meters. The branches are susceptible to overgrowth during especially wet years, and will prematurely die unless pruned or supported. Rows of jumping cacti with their branches tied to stakes are a common sight in Yar's former mining towns.\n\nAt the end of the wet season, a vivid purple and green flower sprouts from the end of each branch of the cactus. If a flower is pollinated by hand or by night-flying insects, the petals will wither and it will develop into a spiny, round, purplish fruit. Branches that don't produce fruit tend to drop off the plant and dry in the desert sun. After four weeks of growth, farmers remove the branches with stunted fruit to concentrate the plant's resources on the branches growing big, healthy fruit. At eight weeks, the barbed, leathery skin of the fruit turns green and is ready to be harvested. Workers traditionally wear protective gear as the spines can pierce skin. The fruit must be de-spined and peeled in order to access the sweet, very tart, astringent flesh.\n\n# DISTRIBUTION\n\nCylindropuntia acerbus is indigenous to Yar and takes easily to any planet with deserts or dry forests. The Red Desert is home to a number of thick forests of the plant that may range over many hectares. It is common to see local fauna with the fruit attached to their hides, which is the main way the plant's seeds are spread in the wild. Some desert animals have adapted to be able to cope with the plant's spines and will break open the unripe fruit to consume it during the dry season. Although the fruit does have hydrating properties, its juice is astringent enough that it often causes a feeling of false dehydration. Yar locals warn against eating the fruit unless another source of water is nearby.\n\n# USES\n\nJumping limes are appreciated for their intense flavor and aroma, though many prefer to eat them cooked rather than raw. When they are roasted, some of the astringency decreases and the sugars caramelize, transforming the flesh from very tannic and sour to bright and acidic. Yar locals will peel, chop, and stew the fruit with sweetener until it's completely broken down into pulp, and then strain it and use the liquid to make jelly. The resulting product is very sour and sweet, slightly bitter, and leaves a dry feeling in the mouth after it's consumed.\n\nWhile [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) who don't live on Yar largely consider the jumping lime jelly an acquired taste, it is popular among [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) for its complex flavor profile. Formerly economically depressed towns on Yar have experienced positive growth in recent years thanks to exports to the [Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) or sales to passing [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron).","g":["jumping lime","yar fruit","fruit","food","cactus","yar","centauri ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/22d9d7cd-e55c-46e9-b8fd-52791912e822"},
{"id":"jupiter-sol-v","gp":"Vy2OMo22wz","t":"Jupiter (Sol V)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Jupiter (Sol V) is the fifth planet from the sun of the Sol system, [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). A gas giant, it is the largest and most massive planet in the system. During the [Human Colonial Expansion Era](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm), [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) constructed some of their earliest attempts at hydrogen fuel refineries around Jupiter. Those that failed were either abandoned or purposely knocked out of orbit so they would be captured by the planet's gravity and plummet into its stormy atmosphere.","g":["jupiter","sol v","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7a849d7f-78b8-42df-a013-efd9e14036b7"},
{"id":"justicestar-satellite","gp":"Rz28X3ApeM","t":"JusticeStar Satellite","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"The JusticeStar Satellite is a space station in the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv). Located at one of the Lagrange points of [Kellog VI's](gp:R6dAQZgGQe) orbit, it serves as the central processing center for new arrivals to the maximum security prison QuarterDeck. It also hosts a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) court to allow for swift trials and sentencing when bounty hunters directly deliver wanted criminals.","g":["space station","uee space station","kellog system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cc019066-d79f-4c27-bc27-760948bd542f"},
{"id":"jynx-gin","gp":"R6dLYlqL2j","t":"Jynx Gin","k":"culture","c":["Food and Beverages"],"x":"Jynx is a brand of gin that is distilled and bottled on [Delamar](gp:0GxoZnAGrg) in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). First brewed In SEY 2901, it resulted from an experimental batch of spirits brewed by the bartender Alta Turei, who was seeking a way to create a drink that used ingredients that could be grown on Delamar. Turei met with multiple failures before landing on a recipe that used [omphalotus mushrooms](gp:VgEwGP7Epe), lending the drink its pink coloration and slight glow.","g":["alcohol","gin","beverage"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a2b85017-9d61-4d73-a6ca-fa684a9126b2"},
{"id":"kyakuing-ailka-ii","gp":"0GxxrPE8oo","t":"K'ya.k'uing (Ail'ka II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"K'ya.k'uing (Ail'ka II) is a barren, terrestrial planet that is second from the sun of the [Ail'ka system](gp:01LLZmEygJ), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Although it is not habited and appears to be deserted, the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government forbids any spacecraft from landing on the planet's surface. Scans taken in the area have shown evidence of gunfire, suggesting that the Xi'an military might use K'ya.k'uing as a training ground or weapons testing area.","g":["k'ya.k'uing","ail'ka ii","ail'ka system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/85674753-7565-44da-a169-d857bbe64bc4"},
{"id":"kyuko-kaipua-iv","gp":"bZk18E457a","t":"K.yuk'o (Kai'pua IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"K.yuk'o (Kai'pua IV) is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Kai'pua system](gp:V3GBmlQoar), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9), and is a gas dwarf. Since its rocky core and diffuse atmosphere have nearly identical properties to those of neighboring planet [Kyu'kyu (Kai'pua III)](gp:RX35GE5vyk), some astronomers speculate that they may have originally formed in the same region before drifting away from each other. One hypothesis suggests that a rogue planet sliced through the system and pulled K.yuk'o out of its original orbit.","g":["k.yuk'o","kai'pua iv","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","kai'pua system","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"kyuyathan-thusuung-ii","gp":"RkGwyK65vz","t":"K.yuy'a'than (Th.us'ūng II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"K.yuy'a'than (Th.us'ūng II) is the second planet from the sun of the [Th.us'ūng system](gp:V8WeExnJge), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Blanketed in a thick, high-pressure atmosphere of sulfur-dioxide, K.yuy'a'than's surface is extremely dangerous, and the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government appears to have left the world alone. However, multiple [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) witnesses claim to have seen bright flashes just underneath the cloud layer. While none of their accounts have so far been confirmed, this mysterious activity has been a recurring subject on the spectrum show [Untold Tales](gp:bZkaoYnLEE).","g":["th.us'uung ii","th.us'uung system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet","k.yuya'than"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5d2879e5-c2d5-497f-a2bb-e0da8c3065e7"},
{"id":"kaua-hyoton-iv","gp":"0qa4Zow7pk","t":"Ka'ua (Hyoton IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Ka'ua (Hyoton IV) is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Hyoton system](gp:RkGDYnpq4L), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). The heart of the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government, it is the home of the [Emperor](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) and the Imperial [House](gp:box9JmxvWL)'s [Council of Three](gp:Rw1DPO8v8q), and is the nerve center of the [Civil Service](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ). Originally uninhabitable, it was the first world chosen to be [terraformed](gp:R6dWOrLEM4) by the Xi'an, partially due to its association with good luck and harmony in ancient Xi'an mythology. It played a vital role as a refuge for the Xi'an population when they were forced to flee their original homeworld [RyiXy'an (Hyoton III)](gp:bBz9mEDyqO) at the end of the [Great Divide](gp:VyvYA5qmqX).","g":["ka'ua","hyoton iv","hyoton system","habitable","habitable planet","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"kabal-cluster-alpha","gp":"VpMkLdZJDz","t":"Kabal Cluster Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Kabal cluster alpha is an asteroid cluster found in the [Kabal system](gp:V3GLNjMnra), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Rich in minerals, there is evidence that the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) mined ores and metals there, but stopped when they abandoned the system at some point before 2541. They left some of their equipment behind, giving archaeologists a glimpse of what Tevarin technology was like before the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546).","g":["asteroid cluster","kabal system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/446c6675-bf67-4bd3-a4f8-ddc7ec4ee8a6"},
{"id":"kabal-i","gp":"0rx3nGQLX9","t":"Kabal I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kabal I is a protoplanet in the [Kabal system](gp:V3GLNjMnra), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Thought to have formed alongside the system's terrestrial planets, it has a differentiated interior, suggesting that at some point in the past it may have been a dwarf planet. Craters on its surface suggest that it suffered impacts that destroyed its once-rounded shape.","g":["kabal system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9a8af37c-c6bf-4fcf-802c-51aa83608513"},
{"id":"kabal-ii","gp":"0n13MP3lMv","t":"Kabal II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kabal II is the second planet from the sun of the [Kabal system](gp:V3GLNjMnra), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A terrestrial desert world, its position in the system's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy) would make it an excellent candidate for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) if not for the ancient abandoned [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) cities on neighboring planet [Kabal III](gp:V8WrG5yroD). In order to protect the integrity of this archaeologically valuable site, colonization of all planets in Kabal is currently prohibited. [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA) has repeatedly petitioned the UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) to open up development of Kabal II under the argument that there are no ruins there to preserve.","g":["kabal system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a527f32e-2b50-44e8-bfdf-031f7b068b7c"},
{"id":"kabal-iii","gp":"V8WrG5yroD","t":"Kabal III","k":"place","c":["Planets","Tevarin"],"x":"Kabal III is the third and furthest planet from the sun of the [Kabal system](gp:V3GLNjMnra), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A naturally inhabitable world, it was colonized by the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) and then believed to have been abandoned en masse at some point before the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546). Archaeologists have yet to uncover the reason behind their departure due to the loss of most Tevarin records during the [Purge](gp:R6dWB877Nn) in the immediate aftermath of the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) (2603 - 2610). The cities found on Kabal III are the best-preserved examples of pre-[Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) contact Tevarin architecture and goods in the known universe.","g":["kabal system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/41735cee-1785-4e84-bc15-cb4ef03eeb8a"},
{"id":"kabal-system","gp":"V3GLNjMnra","t":"Kabal System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Kabal system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), composed of an F-type main sequence star, a protoplanet, two terrestrial planets, and an asteroid cluster. In SEY 2941, stellar surveyor Usuni Colo of the [Imperial Cartography Center](gp:VyvY7nE1k6) discovered a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) to the system from Leir. At first, it appeared that the system was empty, but [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) cities abandoned sometime before the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546) were found on [Kabal III](gp:V8WrG5yroD). Colonization of the system is prohibited to protect the integrity of this important archaeological site.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/eabb1e4b-d7c4-42fa-9640-4602fcc065af"},
{"id":"kaipua-system","gp":"V3GBmlQoar","t":"Kai'pua System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The Kai'pua system is a planetary system in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that consists of a K-type main sequence star, two terrestrial planets, and two gas dwarfs. One of the most important locations in the Xi'an Empire, it is the spiritual center of [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe), the central code of ethics and main religion for the Xi'an people. It was discovered at the end of the [First Imperial Age](gp:VDoPeW55W4) (MXY I.0 - I.14680 / SEY 19668 - 878 BCE), when the final [Ru'a](gp:V3qgaLK82W) Emperor [Se'ang](gp:RWo5gEXjnP) voluntarily renounced the throne and [House Xy.ō](gp:RXlXBrm5o1) ascended as the new Imperial House. When the second planet from the system's sun was found to have a planetary rotation period as long as 100 Modern Xi'an Years (MXY), it was declared significant to Li'tova, named R.aip'uāng, and terraformed into a planet-wide garden.","g":["xi'an system"]},
{"id":"kallis-belt-alpha","gp":"Var3eBNyzx","t":"Kallis Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Kallis belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv). Densely packed with planetesimals, asteroids, dust, and gasses, matter in the belt is constantly pulled out of orbit by the larger bodies forming on its outer edges. The unusually high amount of motion this activity creates poses a hazard for any ships passing through the area.","g":["asteroid belt","kallis system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/33a934ae-e134-48fc-8a59-f82e628cd449"},
{"id":"kallis-belt-beta","gp":"0Ql43A72jo","t":"Kallis Belt Beta","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Kallis belt beta is the second asteroid belt from the sun of the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv). Less dense than its sibling belt, it is primarily composed of dust grains and small asteroids that may be remnants from the formation of [Kallis IV](gp:Rvlm3oZqg8) and [Kallis V](gp:RkG1r6p4Lz).  In 2931, a group of art smugglers from [Bremen](gp:02kd45eyxe) attempted to conceal themselves in the dust of the beta belt before being apprehended by a [UEE Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) patrol ship.","g":["asteroid belt","kallis system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b27dcffd-35a0-402a-8819-9044e3808518"},
{"id":"kallis-i","gp":"0KxPzBrpZr","t":"Kallis I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kallis I is a protoplanet in the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv). A small mass of matter, it is believed that this protoplanet will eventually coalesce with nearby planetesimals and become a planet. Recent changes in its orbit have pushed it closer to its sun, leading to speculation that it may break apart if this migration continues.","g":["kallis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/26a40991-09df-4085-aaaa-18cb0af76e47"},
{"id":"kallis-ii","gp":"Rz2mZOo5zZ","t":"Kallis II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kallis II is a terrestrial planet in the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv). While it shares an orbit with [Kallis III](gp:Var3eB7jXd), it passes slightly closer to its sun during perihelion and has thus been designated as the system's second planet. As it pulls in material from the nearby asteroid belts, it may eventually become massive enough to subsume its sibling planet. It is currently somewhat smaller than Kallis III, but may grow much larger given enough time.","g":["kallis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ad616552-7e06-4609-8bb6-83d701d962c6"},
{"id":"kallis-iii","gp":"Var3eB7jXd","t":"Kallis III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kallis III is a terrestrial planet in the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv) that shares an orbit with another planet, [Kallis II](gp:Rz2mZOo5zZ). More massive than its sibling planet, it is also accruing matter at a higher rate, and is expected to continue increasing in size. Observing scientists believe that it may one day grow large enough to subsume Kallis II.","g":["kallis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3210547b-707b-45f0-b688-5add778ef9e6"},
{"id":"kallis-iv","gp":"Rvlm3oZqg8","t":"Kallis IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kallis IV is the fourth planet from the sun of the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv). Due to its position in the green band, current size, and robust volcanic activity, it seems to be evolving into an Earth-like planet. Survey teams on [OB Station Gryphon](gp:bmG15PAezQ) monitor Kallis IV around the clock and unpiloted drones are constantly collecting data. A great deal of valuable information has been discovered thanks to this long-term study. However, the planet is not expected to finish forming for many thousands of years.","g":["kallis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c7c9a4d2-08c6-44ca-8fd0-89b972fe1d7c"},
{"id":"kallis-ix","gp":"0rxDmN565a","t":"Kallis IX","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kallis IX is a dwarf planet in the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv), and is the ninth planet from its sun. Frigidly cold, its surface is marked with active cryovolcanoes that spew ice and water into the ammonia-rich atmosphere. The planet came to fame in the SEY 2943 Tonya Oriel story Lost Generation, where it appeared as the final resting place of a passenger from the missing long-haul colony ship [Artemis](gp:0jGxngnLzm). [OB Station Gryphon](gp:bmG15PAezQ) faced an influx of tourists wanting to visit the site, not knowing that the story was fictional.","g":["kallis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/10d2bf11-a112-46ad-9607-55faf24c0da4"},
{"id":"kallis-system","gp":"0Ql43d1nrv","t":"Kallis System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"Kallis is an unclaimed, developing planetary system in its accretion phase that consists of a G-type main sequence star, a protoplanet, five terrestrial planets, a gas giant, an ice giant, a dwarf planet, and two asteroid belts. Discovered in SEY 2921 by the staff of the OB Station *Chimera* in the [Oso](gp:bZkAMEarPd) system, it was placed under the protection of the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) despite a lack of sentient life in order to give scientists an opportunity to study a planetary system in its infancy. In 2935, over a hundred people fell victim to a scammer selling land deeds in the system under the misconception that the planets would take only a few more years to finish growing. It is estimated that the system's growth will not conclude for another million Standard Earth Years.","g":["developing system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/af2ec911-716a-40a3-b8ee-84b52c852ec7"},
{"id":"kallis-v","gp":"RkG1r6p4Lz","t":"Kallis V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kallis V is a terrestrial planet in the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv). The fifth planet from its sun, it lacks geological activity and appears to have reached the final stages of its formation. It is surrounded by a wide disk of planetesimals and dust that are likely to be remains from its earlier stages of growth. Two especially large objects growing in the disk may possibly be coalescing into moons.","g":["kallis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c2f2bf79-54e7-4737-bbe6-fffa600e9efb"},
{"id":"kallis-vi","gp":"0GxQvj9nGj","t":"Kallis VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kallis VI is a terrestrial planet in the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv), and is the sixth planet from its sun. Covered in an ocean of molten rock, it is still in an early stage of formation, and its crust is not expected to cool down enough to allow for the formation of continents for many millennia. The high amount of carbon present on the planet has led scientists to believe that when it finishes forming, it will be devoid of water.","g":["kallis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/35d85cad-cdbb-4d29-84af-057a1c9454c4"},
{"id":"kallis-vii","gp":"R5p8GZM9k9","t":"Kallis VII","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kallis VII is the seventh planet from the sun of the [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv). A young gas giant, it formed in the outer parts of the system during the star's stellar nebula phase, where it collected enough mass to attract huge amounts of hydrogen and helium gas over the relatively rapid period of about 200,000 years. It later migrated to its current position, possibly subsuming or displacing other objects in its path. In 2952, [United Empire of Earth Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) officials filed a request to open a refueling station over Kallis VII, citing the cost of importing fuel and the late stage of the planet's development.","g":["kallis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5993627e-067b-4a8a-b00e-18621aa65c38"},
{"id":"kallis-viii","gp":"V7dp8WND2L","t":"Kallis VIII","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kallis VIII is the seventh planet from the sun of the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv). An ice giant, it is composed of hydrogen, helium, and volatile icy compounds. In contrast to its neighboring planet [Kallis VII](gp:R5p8GZM9k9), which began its life in the outer reaches of the Kallis system, it most likely formed closer to its sun and later migrated outwards to its current location beyond the frost line. One leading hypothesis suggests that during Kallis VII's journey inward, it may have displaced Kallis VIII.","g":["kallis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/49176ad2-d280-4eff-a46f-0cb5145e3e26"},
{"id":"kampos-ellis-iv","gp":"RAXxrxr7M5","t":"Kampos (Ellis IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Kampos (Ellis IV) is the first settled and most populous planet in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Famous for a unique ecosystem adapted to high gravity, Kampos is a favorite subject for xenobiologists, paleontologists, and evolutionary biologists. Its most well-known animal and namesake is the [kamposi magnus](gp:0jGgXnAOOz), an extinct aquatic predator that once stalked the oceans. Animals found on Kampos tend to be stocky and muscular, and native edible plants undergo changes in flavor when grown in lower gravity conditions.","g":["kampos","ellis iv","ellis system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/091ec3f3-1f35-4936-9712-d9675f6badd3"},
{"id":"kamposi-magnus","gp":"0jGgXnAOOz","t":"Kamposi Magnus","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"###### KAMPOSI MAGNUS\nThe kamposi magnus was a tusked aquatic animal that inhabited [Kampos (Ellis IV)](gp:RAXxrxr7M5) until roughly 500,000 SEY ago. Kamposi was an omnivorous apex predator with a dense, solid, compact skeleton adapted for the high-gravity, high-pressure environment of Kampos' deep oceans. Though the exact cause of its extinction is unknown, it is hypothesized from fossil records that an underwater volcanic eruption may have triggered  an extinction event that disrupted the kamposi's food chain. The [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) of Ellis IV chose to name its planet Kampos after the kamposi magnus upon receiving recognition from the UEE Senate in 2562.\n\n###### DISCOVERY\nIn 2488, colonist Gary Yahontov of Ellis IV in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) discovered a large fossilized skull while dredging along the shore of his settlement. Yahontov used it as a piece of decoration in his yard for six years. Vira Kamposi, an academic passing through to study gravitational effects on local planet life, stole the fossil in 2493 and transported it via spacecraft to her former teachers at the University of Rhetor. Members of the paleontology department identified it as an undiscovered species and dispatched a research team to Ellis IV. A complete fossilized skeleton was discovered in 2496, 57 kilometers from Yahontov's home. Already nicknamed kamposi by the team, the researchers appended magnus to the name after the skeleton measured 11 meters long. The first herd of kamposi was discovered in 2543, challenging early conjecture that the kamposi was solitary.\n\nWhen she returned to Ellis IV in 2494, Kamposi was arrested and convicted of theft, after which she served six months in prison. Yahontov successfully sued the University of Rhetor in 2501 for repatriation of the skull. It sat in his yard until his death in 2536, upon which it was confiscated by the government of Ellis IV.\n\n###### DESCRIPTION\nReconstructions of the kamposi reveal that it could grow up to 12 meters in length and typically weighed about 40 tonnes. It had four eyes, two pairs of jointed mandibles around its mouth, and a pair of broad tusks on either side of its head. The teeth along the inside of its jaw and analysis of its bones indicate that it consumed both meat and vegetable matter. The mandibles likely facilitated quick consumption of prey, and the tusks probably aided in dredging up bottom-dwellers and uprooting plants from the ocean bed.\n\n###### EXTINCTION\nAbout 500,000 years ago, a supervolcano located near Kampos' equator erupted underwater, causing planetwide tsunamis, substantial seismic shifts, and mass extinctions. The kamposi vanished from the fossil record shortly after the eruption took place. Analysis of kamposi tusks from several thousand years prior to this event indicate that there were no long-term stressors that might have contributed to its demise\n\n###### CULTURAL SIGNIFICANCE\nThe kamposi is considered a symbol of Kampos. Mostly covered in ocean, Kampos is home to a wide spectrum of aquatic life. The kamposi was one of the first major discoveries to come out of Kampos in its colony days. Possibly because it received a moderate amount of fame in the popular media after the first academic publication on it nicknamed the kamposi \"lords of the deep,\" early inhabitants of Ellis IV embraced it as an emblem of their planet's oceans and unique biodiversity.\n\nIn 2945, a scale replica of the kampos skull first discovered by Gary Yahontov debuted in the Puglisi Collection. It remains the bestselling Puglisi item on Kampos.","g":["extinct animals","kampos","ellis iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/991ce2cf-60a3-42e6-92d5-e2a1f3e86ed6"},
{"id":"kastak-arms","gp":"VyvY7QMJ8X","t":"Kastak Arms","k":"company","c":["Weapons","Commerce","Human"],"x":"Kastak Arms is manufacturer of energy weapons  located in the United Empire of Earth (UEE). Founded in partnership with the government of Selene (Vega III) following the SEY 2737 [Vanduul invasion of Virgil](gp:box5moyeoZ), Kastak was intended as a means to build weapons to arm individuals for personal defense ahead of a potential Vanduul threat to Vega. Kastak's collection of weapons include the Coda Pistol, Devastator Shotgun, Karna Plasma Rifle, Roughneck LMG, Custodian SMG, Ravager-212 Twin Shotgun, Scalpel Sniper Rifle, Firestorm Microwave Cannon, and Equalizer HMG.","g":["selene","vega iii","fall of virgil","weapons manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5b9df648-52cc-424a-aaa0-ae3ab2806eb4"},
{"id":"kavische","gp":"bZkyPrB42d","t":"Kavische","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"# KAVISCHE\n\nThe kavische is a cactus hybrid that originated on [Yar (Centauri II)](gp:R6dd5pyOZ5) and is now found throughout the planet. After Yar was [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) in the mid-2800s, numerous plants and cacti were seeded onto the world. A few cycles later, a new hybrid that would come to be known as the kavische was discovered successfully growing across the Red Desert. Due to its rosy coloration and beautiful night-blooming flowers, the kavische is popular among succulent and cactus enthusiasts.\n\n# DISCOVERY\n\nIn the years before it was terraformed, Yar was a desert planet with a very thin hydrogen-oxygen atmosphere; enough to support some forms of life, but not enough to allow Humans to live on the surface without supplemental air. It remained a planet that only attracted botanical and entomological researchers until a vein of titanium was found in the Shunkai Mountains in 2839. Upon receiving this report, the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) authorized minimal terraformation of the world to help facilitate and encourage extraction of the planet's resources.\n\nMany plants that had originated on Earth (Sol III) were seeded on Yar as a part of the terraformation process. Cereus cacti were exceptionally suited to the planet, propagating themselves without [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) assistance as soon as the atmosphere was deemed breathable. However, instead of reproducing only within the cereus genus as expected, the cacti began to hybridize with local plants. Among these cactus seedlings was a new type of hybrid, dubbed \"kavische\" cactus after the plateau upon which it was discovered.\n\n# DESCRIPTION AND LIFE CYCLE\n\nThe kavische proved vigorous, even in the inhospitable Red Desert, an arid region so vast it is visible from planetary orbit. It took on the cylindrical appearance, towering height, and flowering cycle of its cereus parent, and the red coloration and thicker, sharper spines of its Yar parent, the hematic cactus. Over the long term, it outperformed both its ancestors, eventually coming to dominate the landscape.\n\nUpon reaching maturity, a kavische will put out a large flower that ranges in color from white to orange to red to purple, depending on the region in which it grows and the variety of plant. This heavily-scented flower blooms only for one night. Bats introduced from Earth and giant Yar moths pollinate the blossoms, which then close and transform into a water-rich fruit. Desert birds, rodents, and other animals consume the fallen fruit and spread the seeds over a wide area. The dropped seeds lay dormant until a rare rainfall occurs, at which point they sprout, establish roots, and begin to grow. Fully mature kavische can reach almost 2.5 meters in height.\n\n# IN POPULAR CULTURE\n\nThe people of Yar consider the kavische cactus a symbol of thriving in a harsh environment. Homesteads are sometimes heavily planted with the kavische, both as a deterrent to would-be trespassers and as a point of Yar pride. Prospectors planning to search the Red Desert for potential resources to mine are known to carry dried pieces of the kavische with them for good luck. Locals also have been known to create decorative jewelry or embellish their clothing with the spines.\n\nKavische cuttings are a common export from Yar to plant collectors. The cuttings take easily to standard cactus or succulent conditions and will root themselves in sandy soil with the application of very little water. Some dwarf varieties of kavische have been bred outside of Yar and have become popular house plants. Dwarf kavische that produce showier and more colorful flowers have recently appeared in plant markets thanks to the efforts of hobby growers. The low maintenance and durability of the plant have also made it popular among students.","g":["yar","centauri ii","cactus"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/749a1c38-0d5a-4479-b9e6-78146bde6388"},
{"id":"kedsu-reef","gp":"RvlZxvOMMN","t":"Kedsu Reef","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Banu"],"x":"The Kedsu Reef is a space station composed of derelict ships and abandoned military platforms located in the [Hadrian system](gp:RX3r6jlZok), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Founded in SEY 2881 by former [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) indenture Delilah Havers, the construction of Kedsu was inspired by [Banu-style flotilla](gp:0qnN5GrMAa) marketplaces. It is the main hub of commerce in the Hadrian system, and its markets stock goods from all over [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj), and Banu space.","g":["hadrian system","space station","banu flotilla"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/19a2902f-e550-4504-9229-fca9ef36322e"},
{"id":"keeger-belt-nyx-belt-beta","gp":"0NjwaLyKN2","t":"Keeger Belt (Nyx Belt Beta)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Keeger belt (Nyx belt beta) is the outermost asteroid belt in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). Asteroids in the Keeger belt are more thinly-distributed than those of the [Glaciem ring (Nyx belt alpha)](gp:0Kx8gwkXMP) and orbit the system's sun at a lesser velocity. The [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) believes that there may be criminal strongholds hidden within the belt, but, owing to the unclaimed status of the system, none have been officially confirmed.","g":["keeger belt","nyx belt beta","nyx system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c3318ba4-5016-4881-a814-9fa7fcc22c1c"},
{"id":"keene-kilian-vii","gp":"VgEEJGAma3","t":"Keene (Kilian VII)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Keene is a [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) terrestrial planet located seventh from the star of the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A civilian world, Keene is home to many offices and showrooms for spacecraft manufacturers, along with military-aligned corporations and independent businesses. A majority of the supplies needed by the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4)[base at MacArthur](gp:bBp6BmDMGJ) are manufactured on Keene. The population spiked after the [Battle of Orion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) forced [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to flee the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) and seek the protection of the military. A second wave of refugees occurred again after the [Fall of Virgil](gp:box5moyeoZ).","g":["keene","kilian vii","kilian system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/55c5e3c9-1568-49b6-bd31-77781b464198"},
{"id":"kellar-lench","gp":"V7d2g8xxva","t":"Kellar Lench","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Dr. Kellar Lench (2514 - 2573) was the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to locate the [Elysium system](gp:RvlQrKZxPO) and the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) civilization in 2541. A research scientist, his first job after obtaining his doctorate was with the New Horizons Research Institute, a subsidiary of the [Hathor Group](gp:R6v8Dg8o6a). After a solo assignment on [Yar (Centauri II)](gp:R6dd5pyOZ5) that lasted over 250 days, Lench abandoned his post, resigned from New Horizons, and visited [Fujin City](gp:RxNxAeyOq6) on [Saisei (Centauri III)](gp:Vy22NQJ1q6). On 15 November 2541, he discovered a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) in [Centauri](gp:0Qllvmr5v5) that led to a planetary system teeming with life. His decision to share his findings with the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) led to first contact with the Tevarin, which would trigger the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546). Lench went on to become a lecturer at the [Martian Institute of Space Technology (MIST)](gp:RL67MAJreO), where he taught physics until his death from complications related to alcoholism in 2573.","g":["elysium system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/962f4743-d7d7-44fc-b282-ed0b021e7122"},
{"id":"kellars-run","gp":"RxNxDYYJNd","t":"Kellar's Run","k":"history","c":["Illegal Activity","Human"],"x":"Kellar's Run is a 2931 intersystem spacecraft chase that started in the outlaw space station [Spider](gp:VaZwengjJv) in the Cathcart system when Dean Kellar shot and killed an undercover [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) agent during a disagreement over Anvil thrusters. Kellar battled his way out of Spider to his personal spacecraft, where he then led criminals, Advocacy agents, and armed civilians in a series of battles through five systems. The Run ended in the Nexus system, when civilian Anna Flynn killed Kellar during a firefight.","g":["dean kellar","uee advocacy","anna flynn","nexus system","spider","cathcart system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8a3d6c0e-aa46-4560-b6d5-8e8596029a09"},
{"id":"kellog-i","gp":"Rw19kPvGY7","t":"Kellog I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kellog I is a terrestrial planet in the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) protected [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv). The closest world to its sun, Kellog I's surface is mottled with oceans of lava. Its atmosphere is partially composed of vaporized rock, which forms clouds that rain quartz onto its molten surface. A day on Kellog I lasts nearly three times as long as its year.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","kellog system","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7f807844-11f6-4f5c-a606-76bdd444240d"},
{"id":"kellog-iii","gp":"RWo6dAAm7a","t":"Kellog III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kellog III is the third planet from the sun of the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv). With a high-pressure atmosphere of carbon dioxide and a runaway greenhouse effect, temperatures on Kellog III are hotter than those on neighboring planet [Xis (Kellog II)](gp:bmGJeMv2oK). In 2911, a spacecraft containing three escapees from the prison QuarterDeck, located on [Kellog VI](gp:R6dAQZgGQe), briefly hid in the planet's dense yellow clouds during a pursuit from law enforcement. The ship sustained corrosion damage to its hull over time, which eventually forced it to emerge and led to its capture.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","kellog system","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4320912a-9ef9-4688-a601-6b51eac93e88"},
{"id":"kellog-iv","gp":"V3GJZL666W","t":"Kellog IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kellog IV is a super-Earth in the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv), and is the fourth planet from its sun. Early surveys of the planet indicated that it possesses copious mineral resources, but its location near [Xis (Kellog II)](gp:bmGJeMv2oK) has led the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government to deny petitions to begin mining operations there. In 2950, a proposal to start a pilot mining program on Kellog IV that would utilize inmates of the nearby prison QuarterDeck as a potential labor force was presented to the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ). Despite garnering strong support among members of the [Universalist](gp:VDo6qOgLx9) party, it did not gain enough votes for final approval.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","kellog system","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a8e30e36-d9a0-40d4-bcaa-42af1e942d2c"},
{"id":"kellog-system","gp":"Vy28ZQeYZv","t":"Kellog System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Kellog system is a protected planetary system that consists of a G-type main sequence star, five terrestrial planets, and one gas dwarf. Discovered in SEY 2811 by navjumper [Patek Coen](gp:R9vPd4ZjK7), initial surveys revealed that [Kellog II](gp:bmGJeMv2oK) was home to a [sapient species](gp:RzPoqZXqZz), and the system was placed under the protection of the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP). After two jump points to [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) territory were discovered in 2815, the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) approved a plan submitted by Senator [Daniela Argen](gp:RvlxLvYKKv) of [Locke (Idris IV)](gp:RAX8yYv9jm) to establish a prison and an antimatter processing facility on [Kellog VI](gp:R6dAQZgGQe). Frequent visits from bounty hunters and haulers to the planet have made Kellog the most high-traffic system under the FCA.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b9ce64b0-0331-4ba7-acc1-ad87c8a24bea"},
{"id":"kellog-v","gp":"RvlxLZx82A","t":"Kellog V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kellog V is the fifth planet from the sun of the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) protected [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv). A gas dwarf, it has a rocky core and a thick, expansive hydrogen-helium atmosphere, but does not have enough mass to classify as a gas giant. Resources from the planet are sometimes harvested and used to supply the prison on neighboring planet [Kellog VI](gp:R6dAQZgGQe), but only under close supervision from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","kellog system","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3a2b2aee-d430-4687-bda8-a5c1f81c802b"},
{"id":"kelos-costigan","gp":"VJOzBxdJ28","t":"Kelos Costigan","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Kelos Costigan (2855 - present) was [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) from 2941 to 2950. He served as High-Secretary for two administrations and had a failed bid for Imperator in 2930 before being elected to office in 2940 as a member of the [Universalist](gp:VDo6qOgLx9) party. During his time in office, he was responsible for the passage of the [Human-Xi'an Trade Initiative (HuXa)](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) and the recognition of Aremis (Vega II). Prior to entering politics, he had a career in finance as a commodities trader.","g":["uee imperator","uee high-secretary"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1c3b9f37-36e9-497f-aeb1-c724bde7f8b4"},
{"id":"kesseli","gp":"Rz2Q3E9N5l","t":"Kesseli","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Kesseli is the capital city on [Lorona (Banshee III)](gp:bZkDByjyPO), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Dug deep enough into Lorona's surface that radiation suits aren't necessary, it is one of the largest underground cities in the UEE, and is where most of the miners who make the planet their home live. The city is still expanding as new tunnels are dug. Artificial lights on a day/night cycle, powered by a complex network of magnetic coils on Lorona's surface, are installed throughout the city. Bakers in Kesseli specialize in the beutrempe, a sweet or savory puff pastry that uses a local yeast strain to give it a unique and tangy taste.","g":["uee city","lorona","banshee iii","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0484f70c-32b3-4d49-bf18-4665646b55c6"},
{"id":"khartu-al-kaltuaal","gp":"0rqz5L28ad","t":"Khartu-Al (Kal'tuāl)","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Xi'an"],"x":"The Khartu-Al (Kal'tuāl) is a [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) light scout spacecraft adapted for [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) use by [Aopoa](gp:VyvY5jyZwp). Its base model, the [Qhire Khartu](gp:0ODXqrPXYZ) (Kuail Kal'tu), was originally developed for the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) as a scout and interceptor for the military. Aopoa extensively modified the control surfaces and components of the base model for the Human market. Owing to the fact that it was one of the first Xi'an-designed ships sold within the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) it is often referred to as the \"Xi'an Scout.\"","g":["aopoa","khartu-al","kal'tuāl","qhire khartu","kuail kal'tu","light fighter","fighter"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9fdb370f-0fca-42e6-983c-1dca9e1dc274"},
{"id":"kiami","gp":"RkG8lNDMW9","t":"Kiami","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"The kiami is a small, aerial animal indigenous to [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Found in all parts of the planet's atmosphere, the kiami feeds on aeroplankton and tiny pieces of organic matter floating on the wind. It forms an important part of the food chain as the main component of the [stormwal's](gp:RX34BjN2NK) diet. Nearly half of all kiami are consumed by predators each year. Female kiami give birth to thousands of young at a time, and can breed again days after carrying a brood to term.","g":["crusader","stanton ii","crustaceans"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4de86c66-fb3c-49f8-b5b6-1d8a850e3ad1"},
{"id":"kiel-belt-alpha","gp":"VgEvqv3D9N","t":"Kiel Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Kiel belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Located between [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN), and [Kiel IV](gp:V3GOdOLnkp), it was used as a training ground by the UEE military during the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793). Many of its asteroids bear scars from being used as target practice.","g":["asteroid belt","kiel system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5a1f3f96-ffc1-4c73-a920-d44f0ceb5617"},
{"id":"kiel-i","gp":"VJX9anQXLo","t":"Kiel I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kiel I is a small planet that is tidally locked to the sun of the [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Extreme heat and stellar radiation have made the side facing the star dangerously hot and dry, while the far side of the planet is coated in nitrogen and methane ice. Due to the influence of the star's gravity, the planet is slightly deformed, with a bulge at its equator. The perpetual twilight of the solar terminator is a popular subject for artists and a hotspot for off-road driving enthusiasts.","g":["kiel system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b34077e6-6854-47fa-8917-d2c41075199d"},
{"id":"kiel-ii","gp":"Vy2KNQYZkW","t":"Kiel II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kiel II is a terrestrial planet in the [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The second planet from the system's sun, it has a thin atmosphere of nitrogen and methane and is located outside the bounds green band, making it unsuitable for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). Scans of Kiel II have revealed that the planet is rich in resources. However, the UEE has strictly prohibited any mining operations, and will pursue and detain those who attempt to mine illegally. Locals believe that the planet houses a secret underground military installation, though no evidence to support this claim has been found.","g":["kiel system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/98fb68bf-14ae-43d7-aada-428e212aaa53"},
{"id":"kiel-iv","gp":"V3GOdOLnkp","t":"Kiel IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kiel IV is a planet in the [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A gas dwarf, it has a rocky core and a thick atmosphere of hydrogen, helium, and methane. The high concentration of methane gives it a striking deep blue color. In 2939, Senator Janna Thurville of [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN) wore a gown inspired by Kiel IV's coloration to the [Green Gala](gp:RX3Nr11PPk), created by designer Dyna Lei.","g":["kiel system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e4ae263e-67ed-4d0c-8dd6-6eba106c038e"},
{"id":"kiel-system","gp":"Var8kAJnaQ","t":"Kiel System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Kiel system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) with six planets, an asteroid belt, and an F-type main sequence star. Due to its jump point connection with the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) system Horus, it was used as a military hub until the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793). After tensions between the UEE and the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) cooled, the military largely withdrew and abandoned a great deal of infrastructure, especially on [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN). Governor Joona Tzur successfully offered these buildings to numerous aerospace companies in the early 2900s, and began an economic renaissance on Severus that earned the world [Senatorial](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) recognition in 2937. Kiel was voted one of the \"Top Ten Most Livable Systems\" by editors of [New United](gp:RAdjeJe5Y7) in 2946.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ab9ed5e9-93f4-4eb4-ab2f-92999d16e014"},
{"id":"kiel-v","gp":"bo1LdLee1w","t":"Kiel V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kiel V is a gas giant with prominent rings in the [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Known for its beauty, its hydrogen and helium atmosphere is banded with shades of white, orange, yellow, reddish-brown, and pale green. Starting in the early 2920s, it became a trend for local newly engaged couples to travel to Kiel V and be photographed with the planet and its expansive system of rings in the background.","g":["kiel system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a4e62567-442a-4005-b2a1-359029a5053e"},
{"id":"kiel-vi","gp":"RMNOzO4wJW","t":"Kiel VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kiel VI is a tiny protoplanet in the [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). During the formation of the system, it failed to accrete enough matter to become a planet but avoided getting subsumed into [Kiel V](gp:bo1LdLee1w). The farthest object from its sun, it completes its orbit roughly once every 122 SEY. A festival to celebrate its perihelion in 2956 is being planned on [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN).","g":["kiel system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c5537fa5-b7b5-40d0-957f-3d9f53d44776"},
{"id":"kilgroe-and-poole","gp":"02BQ45e4nB","t":"Kilgore and Poole","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Kilgore and Poole (K&P) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of personal armor systems. The company markets to high-end clientele who seek practical, stylish armor for everyday use instead of utilitarian military or industrial component armor made by most armor companies. K&P armor trades defensive power for increased flexibility, a design philosophy which has resulted in armor that allows for a wide range of movement.","g":["k&p","armor manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/793437de-37f7-4b33-9455-376645360b15"},
{"id":"kilian-system","gp":"0ODD4mY9aP","t":"Kilian System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Kilian system is the largest planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Discovered in SEY 2463, it was a key stepping stone in [Humanity's](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) early push outward from the Sol system. Four of its fourteen planets are populated. Kilian became the main headquarters for the UEE military in 2631. [MacArthur (Kilian V)](gp:Rz22dGBlnz) is the base of operations for the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), while [Corin (Kilian IX)](gp:V8WWyl5zGo) is the home base of the [UEE Marines](gp:V7d5ZYEr1a). [Keene (Kilian VII)](gp:VgEEJGAma3) is the system's only populated world with [Senatorial](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) representation.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2f38eae9-f28c-4e10-8517-6ebaf5e05750"},
{"id":"kilian-viii","gp":"RPDDadwZQg","t":"Kilian VIII","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kilian VIII is a smog planet in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that appears to be covered in a tropical ocean made of water. However, the liquid of the planet is a mix of hot, high-density, and volatile fluids. Due to the high-pressure atmosphere and the danger the ocean presents, it is extremely dangerous to attempt a landing on Kilian VIII.","g":["kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1254f88e-74b1-4cb5-a0d1-b11d80707cc1"},
{"id":"kilian-x","gp":"0dXXnzq1mO","t":"Kilian X","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kilian X is a dwarf planet in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Tiny and frigid, nitrogen and methane ice coats the planet's surface, peppered with craters and cracks. Since SEY 2941, mineral rights to Kilian X have been tied up in UEE courts, so no industries have established themselves there to tap into the planet's rich resources.","g":["kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8df74e8e-4691-415c-a21f-0b894317ebfc"},
{"id":"kilian-xi","gp":"0n1167QXrn","t":"Kilian XI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kilian XI is a blue-green gas giant in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Designated as a fuel supply world by the UEE military, it is surrounded by automated harvesting platforms that gather resources from the planet for refinement. Dark storm spots appear and disappear in the atmosphere every few years, making the Kilian XI seem as if it has been bruised.","g":["kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ac95c1c7-2ef7-4732-bf19-e44846927cbc"},
{"id":"kilian-xii","gp":"RAXX7q88Ny","t":"Kilian XII","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kilian XII is a terrestrial planet covered in a thick layer of methane and water ice, located in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Although there is evidence that the planet was once geologically active, all tectonic activity ceased roughly 2.5 billion years ago. The ice located over Kilian XII's northern and southern poles is pinkish in color.","g":["kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3fd608a8-982b-4ab2-9cc4-62a4b958321f"},
{"id":"kilian-xiii","gp":"0GxxrGQoea","t":"Kilian XIII","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kilian XIII is a dwarf planet in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It is enveloped by a tenuous atmosphere of nitrogen and carbon monoxide. Uniquely among planets, it is notable for the enormous deposits of smoky quartz that jut out of its surface, giving it a glittering, otherworldly look.","g":["kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/56fc70ab-b5ac-4c68-a7c1-c10fbc7d19d7"},
{"id":"kilian-xiv","gp":"Rw11AprZJN","t":"Kilian XIV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kilian XIV is a protoplanet that orbits furthest from the sun of the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Because it is a small, frozen, irregularly-shaped rock without an atmosphere, some astronomers have argued that Kilian XIV should not be counted as a planet, and should be reclassified and stripped of its designation.","g":["kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1e0e12b5-5379-4d43-b6dd-e5369bea7911"},
{"id":"kins-belt-alpha","gp":"R4jEA6W4Kw","t":"Kins Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Kins belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the [Kins system](gp:bmGynZ68oP), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Located between the inhospitable planets [Kins IV](gp:bEzvwkmEB2) and [Kins V](gp:0ODqEMK7eZ), it is home to multiple rest stops operated by interconnected webs of [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) that attend to the various needs of visitors. Some Indenture Soulis do business here, and have been known to entrap travelers into signing documents without reading the fine print and selling themselves into indentured service.","g":["asteroid belt","kins system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e32dfe4b-3a03-462d-be71-e31a0cf422bf"},
{"id":"kins-belt-beta","gp":"bBza8oBW15","t":"Kins Belt Beta","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Kins belt beta is the second asteroid belt in the [Kins system](gp:bmGynZ68oP), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). The outermost point in the system, it has traditionally been used as a convenient location to dump unfixable equipment and other types of large waste by spacecraft passing in and out of nearby jump points. It is frequented by Salvage [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) who make a living off processing this waste.","g":["asteroid belt","kins system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1d645e4e-178a-4eaf-a3df-3213da2e4917"},
{"id":"kins-i","gp":"VDzaJLNzGq","t":"Kins I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kins I is the first planet from the sun of the [Kins system](gp:bmGynZ68oP), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A mesoplanet with an iron-rich crust, it has been extensively mined and bears the scars of ancient strip-mining operations. Visitors to the planet have been known to utilize its myriad abandoned mining structures as temporary shelter during the day, when the nearby sun causes dangerously high temperatures.","g":["kins system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e4468bc9-2706-4f01-a55d-77c018a417c2"},
{"id":"kins-ii","gp":"bZk4E6Xn9B","t":"Kins II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kins II is the second planet from the sun of the [Kins system](gp:bmGynZ68oP), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A world with a natural oxygen-nitrogen atmosphere, it is the home of the largest indentured servant market in the Protectorate. Its large cities have historically enjoyed a low crime rate, but as Human visitors have increased, so has the frequency of criminal activity. Outside the cities, there are ruins that don't match any known style of [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) architecture. [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) archaeologists debate whether this is an example of ancient Banu design or evidence of a lost civilization.","g":["kins system","banu planet","habitable","habitable planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3f3c0ca2-6979-40d8-903a-e51e9ac2470d"},
{"id":"kins-iii","gp":"V8WELv1DkX","t":"Kins III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kins III is the third planet from the sun of the [Kins system](gp:bmGynZ68oP), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A massive super-Earth, it has oceans of mixed water and ammonia and an atmosphere composed of nitrogen, oxygen, ammonia, and carbon dioxide. While [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) can breathe the air comfortably, [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj), and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) cannot. A handful of Mining [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) operate on the planet's surface, although most of the planet's most valuable resources have already been extracted.","g":["kins system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a0dbfab8-2117-40b4-bd15-bb9e11c3f573"},
{"id":"kins-iv","gp":"bEzvwkmEB2","t":"Kins IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kins IV is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Kins system](gp:bmGynZ68oP), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Under its dense atmosphere, its surface is coated in solid ice in spite of high temperatures. Atmospheric pressure forces the planet's water to remain solid, creating exotic forms of ice that differ in structure from ice formed under normal circumstances. Surface conditions make it too dangerous for a spacecraft to land there without specialized equipment.","g":["kins system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/57ab6f46-a7c4-4d9e-9ae4-ef8c1071c4a1"},
{"id":"kins-system","gp":"bmGynZ68oP","t":"Kins System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Banu"],"x":"The Kins system is a planetary system in the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) that is made up of a K-type main sequence star, a mesoplanet, a terrestrial rocky planet, two super-Earths, a gas giant, and two asteroid belts. Best known as the location of the Protectorate's main indentured servitude market, it is de facto governed by the Indenture [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) that operate within it. [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) governments issue annual travel warnings that detail how to avoid selling oneself into indenture without informed consent.","g":["banu protectorate"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/eb748a8b-e8ad-4b5e-b7ee-c0659b9e19a5"},
{"id":"kins-v","gp":"0ODqEMK7eZ","t":"Kins V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kins V is the fifth planet from the sun of the [Kins system](gp:bmGynZ68oP), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Pale yellow with some very light red and green banding, its color is due to the presence of ammonia crystals in its upper atmosphere. Although the planet is hundreds of times more massive than Earth (Sol III) it is less dense than water.","g":["kins system","banu planet","not habitable","uninhabitable planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e37989c7-8cd7-499c-af6b-4b1cb2bf2610"},
{"id":"klaus-and-werner","gp":"R6v8Op8ren","t":"Klaus & Werner","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Klaus & Werner (K&W) is a manufacturer of personal and spacecraft-based energy weaponry. The company was founded in SEY 2893 by a former [Behring](gp:0n9vZ4GpQn) designer who believed his talents were not being appreciated and decided to strike out on his own. The company's line of weaponry includes the Bulldog, Badger, Panther, Rhino, Galdereen, and Mammoth repeaters as well as personal weapons like the Demeco Energy LMG, Arrowhead Sniper Rifle, Gallant Energy Rifle, and Arclight II pistol, which was prominently featured on the spectrum show *The Frontier*.","g":["k&w","klaus and werner","weapons manufacturer","earth","sol iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4b449322-b587-4e4a-b23c-b4d553edfdf0"},
{"id":"knightbridge-arms","gp":"RAdjBxowEv","t":"KnightBridge Arms","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"KnightBridge Arms is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of spacecraft ballistic weapons. The company markets their weapons as stylish alternatives to energy weapons; in practice, they are typically inexpensive and mass-produced designs with a focus on appearance over reliability. [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) and [Kruger Intergalactic](gp:0Gz5BWEOEg) mount stock models of the Aurora and P-52 Merlin with KnightBridge Arms Sword-series cannons.","g":["weapons manufacturer","severus","kiel iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d1a3c30e-be8e-4bb3-ab72-2b085278bc55"},
{"id":"koli-eealuth-iii","gp":"Vy29gQ3x4Y","t":"Ko'li (Ē'aluth III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Ko'li (Ē'aluth III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Ē'aluth system](gp:Rw1xW1lzxN), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Soon after it was discovered, the Xi'an government elected to terraform Ko'li and use it as a nature preserve for all known plant and animal species in Xi'an space. It contains a diverse number of biospheres that were meticulously-crafted to suit the needs of all species housed on the planet. \n\nPoaching is restricted, and those caught in the act are subject to heavy punishment. Additionally, the unauthorized import of living species is prohibited to prevent disruption to the ecosystem. In SEY 2933, an outbreak of [flo-pets](gp:V8gJOo3ZGO) caused by a visiting [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) led to increased penalties for anyone caught trying to release an animal or plant vegetation.","g":["ko'li","ē'aluth iii","ē'aluth system","habitable","habitable planet","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ba813129-c90c-4423-83d5-9566aad98e96"},
{"id":"koa-e-koia","gp":"RkGpX3LJJz","t":"Koa e Ko'ia","k":"history","c":["Sports","Xi'an"],"x":"The Koa e Ko'ia is a spacecraft race that combines marathon flights with physical endurance. Held every [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) year (MXY) in alternating locations around the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9), it was first competed in MXY III.690 (SEY 2341) in the [Hyoton system](gp:RkGDYnpq4L). Before each race, the Koa e Ko'ia governing body chooses checkpoints and destinations that are not revealed until the race begins. There is always a mixture of locations in space and in atmosphere. \n\nOnce the race is underway, pilots receive the coordinates of their first checkpoint, and do not learn their second checkpoint until reaching the first, or their third checkpoint until they reach the second, and so on. Pilots must coordinate with their pit crews about when and where they will rest, repair, and refuel, and must choose strategic periods in which to lower their metabolism and extend their flying time without reaching a state of exhaustion. This continues until only one racer is left, which can vary anywhere between 200 and 50 Standard Earth Hours. The pilot who has reached the most checkpoints is declared the winner. Non-Xi'an people were allowed to participate for the first time in SEY 2947.","g":["spacecraft racing","xi'an sports"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dda0ff73-1638-4ff1-b73d-17ad999a0995"},
{"id":"kofi-bafeuma","gp":"bE3rL1DkwW","t":"Kofi Baféuma (Cothi Bat-Thel-Ma)","k":"people","c":["People","Exploration","Banu"],"x":"Kofi Baféuma (Cothi Bat-Thel-Ma) is a [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) explorer, most notable for discovering the [Tamsa system](gp:VYLAnPnYBx) in SEY 2943. They sold the location of the system to the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) on the condition that they be allowed to retain its naming rights. Once the UEE agreed, they named it after the Human visual artist [Tamsa Wheel](gp:RXlXOw9WaN) in an attempt to arrange a meeting with her. They achieved this goal in 2945.","g":["kofi baféuma","cothi bat-thel-ma ","tamsa system","navjumper","banu people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f7421772-0fe3-4260-b23c-056f9e741652"},
{"id":"kopion","gp":"RX39z9OyeP","t":"Kopion","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"The kopion is a fast, carnivorous animal that has become invasive in multiple systems. Indigenous to [Ashana (Nul V)](gp:bZkd47KMB6), it evolved to survive harsh environments spanning across differing biomes. On average, it reproduces twice per Standard Earth Year (SEY), and typically gives birth to between 5 and 10 young. Most of the pups born on Ashana die due to predation, starvation, or exposure. On other, less deadly worlds where it is introduced by those who hope to harvest its horn, the majority of the pups reach adulthood.","g":["canid","ashana","nul v"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a6122ce1-d903-427e-8f52-8a3917ea4f66"},
{"id":"krthak","gp":"RxNxDYkqzz","t":"Kr'thak","k":"species","c":["Civilizations"],"x":"The Kr'thak are a spacefaring civilization indigenous to an unknown area of space. Little is known about them, other than their involvement in a period of turmoil in [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) history called the Spirit Wars. The Xi'an have strict laws in place preventing the populace from interacting with the Kr'thak and have refused to fulfill information requests from the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) government. \n\nWhile some explorers have made attempts to locate [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) into Kr'thak territory, none have so far been found. In SEY 2943, the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) discussed establishing contact with the Kr'thak, but ultimately decided against potentially jeopardizing diplomatic relations with the Xi'an.","g":["spirit wars","extant civilizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d51b3cfb-5546-47ba-a8a0-a0740d8f4c2b"},
{"id":"kraken","gp":"0n11yZd6k9","t":"Kraken","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Kraken is a light carrier manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed) that debuted in SEY 2948. Intended to be a mobile base of operations for a crew of up to ten, the Kraken has six landing pads equipped with repair and refueling stations for smaller spacecraft, as well as a vehicle bay and hangar. The standard model features a comprehensive array of turrets and guns that can be used to defend the ship if attacked. \n\nA variant of the Kraken, the Privateer, was developed in conjunction with [Cousin Crow's Custom Crafts](gp:R5ppgyMJpY) and converts the interior space into a private marketplace, so traveling merchants can operate their own shops without having to pay rental fees for temporary stalls on other worlds.","g":["light carrier","capital ship","drake interplanetary","human spacecraft","carrier"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/13f3ba85-31fd-4e47-b5f7-d1496168fb4d"},
{"id":"kroneg","gp":"V8gJ62kzrx","t":"Kroneg","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Kroneg is a manufacturer of energy weapons for spacecraft. They design their products to appear as intimidating weapons of destruction, but critics claim that the performance fails to live up to that promise. Kroneg's weapons are popular among consumers despite poor ratings from *Whitley's Guide* thanks to their low price. Product lines include the Kroneg FL series led by with their flagship FL-33 Laser Cannon.","g":["weapons manufacturer","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1e2e595b-3090-43a4-ae84-4a50c6dde691"},
{"id":"kruger-intergalactic","gp":"0Gz5BWEOEg","t":"Kruger Intergalactic","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Kruger Intergalactic is a spacecraft, weapons, and spacecraft component manufacturer first founded on [Borea (Magnus II)](gp:R9vGaQPXJN). They started in SEY 2558 as a custom spacecraft and weapons component maker, providing parts to such clients as [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) and [Behring](gp:0n9vZ4GpQn). Operations expanded to weapons manufacture as the company grew. Kruger debuted their first spacecraft after partnering with Roberts Space Industries to provide a small, short-range vessel to be packaged with their [Constellation](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/constellation-series) line of spacecraft. They are headquartered on [Cascom (Castra II)](gp:0dXKkL9a9o).","g":["spacecraft manufacturer","spacecraft component manufacturer","weapon component manufacturer","weapons manufacturer","cascom","castra ii","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/91294640-3a67-4fd5-a0f6-f4c974696e02"},
{"id":"kreel-system","gp":"Rxn25ByeAQ","t":"Krēl System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Krēl system is a planetary system that reportedly consists of one star of unknown type and nine planets. Located along the border of the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9), it is the home system of the [Kr'thak](gp:RxNxDYkqzz) and is thought to be the center of their civilization. Because the Kr'thak have yet to establish first contact with the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE), it has yet to be visited by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) or [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) and there is little information available on its history or composition. There is no evidence that it has been visited by the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4), although it is possible that they did so before [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) and UEE historians began documenting their history. Any existing data on the Krēl system is kept classified by the Xi'an government, and has not been released despite repeated diplomatic requests.","g":["kr'thak system","kr'thak territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b7e3ca14-9bd0-4995-9475-0c7f8c01ac49"},
{"id":"kuail-kaltu-qhire-khartu","gp":"0ODXqrPXYZ","t":"Kuail Kal'tu (Qhire Khartu)","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military"],"x":"The Kuail Kal'tu (Qhire Khartu) is a light fighter manufactured by [Aopoa](gp:VyvY5jyZwp) for the exclusive use of the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military. Fast and agile, the Kal'tu has a complex array of thrusters that boost its maneuverability, allowing it to make sudden turns and dodge incoming attacks. After the dissolution of the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) and the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ), ships resembling the Kal'tu were spotted along the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) border. The UEE military was unable to capture a vessel for study until SEY 2896, when a derelict, pilotless Kal'tu was located and salvaged by a [Naval](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) recon squad. After the signing of the [Human-Xi'an Trade Initiative](gp:01LvKoLvZ8) (HuXa) in SEY 2947, Aopoa debuted the [Kal'tuāl](gp:0rqz5L28ad) (Khartu-al) light fighter in the UEE market, a variant of the Kal'tu adapted for Human use.","g":["kuail kal'tu","qhire khartu","fighter","light fighter","aopoa","xi'an spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0c29b324-ba7c-4755-9e8f-eae8250d8cfd"},
{"id":"kuiper-belt-sol-belt-beta","gp":"0KxZ3KwZvY","t":"Kuiper Belt (Sol Belt Beta)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Kuiper belt (Sol belt beta) is the second asteroid belt from the sun of the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). A circumstellar disc that stretches far beyond the orbit of Neptune (Sol VIII), it consists of a mixture of rocky, icy, and metallic asteroids that are theorized to be leftover material from the time of the system's formation.","g":["kuiper belt","sol belt alpha","asteroid belt","sol system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e3986b55-59c6-4642-ac7e-646769d1c087"},
{"id":"kuaali-yaamon-i","gp":"VgE4oDJLWY","t":"Kuā'li (Yā'mon I)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Kuā'li (Yā'mon I) is the first planet from the sun of the [Yā'mon system](gp:VarxDJ5yLo), [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Tidally locked to its star, one of its sides is in permanent daylight, and the other in permanent night. \n\nDuring the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ), [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) military intelligence identified a facility located on the dark side of Kuā'li that saw frequent traffic and was under heavy guard. Reports suggested that it was a maximum security labor camp. In SEY 2788, the facility was suddenly torn down and the planet left unguarded. The [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) Empire denies that they operated a labor camp on Kuā'li, but have not offered an alternate explanation of its purpose.","g":["kuaa'li","yaa'mon i","yaa'mon system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d9ae0f48-b8e0-40e3-a262-e3cd095c76b7"},
{"id":"kyle-polo","gp":"0dXZQNQMmp","t":"Kyle Polo","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Kyle Polo (SEY 2883 - present) served as [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) of [Angeli (Croshaw II)](gp:0QlxqwG14Q) from SEY 2935 to 2945. During his time in office, he voted for legislation that decreased government spending and lowered taxes for big and small businesses on Angeli. \n\nHis largest piece of legislation, the Polo Initiative, was aimed at curtailing the military budget by placing it under Senate review. Though it initially gathered support, the legislation was voted down on the 4 November 2945 ballot following a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)[attack on the Vega system](gp:0Gz5mkprmg). Polo, up for election on that same ballot, was voted out of office.","g":["uee senator","universalist party","angeli","croshaw ii","human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/42e854f9-ec1a-41b4-b908-4b0b6e147001"},
{"id":"kyukyu-kaipua-iii","gp":"RX35GE5vyk","t":"Kyu'kyu (Kai'pua III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Kyu'kyu (Kai'pua III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Kai'pua system](gp:V3GBmlQoar), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A gas dwarf, it has a thick but low-density hydrogen and helium atmosphere that surrounds a rocky core. There is an ocean of liquid water under the clouds, leading researchers to speculate that the planet could possibly be terraformed. \n\nHouse [Kr.ē's](gp:R6v8OZOrP5) [Council of Three](gp:Rw1DPO8v8q) debated setting up a small platform-based colony in Kyu'kyu's upper atmosphere, but [Emperor Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo) ultimately dismissed the idea to keep traffic from increasing in the system and affecting [R.aip'uāng's](gp:Rw1rnY1AYJ) tranquility.","g":["kyu'kyu","kai'pua iv","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","kai'pua system","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b0ff9181-eb29-4380-9007-a9c67d46af39"},
{"id":"kyonao-taal-vii","gp":"RvlaGZL1B8","t":"Kyu'nao (T.āl VII)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kyu'nao (T.āl VII) is the outermost planet from the sun of the [T.āl system](gp:R4j2mdjZE5), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A gas giant, it has four thick bands of yellow, violet, green, and orange clouds that flow across its prismatic atmosphere. Kyu'nao's appearance informed the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government's decision to give each of the inhabited planets in T.āl a specific color to incorporate into its architecture.","g":["kyu'nao","t.āl vii","t.āl system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"kyuaam-lauo-iii","gp":"RX35G91XA1","t":"Kyu'ām (La'uo III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Kyu'ām (La'uo III) is the third planet from the sun of the [La'uo system](gp:R6demJ8Xmq), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A smog planet, it is enveloped in layers of carbon dioxide, nitrogen, and sulfur dioxide. In the distant past, its surface was too dangerous to land a ship on due to the high-pressure atmosphere. Since the red giant in La'uo's center expanded and began to heat up the system, Kyu'ām's atmosphere has thinned and expanded, giving it the appearance of a miniature hot Jupiter.","g":["kyu'ām","la'uo iii","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","la'uo system","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/91b451b8-7384-4254-a22d-a44602752258"},
{"id":"kyukya-belt-alpha","gp":"0qaJ8W5wZ1","t":"Kyuk'ya Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Kyuk'ya belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the [Kyuk'ya system](gp:RWo69Xx3dP), [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Some of the larger asteroids are occupied by members of the nyayu'a, the professional class of criminals who operate with the conditional approval and oversight of the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government. People conducting inter-civilization business at the trade hub [Pyen'pui.a](gp:RL68MWxZOL) on [Pue'nu (Kyuk'ya 1a)](gp:0jGJZokndn) sometimes hire information dealers, bodyguards, mercenaries, loan collectors, or other nyayu'a who operate from the Kyuk'ya belt alpha when the need arises.","g":["asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/801b0f9a-3515-4678-8de1-143a88fb3e52"},
{"id":"kyukya-i","gp":"bBzPqGr64O","t":"Kyuk'ya I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kyuk'ya I is a gas giant in the [Kyuk'ya system](gp:RWo69Xx3dP), [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9), and is the closest planet to its suns. Orbited by a far-reaching set of rings composed of rock and ice, the sight of the binary stars at the center of Kyuk'ya against the dramatic backdrop of these rings has been a recurring subject in [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) poetry since it was first discovered in MXY III.826 (SEY 2515). The Xi'an government requires that any new space stations built in support of intersystem trade must be placed in orbital positions that will not mar the natural beauty of the rings.","g":["kyuk'ya system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/35d54052-9329-4b1b-9895-bd67a95d9451"},
{"id":"kyukya-ii","gp":"bEzyWM8PQX","t":"Kyuk'ya II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kyuk'ya II is the second planet from the suns of the [Kyuk'ya system](gp:RWo69Xx3dP), [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Due to its acutely tilted axis, it experiences extreme variation in its seasons. For nearly a quarter of each year, the suns shine directly over one of the poles, plunging the rest of the planet into a lengthy and dark winter. When the suns reappear in the sky during the spring, they generate powerful heat and storms that cause catastrophic floods and lay waste to the landscape.","g":["kyuk'ya system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/66a6bfa7-3911-416d-ba7a-be082379af8a"},
{"id":"kyukya-system","gp":"RWo69Xx3dP","t":"Kyuk'ya System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The Kyuk'ya system, also called the Indra system, is a planetary system in the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that consists of an A-type main sequence star, a white dwarf, a gas giant, a terrestrial planet, and an asteroid belt. Discovered in MXY III.826 (SEY 2515) when a Xi'an military convoy picked up an anomalous signature during a routine mining escort operation in the [Yā'mon system](gp:VarxDJ5yLo), it was incorporated into the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) and SEY 2548 when the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) became aware of the Kyuk'ya-Yā'mon jump point. The UEE gave it the military designation Indra after an ancient Human god of war. Following the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793), the UEE updated their charts to reflect the system's original Xi'an name. Kyuk'ya was made into a center of trade between the Xi'an Empire, the UEE, and the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). The largest settlement in the system, located on the moon [Pue'nu (Kyuk'ya 1a)](gp:0jGJZokndn), is a center of Xi'an youth culture.","g":["xi'an system","perry line"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3584ed4f-570a-48cd-b50b-3b19607fb56e"},
{"id":"kyupuaang-eealuth-ii","gp":"02k2J5n1nY","t":"Kyupuaang (Ē'aluth II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Kyupuaang (Ē'aluth II) is the second planet from the sun of the [Ē'aluth system](gp:Rw1xW1lzxN), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A smog planet, it has the densest atmosphere of all rocky bodies in Ē'aluth, which creates levels of surface pressure that are highly dangerous for landing spacecraft. It lacks a magnetic field and instead has an induced magnetosphere, which is carried from its sun by stellar wind. Increased cosmic radiation leads to increased electrical storm activity and an ongoing loss of hydrogen and oxygen ions.","g":["kyupuaang","ē'aluth ii","ē'aluth system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"koorilya","gp":"VlMDKMPqkr","t":"Kōri'lya","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Xi'an"],"x":"Kōri'lya is a major city on [Xi (R.il'a V)](gp:RkGDJnlB2p), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Originally filled with barracks for soldiers and support staff that worked and trained on neighboring planet [Xōl'uu (R.il'a IV)](gp:VYLzwxDrre), the city was reclassified as a residential zone by the Xi'an government after the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793 / MXY III.838 - III.1044). It was additionally opened to non-[Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj), and has become a center of cultural exchange where [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4), [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) intermingle with the Xi'an populace. Surrounded by dense tropical rainforests, it is lushly vegetated and stays warm throughout the year.","g":["xi","r.il'a v","xi'an city","cities"]},
{"id":"lauo-system","gp":"R6demJ8Xmq","t":"La'uo System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The La'uo system (Hui sen La'uo) is a planetary system in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that consists of a red giant, three terrestrial planets, two asteroid belts, and a gas giant. In MXY III.1017 (SEY 2759), a group of Xi'an outlaws discovered a jump point from the Ē'aluth system into La'uo and made it into their base of operations. Although the Xi'an government learned of the system's existence soon afterwards, they declined to claim it due to its lack of [terraformable](gp:R6dWOrLEM4) planets. It became a part of the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) in MXY III.1026 (SEY 2771) when the UEE military detected a jump point from the [Tohil system](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9) system to La'uo, forcing the outlaws that lived there to flee as military ships from both sides of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793 / MXY III.838 - III.1044) flooded in and took their place. In MXY III.1040 (SEY 2789), [Emperor T.uēng se Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo) traveled through La'uo on his way to the Tohil system, where he and Senator [Terrence Akari](gp:RL6ZQLwnko) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) negotiated the terms of what would become known as the [Akari-Kr.ē](gp:bE3rKrl5z6) treaty. The same pirate gangs who once lived in La'uo played a key role in ensuring that Kr.ē could pass through the system and into Tohil undetected. In return, Kr.ē recognized these pirate gangs as [nyayu'a](gp:bZkaBD5alD) and granted them dominion over the La'uo system with the exception of the planet [Yengchuai (La'uo II)](gp:R6demaZlkD).","g":["xi'an system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4f6b029b-d72d-421e-acc4-aa654caaad8b"},
{"id":"lago-nexus-iv","gp":"0dXE5egx98","t":"Lago (Nexus IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Lago (Nexus IV) is a [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) planet in the [Nexus system](gp:RWoj8pnGma), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Formerly host to the largest concentration of outlaws in the system, it is now the center of a resettlement campaign run by the UEE government to establish lasting order. Most of the new population centers are fortified against attacks from the gangs that have not yet been forced out of Nexus.","g":["lago","nexus iv","nexus system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d8d0b85e-a362-4457-ab37-9fad26e53261"},
{"id":"lanes","gp":"0OaB2lkq2A","t":"Lanes","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"Lanes, or space lanes, are the common transit paths for spacecraft within solar systems. They are most commonly used by commercial spacecraft carrying freight or passengers, along with military and other ships. With few exceptions, lanes are typically the shortest path between two points that can be safely navigated. Lanes are considered the safest areas for in-system travel because their more highly trafficked nature and higher rate of security patrol dissuades all but the boldest pirates.","g":["navigation"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/78ce5286-c7fe-4684-90c3-f57705acb19e"},
{"id":"lanisto-tyrol-1a","gp":"R4jwKdNQPJ","t":"Lanisto (Tyrol 1a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Lanisto (Tyrol 1a) is the moon of [Tyrol I](gp:0GxQnP34YP), the closest planet to the two stars of the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N). There is evidence that many years in the past, Lanisto was very geologically active. Empty lava caverns provide temporary shelter to those who want to escape the heat of the nearby suns. The moon's largest settlement, [Front Row](gp:VgEWp1Ox2N), is partially situated within the remains of an ancient, extinct volcano.","g":["lanisto","tyrol 1a","tyrol system","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","unclaimed moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4811e456-3e98-4dc6-8608-677a3fafadd4"},
{"id":"laventi","gp":"0qa398DwqO","t":"LaVenti","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"LaVenti is a luxury fashion brand known for its avant-garde looks. A common sight on the red carpet, the company specializes in haute couture clothing and footwear that is characterized by the use of unusual cuts and 3d elements in its designs. It also offers premium ready-to-wear garments, and operates boutiques in multiple major cities throughout the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The brand made headlines in SEY 2946 when it featured the work of [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) designer Kev in its Generations campaign.","g":["footwear manufacturer","clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c257f1d6-4400-480b-a57d-98e2cadc00a8"},
{"id":"laylani-addison","gp":"VYLvBm6Po1","t":"Laylani Addison","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Laylani Addison (SEY 2889 - present) is the current [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Formerly, she was Dean of Applied Science at Mentor University (2931 - 2947), and before that, Professor of Integrated Science and Xenotechnology at Mentor for nine years. She was sworn-in as Imperator on 1 January 2951. Her platform includes plans for an Innovation Initiative that will loosen the current restrictions on AI research, as well as increase spending on education and scientific research. She seeks to increase funding on publicly subsidized universities, strengthen relations between Human and alien civilizations, provide more funding for [Synthworld](gp:RLMmAnr4gj), and create a government program to locate the lost [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) colony ship, [*Artemis*](gp:0jGxngnLzm). She is not affiliated with a political party.","g":["uee imperator","human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c3eeb67c-e449-4ee8-9758-71eb694406f7"},
{"id":"legatus-exercitus","gp":"0QlKMOJELo","t":"Legatus Exercitus","k":"faction","c":["Government","Military","Human"],"x":"Legatus Exercitus is the [Army's](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) representative in the [High Command](gp:RegxqX26ok) and is the highest possible rank for an officer of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) Army to obtain. Their responsibilities are to set Army policy, directly interpret the orders of the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl), and brief the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) and Imperator in military matters.","g":["human government","uee high command"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2d49138e-7031-4c9c-ac0d-666a7f04bbcb"},
{"id":"legatus-marinuum","gp":"RWolAvP7qp","t":"Legatus Marinuum","k":"faction","c":["Government","Military","Human"],"x":"The Legatus Marinuum is a representative from the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) [Marines (UEEM)](gp:V7d5ZYEr1a) who serves on the [High Command](gp:RegxqX26ok). The highest possible rank for a UEE Marine to obtain, the Legatus Marinuum is responsible for dictating UEEM policy, interpreting and facilitating the orders of the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl), and briefing the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) and Imperator on Marine matters.","g":["uee high command","human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/993bf43f-c6d1-40da-a2cd-c333bca5e847"},
{"id":"legatus-navium","gp":"V7dPXLWYL3","t":"Legatus Navium","k":"faction","c":["Government","Military","Human"],"x":"Legatus Navium is the highest possible rank obtainable in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) and serves as the Navy's representative in the [High Command](gp:RegxqX26ok). The Navium interprets and facilitates the orders of the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) and briefs the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) and Imperator on such matters as the movement of fleets.","g":["uee high command","human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d09b6d54-4ad9-4f9a-9f2b-35743e469b6a"},
{"id":"lgionnaire","gp":"VgE4LO5Z89","t":"Legionnaire","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human","Military"],"x":"The Legionnaire is a medium-sized boarding spacecraft manufactured by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military. After the military failed to intervene in a piracy incident that led to the deaths of two civilians in SEY 2918, they issued an all-call for any type of technology that would help improve the success rate of boarding operations. Anvil's submission, a new spacecraft designed by lead engineer Grott Taylor, was ultimately selected and debuted in 2922. The Legionnaire's advanced integrated infiltration system, two-in-one docking collar able to connect to all UEE-standard apertures, and trio of shield generators streamlined the boarding process and decreased the likelihood of accidents. By 2925, the Legionnaire became the centerpiece of the UEE Navy's interception tactics package. A civilian version of the ship entered the market in 2952 during [Invictus Launch Week](gp:0KnDxLpvkM).","g":["boarding","anvil aerospace","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0f7b14dc-f08f-4c31-9075-ff7a9a1ca689"},
{"id":"leir-i","gp":"VDzAoKox68","t":"Leir I","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Leir I is a small, naturally habitable planet in the [Leir system](gp:0Ql7xwzmzL). Rich in minerals, it was initially settled by independent miners, mostly [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), who established settlements without government support from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It was not officially developed by the UEE when it was discovered in 2677 thanks to [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) [Illyana Messer VI's](gp:bZwQBNmWrL) disinterest in the planet's resources. When a [dangerous cult](gp:V7dLljjOeL) took over neighboring planet [Mya (Leir II)](gp:RxnqNaGr8Q) in 2812, the UEE government chose to allow the Leir system and all its planets to remain unclaimed. Leir I remains autonomous, and is home to a scattered collection of small towns and mining outposts.","g":["leir system","habitable","habitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fc7f9ee7-b7dc-4ba7-9c74-837ac8dfc5a0"},
{"id":"leir-iii","gp":"RkGeZXw9pp","t":"Leir III","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Leir III is the final planet from the sun of the [Leir system](gp:0Ql7xwzmzL). A carbon planet, Leir III's surface is a sandy desert partially covered in towering graphite crystals. Its atmosphere of carbon dioxide, carbon monoxide, sulfur, nitrogen, and ozone gives rise to powerful storms. Soon after its discovery, adventurous colonists attempted to erect permanent installations that would endure the weather, but their efforts were forced to cease when indigenous [valakkars](gp:RMNKXwe51E), the megafauna also known as giant sandworms, repeatedly destroyed  the half-finished buildings. Today, a handful of miners and outlaws live on Leir III in temporary encampments around the planet that can be easily moved ahead of deadly storms or valakkar attacks.","g":["leir system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7bf2e60d-7396-43b0-8ad2-fa6bbf093e45"},
{"id":"leir-system","gp":"0Ql7xwzmzL","t":"Leir System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Leir system is an [unclaimed](gp:VgExMejDPx) planetary system made up of a type-A main sequence star and three terrestrial planets. Discovered in SEY 2677 by a team of [ICC Stellar Surveyors](gp:V8gJvaZ2YW), initial assessments showed that the system was rich in minerals. However, the newly-ascended [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) [Illyana Messer VI](gp:bZwQBNmWrL) chose not to commit [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) resources to its development in favor of strengthening her position. Independent miners soon established themselves on the naturally habitable Leir I. In 2743, the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) rights to [Leir II](gp:RxnqNaGr8Q) were sold to Hatfield & Harding. Although the terraformation was completed, project leader Dr. Marcus Fayel led a takeover of the planet in 2812, backed by a base of followers now known as the [Outsiders](gp:V7dLljjOeL). Today, a small community of miners on [Leir I](gp:VDzAoKox68) are happy to trade with any visitors, but the people of Leir II refuse to purchase goods made in the UEE in order to maintain a \"pure\" society.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0813307e-0961-4e75-8358-d11f056ac1fc"},
{"id":"leonard-casse","gp":"RX3Krj1EKN","t":"Leonard Casse","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Leonard Casse (2563 - 2615) was a notable spacecraft designer and engineer and founder of [Casse Aerospace](gp:RPPx3G1MMX) known for his influence on [J. Harris Arnold](gp:Vy2ZqLy458), [Silas Koerner](gp:V8gJMXjE8o), Jules Parleigh, and other aerospace luminaries. In 2587, he was hired as a junior engineer at [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) and was assigned to the Starbright transport team, where he was promoted after identifying a potentially dangerous flaw in its design. By 2595, he had been named lead designer of the 2600 Starbright, which was praised for its entry system and internal flight controls upon its release. In 2599 he left RSI, citing dissatisfaction with the hierarchical structure, and founded his own company, Casse Aerospace, which operated on a flat organizational model in which everyone's opinions would have equal weight. He was only able to create two ships, the Cosmo Sloop and the [Hurricane](gp:bmNrpdn4gQ) fighter, before perishing in a mid-air collision in 2615. His work rose to fame again in the 2780s, when J. Harris Arnold of [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) began to feature Casse's signature flourishes in his own designs. In 2902, he was inducted into the Edleson Design Institute Hall of Fame.","g":["casse aerospace"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3858b5d0-4034-4b84-8971-aa8119f001c9"},
{"id":"levski","gp":"0dXQqBMAOp","t":"Levski","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Levski is a permanent, independent settlement located on [Delamar](gp:0GxoZnAGrg) in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). Built out of the remains of an abandoned [QV Planet Services](gp:V7d3ZyP9X3) mining facility, it was founded in SEY 2655 by a group of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) political dissenters called the People's Alliance and named after a 19th century Earth revolutionary. Refugees from [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792) Earth (Sol III) were welcomed as early residents to this fledgling egalitarian community, along with fugitives escaping unjust government persecution. Pirates, smugglers, and other outlaws have been known to frequent Levski as well, in spite of opposition from the People's Alliance.","g":["delamar","sealed settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b6d96252-1b4e-4d84-8320-1f9f04106583"},
{"id":"leylands-tortoise","gp":"0rqMrrLpnB","t":"Leyland's Tortoise","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"# Leyland's Tortoise\nLeyland's tortoise is a species of tortoise indigenous to Earth (Sol III). They have glossy shells with minor color variation around the scutes and the edges of the shells. Extremely docile, they are kept as pets by Humans, especially long-haul spacers. Over-collection and habitat destruction have made them nearly extinct in the wild.\n \n# Description\nLeyland's tortoises have smooth, domed shells in shades of green, yellow, and brown. The shell is relatively smooth; even if the tortoise matured in harsh conditions, the shell shows little to no scute pyramiding. The edges of the shell flare out slightly at the sides. The plastron is usually yellow, with green edging where it connects to the shell. The back end of the plastron is indented in a V-shape, underneath which is a small, nubby tail. Each of the tortoise's four legs ends with five claws.\n \n# Range and Behavior\nThe original habitat of Leyland's tortoise was limited to the South American continent, along the Andes mountains and into the central rainforest. Due to habitat destruction, the only remaining wild breeding population of Leyland's tortoise on Earth is found along the Amazon river in protected areas of rainforest. Attempts to establish Leyland's tortoise on other planets have been met with limited success; Saisei (Centauri III) and Locke (Idris IV) both sustain minor Leyland's tortoise populations. In 2875, conservationists attempted to introduce the tortoise to Lo (Corel III). However, Banu residents of the planet consumed it at an unsustainable rate. The population did not take hold.\n \n \nThe tortoises are foragers, most active in the late afternoon until sunset, with a smaller window of high activity from sunrise to midmorning. Seeds, greens, fruit, invertebrates, roots, grasses, and fungi form the bulk of the tortoise's diet. Over 50% of its day is spent at rest in shared burrows with other tortoises. After consuming a large meal, a tortoise might rest, totally immobile, for up to a week at a time. \n \n# Pet Trade\nLeyland's tortoises are popular pets due to their docility, low-cost diet, long lifespan, and adaptability to varying conditions. They are easily kept aboard most spacecraft in roofless enclosures 2 meters wide, 2 meters long, and 50 centimeters high. Plenty of shady spots and heated areas should be provided along with shelter and water. Ideally, a tortoise should not be kept alone. It is recommended that owners choose companions of the same sex to discourage unintentional breeding.\n \n \nBecause the tortoise is nearly extinct in the wild, it is illegal to own one that has been captured instead of captively bred. Any person within the UEE found with a wild-caught Leyland's tortoise in their possession is subject to fine and arrest.","g":["earth","sol iii","saisei","centauri iii","locke","idris iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/23b59086-6f7a-43f7-b5a4-a9562f68f798"},
{"id":"genesis","gp":"0NwprWlxpX","t":"LH307 Genesis","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The LH307 Genesis is a medium-range passenger spacecraft developed by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N). Major space transport services such as Meridian Transit utilize the Genesis in their fleets as a way to standardize repair processes and lower maintenance costs. The spacecraft's interior can be adopted for a number of roles. Passenger and freight transport are the most common configurations of the Genesis, followed by military adaptations such as troop transports and Space Warning and Control System (SWACS) setups.","g":["genesis","crusader industries","passenger transport","starliner","transport","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/24a9dbf6-eecf-4122-b1b8-c0e2be56ef75"},
{"id":"litova","gp":"VJOzBK4PLe","t":"Li'tova","k":"culture","c":["Culture","Xi'an"],"x":"Li'tova is the central code of ethics and main religion for the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) people. It was established in roughly SEY 33900 BCE by early Xi'an. The core of Li'tova centers around the concept of time; specifically, the intent and effect of all actions throughout time, no matter how small. It was codified into Xi'an law in MXY I.0 (19668 BCE) by [Emperor](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) Ya.l'ē se Ru'a, the only surviving daughter of her [House](gp:box9JmxvWL) and the first Xi'an Emperor. A dedicated commune to Li'tova is located on the planet R.aip'uāng (Kai'pua III).","g":["religion","xi'an religion"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/35a2d72d-d0cd-4e36-a507-afaf5fcad87f"},
{"id":"liberator","gp":"bo1wkzBead","t":"Liberator","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Liberator is a light carrier spacecraft manufactured by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). Designed with three open air landing pads and an interior bay that can accommodate up to two ground vehicles, the Liberator is capable of making long-range journeys to transport short-range ships to locations they would otherwise be unable to reach. Its Size 3 [quantum drive](gp:RX3DOkJdxJ) gives the Liberator the same long-distance capabilities as a military-spec carrier. The interior of the ship is outfitted with a spacious cargo hold and sleeping accommodations for a crew of two. Each Liberator is equipped with a manual laser turret, dual automated defense turrets, and four missile launchers.","g":["anvil aerospace","carrier","light carrier","human spacecraft"]},
{"id":"life-labor-style-employee-contract","gp":"RLMmBD2z5d","t":"Life/Labor-Style Employee Contract","k":"company","c":["Human","Commerce"],"x":"The Life/Labor-style employee contract is a controversial legal agreement that gives a corporation a high degree of control over employees in exchange for housing, medical support, and the provision of other social services. It was developed in the early 26th century by [Arial Hurston](gp:0qnN5w4kmW) and continues to be a major aspect of the [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) workforce today. Since its introduction, workers' rights groups have continually protested its use, stating that the contracts are intentionally structured to entrap employees into lifelong service with little avenues to complete or negate the contract.","g":["hurston dynamics","arial hurston","contract"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5895fce7-1724-40bf-9996-074f3fb53616"},
{"id":"lightning-bolt-company","gp":"RxNxDejJ4z","t":"Lightning Bolt Company","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Lightning Bolt Company is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of spacecraft energy weapons. It was founded in early SEY 2921 by Irina Arkadova, who worked as a private military contractor before starting the company. Arkadova first became interested in weapon design after becoming increasingly frustrated with her weapon's performance in the field, a construction fault that she attributed to lack of practical field testing and experience. Their first manufactured weapon, the Mayak range of hardened electron cannons, proved a success among security professionals and allowed the company to begin producing specialized personal weapons as well.","g":["weapons manufacturer","irina arkady"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c78fd083-984e-4647-9d5c-4f88043ae3f9"},
{"id":"linton-messer-xi","gp":"RwZBaD4Mdq","t":"Linton Messer XI","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Linton Messer XI (2745-2792) was the last of the Messers to occupy the office of [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). He assumed control of the UEE in 2781 after seizing power from his father, [Ulysses Messer X](gp:bBp6YZPOGO). During his reign, he sold the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) rights of Garron II to a private company with connections to his family, knowing that the planet was inhabited by sentient beings. Revolutionary group Tide leaked footage of the resulting carnage to the media, sparking the [Anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7). During the uprising, Linton was killed in office.","g":["uee imperator","messer era","messer dynasty","anti-messer revolution","massacre of garron ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0b5507c2-1115-4d1a-ad02-cdd2b4f0dda7"},
{"id":"liston-garrity","gp":"RxnPNwAW4M","t":"Liston Garrity","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Liston Garrity (2248-2317) was a weapons designer who founded weapons design house and manufacturer [Garrity Arms](gp:bE3rLKwr9J) in the late 23rd century. Born on Earth (Sol III), Garrity parlayed the initial success of his Tedge series of combustion pistols to finance a move to the burgeoning Mars colony. Garrity designed fourteen distinct weapons during his lifetime. His family name is still used under license to brand weapons today.","g":["garrity arms"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1baeae9f-6889-43ae-b92a-611d3fc81d59"},
{"id":"livia-messer-iii","gp":"01dWwaQkrL","t":"Livia Messer III","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Livia Messer III (2593-2661) was [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) from 2628 to 2643. She inherited the office from her father, [Deacon Messer II](gp:0j46m4BYge), when he voluntarily stepped down. Livia expanded her father's legal reform efforts by increasing the maximum sentences for convicted criminals and restructuring the definition of prisons, allowing her to build political prisons on Charon III. She also increased government oversight of media, effectively establishing an unofficial office of propaganda, and restricted travel in the interest of security. She, her husband Daniel Scota, and her son [Marius](gp:RxNxAgrXZz) were victims of a shuttle crash in 2641, when their craft malfunctioned upon atmospheric re-entry above Moscow, Earth (Sol III). Though she survived, the rest of her family did not. She retired in 2643, after giving her son the honorary title Marius IV. She died in her sleep in 2661; one month before Deacon II.","g":["uee imperator","messer dynasty","messer era"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/23054b34-978c-413a-853e-7b0e7e5b43e3"},
{"id":"lixaauu-taal-iv","gp":"0GxpmEWOAE","t":"Lixāuu (T.āl IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Lixāuu (T.āl IV) is the fourth planet from the sun of the [T.āl system](gp:R4j2mdjZE5), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Naturally habitable, the acid already-present in Lixāuu's atmosphere convinced officials to make it the home of processing facilities, refineries, and other pollution-causing infrastructure. [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) employed as haulers and refinery workers make up a large percentage of the population. Although it is the least visited planet in T.āl, the working-class food stalls that can be found outside nearly all of the planet's green-tinted factories attract tourists seeking Xi'an street fare.","g":["lixāuu","t.āl iv","t.āl system","habitable planet","habitable","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"lo-corel-iii","gp":"VarAoYEQYd","t":"Lo (Corel III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Lo (Corel III) is the largest populated planet in the [Corel system](gp:R9vQnko7Y2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is represented by one [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ). As a major population center on the border between the UEE and the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3), it is a hub of trade and commerce between the two civilizations and is home to both [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). The largest shipping and customs center, [New Junction](gp:V3G53AXDgY), is located in one of Lo's hottest regions. Meticulous inspection of goods that pass through the planet combined with frequent dust storms often cause long backups in traffic, sometimes requiring haulers to stay overnight.","g":["lo","corel iii","habitable","habitable planet","human planet","corel system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/34a3c169-89e0-4ddf-8b23-a7aa48ce24ec"},
{"id":"locke-idris-iv","gp":"RAX8yYv9jm","t":"Locke (Idris IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Locke (Idris IV) is the sole inhabited planet in the [Idris system](gp:bZkrMGnLdM), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). [Terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and colonized by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) in the early 26th century, it was captured by the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) in 2542 during the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546), and used as a main strike hub for the Tevarin fleet while it was under their control. It became the site of the [Battle of Idris IV](gp:ReJajXKelk) in 2544, a key engagement that turned the tide of the war in favor of the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) and launched [Ivar Messer's](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) political career. Much of the landscape that was destroyed via orbital bombardment has since been rebuilt, though some craters remain. A thriving tourism industry is based in the city of [Tanys](gp:01Lo67xgw1), located in the Corsti Mountains. Additionally, the planet is famous for the quality of its brandy and cognac.","g":["locke","idris iv","habitable","habitable planet","idris system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7ee98c7f-5138-4a4a-8300-26f53a484e80"},
{"id":"lorona-banshee-iii","gp":"bZkDByjyPO","t":"Lorona (Banshee III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Lorona is the third planet from the sun in the [Banshee system](gp:0Gx4BENmKg), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Although the pulsar Banshee has made surface-level [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) impossible, Lorona is home to a series of stable, populated underground cities supported by a mining-focused economy. Coils on the surface of Lorona harvest energy from the star to help power the settlements underneath. Kesseli, the capital, is the largest subterranean city in the UEE.","g":["lorona","banshee iii","banshee system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a02247c8-ad52-4b4e-bc68-3aaa2f8b31cc"},
{"id":"lorville","gp":"Rw1ZlJNE36","t":"Lorville","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Lorville is a city on [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL), home to the headquarters of [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ), the [Central Headquarters and Shared Services Center](gp:R56nmzpqPg) (or Central Tower). Initially founded as a barracks for employees of Hurston Dynamics under the letter designation LOR for \"Local Occupational Residency,\" it has since grown to become the most populous location on the planet. Hurston Dynamics maintains a no-fly zone over the city, and requires spacecraft to land at the nearby Teasa Spaceport or on top of Central itself. The air quality of Lorville is generally poor due to decades of unrestricted pollution.","g":["hurston","stanton i","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b8731d94-492d-4543-930b-4067966e6b47"},
{"id":"lost-squad-show","gp":"0OaBMgylww","t":"Lost Squad (Show)","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*Lost Squad* is a Human historical war drama series starring Callum Robb based on the events surrounding the Fall of Caliban. Written and created by Jaina Tatman and Hadrian Weir and produced by [Devil May Care Productions](gp:VY4Wm4pAmo), the series dramatizes the history of the [89th UEE Naval Support Squadron](gp:0Gz5BNmPqo), who famously gave their lives to allow as many people as possible to escape the Caliban system during [the Vanduul invasion of 2884](gp:0Gz5DNryvE). The first episode premiered on Spectrum in 2944.","g":["devil may care productions"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/90b52af2-ceff-4d11-b7fc-459ef35695c9"},
{"id":"luminalia","gp":"0KxWxZwaBD","t":"Luminalia","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human","Banu"],"x":"# LUMINALIA\n\nLuminalia is a holiday celebrated by both [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) and [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) annually on December 22nd. It originated as the irregularly-held Banu festival *tsikti efanga* (Glow Festival), marked by the lighting of ceremonial lamps that stay lit until their fuel is consumed (about 34,000 beats / 2 Standard Earth Days). While the lamps are burning, all Banu, no matter where they are, are considered one [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron). They invite friends, business associates, and passing strangers into their Soulis and give their guests a gift. In Banu culture, this is so that they will always have something that they could sell. All attendees are expected to provide food, drinks, and/or party favors in return, and if they can't, the host will often have those items available for purchase. Humans in the [Davien system](gp:Rz2g71YlkY) began to participate in the festival with Banu shortly after the [Banu-Human Interstellar Peace and Trade Accord](gp:RzPoJ1aP4z) in 2438. Today, Banu and Humans commemorate Luminalia with gift-exchanges, present hunts, glowing lights, food and drink, limited-time discounts, decorations in green and red, and gatherings of family, friends, business associates, and acquaintances. \n\n# HISTORY\n\nAlthough its origins are unknown due to the Banu practice of not keeping historical records, *tsikti efanga* has existed at least as long as the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) has had contact with other civilizations. In MXY III.367 (SEY 1927), a group of [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) diplomats participated in a planet-wide celebration of the festival on Trise I. Initially there solely to observe Banu culture, they were surprised to see Banu suddenly hang colorful lanterns, fill them with oil, and light them. When asked what was happening, the Banu explained that it was time for *tsikti efanga*, and invited the diplomats to join in the festivities. At first they declined, but ultimately relented after repeated requests. They were then laden with gifts in exchange for samples of Xi'an cuisine, which was met with great enthusiasm from the gastronomically-curious Banu. Additionally, the diplomats witnessed multiple members of two fiercely competitive religious Soulis cheerfully exchange presents with one another. They found this especially intriguing. One diplomat wrote in his report to the Emperor, \"A curiously convivial spirit has arisen where there was once inter-House rivalry. Gifts pass freely from hand to hand, evidently without malice, even between sworn enemies.\" \n\nAnother historically significant tsikti efanga was held in SEY 2441, when the members of a ship repair Souli that had been doing business on [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5) in the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) lit their ceremonial lamps and invited Humans to come and celebrate with them. In contrast to the cautious Xi'an diplomats, Humans did not need to be asked twice. For as long as the lanterns burned, Humans were given gifts if they contributed food, drinks, or other items to the celebration. If guests didn't have any items to provide, nearby merchants from other Soulis conveniently had some for sale at a holiday discount. As more and more Humans joined throughout the night, the party eventually grew large enough that it attracted the attention of a local news crew. The resulting story of this raucous celebration involving Humans and their then-new interstellar neighbors became one of the year's most played clips. \n\nBy the time the next *tsikti efanga* occurred in December 2445, Banu presence on Davien had increased enough that artisans and small business owners located near Soulis noticed a significant boost in sales when festivities began. This success was enough to convince them to organize a night market event centered around the festival the following year. Although this did not coincide with an actual *tsikti efanga*, enough Humans and Banu participated in the market that Davien merchants were satisfied with their profits and began to hold \"Banu holiday events\" every December. Soulis soon began to light their lamps at the same time as these events to attract business of their own, and Humans started throwing private gatherings as an excuse to get together with family and friends. By the dawn of the 26th century, a Human-Banu hybrid version of the *tsikti efanga*, dubbed \"Luminalia\" by the press, had become an annual tradition on Davien.\n\nAs Luminalia increased in popularity, it spread to neighboring systems with less Banu influence and further changed from its original form. Major Human-owned corporations started to mass-market special oil lamps and items for hosts to gift their guests, and for guests to bring their hosts, lessening the importance of food to the holiday. Other Human merchants modified the traditional gift sharing by hiding empty gift-wrapped packages that could be returned unopened in exchange for a surprise like a few credits or a small toy. The increased foot traffic into their stores increased holiday sales and became a tradition in its own right. A popular ad campaign featuring a Banu excited to host a celebration with their Human friends used the colors green and red to represent Luminalia, indelibly associating them with the holiday in the public consciousness. By the mid-26th century, Luminalia celebrations had become so prevalent throughout the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that it was officially added to the Human calendar in SEY 2557.","g":["banu holiday","uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4b8d233b-6fc0-46df-96b3-4a90a77845e0"},
{"id":"luna","gp":"VYLwvrlEz4","t":"Luna","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Luna is a clothing brand that specializes in casualwear and activewear. Known for its commitment to comfort, the company's goal when designing its garments is to create pieces that allow for natural freedom of movement. Each item Luna creates goes through extensive testing before it is mass produced to ensure that it can withstand long periods of vigorous activity without restraining its wearer's motions.","g":["luna (clothing brand)","clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/95f4533b-68bf-4e84-b73b-04b096ce9ff4"},
{"id":"luna-sol-3a","gp":"VYL3vDrYKo","t":"Luna (Sol 3a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Luna (Sol 3a) is the moon of [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Tidally locked to Earth, it has long been a subject of fascination for [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), and became the first celestial body they visited in SEY 1969. In the 22nd century, Humans began to experiment with sealed bases on Luna's surface, marking their earliest attempts at colonization outside Earth. The remains of these nascent bases were declared a protected historical site in 2799. Today, Luna is home to multiple robust sealed colonies.","g":["luna","sol 3a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e5b19745-9db6-4b98-8f45-240dc776981f"},
{"id":"lunes","gp":"RWoo8qZ91P","t":"Lunes","k":"life","c":["Food and Beverages","Plants"],"x":"The lunes fruit, known also as the \"spiral fruit\" due to the circular ridges that form on it as it approaches ripeness, is an edible fruit indigenous to Osha (Kilian VI). Before Osha was [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), the lunes tree was one of the wild plants selected to be re-introduced to the planet after terraformation was complete. [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) who settled on Osha bred subsequent generations of the tree to bear the soft, sweet, and juicy lunes fruit. Lunes fruit are popularly used in ice cream and other desserts.","g":["spiral fruit","fruit","trees","food"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fa9aa562-2371-4f3c-9ef2-5d2780bb7174"},
{"id":"lynx","gp":"0n1lEZd7XZ","t":"Lynx","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Lynx is a luxury exploration vehicle developed by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). The company adapted the Lynx from their existing Ursa rover to include alongside their [Constellation Phoenix](gp:VyvYqezlqW) luxury model spacecraft. The Lynx drops some of the Ursa's armor and internal modularity in exchange for luxury fittings and general quality of life improvements.","g":["all-terrain vehicle (atv)","expedition","luxury","roberts space industries (rsi)","human vehicle"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7aa108d6-ec09-4976-897f-1b23515ec63d"},
{"id":"lyre","gp":"R6v8OmAAlj","t":"Lyre","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Lyre is a major city on [Cassel (Goss II)](gp:RPDy6gqX7Z), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that became a tourism center after Cassel was declared a natural wonder in 2624. The city suffered a significant economic downturn in the mid 2600s due to [Livia Messer III's](gp:01dWwaQkrL) heavy travel restrictions. In the 2800s, restoration work began in Lyre when the inhabitants of the Goss system pooled their resources to revitalize Cassel. Its crystalline buildings, erected during the city's boom years, are among its most popular attractions.","g":["cassel","goss ii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d4007a61-a610-426b-b59b-87fd2825db87"},
{"id":"lyria-stanton-3a","gp":"RvlgwoxzpY","t":"Lyria (Stanton 3a)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Lyria is a natural satellite of [ArcCorp (Stanton III)](gp:bBzpNY6ANd) that orbits more closely to the planet than its sister moon, [Wala (Stanton 3b)](gp:V3GqNknrr2). Water ice geysers and cryo-volcanoes force water vapor into Lyria's oxygen and ammonia atmosphere when they erupt. Although the air is too thin to support life, most commercial pressure suits can use it to replenish their oxygen reserves.","g":["lyria","stanton 3a","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","arccorp moon","stanton iii moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/924197bc-d3a6-4b2f-a468-95b5ee1efacb"},
{"id":"lyris-flotilla","gp":"bo1yaak7LL","t":"Lyris Flotilla","k":"place","c":["Settlements"],"x":"The Lyris flotilla is a vast interconnected network of spacecraft and space stations that orbits the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Located in orbit around [Nogo (Gliese IV)](gp:R4jEkkOAkW), it is the main trade hub in Gliese, and is home to a dense population of [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). While the shape of the flotilla is ever-shifting as ships arrive and leave, the structures at Lyris' heart are hundreds of years old. It is hypothesized that the first ships gathered there when Nogo was abandoned.","g":["gliese system","space station","banu flotilla"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c79d443e-40c7-467f-baaf-458f584b86f5"},
{"id":"luungxyi-taal-iii","gp":"R6d2mppBaq","t":"Lūng'xyi (T.āl III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Lūng'xyi (T.āl III) is the third planet from the sun of the [T.āl system](gp:R4j2mdjZE5), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Dedicated to the production of food and textiles, its vibrant culinary and fashion scenes draw a steady stream of visitors to the planet. High-end dining establishments on Lūng'xyi craft intricate culinary creations that can be sampled nowhere else, all sourced from the myriad farms that cover the lush countryside. The textiles produced in Lūng'xyi's violet-accented cities inform trends across both the Xi'an Empire and the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE).","g":["lūng'xyi","t.āl system","habitable planet","habitable","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"miiyong-ailka-iv","gp":"0jGGDY1yAW","t":"M.iiy'ong (Ail'ka IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"M.iiy'ong (Ail'ka IV) is the fourth planet from the sun in the [Ail'ka system](gp:01LLZmEygJ), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). As a base of operations for the Xi'an military, M.iiy'ong is a densely populated, busy world that houses flight academies, command centers, intelligence facilities, and barracks, among other military-related locations. Many transportation, armor, and weapons manufacturers operate from M.iiy'ong, including military spacecraft company [Aopoa](gp:VyvY5jyZwp). While non-Xi'an are allowed to visit, travel is still highly restricted.","g":["m.iiy'ong","ail'ka iv","ail'ka system","habitable planet","habitable","xi'an asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ed735654-d798-48a9-9e2c-554a0658796a"},
{"id":"m2-hercules","gp":"0Gz5Dk8aGa","t":"M2 Hercules","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The M2 Hercules is a military transport ship developed by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) for the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military. It is utilized by the [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) and [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) in lift and landing missions as well as logistics operations through active war zones. Ground vehicles such as the [Nova](gp:01L8gLYXaY) tank and [Ursa Rover](gp:RAdjOOm67M) and small spacecraft such as the [Aurora](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/aurora-series) can fit inside the M2's cargo hold.","g":["hercules series","military transport","crusader industries","transport","human spacecraft","military spacecraft","starlifter series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7115b2fb-d031-4b58-868c-09b163a68aab"},
{"id":"m50","gp":"V7gMWO7Yo3","t":"M50","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The M50 is a single-seat performance racing spacecraft sold by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). Built for speed and maneuverability, it was first conceived specifically to capture the [Murray Cup](gp:bE3r71yZ87) racing trophy. An interceptor model of the M50 is also produced by Origin; this type is actively operated by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk). Since its last major rework in SEY 2945, the M50 has earned a number of top racing honors.","g":["origin jumpworks","racing","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a0bea646-81a2-4e48-aea4-f1895ebe383e"},
{"id":"matokyaai-tokyai","gp":"RegZqK3adj","t":"Ma'tok.yaai (Tokyai)","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"The ma'tok.yāi is a forest-dwelling apex predator indigenous to Xi (R.il'a V). Speakers of UEE Standard sometimes refer to it as the tokyai. About 2 meters in length, it has occasionally been known to take down prey twice its size. Its long, curved claws help it grip branches, and membranes under its arms help it glide from tree to tree. An ambush predator, it typically waits among the leaves for unsuspecting prey to pass underneath it, then drops down and attacks. Although it is endangered on Xi, there is a healthy population of ma'tok.yāi on the preserve world Ko'li (Ē'aluth III).","g":["ma'tok.yaai","tokyai","xi","r.il'a v"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f5fa5441-334a-4e6b-bf4f-4a45685aaf63"},
{"id":"macarthur-kilian-v","gp":"Rz22dGBlnz","t":"MacArthur (Kilian V)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"MacArthur (Kilian V) is the fifth planet from the sun of the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and serves as the main headquarters of the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). Soon after the planet was [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) to [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) specifications, the Navy constructed boot camps (known locally as Forges), officer training programs, flight academies, medical centers, and other facilities there. The planet is orbited by sprawling space docks and shipyards operated by major spacecraft manufacturers, including [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) and [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw).","g":["macarthur","kilian v","kilian system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet","macarthur naval base","uee navy"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fdaf8866-70db-4def-8b50-e516020fcd21"},
{"id":"macarthur-naval-base","gp":"bBp6BmDMGJ","t":"MacArthur Naval Base","k":"place","c":["Military","Human"],"x":"MacArthur Naval Base is the largest [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) base in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Located on the planet [MacArthur (Kilian V)](gp:Rz22dGBlnz), it is home to the Navy headquarters, shipyards, academies, boot camps, and hospitals. Most of MacArthur is occupied by the naval base; travel, therefore, is tightly restricted.","g":["uee navy","macarthur","kilian v","ueen base"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/16479e5d-29a5-469b-8aeb-b2da7bc4589f"},
{"id":"magda-stanton-1c","gp":"0qanJYxAG7","t":"Magda (Stanton 1c)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Magda is the third-closest moon to [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL). Although its temperature falls into ranges friendly to life, its nitrogen-methane atmosphere cannot be safely breathed. Enormous areas of blue-green dirt on Magda's surface are said to resemble oceans when the moon is viewed from orbit. The moon is named after former [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) CEO [Magda Hurston](gp:V7gMKmw6wa), who recommended that the company purchase Stanton I from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) in 2865. In recent years, natural geological formation Sketto Rock has become a popular location for landscape photography.","g":["magda","stanton 1c","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","hurston","stanton i","magda hurston","hurston dynamics","uee moon","stanton i moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/79232aed-1c65-41ae-89b2-66f2becd292d"},
{"id":"magda-hurston","gp":"V7gMKmw6wa","t":"Magda Hurston","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"# MAGDA HURSTON\n\nMagda Hurston (2833 - 2921) was the CEO of [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ) from 2883 to 2915. It was her initiative that led the company to purchase [Stanton I](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL) from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) in 2865. The [third moon](gp:0qanJYxAG7) of Hurston is named in her honor. She was succeeded as CEO by her son, [Gavin E. Hurston](gp:RzPoAdZpEl).\n\n# EARLY LIFE\n\nThe oldest child of Chesterfield Hurston and Mariah Park Hurston, Magda was born in 2833 on [Rytif (Bremen II)](gp:R5pA7q691W) at a hospital near the site of Hurston Dynamics' secondary headquarters. She received her early education on Earth (Sol III) and attended the Haymore School of Economics in Geneva for her undergraduate and graduate degrees, where she attained a Master of Science in Organizational and Social Psychology. Her dissertation, *Live, Work, and Play: Employee Productivity in Controlled Environments*, was selected as one of the winners of the Best Dissertation Prize for the 2854/2855 academic year. After a year-long internship at the [University of Persei Analytical Research and Quantification (UPARQ)](gp:0n1Mz2WmD7) on [Persei (Rhetor II)](gp:0ODlqM6zKO), she joined the family business in 2856, starting as an Associate Operations Analyst.\n\n# HURSTON DYNAMICS\n\nMagda moved upward through the ranks despite several clashes with distant relatives in higher positions, eventually becoming Chief Operations Officer in 2863. During this period, she made multiple cost-saving operational changes to Hurston Dynamics, such as utilizing nutritional supplements instead of fresh ingredients to reduce the cost of employee meals and opting for in-house production of worker protective equipment in place of renewing expensive outsourcing contracts. In 2865, she spearheaded her largest project: the purchase of governing interest and settlement rights for the naturally habitable planet Stanton I and its four moons from the UEE. It was under her advice that then-CEO Chesterfield Hurston agreed to the unprecedented expense. The changes they could make to the weapon manufacturing process, out from under the strict laws of the UEE, would save the company trillions. Chesterfield approved, and the planet Hurston was officially established.\n\nWhile Hurston Dynamics' mining division broke ground on antimatter precursor mines on the surface of Hurston, Magda supervised the design and construction of the first residential buildings that would later form the heart of the Workers District. She took a brief break in 2867 after the birth of her son Gavin. When Hurston's first antimatter refinery plant was completed in 2872 and workers began to arrive, the need for a much larger settlement became apparent. Magda spent five years identifying areas to cut costs so that new construction could be built quickly and at low price. The city of [Lorville](gp:Rw1ZlJNE36) was officially founded in 2877.\n\nIn 2883, halfway through the erection of [Central Tower](gp:R56nmzpqPg), Hurston Dynamics' new headquarters, Chesterfield died after a short battle with pancreatic cancer. Magda succeeded him as CEO. Under her leadership, daily work hours were extended for those under the [Life/Labor contract](gp:RLMmBD2z5d), and a weekly task-completion competition to shorten workday minutes was introduced. These changes improved overall efficiency by 3%. She oversaw the completion of Central in 2890, as well as a wide expansion of the company's antimatter mining, processing, and weapons construction. The contract she signed to provide the UEE military with antimatter warheads netted record profits. She continued her father's strip-mining operations, exempt from the UEE's anti-pollution laws thanks to the planet's independent status, allowing speedy and cheap extraction of Hurston's natural resources.\n\nShe retired as CEO in 2915 and was succeeded by her son Gavin, though she stayed on the board of Hurston Dynamics in an advisory capacity.\n\n# DEATH\n\nWhile en route from the Hurston Central building to Teasa Spaceport, where she was planning to travel via a private service to her family's vacation home on [Cassel (Goss II)](gp:RPDy6gqX7Z), her shuttle suffered a mid-flight collision with another shuttle. She and six other people died in the crash.","g":["hurston dynamics","gavin e hurston","rytif","bremen ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ac8c7f2f-fd61-4cd4-b6f9-c3d1a456af51"},
{"id":"magma-kilian-iv","gp":"RMNNlkKyon","t":"Magma (Kilian IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Magma (Kilian IV) is a highly geologically active planet in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Rich in rare minerals, Magma is the most active mining area in Kilian in spite of the frequent earthquakes. Lakes of lava often form and drain in the aftermath of volcanic eruptions and other tectonic activity, making the construction of permanent installations very difficult.","g":["magma","kilian iv","kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/59dd67b7-7bab-4616-8b8b-931b3a39081c"},
{"id":"magnus-i","gp":"VDzOrgDnOz","t":"Magnus I","k":"place","c":["Planets","Locations"],"x":"Magnus I is a chthonian planet in the [Magnus system](gp:RWolrNa1Ge) that orbits closest to the sun. Rich with high-value minerals and gemstones, the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) maintains exclusive mining rights to the planet, dating from when its main shipyards were located on [Borea (Magnus II)](gp:R9vGaQPXJN). Borea's [Senators](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) have repeatedly petitioned the UEE to return mining rights to the people of Magnus, but the UEE has thus far refused to capitulate.","g":["magnus system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/882a3807-525d-454e-b98c-1d529117a5a1"},
{"id":"magnus-iii","gp":"RX3D1NeGQk","t":"Magnus III","k":"place","c":["Planets","Locations"],"x":"Magnus III is a super-Jupiter gas giant in the [Magnus system](gp:RWolrNa1Ge), and is the planet furthest from the system's sun. Authorities in the system discourage travelers from visiting the planet due to documented pirate activity in the area.","g":["magnus system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/84ee97d0-eec0-4754-94e4-c58162d038b4"},
{"id":"magnus-system","gp":"RWolrNa1Ge","t":"Magnus System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"# MAGNUS SYSTEM\n\nThe Magnus system is a [planetary system](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/category/planetary-systems) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It was discovered in SEY 2499, and subsequently selected as the headquarters of the [UEE Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). Once the center of a thriving industry centered around the UEEN's shipbuilding facilities, the system's economy crashed when the Navy moved their operations to [Kilian](gp:0ODD4mY9aP) in 2631. Though the system has entered a period of revitalization thanks to [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed) establishing their headquarters and prime production facilities on [Borea](gp:R9vGaQPXJN), its population is low compared to similarly aged systems in the UEE. It is made up of a chthonian planet, a terrestrial planet, a gas giant, and a K-type star.\n\n# DISCOVERY\n\nIn 2499, the Magnus system was discovered as a part of [Project Far Star](gp:0qnNAD6YKa). Initial surveys of the system showed it to be uncommonly empty of asteroid fields, protoplanets, or other potential hazards for space travel. Only one of its three planets was identified as a good candidate for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). The system's then-remote location and abundance of natural resources found in the planet closest to the sun attracted the attention of the then-[United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) Navy (UPEN), who were in search of a new center for shipbuilding. After procuring funding from the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) in 2533, the UPEN began a military-run, closed-terraforming operation on Magnus II. \n\n# PLANETARY SYSTEM\n\nThe system's star, Magnus, is an orange-red K-Type main sequence star that is roughly 5 billion years old. [Magnus I](gp:VDzOrgDnOz), a mineral-rich chthonian planet, orbits closest to the sun. The UEE Navy maintains exclusive mining rights to it, dating from the early 26th century. The super-Jupiter [Magnus III](gp:RX3D1NeGQk), noted for its multi-chromatic bands of gas, orbits the furthest from the sun. Borea (Magnus II), a rocky terrestrial planet, is the only habitable planet in the system. Residents of Borea sometimes claim to outsiders that a fourth planet called [\"Triggerfish\"](gp:0rxrqgzgP6) orbits beyond Magnus III. It does not. This led to the creation of the eponymous popular holiday.\n\n# NOTABLE LOCATIONS\n\n*Borea (Magnus II)*\n\n[Borea](gp:R9vGaQPXJN) is a temperate planet that was identified as a prime terraforming candidate when the system was discovered. It was held up as a landmark example of terraforming success, with many climates closely resembling those of Earth. A century of unfettered shipbuilding, however, polluted the atmosphere, essentially rolling back some of the changes previously made by terraforming and transforming the climate to the harsh one it is known for today. \n\n# CULTURE\n\nThose who did not follow the Navy when it left for Kilian took up residence in Borea's abandoned properties and started up businesses in cheap ship repair and bootleg components fueled by harvested scrap. The system developed a reputation as a place where people who wanted to escape their past could reinvent themselves, no questions asked. \n\nThe empty warehouses and monolithic industrial equipment deemed too expensive to transport by the UEEN are no longer being left to deteriorate. Drake Interplanetary purchased much of them from the UEE in 2845 for very low cost, opting to open factories and set up their headquarters in Odyssa on Borea instead of more cosmopolitan systems like Terra. Job opportunities are increasing, and once-disreputable ghost towns are being repaired as more and more people choose to migrate to Magnus. The system's economy is slowly on the mend.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8d587a84-5b7f-4dd6-9d6a-16a884fd0b46"},
{"id":"magnus-tobin","gp":"RkGZqr8yNQ","t":"Magnus Tobin","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Magnus Tobin (2756 -  2912) is the founder of [microTech](gp:bE3rBB4j7J) and the architect behind the company's purchase of [Stanton IV](gp:VYL46xl5Z1) from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Upon receiving his [Equivalency](gp:Vgg7YGdQDY), he entered his parents' textile company and helped it generate record profits when he overhauled its technical structure. In 2782, Tobin accepted startup funds from his parents to officially incorporate microTech. The company struggled to turn a profit until he partnered with former mentor Aleena Tressler, whose advice led him to hire notable engineers and developers and grant them autonomy over their own projects in the interest of fostering the next great idea. His purchase of the company Empiric Education led directly to Tobin's creation of the first [mobiGlas](gp:01dW3alkmB). Its success ultimately made microTech one of the largest companies in the UEE. Tobin died in 2912, after personally overseeing the construction of [New Babbage](gp:Rw1Zl3vdW7).","g":["microtech (company)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a90eab61-29c1-4b5c-891b-0ff37e05ff9a"},
{"id":"mala","gp":"Rz29NQxqDA","t":"Mala","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Mala is a naturally-occurring psychedelic drug that induces synesthesia in its users. Harvested from the mala fly, when taken in large enough quantities it confuses the cognitive pathways of the brain, causing sensory experiences to cross and mix. Effects vary widely from user to user. Reported experiences include gaining the ability to taste music and colors, see and smell sounds, or hear images. The drug can also dull or alter a user's sense of pain, potentially exposing them to dangerous situations as pain becomes absent or pleasurable.","g":["mala fly","psychedelic drug","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cd8dbd08-e650-47e0-9a82-684393ff1c32"},
{"id":"mantis","gp":"0Gz5vqXlaQ","t":"Mantis","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Mantis is an interdiction spacecraft manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). Designed around the ability to mount a specialized quantum enforcement device, the Mantis is flown by police forces and security concerns to interdict other ships while they are in quantum flight. The system includes a quantum snare capable of pulling targeted ships out of flight and a dampener that prevents nearby spacecraft from re-entering quantum flight. The Mantis often works alongside heavy fighters and other military assets in order to most effectively intercept pirates and black market transports.","g":["stealth","roberts space industries (rsi)","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dae1650d-9600-4bbb-8e02-9b118a4e9503"},
{"id":"marama-helios-2a","gp":"RMNdomKD2Y","t":"Marama (Helios 2a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Marama (Helios 2a) is the moon of [Tangaroa (Helios II)](gp:RX3rnQ3XqM), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Its dense iron and nickel core combined with a very fast orbital period of 4.3 SED contribute to its parent planet's strong tidal forces, sometimes causing waves hundreds of meters high. Like Tangaroa, Marama is highly geologically active, and is dotted with mountains and erupting volcanoes. It has a thin atmosphere of sulfur dioxide.","g":["marama","helios 2a","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","helios system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/27002496-7b59-4072-8f8b-d2b2e30a6d56"},
{"id":"marcus-fayel","gp":"Rw1k2w51XZ","t":"Marcus Fayel","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Marcus Fayel (2719 - 2816) was a [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) expert and religious leader best known as the founder of the [Outsiders](gp:V7dLljjOeL), also called the Sun's Eye Fellowship. Educated at [University of Persei Analytical Research and Quantification](gp:0n1Mz2WmD7) (UPARQ), Fayel was hired by Hatfield & Harding in 2743 to oversee the terraformation of [Leir II](gp:RxnqNaGr8Q). Soon after arriving on the planet, Fayel established his own mining operation without the knowledge of his employers but was otherwise considered a model overseer. In 2803, Hatfield & Harding named Fayel \"Employee of the Year,\" but he declined to receive the award in person. Instead, he sent a vid to the banquet in which he constantly repeated the phrase \"purity of purpose.\" Finally, in 2812, Fayel cut all communication from Leir II and sent out a looped broadcast announcing that the planet's \"purification\" was complete and that he and his followers would be its stewards. Hatfield & Harding dispatched mercenaries to retake the planet, but were rebuffed. Fayel renamed the planet Mya and led his religious order until his death from natural causes in 2816.","g":["outsiders (religion)","sun's eye fellowship","leir ii","mya"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b44c0890-ee6b-46b5-bd18-1b53705aa211"},
{"id":"mariana","gp":"VlMnZv8qY7","t":"Mariana","k":"place","c":["Settlements"],"x":"Mariana, also called Shorebreak by locals, is the capital of [Tangaroa (Helios II)](gp:RX3rnQ3XqM), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Located on and around one of Tangaroa's few permanent islands, it was initially established soon after the system was discovered as a base for scientists to study the system's peculiar main sequence B-type star. The city is known as the unofficial headquarters for the sport of sub-surfing, in which athletes pilot extremely maneuverable submarines on, through, and underneath Tangaroa's towering waves. Today, the city is partially on land and partially underwater, and is protected on all sides by an extensive network of wave breakers.","g":["tangaroa","helios ii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b240c575-d456-49b6-8579-a0b7628235e1"},
{"id":"marie-sante","gp":"RX36PWwe4K","t":"Marie Sante","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Exploration"],"x":"Marie Sante (2504 - 2545?) was a navjumper most notable for her discovery of the [Horus system](gp:bo1JGZpvwZ), which she named after her ship. Born on [Gonn (Oberon I)](gp:VJXAYN81Q5) in 2504, she was the oldest of seven children, and was often left in charge of caring for her siblings while her parents worked in the mines or gambled after work. She ran away from home at age 14, disappearing from public record until her reappearance in 2528 when she disclosed the discovery of the Horus system to the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) government. The extensive planetary charts she provided with this report have led historians to believe that Sante first visited Horus up to a decade earlier, but Sante refused to provide any further information. Her 2542 discovery of a jump point to the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj)-controlled R.il'a system prompted the UPE to add Horus to the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) and close it to non-military personnel. Sante refused to leave. She continued to explore Horus, evading and occasionally clashing with the [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) as they tried to push her out of the system. In 2545, she and her ship vanished without a trace. Sante's ultimate fate remains unsolved, and is a popular subject of stories and documentaries on [Serling (Horus I)](gp:Vy28DwK2a8).","g":["gonn","oberon i","horus system","r.il'a system","human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a1dc62ce-21f9-4ff8-815c-7eabd0f9c6ca"},
{"id":"marisol-belt-terra-belt-beta","gp":"bo13EpQOEZ","t":"Marisol Belt (Terra Belt Beta)","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Marisol belt (Terra belt beta) is an asteroid belt in the [Terra system](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4). It circles the sun beyond the orbit of [Gen (Terra IV)](gp:RMNMv8ekn8). Although it has been actively mined for centuries, it remains rich in basic materials such as iron and carbon compounds.","g":["marisol belt","terra belt beta","terra system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/04c38bd1-2a2b-451e-a1f8-6c173de29543"},
{"id":"marius-messer-iv","gp":"RxNxAgrXZz","t":"Marius Messer IV","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Marius Messer IV (2625-2641) was the only son of [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) [Livia III](gp:01dWwaQkrL) and her husband Daniel Scota, a former pilot. He spent his childhood on Earth (Sol III) with his cousins, [Gammon](gp:0rxrqgDP12) and [Illyana](gp:bZwQBNmWrL). His grandfather [Deacon II](gp:0j46m4BYge) tutored him privately from a young age; Marius would often accompany his mother and Deacon II on their regular tours of the UEE. After attaining his [Equivalency](gp:Vgg7YGdQDY) at age 16, he was accepted to the United Empire of Earth Naval Flight Academy (UNFA). He died alongside his father Daniel in a shuttle crash, when their vessel suffered a catastrophic failure upon atmospheric re-entry over Moscow, Earth. Livia III granted him the honorary title of Imperator before retiring from public life in 2643.","g":["messer dynasty","messer era","uee imperator"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4ec602b2-a4df-440b-93bc-69b540b86b53"},
{"id":"marok","gp":"0qa7v7Q99q","t":"Marok","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"The marok is a large, omnivorous bird that is indigenous to [Branaugh II](gp:RL6524Kx6L). An aquatic animal, it lives the majority of its life in and around rivers, lakes, seas, and other bodies of water. It hunts by diving to catch fish with its long, hooked beak. Corporations purposely introduce genetically modified marok to the environments of [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) worlds to fill ecological niches. This has led to the creation of multiple artificial subspecies that can be recognized by their color morphs and specialized traits. Marok stones, found in the bird's gizzard, have unique conductive properties that make it sought-after for use in computer chips.","g":["bird","branaugh ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1deb4f71-f7e4-482c-8fa2-876b06969346"},
{"id":"mars-sol-iv","gp":"Regn8D76xw","t":"Mars (Sol IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Mars (Sol IV) is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Populous and prosperous, it was the first planet Humans successfully terraformed after a disastrous initial attempt and provided a much needed outlet for their population during a time of crisis on [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB). Its environment was carefully crafted to allow for as much arable land as possible so it could both sustain a self-sufficient colony and grow extra resources to alleviate famines on Earth. The capital, [Port Renatus](gp:RWwZWj9vOZ), is a renowned center of art and culture.","g":["mars","sol iv","habitable","habitable planet","human planet","sol system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a9760159-279c-4a5f-94ae-3653807a39d8"},
{"id":"mars-today","gp":"0OaB2kqeNk","t":"Mars Today","k":"culture","c":["Publications","Human"],"x":"*Mars Today* is a major daily newspaper published in [Port Renatus](gp:RWwZWj9vOZ) on Mars (Sol IV) since the mid-23rd century. It was the first off-world news organization to successfully move from local colonial news reporting into a full featured paper covering distinct cultural and business concerns. Mars Today is still published in hard copy on Mars and is available electronically via [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) throughout the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["news organization","mars","sol iv","news publication"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/16b06da7-10b7-4f3e-a7e0-7a4c8f3b4fc8"},
{"id":"mars-tragedy","gp":"bmNrgKnZ6l","t":"Mars Tragedy","k":"history","c":["History","Human"],"x":"The Mars Tragedy (Mars Disaster, Great Mars Tragedy of '25) was a terraforming disaster that occurred on 13 September 2125. Late in the initial [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) of Mars (Sol IV), an error in the atmospheric processors caused the newly generated oxygen/nitrogen atmosphere to catastrophically dissipate, resulting in the sudden suffocation of 4,876 people. The public outcry against terraforming following the tragedy halted development of the technology for twenty years. In the mid-2150s, better safety protocols and more precise atmospheric processing standards were made standard thanks to data gathered from this event, and Mars was successfully terraformed.","g":["mars","sol iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8998f78e-e60a-40f0-9ec1-ec4d0ce0ed3f"},
{"id":"mars-tragedy-memorial","gp":"V8gJ6nl7Zx","t":"Mars Tragedy Memorial","k":"place","c":["Art"],"x":"The Mars Tragedy Memorial is a monument located near [Port Renatus](gp:RWwZWj9vOZ), Mars (Sol IV) that was constructed to honor the memory of the 4,876 people who died in the Mars [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) disaster of September 13, 2125. It was dedicated in a ceremony by Senator Stephen Nguyen in 2157, who had lost a sibling to the tragedy.","g":["mars tragedy","memorials","mars","sol iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bc9dd3dd-69a8-4361-bb2f-f03299b372fa"},
{"id":"marshall-leon","gp":"bZwQBJmZxE","t":"Marshall Leon","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Marshall Leon (2753-2891) was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) politician who served as [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the United Empire of Earth from 2801 to 2811. Leon started his career in social services in 2774 and worked up to the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) of Reisse (Rhetor III). From there, he was elected as Senator where he served from 2787 to 2793, and then as Diplomatic Secretary of the UEE under Imperator [Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y) from 2793 to 2800. He conceived of the Ark during his time as Diplomatic Secretary, obtaining approval for its construction from the Senate in 2794. During his campaign for Imperator, he was endorsed by Toi on the strength of his diplomatic achievements and his work on the Ark. He attended the opening ceremony for the Ark during his first year in office. When Leon finished his term as Imperator, he joined the Ark's Board of Directors, a position he held until his death.","g":["uee imperator","uee senator","reisse","rhetor iii","uee diplomatic secretary","the ark"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/956786b4-973c-471e-b5f3-52db205d9692"},
{"id":"martian-institute-of-space-technology-mist","gp":"RL67MAJreO","t":"Martian Institute of Space Technology (MIST)","k":"place","c":["Education","Human","Locations"],"x":"The Martian Institute of Space Technology (MIST) is a public research university in [Port Renatus](gp:RWwZWj9vOZ), [Mars (Sol IV)](gp:Regn8D76xw), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Founded in SEY 2221 in response to rapid changes in space technology in the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), MIST places importance on laboratory work, applied science, and other hands-on activities to promote the growth of its students. The institute maintains a complex urban campus that encompasses many well-known laboratories such as the Zemlock Observatory and the Sono and Nyemeto Laboratory. Students and faculty at MIST have won a large number of educational awards over the centuries.","g":["martian institute of space technology","mist","higher education","mars","sol iv","uee higher education","uee education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/48ebcbdd-c455-40b0-b15d-223b7edb6261"},
{"id":"massacre-of-garron-ii","gp":"01dWeqnMr1","t":"Massacre of Garron II","k":"history","c":["History","Human"],"x":"In 2792, [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) sold off the terraforming rights of Garron II to the Bright Worlds Terraforming Group (BWTG). One of the indigenous species, which had shown sentience and was known to both the BWTG and Linton Messer, was exterminated during the terraforming process. An anti-Messer revolutionary group called [Tide](gp:RXlXOpwG6k) obtained footage documenting the atrocity and released it over Spectrum, interrupting broadcasts galaxy-wide. The vids sparked an outrage among the long-oppressed population of the United Empire of Earth (UEE). Subsequent [riots and military action](gp:bE3rKa32P7) led to the end of the 246 year Messer dynasty.","g":["anti-messer revolution","tide (activist group)","messer era","linton messer xi"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2a8308d0-e557-4416-9064-0f042c41b5ff"},
{"id":"mauricio-tusk","gp":"VY4WBM6OZ1","t":"Mauricio Tusk","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Mauricio Tusk (2499-2551) was a law enforcement officer who served in the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) from 2524 to 2541 and then as High-Advocate of the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) from 2541 to 2546. He and High-Secretary [Janis Rezaian](gp:VaZwBAGOBv) publicly criticized then High-General [Ivar Messer](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) for his refusal to compromise with his fellow [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) members. In 2546, after Messer was elected as [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr), he was removed from office when the Tribunal was dismantled. Tusk returned to the Advocacy in 2547. He was killed in action in 2551 while performing a high-risk extraction.","g":["gavin e hurston","tribunal","upe high-advocate"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9e2f29d5-38ba-4cbc-9747-92d0ac1b42ae"},
{"id":"maxox","gp":"VyvYkJrN5z","t":"MaxOx","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"MaxOx is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of personal and spacecraft-mounted weapons. The company was originally formed in the late 28th century to produce medical lasers. Impressed by their laser's power and precision, United Empire of Earth (UEE) government officials contracted with MaxOx founder Burl Hitchens in 2778 to adapt his work to the then-classified weaponized terraforming project codenamed [Vespa](gp:RMXymp7EGn). Hitchens clandestinely sabotaged the project in order to keep such a destructive weapon out of government hands. When Vespa failed to materialize results, the government ended Hitchen's contract and released MaxOx's medical patents to the public. The company's sales drastically impacted, Hitchens pivoted MaxOx into weapon development. Today, MaxOx produces weapons like the NN-series of Neutron Cannons and the 35mm Dredge ballistic cannon.","g":["weapons manufacturer","burl hitchens","reisse","rhetor iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ba9c3eb4-ec4c-4d70-9154-a55278c4b157"},
{"id":"maze","gp":"R5pPk54aQN","t":"Maze","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Maze is a naturally-occurring tranquilizer and psychedelic drug that is harvested from the bark of the mazzi tree. When eaten in large quantities, the psychoactive alkaloids within the bark send users into a near-comatose trance, during which they experience complex audiovisual visualizations that can lead to philosophical, personal, or spiritual insights. [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) in origin, it was traditionally used by warriors once they came of age to help find their path in life. Maze lost its cultural importance after the end of the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv), and today it is mainly used for recreational purposes.","g":["mazzi tree","tranquilizer","psychedelic drug","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/90e2435b-06f3-4be1-bce4-1b2d3d8611ce"},
{"id":"mazzi","gp":"VpMro2z8o1","t":"Mazzi","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The mazzi is a tropical evergreen tree originally from [Jalan (Elysium IV)](gp:VarAXY2zy2), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Preferring moist soil in partial shade, high-humidity, and warm temperatures, it can grow up to five meters in height in ideal conditions. The tree's bark can be cut from the trunk and consumed to induce audiovisual hallucinations in its users. Before the [Tevarin Purge](gp:R6dWB877Nn), use of the bark was a key part of a young [Tevarin's](gp:R6dWB877Nn) coming of age ceremony.","g":["mazzi tree","jalan","elysium iv","trees","maze"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d8cf3253-60ce-4e75-a457-ad1db4a933b5"},
{"id":"medical-emergency-locator-mel","gp":"0QlgNyMa8Q","t":"Medical Emergency Locator (MEL)","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A medical emergency locator (MEL) is a tracking device manufactured by [CureLife](gp:0KxkeN9Oe3) that can be used to trace a person's location in the event of injury, illness, or other dire circumstances. It was included as a part of the uniform of all service members in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military until it was replaced by an improved locator manufactured by [BiotiCorp Limited](gp:RWoe2K4X8a). Now fully phased out of military uniforms, the MEL is still used by the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) and the [UEE Diplomatic Corps](gp:0dXZGgNm1Z).","g":["mel","medical emergency locator","curelife"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/eedb64c0-ef76-4ecb-b099-12a702741096"},
{"id":"medpen","gp":"02k6zXXJj7","t":"MedPen","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A MedPen is a portable, multi-function individual first aid system manufactured by [CureLife](gp:0KxkeN9Oe3). Designed to stabilize wounded patients who are unable to reach a medical facility for immediate treatment, the Pancea MedGel within each MedPen promotes healing in non-fatal injuries by auto-sterilizing the area, stemming blood flow, and stimulating the skin to begin closing over the wound. There are additional types of MedPens that can be used to address specific issues, including but not limited to the OpioPen, used for relieving pain, and the DetoxPen, used to combat drug overdose. Once spent, an empty canister can be discarded.","g":["curelife","medical device"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/80424d2d-6e8b-4860-b2c0-70fa792b21f6"},
{"id":"mentor-rhetor-iv","gp":"RPDlZJeDLX","t":"Mentor (Rhetor IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Mentor is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Rhetor system](gp:0ODlqMJXmP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Located on the far outer edge of Rhetor's green band, Mentor has a harsh, cold year-round climate that keeps its inhabitants mostly indoors. Its academically challenging universities suffer from a higher dropout rate than those on [Reisse (Rhetor III)](gp:0QljXw43Ev) and [Persei (Rhetor II)](gp:0ODlqM6zKO). Mentor is also the site of the UEE's universal seed vaults.","g":["mentor","rhetor iv","rhetor system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/eaed0a25-e431-4e06-be82-9d70e49ca30f"},
{"id":"merchantman","gp":"02BQmpXMYQ","t":"Merchantman","k":"vehicle","c":["Banu","Spacecraft"],"x":"The Merchantman is a freighter commonly seen in the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) and beyond. They are operated as both transport ships and mobile trading posts, with areas aboard ship where traders can display and exchange wares. In [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) culture, Merchantmen are utilized across generations and continually modified, creating a wide variety of different sets of specifications. Although the Merchantman is not as easy to configure as a Human-designed ship, they are valued by Human owners for their reliability and durability.","g":["heavy freight","freight","banu spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ea8ee5ae-ac92-4605-9380-9e5dc9ab17a4"},
{"id":"mercury-sol-i","gp":"V3G8yDedAN","t":"Mercury (Sol I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Mercury (Sol I) is the first planet from the sun of the Sol system, [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). An iron planet, has been extensively mined and stripped of most of its natural resources. When [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) first began mining planets other than their homeworld [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB), hundreds of miners and maintenance workers died on Mercury due to equipment that failed under the heat of the Sun. In 2398, the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) erected a memorial to those who lost their lives during this dangerous time.","g":["mercury","sol i","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","sol system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/221b5e41-93a6-4059-900f-fe4216913861"},
{"id":"mercury-star-runner","gp":"RkZ9m2DO1N","t":"Mercury Star Runner","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Mercury Star Runner is a courier spacecraft designed by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N). Used by the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN) in blockade running operations, the Mercury is a fast, armored runner ship capable of transporting small quantities of valuable goods or storing encrypted information in onboard computers. *The Belligerent Duck*, a Mercury Star Runner operated by criminals, famously escaped the Terra system to Banu space despite a significant amount of pursuers in 2948.","g":["crusader industries","medium data","freight","medium freight","data (role)","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0e1539a8-1f3e-474c-9640-21bff7f5a206"},
{"id":"meridian-transit","gp":"RLMmB9Kl2L","t":"Meridian Transit","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Meridian Transit is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) passenger and commercial transportation company based on Crusader (Stanton II). It manages a large fleet of [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) Genesis-class ships on scheduled flights around the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Meridian has also been licensed for limited operations between the UEE and the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9), with a regular route to Xōl'uu (R.il'a IV).","g":["transport company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7ddea456-eefe-460b-a1a8-9272686eafef"},
{"id":"messer-era","gp":"V8gJ6ZwGqo","t":"Messer Era","k":"history","c":["History","Human"],"x":"The Messer Era (SEY 2546 - 2792) was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) time period during which the Messer family were the absolute rulers of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It started with [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) in 2546, when he seized power of the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) government through a combination of political manipulation and propaganda campaigns to create the position of [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr) in 2546. As the new solitary leader of the UPE, Messer conducted sweeping governmental reforms which transformed the office to that of [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl), a lifelong, hereditary role, beginning a line of succession with his son [Deacon](gp:0j46m4BYge). Though the Messers were popular at first, with each subsequent ruler, their policies became more characterized by draconian enforcement of laws, warmongering, greed, corruption, and abuse of power. The last Messer to hold the position of Imperator, [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq), was executed in his bed by revolutionaries during the [uprising of 2792](gp:bE3rKa32P7).","g":["eras","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e7248614-6f3c-455a-9099-adfabe06a146"},
{"id":"messer-era-war-crimes-trials","gp":"V8gJ66mw9x","t":"Messer Era War Crimes Trials","k":"history","c":["Human","History","Government"],"x":"The Messer Era War Crimes Trials were a series of trials against high-ranking members of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) government for crimes against the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). They lasted from 2793 to 2795. The trials took place on Earth (Sol III) and were broadcast live by [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) news outlets in the system and relayed throughout the UEE. Most officials convicted during these trials were sentenced to life in prison. Many who were found innocent or pardoned of their crimes continued to serve positions in the new UEE government.","g":["uee law","trials","human history"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b8f2979-2131-4938-9d1b-7211037153e7"},
{"id":"micah-zahir","gp":"R5pWGMakx9","t":"Micah Zahir","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Micah Zahir (2460 - 2577) was an independent resource surveyor and landowner most notable for discovering the Oretani system in 2481. Born on [Vann (Croshaw III)](gp:bZkk4l4j2D), Zahir migrated to [Asura (Ferron III)](gp:0qaPo2JOj1) in 2480 to work as a mining scan operator. When he was unable to find employment, Zahir signed on as an escort for supply convoys. Zahir picked up a strange signal during one of these supply runs that he logged to investigate at a later time. When he returned alone to the area, he undertook a thorough search and discovered the [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) to the [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). He named it after his favorite ship from the 2464 vid *Blast Crater*, and used the reward money from the UNE to purchase real estate on [Selene (Vega III)](gp:0qaa69qqNA). At the time of his death in 2577, he was one of the largest landowners in the [Vega system](gp:0jGGODZ6O6).","g":["oretani system","vann","croshaw iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bb657933-be75-424c-8f1a-2418603fad3d"},
{"id":"michelle-saleno","gp":"bZkLx7GxXO","t":"Michelle Saleno","k":"people","c":["People"],"x":"# MICHELLE SALENO\nMichelle \"Sal\" Saleno was a test pilot for the Amecanio Navy and is best known as the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to quantum travel beyond the orbit of [Jupiter](gp:Vy2OMo22wz) and for founding the [999th Test Squadron](gp:0qa16drQN1). A skilled pilot with an intuitive understanding of avionics, her insights into the experimental spacecraft she flew led directly to multiple advances in space travel. Most notably, the changes suggested by Saleno and the members of the 999th to [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) (RSI) enabled the company to successfully complete the [Zeus](gp:VYLd4WxODo), the first civilian ship equipped with a quantum drive. \n\n# EARLY LIFE\n\nBorn in SEY 2096, Saleno was raised in a rural community on [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB). Homeschooled alongside her siblings, she spent her time pursuing whatever subjects of study interested her, particularly physics and mechanical engineering. When she turned fourteen, Saleno learned to fly from her parents, who owned an in-atmosphere agricultural aircraft and performed contract work as crop dusters. They allowed her to take on occasional shifts once they were confident in her abilities, which Saleno would later cite as the start of her lifelong love of flight. She began to take college courses in her spare time, and had attained enough credits and flight experience that by the time she turned 18 that she was accepted into the Amecanio Navy's pilot training program. \n\n# AMECANIO NAVY\n\nSaleno spent the next decade as a fighter pilot in both atmosphere and space. Her flying skills, fast reactions, deep technical knowledge, and daring attitude brought her to the attention of the Admiralty board. In 2124 she was offered a position in the Navy's Test Pilot Training Division. She readily accepted, and was soon evaluating experimental aircraft and spacecraft from both the Navy and private corporations. In 2126, she began working with improved versions of Roberts Space Industries' quantum drive, eventually completing her flight beyond Jupiter's orbit in 2128. \n\nIn 2129, Saleno suffered a concussion when the canopy of her aircraft failed to completely separate during an ejection, and had to spend a month in recovery before she could return to work. During that time, she prepared a report that led directly to significant improvements during the ejection process in the standard issue fighters across the Amecanio fleet. Afterwards, she would become known for incomparable focus on identifying all possible failure points in the craft she was assigned to test. In 2133, her observations on take off and landing led Navy engineers to fix a design flaw in the lift fans of an experimental air to space bomber. \n\n# 999TH TEST SQUADRON\n\nAfter the first full-scale model of their commercial Zeus expedition spacecraft disintegrated during its premiere test flight in 2136, RSI reached out to Saleno for assistance. Saleno saw that once this ship debuted on the civilian market, the Navy would have to rapidly expand to maintain its flight superiority. With the backing of RSI, Saleno proposed that a new squadron be formed to speed the evaluation of cutting-edge spacecraft. The Navy gave their approval, and the 999th Test Squadron was formed. Saleno and her crew spent a year suggesting critical changes to the Zeus, leading RSI to perform a complete overhaul of their hull design. In 2137, Saleno completed her first test flight of the reworked Zeus, and RSI was able to debut the ship on the civilian market in 2140. \n\n# LATER LIFE\n\nSaleno became a media sensation, a position she privately resented for her portrayal as a risk-taker willing to sacrifice herself for the betterment of Humanity. During public appearances, she emphasized that safety was the foremost concern of the 999th and that the completion of the Zeus was a team effort. In 2156, she retired from the Navy and accepted a position as an instructor at a flight school for underprivileged youth.","g":["uee navy","999th test squadron"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/932bc4a8-d71c-44c6-bd02-6f96a91255d2"},
{"id":"microprobe","gp":"0dXEOavWzp","t":"MicroProbe","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"The MicroProbe was a scanner and autonomous probe briefly sold on [Ergo (Nemo III)](gp:VlMYrYzwre) in 2407. Advertised as the next generation in advanced resource detection technology, it saw high early sales after a report was shared on [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) detailing vast stores of natural resources on [Nemo I](gp:RMNOzOLvKW). However, the report was false, and had been written by the creator of the device, conman Marvin Akai Blitz. Local news program *Spectrum News Now: Ergo (SNNE)* delivered an exposé of the tech that prevented further sales before any dangerous expeditions to Nemo I could be launched. In early 2408, sales of the faulty scanner were halted.","g":["marvin akai blitz"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4288dcf4-3042-449c-9ac0-5e1ba6e36d3e"},
{"id":"microtech","gp":"bE3rBB4j7J","t":"microTech (Company)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"microTech is a manufacturer of a variety of electronics, digital displays, software, and computers, including the [mobiGlas](gp:01dW3alkmB) wearable computer. Founded on Earth (Sol III) in SEY 2782 by programmer [Magnus Tobin](gp:RkGZqr8yNQ), it is headquartered in [New Babbage](gp:Rw1Zl3vdW7) on the planet [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1), which the company privately owns. The planet's cold temperature is ideal for the microTech's heat-sensitive computing and manufacturing centers. Widespread use of their products has made it the current largest computer and software developer in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["microtech (planet)","mobiglas","stanton iv","computer manufacturer","spacecraft component manufacturer","electronic consumer goods manufacturer","software company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0f7e17d8-cd43-4f3e-9b89-3ca4d3289f7f"},
{"id":"microtech-stanton-iv","gp":"VYL46xl5Z1","t":"microTech (Stanton IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"# MICROTECH\n\nmicroTech (Stanton IV) is the fourth and farthest planet from the sun in the Stanton system, [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Located at the outer edge of the system's habitable zone, microTech is mostly ice, with some cold-to-temperate areas of tundra. It was purchased from the UEE by the corporation [microTech](gp:bE3rBB4j7J) in the mid-2800s. Its capital, New Babbage, is home to many corporations and startups and is a major center for technological innovation.\n\n# ENVIRONMENT\nMost of microTech is covered in mountains and ice sheets and subject to strong blizzards and ice storms. There are very few liquid bodies of water. Multiple temperate tundra zones exist in areas associated with deep geothermal activity. Camping expeditions and hikes in these greener biomes are popular vacation activities among microTech's full-time population. Cold-hardy plants such as evergreens, wildflowers, grasses, and lichen grow there throughout the year.\n\nThawort, a lichen that grows on microTech and other worlds with arctic climates, is the subject of research for several pharmaceutical startups based in New Babbage. Its antiseptic and antibacterial properties have shown promise in the lab, though the properties are only present in wild-collected specimens. Research to replicate these traits in artificial conditions is ongoing. \n\n# HISTORY\nDiscovered in 2851, Stanton IV is a super-Earth, and one of four planets in the Stanton system's habitable zone. Full development of the system would have taken funds not readily available to the government at the time. After beginning initial [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), the UEE announced the decision in 2865 to sell it and its sibling planets to private interests in order to help pay down its debts and provide a boost to the downturned economy.  \n\nAn early terraforming error resulted in a climate far colder and harsher than initial projections had indicated, leading to multiple debates on the UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) floor regarding the government's ability to sell Stanton IV. However, it was thanks to this error that founder and then-CEO of microTech Magnus Tobin purchased it as the new headquarters for microTech. Tobin sold off land his company had been using for server farms in the leadup to this acquisition. According to a contemporary press release, the \"reliably frigid\" climate of Stanton IV was ideal for keeping their expansive network of servers cool. Tobin personally oversaw the construction of New Babbage, the largest city and now-headquarters of microTech at large. \n# CORPORATE GOVERNANCE \nPlanetary governance is conducted by specialized divisions of the microTech corporation. Population-sustaining departments such as water infrastructure and waste management exist alongside economic ones such as taxation, business licensing, and import/export. Former elected officials or government workers are typically hired for these roles, though those from the private-sector are not barred from selection. Upon their purchase of the planet, microTech upgraded their corporate security force to perform police actions where necessary. Wherever possible, microTech utilizes technology and custom microTech-designed systems and software to automate much of the day-to-day operations, including the enforcement of local laws. As immigration to microTech increases, leaders within microTech have debated the implementation of an eventual population cap. \n\n# CULTURE\nThe city of New Babbage was designed to support the creativity of the highly-skilled workforce needed to drive microTech's future innovation. Areas like the Commons were constructed as creative workspaces, dedicated to providing areas for programmers and engineers to relax, network, and plan. The city's robust nightlife provides an outlet for the workforce's high-pressure crunch times and higher-than-average salaries, and visiting financiers and venture capitalists make regular use of the high-end bars. Inhabitants also like to escape the confines of the city to take part in outdoor cold weather activities. \n\nBleeding-edge technology is a common sight on microTech. Not only due to the company itself, but also the presence of other established tech companies alongside a constantly-cycling roster of startups. Residents who don't keep abreast of the latest advances are generally seen as gauche by their peers, though this outlook varies. Members of the upper-classes of the UEE frequent the markets to secure the newest tech before it officially debuts.","g":["microtech (planet)","stanton iv","habitable planet","habitable","microtech (company)","stanton system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/892ea8dd-7131-48fd-94a7-ebe0ebd03b9e"},
{"id":"midas-fish","gp":"bo1lNKWdA2","t":"Midas Fish","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"# MIDAS FISH \n\nThe Midas fish is an aquatic animal indigenous to the planet [Cassel (Goss II)](gp:RPDy6gqX7Z) in the [Goss system](gp:RxnYdDZj96), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Prized by aquarium enthusiasts for its golden color morph, the Midas fish is a protected species on its home world, and is sometimes poached. A breeding program to replenish their numbers, overseen by Cassel's [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3), has been underway since SEY 2936.\n\n# DESCRIPTION \n\nMidas fish vary from large to small, and have one dorsal fin, four triangle-shaped pectoral, and ventral fins, and an indented tail fin. All Midas fish are protandrous or born male. When they reach around seven Standard Earth Years of age, larger males will change sex, becoming female.\n\nColoration is widely varied, with most wild Midas fish being mixed gray and white with black-tipped tail fins and a gold streak at the corner of both eyes. Pink, orange, white, and black specimens have also been observed. The highly sought gold color morph, characterized by shimmering yellow scales streaked with white, exists in nature in small frequencies. Its prevalence in the hobbyist trade is a product of many generations of selective breeding.\n\n# BEHAVIOR AND ECOLOGY\n\nUsually, Midas fish live in small groups among the warm ocean reefs of Cassel, consisting of one large female and a mature male, along with a few non-breeding immature males. If the female dies, then her reproduction partner will change sex and one of the other males in the group will mature and become her mate. They are herbivorous, and spend most of their time grazing on seagrass, or using their powerful jaws to crush and ingest pieces of algae-coated coral. The polyps along with any coral particulates pass harmlessly through their digestive systems.\n\nWhen it is time to breed, the female will lay eggs in a sheltered area and the breeding male will fertilize them. As the eggs mature over a period of about one week, the group of fish will take turns guarding them from potential predators until they hatch. The fry will disperse after another week of being guarded. They breed yearly, early in their local warm season.\n\n# ILLEGAL PET TRADE\n\nMidas fish are endangered on Cassel. This is partially due to the development of resorts near their habitats, but largely due to over-hunting to supply the pet trade. The capture and trade of wild Midas fish was banned on Cassel in SEY 2927, and in the UEE at large in 2934. Thanks to this ban and Cassel's Golden Touch repopulation project, the Midas fish's numbers have been steadily rising and are expected to reach a non-threatened level in the late 2960s. Captive bred Midas fish remain legal to own and trade.","g":["fish","cassel","goss ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/12eb0199-85d5-4d99-8c3b-a7d3193996bf"},
{"id":"midnight-calathea","gp":"RAX8P8j4Gv","t":"Midnight Calathea","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The midnight calathea is a plant created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke) to survive in extremely low light conditions. As opposed to the green of most plants commonly found on the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) homeworld Earth (Sol III), the midnight calathea's leaves run from deep purple to dark red, and are embossed with blue veins. Its dark color and the altered chlorophyll structure allow the plant to absorb light from the entire visible spectrum.","g":["rayari inc","herbaceous plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/91f03e08-3da7-4dea-88c9-491c93e2810a"},
{"id":"military-reorganiztion-act-of-2793","gp":"ReJa34W5Pw","t":"Military Reorganization Act of 2793","k":"faction","c":["Government","Military","Human"],"x":"The Military Reorganization Act of 2793 is a [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) law that outlined a revision to the command structure of the military. It was written in SEY 2792 in response to the abuses of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792) perpetrated by the Army, Navy, and Marines under direct command of the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl). In lieu of the original [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) position of High-General, under this Act, the UEE High Command was created, a committee of representatives from the three branches of the military to filter and facilitate the orders of the Imperator. Legatus Exceritus represents the Army, Legatus Navium represents the Navy, and Legatus Marinuum represents the Marines.","g":["uee law","uee government","laws"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4009356e-e5ad-4719-96a1-b876ea831712"},
{"id":"militia-mobilization-initiative","gp":"RkZ96m89Jm","t":"Militia Mobilization Initiative","k":"faction","c":["Government","Politics","Human"],"x":"The Militia Mobilization Initiative is a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government program introduced in 2946 to make advanced armaments available for purchase by civilian militias in areas threatened by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO). The official order states that it is intended \"to embolden the general public to help defend the Empire.\" In addition, the initiative offers subsidies for the bulk purchase of weaponry. The [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv)[Eclipse](gp:0NwpZZm6Gr) bomber and [RSI](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) Polaris were made available on the civilian market as part of this effort.","g":["uee government program","uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9fa72038-26d3-47d4-bb3e-87fccaf34b2e"},
{"id":"min-1a","gp":"Vy2ZvDkkzl","t":"Min 1a","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Min 1a is the closest moon to the rogue planet [Min I](gp:RL67MJ9ypd) in the unclaimed Min system. Due to the forces of tidal heating, Min 1a is intensely geologically active, with a network of volcanoes that produce plumes of sulfur that can climb hundreds of kilometers above its surface. Lava flows from the near constant eruptions paint the moon's surface yellow, with subtle streaks of green, white, red, orange, and black. Min 1a sustains a thin atmosphere composed mainly of sulfur dioxide.","g":["min system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5ae4b344-d882-4d89-927c-6b958a31aa9d"},
{"id":"min-1b","gp":"R6dQvNNM7q","t":"Min 1b","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Min 1b is the second moon from the rogue planet [Min I](gp:RL67MJ9ypd) in the [unclaimed](gp:VgExMejDPx) [Min system](gp:VarGZyQ9r2). Unique among known celestial bodies, Min 1b supports life in spite of a total lack of sunlight. The same tidal heating that makes [Min 1a](gp:Vy2ZvDkkzl) violently volcanically active causes geothermal activity on Min 1b, giving it enough internal heat to sustain a liquid water ocean. Additionally, its thick hydrogen atmosphere provides enough of a barrier to prevent too much warmth from escaping, allowing the surface of the ocean to be free from ice in many places. Min 1b is home to countless colonies of bioluminescent bacteria that cluster around hydrothermal vents at the bottom of the ocean, along with some bioluminescent plants. A community formed by researchers interested in studying Min 1b's environment, survivalists, and outlaws drawn to the system's unclaimed status formed in 2816.","g":["min system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6c5d2528-1dfa-4e98-baf1-4312841b8cd7"},
{"id":"min-1c","gp":"V8WpgA9rM1","t":"Min 1c","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Min 1c is the third moon from the rogue planet [Min I](gp:RL67MJ9ypd) in the [unclaimed](gp:VgExMejDPx) [Min system](gp:VarGZyQ9r2). The smallest of the four moons, it has a thin atmosphere of nitrogen and carbon dioxide, and is composed of rocky material and water ices. Like its neighbors, Min 1c experiences tidal heating, though at a low enough level that its tectonic activity is relatively infrequent. In the past, it once had many active volcanoes, enough to possibly have supported an atmosphere that allowed the existence of liquid water. There is a sprawling cavern network beneath its surface.","g":["min system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bd1a268f-9ed1-4d1c-b0a2-e8576f6356c2"},
{"id":"min-1d","gp":"RvlLgp96pY","t":"Min 1d","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Min 1d is the most distant moon from the rogue planet [Min I](gp:RL67MJ9ypd) in the [unclaimed](gp:VgExMejDPx) [Min system](gp:VarGZyQ9r2). Unlike the other moons in its system, it doesn't experience tidal heating, and has no detectable tectonic activity. Its surface is nearly saturated with craters. So many objects have made impact with Min 1d that some craters have overlapped others or formed multi-ringed impact structures. Outlaw groups are known to maintain camps in some of the larger craters.","g":["min system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ebce492a-c99f-49ca-b580-dda902f45340"},
{"id":"min-i","gp":"RL67MJ9ypd","t":"Min I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Min I is the rogue planet that forms the heart of the [unclaimed](gp:VgExMejDPx) [Min system](gp:VarGZyQ9r2). Like other rogue planets, it may have been ejected from its original planetary system, or it may have formed without ever having been gravitationally bound to a star. Its four moons suggest that it may have had its own accretion disk. Although there is no sun to create light, tidal heating generates enough friction in the interiors of Min I's two inner moons to sustain ongoing geological activity, creating conditions that have given rise to life on [Min 1b](gp:R6dQvNNM7q).","g":["min system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/53e8a3a6-9616-44ea-bb04-45aa0b6b24c6"},
{"id":"min-system","gp":"VarGZyQ9r2","t":"Min System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Min system is an unclaimed system of four moons that orbit the rogue planet Min I. Discovered in SEY 2473 by the mining concern the [Hathor Group](gp:R6v8Dg8o6a), it was a company secret until 2672, when the Hathor Group suffered a hack that leaked Min's location. Tall tales began to circulate among outlaw groups about a strange, sunless system haunted by glowing ghosts. Min's existence was officially revealed to the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) in 2702, when [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) agent Hiram Quereshi tracked a smuggling ring through the [Ellis](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ)-Min jump point. The UEE determined that the system was not worth developing and left it unclaimed. The only permanent settlement in Min was established on [Min 1b](gp:R6dQvNNM7q) by researchers, outlaws, and survivalists in 2816.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f793ade8-9144-4c58-8fa6-bf1994a26697"},
{"id":"mining-probe","gp":"VY4WBXqgLW","t":"Mining Probe","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A mining probe is a device that can propel itself through zero gravity environments and latch on to a celestial body in order to collect a sample of it for evaluation. Some mining probes are fully automated, performing analysis and sending results back to their ship of origin without manual interference. Probes are typically used in asteroid or other extraplanetary mining.","g":["mining"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c5493691-5cb8-42fa-8392-b77e4a613b7a"},
{"id":"mira-ngo","gp":"RWoa1mlWdp","t":"Mira Ngo","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Mira Ngo (2891 - present) is Senator of Terra (Terra III) (2936 - present), and the youngest person to have ever been elected to the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ). She was one of the final five candidates running in the 2950 [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) election. A third generation Senator, she has long championed [Transitionalist](gp:0OaylwDmvv) party policies such as relocating the capital of the UEE from Earth (Sol III) to Terra. On 10 October 2949, the day she announced her candidacy for Imperator, her home was burglarized. Shortly thereafter personal files were released that revealed ties between the Ngo family and multiple privately-owned Terra construction companies. In addition to the relocation of the UEE's capital, her campaign promises included the restoration and preservation of historic buildings on Earth, a restructure of funding to [Synthworld](gp:RLMmAnr4gj) and the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) war effort, and criminal justice reforms to ease jail sentences for people convicted of nonviolent crimes.","g":["uee senator"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9f782ced-6ce8-4fab-a078-0e1958dec6fb"},
{"id":"mirai","gp":"Vy2B1o6gn6","t":"Mirai","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human","Spacecraft"],"x":"Mirai is a subsidiary of [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) (MISC) that develops and manufactures high-performance spacecraft. In 2833, then-CEO Kori Desmon created a specialized team within MISC to help it expand its portfolio beyond the industrial craft that it was known for. The team's first creation, the Daedalus, went on to compete in the [Murray Cup](gp:bE3r71yZ87) and placed third in the 2853 race. In 2910, MISC's groundbreaking agreement with the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) granted the company access to new technology, leading the team to design the [Razor](gp:RkZ96DxvgB). The ship's success resulted in MISC branching the experimental team into its own division, which they named Mirai. The Fury fighter, developed with a mixture of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) technology, was the brand's market debut.","g":["spacecraft manufacturer","misc","saisei","centauri iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ca7508f7-9c2e-443d-8f57-d9826261b214"},
{"id":"miranda-sol-7a","gp":"V3GY9Q4rWA","t":"Miranda (Sol 7a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Miranda (Sol 7a) is a moon of [Uranus (Sol VII)](gp:0rxOX3eKQ2), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Round and tidally locked, it has an unusually high orbital inclination that suggests in the past that it was in orbital resonance with [Umbriel (Sol 7c)](gp:0qaj9AgLqq) for a period of time. Although massive enough to have achieved a round shape, the topography of its surface is so dramatic that some scientists theorize that it was partially shattered during its formation period.","g":["miranda","sol 7a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"]},
{"id":"mobiglas","gp":"01dW3alkmB","t":"mobiGlas","k":"vehicle","c":["Science and Technology","Human"],"x":"The mobiGlas is a multi-purpose mobile computing device made by [microTech](gp:bE3rBB4j7J) and first released in SEY 2818. It has strong hardware and software capabilities that facilitate accessing spectrum, viewing vids, organizing information, downloading and storing data, personal communications, and a variety of other functions. The device is ubiquitous enough in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) that the government conducts its census via mobiGlas. Competitors have released their own versions of the technology under different names; however, the word \"mobiGlas\" has entered the standard lexicon as a genericized term.","g":["personal computer","microtech (company)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6d6a7672-8e21-42f8-917b-3b48f9b5fefd"},
{"id":"mole","gp":"0rxZXQBB3a","t":"MOLE","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The MOLE is a medium mining spacecraft developed by [Argo Astronautics](gp:0KnA1vvJEM). Its name is an acronym of the ship's primary function as a multi-operator laser extractor. Designed to support a crew of up to four, the MOLE can be used for longer-term mining missions in remote areas of space. It is equipped with twenty-four mineral pods that can be detached and delivered to cargo vessels or shipping centers when full, and has three mining stations that can be operated independently of one another. In 2949, the MOLE debuted at the [Intergalactic Aerospace Expo (IAE)](gp:R4jpEgezde) and was featured on an episode of [Whitley's Guide](gp:V8WgdOP8px).","g":["mining","argo astronautics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/559a80ae-d02f-44e6-8fb1-c68c8f87f0c9"},
{"id":"monox-pyro-ii","gp":"0jGdgLEjqJ","t":"Monox (Pyro II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Monox (Pyro II) is the second planet from the sun of the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Nicknamed \"Monox\" for the deadly carbon monoxide in its atmosphere, it has a temperate climate, and was seen as a viable candidate for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) shortly after its discovery. However, its proximity to the system's volatile sun made it dangerous for [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) habitation, and the[ United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) refused to clear it for terraformation, instead allowing corporations to harvest its natural resources. Undeterred by the potential risk, outlaws eventually took up residence on the planet when the last corporations pulled out of Pyro in the 26th century.","g":["monox","pyro ii","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","pyro system"]},
{"id":"mpuv-1c-argo-cargo","gp":"0rqzN9vek9","t":"MPUV-1C (Argo Cargo)","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The MPUV-1C (\"Argo Cargo\") is a single-pilot utility spacecraft manufactured by [Argo Astronautics](gp:0KnA1vvJEM). Built for the loading and unloading of cargo containers from orbital spacecraft and installations, the MPUV-1C's design was based on Argo's [Orbital Utility Craft (OUC)](gp:0rqz57XoZY), their first foray into shipbuilding. The MPUV-1C allows larger cargo ships that would otherwise be incapable of making planetary landfall to transfer goods to orbital waystations, as well as planetside.","g":["mpuv-1c","argo cargo","light freight","mpuv","argo astronautics","freight","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/202b16fe-b031-491d-a983-80eaa02443ea"},
{"id":"mpuv-1p-argo-personnel","gp":"0j46je17PK","t":"MPUV-1P (Argo Personnel)","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The MPUV-1P (\"Argo Personnel\") is a single-pilot utility spacecraft manufactured by [Argo Astronautics](gp:0KnA1vvJEM). Intended for the loading and unloading of personnel from orbital spacecraft and installations, the MPUV-1P is a variant of the [MPUV-1C](gp:0rqzN9vek9) cargo ferry, replacing the 1C's cargo area with a habitable space. This allows it to shuttle passengers between space and planetside locations.","g":["mpuv-1p","mpuv","argo personnel","argo astronautics","transport","passenger transport","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/745782ad-a716-4af5-a056-383710a0ba14"},
{"id":"mule","gp":"bo1ryE6MkA","t":"Mule","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation"],"x":"The Mule is a transport vehicle manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed). Designed for the hauling of cargo over rough terrain, the Mule has six heavy-duty wheels that allow it to tackle unexpected obstacles. In addition to its cargo bed, it has external racks that can carry up to six small boxes, and a forklift that can be used for extra mobile storage.","g":["transport","freight transport","drake interplanetary","human vehicle"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/72d9f5ea-5671-48d1-97a1-bcbcf453e6b8"},
{"id":"municipal-transit-line-musit","gp":"0KnAr128Q3","t":"Municipal Transit Line (Mu-Sit)","k":"place","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Municipal Transit Line (Mu-Sit) is a transit system located in the city of Quinton on Angeli (Croshaw II) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Developed under a government contract by [Argo Astronautics](gp:0KnA1vvJEM), it was based on the company's radial networked transit hub in Port Renatus, Mars (Sol IV). While it is functionally identical to the Prime Transit Monorail, also developed by Argo, the Municipal Line covers a significantly larger area.","g":["municipal transport line (mu-sit)","public transportation","argo astronautics","quinton","angeli","croshaw ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fa18b68a-6373-4965-90b0-b0017ae93154"},
{"id":"murray-cup","gp":"bE3r71yZ87","t":"Murray Cup","k":"history","c":["Sports","Human"],"x":"The Murray Cup is a spacecraft race held annually at the end of racing season in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ). Dating back to 2467, when [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) workers of Gaia Planet Services unofficially raced one another to pass the time, the Murray Cup is now the most prestigious event in modern racing. It utilizes natural and artificial obstacles to create two challenges. In the Classic race, pilots are ranked on their speed and navigational skill. In the Blitz race, pilots are allowed to engage in limited combat to disable their competitors.","g":["spacecraft racing","ellis system","racing"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9ceaad45-9503-4c08-af9b-51400db2d61d"},
{"id":"misc","gp":"bE3rB7YJDv","t":"Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC) is a spacecraft manufacturer headquartered in [Fujin City](gp:RxNxAeyOq6) on [Saisei (Centauri III)](gp:Vy22NQJ1q6). Founded in SEY 2805 after a merger between Hato Electronics Corporation and the Musashi Lifestyle Design Unit spinoff of Acorn Limited, MISC primarily produces transport and industrial utility spacecraft, such as the [Freelancer](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/freelancer) and the [Starfarer](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/starfarer), but has also been expanding into the racing market with the [Razor](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/razor). MISC was one of the first corporations in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) to sustain a tech-trade partnership with the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj).","g":["musashi industrial and starflight concern","misc","spacecraft manufacturer","saisei","acorn limited","hato electronics corporation","centauri iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2ce19a43-1fd0-476c-a13f-346b4f16a361"},
{"id":"muse-simpod","gp":"bEzladeon8","t":"Muse Simpod","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"The Muse Simpod is an virtual reality game system and immersive simulation device manufactured by [microTech](gp:bE3rBB4j7J). Most commonly used for playing games, the Simpod can also be used for educational purposes in a wide variety of fields. Specific classes of the Simpod are utilized by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military for flight and combat training.","g":["microtech (company)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4de7bd7d-12f5-4416-8824-505934b5e7f0"},
{"id":"mustang-alpha","gp":"bZwQJN6WYB","t":"Mustang Alpha","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Mustang Alpha is a single-seat civilian spacecraft in the Mustang line of spacecraft developed and sold by [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34). It was developed to the specifications of company founder and CEO [Silas Koerner](gp:V8gJMXjE8o), who intended it to offer radical competition to [Roberts Space Industries'](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) Aurora [line](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/aurora-series) of ships. The Alpha can be purchased with an optional cargo expansion. Mustang variants include the [Mustang Beta](gp:Vgg7rQ7X3N) touring craft, the [Mustang Gamma](gp:V3qgXqrY6W) racing ship and the [Mustang Delta](gp:R56nQ6WpBm) militia spacecraft.","g":["mustang series","consolidated outland","freight","light freight","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e47dcaba-35a7-4bd7-af98-6d33ddb78962"},
{"id":"mustang-alpha-vindicator","gp":"0QxYZx1ABL","t":"Mustang Alpha Vindicator","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Mustang Alpha Vindicator is a limited-edition variant of the Mustang civilian spacecraft developed by [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34). Built to commemorate CitizenCon 2948, the Alpha Vindicator comes with a unique gray, black, and yellow paint scheme. It is smaller and lighter than the [Mustang Alpha](gp:bZwQJN6WYB), and can be outfitted with the same cargo expansion, allowing it to transport light freight.","g":["consolidated outland","mustang series","light freight","freight","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bba1d127-a289-467d-ac77-a7b1589c9066"},
{"id":"mustang-beta","gp":"Vgg7rQ7X3N","t":"Mustang Beta","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Mustang Beta is a variant of the Mustang civilian spacecraft developed by [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34). Officially classified as a touring and exploration ship, the Mustang Beta is an extended-range variant of the [Mustang Alpha](gp:bZwQJN6WYB) with a series of updates to appeal to cost-conscious explorers. Consolidated Outland ships the Mustang Beta with a hardened Tarsus Leaper jump engine as well as a small rear cabin with room for amenities and life support equipment.","g":["pathfinder","consolidated outland","mustang series","expedition","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2f18188d-c002-41aa-95d6-f0ce73afbc0b"},
{"id":"mustang-delta","gp":"R56nQ6WpBm","t":"Mustang Delta","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Mustang Delta is a variant of the Mustang civilian spacecraft developed by [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34). Marketed primarily to militia users in less protected areas of space, the Mustang Delta trades some of the speed and maneuverability of the base model in exchange for the addition of larger main guns and a pair of missile hardpoints.","g":["light fighter","consolidated outland","mustang series","fighter"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/afc26aa6-679f-4fdc-aa8b-938a5dcf6168"},
{"id":"mustang-gamma","gp":"V3qgXqrY6W","t":"Mustang Gamma","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Mustang Gamma is a variant of the Mustang civilian spacecraft developed by [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34). The first racer variant of the Mustang, it was later followed by the limited edition [Mustang Omega](gp:0qnNXnDxQO). Consolidated Outland engineers reduced the overall weight of the base model for the Gamma and upgraded the standard engines. The redesign includes a general improvement in maneuverability over the standard Mustang in exchange for an overall reduction in missiles and guns.","g":["mustang series","racing","consolidated outland","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4e6c2703-4c39-48e8-9565-058fb372f5e4"},
{"id":"mustang-omega","gp":"0qnNXnDxQO","t":"Mustang Omega","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Mustang Omega is a variant of the Mustang civilian spacecraft developed by [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34). Like the [Mustang Gamma](gp:V3qgXqrY6W), the Omega is focused primarily on high performance racing with the addition of an upgraded fuel intake. The ship was produced via a partnership with [Accelerated Mass Design](gp:VaZwQNE48v), who were responsible for additional tuning and styling of the vehicle. Omegas are manufactured with a unique red paint scheme developed by underground artist [Sektor8](gp:RwZBLBJvY6).","g":["mustang series","racing","consolidated outland","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/aed95b2a-855e-43ab-a5df-1edd252644b9"},
{"id":"muymuy","gp":"0GxlOg6MKo","t":"MuyMuy","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"MuyMuy is a casualwear clothing brand that utilizes natural fabrics in its designs. An employee-owned company, it was founded by a group of knitters who had gained local fame for their sweaters, handcrafted from locally-sourced ma'xy.un wool. The company is committed to the use of non-artificial materials in its products, and sources the majority of its supplies from farms located on [Saisei (Centauri III)](gp:Vy22NQJ1q6), the same planet as its company headquarters.","g":["clothing manufacturer","saisei","centauri iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/08a960a0-b12a-481e-967c-09ccc5cfb930"},
{"id":"mya-leir-ii","gp":"RxnqNaGr8Q","t":"Mya (Leir II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Mya is the second planet from the sun of the [Leir system](gp:0Ql7xwzmzL). Although it was discovered in 2677, it remained undeveloped until 2743, when [Galor Messer IX](gp:VyvYAGKxAz) sold the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and mining rights of Leir II to Hatfield & Harding to fund his long-term project to redesign UEE government buildings. The company hired University of [Persei Analytical Research and Quantification (UPARQ)](gp:0n1Mz2WmD7) terraforming expert [Dr. Marcus Fayel](gp:Rw1k2w51XZ) to lead the project. Over the next few decades, Fayel oversaw operations while running a clandestine mining operation of his own and cultivating a base of devoted followers. In 2812, Fayel abruptly ended all communication from the system to Hatfield & Harding and the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) at large. Subsequent attempts by the company to retake the planet were violently rebuffed by what turned out to be a cult with Fayel at the helm that called themselves the [Sun's Eye Fellowship](gp:V7dLljjOeL). They renamed the planet Mya. Now known as the Outsiders for their philosophy of remaining away from the \"impure\" influence of the UEE, this fringe society conducts trade primarily with the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) in order to remain \"pure.\"","g":["mya","leir ii","leir system","habitable","habitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f1625142-4dbf-40d7-a1c2-c17512b0d56e"},
{"id":"najita","gp":"VgEElmgYm3","t":"Najita","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Najita is the most populous city on Keene (Kilian VII). A coastal city, Najita was originally constructed to work in harmony with the sprawling green hills that surround it. This balance was upset in the 2800s when increasing [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) raids in the Caliban system frightened many of its residents to flee to Keene for military protection. Prefabricated residences were erected in the surrounding hills to house the swelling population. These new neighborhoods became permanent after the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) in 2884. Prominent spacecraft manufacturers [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) and [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) maintain showrooms in Najita.","g":["keene","kilian vii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3820dfca-085a-4443-b8b8-a55908023904"},
{"id":"nautilus","gp":"VDoPW99Wr5","t":"Nautilus","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Nautilus is a minelayer and minesweeper spacecraft developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) and utilized by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). It is capable of deploying several different types of mines for both offensive and area-denial purposes along simultaneous vectors in 3D space. Its command deck allows the monitoring and activation of these weapons. A model of the Nautilus has recently become available on the civilian market for private concerns seeking protection for space-based assets like stations or mining claims.","g":["minelayer","aegis dynamics","military spacecraft","human spacecraft","minesweeper"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d29510cd-1de6-411e-8668-660659100dcb"},
{"id":"nav-e7","gp":"R9BwgXdB72","t":"Nav-E7 Gadgets","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Nav-E7 Gadgets is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) spacecraft component manufacturer that produces a wide range of equipment, such as scanner and radar systems, docking collars, and passenger seats. They maintain a contract with [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) to outfit their [Freelancer](gp:RvgzWy7o6v) line of ships with fuel tanks and long-range scanners.","g":["spacecraft component manufacturer","earth","sol iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/56c00167-d2e2-4024-8504-57635d5ea02b"},
{"id":"navy-surplus","gp":"bZklxv25mL","t":"Navy Surplus","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Navy Surplus is a clothing brand that specializes in reselling goods that were made in excess or are no longer being used by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military. A private company, it is the official reseller for the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), and handles the removal of all official decorations and markings from former Navy items before distributing them to consumers. While the majority of its stock does come from the Navy, they do feature goods from the other military branches and various security forces. It also produces clothing of its own design that was inspired by the UEE military.","g":["clothing reseller","clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/151d761f-4960-4569-b694-1146cedd4ece"},
{"id":"neer","gp":"VlMYK22lw7","t":"Ne'er","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Tevarin"],"x":"Ne'er is a majority-[Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) town on [Branaugh II](gp:RL6524Kx6L) in the unclaimed [Branaugh system](gp:VJX9mlar4n). \n\nAfter surveyors for the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) determined that Branaugh II was not a good [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) candidate, they abandoned the structures they lived in while evaluating the planet. A few years after they left, a group of [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) claimed the outposts and turned them into dwellings. More Tevarin arrived over time and more structures were built. Eventually the area became the planet's main trading hub.","g":["branaugh ii","tevarin settlement","towns","tevarin town","independent settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/445ff7f7-24f0-4499-8cd3-47929f2aae3f"},
{"id":"neal-socolovich","gp":"VJX7vxG2BG","t":"Neal Socolovich","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Neal Socolovich (2373 - 2474) was a General in the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q), and a key figure in the negotiation of the [Banu-Human Interstellar Peace and Trade Accord](gp:RzPoJ1aP4z), the first interspecies treaty in Human history. Born on [Angeli (Croshaw II)](gp:0QlxqwG14Q), he joined the UNE Army in 2390. He was promoted to the rank of General in 2415 after completing two deployments to the [Banshee system](gp:0Gx4BENmKg), where he gained a reputation for his ability to settle conflicts with outlaws without opening fire. In 2430, General Socolovich was assigned a command post in the newly discovered [Davien system](gp:Rz2g71YlkY). Historians credit his thoughtful leadership during [Banu-Human First Contact](gp:VY4Wnv7ZgW) in 2438 for ensuring that [Humanity's](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) initial encounter with another civilization was a peaceful one. Upon his retirement in 2441, he purchased a plot of land on his home planet and entered the winemaking business. He passed away in 2474.","g":["banu-human first contact","angeli","croshaw ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/05b76a0c-30c0-4855-9afc-a59a3f98d89f"},
{"id":"nedila","gp":"0QlmN2mla5","t":"Nedila","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human","Tevarin"],"x":"Nedila is a small town on [Jalan (Elysium IV)](gp:VarAXY2zy2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) located in a rocky area south of the planet's capital [Gemma](gp:V7gM71L7mk). Many of its inhabitants are water farmers, and their harvests are distributed to the major population centers on Jalan. The town's natural hot springs were once used by ancient [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) as a popular public bath.","g":["jalan","elysium iv","towns","uee towns"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5f06ae76-5e0d-4a0b-be2c-636e69ced715"},
{"id":"nemo-3a","gp":"RX3jvjEBZq","t":"Nemo 3a","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Nemo 3a, nicknamed the \"Space Whale\" by locals, is the moon of [Ergo (Nemo III)](gp:VlMYrYzwre). A captured asteroid, it is oblong in shape with one end tapering into a smaller one. The silhouette is said to resemble a whale, an ocean mammal indigenous to the planet Earth (Sol III) but not found on Ergo. Local businesses have built a tourist industry around the moon, and sell souvenirs ranging from novelty t-shirts to replicas of the Space Whale.","g":["ergo moon","nemo iii moon","nemo system","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","uee moon","nexus i"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4613123f-466d-48c9-88f2-6a277478e774"},
{"id":"nemo-i","gp":"RMNOzOLvKW","t":"Nemo I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nemo I is a protoplanet that orbits closest to the star of the [Nemo system](gp:R6d454E3Pw), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). An extremely thin atmosphere of oxygen, sodium, and hydrogen surrounds it, essentially identical to the vacuum of space. In 2407, a scanning device advertised as the next-gen in resource-detection technology called the [MicroProbe](gp:0dXEOavWzp) delivered false reports detailing vast stores of untapped minerals under the protoplanet's surface. The local news published an exposé of the shoddy technology before any prospectors could attempt to excavate.","g":["nemo system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4413570a-03a7-40d1-961c-c8e643f0708e"},
{"id":"nemo-ii","gp":"V3GOdOYENj","t":"Nemo II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nemo II is the second planet from the sun of the [Nemo system](gp:R6d454E3Pw), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Over the millennia, countless meteor strikes have impacted the surface of Nemo II, creating a visually dynamic landscape of craters and mountains. In the distant past, it was volcanically active, as evidenced by its ancient lava flows and calderas. It has a relatively robust atmosphere of carbon dioxide, oxygen, and sulfur dioxide that is in the process of dissipating due to a lack of replenishment sources.","g":["nemo system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fc52a9b2-55c9-460d-9ec5-3a58e8639787"},
{"id":"nemo-system","gp":"R6d454E3Pw","t":"Nemo System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Nemo system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) with three planets and an F-type main sequence star. Officially discovered in SEY 2364 by Dae-ho Ochoa of [NemoCo](gp:0rxZpeoD2z), the system's provenance came under question when [Tadmor Terraforming Concern](gp:VarG6NEaDv) filed a lawsuit claiming that Ochoa had discovered the system in 2362 during his time working as a security contractor for their company, and had quit Tadmor in order to keep the discovery to himself. However, the lawsuit was dismissed due to a lack of evidence. The ocean world [Ergo (Nemo III)](gp:VlMYrYzwre) is the system's only populated planet, with so few landmasses that its inhabitants have built their cities on artificial islands.","g":["uee system","tadmor terraforming concern"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1d4033cf-d206-42a4-b9be-7527ca0f6bfb"},
{"id":"nemoco","gp":"0rxZpeoD2z","t":"NemoCo","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"NemoCo is a former [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and mining corporation that is credited with the discovery of the [Nemo system](gp:R6d454E3Pw) in 2364. Founded by Jawahir Norman, Sandeep Ellis, Demont Mau, and Dae-ho Ochoa, it obtained most of its early equipment from the Tadmor Terraforming Concern when the company was struggling with legal problems. Soon after, NemoCo found a jump point in the Fora system and named the new system Nemo, an acronym of the founders' surnames. The company was prosperous for many years thanks to the vast oil reserves on [Ergo (Nemo III)](gp:VlMYrYzwre). However, in 2704 NemoCo went bankrupt while attempting to convert outdated oil rigs into tourist destinations.","g":["mining company","terraforming company","human company","nemo iii","ergo","tadmor terraforming concern"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/27250863-08c4-4e8b-9248-1759c8a75866"},
{"id":"neo-taurii","gp":"RegWPqnepY","t":"Neo Taurii","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Neo Taurii is a city on [Kampos (Ellis IV)](gp:RAXxrxr7M5) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Founded in the early 2800s, it was built along the coast of the Sorghum Sea, where the temperature stays comfortable most of the year. Buildings erected in Neo Taurii are constructed low to the ground and out of concrete and stone-composites to withstand Kampos' high gravity. Graduate students and xenobiologists often pass through Neo Taurii to study the unique ocean life found in the waters of Kampos.","g":["kampos","ellis iv","uee city","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1ce21fea-343e-487f-a4b7-efae66fa2220"},
{"id":"neonazacyclicdienorthoamphetamine-neon","gp":"0NjXvzNdp4","t":"Neonazacyclicdienorthoamphetamine (Neon)","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Neonazacyclicdienorthoamphetamine, more commonly known as neon, is an empathogen–entactogen with slight hallucinogenic and stimulant properties. It was first developed to help treat symptoms related to complex post-traumatic stress disorder (C-PTSD). When used as prescribed, it can reduce the negative self-beliefs and hypervigilance associated with C-PTSD. When taken recreationally, it induces feelings of euphoria, increased self-confidence, empathy for others, and inner peace. It also provides a slight boost to the nervous system, enhancing the physical sensations of its users and creating visual and tactile hallucinations. At high doses, it can lead to poor motor control, an increased heart rate, paranoia, and insomnia.","g":["neonazacyclicdienorthoamphetamine","neon","empathogen-entactogen","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3a48aa6c-1594-4e03-9376-a81f46aad87a"},
{"id":"neptine-sol-viii","gp":"RX3wGrAoW1","t":"Neptune (Sol VIII)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Neptune (Sol VIII) is the eighth planet from the sun of the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The densest of the Sol system's gas and ice giant planets, its atmosphere contains high proportions of ice and traces of hydrocarbons. Roughly every two-and-a-half centuries SEY, Neptune and [Pluto (Sol IX)](gp:0qa1Zo37jk) swap orbital positions for about 20 years.","g":["neptune","sol viii","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","sol system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/72f76ee5-ca16-4ab8-a2a1-8b3fbac25457"},
{"id":"nessa-park","gp":"0j46jmMdOe","t":"Nessa Park","k":"place","c":["Locations","Government","Human"],"x":"Nessa Park is a large public park located at the center of Fujin City on Saisei (Centauri III). The park was established and is maintained by a coalition of local companies including [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) and Astro Armada to provide a recreational space for the large number of workers employed in heavy industry in and around the city. Nessa Park is noted for being a particularly well-cultivated park, and features a variety of native flora and fauna. Public events and music festivals are regularly held in Nessa Park.","g":["uee public park","fujin city","saisei","centauri iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/93d0dbc8-8217-44da-b7fa-433782f22d70"},
{"id":"neville-lott","gp":"VlMgQm7qqM","t":"Neville Lott","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Neville Lott (2851 - 2917) was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) serial killer who hunted, captured, dissected, and dismembered seven hikers in the Tecuya Mountains in Vastac, [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) during the 2880s. After losing his twin and parents in the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) in 2884, Lott, heavily burned and injured, was evacuated to Terra. Through his rehabilitation, Lott showed signs of extensive psychological trauma based on the horrific violence he had witnessed during the attack. He disappeared soon after his release from the hospital and was not heard of until several hikers went missing. When captured by [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) agents in 2891, they determined that his modus operandi was to seek out potential targets by posing as a hiker and joining people on the trail. He would then return to his potential victim's campsite at night wearing a mask stitched from a gunny sack, abduct them to his long-term hideout in the mountains, and dissect them alive. Lott refused to seek any kind of insanity plea at his trial and was convicted without presenting a defense. He died in prison in 2917.  \n\nIn her book *Unspeakable Evil*, Paula Qi presented evidence from childhood associates that Lott exhibited homicidal tendencies before his trauma on Caliban, and has criticized popular dramatizations of his crimes such as 2902 slasher vid *The Hill Horror* for implying that the events on Caliban turned him into a killer.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/72f78cdb-ac08-4aec-ac91-c15102fe87f5"},
{"id":"new-astuin","gp":"VlMM6OowNY","t":"New Austin","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"New Austin is a city on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), and is one of the planet's initial colonization points. While a city of industry, the factories of New Austin are constructed to protect the natural beauty that surrounds it by blending into the environment as seamlessly as possible. Businesses such as [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) maintain headquarters there, taking advantage of the lower cost of real estate compared to that of Terra's capital city [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv). Its most famous landmark is the Old Hall, a former [United Resource Workers](gp:V7dPXPjeBn) meeting area that is situated in the city center.","g":["uee city","terra system","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c922bd87-f6e0-454e-878a-518757f013c3"},
{"id":"new-babbage","gp":"Rw1Zl3vdW7","t":"New Babbage","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"New Babbage is the largest city on [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1) and home to [microTech's](gp:bE3rBB4j7J) main headquarters. Construction of New Babbage was personally overseen by company founder Magnus Tobin, whose goal was to make the city an ideal working environment for the technological innovators at his company. The New Babbage Interstellar Spaceport, situated next to a frozen lake, transports visitors via the MT MetroLoop rapid transit to locations like creative workspace the Commons and the Aspire Grand skyscraper. Many public spaces in New Babbage are under domes to protect inhabitants from the perpetually cold weather.","g":["uee city","cities","microtech (planet)","stanton iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/42ec9fd7-defd-4df3-b28d-4bf60ddf10f8"},
{"id":"new-corvo","gp":"RWwZqmP1w4","t":"New Corvo","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"New Corvo is a city on Aremis (Vega II), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Initially settled by members of the UEE military, it has since become Aremis' most populous urban center. Most spacecraft entering and leaving Aremis first pass through New Corvo to be processed. The city has been noted for its vibrant art and culinary scenes. Though it was devastated in a 2945 [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)[attack](gp:0Gz5mkprmg), New Corvo is on the path to recovery, and is currently experiencing a boom in population growth and in construction noted for its architectural experimentation.","g":["aremis","vega ii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/693d38fd-b43e-4ea1-b8e4-e4de03e33c54"},
{"id":"new-junction","gp":"V3G53AXDgY","t":"New Junction","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"New Junction is a city on [Lo (Corel III)](gp:VarAoYEQYd) in the [Corel system](gp:R9vQnko7Y2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Situated on the plains of the equatorial Quoph region, the city is hot year-round and suffers from frequent dust storms. To cope with these hostile conditions, nearly all of the buildings are fitted with extra insulation and atmospheric filtering to help maintain air quality and temperature. [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) traveling between the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) and the UEE must visit Lo to get their cargo inspected before being allowed to cross the border.","g":["cities","uee city","lo","corel iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d31c21f9-f79b-45b1-a6fa-5bbd7b4375e1"},
{"id":"new-united","gp":"RAdjeJe5Y7","t":"New United","k":"culture","c":["Publications","Human"],"x":"*New United* is one of the oldest news organizations in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Founded in the 2100 as the *United Times*, it had a reputation of mostly objective reporting with a slight conservative bias. It was renamed *United Times/Tribune* after a merger in 2438, later shortened to *United/Tribune* in 2638. One of many news organizations to become a propaganda outlet during the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo), it rebranded itself to *New United* in 2792 to distance itself from its past. Today, *New United* has regained its reputation for objectivity.","g":["news organization","news publication","united times","united times/tribune","united/tribune"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/83f44054-ca53-4a4b-a2b2-1f3c75dacbd8"},
{"id":"nexus-i","gp":"RPDlZz53qq","t":"Nexus I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nexus I is a protoplanet in the [Nexus system](gp:RWoj8pnGma), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). With an orbital speed of roughly 47 kilometers per second, it completes its circuit around its sun in 164 Standard Earth Days. Because of its dangerously high surface temperature, it has largely been left alone by surveyors. Its black and reddish outer crust is known to contain a large concentration of carbon.","g":["nexus system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/287cc8f8-b889-49f1-b1f7-49f9834fe00d"},
{"id":"nexus-ii","gp":"RegKl43g9M","t":"Nexus II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nexus II is the second planet from the sun of the [Nexus system](gp:RWoj8pnGma), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A world with a dense, nitrogen-rich atmosphere, it was used by the then-[United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) as a testing ground to develop new [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) technology to use on smog planets. The UNE's failure to achieve this goal is partially what led to its decision to sell exclusive mining rights to the [Hathor Group](gp:R6v8Dg8o6a).","g":["nexus system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0e188013-1fb4-4270-a006-22b6b89f1248"},
{"id":"nexus-iii","gp":"0QljXA8d49","t":"Nexus III","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Nexus III is a naturally habitable terrestrial planet in the [Nexus system](gp:RWoj8pnGma), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Once the central hub of the [Hathor Group](gp:R6v8Dg8o6a), former owners of exclusive mining rights to Nexus, the planet was inhabited by squatters and outlaws when the company abandoned the system in 2672. It remained a stronghold for smugglers, pirates, and others until 2931, when the UEE Navy launched an operation to retake the system and established a forward operating base on Nexus III. The UEEN maintains strict control of the world and only permits authorized visitors.","g":["nexus system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c439b537-aefd-499c-a80d-1c70eddf16e0"},
{"id":"nexus-system","gp":"RWoj8pnGma","t":"Nexus System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Nexus system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that consists of one protoplanet, three terrestrial planets, a gas giant, an asteroid belt, and an A-type main sequence star. Discovered in SEY 2445 by [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) Navy (UNEN) pilot Dominic Thapa, its existence was initially kept secret from the public due to its only known jump point connection to Cathcart, which was a restricted military system at the time. After [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) [Nexus IV](gp:0dXE5egx98), the UNE suffered a budget shortfall and were unable to continue development of the system. As a solution, the mining rights to Nexus were sold to the [Hathor Group](gp:R6v8Dg8o6a) in 2468. After the company strip mined a large portion of the system and extracted all they could, they left in 2672. Over the course of the next several decades, outlaws took control of much of the abandoned infrastructure and began using the planet [Lagos (Nexus III)](gp:0QljXA8d49) as a base of operations. Following the events of the now infamous [Kellar's Run](gp:RxNxDYYJNd), the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) launched an operation to reclaim the system in 2931 which is still ongoing.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a01a2599-6954-4ab6-9b97-9e62db4bab43"},
{"id":"ngii-yaoyao","gp":"VYLqxADl7v","t":"Ngii (Yao'yao)","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"The ngii, also called the yao'yao after the sound it makes, is a semi-aquatic domestic animal indigenous to RyiX'yan (Hyoton III). A popular pet in the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9), it has lived alongside the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) since they developed farming, and is used for pest control and fishing along with companionship. Ngii typically have free roam of the homes they live in, and sleep on perches meant to mimic low tree branches. Speakers of UEE Standard have been known to refer to the ngii as the yengi cat.","g":["ngii","yao'yao","yengi cat","ryixy'an","hyoton iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a7654fa0-1804-4ea1-9a0e-64df7d9f7516"},
{"id":"nick-croshaw","gp":"VyvYkAr7YW","t":"Nick Croshaw","k":"people","c":["People","Exploration","Human"],"x":"Nick Croshaw (2236-2321) was an astrophysicist and pilot who achieved fame as the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to discover and successfully navigate a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) on 10 April SEY 2271. He was also the first Human to visit a planetary system beyond Sol, which would eventually be named in his honor (Croshaw). Croshaw spent years studying the Neso Triangle, a sector near Neptune (Sol VIII) where spacecraft would vanish without trace or explanation. His findings led him to believe that a previously undiscovered type of astral anomaly was responsible for the disappearances. By utilizing a personally modified quantum drive, he was able to embark on a solo mission to traverse through the anomaly and \"jump\" to another solar system. Croshaw's successful navigation of the first Human-discovered jump point ushered in a new age of [exploration and colonization for Humans](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm).","g":["navjumper","neso triangle","croshaw system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d2c58347-90d4-4e19-a418-ad7abcfd6b54"},
{"id":"night-warrior","gp":"Vgg7YwYjJ3","t":"Night Warrior","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*Night Warrior* is a 2941 vid starring Callum Robb, Khar Alejandro, and Serene Steward, based on a novel of the same name by Carsten Maes. It tells the story of one man's quest to save his colony world from the scheming of an evil super-corporation. The vid was a financial success despite neutral reviews from critics, becoming the ninth highest-grossing film of 2941.","g":["vids"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8c886399-8f60-44d6-966b-af83653fa7e7"},
{"id":"nine-tails","gp":"0Gxpleqwqo","t":"Nine Tails","k":"people","c":["Organizations","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Nine Tails is a criminal organization based in the [Stanton](gp:RX3lKBA3dq) system. First active in SEY 2938, the gang established itself by leading an attack on a prisoner transport vehicle that left [28 Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) police officers dead and liberated Albert \"Sinkhole\" Holden, leader of the Terra-based Rangda syndicate. Investigators believed the group was allied with Rangda until Holden was found floating in space a day later, apparently having been executed. Over the next few years, Nine Tails would conduct unpredictable attacks in over a dozen systems that involved murders, robberies, and the destruction of personal and private property. In 2942, the incidents suddenly stopped. Authorities hoped that internal divisions might have destroyed the gang from the inside out, but in 2943, Nine Tails abruptly reappeared and took over [Grim HEX](gp:0jGGDvYm93) in the Stanton system. Since then, they have opened a black market and have frequently clashed with [Crusader Security](gp:bmNrmYB8MP).","g":["human outlaw factions","stanton outlaw factions","grim hex"]},
{"id":"njeri","gp":"VYLwadeGEp","t":"Njeri","k":"people","c":["People","Banu"],"x":"Njeri, known also as Jerry, was the first [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) to establish contact with [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2). In SEY 2438, Njeri fled through a then-unknown jump point to the [Davien system](gp:Rz2g71YlkY) to avoid punishment after being caught embezzling funds from their [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron). There, they had a chance encounter with navjumper Vernon Tar, who fired upon Njeri's vessel thinking it was someone trying to jump his claim. Njeri's ship suffered only minimal damage, and thanks to Njeri's decision not to fire back, Humans and Banu were able to establish peaceful relations. \n\n# LIFE BEFORE CONTACT\n\nWhen they came of age, Njeri was sold by their Rearing Souli to a Bureaucratic one, where they were put under an [indenture](gp:bZwQBk42OL) contract and began learning data organization skills. In an interview given in SEY 2451, Njeri reported that back then, they were unhappy and underpaid and that they spent much of their free time coming up with ways to purchase their contract. Instead of waiting until it was paid off, Njeri began to embezzle funds from the Souli in the hopes of one day fleeing and buying a contract from an Exploration Souli where they could pursue their true passion: piloting a starship of their very own. \n\nBefore Njeri could gather enough resources, the [Essosouli](gp:R6v8kxEPBD) noticed a discrepancy in the Souli's books and began to investigate. In a panic, Njeri stole one of the Souli's ships and fled, resulting in a multi-system chase. The Souli began to close in on Njeri in the then-unnamed [Cathcart system](gp:RL6524vWO3), but through sheer luck, Njeri detected a signal that turned out to be an undiscovered jump point. Faced with either consequences or possible death if they failed to navigate the tunnel, Njeri chose the latter and entered the jump point. \n\n# FIRST CONTACT\n\nNjeri wasn't in the Davien system for long before they encountered a spacecraft with an unfamiliar silhouette that almost immediately opened fire. Once the barrage was over and their Defender remained unscathed, Njeri realized that this strange vessel might belong to a new species and could therefore be their ticket out of trouble with the Souli. They chose not to return fire, and remained in place while the ship approached. Historians have since pointed out that this was an extremely fortunate circumstance; if Njeri had shot and destroyed the ship, it may have triggered a war between Humans and Banu. \n\nSoon, a team of linguists, scientists, military officials, and diplomats led by General [Neal Socolovich](gp:VJX7vxG2BG) arrived and took Njeri into custody. Njeri was eager to work with them, but the language barrier made things difficult. Undeterred, Njeri assisted in any way they could, and by the time an additional Banu ship arrived in Davien two standard weeks later, the UNE team had made headway into understanding the Banu language and Njeri had learned a few words of UNE Common. The Banu delegation and the Humans spent the next few standard months deciphering one another's languages and engaging in careful political negotiation. The end result of this was the [Interstellar Peace and Trade Accord](gp:RzPoJ1aP4z), which Njeri signed in SEY 2438 in an honorary capacity. \n\n# BACK IN THE PROTECTORATE\n\nAlthough Njeri was given the opportunity to remain in Davien, they returned to the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) to finish out the remainder of their indenture contract. Njeri expected to be celebrated for their accomplishments, but instead they were given a disdainful reception by their Souli for having been caught embezzling the Souli's funds and hijacking the Defender. In addition to this, the Essosouli was uninterested in pursuing relations with Humans as Njeri had hoped, and Njeri was placed in a data sorting-heavy position under close supervision. They spent the next few unhappy years finishing out their contract as quickly as they could. \n\nOnce they officially severed ties with their old Souli, Njeri tried to establish a Human-relations Souli of their own, but found that the market had already been saturated with similar Soulis that could speak UNE Common with far more fluency than Njeri, who had only a few short months of experience with the language. After failing to land multiple contracts, Njeri decided to use the rest of their savings to return to the place they'd been the happiest: the Davien system.\n\n# RETURN TO THE UNE\n\nNjeri was met with a warm, enthusiastic welcome. Unbeknownst to Njeri, they had become famous throughout the UNE as \"Jerry,\" the Banu who had ensured a peaceful first contact between Humans and Banu. With the help of their old friend Natalia Gordillo, who had been a member of the original UNE delegation, Njeri learned Common and embarked on a career doing public appearances and giving talks on daily life in the Banu Protectorate. Gordillo later assisted Njeri in the writing of their biography *Jerry*, in which Njeri describes their time after returning to the UNE as the best of their life. In SEY 2456, Njeri died of advanced age in their home in the Davien system, surrounded by Human and Banu friends.","g":["jerry","banu people","banu-human first contact"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/94b70f84-7922-477e-ac25-267e740f3125"},
{"id":"noah-traeger","gp":"VDzyygGMQ1","t":"Noah Traeger","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Noah Traeger (2759 - 2848) was a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Navy mechanic and engineer most notable for their discovery of the Osiris system in 2788. They joined the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) in 2782, where they repaired damaged spacecraft aboard multiple capital-class starships. While on shore leave in the [Goss system](gp:RxnYdDZj96), Traeger opted out of enjoying the beach and instead worked on a broken scanner. When they went out to test it, they at first thought that their repairs had failed until they traced the strange signal and discovered a previously-unknown jump point. Traeger accepted an honorable discharge in 2808, after which they used the reward money from their discovery to open a ship repair shop on [Cassel (Goss II)](gp:RPDy6gqX7Z).","g":["osiris system","cassel","goss ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/412cacf5-a128-4020-a639-af51c3c05310"},
{"id":"noble-ellis-v","gp":"V8W545NrKo","t":"Noble (Ellis V)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Noble (Ellis V) is a heavily forested planet in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is one of three habitable planets in the system. In the early days after its [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), colonists established settlements and harvested resources as needed with little regard to preserving the natural environment. When visitors from the nearby planets [Kampos (Ellis IV)](gp:RAXxrxr7M5) and [Green (Ellis III)](gp:RWoNrNeLKP) began visiting Noble to enjoy its pristine landscapes, bringing a great deal of income with them, the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) voted to roll back its urban development plans and instead focus on the creation of a tourist industry.","g":["kampos","ellis v","ellis system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/420b6386-c9d3-46e6-9148-2cbbc7f92f09"},
{"id":"noble-ammunition","gp":"RzPoqWkdmr","t":"Noble Ammunition","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Noble Ammunition is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of munitions. Their primary market is the production of small arms ammunition, though they maintain several factories devoted to larger caliber ballistics. Due to multiple high-profile accidents and lawsuits relating to weapon jams, Noble has been accused of cutting corners in their materials and the machining process to keep their cost and price point low. Nevertheless, the company continues to turn a profit.","g":["munitions manufacturer"]},
{"id":"nogo-gliese-iv","gp":"R4jEkkOAkW","t":"Nogo (Gliese IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nogo (Gliese IV) is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Gliese system](gp:V7dEXXD4wa), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A lush, temperate planet with an oxygen-nitrogen atmosphere and a variety of climates, it is nonetheless avoided by the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). It is unclear why Banu refuse to live there, especially in light of ample evidence that they lived there in the past. After a long analysis period that determined that the planet was safe, [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) constructed multiple colonies and have lived there ever since. Agricultural exports to the nearby Lyris flotilla make up the bulk of Nogo's economy.","g":["nogo","gliese iv","habitable","habitable planet","gliese system","banu planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e6e06555-da8c-4ed9-9bd7-68559aff8dda"},
{"id":"nomad","gp":"RegxW5ywdj","t":"Nomad","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Nomad is a light freight spacecraft manufactured by [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34). Designed for single pilots, it is equipped with a variety of features such as a large cargo bay, comfortable living quarters and a comprehensive defensive package. When Consolidated Outland CEO [Silas Koerner](gp:V8gJMXjE8o) announced the ship, he introduced Bix Bista as the lead designer, a production assistant for the company who had submitted a design to a company-wide initiative for new ideas.","g":["human spacecraft","freight","light freight","consolidated outland"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/72442b1d-0202-42a7-a4a8-d910c5c58d76"},
{"id":"north-american-alliance-naa","gp":"RvlxwY23oO","t":"North American Alliance (NAA)","k":"faction","c":["Politics","Human"],"x":"The North American Alliance (NAA) was a supranational political and economic union of multiple member states that were located primarily on the North American continent of Earth (Sol III). Formed in 2189, it rose to help facilitate the sourcing and exchanging of valuable resources made scarce due to the unimpeded environmental destruction wrought during previous centuries. When Mars (Sol IV) was fully terraformed In 2157, member states held a summit reaffirming their intention to maintain the alliance. The NAA lasted until 2380, when it was superseded by the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO).","g":["north american alliance"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/793d1e3e-ff2e-4081-825c-6b429db3d6d9"},
{"id":"northstar","gp":"RMNkJw71Kx","t":"NorthStar","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"NorthStar is a footwear company that manufactures athletic shoes. Made for high-impact exercise, the majority of the brand's products are crafted with a proprietary cushioning system, the makeup of which is a closely-guarded secret. The brand often features professional athletes in its advertisements, and is famous for identifying young, up-and-coming rookies who go on to have long and celebrated careers.","g":["footwear manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/728a420d-fea4-449c-82dd-dce418d442da"},
{"id":"nova","gp":"01L8gLYXaY","t":"Nova","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Human","Military"],"x":"The Nova is a main battle tank developed by [Tumbril Land Systems](gp:VarkpZnxjd). Built around a large, turreted ballistic cannon, the Nova is used by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) and [Marine](gp:V7d5ZYEr1a) armored units. Early models of the tank were used during the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) and distinguished themselves at the [Battle of Koren Pass](gp:01dWmOD45G), where they held off a numerically superior [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) strike force in SEY 2605. Tumbril also makes the Nova available for civilian use.","g":["tumbril land systems","nova (tank)","tank"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8802201f-be06-443b-8af1-654dc70ef21a"},
{"id":"nova-pyrotechnica","gp":"VJOzPjK22n","t":"Nova Pyrotechnica","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Nova Pyrotechnica is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of missiles, rockets, and other ordnance. Founded in 2932, Nova quickly carved a niche in the market by developing a reputation for low-cost, highly-powered weapons. In 2945 allegations surfaced that their products are more prone to technical failure than similar models from other manufacturers. Despite these claims, Nova Pyrotechnica-produced ordnance is still widely used across the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["weapons manufacturer","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c5d54f2b-66de-4a0c-80df-a51e9d746a31"},
{"id":"novariders","gp":"0jGlnaO6pz","t":"NovaRiders","k":"faction","c":["Organizations","Human","Illegal Activity"],"x":"The NovaRiders were an outlaw group that entered notoriety in the early 2500s SEY when they became the first known people to steal a spacecraft mid-flight. During this time, ships were sold at such a high cost that they were primarily owned by the wealthy, and were commonly stolen at stations and ports. The gang was known for their practice of playing loud thrash metal music on all communication frequencies in order to prevent their targets from calling for help. \n\nThe group was disbanded by the military in 2517, but formed again a few years later, utilizing the same techniques. Since then, it has formed and dissolved again multiple times.","g":["outlaw factions","human outlaw factions"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6b80aa59-f7a8-4c58-bd44-ae1457be95b9"},
{"id":"nox","gp":"0OaBoZeqMZ","t":"Nox","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Ground Transportation","Xi'an","Human"],"x":"The Nox is an open-canopy racer developed by Xi'an manufacturer [Aopoa](gp:VyvY5jyZwp) for Human use. It can be operated on the ground or in deep space. The first versions of the vehicle were designed for use by Xi'an pilots and rarely seen in Human space. Following the success of [Drake's](gp:RLMm9KeZed) [Dragonfly](gp:VlNPm8MOor) and [Origin's](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) X1, Aopoa began offering adapted Nox to Human customers in 2947. The first shipment of Nox racers was briefly stolen by pirates, but was recovered thanks to the aid of Citizen and civilian assistance. A limited edition, the Nox Kue, was released at the same time to celebrate the first sale of the Nox to Humans.","g":["nox kue","racing","aopoa","xi'an vehicle","human vehicle"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4ed003ca-013b-430c-8f1b-85ba2f2854a0"},
{"id":"nul-i","gp":"VJXAYvnYro","t":"Nul I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nul I is a mesoplanet in the unclaimed [Nul system](gp:VgEnlpqyJ9), and is the closest planet to its star. In 2510, a research team funded by the University of Persei established a research base at the bottom of one of its deepest craters in order to study how the planet's environment was affected by the temperature and radiation fluctuations in its sun. However, after repeatedly losing their sensors and equipment to thieves, the team's funding was cut and the station was abandoned.","g":["nul system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/846c7e42-ca35-4ebc-897a-bffe880e1ad8"},
{"id":"nul-ii","gp":"VlM1y7lvWA","t":"Nul II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nul II is the second planet from the sun of the unclaimed [Nul system](gp:VgEnlpqyJ9). Large and dense, it is composed mostly of iron, and is thought to be the former core of a super-Earth that lost its mantle. While there is no water to be found, there are many lakes on the planet, including straw-colored lakes of iron carbonyl. In 2599, [Behesht Mines](gp:VpMez1B2qM) accidentally started a fire in one of their most active mines, and was unable to contain it. As the fire spread, the company was forced to suspend operations. Fed by flammable gasses and liquid volatiles, the fire continues to burn, and has opened smoky cracks in the landscape.","g":["nul system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/75ae7c4a-122e-4078-8977-8e671d05381d"},
{"id":"nul-iv","gp":"0OD6qG4zDe","t":"Nul IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nul IV is a gas giant in the unclaimed [Nul system](gp:VgEnlpqyJ9), and is the fourth planet from its sun. A lightning storm that stretches across the entire world has been active on Nul IV at least since it was first observed in the late 2200s. Some spacecraft that attempt to refuel in the upper atmosphere in spite of the danger are often damaged beyond repair. Many of these wrecked ships end up in orbit around the gas giant or drift to its Lagrange points over time.","g":["nul system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ffdb5e26-720a-45dc-9484-812ea2b995d8"},
{"id":"nul-system","gp":"VgEnlpqyJ9","t":"Nul System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Nul system is an unclaimed planetary system that consists of a type G cepheid variable star and five planets. Discovered in SEY 2290 by navjumper Antoine Lebec, it was one of the first systems visited and charted by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) after [Croshaw](gp:0qanKAEJwp) in 2271 and [Rhetor](gp:0ODlqMJXmP) in 2287. The planets of Nul are all located outside the system's [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy) save for [Cole (Nul III)](gp:RMNKLQkw2B), which has resisted all terraforming attempts thanks to its dense and stormy atmosphere. Nul remained mostly uninhabited until 2571, when the [UEES Olympus](gp:0Gxk9rGkej) crashed into [Ashana (Nul V)](gp:bZkd47KMB6) while pursuing anti-[Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) activists. [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) expatriates have claimed the crashed ship along with the abandoned infrastructure left behind from past enterprises.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2b3a93f4-ce4f-4268-a94b-b841fc5f3f15"},
{"id":"nuso-flotilla","gp":"R9vEnnAY2M","t":"Nuso Flotilla","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Banu"],"x":"The Nuso flotilla is an interconnected fleet of ships located in the [Bacchus system](gp:bBzaExgj1o), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Located near the Geddon-Bacchus jump point, it began as a popular location for [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) merchants to park their ships and set up shop in hopes of attracting [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) customers. Some ships became permanent residents after considerable profit. Hundreds of ships have since lashed themselves together to create a continuous marketplace.","g":["banu flotilla","bacchus system","space station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d376e297-cdbe-4358-8bdd-e56ed0d5c019"},
{"id":"nv-tac","gp":"0KnAr6dZgY","t":"NV-TAC","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"NV-TAC is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of personal weapon attachments, such as targeting devices and enhanced gun sights. Originally founded in SEY 2811 as a sensor company, NV-TAC produced technology for long-range scanning stations and surveying operations before pivoting to the personal weapon attachment market. Their bestselling products include the Delta targeting dot, Tau Plus 4x telescopic sight, Theta Pro 8x telescopic sight, and the Gamma Plus 3x holographic sight.","g":["weapon component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d555cb33-6233-4f6e-96c1-55d846d75ef6"},
{"id":"nyx-I","gp":"V3GxjndyDa","t":"Nyx I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nyx I is a coreless planet that orbits closest to the sun in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). Once considered impossible to terraform due to the presence of irremovable chemicals in its atmosphere, Nyx I has been in the process of [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) since SEY 2954 thanks to a new type of technology developed by Genesis Terraforming. The governing body of the People's Alliance has stated that they may pursue additional settlements on the world if the procedure is successful.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","nyx system","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d8b78679-5052-41ae-9cb9-1858a4368c72"},
{"id":"nyx-ii","gp":"0QlKwplYQo","t":"Nyx II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nyx II is a smog planet with a poisonous, corrosive atmosphere of acid and carbon dioxide.  Erosion from the atmosphere has made a dramatic mark upon the planet's surface. Though it is located in [Nyx's](gp:0jGxP6kpG3) green band, its noxious environment cannot be altered under the current limitations of [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) technology.","g":["nyx system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6609fb1c-0cb9-4cfd-92f4-f2a29a8e7fe7"},
{"id":"nyx-iii","gp":"0qaxgzqE5A","t":"Nyx III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nyx III, an ice giant, is the most distant planet from the sun of the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). Its stormy atmosphere is composed mainly of ammonia and water vapor, and an ocean of supercritical water surrounds the planet's rocky core. High, dangerous winds make it difficult for pilots to fly below the cloud tops of the outer atmosphere.","g":["nyx system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8c2e64bc-97b1-4353-b390-84c8061efd13"},
{"id":"nyx-system","gp":"0jGxP6kpG3","t":"Nyx System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"Nyx is an [unclaimed](gp:VgExMejDPx) planetary [system](gp:VaZwNWg372) situated at the border of a dark nebula. It consists of an F-type main sequence star orbited by a terrestrial planet, a smog planet, an ice giant, and two asteroid belts. The system's main settlement, [Levski](gp:0dXQqBMAOp), is located on a large asteroid in the Glaciem ring. Considered a haven for [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) who wish to live beyond the reach of [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE), it was founded by anti-Messer activists known as the People's Alliance in SEY 2655. The system has recently become a hotbed of Vanduul activity with numerous attacks occurring every year. Starting in 2954, Nyx I has been undergoing terraformation using new experimental technology created by Genesis Terraforming.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5dbdba9a-3061-4206-8d8c-5380da665693"},
{"id":"nee-se-ruoth","gp":"V8WPAo6xpO","t":"Nē\" se Ruoth","k":"people","c":["People","Exploration","Xi'an"],"x":"Nē\" se Ruoth (III.796 - III.1125 | SEY 2475 - 2898) was an amateur explorer and historian best known for her MXY III.847 (SEY 2542) discovery of the [Gurzil](gp:0Kxydrxd45)-R.il'a jump point. The youngest daughter of one of House Ruoth's Matriarchs, she was expected to follow in the footsteps of her family and become a political historian. However, she found she preferred exploration and spacecraft piloting. During her time in the [Pō't.ōngp.ū](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ), she served as a scout for the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military, and would explore the outskirts of whatever system in which she was posted during her breaks. This hobby led her to discover a previously-unknown jump point from the R.il'a system to the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN)-controlled Gurzil system, then named Odara. Her appearance in Odara caused an increase in tensions between the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) and the UPE, so while she was commended for her discovery, she was reprimanded for her carelessness in entering the jump point and stripped of her duty as a pilot. She served the remainder of her time in the Pō't.ōngp.ū as a file clerk. After returning to her House, she took up the family business but obtained her own ship and continued flying whenever she could. She won the Koa e Ko'ia in III.1112 (SEY 2881).","g":["nee\" se ruoth","gurzil system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2b8f189a-d836-4784-932b-03cad99cd0d1"},
{"id":"ob-station-chimera","gp":"RMN2oE45WK","t":"OB Station Chimera","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human","Military"],"x":"OB Station *Chimera*, also known as \"Yogi Station,\" is a United Empire of Earth outpost located in the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Oso system](gp:bZkAMEarPd). Charged with preventing outside interference in the system, it is located near the Pyro-Oso jump point to monitor incoming traffic and protect the system from anyone seeking to undermine local protections. In 2943, a Senate inquiry revealed rampant corruption amongst the crew of the *Chimera*, including negligence, bribery, and extortion. It was discovered that smugglers had regularly enlisted the help of [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) soldiers in raids on [Oso II](gp:Rw19lYy9D7), sometimes even in the kidnapping of [Osoians](gp:0NwpEy2LNM). The [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) at the time, [Kelos Costigan](gp:VJOzBxdJ28), responded to this by ordering stricter oversight from [High Command](gp:RegxqX26ok) that incorporated consistent ethics checks from civilian auditors.","g":["yogi station","space station","uee space station","oso system","uee army","ueea station","research station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8b03ac7d-c883-4f58-be42-85cea6b63bf5"},
{"id":"ob-station-gryphon","gp":"bmG15PAezQ","t":"OB Station Gryphon","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human","Military"],"x":"OB Station Gryphon is an observation post operated by the [United Empire of Earth Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) (UEEA) in the developing [Kallis system](gp:0Ql43d1nrv). Located near the Kallis-Oso [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY), the station is the system's main operational hub, and is a required checkpoint for all who wish to visit. All deliveries to Kallis are routed through Gryphon to ensure that [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) protocols are followed. It is staffed by a mix of UEEA personnel and researchers engaged in the study of developing planets.","g":["space station","uee space station","kallis system","uee army","ueea station","research station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/12ae93d7-e7f1-431d-be4a-81d3a63aaad6"},
{"id":"ob-station-heller","gp":"RPD1DYyGwz","t":"OB Station Heller","k":"place","c":["Locations"],"x":"OB Station Heller is a research space station located in the Garron system, [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). It is the main headquarters of the ongoing effort to restore the biosphere of [Garron II](gp:VlMGMLM1lL), which was destroyed at the orders of [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) in SEY 2792. It also houses a museum dedicated to the history of [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP).","g":["space station","research station","uee space station","garron system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f12791a9-7315-418c-bc19-78c0c824107d"},
{"id":"ob-station-kobold","gp":"Rvlxxq9Dn3","t":"OB Station Kobold","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"OB Station Kobold is an observation platform located in the protected [Osiris system](gp:0qaJeqWBZD). Situated in one of the Lagrange points of [Etos (Osiris I)](gp:RAXPPX7g77), its mixture of scientific and military personnel are tasked with studying and protecting the planet's developing inhabitants. In SEY 2939, the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military apprehended a smuggler who had captured a clutch of five adolescent [Phare's Apes](gp:RX3Krj8Mzq). The animals were deemed too injured to be returned to their planet and were rehabilitated aboard the station, where they continue to live and be studied.","g":["space station","uee space station","osiris system","ueea station","uee army","research station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ee218c1b-4e28-430b-8e45-af1479d6546e"},
{"id":"ob-station-pegasus","gp":"V7dJ24aWMm","t":"OB Station Pegasus","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human","Military"],"x":"OB Station *Pegasus* is a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) outpost located in the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv). Situated at a Lagrange point in the orbit of [Kellog VI](gp:R6dAQZgGQe), it was created to monitor the planet [Xis (Kellog II)](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/bmGJeMv2oK-xis-kellog-ii ) and protect the developing [Orm](gp:RzPoqZXqZz) civilization that resides there from outside influence. Its staff is a mix of military personnel and scientists engaged in long-term observation of the Orm.","g":["space station","uee space station","kellog system","uee army","ueea station","research station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2f088e98-4a9e-4687-9b20-04595262db8e"},
{"id":"oberon-sol-7e","gp":"RAXM4Ow2Ym","t":"Oberon (Sol 7e)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Oberon (Sol 7e) is a moon of [Uranus (Sol VII)](gp:0rxOX3eKQ2), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Slightly red in color, it likely obtained its hue from the accretion of materials from other parts of the Uranus system. Meteorite impacts have also knocked ice from the surface, leaving dark, non-ice material behind that has contributed to Oberon's hue.","g":["oberon","sol 7e","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1d548303-b3e0-4d64-8b68-468e434bc932"},
{"id":"oberon-iii","gp":"0n14yXxynn","t":"Oberon III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oberon III is a protoplanet that orbits third from the star of the unclaimed [Oberon system](gp:VYLdlgMqop). Alongside its sister protoplanet [Oberon IV](gp:0dXd5mQWLd), it is theorized that it formed in the Oberon system after its original star went supernova and collapsed into a neutron star. However, it failed to gain enough mass from the dust and gas of the newly-formed accretion disk to become a full planet.","g":["oberon system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/87c35534-150e-4a2d-9da9-8bc921ef1827"},
{"id":"oberon-iv","gp":"0dXd5mQWLd","t":"Oberon IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oberon IV is a protoplanet in the unclaimed [Oberon system](gp:VYLdlgMqop), and is the fourth planet from its star. Like its sister protoplanet [Oberon III](gp:0n14yXxynn), it is theorized to have formed after the original star of the system went supernova. In 2946, multiple stray bombs struck Oberon IV during a circumvented [Vanduul invasion](gp:Rw1gdnOKBp). Scars from the impacts can still be observed today.","g":["oberon system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ea444424-b019-4782-a229-35c7b139d70c"},
{"id":"oberon-system","gp":"VYLdlgMqop","t":"Oberon System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Oberon system is an unclaimed planetary system discovered in SEY 2356 that consists of a neutron star, a super-Earth, a terrestrial planet, two protoplanets, a mesoplanet, a gas dwarf, and a gas giant. In spite of its dangerous, dim star and multiple connections to [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-occupied systems, there are majority-[Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) settlements on [Gonn (Oberon I)](gp:VJXAYN81Q5) and [Uriel (Oberon II)](gp:RL673Gxjjv). Because the neutron star at the system's center makes above-ground colonization profoundly dangerous, nearly all homesteads in Oberon are located underground. In 2946, the [United Empire of Earth Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) (UEEN) received intelligence that a [Vanduul Clan](gp:R9vzjxmEBx) was preparing to launch an invasion of the Oberon system. Under the orders of Admiral [Ernst Bishop](gp:ReJaavPB3k), the UEES *Retribution* ambushed and destroyed the Clan as it entered the system. Since then, the UEEN has maintained a presence in Oberon in case of future Vanduul attacks.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/182f742a-560c-4e5d-9122-d6301a3fcc5d"},
{"id":"oberon-v","gp":"0NjKk8zMO2","t":"Oberon V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oberon V is a mesoplanet in the unclaimed [Oberon system](gp:VYLdlgMqop), and is the fifth planet from its star. Small and dense, Oberon V has a thin atmosphere of nitrogen and carbon dioxide, and has a mantle of mixed methane and water ice. Its surface is nearly white, and it starkly stands out against the blackness of space. There are pinkish-brown spots in some areas where the concentration of methane ice is high.","g":["oberon system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7a3cd20a-0dcd-4cc2-ade0-4bc47c27b198"},
{"id":"oberon-vi","gp":"R5pWx9dLkm","t":"Oberon VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oberon VI is a gas dwarf that orbits sixth from the neutron star of the unclaimed [Oberon system](gp:VYLdlgMqop). Its white, blue, and pale-pink banded atmosphere of hydrogen and helium hides a rocky core covered with ammonia and water ice. Conditions deep within the planet are too high-pressure to allow for a ship to land, but the abundant hydrogen in its upper reaches has made Oberon VI a common refueling spot.","g":["oberon system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/86ef0649-7651-433d-abe3-56ef5d7fa57c"},
{"id":"oberon-vii","gp":"01LkN7D8GL","t":"Oberon VII","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oberon VII is a gas giant that orbits the neutron star of the unclaimed [Oberon system](gp:VYLdlgMqop). Considered by locals to be the only calming sight in the system, Oberon VII has a muted light blue-gray atmosphere that lacks global cloud cover. In 2939, [Uriel (Oberon II)](gp:RL673Gxjjv) resident Ruqayyah Shelton attempted to establish a ship-based retreat that would orbit Oberon VII and use the planet as a backdrop during meditation sessions. After three years, Shelton was forced to shutter his business due to multiple attacks from outlaw gangs.","g":["oberon system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a1dd001f-423c-4c6e-b481-8fe2a2bdf26b"},
{"id":"octagon","gp":"RMNkJwDAlW","t":"Octagon","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Octagon is a workwear company that manufactures a wide range of clothing and gear for blue-collar jobs. Known for durability, all of Octagon's products are made to stand up to the wear-and-tear that comes with daily use in an active environment. The company contracts with multiple corporations to provide uniforms for their employees, including [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N).","g":["clothing manufacturer","footwear manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b853bd5e-3be4-4052-9107-0464fd2e9615"},
{"id":"odin-ii","gp":"0KxloXyPAM","t":"Odin II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Odin II is the planet closest to the [Odin system's](gp:RX3jMavYGk) star, [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Formerly the second-closest planet, it became the first after [Odin I](gp:VlNP3xpMx4) was destroyed sometime during its sun's red giant phase. Odin II is not [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), though it is dotted with sealed stations that serve as testing facilities for various research projects that are risky or involve hazardous materials.","g":["odin system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e8caa3d0-4b39-4269-bd21-9462b823080d"},
{"id":"odin-iii","gp":"0ODlqY5mqO","t":"Odin III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Odin III is a planet in the [Odin system](gp:RX3jMavYGk), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the second closest planet to its sun. In SEY 2943, hiker Akeno Ashraf discovered fossils of ancient animals near the planet's equator during a 25 kilometer trek. These fossils prove that Odin III supported life before its star collapsed into a white dwarf. Since then, paleontologists from various institutions around the UEE have operated digs in hopes of learning more about the planet's history.","g":["odin system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/526c05e1-7ccf-4b92-9fd2-c3337ce73b0f"},
{"id":"odin-iv","gp":"0QljX3BQ6J","t":"Odin IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Odin IV is a gas giant with a hydrogen and helium atmosphere in the [Odin system](gp:RX3jMavYGk), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Much of the deep heat that escapes the planet's interior flows upwards to power enormous storms. Its strong magnetosphere gives rise to spectacular auroras visible above its north and south poles. Many fully automated fuel facilities orbit Odin IV at a safe distance from the volatile atmosphere.","g":["odin system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/62d07062-b5d0-4f72-a3f2-4659ba00de94"},
{"id":"odin-system","gp":"RX3jMavYGk","t":"Odin System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Odin system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It is made up of two chthonian planets, one gas giant, an unusual cosmic anomaly, and a white dwarf star. The anomaly was created when the first planet in the system was destroyed by its star, leaving behind a unique asteroid field beset by constant electrical storms. Corporations and research facilities that deal in dangerous materials conduct testing on [Odin II](gp:0KxloXyPAM).","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3805a290-a734-4b52-a78f-26d1a990598e"},
{"id":"odyssey","gp":"0dXG5LBvOo","t":"Odyssey","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Odyssey is an exploration and mining spacecraft manufactured by [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/misc) (MISC). Designed for long-term expeditions, it was constructed with self-sufficiency in mind, and has living quarters for a crew of up to six people, a medical bay, a spacious cargo hold, and a hangar able to accommodate a small vehicle. Additionally, the Odyssey comes with built-in mining technology and an on-board refinery, which allows for the production of fuel without having to return to landing areas.","g":["expedition","mining","heavy mining","musashi industrial and starflight concern","misc","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cec55425-3e76-4b6d-934a-2b29220f3335"},
{"id":"oilxa-taal-ii","gp":"0rx4XojAed","t":"Oil'xa (T.āl II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oil'xa (T.āl II) is the second planet from the sun of the [T.āl system](gp:R4j2mdjZE5), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). The technological heart of T.āl, its government-assigned function is to fabricate spacecraft, from large-scale ships to advanced ship components to avionics software. It is densely populated, and the constant influx of resources and outflow of products makes it the most frequently visited planet in the system. Its yellow-accented architecture has earned it the nickname \"the Hive\" from [Human]([Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)) visitors. Famed musician Sindo Guerrero's record-breaking hit song, \"Sun Kissed,\" was inspired by the buildings of Oil'xa.","g":["oil'xa","t.āl ii","t.āl system","habitable","habitable planet","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"oisha-suen","gp":"01LrmgveKB","t":"Oisha Suen","k":"people","c":["People","Exploration","Human"],"x":"Oisha Suen (SEY 2694 - 2793) was a pilot, mechanic, and smuggler most notable for her 2716 discovery of the [Tohil system](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9) with her business partner [Aadya Firmino](gp:0Nj5o4M9v2). In 2713, she met [Terra](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa)-born construction heiress Aadya Firmino at [Levski](gp:0dXQqBMAOp) in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3) and the two started a smuggling operation using Firmino's [Constellation Andromeda](gp:0QxY3wEXxQ) as their base. They were exiled by the [People's Alliance](gp:Vy2v4qgG4v) in 2716 after Firmino attempted to steal one too many clients from other smugglers. While they made their escape, Suen detected a strange reading on a scanner she had just repaired. Further investigations revealed that she had discovered a new jump point into what would become the Tohil system. Firmino persuaded Suen into keeping the discovery to themselves until they could fully assess what they had found, but instead reported that she alone had located the new system and collected the reward money for herself. Suen, devastated by the betrayal, went to the [Terra Gazette](gp:RzPo4jJWdZ) for a tell-all interview, which kicked off an investigation by the [Department of Transportation and Navigation](gp:VDoPezP7E1). The government eventually awarded credit for the system's discovery to both Suen and Firmino, and the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) issued warrants for their past smuggling activities. Suen served a reduced sentence for her truthful testimony, and returned to Levski, where her banishment was rescinded and she started a passenger transport business.","g":["tohil system","human people"]},
{"id":"olsen-hendrick","gp":"Varqdy4NMd","t":"Olsen Hendrick","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Olsen Hendrick is a clothing brand that manufactures ready-to-wear formal and business attire. Originally a high-end fashion house, the company fell into decline in the early 2900s SEY and was forced to sell. The new parent corporation re-focused the brand on the mid-range clothing market, and secured a deal with [Voyager Direct](gp:V7dgpKQ7rL) that put its new line of dresses and suits within reach of the average consumer while capitalizing on the high-end reputation associated with the name.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/731bff35-76be-49c5-b101-b4e3ec676056"},
{"id":"olympus","gp":"Regrl72egM","t":"Olympus","k":"place","c":["Settlements"],"x":"Olympus is a settlement on [Ashana (Nul V)](gp:bZkd47KMB6). Built in the remains of the carrier [UEES Olympus](gp:0Gxk9rGkej), which crashed into the planet in 2571 while pursuing a group of [Human](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) anti-[Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) rebels, Olympus became a home to a diverse population of expatriates and outlaws from all known spacefaring civilizations save the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) and [Kr'thak](gp:RxNxDYkqzz). An atmospheric system inside the wreck allows for its inhabitants to move through the settlement without the need for breathing equipment.","g":["uees olympus","ashana","nul v","sealed settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9b8f9b14-8c14-4071-8b53-f44851d45241"},
{"id":"olympus-pool","gp":"bmGxJA35Wl","t":"Olympus Pool","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Olympus Pool is a unique cosmic phenomenon located in the [Goss system](gp:RxnYdDZj96). It is an unusually dense interstellar cloud, packed with reflective, colorful cosmic dust in shades of turquoise, gold, and deep orange that is visible from the surface of all of the planets of the system. Visits to Goss specifically to view the Olympus Pool make a major contribution to the local tourism industry.","g":["interstellar cloud","goss system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8ee7cac4-a739-4b37-bdd2-d40d7ff1f947"},
{"id":"omphalotus-mushroom","gp":"VgEwGP7Epe","t":"Omphalotus Mushroom","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The omphalotus mushroom is a bioluminescent fungus that grows in damp caves. Able to survive in cold, low-oxygen environments, the mushroom can sometimes be found in asteroid fissures, and can be eaten if it is correctly prepared. The omphalotus lends its fluorescent pink coloration to Jynx gin, a spirit distilled and bottled on [Delamar](gp:0GxoZnAGrg) in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3).","g":["fungi"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/857c886c-cdcb-4a63-b79f-3120b621f795"},
{"id":"opalsky","gp":"bBznMqw3PN","t":"OpalSky","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"OpalSky is a clothing brand that manufactures high-end everyday attire. Founded by a group of sub-surfers who used to frequent [Mariana](gp:VlMnZv8qY7) on [Tangaroa (Helios II)](gp:RX3rnQ3XqM), OpalSky creates classic, simple pieces made with top-quality materials. The company is known for its philanthropy, and has donated millions of UEC to environmental protection organizations on Tangaroa.","g":["clothing manufacturer","mariana","tangaroa","helios ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d666c219-bd23-4c63-b04c-7b80301ced9e"},
{"id":"opera-mushroom","gp":"RWoozAmW82","t":"Opera Mushroom","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"# OPERA MUSHROOM\nThe opera mushroom is an artificially engineered fungus developed by a team of researchers at the University of Rhetor's (UR) Department of Genetics. It has a fleshy, violet, trumpet-shaped, fuzz-covered stem that amplifies a natural sound created by the expansion and contraction of the hyphae as water passes through it. Because the mushroom is easily grown on spacecraft, it became popular as an on-board plant shortly after its commercial debut in 2925.\n\n# DEVELOPMENT\nIn 2918, genetics graduate students Mauveine Senae and Phil Ektos started a project to create an edible version of the fast-growing purple chimney mushroom, a toxic fungus indigenous to Reisse (Rhetor III). Dr. Yuki Hexa, Senae's advisor, joined the project after Senae and Ektos presented their early results: a mushroom with a deeper funnel shape and slightly less toxicity. As the team made further modifications to the mushroom's genetic code, the toxicity failed to fall to levels safe for Human consumption, but the divot in its stem deepened. One night, Ektos heard a strange tone in the lab, and traced it to the latest generation of mushrooms.\n\nThe team agreed to reframe their project to bring out the new audio qualities of the mushroom. By the end of 2920, they had developed a stable breeding population of mushrooms that produced varying tones depending on their size. Senae created a personal garden of the mushrooms in her dorm room, arranged so they resembled performers on a tiny stage. Hexa suggested the name \"opera mushroom\" after seeing this display. In early 2921, Ektos and Senae submitted their work on the opera mushroom to their dissertation committees and were awarded doctorates.\n\n# LIFECYCLE\nAfter a four-week growing period, the constant motion of water through the mature mushroom causes ballistospores to slowly eject from the trumpet. After these spores fall onto a suitable substrate, they take root into a mycelium from which the mushrooms emerge. More and more mushrooms grow as the mycelium spreads underground, sometimes resulting in a widening ring-like pattern. Places where opera mushrooms grow can often be heard before they are seen.\n\n# COMMERCIAL DEBUT\nSamples of the opera mushroom were made available to plant nurseries on Reisse in 2925. Thanks to its novelty and fast growth cycles, the fungus was an instant hit. It became a popular houseplant, especially for long-haul spacefarers in need of something low-maintenance to decorate their holds. Skilled gardeners can grow mushrooms in arrangements that produce harmonizing tones. \n\nIn 2926, a wild, self-sustaining population of opera mushrooms was discovered 11 kilometers from the UR Genetics lab. The mushrooms continue to grow in the wild on Reisse today. It's a [Day of the Vara](gp:RkGQqpJwGp) tradition for some social organizations on the UR campus to tell ghost stories in nearby woodland with known opera mushroom populations to try to trick first year students into believing the woods are haunted","g":["fungi","university of rhetor"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7dd4f3b1-dfcc-4b8d-8dd9-bd9e389dce93"},
{"id":"operation-mandrake","gp":"bZkdG98WNE","t":"Operation Mandrake","k":"history","c":["Military","Human","Vanduul"],"x":"Operation Mandrake, also known as the Battle of Oberon, was a 2946 [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military offensive against the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO). Led by Admiral [Ernst Bishop](gp:ReJaavPB3k) of the 65th Battle Group, it took shape when the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) received credible intelligence that a large group of Vanduul was preparing to launch a mass invasion. Bishop dispatched a strike team to sweep the system and engage the Vanduul as soon as they appeared. While these forces engaged the Vanduul in battle, the UEES *Retribution* moved into position to block potential escape routes and then proceeded to destroy the remaining Vanduul fleet, leading to a conclusive UEE victory.","g":["uee military","uee military operation","battle of oberon","battles"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/246d28f7-31b0-4b13-922b-1d824080da88"},
{"id":"operation-unilateral-force","gp":"bBp64B7G79","t":"Operation Unilateral Force","k":"history","c":["Military","Human"],"x":"Operation Unilateral Force was a SEY 2940 military effort on the part of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). It was a combined attempt to incite infighting between [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) clans by disproportionately targeting a single clan. Experts anticipated that by noticeably weakening a single group of Vanduul, it might be possible to cause other clans to turn on the weakened group. The hope was that as the Vanduul battled each other, it would potentially reduce raids on [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) colonies allowing the military to shore up further defenses. While the operation led to the crippling of a powerful Kingship, it did not generate the expected internecine conflict.","g":["uee military","uee military operation"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5dc3b2b4-e45e-4b14-8202-a5ac177f3b6c"},
{"id":"ophion-inc","gp":"0KxPpl3xPr","t":"Ophion, Inc.","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Ophion, Inc. was a geo-development and [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) company that operated from 2501 to 2567. Founded by Eurynome Rhodes, it was initially known for its conscientious business practices and high rates of pay. However, after the founder's son Savion Guerra-Rhodes inherited the company in 2560, he began to implement cost-saving measures that resulted in shoddy products and low levels of employee satisfaction. Guerra-Rhodes utilized the resulting capital to purchase terraforming rights to [Taranis II](gp:02kg3Pkjwp) and its [moon](gp:bmG1Mo8q2L) from the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) government, where he planned to test the effectiveness of a new technology meant to utilize the orbital energy of Taranis 2a as a power source. Instead, the company caused a catastrophic accident that destroyed Taranis 2a, and the resulting financial and public fallout forced the company to close its doors in 2567.","g":["ophion inc","terraforming company","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3ca3efc5-29fc-4849-be19-023c009c7856"},
{"id":"orbital-platform","gp":"box5vnAx5w","t":"Orbital Platform","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"An orbital platform is a space station, generally constructed for one purpose, that orbits a celestial body such as a planet, asteroid, or star. Orbital platforms have been used as bases for fuel refineries, terraforming operations, orbital bombardment, mining operations, border control, shipyards, and shipping centers, among many other things.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/daa994ff-45e4-4226-9c23-24bf9a7b491c"},
{"id":"ouc","gp":"0rqz57XoZY","t":"Orbital Utility Craft (OUC)","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Orbital Utility Craft (OUC) is a type of support spacecraft debuted by [Argo Astronautics](gp:0KnA1vvJEM) in SEY 2578. A short-range loading spacecraft, it was built to transfer cargo pallets from orbital transports into ground-based rail networks for rapid deployment. Development of the OUC lead to the design of the [Argo Multi-Purpose Utility Vehicle](gp:0rqzN9vek9) (MPUV). OUC are no longer operated and have since been replaced by the Argo MPUV and other specialized spacecraft.","g":["industrial spacecraft","argo astronautics","support spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/615603f2-3f47-4023-9a41-d8040797ab35"},
{"id":"oretani-belt-alpha","gp":"0OD6YpqyWw","t":"Oretani Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Oretani belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the lost [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). When [Turiya Terraforming](gp:VarGepjj5o) surveyors discovered that many of the asteroids were rich in nitrogen, they established numerous agricultural stations to grow food for the thousands of workers living in space stations around [Oretani II](gp:VpMezplMwO). When the only [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) collapsed in 2485, many were hopeful that these farms could help those stranded in the system survive.","g":["oretani system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4c38de93-7b7a-44e2-91ed-cb49c488d633"},
{"id":"oretani-i","gp":"RWodWpArga","t":"Oretani I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oretani I is a mesoplanet in the lost [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). In a close orbit around its star, it has extreme temperature differences between night and day. Before the [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) collapsed, [Turiya Terraforming](gp:VarGepjj5o) had started construction on a temporary underground base to keep their surveyors safe from the harsh sun.","g":["oretani system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d5b2612b-79c0-4fc7-b0c2-f83eb1d965ba"},
{"id":"oretani-ii","gp":"VpMezplMwO","t":"Oretani II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oretani II is the second planet from the sun of the lost [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). An ocean world with small land masses, it was located on the system's green band, and had been chosen as a prime candidate for future settlement. [Turiya Terraforming](gp:VarGepjj5o) took on the task of making the planet fit for Human habitation in 2483. Thousands of workers and their families took up residence in orbital stations on the condition that they would move to the planet once it was inhabitable. Early reports indicated that the results were positive, and that [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) would likely be completed ahead of schedule. It is uncertain whether those left stranded there after the 2485 [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) collapse were ultimately able to relocate to the planet.","g":["oretani system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7b0fe486-385f-4a1f-a2c7-2d67865bfca4"},
{"id":"oretani-iii","gp":"0Kx7zwjyy3","t":"Oretani III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oretani III is the third planet from the sun of the lost [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). Located just beyond the [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), it was nevertheless identified as a potential candidate for [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) after extensive surveys by [Turiya Terraforming](gp:VarGepjj5o). Although the company never publicly shared their findings, experts speculated that they may have found valuable resources underneath the water ice glaciers that covered most of the planet's surface. However, the only [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) to the system collapsed in 2485, and Turiya's motivations remain unknown.","g":["oretani system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/48907bb5-1a1b-436c-9a02-cb87c0312cc8"},
{"id":"oretani-iv","gp":"0rxem21LDq","t":"Oretani IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oretani IV is the fourth planet from the sun of the lost [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). A gas dwarf, its thick, expansive atmosphere is composed of hydrogen and helium. At the time of the Oretani-[Ferron](gp:Vy2Qo1dB18) [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) collapse in 2485, there was a single harvesting station in orbit around the planet. It is possible that those stranded in the system may have utilized resources extracted from Oretani IV to survive.","g":["oretani system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/930b57c2-2f34-437c-8cb1-bfb132f52b20"},
{"id":"oretani-system","gp":"bo1eNYWqqN","t":"Oretani System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Oretani system is a planetary system that consists of a K-type main sequence star, a mesoplanet, a terrestrial planet, an ice planet, a gas dwarf, a gas giant, a dwarf planet, and an asteroid belt. Discovered in 2481 via the [Ferron system](gp:Vy2Qo1dB18), it was immediately cleared for development by the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE). [Turiya Terraforming](gp:VarGepjj5o) dispatched a team of over two thousand workers and their families to prospecting stations in orbit around the ocean planet [Oretani II](gp:VpMezplMwO) in 2483 to kickstart the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and colonization process. In 2485, the system's only known [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) suddenly collapsed. To date, no communications have since been received from the colonists and no additional jump points to the system have been discovered, leaving the fate of those initial colonists in question.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/77d4a986-3129-4c80-a0d1-a2cdc2d8ee0f"},
{"id":"oretani-v","gp":"bo1eNzzy6N","t":"Oretani V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oretani V is the fifth planet from the sun of the lost [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). The largest planet in the system, it is also believed to be the oldest, and likely formed beyond the frost line over the course of three to four million years. [Turiya Terraforming](gp:VarGepjj5o) had outlined plans to build a network of harvesting stations in orbit around Oretani V, but at the time of the [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) collapse in 2485, construction had not yet begun.","g":["oretani system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/048ac242-6d27-485f-9b72-74117bbfe33f"},
{"id":"oretani-vi","gp":"0GxAvne3wa","t":"Oretani VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oretani VI is the sixth planet from the sun of the lost [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). Located on the very outskirts of the system, the planet has an orbit that takes thousands of days to complete. Oretani VI is largely dark red in color, caused by the presence of a hydrocarbon sludge on its surface formed from simple organic compounds long exposed to ultraviolet radiation. Methane ice is visible in the areas around impact craters.","g":["oretani system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8b022d40-5b09-435a-a99b-5e1b43b1978b"},
{"id":"origin-jumpworks","gp":"VY4WOMoj2v","t":"Origin Jumpworks","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Origin Jumpworks is a personal luxury spacecraft manufacturer based on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The move to Terra is recent; until SEY 2913, the company was located on Earth (Sol III), and had a policy only to use materials created in the Sol System to manufacture its [600 line](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-600-series) of ships. Since the move, it has changed its outsourcing policy to accept components from across the UEE. The [300i](gp:0j46jjYgOn) and [890 Jump](gp:RzPoqed1Jr) are among its bestselling designs.","g":["terra iii","terra","spacecraft manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ebeeab2a-a9cb-46bc-aefa-6db0fd6016d7"},
{"id":"orion","gp":"VyvYqXEgPv","t":"Orion","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Orion is a mobile mining platform manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). It was designed as a solution for mining concerns that wish to conduct operations using a single ship. Built with an array of dedicated mining equipment, it includes extensive storage for resources, drone docks, and an on-board refinery. RSI advertises the ship as a \"one and done\" solution for large scale-mining that allows crews to locate, identify, and then extract minerals without needing additional support vessels. It is the largest civilian ship type currently sold by RSI.","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","mining","heavy mining"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5a8c0301-2eb5-44a8-9ce2-7c38305572fc"},
{"id":"orion-belt-alpha","gp":"V3GrKl6dyN","t":"Orion Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Orion belt alpha is the only asteroid belt in the Orion system. It orbits the system's sun between [Armitage (Orion III)](gp:RL6KLK4ylo) and the gas giant [Orion IV](gp:0KxK3vQk3Y). In 2699, [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) discovered deposits of gold and platinum there and set up small mines. However, these were abandoned when Humans fled the system after the [Battle of Orion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) in 2712. [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) have been observed harvesting resources from some of the belt's asteroids.","g":["asteroid belt","orion system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f555d717-901e-4ce7-ae6a-800b81941e45"},
{"id":"orion-i","gp":"VYLNwNvmxx","t":"Orion I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Orion I is a protoplanet in the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled [Orion system](gp:VlMpwMky6d). In 2709, the largest stellar flare yet recorded in the system erupted from its sun, melting the majority of Orion I's sun-facing surface. After the lava fully cooled, one side of the planet became a mixture of solidified lava, glass, and charred rock.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","orion system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ee6dc181-0e3c-4a88-946d-f6ac591fab0d"},
{"id":"orion-ii","gp":"VJXwowOzw5","t":"Orion II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Orion II is the second planet from the sun of the [Orion system](gp:VlMpwMky6d).  A smog planet, it has a high-pressure atmosphere composed of carbon dioxide and sulfuric acid, giving the planet a yellow-brown appearance. There have so far been no recorded spacecraft landings on the planet's surface; however, scans have detected anomalies that may be structures. Scientific interest in Orion II was disrupted when the [system was lost](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) to the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) in 2712.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","orion system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fad464cb-c09b-4049-acc5-d29549ede372"},
{"id":"orion-iv","gp":"0KxK3vQk3Y","t":"Orion IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Orion IV is a gas giant in the [Orion system](gp:VlMpwMky6d), nicknamed \"Abyss\" for its iconic deep black atmosphere. So little light reflects from Abyss that it is difficult to observe with the naked eye, save for a faint red glow that gives it the appearance of a lump of slightly glowing coal. Some tourists before the 2712 [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)[invasion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) visited the system solely to see Abyss in person.","g":["abyss","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","orion system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/caf3fc6d-3c5f-47ac-8250-37386e9e536b"},
{"id":"orion-system","gp":"VlMpwMky6d","t":"Orion System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Orion system is a planetary system in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), formerly of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). [Armitage (Orion III)](gp:RL6KLK4ylo) was once a recognized planet with [Senatorial](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) representation in the UEE. It was also the site of the UEE's violent first contact with the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) in SEY 2681. In 2712, the Vanduul launched a [mass invasion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) that forced the UEE to cede the system.","g":["vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/802afae6-9a5e-496f-8c9f-6af97c227aee"},
{"id":"orison","gp":"V7dgN8Pkrm","t":"Orison","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"# ORISON\n\nOrison is a city based on a series of interconnected floating platforms located in the upper atmosphere of [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav). Originally constructed by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) to provide repair facilities for their capital ships, [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) looked at the existing infrastructure as an ideal location for their commercial shipbuilding operations. Over time, as the city drifts from its position, it must be occasionally moved into safe orbit by the synchronized firing of large thrusters built into each platform. Due to the gas giant Crusader's natural beauty and the presence of unique fauna such as the [stormwal](gp:RX34BjN2NK), Orison has become a popular tourist destination for visitors to the Stanton system. Cloudview Center serves as the main hub for habitation, tourism, and commerce. The Skyway Shuttle provides public transportation between platforms. \n\n# HISTORY \nIn the mid-2800s SEY, the discovery of natural hydrogen and oxygen on the low-mass gas giant Stanton II made waves in the UEE. Colonization of a gas giant, long considered impossible, was now in reach. Initially, the planet was claimed by the UEE Navy, who constructed a series of platforms in 2855 designed to float in the upper reaches of the atmosphere in a region with gravity friendly to [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) as a way to work on its capital ships in a breathable atmosphere. For a few years, a skeleton crew served on the platforms, conducting repairs as needed for the vessels that passed through the system. \n\nWhen the UEE made the decision to offer Stanton II up for sale in 2865, CEO of Crusader Industries Kelly Caplan purchased it. She considered the latticework of platforms the ideal place to save credits on the manufacture of their massive ships. After officially taking possession of the planet, CI converted the main capital ship repair drydock, Providence Platform, into a manufacturing center for commercial spacecraft. The company went on to save 40% on ship construction costs after only a year. \n\nCaplan's success earned her a position of trust with the board of directors, who were initially skeptical of her plan to buy Stanton II. Her next proposal, to use a portion of the company's new profits to develop the platforms beyond the shipyard complex, was approved the day the documentation was submitted. She named the settlement Orison after an old Human word for \"prayer,\" in reference to what she described as the \"meditative nature\" of Crusader.\n\n# CITYSCAPE \nNamed after the founder of CI, the August Dunlow Spaceport is the city's main point of entry and is connected via Skyway Shuttle to the industrial district's Providence Platform and the commercial and residential district's Cloudview Center. The Cloudview platforms contain residences, shops, places to eat and drink, a Crusader Industries Showroom, Orison General Hospital, the Crusader Visitor's Center, and other amenities. Parks and other plant-filled areas built to invoke nature are scattered throughout each district. The iconic hosanna tree that decorates the walkways was created by CI to withstand high winds and low humidity, to self-pollinate, and beautify Orison with its pink flowers.\n\n# TOURISM \nOrison enjoys a steady stream of tourists to the Stanton system, drawn to Crusader for its scenic aspects and unique ecosystem. Visitors interested in the skies of Crusader can visit the Grande Observatory underneath the visitor's center, which provides views of Crusader's prismatic clouds. Storms deep in the atmosphere can be observed there, along with passing animals that live their lives in the air.\n\nOne such animal, the stormwal, is another of Orison's main attractions. A colossal creature that can grow up to 100 meters long, the stormwal is a planktivore that subsists on the thousands of tiny plankton-like animals that float in the currents of the wind. Enthusiasts can board a Discovery Tour to visit the nearby Stormwal Sanctuary and observe these majestic fauna in their natural habitat. Those more inclined to stay in Orison can visit the stormwal statute \"Until Then\" by artist Biphasha Zhu in the Cloudview Center.","g":["crusader","stanton ii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://static.robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/upload/b915a7f6-9886-412e-bdaf-5212dbf8bccc"},
{"id":"orm","gp":"RzPoqZXqZz","t":"Orm","k":"culture","c":["Civilizations"],"x":"The Orm are a developing civilization indigenous to the northern polar region of Xis (Kellog II) capable of creating tools, hunting, and building shelter. Xenoanthropologists estimate that it will be ten or more millennia before they are capable of space flight. Study of the Orm is restricted to observational research only under the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP).","g":["developing civilizations","xis","kellog ii","fair chance act","extant civilizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b47ccd6b-eac7-46a4-ba7c-e52ed435f525"},
{"id":"osha-kilian-vi","gp":"VDzzWMPo55","t":"Osha (Kilian VI)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Osha is a [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) super-Earth located in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Many of the original settlers of Osha were service members' families and [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) support personnel due to its proximity to [MacArthur (Kilian V)](gp:Rz22dGBlnz). While most of the people on Osha are connected to the military in some way, the planet has developed a strong music scene thanks to the varied cultural influences of its inhabitants.","g":["osha","kilian vi","kilian system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/178785bb-87ae-4983-b67a-559b59785e43"},
{"id":"osiris-belt-alpha","gp":"0QlPPynjOQ","t":"Osiris Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Osiris belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Osiris system](gp:0qaJeqWBZD). One of the densest belts so far discovered, it experiences frequent collisions between asteroids, creating fields of debris that contribute to the already hazardous travel conditions. A catastrophic collision could endanger the developing life on [Etos (Osiris I)](gp:RAXPPX7g77). The [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military patrols the area to monitor for and divert or destroy any rogue asteroids that may become an issue.","g":["asteroid belt","osiris system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d5e68ad2-4e19-4812-9131-f85880502ff6"},
{"id":"osiris-ii","gp":"RAXPP5ZvLA","t":"Osiris II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Osiris II is the second planet from the sun of the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Osiris system](gp:0qaJeqWBZD). Although access to the system is limited by the FCA, the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government has allowed the placement of multiple fuel refineries to help offset the cost of the long-term observation program aboard [OB station Kobold](gp:Rvlxxq9Dn3). An outbreak of smuggling incidents starting in 2931 that utilized these platforms as launching points has resulted in increasingly negative press over their presence.","g":["uninhabitable planet","not habitable","osiris system","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8aaaef96-13ef-46ad-84fa-a6f2a528e0f4"},
{"id":"osiris-system","gp":"0qaJeqWBZD","t":"Osiris System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Osiris system is a protected planetary system that consists of a K-type main sequence star, a terrestrial planet, a gas giant, and an asteroid belt. Discovered in 2788, it became the first system to be protected under the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) when detailed surveys, delayed by the [events](gp:01dWeqnMr1) of the [anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7), finally concluded in 2799 and revealed a complex biosphere beneath the cloud cover of [Osiris I](gp:RAXPPX7g77) (later nicknamed Etos). [OB station Kobold](gp:Rvlxxq9Dn3), tasked with observing and protecting the developing life on Etos, sits in one of the planet's Lagrange points.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7c3c2aea-fee9-468c-a3f0-6e6721d58c7c"},
{"id":"oso-i","gp":"RWo6GEwxrp","t":"Oso I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oso I is a terrestrial planet on the [Oso system](gp:bZkAMEarPd), and is the first world from its sun. Tidally locked, one of its sides permanently faces its star, leaving the other side dark and cold. The warm side of Oso I is covered in a sea of lava that ends at the dividing line between night and day. Early surveys found that the reddish-black crust on the cool side was rich in iron. Before the [Osoians](gp:0NwpEy2LNM) were discovered on neighboring planet [Oso II](gp:Rw19lYy9D7), Oasis Resort had given a press conference announcing speculative plans to create a luxury hotel with \"sweeping views of the awe-inspiring lava sea\" on a chain of islands near the solar terminus. They were forced to cancel their scheme when the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) was applied.","g":["oso system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/770fc250-0034-4c0e-bf7c-d74883b91608"},
{"id":"oso-ii","gp":"Rw19lYy9D7","t":"Oso II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oso II is an inhabited terrestrial planet in the [Oso system](gp:bZkAMEarPd), best known as the home of the developing [Osoian](gp:0NwpEy2LNM) civilization. The second world from its sun, it sits in a temperate location in the green band and is covered in lushly forested continents and brackish liquid water oceans. While the atmosphere is naturally breathable, landing is prohibited in the interest of protecting the [Osoians](gp:0NwpEy2LNM) from outside interference and potential poachers. Its high-gravity environment has led to the evolution of many unique species that are a favorite research subject of xenobiologists stationed at off-world observation platforms.","g":["oso system","habitable","habitable planet","osoian planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/89a6952a-df61-48c1-8f20-f862f9f063ab"},
{"id":"oso-iii","gp":"0rxanlPMQ3","t":"Oso III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oso III is a gas giant in the [Oso system](gp:bZkAMEarPd) and is the third planet from its sun. Slightly green and white in color, its atmosphere is rich in silicate and iron clouds. Evidence suggests that it was once a rogue planet that was pulled into orbit around Oso's star at some point before the evolution of the [Osoians](gp:0NwpEy2LNM) on neighboring planet [Oso II](gp:Rw19lYy9D7). Comets that pass through the Oso system are sometimes pulled into Oso III's atmosphere, where they are destroyed by high temperatures and violent weather conditions.","g":["oso system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0df2d092-c4ce-4d6d-80f7-bedec65d948b"},
{"id":"oso-iv","gp":"0ODdLElxle","t":"Oso IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oso IV is a terrestrial planet in the [Oso system](gp:bZkAMEarPd), and is the fourth planet from its sun. Lacking a core, it has an undifferentiated interior that is rich in a wide variety of minerals. Soldiers from the nearby [United Empire of Earth UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Army observation base [Chimera](gp:RMN2oE45WK) must keep Oso IV under guard to prevent rogue mining operations from forming there. In 2877, the [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) made its largest arrest when they discovered an underground mine in the equatorial region that had been in use undetected for over 3 SEY.","g":["oso system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/13941a2c-3956-4d54-a0d7-007d10d79b4b"},
{"id":"oso-system","gp":"bZkAMEarPd","t":"Oso System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Oso system is a [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected planetary system that consists of an F-type main sequence star, three terrestrial planets, one gas giant, one ice giant, and one dwarf planet. Discovered in 2861 by amateur explorer Errol Navis, who named it after his daughter, it seemed to be an excellent prospect for terraforming until a young civilization was detected on [Oso II](gp:Rw19lYy9D7). Barred from their development plans, some surveying corporations leaked their planetary assessment findings to the press in an attempt to convince the public that it was the [United Empire of Earth's](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) duty to open the system. From these leaks, a popular movement formed in favor of uplifting the intelligent [Osoians](gp:0NwpEy2LNM). Ultimately, the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) chose to invoke the Fair Chance Act and set up a permanent military station to keep the system safe from potentially unscrupulous visitors.","g":["developing system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/152fc788-d9c9-43d4-807e-cdc88e91a3aa"},
{"id":"oso-v","gp":"RL6yYEnXmL","t":"Oso V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oso V is an ice giant in the [Oso system](gp:bZkAMEarPd), and is the fifth planet from its star. With an atmosphere of ammonia vapor and other volatiles, it is nearly white in appearance, and has a complex, layered cloud structure. Thanks to its distance from [Oso II](gp:Rw19lYy9D7), it supports a [Covalex](gp:V3qgXNEGQW) shipping hub and a handful of utility stations that help supply [OB Station Chimera](gp:RMN2oE45WK) and any haulers that pass through the system with food and fuel.","g":["oso system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0ca96914-ddcf-40ca-8dba-902f5258784a"},
{"id":"oso-vi","gp":"R9vPNk2oPk","t":"Oso VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oso VI is a dwarf planet in the [Oso system](gp:bZkAMEarPd), and is the last planet from its star. Uniform in appearance, its surface is coated in tholin, a hydrocarbon sludge that colors the world dark red and covers up deep layers of methane and water ice. Like neighboring planet [Oso V](gp:RL6yYEnXmL), it is orbited by several utility stations that serve haulers who pass through the system on their regular trading routes.","g":["oso system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9eedc7d7-fc3c-4521-8ded-43d3e9268389"},
{"id":"osoians","gp":"0NwpEy2LNM","t":"Osoians","k":"species","c":["Civilizations"],"x":"The Osoians are a developing civilization indigenous to Oso II. They are in an early stage of development, having discovered tools and weapons, and created villages with free-standing dwellings. Language scientists are particularly interested in the Osoians thanks to their unique method of communicating: through flashes of color generated by the skin of their foreheads. They are protected by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) under the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP).","g":["developing civilizations","oso ii","fair chance act","extant civilizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/693ad7e1-5be9-4d1c-bbf3-3c917b5b3f8c"},
{"id":"oya-i","gp":"Var16zLQmx","t":"Oya I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oya I is a terrestrial planet in the [Oya system](gp:0KxGow1ly4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the first planet from its sun. Small and hot, its barren landscape is riddled with deep canyons that were formed by ancient lava flows. Although all of its volcanoes appear to be extinct, the planet is still geologically active and experiences quakes, with major events estimated to occur every few million years. Its youngest volcano is roughly 100 million years old.","g":["oya system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bbf5a2f9-d0ae-4002-94e9-d819771b3ea5"},
{"id":"oya-ii","gp":"0Ql5X9xE5o","t":"Oya II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oya II is the second planet from the sun of the [Oya system](gp:0KxGow1ly4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Although it lacks a metallic core, it has a magnetic field that is generated by large deposits of magnesium oxide deep in its mantle. During the 2580s (SEY), a group of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) anti-[Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) separatists set up a small settlement on Oya II, choosing it over the naturally-inhabitable Oya III due to the presence of a small Xi'an colony there. They were able to remain undetected by the Xi'an colonists until MXY III.882 (SEY 2587), when the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) located the Oya-[Castra](gp:R4jxkAd8El) jump point while trying to track down the separatists who had been conducting raids in the Castra system when they were low on supplies. Xi'an colonists who witnessed the UEE Navy ships attacking and killing their own people reported to the Xi'an government that there seemed to be elements within the UEE that rejected Messer leadership. Currently, the planet is home to several active mining operations.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet","oya system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/45721ce4-127e-4cd7-8136-fa98ab474207"},
{"id":"oya-iii","gp":"RkGwyKpgr9","t":"Oya III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oya III is a terrestrial planet in the [Oya system](gp:0KxGow1ly4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the third world from its sun. With a temperate climate and naturally-occurring nitrogen-oxygen atmosphere, it was identified as a prime colony world by the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) after its MXY III.866 (SEY 2566) discovery. A small settlement was established there that same year. However, the Xi'an government recalled the inhabitants in MXY III 882 (SEY 2587), when the UEE located the Oya-[Castra](gp:R4jxkAd8El) jump point. At the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793 / MXY III.838 - III.1044), the newly-reformed UEE government returned the former settlement to the Xi'an Empire as a gesture of goodwill. It is the only sovereign alien territory contained within the UEE.","g":["oya system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e00f8870-131f-4622-86af-87b623b69447"},
{"id":"oya-iv","gp":"RkGwyKDGp9","t":"Oya IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Oya IV is a dwarf planet in the [Oya system](gp:0KxGow1ly4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the fourth world from its sun. Reddish-pink in color, its surface is encased in thick methane-ethane that is coated with a thin layer of hydrocarbon sludge. In the 28th century SEY, there was a short-lived cosmetics trend that claimed the surface of Oya IV had \"age-reversing\" properties and utilized sludge harvest from the planet's surface in a wide variety of skin care products.","g":["oya system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3a9ba0d8-a1e2-448c-96b8-79739d69ae74"},
{"id":"oya-system","gp":"0KxGow1ly4","t":"Oya System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Oya system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that consists of a G-type main sequence star, three terrestrial planets, and one planetoid. In MXY III.866 (SEY 2566), it was discovered by test pilots for [House Ng.at'ak](gp:RWolrAj1vm) during the preliminary flight of a cargo ship prototype. The Emperor ordered the construction of a colony on the [third planet](gp:RkGwyKpgr9) from the star, which had a naturally-occurring nitrogen-oxygen atmosphere and favorable climate conditions. However, after Lieutenant Eli Price of the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) located the Oya-[Castra](gp:R4jxkAd8El) jump point in SEY 2587 (MXY III.882), the Xi'an government recalled the colonists and left their unfinished settlement abandoned. The UEE claimed the system and added it to the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO), naming it Oya after an ancient [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) deity of wind, storms, and death.","g":["uee system","perry line"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d66b560d-eb32-4395-9faf-2024f0c38b99"},
{"id":"oza","gp":"RPDDZz4Zam","t":"Oza","k":"life","c":["Food and Beverages","Plants"],"x":"The oza is a commercial tree fruit grown in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A hybrid of citrus trees that originated on Earth (Sol III), the oza was first grown on [Angeli (Croshaw II)](gp:0QlxqwG14Q) in 2812. Underneath its deep green rind is bright orange flesh with a tart, sweet, and bitter taste. Generally considered by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) to be too fibrous to eat, the juice is prized for its complex taste and is popularly used as flavoring in sweet and savory applications, as well as in numerous cocktail recipes.","g":["fruit","trees","food"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ef475e68-c101-4955-9398-e15a781c47ec"},
{"id":"p-52-merlin","gp":"RXlXBj5rrk","t":"P-52 Merlin","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The P-52 Merlin is an ultralight snub fighter spacecraft developed by [Kruger Intergalactic](gp:0Gz5BWEOEg). [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) commissioned the original design of the Merlin for use aboard models of the Constellation multi-crew spacecraft. Merlins require a mothership or static facility to operate, as they lack a quantum drive system.","g":["kruger intergalactic","snub fighter","human spacecraft","fighter","snub"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/074d7e61-2108-4ce1-960a-c2177f4c4522"},
{"id":"p-72-archimedes","gp":"RMXyBO9elE","t":"P-72 Archimedes","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The P-72 Archimedes is an ultralight luxury racing spacecraft developed by [Kruger Intergalactic](gp:0Gz5BWEOEg) and spun off of the [P-52 Merlin](gp:RXlXBj5rrk). [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) sponsored development of the design to pair with their Constellation Phoenix luxury spacecraft. While visually similar to the Merlin, the Archimedes features additional luxury styling and a special focus on performance realized through the use of lighter hull materials and an additional power plant intake.","g":["racing","kruger intergalactic","human spacecraft","luxury"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0ebde727-b18c-41df-9688-d6ddca3bee03"},
{"id":"puayaha-rila-ii","gp":"RWoOMAm5yw","t":"P.uay'aha (R.il'a II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"P.uay'aha (R.il'a II) is the second planet from the sun of the [R.il'a system]([R.il'a system](gp:Rw1xWXME1B)), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Classified as a puffy planet, or hot Jupiter, it has a large radius but a very low density due to its proximity from its star. Since R.il'a's discovery, the planet has been the main source of hydrogen for all the ships in the system, and is orbited by multiple automated refinery platforms and refueling stations.","g":["p.uay'aha","r.il'a i","r.il'a system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"p5-g-gladius","gp":"0j46NP5eB3","t":"P5G Gladius","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"# P5G Gladius\n\nThe Gladius is a long-serving military light fighter spacecraft developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) and first utilized by the [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) in the 26th century SEY. Its frame is easily modified, and has undergone numerous technology retrofits in the past three centuries. Beginning in the 2930s, squadrons began to phase out the Gladius and convert to newer craft like the [F8 Lightning](gp:bZwQ7r6nkE), the [F7A Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk), and the [Anvil](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) [Arrow](gp:box5ODOk6L), and surplus Gladius became available on the civilian market. In 2951, Aegis increased the budget on Gladius production and invested in upgrade packages and next-generation variants of the design. \n\n\n# DEVELOPMENT\nThe Gladius' development began in 2573 as a replacement for the obsolete Elio-Harman [Stiletto](gp:R4ZG3A66v5) interceptor, which suffered from an inability to adapt to more modern shield components and faced increased supply chain issues following [Elio-Harman Aerospace's](gp:Vgg7yZjdGn) bankruptcy. The Gladius was created for service aboard smaller capital ships that weren't outfitted for full-scale aerospace operations. It was also the first ship to introduce a civilian-style modularity into fighter design; this allowed the Gladius to be quickly upgraded or outfitted for other missions without requiring a longer stay in the hangar for a refit. \n\nThe Gladius saw widespread adoption upon its rollout in 2579. Its base model has been continually upgraded over the years, to the point that a present day Gladius Mark VI pilot would have a difficult time flying a Mark I or Mark II model. \n\n# SERVICE HISTORY\nThe Gladius has seen service in almost every type of operation and engagement involving the Human military for the past three centuries and recorded thousands of kills against pirates, armed rebels, raiders, and unidentified aggressors. Anti-piracy operations, reconnaissance, search and rescue missions, jump scouting (with extended duration packs installed) and countless other roles have been fulfilled by the Gladius. \n\nThe Gladius has proven effective against the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) Blade, to which it is considered a rough 1:1 match. The design suffers against the latest [Blade](gp:RegdeBENkw) spacecraft encountered on the frontier, although exceptional Gladius pilots have made headway in developing techniques for countering the superior alien starfighters. A safer \"weave style\" maneuver has also been adapted for countering superior Vanduul forces. \n\n# CURRENT STATUS\nThe rollout of the F8 Lightning has changed the dynamic for the UEE fighter force, freeing up additional battle-tested Hornets to be handed down. The Navy has begun swapping second tier Gladius units over to Hornets as more elite squadrons go from the Hornet to the Lightning. This has not impacted every duty station as the Hornet is not a 1:1 replacement for the lighter Gladius. Nevertheless, the decommissioning process has created a major surplus of Gladius hulls and parts which have been made available to civilians with their weapons technologies and other classified components removed.\n\nGladius and their parts are still produced by Aegis, though not in the numbers seen at the height of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792). There is an upgrade team still at work which continues to develop functionality for the now widespread civilian adoption of the Gladius.","g":["gladius","aegis dynamics","light fighter","fighter","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a5ad0f3a-2ce4-48bd-87bb-4e4860a3b44c"},
{"id":"parker-terrell","gp":"Rxnza3Qdqd","t":"Parker Terrell","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Parker Terrell (2888 - present) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) investigative journalist and host of the talk show [Plain Truth](gp:bZwQ6lpJEd). Until 2943, he worked as a reporter for [New United](gp:RAdjeJe5Y7), where he published multiple exposés and built a reputation as a tenacious and opinionated columnist. Terrell vanished for three months after appearing on the debate program [Showdown!](gp:RwZBw4Lrxz), where he asserted that the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government had illegally used a super-weapon to destroy the surface of the planet Ellis XI. After he was found on Vann (Croshaw III) and questioned by [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) officials, he again appeared on *Showdown!* and insisted that he had been chased into hiding for speaking the truth. *New United* shortly terminated his contract. In the wake of this controversy, Terrell accepted a job offer from [Spectrum](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/spectrum-show) to develop a talk show. *Plain Truth* debuted in 2944.","g":["plain truth"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fc606fd1-4a89-451a-824a-082ac4e84bee"},
{"id":"patek-coen","gp":"R9vPd4ZjK7","t":"Patek Coen","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Patek Coen (2786 - 2867) was a navjumper most notable for his discovery of the [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv) in 2811. Born on [Kampos (Ellis IV)](gp:RAXxrxr7M5), Coen began his career as a pilot for a private ferry service from Kampos to neighboring planets [Green (Ellis III)](gp:RWoNrNeLKP) and [Noble (Ellis V)](gp:V8W545NrKo). He became interested in navjumping after reading a biography on [Antoine Lebec](gp:0ODddzO7Dq), and took on private training courses in navigation and detection in his spare time. It was his goal to eventually live in a system he discovered himself. After nearly a decade of searching, Coen found a jump point to Kellog, but was disappointed when the existence of the [Orm](gp:RzPoqZXqZz) civilization on [Kellog II](gp:bmGJeMv2oK) came to light and the system was placed under the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP), meaning that he could not reside there. He retired from navjumping in 2839 when his autobiography *A Refuted Dream* became an unexpected bestseller.","g":["patek-coen","kellog system","kampos","ellis iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/05ba40c2-9a0a-41d5-b824-46273460406b"},
{"id":"paul-lesalle","gp":"VgE5krya9w","t":"Paul LeSalle","k":"people","c":["Human","People"],"x":"Paul LeSalle (2881 - present) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) businessman, former chairperson of the [Centralist](gp:01dWmzB3aG) party (2942 - 2948), and former Senator of Cassel (Goss II) (2915 - 2939). As a Senator, he advocated for lower taxes and created an incentive system for businesses to move their operations to Cassel. LeSalle retired from the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) in 2939, shortly after his former business partner Alin Hastings was convicted of multiple counts of embezzlement and tax evasion. After spending three years growing his hauling company and spending time with his family, he returned to politics as chair of the Centralist party in 2942. In April 2950, he succeeded in his bid to be elected as one of the five final candidates for [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). His campaign promised to include tax breaks for corporations and small business owners, reassessing the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP), creating programs to support bounty hunters and local militias, mandatory military service to receive certain civil benefits, and the implementation of the Safe & Secure Initiative: a program to replace jail time for minor criminal infractions with a system of fines and service.","g":["uee senator"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fb9612cd-3d89-4195-8507-6922b788294d"},
{"id":"pax-humana","gp":"RAX28pjKWM","t":"Pax Humana","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"Pax Humana is a holiday celebrated annually on November eighth in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It was first held in 2380, when the armed forces of Earth (Sol III) were consolidated upon the foundation of [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO). To symbolize the event, military delegations from each formerly-independent coalition marched from different locations in New York City, converging at the newly-built [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ). Laurel wreaths were distributed to all soldiers, who made an oath to protect all of Humanity; the same oath that is used to swear-in recruits today. The parade and the ceremony remain the holiday's main event, with the [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q), and [Marines](gp:V7d5ZYEr1a) marching towards the Senate. In the spirit of service, many celebrants spend the day volunteering with charities or planning special events or projects.","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3b4521e8-d89f-4541-91cd-b940bf25113c"},
{"id":"pegasus","gp":"bBp64jrA7d","t":"Pegasus","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military"],"x":"The Pegasus is an escort-class carrier spacecraft and capital ship manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) for the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military. Capable of supporting the operations of over 30 fighters, it is a standard component of [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) fleets and is sometimes used as the command center for a flight squadron. Its repair bays and accommodations are able to support those aboard during long-term missions. In addition to providing protective escort for ship convoys, Pegasuses are used for fighter transportation, fleet support, and hunter-killer missions.","g":["escort carrier","capital ship","carrier","human spacecraft","roberts space industries (rsi)","military spacecraft"]},
{"id":"penselin-davien-2a","gp":"V8WkA3d7LG","t":"Penselin (Davien 2a)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Penselin is the moon of [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5), a planet in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It was named for Dr. Daniel Penselin, a physicist who died there testing his improvements to the quantum drive. Its radius is only a few meters longer than that of Earth's moon.","g":["penselin ","davien 2a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","davien system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7b17d40a-405c-41bc-90b8-e69f56723a3c"},
{"id":"peoples-alliance","gp":"Vy2v4qgG4v","t":"People's Alliance","k":"faction","c":["Organizations","Politics","Human"],"x":"The People's Alliance is an independent [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) political group that exists outside the governance of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) and seeks a social order based on egalitarianism and community. It formed during the reign of [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Corsen Messer V](gp:0OaB8O6awO) (SEY 2609 - 2662), in response to his increasingly harsh policies on crime, which included broad expansion of the death penalty and suspension of the right to trial for political crimes. The group initially formed as they participated in community aid programs and staged peaceful protests of the new laws. However, as more and more of their members were arrested, imprisoned, and executed, their goals shifted from one of changing Human society to creating a society of their own. They founded [a settlement](gp:0dXQqBMAOp) in 2655, utilizing an abandoned mining outpost on the asteroid [Delamar](gp:0GxoZnAGrg) in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3). Named Levski after a historical revolutionary figure, the People's Alliance welcomed anyone fleeing the rule of the [Messers](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/messer-dynasty), and the community grew. Today, the People's Alliance continues to accept new residents who wish to live away from under government rule.","g":["delamar","levski","human political group"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a34b2c49-3271-4a42-a9cf-0ccb4f0cdd81"},
{"id":"perry-line","gp":"V8gJQMY9mO","t":"Perry Line","k":"faction","c":["History","Politics","Xi'an","Human"],"x":"The Perry Line was a military designation for a group of eight planetary systems that marked the borderlands between [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) and [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-controlled space during the [Xi'an-Human Cold War (2530-2789)](gp:RXlLjDewkZ). Named after Armistead Perry, the Navy general who introduced the strategy in 2542, the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) designated the systems as no-fly zones and utilized them as military staging grounds. Each system was named after a god of war. After the signing of the Perry Line Pact dissolved the militarized zone in 2793, the systems were divided evenly between the Xi'an and Human governments. While the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) maintained the original names for its systems ([Gurzil](gp:0Kxydrxd45), [Horus](gp:bo1JGZpvwZ), [Oya](gp:0KxGow1ly4), and [Tohil](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9)), the Xi'an renamed the Hadur ([Yā'mon](gp:VarxDJ5yLo)), Indra ([Kyuk'ya](gp:RWo69Xx3dP)), Pallas ([Th.us'ūng](gp:V8WeExnJge)), and Virtus ([La'uo](gp:R6demJ8Xmq)) systems.","g":["messer era","perry line pact","xi'an-human cold war"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2ac09a31-c2a5-4813-8fc1-8231f20a0620"},
{"id":"perry-line-pact","gp":"0Gx9GdvqAQ","t":"Perry Line Pact","k":"faction","c":["Politics","History"],"x":"The Perry Line Pact is a peace treaty between the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) and the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) (SaoXy'an). After the signing of the [Akari-Kr.ē Treaty](gp:bE3rKrl5z6) brought an unofficial end to the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ), the question of what to do with the eight disputed planetary systems that made up the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) remained. In 2793, Ambassador Ramon Coen of the UEE presented a proposal to the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government outlining a plan to divide the systems fairly between the UEE and the Xi'an Empire. Additionally, the treaty required the two governments to work together in removing anti-ship mines from the Perry Line systems, and that they keep their borders open to one another. The signing of this treaty officially ended the Cold War.","g":["perry line","xi'an-human cold war","ramon coen"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e43be087-f334-4129-b9b2-07531f8f6800"},
{"id":"persei-rhetor-ii","gp":"0ODlqM6zKO","t":"Persei (Rhetor II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Persei is the second planet from the sun of the [Rhetor system](gp:0ODlqMJXmP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Soon after the system was discovered in 2287, surveyors identified vast deposits of rare elements in the crust. The [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) government used profits from selling the mining rights on Persei to fund the [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) of [Reisee (Rhetor III)](gp:0QljXw43Ev) and [Mentor (Rhetor IV)](gp:RPDlZJeDLX). Land not used for mining was set aside for the state-run [University of Persei](gp:Rz2XZkMrmN). Today, Persei is home to many research public and private research institutions, most notably the University of Persei Analytical Research and Quantification ([UPARQ](gp:0n1Mz2WmD7)) center.","g":["persei","rhetor ii","rhetor system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8ea6d1de-6cf2-4559-b1a0-0e729698f739"},
{"id":"perseus","gp":"bEzXg6qGe6","t":"Perseus","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human","Military"],"x":"The Perseus is a large gunship manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). First developed in 2528 for the [United Planets of Earth Navy (UPEN)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN), it was used in blockades and security patrols, most notably the Incident at Red Ridge in 2529. It became a mainstay along the former [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) after [Xi'an-Human First Contact](gp:R4ZQpYEEvx) in 2530. In 2863, it was retired from production at RSI. In 2946, [Admiral Ernst Bishop](gp:ReJaavPB3k) witnessed an aging Perseus participate in [Operation Mandrake](gp:bZkdG98WNE) and requested that an updated Perseus-class fleet be put into production. After the creation of the [Militia Mobilization Initiative](gp:RkZ96m89Jm), RSI expanded development to include a civilian version. The new Perseus, equipped with modernized weapons and a redesigned lower deck, was released in 2950.","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","gunship","heavy gunship","military spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8eb43602-86ee-4138-99d6-c171b3d75d73"},
{"id":"ptv","gp":"bBp6YmmjGJ","t":"Personal Transport Vehicle (PTV)","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Personal Transport Vehicle (PTV) is a small vehicle developed by [Greycat Industrial](gp:02BQlmgoDy). PTVs are intended for road travel and are capable of transporting two personnel and a small amount of cargo. Sometimes referred to as buggies or carts, they are commonly used in spacecraft hangars and on flight lines to deliver crews to spacecraft stored outside comfortable walking distance.","g":["ptv","greycat industrial","personal transport","transport","human vehicle"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a8527d93-b489-4c61-9ee6-e6399dc49153"},
{"id":"petram-terra-1a","gp":"0dXxPx5XNo","t":"Petram (Terra 1a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Petram is a captured carbonaceous asteroid, one of two natural satellites of [Aero (Terra I)](gp:RxnzEP5m1Q), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It orbits closer to Aero than its sister moon, [Petrus](gp:0qax2xKova).","g":["terra 1a","petram","aero moon","terra i moon","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","terra system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6a694e6b-6e7e-4ece-9b49-cf1426ff47b2"},
{"id":"petrus-terra-1b","gp":"0qax2xKova","t":"Petrus (Terra 1b)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Locations"],"x":"Petrus is a natural satellite of [Aero (Terra II)](gp:RxnzEP5m1Q), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Irregularly shaped, pockmarked with craters, and following an inclined orbit, Petrus may possibly be a remaining piece of a once larger celestial body.","g":["petrus","terra 1b","aero moon","terra i moon","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","terra system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9b953c5c-8db2-4b05-9ac5-af4baaf1abcd"},
{"id":"phares-ape","gp":"RX3Krj8Mzq","t":"Phare's Ape","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"The Phare's ape is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-like primate indigenous to Etos (Osiris I). A nocturnal animal, the ape spends its days sleeping in caves or under self-created dwellings, and its nights foraging for fruit, seeds, leaves, and other plant-based foods. Biologists believe that it has the potential to develop higher thinking thanks to its use of tools and practice of constructing shelter. It is largely due to the presence of Phare's ape that Etos is under the protection of the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP).","g":["primates","etos","osiris i"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/03633c5c-074b-4833-9b35-cad3c296f4c6"},
{"id":"phiyi-tower","gp":"01dW3XmX3L","t":"Phiyi Tower","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"The Phiyi Tower is a skyscraper located in the state of [Acheron](gp:VJOz3gMM85) on Charon III. Designed by Alia De Monde, it was constructed to inspire hope in the people of Acheron after a deadly 2934 earthquake destroyed many historical and beloved buildings. Though it is now considered a masterwork of Supermodernist architecture, at the time, its construction was costly and complex. The project also endured numerous protests claiming mistreatment of laborers.","g":["acheron","charon iii","supermodernist architecture"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/61012780-8e92-4d93-9c97-5f8d217e1617"},
{"id":"phobos-sol-4a","gp":"Rw1jNJvQk7","t":"Phobos (Sol 4a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Phobos (Sol 4a) is the closest moon to [Mars (Sol IV)](gp:Regn8D76xw), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The larger of the planet's two satellites, it is a non-spheroid object with a jagged surface covered in grooves and streaks. In the next 30 to 50 million years, Phobos will be pulled in by Mars' gravity and will break apart during its descent.","g":["phobos","sol 4a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6d45413c-dbfc-48e4-bbfb-00334770c506"},
{"id":"pipa-rila-vi","gp":"RPDeXypKKz","t":"Pi'pa (R.il'a VI)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Pi'pa (R.il'a VI) is the sixth planet from the sun of the [R.il'a system](gp:Rw1xWXME1B), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A tiny dwarf planet on the edge of the system, it has no atmosphere and maintains a frigid temperature. From the surface of Pi'pa, the system's sun appears to be a bright and distant star. During R.il'a's time as a military system, soldiers would conduct deep cold training exercises on Pi'pa, utilizing its hostile terrain to help drill survival skills into new recruits to the Xi'an military.","g":["pi'pa","r.il'a vi","r.il'a system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"pitua-lauo-i","gp":"bBz3m2e12d","t":"Pi'tua (La'uo I)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Pi'tua (La'uo I) is the first planet from the sun of the [La'uo system](gp:R6demJ8Xmq), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A chthonic planet, it was the core of a hot Jupiter until the surface of the red giant it orbits expanded. Most of its atmosphere has evaporated, and what little remains continues to sublimate away in the heat. This has created a comet-like streak of gas and dust that trails the planet on its journey around its sun.","g":["pi'tua","la'uo i","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","la'uo system","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b2110fb2-6f71-4a37-8400-12c6963857c3"},
{"id":"pico-the-penguin","gp":"V3GqNBoPDZ","t":"Pico the Penguin","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Pico the Penguin is the official mascot of [New Babbage](gp:Rw1Zl3vdW7), the largest city on [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1). Debuted in 2902 by the microTech Tourism Board as part of that year's Snow Sport Invitational, the penguin was embraced by the inhabitants of the city and around the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Pico wears a helmet and a snow jacket and often carries a snowboard in honor of the popularity of outdoor activities in New Babbage. In recent years, it has become a trend on microTech for people to place Pico plushes in various locations around the world.","g":["toys","microtech (company)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a4a4bb69-e33b-4bce-a4b3-ff4179151a4f"},
{"id":"pike-terra-ii","gp":"Rvl7EggdAr","t":"Pike (Terra II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Locations"],"x":"Pike is the second planet from the sun in the [Terra system](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). While its proximity to the sun and the thinness of its atmosphere make it a hostile environment, the rich reserves of resources on the planet have made it host to thousands of mining operations and refineries. While many outposts are built underground or in sealed arcologies to protect workers, processes are typically automated when possible in order to minimize [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) exposure to the elements.","g":["pike","terra ii","terra system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6a4b7485-7c2f-4fec-bf98-399190d91057"},
{"id":"pinecone-ellis-xiii","gp":"Rz2QE38BvN","t":"Pinecone (Ellis XIII)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Pinecone (Ellis XIII) is a protoplanet in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Nicknamed pinecone for its craggy surface, it's a major mining hub, rich in heavy metals and valuable minerals. Long-haul miners harvest resources from Pinecone, stop at [Walleye](gp:0n1Ppn9Kr9) for a refuel, and make the trek back to Earth (Sol III) to sell their cargo at a premium price.","g":["pinecone","ellis xiii","ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/76ab7010-9fb0-4e03-b06e-32ed1d08e581"},
{"id":"pingleth-rila-iii","gp":"R5p2eq7OEm","t":"Ping'leth (R.il'a III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ping'leth (R.il'a III) is the third planet from the sun of the [R.il'a system](gp:Rw1xWXME1B), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Orbiting just outside of the inner boundary of the green band, it was not terraformed when the Xi'an government initially developed two other planets in the system. The jagged mountains that dominate the planet's rocky surface were the subject of a series of abstract sculptures constructed by the famed artist [Tamsa Wheel](gp:RXlXOw9WaN) in SEY 2951.","g":["ping'leth","r.il'a iii","r.il'a system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"pioneer","gp":"R6v8glgLWn","t":"Pioneer","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Pioneer is a colonization and factory spacecraft sold by [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34), the second project pursued by the company. Introduced in 2947, the Pioneer was developed using funds from the successful Mustang series of single seat spacecraft and was intended to disrupt the then-standard process for locating, claiming and establishing homesteads on newly-explored worlds. The vessel is capable of deploying standardized claim buoys and constructing and deploying modular outposts using an onboard production line.","g":["consolidated outland","heavy construction","expedition","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8900862e-cb6f-481f-afd4-b0eb15697ffc"},
{"id":"piracy-space","gp":"0n9vE6QWGn","t":"Piracy (Space)","k":"faction","c":["Illegal Activity"],"x":"Piracy (space) is an act of organized theft and criminal violence committed by spacecraft-based attackers. Acts of piracy can range from one-off attacks by one-person spacecraft to extremely organized, highly-planned operations that make use of dozens of pirates and multiple spacecraft. Piracy tends to flourish in unclaimed [systems](gp:VaZwNWg372) or away from frequently traveled transit lines. It usually focuses on the robbery of commercial [transports'](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/passenger-transport) cargo and/or spacecraft.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f3b6be76-ae22-40e1-bfed-e2a2a4083040"},
{"id":"pitambu","gp":"0dX8WPr1qO","t":"Pitambu","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The pitambu is a leafy plant that produces fruits of the same name. Originally cultivated on [Reisse (Rhetor III)](gp:0QljXw43Ev), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)  (UEE), the pitambu can be grown in a wide variety of environments and is often found in the wild. Its leaves grow in an elliptical pattern from its stem, and the fruit has waxy, bright orange-red skin that covers bright red flesh with a mild, nutty taste. When it blooms, the flower it produces can be eaten or steeped as a tea that eases stomach pain.","g":["reisse","rhetor iii","fruiting plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3904e46d-2762-44aa-a94e-7dd49f25fac5"},
{"id":"plain-truth","gp":"bZwQ6lpJEd","t":"Plain Truth","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"# PLAIN TRUTH\n\n*The Plain Truth* is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) tabloid talk show broadcast by [SSN/CAtv](gp:0QxYwPK88l) and hosted by former [New United](gp:RAdjeJe5Y7) reporter [Parker Terrell](gp:Rxnza3Qdqd). It premiered in SEY 2944, in the wake of a widely reported upon, three-month disappearance by Terrell. After his sudden reappearance, Terrell was fired by his former employers at the New United and established *Plain Truth*. The show is filmed on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). It currently operates as an independent investigative unit, focusing on controversial and sensationalist Human interest and political stories. The show is often critical of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government. \n# HISTORY\nParker Terrell was an investigative journalist with the New United for 11 years, where he developed a reputation for often combative political stories. He was sometimes censured by his employers for taking too much of an editorial stance in his columns, but as his articles drew in audiences, he was retained. On 19 June 2943, Terrell appeared on the debate show *Showdown* where he asserted on the air that the UEE used an illegal super-weapon to destroy the surface of the planet Ellis XI. He disappeared less than a week later. A missing persons report was filed on 30 June. No note was found, and Terrell's personal ship was missing from its hangar. \n\nTerrell's ship was recovered from Vann (Croshaw III) on 10 August 2943. Terrell himself was discovered shortly after, on 16 September 2943. The Advocacy brought him in for questioning and released him on the same day. On 08 October 2943, Terrell appeared on *Showdown*, where he asserted that 'shadowy government agents' had chased him into hiding and repeated his accusation that the UEE had tested a planet-killing weapon on Ellis XI. After he refused to recant, the *New United* NewsOrg chose to terminate his contract.\n\nTerrell was hired by SSN/CAtv on 11 October 2943 to develop a news show. The first episode of *Plain Truth* premiered on 01 April 2944. In it, Terrell interviewed Daniel Warden, an independent courier who had been stopped by UEE Customs upon his entry in the Helios system and unlawfully detained for three weeks. During his imprisonment, Warden was questioned by Advocacy agents about people he had never met and about his activities in the Nexus system. Following Terrell's broadcast, Warden received an undisclosed amount of credits as compensation from the UEE for his detention. Since then, *Plain Truth* has run on a weekly basis, and has enjoyed moderate ratings. \n# CONTROVERSY\nWhile *Plain Truth* is billed as a purely investigative journalism-centered program, there has been criticism from other news organizations that the show promotes conspiracy theories rather than fact. \n\nIn 2945, Terrell interviewed Janis Tarkis, former journalist for the Terra Gazette. Tarkis asserted that the Galactic Aid Organization (GAO), a well-known charity that supplies those in need with cybernetic and artificial organs, had sold faulty organs on the black market for profit. After the episode aired, offices of the GAO across the UEE were inundated with comms accusing them of organ harvesting. Donations sharply dropped and multiple offices were vandalized. Terrell claimed no responsibility, stating that his job was to bring the truth to people, not dictate their actions. A subsequent formal investigation into GAO revealed no wrongdoing.","g":["parker terrell","news show","spectrum show","terra","terra iii","talk show"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4f0a3104-e63a-4d84-a3fd-182c5383e496"},
{"id":"planetary-surveying","gp":"V7gMW87ekn","t":"Planetary Surveying","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Planetary surveying is the profession of assessing and documenting the potential of a planet. Usually enacted upon initial discovery, surveyors map and catalog the planet's natural resources, and create recommendations that will determine the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) possibility of a planet, evaluate the planet's potential economic value, and identify prime settlement areas. Planetary surveyors use a mix of physics, engineering, astronomical and geological science, and applied technique to achieve their tasks. A surveyor must also be familiar with law in addition to their many other skills. Once a planet is surveyed, a surveyor usually continues in their work with the cooperation of a terraforming team or corporate and governmental concerns.","g":["terraforming"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/edc48860-1c9e-446b-a09c-9fcecb146937"},
{"id":"platform-based-colonization","gp":"R6v8mW6rxD","t":"Platform-Based Colonization","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Platform-based colonization is the use of platforms as bases for building colonies in environments which provide no other means of stable settlement. Platforms can be orbital, situated within a planet's atmosphere, built onto a planet's bedrock, or can float on bodies of water. Crusader (Stanton II) and Ergo (Nemo III) contain examples of this practice.","g":["colonization method"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a86ed005-12ea-410c-b09d-4e4eaa14dd7d"},
{"id":"pluto-sol-ix","gp":"0qa1Zo37jk","t":"Pluto (Sol IX)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Pluto (Sol XI) is a dwarf planet and one of the farthest celestial bodies from the sun of the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Not the most distant object, it is included as an honorary ninth planet in star charts due to its relative proximity to the [Croshaw](gp:0qanKAEJwp)-Sol jump point. After [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) first discovered jump points, interest in Pluto skyrocketed and countless permanent, sealed settlements, shops, and research stations were erected there despite its frigid climate. This gave Pluto enough population and economic importance that it was one of the earliest planets to be recognized by the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) after its formation in SEY 2380.","g":["pluto","sol ix","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","sol system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d2af2238-06ef-45dd-8be4-8be98aa5819c"},
{"id":"polaris","gp":"VJOzNNAGe4","t":"Polaris","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The Polaris is a corvette-class capital ship developed by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) for the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Navy. Intended for combat situations, the Polaris was designed with a command center, repair and refuel facilities, and a bay capable of transporting one or more small fighters. It is used by the UEEN to conduct patrols and conduct search and rescue operations. Development of this ship was accelerated as a part of the [Militia Mobilization Initiative](gp:RkZ96m89Jm) (2946), after which a limited number of Polaris were made available for purchase on the civilian market.","g":["corvette","roberts space industries (rsi)","capital ship","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2a0f9f3c-ad11-4a08-823a-094d4921f5a8"},
{"id":"polaris-ironworks","gp":"bZklxvBj6D","t":"Polaris Ironworks","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Polaris Ironworks is a company that manufactures personal armor, components for vehicles and ships, and other industrial goods. Solely a component maker until SEY 2929, it branched out into armor production when a stylized set featured in one of its advertising campaigns attracted interest from consumers. Goods made by Polaris Ironworks have a rough, industrial look and feel.","g":["armor manufacturer","commercial and industrial goods manufacturer","spacecraft component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/42f560dd-3fd6-4af5-8d6c-f871559410a6"},
{"id":"port-conrad","gp":"R9v7LK4lW7","t":"Port Conrad","k":"place","c":["Settlements"],"x":"Port Conrad is a former city on [Armitage (Orion III)](gp:RL6KLK4ylo) in the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled [Orion system](gp:VlMpwMky6d). Founded in the mid-2600s by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), Port Conrad was the fastest-growing settlement on Armitage. It was on the way to being selected as the new capital after Armitage's 2711 recognition from the UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ). However, it was lost to the Vanduul in 2712. Today, burnt-out buildings, craters, and other ruins cover what was once a vibrant city. Some of the [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) who have chosen to live on Armitage in spite of the ever present threat of Vanduul violence use Port Conrad as a center of trade.","g":["armitage","orion iii","cities","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d864d540-3709-41d3-85b5-185b1a0b00cb"},
{"id":"port-fairfax","gp":"0jG8wK5LDJ","t":"Port Fairfax","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Port Fairfax is a [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) base located on [Goss III](gp:VlMnJ8v4J5), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Constructed during the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792), it was originally intended to be a staging point for the invasion of the [Terra system](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4) in case it tried to secede. After the events of the [anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7), the base was converted into a large military hospital complex.","g":["uee city","goss iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/194fad6b-cebb-4541-951f-d31a5e89863a"},
{"id":"port-olisar","gp":"RvlgwMlEpr","t":"Port Olisar","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"Port Olisar is a space station and trade hub owned and operated by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N). Normally located in orbit above the gas giant [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav), it was decommissioned in 2943 for extensive repairs and updates. When in use, it serves as a rest stop and gateway to the company's orbital shipyards, offering shops, accommodations for visitors, and parking areas for large spacecraft.","g":["space station","stanton system","crusader industries"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/43778f99-9ce7-4bc5-8ab7-621a386625ea"},
{"id":"port-renatus","gp":"RWwZWj9vOZ","t":"Port Renatus","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Port Renatus is the capital city of Mars (Sol IV), and is the first permanent [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) settlement to be built on a planet outside Earth (Sol III). Once Mars' second attempted [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) was successfully completed in the 22nd century, Port Renatus grew into a city-sized settlement as it became the de facto spaceport for all persons arriving to further develop the planet. The architecture of Port Renatus is studied by historians as an example of Humanity's first attempts to build modular cities.","g":["mars","sol iv","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3dee3423-dd7a-4cbf-8df5-2ed6ab5f25da"},
{"id":"port-tressler","gp":"0qaarZkZvq","t":"Port Tressler","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"Port Tressler is a space station that serves as the main transfer hub to [New Babbage](gp:Rw1Zl3vdW7) on [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1). Named after Aleena Tressler, a mentor of [microTech's](gp:bE3rBB4j7J) founder [Magnus Tobin](gp:RkGZqr8yNQ), it is owned and operated by microTech, and houses multiple shops and services focused on hospitality. Exports from microTech and other companies on the planet below pass through Port Tressler before they are loaded onto transports and distributed across the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["space station","stanton system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1ca2c06d-1013-469f-af13-3cc3733b2f94"},
{"id":"pox-cano-iv","gp":"RWoy1A9eWm","t":"Pox (Cano IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Pox is the fourth planet from the sun in the [Cano system](gp:Rxn9DYKdnd), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A gas giant with rust-colored banding, it is constantly beset by storms up to a thousand kilometers wide. Pox's erratic weather is a favorite subject of atmospheric scientists.","g":["pox","cano iv","cano system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9c5a5e49-5a50-425a-bcfb-4cafc346e6f6"},
{"id":"preacher-armament","gp":"RMXympByLo","t":"Preacher Armament","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Preacher Armaments is a manufacturer of personal and vehicle-mounted weapons with a specific focus on professional-grade manufacturing intended for use by working security. The company was founded in SEY 2931 on Rytif (Bremen II) by Kino Walton, who created weapons in his personal workshop. These weapons sold well enough among the local militia that Walton was able to secure funding to expand operations and make Preacher weapons available across the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). They are best known for their lines of scatterguns such as the Salvation, Absolution, and Condemnation. Preacher also produces the popular Inquisition XXII ballistic gatling gun. The company's branding and marketing has a slight religious angle, with their current advertising utilizing the slogan \"With Preacher on your side, they haven't got a prayer.\"","g":["weapons manufacturer","kino walton","rytif","bremen ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9fc22a3f-048f-405f-a3e3-c01ff0066f81"},
{"id":"pressurized-research-station","gp":"Rvgp3vz3qN","t":"Pressurized Research Station","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Research stations situated in hostile settings, such as non-terraformed planets, are built airtight, with artificially raised or lowered pressure to create environments friendly to researchers. These research stations can be used to study phenomena that would be otherwise inaccessible, such as smog atmospheres, flare stars, ice planets, and asteroids. [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) research stations show a great deal of resilience in high-pressure atmospheres. [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) researchers have yet to crack the secret behind this technology.","g":["colonization method"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1c368de7-af63-4be3-bcf1-26daa9d7cf87"},
{"id":"prime","gp":"RLMmA78vBv","t":"Prime","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Prime is the capital city of [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) and is considered a cultural and economic center of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Utilizing extensive urban planning, it has been designed to strike a harmonious balance between nature and city. Since the [fall](gp:bE3rKa32P7) of the [Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) government in 2792 there has been a [vocal contingent](gp:0OaylwDmvv) of the populace vying to make Prime the new capital of the UEE.","g":["terra","terra iii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0dae5b29-40c7-43f1-87b0-676d6b4e7742"},
{"id":"prime-citizen","gp":"V7gM82vNmr","t":"Prime Citizen","k":"faction","c":["Politics","Government","History","Human"],"x":"Prime Citizen was the highest government office obtainable by a resident of the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN). Created in 2546, the office was proposed by [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q), then High-General of the UPE, in response to a [series of bombings](gp:0Gz5GgEvkj) reported as terrorist attacks on multiple populated planets. After the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) failed to apprehend those responsible for the bombings, the [Citizens](gp:RLMmop8rkr) of the UPE voted to dissolve the executive council known as the [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) and establish the office of Prime Citizen. On December 15th of that year, Messer was elected Prime Citizen in a landslide victory.","g":["ivar messer i","messer era","upe government","human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ff958e47-67a4-4bc5-95ce-04870b347125"},
{"id":"ptm","gp":"R4ZGgXjq95","t":"Prime Transit Metrorail (PTM)","k":"place","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Prime Transit Metrorail (PTM) is a public transportation system located in [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv) on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), developed under government contract by [Argo Astronautics](gp:0KnA1vvJEM) in 2545. The PTM's main city center station sits in downtown Prime, with lines connecting it to hubs located in the city's main spaceport on Corsa and the historic Barrows neighborhood. Lined with greenways, waterways, and specially designed terraced gardens, it was designed to blend harmoniously into Prime's natural environment. Every year on the second week of May, the PTM celebrates the anniversary of its founding by planting a new tree along a randomly-selected route.","g":["public transportation","prime","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b6de056-b671-4688-8aa9-6e3f23ea4096"},
{"id":"privately-owned-world","gp":"bmGaGlN3L8","t":"Privately-Owned World","k":"faction","c":["Government","Commerce"],"x":"Privately-owned world in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) is a recently created designation for a planetary body that is owned and governed by corporations or individuals. First created for the Stanton system, these planets are more akin to corporations than nations, eschewing democratic leadership and the requirements for senatorial representation. The majority of their inhabitants generally work for the corporate owner, with any additional population being made up of those who have set up independent businesses to supply food, clothing, non-corporate provided housing, and other necessities. Inhabitants are protected by the UEE's Common Laws, but the enforcement of said laws is up to the discretion of the corporation.","g":["privately-owned worlds","uee legal definition","uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/553265ff-9e24-434b-8261-11a30638cce7"},
{"id":"production-system","gp":"VlNPvJOnPM","t":"Production System","k":"faction","c":["Commerce","Xi'an","Government"],"x":"Production systems are planetary systems in the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that have been specifically designated as work zones. Each planet in such a system has been [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) from the ground up for a specific purpose, such as farming or manufacturing. They perform their functions under the supervision of the Xi'an government, and are subject to Imperial law.","g":["xi'an legal definition","xi'an government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c397e29c-a0a9-45fb-8840-b13271df4b2e"},
{"id":"project-archangel","gp":"RLMmAnr4gj","t":"Project Archangel","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"Project Archangel is the official designation for a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)-funded program to create an artificial planet. Commonly known as Synthworld, the project was announced in 2872 during Corbyn Salehi's tenure as [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) as a way to move beyond the inherently destructive process of terraforming a planet. Popular at the time, it was considered the next step beyond the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) in protecting indigenous life while still allowing the UEE's expansion. The [Chronos system](gp:RvlQZKy95l) was chosen for its Sol-like star and lack of planets in the green band. The project has since come under fire by the public for the amount of funds poured into it with little apparent progress towards its goal.","g":["uee government program","synthworld","corbyn salehi","massacre of garron ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c87928eb-36aa-4dd5-945b-ac3af861b891"},
{"id":"project-far-star","gp":"0qnNAD6YKa","t":"Project Far Star","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"Project Far Star was a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) funding initiative initiated to expand its borders outward from the Virgil system. [Terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) companies and navjumpers who focused their exploration efforts in this direction were granted priority funding from the UEE for their efforts. This led to the discovery and colonization of the [Terra](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4), Tiber, and Orion systems, among others. The program ran from 2412 to 2681.","g":["uee government program","messer era","human colonial expansion era"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8dbb8277-834e-4a6c-a583-a38db0958563"},
{"id":"project-vespa","gp":"RMXymp7EGn","t":"Project Vespa","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"Project Vespa was a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government project with the goal of developing a method to weaponize terraforming. Files were declassified and disclosed to the public in 2795 in the wake of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) War Crimes Trials (2793-2795). The project's leader and creator, Dr. Thessaly Tayac, led the terraforming, de-terraforming, and re-terraforming of [Tayac I](gp:RX33y7kp9q) until his death in 2590. Project Vespa ended in 2750, when the planet became too unstable for the project to continue. Shortly thereafter, the project was discontinued.","g":["thessaly tayac","messer era","uee government program","tayac system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/48481726-9d2b-4370-aeac-e11abb3fa049"},
{"id":"prospector","gp":"0QxYA5BPGj","t":"Prospector","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Prospector is a mining spacecraft developed by [Musashi Industrial & Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). Spun off from the [Freelancer](gp:RvgzWy7o6v) project in 2925, the Prospector exchanges its sister ship's modularity in favor of a focus on small scale mining via its suite of boring and extraction tools. Able to mine and transfer ore collected on both planetary surfaces and in space, Prospectors are favored by independent operators for their flexibility.","g":["prospecting","mining","misc","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1c8b69f7-1900-43c0-93ba-3e883890f5db"},
{"id":"prota","gp":"0NjQqDJz42","t":"Prota","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"Prota is a slime mold that secretes an adhesive that can be distilled and turned into a commercial-grade glue. Able to survive in environments with corrosive, high-pressure atmospheres, the prota is known for its resilience and can sometimes be found on worlds that are largely uninhabitable. As long as it has access to water, it thrives in areas that have been heavily polluted by acid.","g":["slime mold"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5c0a5954-6a0d-41d7-b979-64fbef014ec6"},
{"id":"prowler","gp":"02BQOJQQP7","t":"Prowler","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Tevarin","Human"],"x":"The Prowler is a [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X)-designed combat personnel carrier built with air-shielded rapid deployment doors. Its name comes from the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) designation for the original armored carrier initially observed during the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM)(2541-2546). The Prowler was utilized again in the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv)(2603-2610), until the Tevarin were defeated by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2). Prowlers that had not been lost in the war were destroyed during the Tevarin Purge. In the 2940s, [Esperia](gp:0OaBKL7wlv) obtained Tevarin spacecraft and other material from a cache of original Tevarin artifacts recovered in the Kabal System, leading the company to develop a modernized [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-manufactured recreation of the craft.","g":["dropship","esperia","tevarin spacecraft","human spacecraft","stealth"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/36b4b1f0-fd00-41d0-8f87-421ac48653df"},
{"id":"puaangkiil-eealuth-v","gp":"bEzeJpqwMJ","t":"Puaangkiil (Ē'aluth V)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Puaangkiil (Ē'aluth V) is the fifth and final planet from the sun of the [Ē'aluth system](gp:Rw1xW1lzxN), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A gas giant with a pale red and white atmosphere, it is the sole source of unprocessed hydrogen in the system. Although most mining is prohibited in Ē'aluth in order to protect the nature preserve on [Ko'li (Ē'aluth III)](gp:Vy29gQ3x4Y), a few automated fuel processing platforms and service stations have been allowed to extract hydrogen from Puaangkiil. Visitors can have their spacecraft towed to these stations in the event of an emergency.","g":["puaangkiil","ē'aluth v","ē'aluth system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7f4c705a-3f4e-44bd-83a3-25f1375fd169"},
{"id":"puenu-kyukya-1a","gp":"0jGJZokndn","t":"Pue'nu (Kyuk'ya 1a)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Xi'an"],"x":"Pue'nu (Kyuk'ya 1a) is the moon of [Kyuk'ya I](gp:bBzPqGr64O), [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). During the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793), it was the site of a [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military base that was used as a launch point for scouting missions into [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) territory. In 2798, a few years after the dissolution of the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO), the Xi'an government converted [the base](gp:RL68MWxZOL) into a hub to facilitate trade between the Xi'an Empire, the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3), and the UEE. The free contact between these civilizations has fostered the emergence of a Xi'an youth movement that rejects traditional values and embraces trends from other cultures.","g":["pue'nu","kyuk'ya 1a","kyuk'ya system","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","xi'an moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4ed2717e-3bab-4eb0-b686-b3abff747cf4"},
{"id":"pyenpuia","gp":"RL68MWxZOL","t":"Pyen'pui.a","k":"place","c":["Locations","Xi'an"],"x":"Pyen'pui.a is a large [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) shipping base and orbital scaffolding array located on the moon of [Kyuk'ya I](gp:bBzPqGr64O). Ships moving through the system offload their cargo at the array, where it is then processed and distributed. Crews often spend time at the base on the surface while this is being done. Because of its position as a major trading center between the Xi'an, [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), and [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) people, the base is unusually highly populated, and has become a hotspot for Xi'an youth counterculture.","g":["space station","xian space station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/21ef10a4-8410-4b61-bddc-77e2e34f8378"},
{"id":"pyro-i","gp":"RMNjxnZp3n","t":"Pyro I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Pyro I is the first planet from the sun of the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Its thick, high-pressure atmosphere hides a strange landscape beset by powerful winds and lightning strikes. Under the clouds, there is an ecosystem of plants and animals that endure its extremely high temperatures, even during powerful stellar flares. Surveyors and scientists constructed shielded research centers and mining outposts on Pyro I's surface starting in 2510, allowing a sparse population to attempt to utilize the planet before the facilities were abandoned by the close of the 26th century.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","pyro system"]},
{"id":"pyro-iv","gp":"RX3AzOBxeM","t":"Pyro IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Pyro IV is the outermost moon of[Pyro V](gp:RAXv9Yeqay), and astronomers theorize that it was once the fourth planet from the sun of the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). At some point before [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) discovered Pyro, a massive celestial body collided with Pyro IV, catastrophically warping its landscape, destroying its atmosphere, and knocking it into the orbit of nearby gas giant Pyro V. Although the tectonic activity that resulted from this impact has quieted and a new atmosphere has formed, Pyro IV is far from stable. It is on a long, slow collision course with Pyro V, and will one day either crash into it or break up into a ring.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet","pyro system"]},
{"id":"pyro-ryt-multi-tool","gp":"01LxzZ1DDJ","t":"Pyro RYT Multi-Tool","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"The Pyro RYT Multi-Tool is a portable tool that is manufactured by [Greycat Industrial](gp:02BQlmgoDy). Invented by the engineer Ruben Pardue, it sold so well after its initial release that the company could not keep it in supply. This opened the door for competitors to design and sell cheap knockoffs, eventually leading to the generalization of the word \"multitool\" to refer to any handheld tools with attachments capable of light mining, scanning for minerals, repairing vehicles, moving objects via tractor beam, healing wounds, and cutting metal.","g":["multitool","greycat industrial","tools"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8acfbf09-ac96-4eb8-8af4-ef16598f5e1b"},
{"id":"pyro-system","gp":"0ODxJM917N","t":"Pyro System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Pyro system is an unclaimed planetary system that consists of a K-type flare star, five terrestrial planets, and a gas giant. Discovered in SEY 2493 by [Pyrotechnic Amalgamated](gp:VpM4anYBn1), it was not claimed by the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) due in part to the dangers surrounding its star. Instead, it was exploited by corporate interests until the 2560s, when the potential resources extracted from the system stopped outweighing the increased cost of maintaining equipment under a volatile sun. Pyro became a haven for outlaws by the early 2600s. \n\nToday, it is mostly populated by criminal factions that frequently struggle against one another for dominance. [Rough & Ready](gp:RMNjxwk8pB) took control of the station in 2951, ousting the extremist gang [XenoThreat](gp:VgExkEAB19), who had held it since 2947.  \n# PLANETARY SYSTEM\nPyro, the system's star, is roughly 11.3 billion years old. It is classified as a flare star, or a variable star that undergoes dramatic increases in brightness within a few minutes, releasing powerful bursts of radiation. The closest planetary body to it is [Pyro I](gp:RMNjxnZp3n), a terrestrial planet with a dense atmosphere and a silicate crust. Of the other terrestrial planets, [Bloom (Pyro III)](gp:0KxjqgQdNY) is the only one with naturally habitable conditions. [Monox (Pyro II)](gp:0jGdgLEjqJ) has enough oxygen in its atmosphere to allow a person to breathe without protective equipment for only a short time before deadly health consequences set in. Those who visit the surface of [Terminus (Pyro VI)](gp:RAXv9kpk5m) can breathe there for long periods of time, but not comfortably. The gas giant [Pyro V](gp:RAXv9Yeqay) has six true moons. The planet [Pyro IV](gp:RX3AzOBxeM), which was likely knocked out of its original orbit around the star by a massive celestial body, now circles Pyro V as its seventh and outermost \"moon.\"  \n\n# DISCOVERY\nIn 2463, the watch officer of the Earth-flagged tanker ship *Roustabout*, Raj MacEwan, detected a strange signal in the [Cano system](gp:Rxn9DYKdnd). He conducted an analysis and compiled his findings into a detailed report, which he sent to the owners of the ship, Pyrotechnic Amalgamated. The board of directors chose to take no action at that time. In 2493, CEO Cecile Uchiha ordered that legacy flight records be reassessed to factor in advances in jump point detection technology. MacEwan's original report was found during this review, and the company dispatched an exploration ship to the region. After careful investigation, they discovered a jump point at MacEwan's coordinates, and entered it to find what would later be named the Pyro system on the other side. \n\n# HISTORY\nPyrotechnic Amalgamated celebrated the discovery until surveys revealed the existence of the flare star. Although scans of Pyro II had found valuable mineral deposits, the unpredictable bursts of radiation from the system's sun would make their extraction with the technology of the day a costly endeavor. The company made the decision to report the discovery to the UNE, planning to collect government subsidies that would fund their operations and guarantee future profits. Uchiha personally reported news of the discovery, and Pyrotechnic Amalgamated was granted first crack at the system when the UNE opened it for commercial activity.\n\nWhile the UNE gave corporate interests like Pyrotechnic Amalgamated the green light to enter Pyro, they held back on allowing full colonization. The flare star presented a completely unknown quantity, one that could have disastrous effects on [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) life. Government officials elected to conduct a voluntary ten-year pilot program that would document the effects of the star's flares on Humans. If the conclusion of the study was favorable, they would sanction colonization and officially claim the system. However, the program became one of many that were cut short in 2499, when [Project Far Star](gp:0qnNAD6YKa) located the [Magnus system](gp:RWolrNa1Ge) and the Senate voted to channel all possible resources to the [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) of [Magnus II](gp:R9vGaQPXJN) and the construction of a new center of shipbuilding for the [UNE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). In 2516, when more funds might have become available, the discovery of the [Terra system](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4) funneled any available capital towards the development of the naturally-habitable [Terra III](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). 2523 brought the advent of the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE), and along with it, a complete reorganization of the government. The question of what to do with Pyro was put on indefinite hold, and the system remained unclaimed.  \n\nOver the next few decades, commercial interest in Pyro waned as valuable minerals became thin on the ground and government subsidies dried up. After the end of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546), improvements in shielding technology allowed the few companies that remained in the system to extend their operations to previously unreachable areas, but this also increased the presence of outlaws as they too gained access to this tech. Eventually, bandit raids made turning a profit impossible. Some companies were forced to declare bankruptcy, including Pyrotechnic Amalgamated. By the end of the 2500s, almost all corporations had pulled out of Pyro, paving the way for outlaws to become the dominant force in the system.\n# CULTURE\nInstead of having formal, organized government, competing gangs rule over the Pyro system, creating a series of fiefdoms that are subject to change if the local dominant faction is ousted from power. Gangs that hold particular strategic points are seen as more powerful than others, especially those who control Ruin Station and the drug labs within it. Many gangs maintain strongholds on the surface of Terminus, the planet the station orbits, that they use as launching points for attacks. \n\nOutside of its criminal organizations, Pyro maintains a moderate population of mostly Human inhabitants whose main occupation is survival. Monox's mining infrastructure, long-abandoned by its former owners, houses squatters who will fiercely defend their right to live there in spite of its hostile environment. Those who live on the naturally habitable Bloom have an easier existence, but still struggle day to day. Joining a gang and attaining its protection is largely seen as a way of attaining a better life, and many choose this path if it's made available to them. Still, numerous others refuse the option, preferring the known risks of subsistence living over the constant dangers associated with gang membership.","g":["unclaimed system"]},
{"id":"pyro-v","gp":"RAXv9Yeqay","t":"Pyro V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Pyro V is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). It was given the classification of \"Pyro V\" when researchers came across strong evidence that its outermost moon once maintained a stable orbit around the system's star between [Pyro III](gp:0KxjqgQdNY) and Pyro V. When Pyro IV was struck by an unknown celestial body, it was knocked into Pyro V's gravitational sphere of influence. Residents of and travelers through the Pyro system are known to harvest hydrogen from Pyro V's green and yellow atmosphere.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet","pyro system"]},
{"id":"pyrotechnic-amalgamated","gp":"VpM4anYBn1","t":"Pyrotechnic Amalgamated","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Pyrotechnic Amalgamated was a mining company most notable for discovering the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N) in 2493 and the [Hadrian system](gp:RX3r6jlZok) in 2510. Founded in 2409 by Tromo Nivelin, it started out specializing in scouting and prospecting remote areas for viable claims and taking control before the arrival of potential competitors. It began extracting resources from the Pyro system in 2493, shortly after receiving the green light from the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE). The profits from this venture allowed the company to quickly expand its operations in Pyro, constructing countless bases and space stations throughout the system. In 2516, the company suffered a heavy financial blow when it overbid on what turned out to be a worthless mining claim on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) that was later revealed to have been based on faulty data. It faced another massive loss in 2539, when the discovery of the Hadrian-[Gurzil](gp:0Kxydrxd45) jump point caused it to lose access to its claims in the Hadrian system. Valuable resources in the Pyro system became harder to find in the 2540s, and the company truly began to struggle. Although the development of improved shielding technology in the 2550s allowed Pyrotechnic Amalgamated to expand into previously unreachable areas, the company was eventually forced to declare bankruptcy in 2563, when increased outlaw attacks and the cost of maintaining their equipment completely eclipsed their bottom line.","g":["human company","mining company"]},
{"id":"quantainium","gp":"bBzkEK7Ojd","t":"Quantainium","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Quantainium is a deep red-orange mineral that occurs in igneous rock formations. A key ingredient in [quantum fuel](gp:RX3DOkJdxJ), quantainium becomes unstable when it is extracted, and is prone to breakage and degradation. Over time, it becomes more and more likely to combust, which sometimes results in explosions. Mining companies that extract quantainium must operate under strict safety regulations. Some independent miners have become injured or have died due to quantainium-related accidents.","g":["quantainium ","geology","minerals"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f2218d28-6cd0-409a-870a-ebf22975e556"},
{"id":"quantum-drive","gp":"RX3DOkJdxJ","t":"Quantum Drive","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A quantum drive is a type of engine that generates a Chan-Eisen field, enabling spacecraft to travel at approximately 20% of the speed of light. Because it takes a great deal of energy for a quantum drive to work, larger ships with more room for specialized power and cooling devices can remain in quantum travel longer than smaller ships. Quantum drives can be altered with a jump module to become a jump drive capable of [traversing interspace](gp:bBp6Bx33wm).\n\nThe first [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) quantum drive was created in MXY 0.5171 (SEY 25343 BCE) by House Yaing. Having recently developed [terraforming](gp:R6dWOrLEM4), the Xi'an used their new technology to expand beyond their home planet of RyiXy'an (Hyoton III), eventually colonizing Ka'ua (Hyoton IV) and Tethle'a (Hyoton II). The first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) quantum drive prototype was created by Dr. Scott Childress and his team in SEY 2075 and was capable of achieving 1/100th the speed of light. The debut of the quantum drive led to a sharp increase in exploration of the Sol system, conducted by institutions and private individuals. Historians are unsure exactly how long the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) have had quantum engine technology due to their lack of historical data.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8397d8c8-5c00-49af-87d8-3e18ee65f816"},
{"id":"quarterdeck","gp":"bEzln9kyjJ","t":"QuarterDeck","k":"place","c":["Locations"],"x":"QuarterDeck is a maximum-security prison located on [Kellog VI](gp:R6dAQZgGQe) in the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv). Built to withstand the planet's frigidly cold, low-oxygen atmosphere, the penitentiary is under heavy guard and is considered virtually inescapable. The [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) allows prisoners at QuarterDeck to work off their sentences in a nearby full-process antimatter refinery. This has led to accusations of Human rights abuses and nearly led to the shutdown of the prison in SEY 2943. The proposal to close it was defeated in the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) by a narrow margin.","g":["quarterdeck prison","kellog iv","uee prisons"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f65a4ed9-63fd-4046-adda-d4fa7ce5ace1"},
{"id":"quarterdeck-kellog-vi","gp":"R6dAQZgGQe","t":"QuarterDeck (Kellog VI)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"QuaterDeck (Kellog VI) is the sixth planet from the sun of the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv). Named for the maximum security prison located on its surface, it is covered with ice and is inhospitable to [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) life outside environmentally-controlled facilities. An [antimatter processing plant](gp:V3qgy3L7ra) located near the penitentiary is staffed by inmates of QuarterDeck, some of whom volunteer for the job in exchange for reduced sentences despite its dangerous and sometimes deadly conditions. In 2943, [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) Ghata Veras of [Lo (Corel III)](gp:VarAoYEQYd) proposed that the prison and the plant be decommissioned due to its harsh conditions and track record of Human rights violations. The proposal was defeated by a narrow margin, leading many political commentators to speculate that it will be resurrected in the future.","g":["quarterdeck","kellog vi","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","kellog system","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b2c17a5-f2a8-4bf2-865c-2a1d3570888a"},
{"id":"quasi","gp":"0Njj7PwPAM","t":"Quasi","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Quasi is the second largest city on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), located in the southern hemisphere in the shadow of the Neesay Mountains. Most known for the large complex of ancient ruins discovered early in Terra's settlement, Quasi maintains a bustling tourist industry, and is home to the Quasi Institute for Xenological Studies (QIXS). Summers in Quasi are relatively cool, while winters are long and subject to more than 200 mm of snow per season.","g":["uee city","terra","terra iii","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/93e83678-04b4-4b91-bd92-e65a0a621c34"},
{"id":"quasi-grazer","gp":"VlM7x7WZG7","t":"Quasi Grazer","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"The Quasi grazer is a large, warm-blooded herd animal that is indigenous to the vast plains of [Quasi](gp:0Njj7PwPAM) on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). Most notable for its unusual method of carrying their eggs on its underside, the Quasi grazer has become one of the standard seed animals used in the terraforming process and can be found on most terraformed planets in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). This practice has led to the creation of various subspecies that were genetically enhanced to better survive in different biomes. Their eggs and their meat can be eaten and their hides can be used to make leather, making them an important resource for newly-established colonies.","g":["quasi","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7c75f139-f41c-47e9-b2ed-20a0e3720734"},
{"id":"quasi-institute-for-xenological-studies","gp":"V7dDyYvQpL","t":"Quasi Institute for Xenological Studies (QIXS)","k":"place","c":["Education","Human","Locations"],"x":"The Quasi Institute for Xenological Studies (QIXS) is a public research university located in the city [Quasi](gp:0Njj7PwPAM) on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). Best known for its xenoarchaeology program, the QIXS curriculum emphasizes field work, the study of ancient languages, and the use of primary sources in historical research. It was founded early in Terra's settlement period after the SEY 2517 discovery of a large complex of ancient ruins of unknown origin in the Neesay Mountains.","g":["quasi institute for xenological studies","qixs","quasi","terra","terra iii","higher education","uee education","uee higher education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d367c492-a95c-4d5d-86b7-9dce26cebb82"},
{"id":"quinton","gp":"VY4Wg52JY1","t":"Quinton","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Quinton is the largest city on Angeli (Croshaw II), and the oldest [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) city outside the Sol system. Located near the equator of Angeli and bordered by mountains and long, tropical plains, it experiences long wet and dry seasons. The city is famous for the beauty of its natural landscape and for its skyline. Skyscrapers in Quinton are all built with earthquake resistant materials and deep, flexible, strongly reinforced foundations to keep the buildings standing against frequent seismic activity.","g":["angeli","croshaw ii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9e68e129-7d12-4c2b-a5b7-04d0e035996c"},
{"id":"quirinus-tech","gp":"bE3rPeG8Wv","t":"Quirinus Tech","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Quirinus Tech is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of protective armor, known for using advanced flexible weaves and alloys to produce lighter pieces that match the stopping power of more traditional materials, albeit often at a higher cost. Because of their streamlined appearance, they are often used by private security firms who wish to maintain a lower profile. [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) partnered with Quirinus to include their Calva helmet with the initial launch of the [Mantis](gp:0Gz5vqXlaQ) interdiction ship.","g":["armor manufacturer","mantis"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/10bfe2c2-7eff-4a4c-8c59-e73cf4ee788f"},
{"id":"qv-planet-services","gp":"V7d3ZyP9X3","t":"QV Planet Services","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"QV Planet Services were a mining corporation based in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Founded in SEY 2589, their attained their initial capital by convincing investors that they could quickly construct infrastructure and begin work in the newly-discovered [Nyx system ](gp:0jGxP6kpG3) before other companies got a foothold there. When the UEE accepted their bid to establish operations, they followed through with their promise and rapidly built a network of infrastructure across the system. In the 2630s, another company discovered massive caches of many of Nyx's most valuable commodities elsewhere, tanking market prices. QV formally shut down in 2644 and abandoned their equipment, choosing to recoup the investors with what little funding they had left instead of spending it to dismantle everything.","g":["mining company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2ad68b41-ad3a-4634-b519-d48ce71cf45a"},
{"id":"raipuaang-kaipua-ii","gp":"Rw1rnY1AYJ","t":"R.aip'uāng (Kai'pua II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"R.aip'uāng (Kai'pua II) is the second planet from the sun of the [Kai'pua system](gp:V3GBmlQoar), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). One day on R.aip'uāng is equal in length to 100 Modern Xi'an Years (MXY), a coincidence with enough significance for it to have been turned into the spiritual center of [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe) at the conclusion of the [First Imperial Age](gp:VDoPeW55W4) (MXY I.0 - I.14680 / SEY 19668 - 878 BCE). Most of its surface is covered in verdant fields and cultivated gardens, with temples built so there is always one visible on the horizon no matter one's location. It is considered a huge achievement to meditate on R.aip'uāng for a full day, a feat achievable only by those who have mastered manipulation of their metabolic state. No manufacturing or mining activities are allowed beyond the essential in order to maintain tranquility, and most visitors to the planet are encouraged to limit their travels to the capital city and its immediate surroundings.","g":["r.aip'uāng","kai'pua ii","habitable","habitable planet","kai'pua system","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"rila-system","gp":"Rw1xWXME1B","t":"R.il'a system","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The R.il'a system is a planetary system in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that consists of one protoplanet, one puffy planet, two terrestrial planets, one super-Earth, and one dwarf planet. First developed as a military training system by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government, it has been transformed into a center of industry since the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793 / MXY III.838 - III.1044) in the interest of sustaining peace between the Xi'an Empire and the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It has become a center of trade between the two Empires thanks to its jump point to the UEE-controlled Horus system and financial incentives from the Xi'an government, who have relaxed restrictions on immigration.","g":["xi'an system"]},
{"id":"r6-pro","gp":"R4jl95aalq","t":"R6 Pro","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"R6 Pro is a footwear brand that manufactures shoes for security professionals and outdoor enthusiasts. The company was founded by the family of a [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) soldier who would frequently complain about foot pain caused by her military-issue boots. Her parents commissioned a local artisan to make custom shoes for her, and were so impressed with the result that they bought the rights and used it as the flagship design when they launched the company.","g":["footwear manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7ea048d8-c0ac-48b1-8cdc-cad8cca44adf"},
{"id":"radegast-distillery","gp":"0qn8vv36G5","t":"Radegast Distillery","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Food and Beverages","Human"],"x":"# Radegast Distillery\nRadegast Distillery is a historic producer of whiskey located in Port Renatus on Mars (Sol IV). Initially founded as a bar in 2520 by the Wilkes family, Radegast became a common stopover point once word spread about the house whiskey they produced in the back. Its popularity grew to the point where a full-size distillery was added in 2574.\n \nBoth bar and distillery were purchased from the Wilkes family by the Pan-Galactic Beverage Corporation (PGBC) in 2602. Radegast enjoyed 300 years of galactic success before falling out of the public eye in the early 29th century. In 2920, the brand underwent a resurgence when a private investor bought and rebuilt the original bar in the style of the 26th century. Today, Radegast is consistently ranked as one of the biggest sellers of Martian Whiskey in the UEE.\n \n# History\nDimitri and Danica Wilkes, eldest children of a second-generation Mars-born family, opened Radegast Bar in 2520. The bar saw early popularity among the Port Renatus locals, winning Most Welcoming Bar/Restaurant in a 2532 edition of Mars Today. Dimitri used the storage room (and his regulars) to experiment with home-brewing. He tried several unsuccessful beer recipes and made a notorious attempt at distilling gin, before finally trying his hand at whiskey. The recipe was an instant hit, catapulting the bar to even greater heights of popularity. Eventually, the Wilkes siblings retired on their profits and passed the bar down to their children.\n \nIn 2574, Danica's granddaughter added a permanent distillery to the family operation. Zara Wilkes' house whiskey, Radegast Gold, gained a wide-reaching reputation for smoothness and clarity of flavor. Radegast Distilleries opened a second facility on Angeli, Croshaw in 2585. The first untapped casks of Angeli whiskey were shipped to Port Renatus in 2598. The journey unexpectedly, but pleasantly, changed the Whiskey's flavour, prompting the launch of Radegast Homeward. This limited release was stored in Angeli oak barrels, but matured in zero-G, before returning to Mars for its final aging.\n \nThe company's success drove the Pan-Galactic Beverage Corporation (PGBC) to make an offer to buy the Radegast name, whiskey, and bar in the late 26th century. The Wilkes family wanted to make sure that the label stayed under their control, so a formal sale wasn't finalized until 2602. With the added benefit of PGBC's production and distribution network, Radegast whiskey began to appear in all corners of the UEE.\n \n# Decline\nThe last member of the Wilkes family left the Radegast brand in 2754, citing personal differences with the leadership of PGBC. This ended 180 years of Wilkes-led distillation of Radegast whiskey, as well as PGBC's access to the Wilkes-owned water source on Mars, Perepllut's Well. However, PGBC retained the rights to the Radegast name, and began selling a low-cost version of its Gold whiskey in 2766. Their first attempt at a new recipe, Radegast Neo, was appallingly received.\n \nIn the early 2800s, PGBC came under fire after they were accused of diluting Radegast Gold and passing it off as full strength. The company denied the accusations. However, the scandal repeated throughout the 2810s, finally reaching its climax in 2821 when evidence was published on Spectrum by independent investigator Willis Kemper. The Radegast brand was unable to maintain its reputation, and while the high-end limited editions were still considered top quality whiskeys, sales plummeted.\n \n# Revival\nPGBC dissolved in 2918, and with it, their right to the Radegast name. A private investor purchased the brand and the building where the original bar once operated. Two years later, the newly rebuilt Radegast bar reopened, rebuilt to look as it did in the 26th century.\n \nDescendants of the Wilkes family were hired to distill classic versions of their whiskey from the original recipes crafted by Dimitri and Zara. The new Radegast whiskeys soon grew in reputation, and the brand was reborn. Master Distiller Hanshi Wilkes currently oversees all production.\n \n# List of Products\nRadegast <br/>\nRadegast Gold <br/>\nRadegast Neo (Discontinued) <br/>\nRadegast Mars Oak Reserve <br/>\nRadegast 18 SEY Old <br/>\nRadegast Archive 21 SEY Old <br/>\nRadegast Wilkes' Reserve\n \n# Limited Release\nRadegast Homeward 15 SEY Old <br/>\nRadegast Homeward 40 SEY Old <br/>\nRadegast Master Distiller's Edition <br/>","g":["alcohol","mars","sol iv","radegast whiskey","port renatus","pan-galactic beverage corporation","beverage","beverage company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/eb190560-44a6-4248-90fb-3b69cd5813cd"},
{"id":"raft","gp":"R4jdlj8JLE","t":"RAFT","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The RAFT, or Reinforced Advanced Freight Transport, is a small hauler manufactured by [Argo Astronautics](gp:0KnA1vvJEM). Outfitted with remote turrets and laser repeaters, the RAFT was designed with a thick hull and heavy shielding to protect its two-person crew and any cargo they may be carrying through potentially dangerous areas of space. The three 32 SCU exterior containers can be removed from the bottom of the ship and replaced, eliminating the need to hand-load crates.","g":["argo astronautics","human spacecraft","freight","medium freight"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f93dc0d4-5f1b-4788-ad35-852fad58c2e4"},
{"id":"railen","gp":"VpMxKQx7E1","t":"Railen","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Xi'an","Human"],"x":"The Gatac Railen (Ng.at'ak Sanrailen) is a cargo spacecraft released in 2951 and developed by [Gatac Manufacture](gp:bo13Earlar) (Ao't.o'a'Ng.at'ak) for the Human and Xi'an markets. Development of the Railen began after the [Human-Xi'an Trade Agreement (HuXa)](gp:01LvKoLvZ8) was passed by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government in 2947. In addition to a weapons system and armored hull designed to protect the ship in dangerous areas of space, the Railen is equipped with habitation facilities suitable for both [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) and [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) crew.","g":["ao't.o'a'ng.at'ak","gatac manufacture","human spacecraft","xi'an spacecraft","freight","medium freight"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1cf9f146-7680-4a8d-8fe9-2318bd0f1a94"},
{"id":"raleigh-station","gp":"RkZ9rDD944","t":"Raleigh Station","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Raleigh Station is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) settlement on the moon of [Odin II](gp:0KxloXyPAM), [Vili (Odin 2a)](gp:0dXE5Ny6Qd). Initially established in 2602 by a now defunct weapons firm to test weapons on the nearby planet, it now serves as a waypoint for various corporations and research centers operating on Odin II. Although Raleigh is open to the public, it is not heavily trafficked due to the specialized nature of industry in the area and a difficult-to-traverse asteroid belt. There are few amenities for travelers.","g":["odin 2a","vili","research station","sealed settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9e90afa6-f720-4771-a412-767e6ea96e83"},
{"id":"rambler","gp":"RxnQXal55a","t":"Rambler","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Rambler is a clothing and accessory brand that specializes in rugged, outdoor gear with a decorative touch. Intended for the explorers or colonists of newly-discovered, unclaimed, or undeveloped worlds, its Explorer line of goggles has found success among hobbyist climbers and winter sports enthusiasts for its strong levels of UV protection.","g":["clothing manufacturer","footwear manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/67c61f3a-4fbc-4d7a-b7fa-3d91af66e939"},
{"id":"ranger","gp":"RMNxqW2qjK","t":"Ranger","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Ranger is an all-terrain motorcycle manufactured by [Tumbril Land Systems](gp:VarkpZnxjd). Featuring patented X-TEC off-road technology that is designed to increase the vehicles responsiveness, it is most commonly used for personal transport and exploration on undeveloped worlds. Variants include the Ranger CV touring model, the Ranger RC racing bike, and the more heavily armed Ranger TR combat type.","g":["tumbril land systems","all-terrain vehicle (atv)","human vehicle"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/851938ef-e4ca-48b0-be08-61da5fa6d87a"},
{"id":"rayari-inc","gp":"0jGnJnMwke","t":"Rayari Inc","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Rayari Incorporated is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) research company that specializes in agriculture and bio-engineering. Founded in 2803 by Clara Douglas, Edward Kesamyn, and Asif Reader, it first came to prominence when the founders created a complete line of plants recreated from the genetic code of ones indigenous to the then [recently-massacred](gp:01dWeqnMr1) planet Garron II. In 2863, the company expanded into social engineering, creating large arcologies such as [Reza's Landing](gp:Vgg7jB2YE9) designed for planets with hostile environments. The company maintains many labs throughout the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE).","g":["commercial and industrial goods manufacturer","research and development company","vosca","elysium iii","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e87fe0a1-3379-4521-a432-5e375cb37599"},
{"id":"razor","gp":"RkZ96DxvgB","t":"Razor","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Razor is racing spacecraft developed by [Mirai](gp:Vy2B1o6gn6), a subsidiary of [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) (MISC). In 2947, Mirai launched the Razor in a bid to disrupt [Origin's](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) dominance of the [Murray Cup](gp:bE3r71yZ87) and as a potential competitor for the [Koa e Ko'ia](gp:RkGpX3LJJz) endurance races. Thanks to MISC's lend lease agreement with the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj), the Razor was designed and built at MISC's R.il'a facility under the supervision of veteran Ship Engineer To.k'o se Lyil and offers advanced thrusters and other systems not currently available on competing racers. Variants include the [Razor EX](gp:bZwQKOegDL) stealth interceptor and the overclocked [Razor LX](gp:VpGE54wvlk), which trades maneuverability and weaponry for a focus on pure one-directional speed.","g":["racing","misc","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f6a0219a-63a9-4dba-be17-d9bea807fd01"},
{"id":"razor-ex","gp":"bZwQKOegDL","t":"Razor EX","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Razor EX is a stealth variant of the [Razor](gp:RkZ96DxvgB) racing spacecraft developed by [Mirai](gp:Vy2B1o6gn6), a subsidiary of [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) (MISC). It was initially developed to [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) specifications for use as a surveillance and extraction ship. The model trades a maximum speed and overall acceleration in exchange for an increase in stealth capability, achieved through the inclusion of signature-reducing materials in its hull plating. While the Razor EX has only been available to civilians in limited quantities, Mirai continues to produce the model for government sales.","g":["stealth","misc","human spacecraft","razor"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/930c89bc-7a0e-434b-ab8e-30a25561ee93"},
{"id":"razor-lx","gp":"VpGE54wvlk","t":"Razor LX","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Razor LX is a limited edition variant of the [Razor](gp:RkZ96DxvgB) racing spacecraft developed by [Mirai](gp:Vy2B1o6gn6), a subsidiary of [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) (MISC). The LX model was developed as part of a marketing push to celebrate MISC's 50th anniversary. It features a singular focus on straightaway speed at the cost of overall maneuverability, which it achieves with an overclocked engine. The Razor LX has been built in only limited numbers.","g":["racing","razor","misc","luxury","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/48715d57-f103-4b4b-bfab-614b3bed8a89"},
{"id":"reclaimer","gp":"ReJa8MBg4k","t":"Reclaimer","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Reclaimer is a specialized spacecraft manufactured by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). Designed to gather spaceborne salvage, it is equipped with a large mechanical arm operated remotely from the crew deck. Salvage is then processed into raw metals using automated facilities to the rear of the spacecraft before being sorted in a series of internal containers.","g":["heavy salvage","aegis dynamics","salvage","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ff2e7903-52d8-4bb4-a92b-de826262f1df"},
{"id":"red-festival","gp":"RAXpZ2z6YY","t":"Red Festival","k":"history","c":["Human","Holidays"],"x":"Red Festival is a holiday celebrated in late January or early February annually in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It originated in old Earth (Sol III) customs that celebrated the end of the year by tracking the lunisolar cycle instead of the solar cycle. [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) who followed the lunar calendar took their practice with them during the [Human Colonial Expansion Era](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm) (2380-2530), often cementing the Red Festival as a tradition as early as the date of a colony's foundation. Today, the festival is celebrated by wearing colors that symbolize good fortune such as red and gold, eating long foods such as dyed red noodles or calossk tentacles, and the exchange of gilded red envelopes containing good luck tokens or credits. Recently, instead of handing the envelope directly to a recipient, givers will hide the envelopes for those deemed in need by fate to discover. [Banu](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) often join the festivities, hiding red envelopes in honor of Cassa, the Patron of Luck.","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/62058112-1332-4b23-8008-6aaf17382a2d"},
{"id":"redeemer","gp":"0OaB4g9O2e","t":"Redeemer","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Redeemer is a gunship developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) for the [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). An armored spacecraft equipped with turrets and missiles, it is commonly used by planetary security forces. The Redeemer has also been used in extensive operations against the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO). Surplus models are sold in the civilian market.","g":["gunship","aegis dynamics","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fec8c280-6dd1-483d-a07f-343b4c4c8d4b"},
{"id":"reisse-rhetor-iii","gp":"0QljXw43Ev","t":"Reisse (Rhetor III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Reisse is the third planet from the sun in the [Rhetor system](gp:0ODlqMJXmP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The majority of Reisse's population are either students or faculty of the many universities on the world's surface. As such, Reisse is a major generator of research, and is supported by one of the largest number of communications relays in the UEE. The culture of Reisse is centered around the free exchange of ideas, and its politicians are often at the forefront of cultural and political movements.","g":["reisse","rhetor iii","rhetor system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4ba66036-71b5-480d-8b82-f78d7263484b"},
{"id":"reliant-kore","gp":"0Gz5jp112E","t":"Reliant Kore","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Reliant is a light freighter developed by [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC)]((https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/bE3rB7YJDv-misc)) as a versatile and agile entry to the intro-level ship market. The [series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/reliant) was introduced in SEY 2946 as a followup to the [Freelancer](gp:RvgzWy7o6v) design. Like the Freelancer, the Reliant Kore integrates a variety of [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) technologies and design aesthetics including a vertical flight mode. Variants include the [Sen](gp:R6v8XE3LND) research ship, the [Tana](gp:0KnArjgO9P) fighter and the [Mako](gp:V8gJQwJ22O) broadcast suite.","g":["light freight","reliant","misc","freight","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/865deed9-301f-440a-a2f2-9399d5f0d2a5"},
{"id":"reliant-mako","gp":"V8gJQwJ22O","t":"Reliant Mako","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Reliant Mako is a variant of the [Reliant](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/reliant) spacecraft developed by [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC)]((https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/bE3rB7YJDv-misc)). The Mako modifies the standard [Kore](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) and installs broadwave spectrum technology and a suite of compound lens cameras to capture and relay footage. MISC established the idea after seeing the need for improved broadcasting capacities during natural disasters and an increasing number of [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) and pirate attacks. The Mako includes bespoke equipment to support its broadcaster role, including an image enhancement suite and a turret-mounted optical array.","g":["reporting","misc","human spacecraft","reliant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/11568db9-32ce-4e3b-b69f-edf1967db495"},
{"id":"reliant-sen","gp":"R6v8XE3LND","t":"Reliant Sen","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Reliant Sen is a variant of the [Reliant](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/reliant) spacecraft developed by [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) that adapts the Kore platform for use as a single-ship explorer and science platform. The spacecraft comes pre-configured with an additional scanner suite and component upgrades that expand its overall range. Larger concerns seeking to add light craft support when operating the similarly MISC-produced [Endeavor](gp:RXlXZ6Pw9N) science ship have adopted the Reliant Sen as a part of their standard fleets.","g":["science","light science","misc","human spacecraft","reliant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/daf7663e-052f-400b-9bef-0386185d69fe"},
{"id":"reliant-tana","gp":"0KnArjgO9P","t":"Reliant Tana","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Reliant Tana is a variant of the [Reliant](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/reliant) spacecraft series developed by [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). The most produced of the Reliant variants, the Tana was first developed by MISC engineers as a dedicated model for use by security operators and law enforcement circles looking for a cheap, but durable addition to their fleet. The Tana drops the specialized utility component of other Reliant variants in exchange for the addition of a second size three weapons mount.","g":["light fighter","fighter","misc","human spacecraft","reliant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8386984c-fb0a-4850-9525-d90c8013318a"},
{"id":"republic-of-one","gp":"R6dY9N8akw","t":"Republic of One","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Republic of One is a premium fashion house known for its cutting-edge suits and dresses. Favored by celebrities of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE), the company's signature complex, form-fitting designs are a common sight at vid debuts. Lead designer Laren'zo frequently incorporates eye-catching details such as partially-hidden gemstones or colorful panels that are revealed when the wearer moves in the brand's garments.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bf4d28ef-d13f-4b25-83eb-a6131f689d8b"},
{"id":"research-drone","gp":"VY4WgzZd9p","t":"Research Drone","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Research drones are automated, self-propelling devices that can be remotely controlled through dangerous or otherwise inhospitable environments. They can also be used to collect hazardous materials and perform limited on the spot computer analysis. Drone operators with enough clearance from the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) government can use research drones in systems protected by the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP).","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f7336199-18b3-47a6-abe7-c2bd0034128e"},
{"id":"rest-and-relax","gp":"VaZwe6zqEw","t":"Rest & Relax","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Rest & Relax is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) company that maintains a chain of hospitality waystations throughout human space. Engineer Johann Alejandre founded Rest & Relax as a single rest stop in the [Baker system](gp:Rz2KGkv13N) in 2901. The company initially operated by purchasing and adapting decommissioned stations near well-traveled lanes. As they expanded, they developed a standard pre-fabricated Rest & Relax station that could be easily shipped and assembled on site. Though individual amenities may vary per station, they generally offer refueling and repair options for their customers.","g":["rest and relax","spacecraft repair","johann alehandre","baker system","spacecraft refuel"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a310edd5-a8cc-49e2-81ab-eb56deee5a05"},
{"id":"retaliator","gp":"0qnN6j2Gq7","t":"Retaliator","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Retaliator is a strategic bomber developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) for the [United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). Variants of the spacecraft have been used in the UEEN for three centuries. Despite distinguishing themselves in various operations such as the [Battle of Idris IV](gp:ReJajXKelk) in SEY 2544, they are most commonly associated with the abuses of the [Messer regime](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo). The current model of the Retaliator was built with modular bays which allow it to be converted from its original role to service as a cargo or dropship. Civilians are known to extensively customize surplus Retaliators for non-wartime roles.","g":["heavy bomber","aegis dynamics","bomber","military spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5f701c92-8c21-4237-b409-a7b06c1a2d21"},
{"id":"retribution","gp":"VDoP9a3lKz","t":"Retribution","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"Retribution is a dreadnought spacecraft manufactured by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military in cooperation with multiple major manufacturers. Designed to counter [Vanduul Kingships](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm), the Retribution is the largest type of capital ship used by the UEE military at around 2700 meters in length. It was codenamed Project Ouadeen during its development period. Initially started in 2931, the project proved too costly and was put on hold multiple times in order to acquire more funding. The project was resurrected in the wake of the [Battle of Vega II](gp:0Gz5mkprmg) and in SEY 2946, the first completed Retribution was assigned to the 65th Battle Group under the command of Admiral [Ernst Bishop](gp:ReJaavPB3k).","g":["capital ship","dreadnought","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/33ad3d53-9d2b-4148-b8ed-81f54bbdf661"},
{"id":"revel-and-york","gp":"ReJa7vZlJX","t":"Revel & York","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Revel & York is a high-end [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) design firm, specializing in furniture and hangar manufacturing. After being founded as a couture design group, the company made an unexpected turn to hangar development in the early 30th century. Revel & York gained a foothold in the market by privately working for elite customers to produce fully featured, bespoke spaces. The service proved so popular that the company soon began offering the service to the public. Hangars developed by Revel & York are usually larger than others on the market, catering to owners of multi-crew ships and larger freighters.","g":["revel and york","hangar manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cfc91e6c-34b2-4cea-88cd-35187c7b527d"},
{"id":"revenant-tree","gp":"0Oa5AMlQAw","t":"Revenant Tree","k":"life","c":["Plants","Human"],"x":"# Revenant Tree\n\nThe revenant tree is a variety of altrucia, a leafy tree indigenous to [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). It emerged after the altrucia was introduced to [Hyperion (Fora III)](gp:RegWGPlxqy) by geoengineers in an attempt to create shelterbelts against dust storms. While most of the trees didn't survive the environment, the ones that did adapted, giving rise to plants that seemed dead until closer observation. Its pollen is used to make the illegal drug altruciatoxin.\n\n# Description and Life Cycle\nIn contrast to the leafy, colorful altrucia, the revenant tree has coarse, spiny leaves and is dusty brown in color. Its thick, dense bark prevents collected moisture from evaporating in Hyperion's heat and high winds. Most of its nutrients come from the soil. Because its environment is covered by thick dust clouds for the majority of the year, it goes through long periods of dormancy followed by fast growth phases when exposed to sunlight and water.\n\nFollowing the brief wet season, the revenant enters its reproductive cycle, directing all of its stored energy towards producing flowers sturdy enough to withstand storm-force winds. The flowers open in the morning and evening. Wind currents pick up the pollen and distribute it to other plants. Once it has been fertilized, the revenant flower becomes a cone and produces seeds that too can be carried by the wind when they reach maturity.\n\n# Houseplant\nThe revenant thrives as a houseplant. Since it grows well under low-light, low-moisture conditions, it can be raised in places that receive little sunlight, such as sealed colonies or spacecraft. If it is over-fertilized and overwatered, its roots may rot or the bark may split and open the inside of the tree to potential infections. For these reasons, a revenant tree is best kept in an ecosphere set to mimic the conditions on Hyperion and prevent overzealous care. Inside the ecosphere, it will go through its full lifecycle. However, it will not successfully reproduce unless it is removed from the ecosphere and purposely exposed to another revenant. Well-tended revenant trees can live for a century or more.\n\n# Uses\nThe revenant is cultivated for its pollen which, though illegal under UEE law, can be chemically processed into a prohibited substance called altruciatoxin. Also known as dust, candy, or round off, altruciatoxin is powdered and can be absorbed through the mucus membranes. Those who wish to experience a reduced high may smoke it instead. It causes sensory enhancement, muscular relaxation, and lethargy in its users. Though uncommon, usage of the drug can induce a violent and rarely deadly allergic reaction, especially in those who are already sensitive to pollen.\n\nWild revenants can be used as a source of water. While the insides of the tree will induce vomiting if eaten raw, if passed through a fine-meshed sieve, the bitter liquid is safely drinkable can hydrate in an emergency.","g":["altrucia","hyperion","fora iii","altruciatoxin"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6c7d055c-a276-43f9-a59e-d7f47e0985f4"},
{"id":"reverie-ar-lens","gp":"0qaBdrgN47","t":"Reverie AR Lens","k":"vehicle","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"The Reverie AR Lens is a contact lens manufactured by [microTech](gp:bE3rBB4j7J). Designed to integrate with the mobiGlas 2.0 and all subsequent models, it is a thin lens made with a proprietary hypoallergenic material that is placed directly on the surface of a user's eye. While worn, it transmits real-time information from the mobiGlas directly into a user's field of vision.","g":["microtech (company)","computer component"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/67ca0f6f-1bac-4ef5-ba2a-a5c10db87e51"},
{"id":"rezas-landing","gp":"Vgg7jB2YE9","t":"Reza's Landing","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human","Tevarin"],"x":"Reza's Landing is a city arcology built to withstand the harsh environment of [Vosca (Elysium III)](gp:R9vQWkLNNM). The structure was constructed by research company Rayari Inc. in order to protect their equipment from damage due to persistent sandstorms on the surface. The company would eventually allow non-affiliated residents to move in, and over the years several underground expansions have been built until it reached the size of a small city. Today, it is the primary center of commerce on the planet.","g":["cities","rayari inc","vosca","elysium iii","uee city","sealed settlement","tevarin settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d976d8d2-0521-4c71-809c-c7d2ee23d5de"},
{"id":"rhea-sol-6b","gp":"R4jo9g7Z2J","t":"Rhea (Sol 6b)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Rhea (Sol 6b) is a moon of [Saturn (Sol VI)](gp:0jGpvn8AOW), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Composed of water ice and rock, it has numerous high-albedo ice cliffs that appear as streaks on the surface when viewed from space with the naked eye. Although it does experience some endogenic activity in the forms of cryovolcanoes, it is only slightly geologically active.","g":["rhea","sol 6b","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/17ac0ac6-ca73-4446-a96f-cc73a1127447"},
{"id":"rhetor-i","gp":"RL653GMraL","t":"Rhetor I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Rhetor I is a mesoplanet in the [Rhetor system](gp:0ODlqMJXmP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Because it lacks an atmosphere, there is an extreme difference between its day and night temperatures. Despite its extreme daytime heat, there are patches of water ice on Rhetor I, generally located on the floors of deep craters around the north pole.","g":["rhetor system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/75b5b313-ef7f-49f6-98d3-abbbba72519d"},
{"id":"rhetor-system","gp":"0ODlqMJXmP","t":"Rhetor System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Rhetor system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that consists of a G-type main sequence star, a mesoplanet, three terrestrial planets, and a gas giant. Discovered in 2287 by PhD students Neil Nyemeto and Leona Sono from the [Martian Institute of Space Technology (MIST)](gp:RL67MAJreO), their decision to share their discovery with MIST's president Adrianne Zemlock led to Rhetor becoming a system that is dedicated to education rather than corporate interests. [Persei](gp:0ODlqM6zKO) is a center of public education and private research institutes, and some of the most prestigious universities in the UEE are located on [Reisse](gp:0QljXw43Ev) and [Mentor](gp:RPDlZJeDLX).","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f493c087-687c-45fd-9166-4654123d99de"},
{"id":"rhetor-v","gp":"02kPEOz56e","t":"Rhetor V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Rhetor V is a gas giant, and is the fifth planet from the sun of the [Rhetor system](gp:0ODlqMJXmP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Its multicolored atmosphere and swirling storms make it a popular destination for tourists, pilots, and students from nearby planets. Reportedly, students from [Mentor (Rhetor IV)](gp:RPDlZJeDLX) are known to take the hallucinogenic drug Maze and stare at the planet for hours to de-stress, especially during exam season.","g":["rhetor system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/20d7ba4e-532c-4df5-9b79-428ff863eea5"},
{"id":"rijora","gp":"VlM4KG6XN5","t":"Rijora","k":"culture","c":["Culture","Tevarin"],"x":"Rijora is a set of guidelines and principles concerning the behavior and lifestyle of the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) people. Written by many authors over a long period of time, it was created in response to early Tevarin perishing repeatedly at the hands of predators on their homeworld [Kaleeth](gp:VarAXY2zy2) (now Jalan, Elysium IV). It emphasizes an active existence and requires responsibility to oneself and one's community. Followers are required to develop and consistently maintain physical and mental skills, especially as pertains to warfare. Before the end of the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) (SEY 2603 - 2610) all Tevarin were required to memorize the Rijora and could recite it on command. Rijora was renounced by many Tevarin after the war due to its failure to uphold its promise to deliver victory. During the events of the [Tevarin Purge](gp:R6dWB877Nn), parts of Rijora were lost when the authoritative codex that recorded it in its entirety was destroyed; namely, passages that had been revised or redacted from print but had been documented for historic purposes. Rijora has seen a resurgence in popularity in recent years thanks to an ongoing movement to revive Tevarin culture.","g":["religion","tevarin religion"]},
{"id":"rijoran-temple","gp":"0Gz5vY1poE","t":"Rijoran Temple","k":"place","c":["Archaeology","Tevarin","Locations"],"x":"The Rijoran Temple on [Jalan (Elysium IV)](gp:VarAXY2zy2) is one of the few remaining religious buildings constructed by the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) that was not lost during their cultural [Purge](gp:R6dWB877Nn) after the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv). During the Purge, Tevarin made several attempts to destroy this temple, but [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) militias were able to protect it. Today, it is one of the most popular tourist attractions on Jalan.\n\nRijora was a doctrine that emphasized active existence and responsibility to the self and others. Followers were required to develop and consistently maintain physical and mental skills, especially as pertained to warfare. Many temples, including the final standing one on Jalan, were built without seating in order to provide wide spaces open to all followers of Rijora to train.","g":["rijora","religion","tevarin religion","building"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7eccb9c5-30a9-48e2-a81d-d52404e2a9fa"},
{"id":"rsi","gp":"RWwZDn2Xrw","t":"Roberts Space Industries (RSI)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Military","Human"],"x":"Roberts Space Industries (RSI), founded in the early 21st century SEY, is one of the oldest and most influential space technology companies in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Spacecraft, spacecraft components, and [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) technology make up the bulk of their products. In 2075, RSI created the [quantum core engine](gp:RX3DOkJdxJ), and in 2113, the company released the earliest terraforming machinery utilized by [Humans](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl). \n\nRSI entered a period of decline during the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo), when their military contracts were terminated in favor of [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv), and further shrank 2757, when [Ulysses Messer X](gp:bBp6YZPOGO) publicly blamed the company for the death of [Anthony Tanaka](gp:RwZBdpj2rz). It wasn't until the [end of the Messer Era](gp:bE3rKa32P7) that RSI's military contracts were reinstated. Today, their [Bengal](gp:RwZBLqLQdp) line of carrier ships and [Pegasus](gp:bBp64jrA7d) line of escort carriers are utilized by the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4).","g":["rsi","earth","sol iii","spacecraft component manufacturer","terraforming company","armor manufacturer","spacecraft manufacturer","vehicle manufacturer","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fb043453-1385-4ed0-b299-6aee53c2fe13"},
{"id":"rook-heavy-metals","gp":"RLMmAGGOZO","t":"ROOK Heavy Metals","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"ROOK Heavy Metals is a manufacturer of combat armor and personal protection gear. Their products have a good reputation for defense, but the heavier models are generally less maneuverable than other manufacturers' alternatives. Though not intentionally designed for intimidation, the large and boxy profile of the armor strikes a memorable silhouette on the battlefield.","g":["armor manufacturer","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6af4c1f2-f9da-4c9a-929a-09a4b56f4503"},
{"id":"rough-and-ready","gp":"RMNjxwk8pB","t":"Rough & Ready","k":"faction","c":["Organizations","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Rough & Ready is a major criminal organization known for operating refueling stations throughout the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). \n\nFounded by former Headhunters enforcer Rook Garavis in SEY 2939, the gang's early focus was to pull back on active criminal activity and gain enough capital to do more than just survive. They conducted a series of meticulously planned raids on multiple refueling stations, taking them over and establishing themselves as the off-market version of [Rest & Relax](gp:VaZwe6zqEw). By the 2940s, their refueling stations had become a dominant force in Pyro. \n\nWhile they charge high prices, the protection they offer to those using their stations is considered worth the price. Likely in honor of their founder, chess pieces are a prominent part of their symbolism. Their major base of operations, [Checkmate Station](gp:RPDeA41EZX), is located near [Monox (Pyro II)](gp:0jGdgLEjqJ).","g":["outlaw factions","human outlaw factions","pyro outlaw faction"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/84039358-0c72-4f25-adb3-656665d809f6"},
{"id":"roussimoff-rehabilitation-systems","gp":"RMXymwgLYn","t":"Roussimoff Rehabilitation Systems","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Roussimoff Rehabilitation Systems is a multi-disciplinary manufacturer of personal and spacecraft-mounted weaponry and protective armor. Headquartered on [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB), it is distinct among defense corporations in that it mostly produces non-lethal weaponry. Roussimoff's signature product is the Faction-9 stun baton which has been broadly adopted by the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk). Their lines of body armor are frequently produced under contract for police organizations and corporations.","g":["armor manufacturer","weapons manufacturer","earth","sol iii","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cee15f45-f9e2-4199-bec8-82e76a6305a3"},
{"id":"ruin-station","gp":"RX3AzPdnw8","t":"Ruin Station","k":"place","c":["Locations"],"x":"Ruin Station is a space station that orbits [Terminus (Pyro VI)](gp:RAXv9kpk5m) in the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). \n\nConstructed by [Gold Horizon](gp:bmNrApJp3P) for [Pyrotechnic Amalgamated](gp:VpM4anYBn1) in SEY 2512 as the company's new base of operations, the station, then known as MacEwan Station, served as the main processing point of exports from Pyro and saw continual use for decades. When Pyrotechnic Amalgamated declared bankruptcy in 2563, the company decided to abandon the station instead of bearing the cost of decommissioning it. It was shortly thereafter claimed by outlaws, who gave it its current nickname. \n\nToday, Ruin Station is Pyro's main hub of drug manufacture, blackmarket sales, and other criminal enterprises, and has been the site of many major power struggles between rival gangs. Criminal organization [Rough & Ready](gp:RMNjxwk8pB) took control of the station since 2951, ousting the extremist gang [XenoThreat](gp:VgExkEAB19), who had held it since 2947.","g":["macewan station","space station","pyrotechnic amalgamated","independent space station","rough & ready","pyro system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/917d340c-9e3b-4f95-9467-36993c65f8a0"},
{"id":"rust-society","gp":"RxnjXwZ7lQ","t":"Rust Society","k":"company","c":["Organizations","Human"],"x":"The Rust Society is a majority-[Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) organization of haulers and salvagers who mentor newcomers in both fields. Founded in SEY 2423 by Franklin \"Knocks\" Yeung, it began as an informal, irregular gathering of pilots who shared job postings with one over glasses of Rust, a potent grain alcohol. Over the years, it evolved into an information-sharing and mentorship organization funded by membership dues and expanded onto other worlds. When military supply lines were interrupted during the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM), the Rust Society stepped in to help, leading to sharp increase in membership. Today, there are chapters in most [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) systems.","g":["non-profit organization","uee organizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/644087e7-b9b6-46b1-b57d-18445589064d"},
{"id":"ryixyan-hyoton-iii","gp":"bBz9mEDyqO","t":"RyiXy'an (Hyoton III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"RyiXy'an (Hyoton III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Hyoton system](gp:RkGDYnpq4L), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9), and is the homeworld of the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) people. Once a lush world teeming with life, its atmosphere was accidentally tainted with poison by [House Kl.ō](gp:V8gJ62qO81) during an assassination attempt gone awry, killing millions and forcing its remaining inhabitants to flee to the nearby colony world [Ka'ua (Hyoton IV)](gp:0qa4Zow7pk). This event abruptly ended the ongoing [civil war](gp:VyvYA5qmqX) and forced the Xi'an to reassess their culture. Now classified as a smog planet, RyiXy'an has resisted all [terraformation](gp:R6dWOrLEM4) attempts, and little life remains beneath its toxic clouds.","g":["ryixy'an","hyoton iii","hyoton system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet","xi'an homeworld","homeworlds"]},
{"id":"rytif-bremen-ii","gp":"R5pA7q691W","t":"Rytif (Bremen II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Rytif is an inhabited planet in the [Bremen system](gp:02kd45eyxe), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The second planet from the sun, it was slowly [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) for [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) habitation after the system was discovered in 2441. Rytif was a major center of food production during the [Second Tevarin War (2603 - 2610)](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv), and was used as a headquarters for anti-Messer activists in the years leading up to the [2792 revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7). Its capital, [Stalford](gp:VY4Wj6Yrj1), is the home of spacecraft manufacturer [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34).","g":["rytif","bremen ii","habitable","habitable planet","human planet","bremen system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0ea89337-cc38-4d58-a45c-3901a5f360a2"},
{"id":"ryool-taal-v","gp":"0qa4ZPez9A","t":"Ryōl (T.āl V)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Ryōl (T.āl V) is the fifth planet from the sun of the [T.āl system](gp:R4j2mdjZE5), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). All buildings on the planet sport orange accents, giving them a fiery appearance in correct lighting conditions. \n\nA center of product manufacturing, its most prominent economic activity is the construction of weapons. The [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military maintains a strong presence on Ryōl, simultaneously protecting sensitive information pertaining to arms development and enforcing order.","g":["ryōl","t.āl iv","t.āl system","habitable planet","habitable","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/99efb383-f067-48e1-8e28-67df702eb4f4"},
{"id":"s-pop","gp":"bE3rkJvqJ7","t":"S-Pop","k":"culture","c":["Music","Human"],"x":"# S-POP\n\nS-pop (abbreviation of Saisei Pop) is a form of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) popular music originating on [Saisei (Centauri III)](gp:Vy22NQJ1q6). Common characteristics of S-pop include the incorporation of relaxing organic-sourced sounds and traditional Saisei instruments. The term can refer either specifically to the popular music of Saisei or to any music functionally derived therefrom. \n\n# ORIGIN\nThe earliest iteration of traditional Saisei music evolved in the 25th century, when Saisei was first established and built up as a colony world. The form owes a significant amount to the slow, methodical process involved in planning and constructing Saisei colony. While typical colonies grow in fits as interest in particular exports drive commerce and immigration, Seisei was instead built up deliberately according to a long-term plan. Lacking the booms and busts of traditional early colonial development that leave newly settled worlds more closely tied to a home culture, Saisei developed its own disparate takes on a variety of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) art forms. \n\nDuring the initial settlement period, luxury imports from Earth (Sol III) were extremely limited. As a result, traditional Human instruments were uncommon beyond those carried as part of the first wave's personal preference kits. Colonists turned to local materials to develop their own offshoots. Trees seeded during the early [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) process produced softer wood than is traditionally used to create stringed instruments. This limitation ultimately gave rise to the Saisei-made softwood guitar, or s-guitar, which produces a mellower, more resonant sound than its Earth-made equivalent. \n\nSaisei musicians soon began experimenting with natural sounds. By the middle of the 27th century, a typical Saisei arrangement might include several dozen different natural samples, often arrayed so elaborately that their source could not be externally determined. \n\n# WIDESPREAD POPULARITY\nFor roughly four hundred years, Saisei traditional music was not widespread beyond the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5). That changed in 2932 when Saisei-based band [The Claw](gp:0n9vkMLlzd) appeared on [Terra, Show Me the Music!](gp:RwZBwjdr5X), a popular [Spectrum](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galacapedia/article/VaZwen9E2Q-spectrum)-based showcase for aspiring bands. Instead of performing an original song, The Claw chose to perform a Saisei-styled interpretation of [Clover's](gp:box5qg83aL) \"Moonlight,\" then at the height of its popularity. The group used a traditional s-guitar and an array of cultivated aquatic insect sounds to give the song what the series' host termed \"eerie, still movement.\" The performance was accompanied by a holographic light show based in traditional Saisei culture. \n\nIn under two weeks, The Claw had the number one single on popular music charts of both Earth and [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). Viewers initially curious about the light show and the unusual sounds became interested in the music itself. The Terra Gazette dubbed this style of music S-pop. A brief S-pop craze followed The Claw's larger UEE debut with music producers rushing to sign hitherto unknown acts from Saisei and other performers around the galaxy eager to emulate what they considered an exciting new discovery. \n\nS-pop ruled Spectrum from November 2932 to December 2934 with dozens of songs taking top positions. Although interest in S-pop has waxed and waned in the ensuing years, the impact of the fad has had permanence.","g":["music genre","saisei","centauri iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/eeaed451-ebeb-42e3-a81a-cf3c504878d1"},
{"id":"sapuaang-lauo-iv","gp":"bBz3m21j78","t":"S.ap'uāng (La'uo IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"S.ap'uāng (La'uo IV) is the fourth planet from the sun of the [La'uo system](gp:R6demJ8Xmq), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A gas giant with an orange, white, and brown-belted atmosphere it is the brightest natural object in the La'uo system. Violent storms rage along the borders of its latitudinal bands, which move in conflicting circulation patterns. The wind in the upper atmosphere is very turbulent, with jet streams that commonly move at over 100 meters per second.","g":["s.ap'uāng","la'uo iv","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","la'uo system","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bd414184-32bb-4ca5-9119-097f446c3e2e"},
{"id":"sabre","gp":"0NwpeQOqY4","t":"Sabre","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Sabre is a space superiority fighter sold by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). Aegis developed the Sabre in response to a United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN) request for a fighter capable of out-matching the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) Stinger heavy fighter. Aegis pursued development as part of a company-wide initiative to unseat [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) and restore their place as the UEE's prime military spacecraft contractor. While the Sabre bid has yet to be accepted by the UEEN, the ship is currently available for purchase by civilians. Variants of the Sabre include the Raven intelligence model and the Comet special edition.","g":["stealth fighter","aegis dynamics","stealth","fighter","human spacecraft","sabre series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d59a069b-0da5-459a-ab99-57261aa1bc44"},
{"id":"sabre-comet","gp":"0NjZkNmlLp","t":"Sabre Comet","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Sabre Comet is a medium fighter manufactured by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). A variant of the [Sabre](gp:0NwpeQOqY4) space superiority fighter, it was created as part of the \"Masters of Flight\" series in conjunction with the flight sim game [Arena Commander](gp:VyvY5LQXd6). It pays tribute to famed pilot Captain Kamur Dailon for his work with Aegis to create the original Comet fighter upon his retirement from the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) after the [Battle of Idris IV](gp:ReJajXKelk). Like the original Comet, this Sabre variant comes with a weapons loadout that emphasizes dogfighting.","g":["fighter","medium fighter","aegis dynamics","human spacecraft","sabre series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/564d3b79-d6cf-4969-8e77-556eb265282e"},
{"id":"sabre-firebird","gp":"VpMOy27NzX","t":"Sabre Firebird","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Sabre Firebird is a medium fighter manufactured by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). A variant of the [Sabre](gp:0NwpeQOqY4) space superiority fighter, it was redesigned to emphasize ambush strikes. A specialized missile rack paired with two gatling cannons allows the Firebird to execute rapid attacks, and the addition of extra thrusters when compared to the base model gives the ship an extra speed boost to help it escape before the enemy can strike back.","g":["fighter","medium fighter","aegis dynamics","human spacecraft","sabre series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8dc15ace-0e2b-4d5c-8475-3c427417cc8d"},
{"id":"sabre-raven","gp":"V3G8Ez95Jm","t":"Sabre Raven","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Sabre Raven is an interdiction spacecraft manufactured by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). A variant of the [Sabre](gp:0NwpeQOqY4) space superiority fighter, the Raven maintains the speed and maneuverability of the base model but has a lower ship signature and decreased wingspan, thus increasing its stealth capabilities. In place of the missile racks found on the base variant, it has two EMP generators that can be used to scramble enemy systems.","g":["fighter","medium fighter","aegis dynamics","human spacecraft","sabre series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c8220e03-7f1d-46f2-b494-50a03a1d8320"},
{"id":"sail-casia","gp":"RAX8P87825","t":"Sail Casia","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The sail casia is a genetically modified plant created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke). First sold in 2930, it is a part of Rayari Inc's line of plants designed to aid in the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) process. It has quick-growing, pliable, leaves that can be used as a plastic substitute on newly-settled worlds. When cut into strips and tightly woven together, sheets of sail casica leaves can become water-repelling tarps or raincoats.","g":["rayari inc","herbaceous plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e519c89a-7a5c-4c04-8769-79c26046e06e"},
{"id":"saisei-centauri-iii","gp":"Vy22NQJ1q6","t":"Saisei (Centauri III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Saisei is an inhabited planet in the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Its buildings and urban development were designed to exist in harmony with the natural landscape. The environmental laws of Saisei prohibit excessive population growth and tightly control allowable levels of pollution from local businesses. Thanks to Saisei's carefully preserved environment and organic architecture, tourism is one of the planet's main industries. Spacecraft manufacturer [Musashi Industrial and Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv) maintains its headquarters in the capital, [Fujin City](gp:RxNxAeyOq6).","g":["saisei","centauri iii","centauri system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e13463f0-b962-4b42-961a-a4725603a8dc"},
{"id":"sakura-sun","gp":"VpGEzn5edL","t":"Sakura Sun","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human","Weapons"],"x":"Sakura Sun is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturing conglomerate headquartered in Tokyo, Earth (Sol III) that produces a diverse range of consumer products such as home goods, children's toys, and starship engines. Spacecraft components are developed under the Sakura Sun Space Sciences Division (S4D). In 2922, Sakura Sun released the multi-particle wave cannon, a spacecraft weapon developed through research of [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) technology. In 2943, they debuted their first power plant, the Light Blossom, designed for low-emission travel.","g":["spacecraft component manufacturer","commercial and industrial goods manufacturer","armor manufacturer","earth","sol iii","weapons manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a2a2aa45-2b9c-447c-963d-70550d6b5659"},
{"id":"samuel-messer-viii","gp":"RkZ9W2L2NB","t":"Samuel Messer VIII","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Samuel Messer VIII (2678-2715) was [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) from 2697 to 2715, though some historians date his rule from 2701. He had officially been named successor by his mother [Illyana VI](gp:bZwQBNmWrL), but his cousin [Astrid](gp:0KnA1D5nQM) seized power upon her death and ousted Samuel from power. After a four year civil war, agents of Samuel orchestrated Astrid VII's assassination, and Samuel officially took the office of Imperator. He tightened restrictions on free speech during his rule and ordered multiple military suppressions of civilian protests. He was succeeded by his older brother [Galor Meser IX](gp:VyvYAGKxAz) in 2715.","g":["uee imperator","messer dynasty","messer era"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0bcf7968-79d4-4a2e-86d7-f55221ede019"},
{"id":"santokyaai","gp":"RWolyEwlxZ","t":"San'tok.yāi","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Xi'an"],"x":"The San'tok.yāi is a medium fighter manufactured by [Aopoa](gp:VyvY5jyZwp) for the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) market that debuted at the 2948 Intergalatic Aerospace Expo. Over a decade of intelligence collected by various branches of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) confirms that the ship is a near exact replica of a front line medium fighter utilized by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military. Though it has been adapted for Human pilots, it retains the dexterity and tight handling long observed in its Xi'an precursor.","g":["aopoa","fighter","medium fighter","xi'an spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/97bfcb7b-7a93-4030-9692-f17e5d7546fd"},
{"id":"saturn-sol-vi","gp":"0jGpvn8AOW","t":"Saturn (Sol VI)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Saturn (Sol VI) is the sixth planet from the sun of the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The second largest planet in the system, it is also the least dense, and has long been a subject of fascination to [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) due to its beautiful set of rings. Vacation homes that orbit Saturn with a view of the rings are some of the most prized pieces of real estate in the system, and the more luxurious ones are often sold for billions of credits.","g":["saturn","sol vi"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a8532e83-ce05-4d0d-b206-00fcd18a1565"},
{"id":"scanner","gp":"R9vlW7AgQM","t":"Scanner","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"A scanner is a type of device that can take in a wide range of data, perform an analysis, and compile a report on its findings. Basic scanners can be used to provide general information about the world, such as the identification of a person or object. Specialized scanners can be used to attain in-depth knowledge about the subject being scanned, such as the mineral contents of asteroids. Scanners are also utilized on spacecraft alongside radar to detect the presence of enemy combatants.","g":["energy shield"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a3236a77-2850-41b6-bf1d-618086094731"},
{"id":"schui","gp":"VDzM7K6o45","t":"Schui","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Schui is a high-end clothing and accessory brand that specializes in suits, gowns, and formalwear. Known for its experimental designs, garments from Schui often utilize textured fabrics or unusual cuts to create non-standard silhouettes. In SEY 2942, the brand made record profits when it debuted the Dafne eyewear collection, made up of pieces inspired by historic [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) fashion but with a modern twist.","g":["clothing manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b3c9cc4e-e528-412b-9610-2edd4bfe65a8"},
{"id":"schwester-chronos-ii","gp":"bEzjpwJ452","t":"Schwester (Chronos II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Schwester (Chronos II) is an uninhabitable planet located second from the sun of the [Chronos system](gp:RvlQZKy95l), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). In 2925, a [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) attaché was tasked with creating a progress report on a cluster of harvesting and refining facilities that had been constructed to draw resources for the [Synthworld project](gp:RLMmAnr4gj) from Schwester's dense atmosphere. When she arrived, she discovered that the facilities were never actually built. After an investigation, Ellie Kanis, senior foreman of the project, was found guilty of skimming from the project fund. The fallout from the scandal and the vast amount of credits she and her co-conspirators stole resurrected public debate against the overall cost of the Synthworld project.","g":["schwester","chronos ii","chronos system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/62104aaf-2383-4a34-8842-8c815e9ed6d8"},
{"id":"scorpius","gp":"bEzDv21QwW","t":"Scorpius","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Scorpius is a heavy fighter manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) (RSI). Developed by the Applied Innovations division of RSI, it was evaluated by the 999th Test Squadron of the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) and was proven capable of matching multiple types of [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) ships. Each Scorpius is outfitted with an array of offensive and defensive weapons, including remote turrets and decoy launchers. Its convertible spaceframe can be configured into a compact form for landing.","g":["fighter","roberts space industries (rsi)","human spacecraft","scorpius series","heavy fighter"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b5b60c6e-000d-4b28-af76-534414c64090"},
{"id":"scorpius-antares","gp":"R6dwElmjaq","t":"Scorpius Antares","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Scorpius Antares is a heavy fighter manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) (RSI). A variant of the [Scorpius](gp:bEzDv21QwW), it has been redesigned to focus on the short-range disabling and boarding of enemy vessels. The turrets from the base model have been replaced with an EMP device that allows its pilot to scramble enemy systems, and a quantum dampener has been added to help to prevent combatants from escaping into quantum travel during battle.","g":["fighter","heavy fighter","roberts space industries (rsi)","human spacecraft","scorpius series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/27002589-b162-47e3-aace-d927aa739a53"},
{"id":"scott-childress","gp":"R5p68KXk5X","t":"Scott Childress","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Dr. Scott Childress (2032 - 2121) was the head engineer of the team of scientists at [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) that created the first [Human](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)-made [quantum drive](gp:RX3DOkJdxJ) in 2075. His doctoral thesis, *A new framework for the construction of high-speed spacecraft engines*, caught the attention of RSI founder Chris Roberts, who hired Childress soon after his graduation from the Fairchild Institute of Science and Technology in 2061. Allowing travel at 1/100th the speed of light, the RSI quantum core engine developed under the leadership of Dr. Childress ushered in a new age of space exploration within the Sol system and is generally credited as laying the groundwork for Humanity's expansion into the stars.","g":["quantum drive"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e2b140c0-4d8b-48c1-bc28-094fe42ca0d1"},
{"id":"scythe","gp":"0qakL3mmmq","t":"Scythe","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Vanduul"],"x":"The \"Scythe\" is the official [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) designation for a standard fighter operated by [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) forces. Having been encountered by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) for decades, they have become visually synonymous with the terror of Vanduul raids. Specialty spacecraft manufacturer [Esperia](gp:0OaBKL7wlv) produces a flyable replica of the Scythe, and is used as an aggressor in UEEN training units. Esperia has made an extremely limited number of Scythe replicas available to civilian hobbyists. Some pilots who capture Vanduul Scythes convert them for Human use, often with the aid of Esperia's resources.","g":["vanduul scythe","vanduul spacecraft","fighter","medium fighter","esperia"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7de8c799-f408-4a7e-bbb6-2d43f4e9aa60"},
{"id":"sekith-thusuung-iii","gp":"bo1wy7GZNr","t":"Se'kith (Th.us'ūng III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Se'kith (Th.us'ūng III) is a terrestrial planet in the [Th.us'ūng system](gp:V8WeExnJge), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9), and is the third world from its sun. Soon after its MXY III.802 (SEY 2483) discovery, the Xi'an government designated it as a testbed for new [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and geohacking technologies. These endeavors were abandoned in MXY III.838 (SEY 2530), when Human terraforming company Gaia Planet Services dispatched a survey team to the planet without oversight from the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) government. They were taken into custody by the military, where they were held captive until the UPE agreed to reveal the extent of their territory and the locations of all their systems. This was the first encounter between [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj), and historians credit tensions arising from this incident as one of the primary causes of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (MXY III.838 - III.1044 / SEY 2530 - 2793).","g":["eli price","th.us'uung iii","th.us'uung system","habitable planet","habitable","xi'an system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4c959980-6d5c-428e-9bf3-f92a55fbd0b3"},
{"id":"second-imperial-age","gp":"RAdjOk77n7","t":"Second Imperial Age","k":"history","c":["History","Xi'an"],"x":"The Second [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) Age, ruled by [House Xy.ō](gp:RXlXBrm5o1), was the shortest dynasty in [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) history, lasting over 1700 MXY. During this time, Xi'an explorers discovered multiple planetary systems and expanded the borders of the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). In MXY II.914 (SEY 291), they achieved first contact with the [Kr'thak](gp:RxNxDYkqzz) culture and attempted to establish a trade relationship. After several decades of strained relations, the [Spirit Wars](gp:0dQ4DYJ9W8) (II.961 - II.1735 / SEY 351 - 1342) erupted, ravaging the latter half of the Age. The entirety of House Xy.ō was killed in a bombing incursion by the Kr'thak in II.1706 (SEY 1305). This began [the Dark](gp:VyvYXnM2Pl)  (II.1706 - II.1824 / SEY 1305 - 1457), an era in which the Xi'an Empire had no official Imperial House. Xi'an historians group the Dark in with the Second Imperial Age, formally ending it at the ascension of [House Kr.ē](gp:R6v8OZOrP5) to the imperial throne in II.1824 (SEY 1457).","g":["house xy.ō","spirit wars","kr'thak","eras"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e5089f6e-9bc6-4fb8-b532-8ca58da282e9"},
{"id":"second-sister-kilian-ii","gp":"RPDDaX8AWg","t":"Second Sister (Kilian II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"The Second Sister (Kilian II) is a protoplanet in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Misshapen and low in mass, it is theorized that the Second Sister was trapped in the orbit of the [First Sister (Kilian I)](gp:VlMMagKEzd) as it was passing through the system. The [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) uses the Second Sister as a testing ground for weapons. Due to this, access to the Second Sister is restricted.","g":["second sister","kilian ii","kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet","three sisters"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/749983d3-58fd-4fa1-98ec-6c4fae20dbf3"},
{"id":"second-tevarin-war","gp":"bE3rPrz3Pv","t":"Second Tevarin War","k":"history","c":["History","Tevarin","Military"],"x":"The Second Tevarin War was an armed conflict between the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) and the [United Empire of Earth](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) that lasted from SEY 2603 to 2610. It began when Corath'Thal, a Tevarin warlord, launched a campaign to take back the Tevarin homeworld, [Jalan (Elysium IV)](gp:VarAXY2zy2), from the UEE. Lacking the numbers and resources of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM), the Tevarin waged a protracted, guerilla-based campaign over the next seven years. When it became clear to Corath'thal that the Tevarin were going to be defeated after the [Battle of Centauri](gp:VlM1yqjoNv), he and his remaining forces removed the thermal shielding from their ships and dove into the atmosphere of Jalan. Their self-immolation prompted the Tevarin to cast off the culture that had failed them and fully assimilate into the UEE under the rule of [Deacon Messer II](gp:0j46m4BYge).","g":["united empire of earth","warlord corath'thal","wars"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c9491c02-e28d-4f89-b019-1013ffc4e828"},
{"id":"sector-of-space","gp":"0QxY3YeJGj","t":"Sector (Space)","k":"place","c":["Space","Human","Xi'an"],"x":"A sector of space is a physical area of space within a [planetary system](gp:VaZwNWg372). Sectors are used to provide orientation to navigators and pilots in areas which would otherwise have no direction markers. To define a sector, cartographers typically lay a three dimensional grid over a planetary system and chart areas into equal sections. Once this is approved by the government, official sectors are declared and released to the public. Sizes of sectors will vary depending on a system. [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) governments both utilize sectors in mapping.","g":["navigation"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/67b09df5-f68e-4060-b8cc-aef70057746f"},
{"id":"sektor8","gp":"RwZBLBJvY6","t":"Sektor8","k":"people","c":["People"],"x":"Sektor8 is the pseudonym of a street artist who lives and works on Rytif (Bremen II), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE). They specialize in colorful, abstract pieces that they put up on public buildings over the course of a single evening. In 2948, the artist was contracted by [Accelerated Mass Design](gp:VaZwQNE48v) and [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34) to create a custom skin for their limited-edition [Mustang Omega](gp:0qnNXnDxQO) racing spacecraft.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ca8d98ef-01ff-49bc-b9a1-0b64e4df822c"},
{"id":"selene-vega-iii","gp":"0qaa69qqNA","t":"Selene (Vega III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Selene is a terrestrial planet in the Vega system, [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that was minimally [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) to [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) specifications. From 2550 to 2712, Selene was a center of industry, trade, tourism, and culture, serving as a key travel hub in the UEE. After the [Battle of Orion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) in 2712, Selene experienced a sharp drop in population as inhabitants of the system fled to other worlds in fear of an imminent [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) invasion. In 2737, after the dual losses of [Virgil](gp:box5moyeoZ) and [Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq), Vega became the closest UEE system to [Vanduul space](gp:RPDAMLKP74). While refugees from Virgil and Tiber filled in some of the gaps left by its fled populace, Selene's population numbers never reverted to pre-Vanduul levels. Today, many of Selene's buildings and construction projects are abandoned.","g":["selene","vega iii","vega system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5ddaadae-ccca-4227-9afd-caa93fe55701"},
{"id":"self-land","gp":"V7gM8M7Len","t":"SELF-LAND","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"SELF-LAND is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) spacecraft hangar manufacturer responsible for a series of modular berths produced under the same name. It was founded in the mid-29th century by Peter Weatherman, a tanker owner whose ship was stripped of components after he was jumped by a gang of thieves in an open hangar. As a result of this experience, Weatherman started his company to create a system of enclosed, private hangars that could be easily placed at any settlement and could rely on a unified supply chain for maintenance and support. The SELF-LAND hangars sold well, and have since become a common sight around the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["hangar manufacturer","peter weatherman","vann","croshaw iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/10d2bbf8-3422-4822-aab6-49829442804f"},
{"id":"senate","gp":"VaZn8OqaNZ","t":"Senate","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The Senate is a governing body responsible for writing, evaluating, amending, and passing or rejecting legislation, setting the governmental budget on a yearly basis, advising the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl). It is composed of elected representatives from each recognized planet within the borders of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Each planet is represented by a number of Senators determined by the planet's population or sphere of influence. A Senator serves for five years and can be elected an unlimited number of times. Formed in 2380, it is the oldest continuous branch of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) government.","g":["human government","united nations of earth","united planets of earth","united empire of earth"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f22ce93b-99ab-4c97-8579-267d2f506af1"},
{"id":"sentient-rights","gp":"ReJa7aaoYr","t":"Sentient Rights","k":"faction","c":["Culture","Government"],"x":"Sentient rights is a moral principle that states all sentient beings are entitled to basic rights and legal protections. These rights are understood as inherent and inalienable, and applicable to any species that reaches a threshold level of sentience regardless of its planet of origin or stage of development. This doctrine influenced the establishment of the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP), which serves to codify sentient rights within [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) law.","g":["fair chance act","uee legal definition"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c946a91f-28a9-44bc-8214-909db480e684"},
{"id":"sentient-trading","gp":"R6dBqreLen","t":"Sentient Trading","k":"faction","c":["Illegal Activity"],"x":"Sentient trading, also called slavery or sentient trafficking, refers to the practice of transporting, buying, and selling self-aware beings for the purpose of forced labor. Those who engage in the practice of sentient trading are commonly referred to as \"slavers.\" Illegal in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) and the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9), it is condemned by sentient rights organizations as a violation of personal autonomy. In the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3), sentient trading is referred to as indentured service and is governed by contracts with set beginning and end dates or set debt thresholds.","g":["slavers"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4e1531f6-514c-49eb-a1a2-6e4f1256d24e"},
{"id":"sentinel","gp":"VY4Wog4K8e","t":"Sentinel","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Vanguard Sentinel is a variant of the [Vanguard](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/vanguard) deep space fighter developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). An electronic warfare platform, it was created to be used in the suppression of enemy air defense and tracking capabilities. The remodel replaces some of the Vanguard's direct armament with an external electronic countermeasures pod, decoy missiles, and a set of electro-magnetic pulse (EMP) charges to be used in asymmetrical warfare operations. While it was designed to [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) specifications, Aegis has made the Vanguard Sentinel available for civilian and corporate users.","g":["vanguard","aegis dynamics","interdiction","military spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/393a41c1-7361-411d-9260-1b873daef35c"},
{"id":"serling-horus-i","gp":"Vy28DwK2a8","t":"Serling (Horus I)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Serling (Horus I) is the first planet from the sun of the [Horus system](gp:bo1JGZpvwZ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Tidally locked to its star, its day half is hot and cloudy and its dark half is icy and cold. A permanent wind system that exchanges air from each side keeps the climate from veering into life-threatening extremes and creates habitable conditions along the perpetually-twilit solar terminator. Further colonized by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) after the dissolution of the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) in 2793, it is a center of trade between the UEE and the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9), which is connected to the Horus system via two jump points.","g":["serling","horus i","horus system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bbfa1035-dfdb-4f9b-a35f-dc6cecd7c377"},
{"id":"severus-kiel-iii","gp":"V3GOdL9lYN","t":"Severus (Kiel III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Severus (Kiel III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Kiel system](gp:Var8kAJnaQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The sole populated planet in Kiel, Severus was historically used as a base of operations for the [UEE military](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/uee-military) during the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793). After the [fall of the Messers](gp:bE3rKa32P7), the military trickled out of the system, taking resources and jobs with them, and the planet's economy went into a recession. Beginning in the early 2900s, Governor Joona Tzur recruited businesses to the planet that could capitalize on the military's abandoned infrastructure. The program was a success, and after a period of rapid growth, Severus was recognized by the UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) in 2937. Severus is the central host planet for the [Intergalactic Aerospace Expo](gp:R4jpEgezde).","g":["kiel iii","severus","kiel system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c2dc475f-240c-4526-88b3-01aa3e3163db"},
{"id":"shepherd-tayac-iii","gp":"bZkkxB94eB","t":"Shepherd (Tayac III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Shepherd is a dwarf planet, third from the sun in the [Tayac system](gp:RAXX4N3w4B), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Composed of rock and ice, it has a deep red and white surface inhospitable to life. It was nicknamed \"Shepherd\" because it orbits so closely to the outer edge of the [Tayac belt](gp:RkGGQWPj7n) that it appears to be supervising the nearby asteroids in their path around the sun.","g":["shepherd","tayac iii","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","tayac system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/35a10407-0443-460d-9492-18fb7c24200d"},
{"id":"sherman","gp":"R4jxLALWgJ","t":"Sherman","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Sherman is a settlement on [Cascom (Castra II)](gp:0dXKkL9a9o), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Originally built as a military landing base, it was constructed above the cloud line on a mountain to make it easier for atmospheric ships to launch or land. It was changed into a civilian town at the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793), and is now a center for trade thanks to its port.","g":["cascom","castra ii","towns","uee towns"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1c4afa2a-9c0f-41b9-bbb1-ca9a11c09c1f"},
{"id":"shipping-checkpoint","gp":"R6v8nqQMJD","t":"Shipping Checkpoint","k":"faction","c":["Government"],"x":"A shipping checkpoint is a government-run agency in which the cargo manifests of spacecraft are examined to make sure they are in compliance of the law. They are typically located in platforms near [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) that cross into sovereign systems, with a checkpoint on either side. The [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) and the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) require by law for all spacecraft to stop at these checkpoints when crossing from one territory to another. The [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) only enforces stoppage if the local system requires it.","g":["uee government","xi'an government","banu sociopolitics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/54af146d-eced-4eed-9e97-8ac6113789dc"},
{"id":"shoel","gp":"RL6dPrzK6r","t":"Shoel","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Shoel is one of the only settlements on [Hyperion (Fora III)](gp:RegWGPlxqy), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Briefly prosperous during a mining rush in the twenty-fifth century, the city fell into disrepair after mineral veins ran dry and the inhabitants abandoned it. Most of the urban sprawl is dominated by empty buildings being swallowed by [HyperClay](gp:RkZ9W2BkDz). Shoel was used as a hideout during the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792) for political refugees. One of the only remaining statues of [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q), erected under orders from [Corsen Messer V](gp:0OaB8O6awO) in 2660 to remind the populace of their subjugation, stands at the town center. It is heavily vandalized and defaced.","g":["hyperion","fora iii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/627753ed-4a3d-4137-a314-36231e445ab1"},
{"id":"showdown","gp":"RwZBw4Lrxz","t":"Showdown!","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Politics","Human"],"x":"*Showdown!* is an [SSN/CAtv](gp:0QxYwPK88l) current events debate program that first began airing in SEY 2521. In each episode, two guests of opposing views are brought on to debate key issues of the day. *Showdown!* has been canceled and revived multiple times. The most recent version has continuously broadcast since 2799 and is hosted by [Eria Quint](gp:V7gMqNgeOa). \n# CURRENT FORMAT\nThe host of *Showdown!* opens every episode with a summary of the debate topic at hand, usually a current events news story. The host then introduces guests of opposing viewpoints to present their takes on the issue and debate it with one another. Generally, two guests are present, but sometimes the host will conduct a one-on-one interview or allow three or more guests to debate with one another. As the debate progresses, the host serves as moderator, asking questions as needed. Between one and five topics are covered per episode. \n# HISTORY\nThe concept for *Showdown!* began in 2511, on [Angeli (Croshaw II)](gp:0QlxqwG14Q). Local politicians in Quinton would join radio news anchor [Upasna Dixit](gp:0Gx2n4G7na) to debate upcoming legislation. After nine years on the air, Dixit was approached by the now defunct news network [Angeli On Air (AoA)](gp:0dQ4n4oJ1m) to adapt *Showdown!* as a 30-minute current events debate program. Dixit signed for an undisclosed amount and began production on the new show. The first episode aired throughout Croshaw on 9 September 2521 in a late-night time slot.\n\n*Showdown!* soon became popular and was shuffled to a more popular time slot. It saw high enough ratings that in 2522, SSN/CAtv bought the rights from AoA and broadcast it for the first time to an interplanetary audience that same year. In 2523, they launched a special series of episodes where various political experts, authors, and laypeople debated the merits and drawbacks of the new [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) government without Dixit's moderation. However, the lack of an arbiter caused conversations to go off track, leading to a drop in the show's ratings. Ratings rose again when Dixit returned in 2524.   \n\nDuring Dixit's run as host, *Showdown!* covered such issues as [first contact with the Xi'an](gp:R4ZQpYEEvx) (2530), The outbreak of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2542 - 2546), and the ascension of [Ivar Messer](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) to the newly created office of [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr) (2546). Dixit chose to retire after Ivar Messer created the position of [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl), stating that she preferred not to lead debates on pros and cons of fascism. \n\nThe new host, [Inácio Santos Melo](gp:0qnNMa3Mgq), developed a confrontational moderation style in contrast to Dixit's cool and impartial one, often aligning himself against his guests in heated three-way debates. Melo was criticized by other news networks for this behavior, but *Showdown!* experienced an upswing in popularity. This tone became the program's norm even after Melo's retirement in 2588. \n\n*Showdown!* has been canceled and rebooted multiple times. It ran uninterrupted from 2547 to 2619. On 09 May 2619, *Showdown!* was canceled due to a dip in ratings. It was revived from 2648 to 2662, canceled again due to a contract dispute, and then brought back to fill an empty late-night slot from 2687 to 2697. It was one of many news programs to be censored into cancellation during the power struggle between [Astrid Messer VII](gp:0KnA1D5nQM) and [Samuel Messer VIII](gp:RkZ9W2L2NB) (2697 - 2701), and wasn't revived again until 2718, three years after the ascension of [Galor Messer IX](gp:VyvYAGKxAz). This version of *Showdown!* lasted until 2789, when it was censored again by the Messer government, this time for inviting [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ)[Terrence Akari](gp:RL6ZQLwnko) of [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) as a guest. It was revived for the fifth time in 2799 in the run-up to the ratification of the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP). \n\nSince 2799, *Showdown!* has been shuffled between time slots, but has not seen another cancellation. The current host, Eria Quint, took over in 2935.","g":["ssn/catv","angeli on air","debate show","spectrum show"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fced6a57-516d-4a36-9e76-228a5c9bcff4"},
{"id":"shubin-interstellar","gp":"V7gM8ZBodA","t":"Shubin Interstellar","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Shubin Interstellar is a major corporation headquartered on [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Founded as an investment group, it acquired the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) conglomerate [Worldmaker](gp:VlMxQMw23Y) in the late 25th century SEY, and [Fulcrum Mining Associates](gp:0OaB8LgXlZ) in the mid-26th. It sells mining equipment and operates mining facilities, factories, support pipelines, and other industrial centers in nearly every UEE-held planetary system. Their current CEO is Gavin Arlington. \n\n# HISTORY\nShubin Interstellar was founded in SEY 2410 by a group of investors led by Martha Shubin, whose company, Alanko Northal Consolidated Construction, had greatly profited during the terraforming boom that marked the first decades of the Human Colonial Expansion Era. Seeking to further capitalize on the settlement of new worlds, Shubin Interstellar operated by providing capital and other credit lines to a variety of terraforming concerns and was able to see massive returns on the group's investments. By 2480, Shubin Interstellar had acquired a controlling interest in Worldmaker, then the third largest terraforming conglomerate in the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE), and took on the terraforming process themselves.\n\nAs Shubin Interstellar acquired more contracts, they found themselves with a quickly increasing overhead cost. Once the terraformation process was complete, the equipment they built up in a system had to be sold, often at a considerable loss. In 2554, Fulcrum Mining Associates, a growing mining concern, reached out to Shubin Interstellar to purchase standing corporate assets in the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5) as a part of a development project there. Shubin Interstellar instead purchased Fulcrum outright, beginning a three-decade effort to retrofit their terraforming efforts to a mining focus. The company split into two divisions: one that specialized in planetary engineering, and the other in mining. By the 27th century, mining made up 60% of Shubin Interstellar's net worth.\n\n# PRESENT DAY\nWhile Shubin Interstellar continues to invest in terraforming projects, mining remains their primary focus, and Shubin mining stations can be found around the galaxy. The company makes an effort to keep all of the mining process in-house, and manufactures its own mining stations, mining equipment, and crew training facilities, and has even begun to oversee agricultural efforts to supply their workers with food. While Shubin Interstellar works to re-use their equipment and facilities whenever possible to cut costs, it is not uncommon for larger bases to be abandoned when they can not be moved. \n\nShubin Interstellar's current CEO is Gavin Arlington. Under his leadership, corporate headquarters have been relocated to [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1), and the company has transitioned from hiring permanent workers to employing external contractors.","g":["microtech (planet)","stanton iv","mining company","terraforming company","mining equipment manufacturer","commercial and industrial goods manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9e53e102-53a7-4b23-9241-83b5315c52b7"},
{"id":"siege-of-tiber","gp":"0OaBY5pGrq","t":"Siege of Tiber","k":"history","c":["History","Vanduul","Military"],"x":"# SIEGE OF TIBER \nThe Siege of Tiber was a key battle between the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and invading [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO). Lasting from SEY 2732 to 2736, it consisted of extensive ground and air engagements, mass bombings, and a military blockade from the Orion and [Vector (VS-1)](gp:VgEE5KQeWY) [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) by Vanduul forces and the Virgil and Oberon jump points by UEE forces. Losses were heavy on both sides; conservative estimates put [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and Vanduul combined casualties in the lower millions. The Siege ended with UEE defeat on 29 December 2736, when a [Kingship](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm) jumped into the [system](gp:VaZwNWg372) from Orion. Half of the UEE's forces in Tiber were destroyed in the subsequent battle. After such heavy losses, the UEE was forced to cede Tiber to the Vanduul.  \n\n# BACKGROUND\n\nOn 18 February 2712 Tiber's neighboring system, Orion, was unexpectedly [lost to the Vanduul](gp:RMXyYxqw8K). UEE forces that had defended Orion fell back to the Tiber system and formed a secondary defense line in anticipation of another invasion. However, the Vanduul remained in Orion to harvest its resources, and showed no intention of pursuing the retreating UEE ships. After several tense months, UEE leadership concluded that another unified incursion of allied [Vanduul Clans](gp:R9vzjxmEBx) at the scale of the Battle of Orion was unlikely to occur. The Imperator authorized the buildup of military forces at an accelerated pace to fortify the system. \n\nRegular intelligence-gathering missions were launched into Orion to spy on the Vanduul. The system didn't have a single incident until 04 February 2726, when a solitary Vanduul [Blade](gp:RegdeBENkw) exited the Orion jump point. By 16 November 2726, Vanduul Clans were regularly launching raids on Tiber. It seemed that another invasion might be on the horizon. \n\n# THE SIEGE\n\nOn 19 April 2732, a large Clan took and held the Tiber-Orion jump point. The UEE responded by dispatching the 81st, 22nd, 6th, and 31st Battle Groups, commanded by Grand Admiral Tesca Halimeade, to eradicate the invaders. Key ships in the Battle Groups were sent to guard the Virgil and Oberon jump points and defend other areas identified as potentially threatened. In a surprise move, Halimeade issued orders that no ship was to directly engage the Vanduul around the Orion jump point, hoping that a defensive position would stall the invasion and give him enough time to find a diplomatic solution to the conflict.\n\nBy mid-2733, multiple Clans drawn into Tiber by the continued fighting were battling one another over space stations and outposts as often as they clashed with UEE forces. Most of the UEE's capital ships remained in dock during this time as Halimeade searched for a way to communicate with the Vanduul. By early 2734, three of the Clans that had emerged victorious from repeated battles against the other Clans launched separate concentrated assaults on Tiber II. They tore through the UEE's lines of defense, dropped [Harvesters](gp:0n1MYzOkG7), and established encampments across the planet. \n\nWith the loss of the Tiber II, Halimeade was forced to abandon his strategy and go on the offensive. The main flagship of the 31st long docked at [INS Aniene](gp:VlNPQMPnrA), the UEES *Aquilon*, led the fleet to the outskirts of Tiber II in order to lure the Vanduul camped there into attacking. The strategy paid off; most Vanduul on the planet eagerly joined the fray, leaving their on-ground encampments only lightly guarded. As the battle continued, strike teams from the 81st and 22nd Battle Groups entered Tiber II's atmosphere with little resistance and conducted aerial bombardments of the Vanduul strongholds there, destroying the majority in under a few hours. The decimated Clans fled the system. \n\nFinally committed to total war, Halimeade used this bait-and-switch tactic again and again to reclaim lost territory. For over a year, Vanduul numbers slowly dwindled. However, due to more Clans entering Tiber as often as defeated Clans fled it, progress was not going as fast as UEE authorities would have liked. \n\nOn 04 November 2735, a large Clan appeared in what seemed to be an insignificant part of the system. The UEES *Aquilon* and a selection of support vessels, personally led by Halimeade, went to investigate the situation. As they approached, hundreds of Vanduul poured through a previously-unknown jump point from the Vanduul system designated Vector, ambushing Halimede. The *Aquilon* was destroyed. All aboard were lost. \n\nAdmiral Mira Triolo assumed authority over the four Battle Groups in Tiber after Halimeade's death, and her aggressive strategy of confronting the Vanduul head-on resulted in a sharp increase in casualties. Under her command, the UEE made multiple attempts over the next year to expel the Vanduul, but no attack was successful; Clans continued to enter Tiber from the Orion and Vector systems, and the Harvesters at work on Tiber II kept supply levels high. UEE ground troops and bombers would succeed in destroying one Harvester only for two more to be dropped in its place. Morale was low. It seemed that as long as the Vanduul held Tiber II, it would be impossible to retake the system. \n\nOn 07 September 2736, Imperator [Galor Messer IX](gp:VyvYAGKxAz) ordered the military to bomb the planet into oblivion. The bombing, conducted by the 6th Battle Group on 15 November, annihilated all Vanduul encampments on Tiber II, and the planet itself was rendered to ruin. Emboldened by this success, UEE forces routed Vanduul encampments from the asteroid belt, chasing them through the Vector jump point. By 29 November, the UEE held Tiber II, the belt, and the Vector jump point. The only Vanduul left in the system set up a defensive perimeter around the jump point to Orion. Unless they retreated, their supplies would eventually run out. The 22nd and 31st returned to [MacArthur](gp:bBp6BmDMGJ) for much-needed repairs, while the 81st and 6th remained behind to pick off the rest of the Vanduul. It seemed that the UEE was finally on the brink of victory. \n\nOn 29 December 2736, a Kingship, a powerful class of Vanduul capital ship that had not been encountered by Humans since the Battle of Orion in 2712, entered Tiber through the Orion jump point. The combined power of the Kingship and the enormous Clan that accompanied it overwhelmed the 81st; three-quarters of its ships were wiped out in a 13 hour period, and INS Aniene was destroyed. The remainder of the Battle Group fell back to the [INS Flavus](gp:RkZ9WG9L7n) before receiving order to retreat into Virgil. Admiral Triolo and the 6th stayed behind to hold the line against the Kingship. Reports from survivors indicate that the 6th was able to deal modest damage to the Kingship before losing Triolo, all its capital ships, and the majority of its carriers. As the last of the 6th Battle Group retreated into Oberon, having been cut off from Virgil, Tiber was fully surrendered to the Vanduul.\n\n# AFTERMATH\n\nThe UEE had poured all its resources into holding Tiber. When the Vanduul [launched an attack](gp:box5moyeoZ) on the Virgil system immediately after Tiber's loss, the UEEN was unable to mount a sufficient defense to stop them. The beaten remains of the 81st Battle Group fought off the Vanduul fleet while Squadron 214 aided the civilians evacuating from Virgil I, conducting multiple runs back and forth from Virgil through the Vega jump point. Given the choice between performing a final run and remaining safe, the 214th chose to go into Virgil one last time. Thanks to their actions, over a million civilians escaped from Virgil I. \n\nThere was every expectation that Vega would be the Vanduul's next target. Instead, the Vanduul would not launch another massed attack on UEE territory until the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) in 2884. \n\nToday, Tiber remains a Vanduul stronghold. Harvesters continue to chew through the system's resources, strengthening any Clan that passes through the area. Because Tiber is connected to both Oberon and Virgil, it provides the Vanduul with easy raiding access to UEE territory. Oberon and Vega are frequent raiding targets. The UEE conducts periodic bombing runs to Tiber, targeting Vanduul encampments and Harvesters on Tiber II along with bases in the asteroid belt, but has been unable so far to reclaim the system.","g":["battles","vanduul clans","united empire of earth","tiber system","vanduul invasions"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d3e8a511-6b18-43fb-9ea8-96369003fde7"},
{"id":"silas-koerner","gp":"V8gJMXjE8o","t":"Silas Koerner","k":"people","c":["People"],"x":"Silas Koerner (2899-present) is the founder, sole owner, lead designer, and CEO of [Consolidated Outland](gp:0KnAYqez34). Born on Rytif (Bremen II), Koerner was the only heir to his family's fortune. He invested his family money in a wide range of areas, including fish farming, mining, remote charting, and electronics before founding the spacecraft company Consolidated Outland.","g":["consolidated outland"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1d2b8d94-8371-456b-bb4b-8c557a4db91b"},
{"id":"silent-song","gp":"VaZwNW43ym","t":"Silent Song","k":"culture","c":["Art"],"x":"*Silent Song* is a piece of interactive artwork located in the Tayac system asteroid belt, between Tayac II and Shepherd (Tayac III). The work was commissioned in honor of the Ark's centennial and to highlight xeno-relationships. It was created in collaboration by Human artist Yosef Colt, Xi'an artist Nyalā Ao'ro, and a Banu fabrication Souli. Beginning in 2890, the artists and fabricators spent a decade living together while developing the installation. *Silent Song* was designed to be visited and appreciated via spacecraft.","g":["nyalā ao'ro","yosef colt","tayac system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/750a5b99-6f24-4a83-87e8-3e4cc3365765"},
{"id":"sindo-guerrero","gp":"01LNooPKYr","t":"Sindo Guerrero","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Music"],"x":"Sindo Guerrero (SEY 2902 - present) is a flamenco and psychedelic fusion musician most notable for his song \"Sun Kissed.\" As a child he was uninterested in music, but became curious about it in his late teens when his friends needed a singer for their band. He spent the next five years immersed in performing with them and learning the guitar and keyboards. When his parents relocated to the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), he took this as an opportunity to launch a solo act, and was soon making headlines for his unique sound and magnetic stage presence. His first hit, \"Outsider Again, I...\" made it into the top ten of the New United music chart and secured him a lucrative recording contract. After the release of his second album, he and his family took a trip to the [T.āl system ](gp:R4j2mdjZE5)in 2929, where the sight of the yellow-tinted architecture on [Oil'xa (T.āl II)](gp:0rx4XojAed) inspired him to write what would become his record-breaking number one hit \"Sun Kissed.\" In 2937, after nearly two years of continuous touring and the end of his ten year contract, Guerrero retired, stating that he'd made enough credits to last a lifetime. He is known to collaborate with other musicians, but has not toured since his retirement.","g":["human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8f22d89b-5145-494f-9c5f-92356b80cad8"},
{"id":"sino-virgil-ii","gp":"RPDQP1Zjqg","t":"Sino (Virgil II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Virgil II, nicknamed Sino, is the second planet from the sun of the [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). A world blanketed with thick and impenetrable smog, little is known about its surface. The majority of probes that were sent there before the [Fall of Virgil](gp:box5moyeoZ) only lasted minutes before they were crushed by atmospheric pressure. Military intelligence reports have noted that even the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) seem to give it a wide berth.","g":["sino","virgil ii","virgil system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7696e6eb-6dc8-458e-a03c-2866ed0b16f2"},
{"id":"sky-palm","gp":"VlMjw2rEd4","t":"Sky Palm","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The Sky Palm is a genetically modified plant that was created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke) to grow on worlds with thick, occlusive atmospheres. With long, thin trunks crowned with clusters of evergreen leaves that resemble large feathers, the sky palm's cell structures were tweaked to absorb a wider spectrum of light than the plants from which it was derived. It can also absorb a great deal of carbon dioxide, and is capable of surviving at high elevations.","g":["rayari inc","trees"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/72b7caf0-3d05-4df2-affd-af264bf6e091"},
{"id":"slam","gp":"VY4Wg2rD24","t":"SLAM","k":"culture","c":["Illegal Activity","Science and Technology"],"x":"SLAM (silicate adrenomethosterone), also known as redline, bounce, or berserker, is Class A narcotic and steroid and stimulant with analgesic effects. Most commonly available as an inhalant, it was originally only available in liquid form and was taken via intravenous injection. Derived from adrenomethosterone, a medical-grade steroid used to treat severe autoimmune conditions, it gained popularity as a performance-enhancing drug for athletes. The crystalline version that forms the basis of the inhalant emerged as a faster, cheaper method to make the drug. Effects of the drug include inducing hyper-aggression and a temporary burst of strength and endurance in its users while dulling their sense of pain. Long-term use can lead to sudden heart failure. Prolonged use of the drug over years is known to cause involuntary tremors in the body.","g":["redline","bounce","berserker","controlled substance","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ba072e63-ba14-4bf7-82ef-824130af46b8"},
{"id":"sloma","gp":"boxDDjWYJ7","t":"Sloma","k":"culture","c":["Banu","Food and Beverages","Culture"],"x":"# Sloma\nSloma is a beverage often consumed by the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) before they begin the negotiation process for new business deals, or during various social gatherings. Sloma is made up of a base liquid that is then altered by the addition of disparate ingredients brought to the table by everyone involved in the given social situation. After the concoction brews for a few moments, the resulting beverage is called sloma.\n\n# Known History\nSince they were initially encountered, Banu have usually opened negotiations, be they political, business-related, or otherwise, with the creation and consumption of sloma. The first [Banu-Human Interstellar Peace and Trade Accord](gp:RzPoJ1aP4z) was hashed out over sloma created from ingredients contributed by General Neal Socolovich and a Protectorate Trade [Essosouli](gp:R6v8kxEPBD), among others. Because Banu do not keep historical records, there is no definitive evidence that points to the origin of the practice. The Essosouli present at the first Peace and Trade Accord, when asked about sloma, simply replied that it was how things were done. Human and Xi'an xenoanthropologists believe that the practice likely began before either civilization encountered the Banu.\n\n# Details of the Practice\nBefore negotiations begin, either a Banu who is hosting or a Banu who has previously agreed to host will provide the slomaddon, a usually ornately decorated vessel in which sloma is prepared. It will be partially filled with one of a variety of carrier liquids. Once the slomaddon has been opened, each participant of the deal or meeting will add something to it. Spice is one of the more popular additives, as it is light, easy to carry, and can significantly alter the sloma's flavor. However, anything that is safe to eat or drink is acceptable. This can create unique flavors. Banu can safely consume food that is dangerous for Humans, Xi'an, and Tevarin, so it is a good idea to request that everyone bring ingredients that are respectful of their various dietary limitations. After the sloma has macerated for a few minutes, the host will provide cups, into which they will serve the resulting drink. Everyone is expected to partake.\n\nMethods by which Banu create and consume sloma can vary: some may serve it hot, some may serve it cold, some may ask you to bring a carrier liquid and vessel, some may insist upon drinking directly from the slomaddon, some may not use liquid at all and instead offer to share food. As with the original version, participants are still expected to add something to the dish. While food isn't technically sloma, it fulfills the same purpose.\n\nConsensus among Banu is that sloma is used to ensure all involved in a contract are entering into it without ill intent. Because everyone, from low-ranking assistants to the most powerful Essosouli, must drink the sloma from the same vessel, so no one can slip poison to anyone else. Especially careful Banu may insist upon randomly mixing cups, in case someone has laced one or more of them with poison instead of the sloma. Some Banu believe that the flavor of the sloma can positively or negatively portend how negotiations will go. Other Banu attach no importance to the flavor whatsoever.","g":["slomaddon","banu cuisine","banu sociopolitics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e2960a6e-5e24-4403-a6ab-0af238840ea8"},
{"id":"sol-system","gp":"Rz2zy6DGB5","t":"Sol System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Sol system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) that consists of a G-type main sequence star, one mesoplanet, three terrestrial planets, two gas giants, two ice giants, a dwarf planet, an asteroid belt, and many other celestial bodies. The original home system of [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), it is the center of the UEE's government and is where the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) and the chambers of the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) are located. Two of its planets are fully colonized, alongside multiple moons. The third planet from its sun, [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) is both the Human homeworld and the current capital of the UEE.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ee2f1912-5071-494e-80ba-e13fbb7bd793"},
{"id":"something-every-tuesday","gp":"V3GJNlQakW","t":"Something Every Tuesday","k":"culture","c":["People","Human"],"x":"*Something Every Tuesday* is a weekly entertainment talk show hosted by comedian Esen Landari. Each episode opens with a monologue that comments on current events, and then segues into interviews with a series of celebrity guests. Landari has used the program to invite little-known musical acts, comic performers, and authors to allow them to showcase their work. It first aired in 2934 in the Tuesday late-evening programming slot and was moved to an earlier time in 2935 after Landari's easy rapport with guests and a few surprise-hit sketches helped it earn high ratings.","g":["talk show","spectrum show","esen landari"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d66e613e-996a-4731-8934-a68da56dd33e"},
{"id":"souli","gp":"RAdjm4mron","t":"Souli","k":"culture","c":["Banu","Culture"],"x":"A Souli is a group of cohabiting [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) who have formed an alliance centered around a specific, shared skill set. Akin to a combination of a family and a corporation, members of a Souli have been raised by the group since they were young. There is a Souli to cover every aspect of life, including medicine, item manufacturing, repair, writing, politics, religion, bureaucracy, trade, and so forth. The Souli is the single most important group in the life of a Banu.","g":["banu sociopolitics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/89f8e5af-6e07-4f45-9cc8-8f1f8e9f101f"},
{"id":"spacecraft-races-of-yulin","gp":"VJOzN6XwY4","t":"Spacecraft Races of Yulin","k":"culture","c":["Sports","Banu"],"x":"The Yulin system is home to many spacecraft races (Banu: **eponatae fodai**) run by the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4)[Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron) that make their homes there. Yulin IV is the Banu's preferred racetrack, as the myriad natural formations create the most exciting and dangerous routes. Crashes are not uncommon. Betting is encouraged, and some fortunes have been made or broken on the outcome of these races.","g":["spacecraft racing","yulin system","yulin iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/229a80eb-6d52-4926-86cf-d7f2b8531bff"},
{"id":"spacecraft-racing","gp":"RWwZWKw1y6","t":"Spacecraft Racing","k":"culture","c":["Sports"],"x":"Spacecraft racing is the competitive sport of racing two or more spacecraft. Spacecraft racing can take many forms, ranging from informal drag races between two pilots to highly organized, multi-part racing challenge events. A variety of racing leagues exist for the broadcasting and promotion of spacecraft racing. Some spacecraft manufacturers design bespoke racing spacecraft or variants of existing spacecraft to participate in racing challenges. Major racing events include the [Murray Cup](gp:bE3r71yZ87) in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ) and the [Able Baker Challenge](gp:RPP4LXMeBZ) in the [Baker system](gp:Rz2KGkv13N).","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/010ff691-b9d8-4a0f-a2b8-10fc3dd33a47"},
{"id":"spar-van-miles","gp":"0dXW3YrvjZ","t":"Spar Van Miles","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Spar Van Miles is a clothing brand that incorporates elements of casualwear into its business attire designs. Intended for both office and everyday use, garments from this company are inspired by contemporary trends in youth culture, and feature offbeat flourishes. Once per Standard Earth Year, the company holds a best-dressed contest in its headquarters on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) and awards the winner with a new ensemble from its latest collection.","g":["clothing manufacturer","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9816b441-e060-4d1e-a23b-d6276acbdde5"},
{"id":"spartan","gp":"0QlyWlqqyJ","t":"Spartan","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Spartan is an armored personnel carrier manufactured by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military, designed safely to transport people through combat zones and other dangerous areas. Built with the same Atlas Platform chassis as Anvil's [Ballista](gp:V8gJyXMDrM), the Spartan replaces the missile turret with a crew hold that accommodates eight secure jump seats, along with personal weapons storage. The top of the Spartan is equipped with a remotely-operated turret.","g":["anvil aerospace","human spacecraft","tank","transport","passenger transport","atlas platform"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/41b9c85a-6fb2-4d76-9e5c-4f8a9b2955d3"},
{"id":"spearfish","gp":"02BQOg37gY","t":"Spearfish","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Spearfish is a [weapon manufacturer](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/weapons-manufacturer) known for their line of electromagnetic pulse weaponry (EMP). The team at Spearfish are responsible for adapting the technology to a variety of platforms, including straight pulse generators, ship-mounted guns, and projectiles. Spearfish also produces the Arrestor missile series, combining infrared sensors with advanced processing software to deliver single-use EMP pulse devices to specifically targeted spacecraft.","g":["weapons manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c0497fc9-cc37-443d-a4f4-ad27cebb7eec"},
{"id":"spectrum","gp":"VaZwen9E2Q","t":"Spectrum","k":"company","c":["Entertainment","Science and Technology","Commerce","Human"],"x":"Spectrum is an interstellar media-services provider that connects all aspects of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) civilization, and is widely accessible around the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) through a network of communications arrays. It allows both direct communication between individuals and the broadcast of all types of material, including but not limited to news, sports, vids, and traditional linear programming.","g":["media-services provider"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fac75740-7b8c-4aad-a8c5-ceb2a10e95a7"},
{"id":"spectrum-spectator","gp":"RkZ9r7BlgQ","t":"Spectrum Spectator","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*Spectrum Spectator* is a weekly [Human](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) talk show that provides reviews and commentary on vids and general pop culture. The program is hosted by Lars Gonall and Daisy Wences and is known for its casual and uninhibited commentary. In addition to news and reviews, *Spectrum Spectator* often engages in speculation about serial programs and invites the viewer to guess at upcoming storylines.","g":["spectrum show","talk show"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/beeef032-a16b-492b-a195-e2a3dd9395a7"},
{"id":"spider","gp":"VaZwengjJv","t":"Spider","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Spider is a habitable space station in the unclaimed [Cathcart system](gp:RL6524vWO3). The station was fabricated by squatters from a half-finished platform and hundreds of abandoned spacecraft hulls that were dumped in the system. Despite its reputation for lawlessness, the station's location among a dense nest of garbage protects it from a large military or police force. Over the centuries, several major outlaw groups have utilized it as their base of operations. It is also home to an extensive black market. The name originates from the station's unusual shape; the various attached spacecraft resemble the web of a spider.","g":["space station","independent space station","independent settlement"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3dd2c651-66df-4403-819c-508c9e37691c"},
{"id":"spirit-wars","gp":"0dQ4DYJ9W8","t":"Spirit Wars","k":"history","c":["Xi'an","History","Military"],"x":"The Spirit Wars were an interconnected series of massed conflicts between the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) and the [Kr'thak](gp:RxNxDYkqzz), spanning multiple centuries (II.961 - II.1735; SEY 351 - 1342 ). These wars had a profound effect on Xi'an society; during a Kr'thak incursion in II.1706 (SEY 1305), [Emperor](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) Iith se Xy.ō and all in [her House](gp:RXlXBrm5o1) were exterminated. The Second Imperial age came to an abrupt end and [a century of anarchy](gp:VyvYXnM2Pl) rose in its place.","g":["kr'thak","xi'an empire","second imperial age","wars"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/066acf50-c361-4395-a0f7-d7ccadae18e4"},
{"id":"squadron-118","gp":"V3GP3rrD4j","t":"Squadron 118","k":"faction","c":["Military","Human"],"x":"The 118th Fighter Squadron (Squadron 118, the \"Hare Triggers\")  is an active [United Empire of Earth](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) unit. Currently assigned to the 5th Fleet, 87th Battle Group, the unit was first formed in the midst of the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) in SEY 2609. During the war, the 118th earned its nickname due to its reputation for consistently landing the first hit on enemy combatants during ship to ship engagements. It was a part of the 6th Fleet until it was transitioned into the 5th in 2917.","g":["ueen squadron"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/333bd9aa-7ec1-49f7-9d3b-c7c98a990afb"},
{"id":"squadron-214","gp":"RXlXOK7XW8","t":"Squadron 214","k":"faction","c":["Military","Human"],"x":"The 214th Multi-level Force Applicator Squadron (Squadron 214, \"the Black Crows\") is a carrier-based unit of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Navy (UEEN). Squadron 214 was activated in 2675, and has served in multiple conflicts, but it is best known for its role in the [Siege of Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq) and a dangerous bombing run into the Virgil system in 2932. Because of this, the squadron is most commonly associated with [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) [Gladiators](gp:RWwZQYNy4a), but has been composed of multiple types of spacecraft including [Hornet](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) fighters and [Gladius](gp:0j46NP5eB3) interceptors over the years.","g":["ueen squadron","black crows"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/293765c8-6229-4a8b-be52-d2c7faadb118"},
{"id":"squadron-42","gp":"RWoeByvQap","t":"Squadron 42","k":"faction","c":["Military","Human"],"x":"The 42nd Special Fighter Squadron (Squadron 42) is an active unit of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). Currently assigned to the 2nd Fleet, 65th Battle Group, Squadron 42 is most often deployed for missions that require a high level of skill. Originally established as a disciplinary unit for soldiers who failed to follow orders, it came to fame in SEY 2610 during the [Battle of Centauri](gp:VlM1yqjoNv) at the end of the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv). Their newly assigned commander Captain Alexandra Dunlevy noted the individual talents of the pilots during missions and began to give them leeway to make their own calls. This strategy led to a series of successes that eventually put the 42nd in the path of Warlord [Corath'Thal](gp:RkGxWGQ2Qp). Under their own direction, the 42nd ambushed the fleet as it was funneling through a jump point to the [Elysium system](gp:RvlQrKZxPO) and disabled their shields, thus opening the way for the UEE Navy's carrier ships to move in and decimate the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) armada. This brought an end to the long war and marked the beginning of the 42nd's history of prestige.","g":["battle of centauri","ueen squadron"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/65f7eec8-4c4c-4e52-a87c-b640e1b0e5db"},
{"id":"squadron-89","gp":"0Gz5BNmPqo","t":"Squadron 89 (The Lost Squad)","k":"faction","c":["Military","Human"],"x":"The 89th Logistic Support Squadron (Squadron 89, \"the Lost Squad\") is an inactive [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Navy (UEEN) unit. Founded in SEY 2608, the squadron served as a logistics and operations support squadron to various units, bases, and capital ships until its final posting to the Caliban system in 2792. The 89th became publicly revered due to their defense of the Caliban system against a massed Vanduul invasion for two days without reinforcements, allowing millions of civilians to escape ([Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE), 2884). A single unnamed pilot survived the prolonged assault. All others were killed in action. In honor of their sacrifice, the UEE Navy officially retired the 89th in 2885. Their motto was \"Stand and Deliver.\"","g":["squadron 89","lost squad","fall of caliban","ueen squadron"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/83a0b6d7-1216-4129-8077-5e1653a0c05d"},
{"id":"ssncatv","gp":"0QxYwPK88l","t":"SSN/CAtv","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Commerce"],"x":"# SSN/CATV\n\nSSN/CAtv is a spectrum network that provides news, political analysis, commentary programs, news magazines, and talk shows. It was founded in SEY 2458 as a result of a merger between former news channels Sheridan Special News Television (SSNtv) and Communications Alliance (CA). It was the first news network to broadcast to all [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) planetary systems. While it currently has hundreds of affiliates and satellite offices, it primarily broadcasts out of [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa).\n\n# HISTORY\n\nSSNtv was the first network originating from Earth (Sol III) to broadcast to Mars (Sol IV) and was the dominant news network among Humans until the discovery of the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp) in 2271. As Human territory expanded to other planetary systems, SSNtv's reach narrowed due to limitations in communication technology. Content delivery delays of several days to several weeks were common between systems. Rival network CA was established on [Reisse (Rhetor III)](gp:0QljXw43Ev) in 2398 to combat this gap. Thanks to the Rhetor system's cutting-edge communications network, CA's reach expanded more quickly than SSNtv's, and the network began to struggle. In 2458, SSNtv accepted a merger proposal from CA and SSN/CAtv was born.\n\nSSN/CAtv initially transmitted a continuous stream of news, hosted by a rotating cast of anchors. It gradually increased its focus on politics, purchasing [Showdown!](gp:RwZBw4Lrxz) in 2522 as its keystone debate program. This shift in content brought high profits with it, enabling the network to open a new headquarters on [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5) in 2525. In 2529, SSN/CAtv provided on-the-ground coverage of the [Unified Currency Riot](gp:0QlvpyjLvJ) in [Jata](gp:Rz2PmWxpMM), Cestulus, including its quelling by the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN)  military. After [first contact](gp:R4ZQpYEEvx) with the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) in 2530 and discovery of the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) in 2541, the network's content began to gradually lean pro-war and anti-alien. \n\nUpon the ascension of [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) to the office of [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr) in 2546, SSN/CAtv's content took a hard pro-government shift. The host and crew of *Showdown!* were fired and replaced after they aired a special episode urging people to act against Messer's consolidation of power. [Deacon Messer II](gp:0j46m4BYge) became one of the network's prime shareholders in 2601. After this point, SSN/CAtv became one of the cornerstones of the [United Empire of Earth's (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) propaganda machine. \n\nIn 2630, SSN/CAtv relocated to an expansive headquarters on Terra. The network slowly began to allow some UEE-critical content to air, while still maintaining a pro-Messer stance in the majority of its programming. For example, SSN/CAtv played a pivotal role in discrediting Terran Senator [Assan Kieren's](gp:RWwZQK774P) reputation during his call for Terran sovereignty in 2638, but it also allowed its pundit and debate programs to feature anti-military and pro-secession guests. \n\nDuring the power struggle between [Astrid Messer VII](gp:0KnA1D5nQM) and [Samuel Messer VIII](gp:RkZ9W2L2NB), reporters on multiple shows stepped too far out of line, harshly criticizing the Messers for their infighting. In 2699, Astrid Messer VII retaliated by conducting mass arrests and censoring over half the network's programming into cancellation. Samuel Messer VIII rescinded the mass censorship upon taking office in 2701, but ordered that all content aired henceforth on the network had to be approved by the [Imperator's](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) office. Those imprisoned by Astrid Messer VII were not pardoned, and were forced to serve out the remainder of their sentences. \n\n# ROLE IN THE DEPOSITION OF THE MESSER REGIME\nAnonymous SSN/CAtv insiders began organizing with anti-Messer activists as early as 2702. They aided the resistance in two key ways: they allowed the rebels to pass along encrypted messages via the network's communications arrays, and fed them information uncensored by the Messer government. Once such piece of information was footage from the [Massacre of Garron II](gp:01dWeqnMr1). On 11 April 2792, technicians responsible for the network feed allowed footage of the Massacre, along with a message from the resistance group [Tide](gp:RXlXOpwG6k), to interrupt a broadcast of SSN/CAtv Nightly News. This broadcast was the inciting incident of [the revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7) that would eventually depose the Messer regime.\n\n# TODAY\nSSN/CAtv hosts a wide variety of news and news-related content. Some of their flagship programs include pure news shows [Empire Report](gp:RwZBqM4K9J) and [SSN/CAtv Nightly News](gp:bZwQ6AxomO), the pundit-centered debate program *Showdown!* and the UEE-critical talk show [Plain Truth](gp:bZwQ6lpJEd). It has satellite offices on most recognized planets in the UEE.","g":["spectrum network","sheridan special news television","communications alliance","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9383b967-a805-4d0c-bf95-d8acd53d93bb"},
{"id":"ssncatv-nightly-news","gp":"bZwQ6AxomO","t":"SSN/CAtv Nightly News","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"SSN/CAtv Nightly News is a [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) news show that airs after its sister show [Empire Report](gp:RwZBqM4K9J). It covers more local news stories that are not aired on Empire Report, but are still deemed newsworthy by [SSN/CAtv](gp:0QxYwPK88l).","g":["news show","spectrum show","news organization","ssn/catv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/422604b4-aec2-4c6f-838e-6bde9ecb1d58"},
{"id":"stalford","gp":"VY4Wj6Yrj1","t":"Stalford","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Stalford is a mid-sized city located on [Rytif (Bremen II)](gp:R5pA7q691W). Positioned just north of the planet's equator, Stalford is home to numerous water farms and commercial vivariums. Stalford is also the headquarters of spacecraft designer and manufacturer [Consolidated Outlands](gp:0KnAYqez34). In SEY 2792 during the late [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo), anti-Messer activists used Rytif as a hub of operations to organize the [overthrow](gp:bE3rKa32P7) of [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq). In recent years, the city has become a tourist site, owing to a variety of monuments commemorating Rytif's role in the fall of the [Messer](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/messer-dynasty) regime.","g":["rytif","bremen ii","uee city","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e4a00b0a-6091-4e10-a4ff-5c3b52fc936e"},
{"id":"stalker","gp":"0qnN6jyoa5","t":"Stalker","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Stalker is a variant of the [Avenger](gp:ReJanvr73r) patrol ship developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). When the standard Avenger fighter failed to connect with military users, Aegis adapted it as a police spacecraft with the addition of the Stalker Prisoner Transport Module, a system of cell and restraints that allowed safe prisoner transport. These changes also attracted bounty hunters to purchase the ship, in need of methods by which to bring in their targets alive. Although the Stalker was the first variant of the Avenger developed, its popularity eclipsed that of its parent model, leading many to incorrectly assume it was the original Avenger type.","g":["passenger transport","aegis dynamics","interdiction","transport","avenger series","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/84733dc1-feed-478e-a064-932b6d154c45"},
{"id":"srv","gp":"02BQ1wNGKQ","t":"Standard Recovery Vehicle (SRV)","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The SRV (Standard Recovery Vehicle) is a tug spacecraft designed by [Argo Astronautics](gp:0KnA1vvJEM). Like Argo's [MPUV](gp:0rqzN9vek9), the SRV was designed as a dockyard support spacecraft capable of manually towing freight and cargo and conducting search-and-rescue missions. The SRV's tractor system can tow smaller spacecraft or can be combined with other SRVs for larger tasks. Operated by most major [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)-based freight companies as well as the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), SRVs are a common sight around major ports.","g":["srv","argo astronautics","industrial spacecraft","support spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2337be81-dda1-4e9c-8fdf-634b48b2d768"},
{"id":"stanton-system","gp":"RX3lKBA3dq","t":"Stanton System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"# STANTON SYSTEM\n\nThe Stanton system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), discovered in SEY 2851 by navjumper Toshi Aaron. It is one of only two fully colonized systems in the UEE, and is made up of three super-Earths, a gas giant, an asteroid belt, and a G-type star. All planets in the system were sold by the UEE government to four major corporations soon after their discovery. While inhabitants are protected under UEE's common laws, they are also subject to rules imposed by the individual corporations that own each planet.\n\n# PLANETARY SYSTEM\nThe system's star, Stanton, is a G-type main sequence star about the same size as Sol, and is roughly 4.6 billion years old. Its three terrestrial planets, [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL), [ArcCorp (Stanton III)](gp:bBzpNY6ANd), and [microTech (Stanton IV)](gp:VYL46xl5Z1) all sit in the system's green band, and were terraformed to support [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) life. Unique among gas giants, [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav) has a nitrogen-oxygen upper atmosphere and a natural ecosystem made up of plants and animals that live their entire lives in midair. A dense [asteroid belt](gp:bBzpN9A5w8) sits between ArcCorp and Crusader.\n\n# DISCOVERY\nIn 2851, navjumper Toshi Aaron was scanning for anomalies in the outskirts of the [Magnus system](gp:RWolrNa1Ge). She had spent the last decade trying to fulfill her dream of discovering a jump point, spending as much time as she could in pursuit. A week before her 49th birthday, she detected a strange signal. She noted the location, recorded all the data she could, and headed home to analyze what it could mean. All signs pointed to the likelihood that she had indeed found what she'd been looking for. A few days later, with a ship fully equipped to make the leap, she returned to the location and entered the jump tunnel. After a few harrowing moments traversing interspace, she found herself on the other side. \n\n# HISTORY\nAaron's discovery made waves in the UEE government. Not only were all the planets in the system located within the green band, but when UEE pathfinders surveyed the system, they found a jump point that connected Stanton to [Terra](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4). The UEE immediately claimed the system and dispatched naval engineers to determine what would be needed to make the three terrestrial planets habitable. Their eventual report brought bad news: the funds required to terraform these planets would be far more than the then cash-strapped government had available to them. While officials debated what to do, they gave the Navy authorization to construct a shipbuilding latticework on Stanton II's upper atmosphere, and allowed engineers to begin preliminary terraforming activity on the other planets. \n\nBy 2865, the UEE Senate, facing a potentially recession-causing budget shortfall, announced that it would be selling each of the planets in the system to the highest bidders. Multiple megacorporations reached out to or were contacted by the UEE government. After a long period of closed-door negotiations, four corporations emerged victorious: [Hurston Dynamics](gp:RxNxAZpWlQ), who purchased Stanton I and began major mining operations at once; [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N), who claimed Stanton II and its skeletal shipyards for the construction of their Starliners; [ArcCorp](gp:0dQ47zYd6O), who immediately began developing Stanton III to support their diverse industries; and [microTech](gp:bE3rBB4j7J), who considered the Stanton IV's frigid climate as beneficial for cooling their extensive network of servers.\n\n# CULTURE\nIn essence, the Stanton system is an enormous business park. While all who reside within it are protected under the UEE Common Laws, the enforcement of these laws is left up to the private security forces each corporation employs. Nearly everyone in Stanton works for one of the four corporations, or for companies that lease land or office space from them. As such, each planet is operated according to the business practices of its particular company. On Hurston, for example, Hurston Dynamics' lax environmental policy has led to a polluted atmosphere and a low quality of life for its people. Conversely, Crusader Industries' commitment to design has transformed the once sparse Navy shipbuilding platforms into beautiful live-work spaces lined with flowering trees.\n\nThe leaders of Hurston Dynamics, Crusader Industries, ArcCorp, and microTech hold the Stanton System Conference once a year to discuss system-wide issues. Commonly discussed topics include regulations on imports and exports, who has jurisdiction over what parts of the Aaron Halo (Stanton belt alpha), and strategies to deal with criminal activity.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6f7bc5ed-b252-436d-a7a8-ec3a2a1aa46a"},
{"id":"star-marine","gp":"bE3rke4j28","t":"Star Marine","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*Star Marine* is a series of sim-games developed by [InterDimension Software](gp:R9Bw9vjxv7) as ultra-realistic tactical shooters focusing on battles between [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Marines and various outlaw forces. Development of the first *Star Marine* started in 2941 with the formation of the InterDimenision; it was released in 2945 to positive reviews and has become a popular competitive game. Multiple games in the series have been used as simulators for actual combat training by the UEE military. The games are also the basis for the popular action vids *Star Marine* and *Star Marine 2: BloodLock*.","g":["combat simulator","interdimension software","games"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/33c39b65-ce41-4880-94ee-16f1f0a91625"},
{"id":"starburst-collective","gp":"RkG2Xg2yOB","t":"Starburst Collective","k":"culture","c":["Music"],"x":"Starburst Collective is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)[S-pop](gp:bE3rkJvqJ7) band based in Saisei (Centauri III). The group is composed of S-guitar player Haruhiko Maeda, synthesizer player and keyboardist Zen Shirogawa, drummer, violinist, and vocalist Aya Saito, and bassist and vocalist Maya Watanabe. Mostly S-pop, Starburst Collective also incorporates indie rock, electronic dance, experimental pop, and traditional Human folk into their sound. Their second album, *The Sun, the Stars, and...* has consistently been included among the best albums of the 30th century in a wide variety of music publications. Their third album, *The Stars are Mine*, was ranked third on *New United's* \"Top 100 Albums of SEY 2943.\"","g":["s-pop","saisei","centauri iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/08159fd7-fa5f-4bca-bc3e-fb460cb4afbd"},
{"id":"starfarer","gp":"RLMmv3QE7r","t":"Starfarer","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Starfarer is a tanker developed by [Musashi Industrial Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv). Starfarers are a common sight throughout the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), performing fuel-related roles such as simple transport, in-flight refueling, and the collection and refining of fuel from spaceborne sources, among other functions. The UEE military operates a hardened variant produced under license by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) called the [Starfarer Gemini](gp:02BQLE2ypz).","g":["refuel","heavy refuel","misc","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d4e94ddb-4caf-4eb4-9b1f-80188f2b2a6c"},
{"id":"starfarer-gemini","gp":"02BQLE2ypz","t":"Starfarer Gemini","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human","Military"],"x":"The Starfarer Gemini is a hardened variant of the [Musashi Industrial Starflight Concern (MISC)](gp:bE3rB7YJDv)[Starfarer](gp:RLMmv3QE7r) tanker modified under license by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) for the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN). The Gemini militarizes the original tanker design by adding additional armor plating and a range of defensive weaponry. Gemini serve in support roles in the UEEN supply chain and are utilized as front line refuelers. Aegis has made the Gemini available to civilian buyers in limited numbers.","g":["refuel","heavy refuel","starfarer","misc","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/237aadc2-3088-4ace-a2de-c83159069bad"},
{"id":"starliner","gp":"RWwZ7OAjXw","t":"Starliner","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"A starliner is a type of commercial spacecraft used primarily for the transportation of passengers. A significant portion of total interstellar travel within the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) is done aboard these vessels. The [Genesis](gp:0NwprWlxpX) starliner, manufactured by [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) and assembled in the upper atmosphere of [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav), is one of the most common models of this type of ship. Major transportation companies such as [Meridian Transit](gp:RLMmB9Kl2L) primarily operate starliners.","g":["passenger transport","transport","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c52401f7-bbb2-4e41-befe-84008f3cbb08"},
{"id":"starwatch","gp":"R5poE41lEA","t":"StarWatch","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*StarWatch* is a popular celebrity gossip and pop culture talk show produced for [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) that debuted in 2940. Fans of the show refer to themselves as StarWatchers. Most episodes of the program open with a segment in which the host comments on pieces of celebrity gossip accompanied by images and video, some of which is reported by StarWatchers. Guests often appear to discuss various pop culture topics or to be interviewed. The current host of *StarWatch* is Carolyn Choy, known as Callie C.","g":["spectrum show","talk show"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b41708cb-8174-47ff-8793-367fa067f08a"},
{"id":"state-uee","gp":"RWwZ78lypa","t":"State (United Empire of Earth)","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"A state is a non-sovereign political organization within the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), usually referring to centralized governing bodies within unified territories. States on [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) colony worlds are typically formed around settlements or other developed areas. States maintain a variety of local types of governments which manage their local affairs within their place in planetary governments and the UEE as a whole. On worlds with UEE [senatorial](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) representation, states are managed by a [Governor](gp:RkZ9A5KjBL) and a hundred [Representatives](gp:0KnAzj9B1o).","g":["uee states","uee representative"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/65243fd1-6f15-4ab0-87da-d131d937c0b5"},
{"id":"stegmans-clothing-and-uniforms","gp":"RX3JyXyP6P","t":"Stegman's Clothing and Uniforms","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Stegman's Clothing and Uniforms is a workwear clothing brand that makes uniforms and protective gear. Founded by husband and wife Greg Stegman and Ahanti Riordan, the company began in SEY 2635 as a storefront owned by Riordan's family, where Stegman would sell handmade workwear. In 2643, they had grown to the point where they were able to open a factory and distribute their products throughout the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE).","g":["clothing manufacturer","footwear manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1606809e-93be-4b6c-a510-c94d1d7e32b4"},
{"id":"stella-fortuna","gp":"0qn8vv3Aw1","t":"Stella Fortuna","k":"history","c":["Culture","Holidays","Human"],"x":"# Stella Fortuna\nStella Fortuna is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) cultural celebration associated with good fortune and success in new ventures. It was first established as a commemoration of the successful colonization of Mars (Sol IV). Feasting, fireworks, festivals, and other forms of mass celebration are hallmarks of the holiday, along with the colors gold and green. It is celebrated each year on March 15th throughout the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).\n \n# Origin\nIn the mid-22nd century, the people of Earth (Sol III) established Humanity's first successful extraplanetary colony on Mars. This was the second attempt at colonization; the first Human colony on Mars [failed](gp:bmNrgKnZ6l) late in the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) process when an error in the atmosphere processors led to sudden mass atmospheric collapse. 4,876 Humans died. The second attempt at a colony was largely regarded as doomed. In a widely-circulated article on the potential dangers a Mars immigrant might face, Kelsey Forset of Sentinel NewsOrg simply wrote, \"Don't tempt fate.\" This message was ultimately co-opted: \"Tempt Fate\" with \"Don't\" crossed out became an unofficial slogan of the early Mars colonists.\n \nIn 2200, multiple Earth-based governments announced plans for an interplanetary holiday to celebrate 45 successful years of Human habitation on Mars. It would be held during the following Earth-Mars conjunction (18th March 2202) to emphasize the connection between the planets. Martian schoolchildren were invited to submit possible names for the new holiday. \"Stella Fortuna\" was selected from an entry provided by Estelle Priya, age 11, of [Port Renatus](gp:RWwZWj9vOZ) Public School 17.\n \nLarge public carnivals sponsored by space travel and terraforming companies were held on Mars and Earth. They featured rides, food, games, and half-price tickets to attractions throughout the Sol System, from space stations on the asteroid belt to the volcanoes of Io. New parcels of land on Mars were raffled off to festival attendees, along with a ship outfitted with a quantum engine provided by [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw). Local businesses sold souvenirs stamped with the slogan \"We Tempted Fate: Stella Fortuna 2202.\" The day ended with a green and gold firework display.\n \nStella Fortuna was held at varying times of the year during Earth-Mars conjunctions for over a half century. In 2257, the majority of governments on Earth and Mars declared March 15th the official holiday. While March 18th was initially proposed, it was not selected due to conflict with another holiday - the anniversary of the first Human born on a planet other than Earth.\n \n# Celebration and Traditions\nStella Fortuna has evolved from a holiday commemorating the early Mars colony to one that celebrates good fortune, boldness, tempting fate, and embarking on new business ventures. This was caused by a number of factors, but the against-all-odds success of the Mars colony combined with the long-term success of early settlers were two major influences. In particular, the families who won land during the first Stella Fortuna did a great deal to promote the idea that the holiday was associated with good luck. By the time the holiday's final date was selected, people preparing for interplanetary trips were already asking the stars for their blessing. It became a tradition in the late 2200s for explorers to toast the stars before embarking on searches for jump points, or for people launching new business ventures to begin them on March 15th.\n \nThe largest celebrations still occur on Mars. Most businesses close for the holiday and the day after. The festival officially kicks off with a parade featuring elaborately decorated floats in the form of spaceships or stars. Celebrants clad in colorful, light-up costumes throw candy, raffle tickets, or other small prizes from atop the floats into the crowd. Carnivals filled with rides and games run throughout the day and night. Intoxicated crowds will spontaneously burst into traditional songs such as \"Aim for the Stars but Strike from Mars\" and \"Illuminate the Way.\" Marriage proposals are as common as new business ventures; the green and gold firework display that concludes the festival is a favorite time to seal the deal on business and romantic partnerships alike.","g":["sol iv","mars","mars tragedy","uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bb6837a4-48a0-49cb-b299-7585ee64a942"},
{"id":"stiletto","gp":"R4ZG3A66v5","t":"Stiletto","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human","Military"],"x":"The Stiletto was a medium interceptor sold by the now-defunct company [Elio-Harman Aerospace](gp:Vgg7yZjdGn) in the early 26th century. It was one of the last spacecraft designs commissioned by the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) and was used specifically to intercept enemy bombers. The Stiletto was withdrawn from service in 2580 in favor of the [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) [Gladius](gp:0j46NP5eB3) following issues with its supply chain and the design's inability to adapt to rapid advances in shield technology.","g":["elio-harman aerospace","interdiction","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9edb6171-ece1-4821-a9e5-4c8959a6d7e6"},
{"id":"storall","gp":"Vgg7YBnE4w","t":"Stor*All","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Stor•All is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) shipping container manufacturing company that sells such well-known products as the Big Box series found on many ships. Originally incorporated as TransGo in the Corel system in 2745, it rebranded as Stor•All during a period of increased trade between the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). Their vacuum-proof containers are built to transport a wide range of materials via different spacecraft designs.","g":["stor-all","transgo","commercial and industrial goods manufacturer","corel iii","lo","big box shipping container"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f32f70ab-e515-48cb-9b99-2cc57877dfe6"},
{"id":"storm","gp":"0qa162rkKp","t":"Storm","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Military"],"x":"The Storm is a single-seat combat support vehicle manufactured by [Tumbril Land Systems](gp:VarkpZnxjd). An updated version of the historic tank that was used during the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv), the Storm is fast and agile and has a steering system that allows for precise control of the tank and its weapons. Tumbril has developed the updated Storm to act as an anti-artillery support to the Nova tank.","g":["storm series","tank","tumbril land systems"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c38c01ad-d70d-475b-bd8c-2d70a7656016"},
{"id":"storm-aa","gp":"RkGO4No4wB","t":"Storm AA","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Military"],"x":"The Storm AA is a single-seat combat support vehicle manufactured by [Tumbril Land Systems](gp:VarkpZnxjd). A variant of the anti-artillery [Storm](gp:0qa162rkKp) tank, the AA has been reconfigured with anti-aircraft swarm missiles, and is capable of targeting low-flying spacecraft. The AA was designed to work in concert with the Storm, providing air defense while the Storm performs ground support.","g":["storm series","tank","tumbril land systems"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a3bc107d-9dc5-458b-b038-dffd09a58929"},
{"id":"storm-rider-palm","gp":"R9vnN6lrBd","t":"Storm Rider Palm","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The storm rider palm is a tree created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke) as a part of its line of plants meant to aid in the planet [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) process. Tall and robust, its flexible trunk and lacy leaves allow it to endure very strong winds. Rayari Inc is currently developing a variant of the storm rider palm meant to withstand the [HyperClay](gp:RkZ9W2BkDz)-infused dust storms on [Hyperion (Fora III)](gp:RegWGPlxqy).","g":["rayari inc","herbaceous plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c1bba9d2-ebb7-48ca-a5b8-9ce67f088d65"},
{"id":"stormwal","gp":"RX34BjN2NK","t":"Stormwal","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"# STORMWAL\n\nThe stormwal is a warm-blooded vertebrate indigenous to [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It was discovered in 2855, when three workers assembling Providence Platform for the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) were startled by a stormwal rising from the depths of the planet's atmosphere, causing them to drop some of their tools. The stormwal is the largest known animal with the ability to fly. \n\n# DESCRIPTION\n\nSome stormwals can reach 100 meters in length upon reaching adulthood. They are most commonly rosy-gray in color, with iridescent red fins and lightly-striped hides flecked with gold. Deep blue stormwals with blue-gray fins have also been observed. They have long, spade-shaped snouts and four eyes, two on each side of the head. Four long barbels trail off the head from the chin and the brow, which are used alongside the filaments on their pectoral, dorsal, and tail fins to sense the miniscule electrical fields of aeroplankton and [kiami](gp:RkG8lNDMW9), their main prey. Four other elongated non-frilled fins are situated on the left and right side of the stormwal's belly. Six nostrils on either side of the snout and two enormous cavities just behind the head take in air that is internally distilled by specialized organs to contain only helium and hydrogen, which is then used to fill inner flight bladders that enable the stormwal to maintain flight. Excess air is expelled, and new air is taken in as needed. \n\n# BEHAVIOR AND ECOLOGY\n\nAdult stormwals must eat between 1000 and 1500 kg of aeroplankton, kiami, small floaters, and other animals each day. They cooperate with their pods when hunting, flying in circles to force prey to concentrate in the center of an air vortex. The stormwals then take turns swimming into the trapped prey, taking huge gulps of air until they are sated. Solo stormwals often eat by diving into cloud formations that are densely-populated with aeroplankton. \n\nElectricity is vital to a stormwal's life cycle. To communicate, either to signal that a food source has been found, seek mates, call young who have flown too far from their parents, or simply to engage in bonding behavior, stormwals send electro-magnetic pulses to one another over long distances. When engaging in courtship, each stormwal will weave an intricate electro-magnetic pattern and transmit it to their prospective mate. This process can take several days. If either animal dislikes the pattern, they will break away from one another and seek mates elsewhere. \n\nStormwal reproduction is a coordinated affair. Because they give live birth and stormwals do not land, a stormwal in labor must be watched by one or more other stormwals. When the squall emerges from its mother, one of the watching stormwals will catch it and let it rest, so that it has time to slowly fill its internal air cavities. Squalls that are not caught are in great danger of falling to their deaths. When the squall is finally able to float, it is returned to its mother, where it latches onto her mammary gland and feeds. It will nurse as its primary food source for up to two SEY. \n \n# IN CULTURE\n\nDenizens of [Orison](gp:V7dgN8Pkrm) consider the stormwal a symbol of their city. A large statue of a stormwal entitled \"Until Then\" by artist Biphasha Zhu sits in Cloudview Center, and the official mascot of the city, Finley the stormwal, can be purchased in plush form in local shops. Visitors to Orison can book tours to the nearby Stormwal Sanctuary, where they try to catch a glimpse of the animals in their natural habitat. \n\nIn recent years, poachers have been spotted hunting and killing stormwals within the bounds of the Sanctuary, to the outrage of locals. [Crusader Security](gp:bmNrmYB8MP) has increased its presence in the area as a deterrent to further attacks.","g":["crusader","stanton ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b093bc63-2f2a-4018-97f0-56a33406a332"},
{"id":"suj-kossi","gp":"RMNgraDJAA","t":"Suj Kossi","k":"people","c":["People","Tevarin"],"x":"Suj Kossi (b.2900) is a [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) for [Jalan (Elysium III)](gp:VarAXY2zy2), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Kossi began his political career after his honorable discharge from the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), where he received a Medal of Valor for his service during a dangerous repair mission under fire from the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO). After a race against Gabrielle Gracián and Sakae Marigold, he became the first [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) to be elected to the office of Senator in 2946. He was re-elected in 2951.\n\n# EARLY LIFE\n\nKossi was the second youngest child of six children, born in 2900 to Sei Kossi and Qy Rusfa in the hills outside [Gemma](gp:V7gM71L7mk), Jalan. His parents and extended family, who shared Kossi's home, were career criminals who primarily targeted and robbed homes, outposts, or other potentially profitable locations. From the time he was ten, he joined his family on low-risk raids, eventually taking on more dangerous tasks after he turned fifteen. In 2919, a raid on a water farm outside [Nedila](gp:0QlmN2mla5) erupted in violence, and Kossi's eldest sister Fef Rusfa was killed in the firefight, alongside all three of the farmers who had tried to defend their home. In the aftermath, Kossi and his surviving family members learned that all of the farm's equipment was broken, and there was nothing worth stealing. Overcome with a feeling that his sister had died for nothing and he'd wasted his life, Kossi ran away from his family and enlisted in the [UEE Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q).\n\n# MILITARY CAREER\n\nFor six years, Kossi served with distinction, reaching the rank of Sergeant in 2925. He was selected soon after for a transfer to the Navy for flight training. As a pilot, he ran sensor repair missions until 2928, when a surprise Vanduul raid interrupted what should have been a routine mission in the Oberon system. Kossi used his ship to shield three technicians under his command from ongoing enemy fire, saving their lives at the cost of sustaining grievous injuries. He spent the next sixteen months in an intensive care unit. Though he recovered, long-term effects from his injuries ended his military career. Kossi was awarded [Citizenship](gp:RLMmop8rkr), the Medal of Valor, and an honorable discharge for his service.\n\n# POLITICAL CAREER\n\nKossi moved to an apartment owned by Ustiel Housing Development, a small corporation that owned and managed a handful of low to middle-income habitations around Gemma. After his neighbors suffered a series of unjust evictions after weeks of intimidation tactics from their building manager, he conducted some research and noticed that this pattern occurred across all properties owned by Ustiel stretching back 15 years. Kossi responded by organizing a class-action lawsuit that eventually resulted in a criminal inquiry. \n\nIn 2933, Kossi ran for a position on the Gemma city council, which he lost. Undeterred, he ran again in 2937 and was elected based on a platform of ensuring housing equality. He began to appear on local news programs as an advocate for renters and a de facto spokesperson for Tevarin, a role which earned him some criticism from the Tevarin community. After successfully enacting a rent-control ordinance in 2944 during his second term, Kossi announced his intention to run as Senator on the [Universalist](gp:VDo6qOgLx9) ticket. In 2946, he temporarily suspended his campaign for a week following the [Battle for Vega II](gp:0Gz5mkprmg) to report for duty with the Naval Reserves. Analysts believe that this action pushed his poll numbers high enough to ensure his successful election at the end of the year.\n\nSince taking office, Kossi co-authored several important pieces of legislation, sat on the Subcommittee on the Interior, led outreach programs to raise the Tevarin vote, and became a regular guest on popular spectrum news programs. He is a strong supporter of loosening current Citizenship requirements and expanding enfranchisement across the UEE. After [Laylani Addison](gp:VYLvBm6Po1) became Imperator in 2950, he worked with her to draft legislation that would create programs to incentivize Tevarin involvement in the public sector. He was re-elected in 2951. Koto Dodson of the [Terra Gazette](gp:RzPo4jJWdZ) has speculated that Kossi will run for [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) in 2960, a rumor that the Universalist party has neither confirmed nor denied.","g":["uee senator"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/75745f87-929c-45f8-8949-f8caa4bcc6e5"},
{"id":"sunset-berry-bush","gp":"VgEwG2xWoN","t":"Sunset Berry Bush","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The sunset berry bush is a shrub that produces clusters of red-orange berries. Extremely toxic, the berries are tannic and have a bitter flavor, and can cause vomiting and cramping if eaten raw. If fermented, they become very sweet but are much more dangerous to consume. The bush grows wild in cold climates and can survive in most types of soil. It is susceptible to wilting if subjected to high temperatures.","g":["bushes"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/15a6d129-8d72-464d-a975-9b6e92f65cb8"},
{"id":"supermodernist-architecture","gp":"RxNxl241Qa","t":"Supermodernist Architecture","k":"culture","c":["Art","Human"],"x":"Supermodernist architecture is an architectural school of style that blends the use of developments in high technology with a sense of hopeful meaning. The style rose in popularity in the early years of the 30th century. The [Phiyi Tower](gp:01dW3XmX3L), constructed in the wake of the 2934 earthquake in [Acheron](gp:VJOz3gMM85) on Charon III, is a masterwork of the style.","g":["architecture style","phiyi tower"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/42741077-5d12-40c9-b68e-894934d21b82"},
{"id":"syang-fabrication","gp":"0Njq1K5ZE4","t":"Syang Fabrication","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Syang Fabrication is an armor and undersuit manufacturer operated by House Syang. For centuries, the company has produced products meant to withstand the rigors of space travel and battle for generations. Consequently, pieces made by Syang are considered valuable heirlooms in some [Xi'an Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL). In SEY 2953, they entered the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) market with the Xanthule line of suits, helmets, and backpacks.","g":["armor manufacturer","house syang"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/86d43891-cabf-4712-9901-e93919624df6"},
{"id":"sydney-kamarck","gp":"VaZwNWd7lm","t":"Sydney Kamarck","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Sydney Kamarck (2761-2864) was a historian of Human Political Systems at the University of Rhetor, most well-known for her 2812 book *The Path to Prime Citizen*. In 2806, the Truth and Reconciliation Commission released thousands of personal and official records connected to the [Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) family to the public. Researching these documents, Kamarck discovered that [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) may have orchestrated the series of bombings that claimed thousands of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) lives in 2546. In her book, she alleged that while Messer's former squadmates [Adam Corr](gp:V3qgyvG8ZY) and [Cyrus Ishitaka](gp:R4ZGy5XJXe) most likely perpetrated the attacks, they did so under Messer's orders.","g":["the path to prime citizen","atrocity at jata","university of rhetor"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e610b5ec-bf51-4f4a-bc6d-b1fdd72d6fdf"},
{"id":"sylvie-randall","gp":"V3qgj86Wz2","t":"Sylvie Randall","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Commander Sylvie Randall (SEY 2835 - 2884) was a [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Naval Officer, most famously known as the final commanding officer of the [89th Logistic Support Squadron](gp:0Gz5BNmPqo) (\"the Lost Squad\"). She took command of the 89th in 2878, and spent her tenure requesting more funding and supplies from the UEE Navy and spending what assets she could gather on the repair of Caliban's early warning system. Her last act as commander was to order the 89th to defend and evacuate the civilian population of the Caliban system. She died alongside her squadron during the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) in 2884.","g":["squadron 89","lost squad","fall of caliban"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/11e164da-aefb-425d-a8ef-de9122574f4f"},
{"id":"synergy","gp":"RkGG75dZX4","t":"Synergy","k":"culture","c":["Food and Beverages","Human"],"x":"Synergy is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) brand of wellness-themed energy drinks manufactured by conglomerate [Sakura Sun](gp:VpGEzn5edL). The beverage was first developed in 2865 by a team of researchers led by Dr. Taka Jeong. Originally, it was marketed purely as an energy drink, with commercials featuring deep-space explorers and long-haul spacers using the beverage to stay awake and alert while navigating dangerous territory. After modest success, Sakura Sun switched Synergy to natural ingredients and re-branded it as a healthy alternative to other energy drinks. Varieties include Synergy+, which delivers stimulants over an extended period of time, and the electrolyte drink SynergySport.","g":["soft drink","beverage","human beverage","sakura sun"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d4e1ff97-eef8-4ba4-b1a9-5c9c094d75fa"},
{"id":"syntek","gp":"VJOzQ3L29P","t":"Syntek","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Syntek is a synthetic material created by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v). It is designed to emulate the look, feel, and strength of titanium while increasing durability and reducing the weight. Origin uses Syntek in the construction of their [X1 Velocity](gp:bmNrP5oD4E) spacecraft.","g":["origin jumpworks","x1 velocity"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2aea152e-71b5-449e-bfc0-02983a371ba2"},
{"id":"synthworld-chronos-iii","gp":"bZkyrEPLra","t":"Synthworld (Chronos III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Science and Technology"],"x":"Synthworld (Chronos III) is an incomplete artificial planet located in the green band of the [Chronos system](gp:RvlQZKy95l), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). In 2872, [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) Corbyn Salehi announced a new scientific endeavor to construct a planet in the Chronos system as a way to move beyond the inherently destructive process of [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), made unpopular at the time thanks to the [Massacre of Garron II](gp:01dWeqnMr1). The project was designated [Project Archangel](gp:RLMmAnr4gj), and construction began immediately. The proposed Synthworld would ultimately have a radius of about 7500 kilometers, and is projected to have an Earth-like gravity upon its completion. However, its continued setbacks, no visible end date, and the many financial scandals that have stemmed from it have made Synthworld a point of contention among [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2).","g":["synthworld","chronos iii","chronos system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet","project archangel"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9201d837-c931-4d97-86a8-5d07f458f853"},
{"id":"system","gp":"VaZwNWg372","t":"System","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The term system is most frequently used by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) as shorthand for planetary system, the grouping of all planetary bodies and other satellites that orbit a given star. The planets of a particular planetary system are by default given the name of the star itself followed by a roman numeral, ordered beginning with **I** as the innermost planet. Satellites of those planets are designated with an Arabic numeral matching the planet they orbit followed by a lowercase letter starting with **a** for the innermost moon. Less frequently, system may refer to a star system, a group of multiple stars which are impacted by one another's gravity and proximity.","g":["planetary system","system (star)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c967707f-22ef-4f34-86ac-d6f91193e016"},
{"id":"syulen","gp":"R6dwElQMln","t":"Syulen","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Syulen is a light cargo spacecraft developed by [Gatac Manufacture](gp:bo13Earlar). Designed to meet the needs of both [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) and [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) pilots, it debuted at the SEY 2953 [Intergalactic Aerospace Expo](gp:R4jpEgezde) as [House Ng.at'ak's](gp:RWolrAj1vm) latest foray into the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) market. It was crafted with a focus on maneuverability, and is outfitted with an array of over thirty thrusters. The frame embodies Xi'an aesthetics, with a marbled hull and six thruster arrays that can be folded for landing.","g":["freight","light freight","gatac manufacture","xi'an spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ceb54f5f-8f60-4f6c-8b17-65cc8dc220ac"},
{"id":"taal-system","gp":"R4j2mdjZE5","t":"T.āl System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The T.āl system is a planetary system in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that consists of an A-type main sequence star, one mesoplanet, four terrestrial rocky planets, one super-Earth, and one gas giant. Designated as a production system by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government, each habitable planet has been zoned to handle a different type of economic activity. It is a major center of trade between the Xi'an Empire and the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE), who were first notified of its existence in SEY 2789 after the signing of the [Akari-Kr.ē Treaty](gp:bE3rKrl5z6). In addition to their appointed functions, the populated planets of T.āl were assigned distinct colors to incorporate into their architecture, giving each settlement a unified appearance that can be overwhelming to first-time visitors.","g":["xi'an system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b77643cf-1acb-486a-a48a-d4d27d2cf8d6"},
{"id":"tadmor-terraforming-concern","gp":"VarG6NEaDv","t":"Tadmor Terraforming Concern","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Tadmor Terraforming Concern (TTC) was a [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) company that operated from SEY 2298 to 2369. Founded by tech entrepreneur Korian Tadmor and backed by venture capitalist funding, the company won terraforming rights to [Fora II](gp:RxnB5EqL2M) in 2308. Although the planet was located outside the [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), they hoped that recent advances in technology would allow for the resource-rich world to be terraformed. However, after many years of fruitless attempts, TTC's financial backers brought a lawsuit against the company in 2364 for failing to deliver on its promises. TTC sold all its [Fora](gp:bo1PDEgGv2)-based terraforming platforms to the new company [NemoCo](gp:0rxZpeoD2z) in order to fund its legal battle. When NemoCo announced it had discovered a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) to a new system in Fora with help from former Tadmor employee Dae-ho Ochoa, TTC filed suit against them, alleging that Ochoa discovered the system while employed with TTC and thus TTC was entitled to a stake in NemoCo's operations. Due to a lack of evidence, the suit was dismissed in 2369, and TTC was subsequently dissolved.","g":["terraforming company","human company","cestulus","davien ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bec8e561-3727-4f30-9176-938bec48d8fc"},
{"id":"taernin-the-great-traveler","gp":"V7dpX4zqJk","t":"Taernin, the Great Traveler","k":"culture","c":["Culture","Banu"],"x":"Taernin, the Great Traveler, is the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) god of travelers, crossroads, and navigation and is one of the most common deities in the [Banu pantheon](gp:RXlXGygBPD). Due to the Banu practice of not recording historical events, its origins are shrouded in mystery. When it is depicted, Taernin closely resembles a Banu, and is often portrayed standing in a boat and holding an oar. [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) that depend upon travel for trade often commission prayers to Taernin from Religious Soulis to keep them safe from unforeseen obstacles. Xenoanthropologists believe that Taernin worship may have originated on the Banu homeworld.","g":["taernin","the great traveler","religion","banu religion","gods","banu gods"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/60980bf5-71fe-43a1-bba7-7aeab0ca5e26"},
{"id":"takto-geddon-i","gp":"0jGynn5Nnn","t":"Takto (Geddon I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Takto (Geddon I) is the only planet of the [Geddon system](gp:bo1yaaL4wN), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A windswept mass of volcanic rock, it is home to a sizable population of [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) who reside beneath the planet's surface. The atmospheric pressure and mixture of gasses that would be fatal to [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj), [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) pose no trouble for Banu. Within deep underground arcologies, [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) utilize underground volcanoes to produce extremely pure black glass and gray oil, both of which are in high demand.","g":["takto","geddon i","geddon system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b88820d-84aa-4cbc-8242-7e4bbedfc8fa"},
{"id":"talisman","gp":"RX3JvdMkgk","t":"Talisman","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"Talisman is a defense company that specializes in heavy armor, spacecraft armor, and ship components. Known for the use of plating in their designs, the company utilizes a proprietary blend of metals, plastics, and other ingredients to create a thick, damage-resistant material that can be molded into various sizes. In SEY 2941, they entered the market of energy-based barriers with a line of shield generators.","g":["armor manufacturer","spacecraft component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/83f3b7c5-57b1-43ae-8fba-ecaff125d997"},
{"id":"talon","gp":"01LQXljox8","t":"Talon","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Tevarin"],"x":"The Talon is a light fighter manufactured by [Esperia](gp:0OaBKL7wlv). A replica of the historic [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) fighter designated \"Talon\" by the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) military during the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546), the spacecraft features maneuverable phalanx-style shields that can be moved to protect vital points. In 2941, three partial hulls of Talons were discovered on [Kabal III](gp:V8WrG5yroD), alongside a cache of other Tevarin artifacts that survived the Purge that took place at the end of the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) (2603 - 2610). Esperia used these recovered hulls to create modern replicas, which they debuted at the [Intergalactic Aerospace Expo](gp:R4jpEgezde) in 2950.","g":["esperia","fighter","light fighter","tevarin spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/31d27459-7f1c-4416-b0bc-0b14fa9693f5"},
{"id":"talon-shrike","gp":"01LQXlJpPB","t":"Talon Shrike","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Tevarin"],"x":"The Talon Shrike is a variant of the [Talon](gp:01LQXljox8) light fighter manufactured by [Esperia](gp:0OaBKL7wlv), and is a replica of the historic [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) fighter designated \"Shrike\" by the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) military that was first observed in use during the latter years of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546). The Shrike has a modified, missile-focused configuration compared to the base Talon, and is armed with internal missile racks to increase damage inflicted during hit-and-run attacks. Esperia consulted Tevarin and [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) historians to ensure that the modern reproduction of the Shrike was as authentic as possible.","g":["shrike","talon","esperia","light fighter","fighter","tevarin spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ef4b7f93-635f-4de0-9394-5bffb2e88599"},
{"id":"talon-weapons-systems","gp":"VaZwNpkqqm","t":"Talon Weapons Systems","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Talon Weapons System is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) weapons and munitions manufacturer based in the Croshaw system. Founded in the early 27th century by Taisei Jessop, it produces weapons designed to be mounted aboard civilian spacecraft. These were first produced in order to provide protection against guerrilla [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) during the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) (2603-2610). After the war ended, the company was hit by multiple legal challenges regarding their production of civilian weaponry. The company's victory in the courts set precedent for how civilian spacecraft are armed. Today, Talon produces a variety of missiles, torpedoes, ordnance racks, and grenades.","g":["weapons manufacturer","munitions manufacturer","angeli","croshaw ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3dbc70b9-d948-4647-9dc2-b0c775fe37b5"},
{"id":"tamsa-i","gp":"VJX9mrW794","t":"Tamsa I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tamsa I is a chthonian planet that orbits the black hole at the center of the [Tamsa system](gp:VYLAnPnYBx), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Once a gas giant, it lost its atmosphere via hydrodynamic escape due to proximity to its former star, leaving its dense metallic core intact. Astrophysicists speculate that when its original star went supernova, it was ejected from orbit and became a rogue planet until it was eventually captured by the gravitational pull of Tamsa's black hole.","g":["tamsa system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/68b20804-cb98-4068-ab0d-b43f2e96282c"},
{"id":"tamsa-ii","gp":"VgEv9PmMA9","t":"Tamsa II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tamsa II is a gas giant in the [Tamsa system](gp:VYLAnPnYBx), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Unlike the former rogue planet [Tamsa I](gp:VJX9mrW794), it naturally formed in the wide accretion disk that orbits the black hole at the center of the system. The internal heat of Tamsa II is very low, with an upper atmospheric temperature of around 200 degrees Celsius. However, the deepest sections of its mantle are just hot enough to decompose methane into elemental carbon. Once formed, the carbon then floats upwards and combines with other carbon atoms to become diamonds. These diamonds rain down into the mantle, where they are broken into carbon again, and the cycle repeats.","g":["tamsa system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4f15eb50-41e4-4b2e-9c1d-5f3580c4a548"},
{"id":"tamsa-system","gp":"VYLAnPnYBx","t":"Tamsa System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Tamsa system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Uniquely among UEE systems, its two planets revolve around a black hole rather than a star. The innermost world is thought to have been a rogue planet before it was captured by the black hole, while the outermost planet likely formed in the black hole's accretion disk. The system was discovered in SEY 2943 by [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) explorer [Kofi Baféuma](gp:bE3rL1DkwW), who sold the rights to the system to the UEE under the condition that they be allowed to name it after noted [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) visual artist [Tamsa Wheel](gp:RXlXOw9WaN). Currently, Tamsa is accessible only via the [Banshee](gp:0Gx4BENmKg)-Tamsa [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY), but UEE officials hope that other jump points will be found in the near future.","g":["uee system","unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9ff6d6fe-c63f-4a1c-adde-3c82d2aef80a"},
{"id":"tamsa-wheel","gp":"RXlXOw9WaN","t":"Tamsa Wheel","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Tamsa Wheel (2883-present) is a noted [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) visual artist known for creating interpretive large-scale sculptures from unexpected mixed media types. As described by art critic Herin Chiber, her work portrays the \"...delicate balance between mathematical precision and the universe's unbridled chaos.\" Banu explorer [Kofi Baféuma](gp:bE3rL1DkwW) named a planetary system, [Tamsa](gp:VYLAnPnYBx), after Wheel in 2943 because of their passion for her artwork.","g":["tamsa system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cb2d888f-c6a9-4e57-8726-a63d4d452406"},
{"id":"tanga-belt-alpha","gp":"VarGezrLPm","t":"Tanga Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Tanga belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the unclaimed [Tanga system](gp:0GxAv6oweE). Astronomers hypothesize that its asteroids are the remains of one or more terrestrial planets that broke apart when the star expanded into a red giant. Since then, the star has collapsed into a white dwarf, leaving a vast empty gap between the belt and its sun. Many of the asteroids, long-exposed to the heat of the white dwarf, have been sublimated into ovoid shapes.","g":["tanga system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d95295ed-deae-4747-b651-4380d5a4771e"},
{"id":"tanga-i","gp":"RWodWxyXj2","t":"Tanga I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tanga I is a chthonian planet in the unclaimed [Tanga system](gp:0GxAv6oweE). Dense and metallic, it was once the core of a gas giant and has high gravity in spite of its relatively small size. When its sun expanded into its red giant phase, its newly close proximity to the star's surface stripped away the world's hydrogen and helium atmosphere via hydrodynamic escape. Any ice that once surrounded the core evaporated away, leaving only metal and silicates behind it.","g":["tanga system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/06fd45d8-5cae-4d9c-9438-d2be40d45e9e"},
{"id":"tanga-ii","gp":"bmGe578ZyP","t":"Tanga II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tanga II is an ice planet in the unclaimed [Tanga system](gp:0GxAv6oweE), and has a surface coated with thick sheets of water, ammonia, and methane ice. When it first formed, Tanga II orbited beyond the frost line, which shifted when its star entered its red giant phase. After the red giant collapsed into a white dwarf, its temperature spiked and Tanga II began to sublimate. A trail of expelled vapor follows Tanga II as it traverses around its sun.","g":["tanga system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/996229f7-d47b-4d1c-96e0-b9bf8f7c5a18"},
{"id":"tanga-system","gp":"0GxAv6oweE","t":"Tanga System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"Tanga is an unclaimed planetary system that shares [jump points](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) with the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). It consists of a young white dwarf star, two planets, and an asteroid belt. Astronomers speculate that before the star entered its red giant phase, one or more planets could have existed in the system between the [asteroid belt](gp:VarGezrLPm) and [Tanga I](gp:RWodWxyXj2). When the star expanded in diameter, it likely destroyed any celestial bodies that orbited it too closely. At the end of its red giant phase, the star collapsed into a white dwarf and expelled the picturesque planetary nebula that surrounds the system.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e0ff30a0-6a3b-4a7f-8ff7-d61ab4efebed"},
{"id":"tang","gp":"RX3rnQ3XqM","t":"Tangaroa (Helios II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Tangaroa (Helios II) is a terrestrial planet located in the [Helios system](gp:0KxpdzWBK4), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Highly geologically active, volcanic eruptions are frequent and unpredictable, often giving rise to short-lived landmasses that are reclaimed by the sea. Its few permanent islands are located mostly at the planet's poles. Due to a combination of tidal forces and lower gravity, enormous waves hundreds of meters high are frequent on the planet. The capital city [Mariana](gp:VlMnZv8qY7) is located partially on land and partially under the sea, and is home to a thriving culture of extreme water sport enthusiasts.","g":["tangaroa","helios ii","helios system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/77e7ed9f-195c-43c0-9baf-aa6ee7c51f96"},
{"id":"tanys","gp":"01Lo67xgw1","t":"Tanys","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Tanys is a city located in the Corsti Mountains on [Locke (Idris IV)](gp:RAX8yYv9jm), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Founded as a resort town for climbing enthusiasts, in 2542 Tanys became the center of the resistance movement against the invading [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) called the Greys. When Idris IV was officially recognized by the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) in 2546, the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) chose to name the planet after Rachel Locke, leader of the movement. The natural beauty of the surrounding landscape and the city's importance to UEE history have given rise to a thriving tourism industry.","g":["locke","idris iv","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/76153656-4991-41ec-8469-102ce27e5e49"},
{"id":"taranis-2a","gp":"bmG1Mo8q2L","t":"Taranis 2a","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Tarnis 2a is the moon of [Taranis II](gp:02kg3Pkjwp), the second planet from the sun of the unclaimed [Taranis system](gp:RkG1nnXYE4). During the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792), the geo-development company [Ophion, Inc.](gp:0KxPpl3xPr) used Taranis 2a and its parent planet as testbeds for various new [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) technologies, including a dubiously-designed platform that was meant to utilize the moon's orbital energy as a power source. A combination of errors in math from the overworked and underpaid engineers, mistakes in construction from the exhausted workers, overall poor design, and the use of shoddy parts led to a catastrophic energy discharge from the largest platform that ruptured the mantle of Taranis 2a, eventually causing the moon to break apart. The \"Broken Moon of Taranis\" map featured in the popular space flight simulator [Arena Commander](gp:VyvY5LQXd6) was inspired by Taranis 2a.","g":["taranis system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3d1ae7b4-1384-4c74-8b22-36e461968f0a"},
{"id":"taranis-belt-alpha","gp":"0NjaMxW1mr","t":"Taranis Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Taranis belt alpha is the first of the unclaimed [Taranis system's](gp:RkG1nnXYE4) asteroid belts. Densely packed with asteroids, frequent collisions occur that eject dust, rocks, and other material into the already crowded area. As a consequence, travel there can be treacherous, and there has been little large-scale commercial activity. Some smaller operations have attempted to turn a profit via mining and other means, but the belt has otherwise been left largely untouched.","g":["taranis system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2145e1bc-f451-4b2b-a41d-11a4ab4fd1e1"},
{"id":"taranis-belt-beta","gp":"RX3KrjDEnq","t":"Taranis Belt Beta","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Taranis belt beta is the second asteroid belt in the unclaimed [Taranis system](gp:RkG1nnXYE4). Like its [sibling belt](gp:0NjaMxW1mr), it is dense with asteroids and dangerous to traverse. Nevertheless, some individuals use it as a place to hide from pursuers. Smugglers, pirates, and other outlaws have been known to operate there, making civilian travel in the belt a risky prospect at best.","g":["taranis system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4dcecf9f-6a13-44f1-878c-99e76a2efed2"},
{"id":"taranis-i","gp":"bEzXpZGyy2","t":"Taranis I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Taranis I is a mesoplanet in the unclaimed [Taranis system](gp:RkG1nnXYE4). The closest planet to its sun, temperatures on Taranis I are sometimes high enough to warp hulls. In 2559, the planet came to fame when a new review of survey data captured in the wake of the system's discovery revealed what appeared to be a Human face carved into its northern surface. Nicknamed the \"Face of Taranis,\" this anomaly created a brief cultural craze that eventually led to a privately-funded investigatory expedition. Reports confirmed that the so-called face was actually a mountain range that had been photographed in an unusual position. Public interest dissipated shortly after.","g":["taranis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/156f9df4-8e8c-4052-9d86-05533ea7b7b4"},
{"id":"taranis-ii","gp":"02kg3Pkjwp","t":"Taranis II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Taranis II is the second planet from the sun of the unclaimed [Taranis system](gp:RkG1nnXYE4). Although Taranis II was classified as a poor choice for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) after its discovery, geo-developer [Ophion Inc](gp:0KxPpl3xPr). attempted to terraform the planet in 2566 using an experimental process. The company's history of utilizing underpaid and underqualified labor along with substandard parts to cut costs led to numerous accidents, the worst of which scarred the planet's landscape and cracked its [moon](gp:bmG1Mo8q2L) in half. Matter from the resulting debris field has been striking Taranis II ever since. Much of the terraforming machinery Ophion abandoned has fallen to the planet's surface, where it continues to burn.","g":["taranis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/402425c4-ac04-4f7e-aa14-5f36d1fa2a92"},
{"id":"taranis-iii","gp":"VYLqxAqQvo","t":"Taranis III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Taranis III is the third planet from the sun of the unclaimed [Taranis system](gp:RkG1nnXYE4). A smog planet, it has a thick and high-pressure atmosphere that gives rise to frequent storms. Although the air isn't breathable, it is home to a sizable settlement of [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) situated in an abandoned research station called [Bethor](gp:RMXyYx3lWx). Established in 2536, it was originally created as a base of operations for a privately-funded research team interested in weather control techniques. Expats from the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) claimed the abandoned station in 2551, and have since expanded it.","g":["taranis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bde1a7bf-cb74-409d-806e-b61f1845f05b"},
{"id":"taranis-iv","gp":"VgEWXvlLG3","t":"Taranis IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Taranis IV is the fourth planet from the sun of the unclaimed [Taranis system](gp:RkG1nnXYE4). Its hydrogen and helium atmosphere is pale yellow, banded with cream and tan. As the system's main stop for harvesting fuel, it sees occasional traffic from independent travelers. However, its thick ring of captured asteroids discourages stops from larger commercial ships.","g":["taranis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c842152b-e3d9-4a2d-a851-23f182549925"},
{"id":"taranis-system","gp":"RkG1nnXYE4","t":"Taranis System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Taranis system is an unclaimed planetary system that consists of an A-type main sequence star, a mesoplanet, two terrestrial planets, a gas giant, and two asteroid belts. Discovered in SEY 2478 by the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) survey ship *Mythic Horizon*, the initial scouting report classified its planets as high-risk candidates for [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and the system was left largely untouched. During the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792), Taranis was sometimes used as a testbed for new technology, which led to a 2566 accident that destroyed the moon of [Taranis II](gp:02kg3Pkjwp). In addition to the dangerous debris field created by this incident, the system's two dense asteroid belts pose a persistent navigational hazard for travelers.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c4407dbc-95d1-4214-bca6-930bb1d589c6"},
{"id":"tarquin-klast","gp":"0dQ4mGDJYd","t":"Tarquin Klast","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Tarquin Klast (2879-present) is the elected [Governor](gp:RkZ9A5KjBL) of the state of [Dellin](gp:0OaBKD9Kwk) on the planet Charon III. Born to a low-income family, he was elected governor amidst the ongoing conflict Between Dellin and its neighboring state of [Acheron](gp:VJOz3gMM85). Klast has been accused by newsorgs and watchdog groups of removing the checks and balances of his own government, arguably to maintain power. He has responded to these accusations that these changes have been necessary to safeguard Dellin from hostile Acheron military action.","g":["uee governor","charon iii","dellin"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d5049499-f97c-4f45-84d3-7ab0c91553cc"},
{"id":"tatavo","gp":"VpMv8Y7Jq7","t":"Tatavo","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Tatavo is a high-end design firm that specializes in bespoke furniture, especially for spacecraft. Located on Cassel (Goss II), it was founded by carpenter Eva Tarvel and metalworker Samvel Vanlian, after the long-time friends renovated the interior of Vanlian's ship. Members of Vanlian's family, impressed with what the pair had done, requested custom work of their own. As word of mouth spread, they took on more and more renovations as independent contractors until officially founding Tatavo in 2901. [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) partnered with Tatavo to design the furniture used in the luxury spacecraft [600i](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/origin-600-series), released in 2947.","g":["furniture manufacture","constellation phoenix","cassel","goss ii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1808b5d6-3a46-4abc-b6bf-490b26a75c45"},
{"id":"tayac-belt-alpha","gp":"RkGGQWPj7n","t":"Tayac Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Tayac Belt Alpha is a circumstellar asteroid belt in the [Tayac system](gp:RAXX4N3w4B) located between [Tayac II](gp:0ODDm26XmA) and [Tayac III](gp:bZkkxB94eB). It is best known as the home of the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj)-[Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-[Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) art installation [Silent Song](gp:VaZwNW43ym), an enormous art piece completed in 2900 and created over the course of a decade to celebrate [the Ark's](gp:0qnNMX5lAk) centennial anniversary.","g":["asteroid belt","tayac system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5be39483-16d6-4278-aa1c-d36d98c51d9e"},
{"id":"tayac-i","gp":"RX33y7kp9q","t":"Tayac I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tayac I is a small, terrestrial planet without an atmosphere in the [Tayac system](gp:RAXX4N3w4B), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). From 2546 to 2750, the planet was [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and de-terraformed multiple times by the leadership of [Project Vespa](gp:RMXymp7EGn), a [Messer](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/messer-dynasty)-backed initiative to develop a planet-destabilizing super weapon. The damage done to the planet during that time has rendered it unable to be terraformed.","g":["tayac system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3e9d88aa-ecf8-45fc-bd12-6eb50deaa5b6"},
{"id":"tayac-ii","gp":"0ODDm26XmA","t":"Tayac II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tayac II is a gas giant in the [Tayac system](gp:RAXX4N3w4B), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Its planetary rings are among the largest and densest in the known universe. Visitors to Tayac often take special trips to see the rings up close during their time in the system. Postcards featuring the dark rings against Tayac II's bright atmosphere are commonly sold in rest stops and gift shops in the system.","g":["tayac system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/10fefd88-01d9-4574-9ff2-0a67486facd7"},
{"id":"tayac-system","gp":"RAXX4N3w4B","t":"Tayac System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Tayac system is a small planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), made up of a G-type main sequence star, a terrestrial planet, a gas giant, a dwarf planet, and an asteroid belt. Starting in 2546, Dr. Thessaly Tayac, for whom the system is named, conducted a long-term [research project](gp:RMXymp7EGn) on Tayac I to explore the possibility of weaponizing the [terraformation process](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and [technology](gp:bmNrZOQ2pQ). Thanks to his experiments and those of his successors, the surface of [Tayac I](gp:RX33y7kp9q) has become too unstable to support permanent terraforming. Tayac is best known as the home of [the Ark](gp:0qnNMX5lAk), a neutral library and archive built for the use of all civilizations.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c70df3b6-08b8-46ad-8aa8-b19b70521111"},
{"id":"tdd-station-kesner","gp":"VDzlMglNMd","t":"TDD Station Kesner","k":"place","c":["Locations"],"x":"The Trade and Development Division (TDD) Station Kesner is a shipping station located in the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Operating near the Sol-[Croshaw](gp:0qanKAEJwp) jump point, it is a large facility with commercial docks, hangars, shops, and housing. Most cargo entering Sol with [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) as its final destination is first processed aboard Kesner.","g":["sol system","space station","uee space station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/56a0c4da-f708-496d-89fb-78e438273f69"},
{"id":"tears-of-fire","gp":"0qn8vvz9YW","t":"Tears of Fire","k":"culture","c":["Culture","Art"],"x":"# Tears of Fire\nTears of Fire is a painting by the early [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) landscape and military artist Aaron Fring. It was completed in SEY 2610, after Fring witnessed [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) Warlord Corath'Thal and his fleet falling through the atmosphere of [Jalan](gp:VarAXY2zy2) (Elysium IV, formerly Kaleeth) in an act of self-immolation.\n \nTears of Fire is Fring's only work to have been inducted into the UEE Historical Vault for Antiquity. It hangs in the Bentley National Gallery on Jalan.\n \n# Background\nThe Tevarin lost their homeworld, then called Kaleeth, to the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) a the end of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) On 09 March 2603, a faction of Tevarin led by Warlord Corath'Thal sparked the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv); a protracted and brutal guerrilla war for the Elysium system against the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). On 24 June 2610, after a catastrophic defeat in the [Centauri system](gp:0Qllvmr5v5) at the hands of [Squadron 42](gp:RWoeByvQap), it became clear to Corath'Thal and his forces that they could not defeat the UEE military and an armed populace. Faced with the choice between surrender and death at the hands of his enemy, Corath'Thal chose a third option: he ordered his surviving loyal forces to charge through the UEE military blockade for Elysium.\n \n# Subject\nOn 25 June 2610, the remains of the Tevarin fleet reached Jalan's atmosphere. The residents of the planet braced for an attack. Instead, Corath'Thal and his fleet dropped their thermal shields and dove for the planet. As they burned in the atmosphere, Corath'Thal's final words were picked up by human communication devices: \"We die at home, and we die free.\"\n \n# Artist\nAaron Fring was born on Ferron on 13 October 2578 to teacher Max Fring and pilot Mary Fring. He learned to draw and paint as a child, during a period in which he was bedridden with Kilos' Malady. As an adult, his illness prevented him from following his mother into service with the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), so he joined the UEE Expeditionary Force (UEEEF) as a Field Medic. The UEEEF eventually stationed him on Jalan. He fell in love with the landscape there and was inspired to resume painting. The night of Corath'Thal's descent, Fring was taking an evening walk, having left all his communication devices at his home. As he approached the crest of a hill, he noticed strange lights in the sky, and saw the first of the Tevarin fleet push through the clouds. Fring watched until the last of the ships had either broken apart or crashed. He began work on Tears of Fire the next day.\n \nThe debut of Tears of Fire at the Gemma Gallery of Art launched Fring's career as a full-time painter. He went on to produce more pieces centered around the Tevarin Wars, to continual acclaim. His portrait of Corath'Thal, referenced from holos and oral descriptions, is noted for its use of smoke and lighting. He died on 11 November 2631 from Kilos-related complications, aged 53 years. Tears of Fire was inducted into the UEE Historical Vault for Antiquity in 2633.\n \nFring cited human Romantic-era [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) art as one of his primary influences, particularly the use of light and color in Ivan Aivazovsky's 1848 painting Battle of Chesma. A copy of the painting hung in Fring's studio. Tears of Fire inspired a revival of Romantic-style art in the UEE, notably pieces with glowing, effusive sources of light.","g":["aaron fring","warlord corath'thal","kaleeth","second tevarin war","kilos' malady","bentley national gallery","painting","jalan","elysium iv"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/36cc4340-6f3b-40e2-8af3-b8f94be069cb"},
{"id":"tedge-8","gp":"R4ZG6lz41x","t":"Tedge 8","k":"history","c":["Weapons","History","Human"],"x":"The Tedge 8 is a combustion pistol manufactured by [Garrity Arms](gp:bE3rLKwr9J) from 2280 to 2516. The Tedge 8 is prized by collectors today and is considered an iconic weapon representative of the early, roughshod [era](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm) of interstellar colonization. It is a traditional combustion ballistic pistol powered by a disposable neon pressure canister. An unmodified gun has a clip size of eight bullets, though aftermarket modifications can significantly alter this capacity.","g":["garrity arms","combustion gun","human colonial expansion era"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4f250748-0f21-4716-ac59-854e478297e8"},
{"id":"teesa-morrison","gp":"01LrNgqDrL","t":"Teesa Morrison","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Teesa Morrison (SEY 2492 - 2571) was an explorer best known for her discovery of the [Baker](gp:Rz2KGkv13N)-[Yā'mon](gp:VarxDJ5yLo) jump point. Born on a tanker ship that was passing through the [Cano system](gp:Rxn9DYKdnd), she was a self-described \"full-time spacer and explorer\" who funded her expeditions to new or uncharted areas of space by taking odd jobs as needed. While flying through the Baker system in 2531, she detected a signal that she determined to be a jump point after days of analysis. When she completed the jump, her exuberance of discovering what appeared to be an unknown system was short lived when she encountered a [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military unit and was forced to retreat back through the jump tunnel. The [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) military tried to contain news of the discovery, but a recording of Morrison's encounter leaked to newsorgs and became a major story. Two standard weeks after her initial crossing, a Xi'an scout emerged from the jump point into Baker, nearly sparking a war. With all the increased media attention, rather than fighting, the [UPE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) took a more cautious approach and an outright conflict was avoided. Later, Morrison would use the money awarded her from the UPE government for her discovery to purchase a larger ship, which she made into her permanent home. She died of natural causes in 2571 while traversing the [Goss system](gp:RxnYdDZj96).","g":["yaa'mon system","human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/08f9caa8-cd75-4258-ae6e-f3f971f9674d"},
{"id":"tehachapi","gp":"VJOzQJGeqY","t":"Tehachapi","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Tehachapi is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) producer of defensive combat armor. Their products are marketed as an affordable but sturdy alternative to combat armor produced by companies like [ROOK Heavy Metals](gp:RLMmAGGOZO) and [Clark Defense Systems](gp:0QxYZvWY7N). Tehachapi uses a mix of armor plating and a strong polymer weave to reduce its overall weight and keep its cost down.","g":["armor manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/88448a84-9fcb-43c0-82c2-8ea2a970e287"},
{"id":"terminus-pyro-vi","gp":"RAXv9kpk5m","t":"Terminus (Pyro VI)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Terminus (Pyro VI) is the outermost world of the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Its nitrogen-oxygen atmosphere is technically breathable, but contains high enough amounts of methane and carbon dioxide that it has a negative effect on one's health after extended exposure. [Pyrotechnic Amalgamated](gp:VpM4anYBn1) placed their main hub of operations in orbit around Terminus, later abandoning the station when they left the system. Now nicknamed [Ruin Station](gp:RX3AzPdnw8), it has become a flashpoint for power struggles in Pyro. Terminus' proximity to the station has made it the site of frequent clashes between gangs.","g":["terminus","pyro vi","habitable","habitable planet","unclaimed planet","pyro system"]},
{"id":"terra-terra-iii","gp":"RL6ZrMrLNa","t":"Terra (Terra III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Terra is the third planet from the sun of the [Terra system](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4). Naturally habitable, it was colonized shortly after its discovery in SEY 2516 and has since become the most populous planet in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE), as well as a center of culture and commerce. Terra's political leaders played [key roles](gp:bE3rKrl5z6) in the movement that ended the despotic rule of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo). Today, Terra remains a center of progressive politics, and is home to the [Transitionalist](gp:0OaylwDmvv) political party.","g":["terra","terra iii","terra system","habitable","habitable planet","transitionalist party","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f0f05252-7a54-46b4-b99d-21d1ab2ca829"},
{"id":"terra-gazette","gp":"RzPo4jJWdZ","t":"Terra Gazette","k":"culture","c":["Publications","Human"],"x":"The *Terra Gazette* is a news organization based on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). Founded in SEY 2521, it is one of the oldest extant news organizations in the Terra system. The *Gazette* was one of the few major media outlets that attempted to maintain its independence during the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792), though it was forced in 2638 to take on a pro-Messer stance. The *Terra Gazette's* reporting today leans [Transitionalist](gp:0OaylwDmvv).","g":["news organization","news publication","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0b43ec9d-9de8-4c45-a1cd-157643cfafba"},
{"id":"terra-mills-terragra","gp":"0Gz5Z39z1a","t":"Terra Mills (Terragra)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Terra Mills is a manufacturer of consumer foods that was founded in SEY 2665 on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). It produces a wide variety of well known brands, such as Pips, Fieldsbury, Prallies, and [Big Benny's](gp:V3GPzWZXNA). Formerly known as Terragra, the company merged with Bremen Mills in 2717, and the resulting corporate entity was renamed Terra Mills. With the resources of Bremen Mills and Terragra's distribution network, the company became a dominating force in the market and remains a top food and beverage manufacturer. Terra Mills is one of the largest employers in the [Bremen system](gp:02kd45eyxe).","g":["terra mills","terragra","bremen mills","food company","terra","terra iii","beverage company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/931ff239-3601-4153-9a20-ad725799082b"},
{"id":"terra-system","gp":"VlMX7Mo9B4","t":"Terra System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Terra system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) made up of one mesoplanet, one terrestrial planet, two super-Earths, and one G-type star named Terra Nova. Located at the nexus of seven jump points, the system was first charted in SEY 2516 as part of [Project Far Star](gp:0qnNAD6YKa). It was quickly colonized upon the discovery that the third planet was naturally habitable, and one other planet was located in the green band. The lush and resource-rich planet [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) became a hub of trade and culture, eventually growing in population and prominence to the point that its government was able to maintain a progressive stance even under the rule of the [Messers](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo). It continues to be one of the most influential systems in the UEE. The [Transitionalist](gp:0OaylwDmvv) party, based on Terra, believes that the system should be the center of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) government.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0eef1d2a-773d-444b-8f64-f64a8af51702"},
{"id":"terra-show-me-the-music","gp":"RwZBwjdr5X","t":"Terra, Show Me the Music!","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Music"],"x":"*Terra, Show Me the Music!* Is a [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) show best known for showcasing up and coming musical performers. The series' producers have been credited with discovering many popular entertainers. Performing on the program has helped smaller bands reach larger audiences, such as Saisei-based band [The Claw](gp:0n9vkMLlzd), who found widespread popularity after their appearance on the program in 2932. The \"show\" aspect of the title refers to the series' signature electronic visualizations, displayed over the final song performed on a broadcast.","g":["terra show me the music","spectrum show","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4945a1b7-7cce-4da5-8b7d-4d69a17511a6"},
{"id":"terraformer","gp":"bmNrZOQ2pQ","t":"Terraformer","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Terraformer is the common name for industrial machinery used to alter the atmosphere and environment of inhospitable worlds in order to make them habitable. The technology can either be orbital platforms or built on the surface of the world itself, but is most often a combination of orbital and terrestrial terraformers. The number and type vary depending on the needs of the particular world that is being [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), and must be customized for every project.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8856f4c1-010b-4d7b-b348-13465db5a5f7"},
{"id":"terraforming","gp":"V3qgj8vjnj","t":"Terraforming","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Terraforming is the process of rendering an environment habitable for particular inhabitants through the use of industrial technology applied on a planetary scale. [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) have been terraforming worlds since the early 22nd century SEY, allowing for a more rapid expansion into the galaxy than would otherwise be possible. [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) have been terraforming since roughly 25400 BCE (0.5085 MXY). Terraforming is an extremely difficult process. When done incorrectly or with substandard materials and processes, it can lead to major disasters. It additionally has a devastating effect on existing flora and fauna on the planet and can lead to [mass extinction events](gp:01dWeqnMr1).","g":["colonization method"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6b167e49-b685-4773-89d8-48824510e50e"},
{"id":"terrapin","gp":"RWwZQYmBAe","t":"Terrapin","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Terrapin is a deep-space armored scout ship developed by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) for the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) Navy. Outfitted with sensitive scanners, it is used for long duration reconnaissance and leg patrol missions where crew members might need to be separated from support facilities for weeks at a time. The spacecraft is encased with heavy armor that allows it to survive skirmishes with lighter raiding craft. The Terrapin was the first military contract awarded to Anvil Aerospace.","g":["pathfinder","anvil aerospace","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6ed6b29d-8035-4de7-b56e-84b280eddcd7"},
{"id":"terrence-akari-rl6zqlwnko","gp":"RL6ZQLwnko","t":"Terrence Akari","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Terrence Akari (2737 - 2833) was a [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) of [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) who was instrumental in crafting the [Akari-Kr.ē Treaty](gp:bE3rKrl5z6), the first pact of nonaggression between [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj). He was first elected as Senator in 2772, after a decade of work on the [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv) city council. A lifelong advocate of peace between Humans and aliens, Akari ran on a platform that promised to ease the tensions between Xi'an and Humans on Terra. In 2789, [anti-Messer activists](gp:RXlXOpwG6k) smuggled him to the Tohil system, where he met with [Emperor Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo) to hammer out the details of the Akari-Kr.ē Treaty. Akari was forced to go into hiding until the events of the [Anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7) toppled [the Imperator](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq). When the new [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y) offered him a position as ambassador to the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9), Akari chose instead to rejoin with the Senate and work to rebuild the UEE. He helped craft the [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP), [Military Reorganization Act of 2793](gp:ReJa34W5Pw), the [Historical Truth Act](gp:0OaB8KmBKq), and many other key pieces of legislation that reshaped the UEE's government. He died in office of natural causes in 2833.","g":["akari-kr.ē treaty","uee senator"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/14ca4b69-3b37-41bf-885f-a9ef7b1f4eef"},
{"id":"terrence-akari-v3qgjk7jor","gp":"V3qgjK7Jor","t":"Terrence Akari","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Terrence Akari (2743-2859) was the [Senator](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) of Terra (Terra III) from 2781 to 2789, and again from 2792 to 2812. He was the first Human to defy [Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) and broker détente between [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj). In 2789, Akari secretly crossed the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) to Tohil III with the aid of Advocacy Section Chief for Terra Nathan Warrick to negotiate [a non-aggression pact](gp:bE3rKrl5z6) on behalf of Terra with [Emperor Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo). Upon his return to Terra, Akari convened an emergency delegation of the [Governors' Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) to ratify the treaty he had negotiated. It was unanimously approved. Terra officially declared its refusal to support any acts of war against the Xi'an. Because the declaration was seen as an act of treason, Akari was forced to go into hiding for a short time to escape Linton's agents. After 2792's [Anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7), Akari helped create the Office of Executive Services in 2794. He retired from the Senate in 2812.","g":["uee senator","akari-kr.ē treaty","office of executive services","messer era"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b02bdc99-38e2-43f3-a9d9-ddd3a3171963"},
{"id":"tethlea-hyoton-ii","gp":"0GxpmKaqzg","t":"Tethle'a (Hyoton II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tethle'a (Hyoton II) is the second planet from the sun of the [Hyoton system](gp:RkGDYnpq4L), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). From the surface of the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) homeworld [RyiXy'an (Hyoton III)](gp:bBz9mEDyqO) it is the brightest \"star\" in the sky, and was associated with intelligence and clarity of thought in ancient Xi'an myths. The second world to be successfully [terraformed](gp:R6dWOrLEM4) by the Xi'an, it has a hot and humid climate that supports a vibrant ecosystem. The area around the equator is especially sweltering, and as a result is less populated than the more temperate regions beyond the tropics. The still very hot climate in these areas is nearly identical to that of the RyiXy'an before it was rendered uninhabitable at the end of the [Great Divide](gp:VyvYA5qmqX), and is seen as a very desirable place to reside. Many ancient and prestigious Houses maintain seats of power on Tethle'a.","g":["tethle'a","hyoton ii","hyoton system","habitable planet","habitable","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"tethtaam-hyoton-v","gp":"bo14kaED2w","t":"Tethtām (Hyoton V)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tethtām (Hyoton V) is the farthest planet from the sun of the [Hyoton system](gp:RkGDYnpq4L), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). An orange and cream-colored gas giant, it has an atmosphere of hydrogen and helium and is the main source of fuel in Hyoton. It symbolized emptiness and time in ancient Xi'an mythology, and came to be associated with [Li'tova](gp:VJOzBK4PLe) after the philosophy was encoded into Imperial Law at the beginning of the [First Imperial Age](gp:VDoPeW55W4). Tethtām is orbited by a Li'tova temple that was made with a large viewport that always faces the planet.","g":["tethtām","hyoton v","hyoton system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"tethyeng-hyoton-i","gp":"bBz9mE3lQ8","t":"Tethyeng (Hyoton I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tethyeng (Hyoton I) is the first planet from the sun of the [Hyoton system](gp:RkGDYnpq4L), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Given the name \"fire world\" by ancient [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) astronomers, the soil on Tethyeng's surface is deep rust in color, making the planet appear to be a red star when observed from the surface of the Xi'an homeworld, [RyiX'yan (Hyoton III)](gp:bBz9mEDyqO). It is associated with joy and abundance in Xi'an myth, and was thought to aid in the quality of fermentation. Pictograms of Tethyeng, traditionally drawn as a nine-pointed star, are still used to decorate fermentation vessels.","g":["tethyeng","hyoton i","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","hyoton system","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"tethys-sol-6c","gp":"bEzYGPN8XX","t":"Tethys (Sol 6c)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Tethys (Sol 6c) is a moon of [Saturn (Sol VI)](gp:0jGpvn8AOW), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). One of the least dense of all the major moons in the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), it is made almost entirely of water ice. Due to tidal and rotational forces, it is not quite round, taking a slightly elliptical shape. Hematite and iron have been detected in trace amounts on its surface.","g":["tethys","sol 6c","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f72a60e4-ebf4-40d7-8cca-5ae027414aca"},
{"id":"tevarin","gp":"V8gJv3nB3X","t":"Tevarin","k":"species","c":["Tevarin","Civilizations"],"x":"The Tevarin are bipedal beings indigenous to the planet [Jalan (Elysium IV)](gp:VarAXY2zy2); formerly Kaleeth. In 2541, [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) researcher Dr. Kellar Lench discovered a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) into their system. At that time, the Tevarin were capable of space flight, quantum travel, and had highly developed shielding technology. Their society was martial, built around the warrior ethos of Rijora. \n\nThe Tevarin attacked the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) upon first contact and sparked the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM)(2541-2546), which they eventually lost. Their systems were annexed into the UPE and [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) set up colony towns on the Tevarin homeworld. \n\nSurviving Tevarin were either absorbed into Human society or spread outwards in a diaspora. After the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv)(2603-2610) ended in a similar defeat, the majority of Tevarin renounced their culture in a movement known now as the [Tevarin Purge](gp:R6dWB877Nn), and fully assimilated into the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2). As a subset of the UEE, many Tevarin, due to myriad social and economic factors, have historically been involved in the criminal underworld, but a growing number have become involved with public service and a burgeoning cultural revival movement.","g":["first tevarin war","second tevarin war","extant civilizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f7f4de43-d05a-4897-bf06-e5d6742e917b"},
{"id":"tevarin-diaspora","gp":"VY4WjwXngx","t":"Tevarin Diaspora","k":"history","c":["Tevarin","History"],"x":"The [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) diaspora refers to the general movement of Tevarin in the centuries following their defeat in the [First]((https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/bZwQm3meJM-first-tevarin-war)) (2541-2546) and [Second]((https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/bE3rPrz3Pv-second-tevarin-war)) (2603-2610) Tevarin Wars. Following the loss of Jalan (Elysium IV) to the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) in 2546, the Tevarin that had not already fled the planet were forcefully removed from their [homeworld](gp:VarAXY2zy2) and made to inhabit camps and resettlement communities established throughout the UEE. While many Tevarin were eventually integrated into [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) society, others opted to distance themselves from the UEE and form isolated enclaves and communities in less settled areas of the known galaxy, such as the Tevarin settlement on Branaugh II.","g":["first tevarin war","second tevarin war"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b9933d31-89ec-4428-b7aa-0e81c79751c4"},
{"id":"tevarin-purge","gp":"R6dWB877Nn","t":"Tevarin Purge","k":"history","c":["Tevarin","History"],"x":"The Tevarin Purge was a movement sparked in the immediate aftermath of the [Second Tevarin War]((https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/bE3rPrz3Pv-second-tevarin-war)) (2603-2610), in which the [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) voluntarily severed connection with their culture. They destroyed records, denounced the Rijoran code, tore down temples, and obliterated other aspects of the civilization that had previously defined and ultimately failed them. Most Tevarin abandoned their homeworld and assimilated into the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and a tiny minority disappeared into unknown parts of space. Most preserved records about the former Tevarin way of life only exist thanks to [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) interference. Beginning in the early 30th century, there has been a growing movement among Tevarin to reconnect with their former culture and language.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/34d53c84-3862-4c55-8199-1a38c9cc4511"},
{"id":"tevarin-human-first-contact","gp":"Vgg7YGkaEw","t":"Tevarin-Human First Contact","k":"history","c":["Tevarin","History","Human"],"x":"[Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) first made contact with one another shortly after Dr. Kellar Lench of the New Horizons Research Institute discovered a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) into the Elysium system. Observing signs that the system was occupied by a technologically advanced civilization, he dispatched a research drone to gather data without disturbing its inhabitants and found a spacefaring people living on [Elysium IV](gp:VarAXY2zy2). Initial diplomatic attempts by the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) first contact team proved unsuccessful. The Tevarin, facing an overpopulation problem due to their lack of [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) technology, soon attacked the invaders in an effort to take Human colonies in neighboring systems for themselves, sparking the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541 - 2546).","g":["united planets of earth","first tevarin war"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6fcb5807-5410-4b33-b1d7-031623c49c99"},
{"id":"thusuung-i","gp":"bZk149jv4B","t":"Th.us'ūng I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Th.us'ūng I is the closest planet to the sun of the [Th.us'ūng system](gp:V8WeExnJge), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A terrestrial planet, it has a thin mantle that partially exposes its iron core. The [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government prohibits commercial mining on Th.us'ūng I, and instead utilizes it as a testing area for mining technology that is designed for hostile environments. In addition, some major Houses have special dispensations to conduct related experiments here under the direct supervision of government representatives.","g":["th.us'uung i","th.us'uung system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/04884893-759d-4ed4-bf0b-c1b7c1f6cbd4"},
{"id":"thusuung-system","gp":"V8WeExnJge","t":"Th.us'ūng System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The Th.us'ūng system is a planetary system in the Xi'an Empire, consisting of a G-type main sequence star, three terrestrial planets, one gas giant, one dwarf planet, and one asteroid belt. Discovered in MXY III.802 (SEY 2483) by a scanning drone owned by the [Xi'an Service (Pō't.ōngp.ū)](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ), the system was primarily used by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government as a testbed for experimental [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) technology. In MXY III.838 (SEY 2530), [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) navjumper Kathryn Segovia discovered the Th.us'ūng-[Baker](gp:Rz2KGkv13N) jump point and sold its location to the terraforming company Gaia Planet Services (GPS). In order to offset the cost of this purchase, GPS chose not to report the jump point to the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN). When their surveyors landed on the [third world](gp:bo1wy7GZNr) from the system's sun, they were quickly captured by the Xi'an, thus kicking off the events that would start the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (MXY III.838 - III.1044 / SEY 2530 - 2793).","g":["th.us'uung system","xi'an system","perry line"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9f531845-31a0-4630-a189-c0238ce574e9"},
{"id":"the-ark","gp":"0qnNMX5lAk","t":"The Ark","k":"place","c":["Culture","Human","Locations"],"x":"The Ark is a vast library and archive station located in the [Tayac system](gp:RAXX4N3w4B), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The largest library and archive in the UEE, the Ark houses records, curated information, and artifacts pertaining to the accumulated knowledge of all known spacefaring civilizations. \n\nThe initial concept for the Ark was presented to the [UEE Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) in SEY 2794 by then-Diplomatic Secretary [Marshall Leon](gp:bZwQBJmZxE) as a neutral information repository for the benefit of all cultures and civilizations. It was approved the same year and completed in 2800. The Ark Galactapedia and the Ark Starmap are its two most utilized resources.","g":["library","space station","ark galactapedia","ark starmap","marshall leon","uee institute","uee space station","tayac system","uee culture"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b98e3a5c-0719-4c75-af01-4cb5cb100066"},
{"id":"the-claw","gp":"0n9vkMLlzd","t":"The Claw","k":"culture","c":["Music","Human"],"x":"The Claw is a [Human](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/category/human) band based out of Saisei (Centauri III) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), credited with popularizing [S-pop](gp:bE3rkJvqJ7). In 2932, the band performed a stylized cover of [Clover's](gp:box5qg83aL) \"Moonlight\" on [Spectrum](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galacapedia/article/VaZwen9E2Q-spectrum) show [Terra, Show Me the Music!](gp:RwZBwjdr5X) They went on to hold the number one single on multiple music charts for six weeks. Many other S-pop bands signed to major labels in the wake of this success. The band went on indefinite hiatus in 2941.","g":["s-pop","saisei","centauri iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f6163e35-fbe0-4bdf-b41a-fe51b7e26571"},
{"id":"the-coil","gp":"VlNP3xpMx4","t":"The Coil","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Coil is an energy phenomenon that exists in the unusually dense [asteroid cluster](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/asteroid-cluster) that closely orbits the white dwarf [Odin](gp:RX3jMavYGk). Scientists speculate that the Coil phenomenon was created in the aftermath of the star Odin's collapse into a white dwarf. Sometimes called a storm in space, the Coil manifests as distortion energy and electricity bolts that jump from asteroid to asteroid. Lightning from the Coil has been known to destroy spacecraft.","g":["odin system","asteroid cluster","unclaimed asteroid cluster"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/32a96571-e000-4dc8-8b8e-45559bde7289"},
{"id":"the-dark","gp":"VyvYXnM2Pl","t":"The Dark","k":"history","c":["Xi'an","History"],"x":"The Dark (MXY II.1706 - II.1824; SEY 1305 - 1457) was a period at the end of the Second [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) Age in which the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) had no ruling Imperial House. Due to the destruction caused by the Spirit Wars (MXY II.961 - II.1735; SEY 351 - 1342), the Xi'an were unable to unify and select a house to succeed the destroyed [Imperial House Xy.ō](gp:RXlXBrm5o1). Armed conflict between Houses and assassination of political rivals once again became commonplace. The Dark ended when [House Kr.ē](gp:R6v8OZOrP5) was selected as the Third Imperial House in MXY III.0 (SEY 1457)","g":["kr'thak","spirit wars","third imperial age","house xy.ō","xi'an empire","second imperial age","eras","house kr.ē"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2b1c26eb-23a5-4b78-bc68-d2c746288047"},
{"id":"the-gathering","gp":"V7gM7yNAeK","t":"The Gathering","k":"faction","c":["Banu","Politics"],"x":"The Gathering is an irregular meeting of [Essosouli](gp:R6v8kxEPBD) held on Bacchus II to discuss issues that have the potential to affect all [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). Essosouli generally meet two to three times per year, though rarely they will go multiple years without meeting. At each Gathering, legal and trade issues are debated and codified.","g":["banu sociopolitics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2e65947f-465a-4502-8dc3-87f68c7aedb1"},
{"id":"the-great-divide","gp":"VyvYA5qmqX","t":"The Great Divide (Xi'an Civil War)","k":"history","c":["Xi'an","History","Military"],"x":"The Great Divide (the Xi'an Civil War) took place from 20044 to 19770 BCE. The outcome of millennia of inter-[House](gp:box9JmxvWL) conflicts and complex webs of enmity and allyship, it began when the last daughter of House Kl.ō attempted defection to [House Uai'i](gp:RMXyBdkAQA). Hostilities between the Houses grew deadly, and Houses [Chii](gp:0qnNZOo3lk) and [Ru'a](gp:V3qgaLK82W) were compelled to join a now system-wide civil war. The war concluded when members of [House Kl.o](gp:V8gJ62qO81) sabotaged RyiXy'ans (Hyoton III) network of antique weather satellites, intending to assassinate the leadership of Houses Uai'i, Ru'a, and Chii during tentative peace talks. This inadvertently triggered a chain reaction that destroyed RyiXy'ans atmosphere, rendering the planet uninhabitable and killing millions. Survivors evacuated to the colony world Ka'ua (Hyoton IV). The events of the Great Divide forced the Xi'an to reassess their culture. The calendar was reset to I.0 (19668 BCE), the [Civil Service](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ) was established, a new capital was established on Ka'ua, and Ru'a was elected to serve as the first [Imperial](gp:VyvYA5qmqX) House.","g":["xi'an civil war","house ru'a","house kl.ō","house chii","house uai'i","ryixy'an","hyoton iii","the great divide","xi'an empire","wars"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f372e2e0-0c71-431e-a0bb-86b95cca9747"},
{"id":"inhabitants-of-genesis-ii","gp":"01dWXY9edJ","t":"The Inhabitants of Genesis II","k":"culture","c":["Civilizations"],"x":"Genesis II, a richly biodiverse world, is home to at least five species that have evolved to varying stages of development. Two such groups, an ocean-dwelling, cephalopod group and a land-dwelling, avian-reptoid group, are of special interest to observing scientists. Factions of the octopoids have been making incursions onto land, and have engaged in deadly skirmishes with some of the avian-reptoids. Many observers believe this will lead to war. Ethicists, scientists, and academics are embroiled in a debate on whether or not to stop this war before it results in the annihilation of one or more of the groups involved. The [Fair Chance Act](gp:RXlXmnaYGP) prohibits outside interference in this development.","g":["inhabitants of genesis ii","genesis ii","fair chance act"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2da62dce-1481-4b92-b608-be46265cda37"},
{"id":"the-outsiders","gp":"V7dLljjOeL","t":"The Outsiders","k":"faction","c":["Human","Organizations","Culture"],"x":"The Outsiders, also known as the Sun's Eye Fellowship, are a religious cult established by [Dr. Marcus Fayel](gp:Rw1k2w51XZ) that has occupied [Mya (Leir II)](gp:RxnqNaGr8Q) since the early 2800s. While Fayel oversaw the [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) of Mya, he cultivated a group of followers and organized an eventual armed takeover of the planet; a feat he achieved in 2812. The Outsiders believe that in order to maintain purity, they must reject all trappings of the modern world, especially the overwhelming consumer culture of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). They say that in order to attain a pure state, one must embrace self-reflection without the smothering distraction of potential societal judgment. The sun is the ultimate example of purity, and is a key part of the meditation necessary on the journey to purity.","g":["outsiders (religion)","sun's eye fellowship","religion","human religion"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d929d6f1-34f1-4ee3-a8ad-e65efec9c0b8"},
{"id":"the-red-god-nexus-v","gp":"0jGayj2BMW","t":"The Red God (Nexus V)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Nexus V is a gas giant in the [Nexus system](gp:RWoj8pnGma), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the most distant planet from its sun. Nicknamed \"The Red God\" by locals, its swirling, stormy atmosphere is a mix of swirling shades of red with streaks of dark brown. Although the origin of the name is unknown, the prevailing hypothesis is that it originated with Sang Gestas, an outlaw gang on Lago that believed the planet possessed supernatural powers.","g":["the red god","nexus v","nexus system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2c1fb77c-46a4-4899-94cb-ac29cafea73d"},
{"id":"theresa-branaugh","gp":"VpMeGzBPyz","t":"Theresa Branaugh","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Theresa Branaugh (2835 - 2873?) was a geologist, surveyor, and explorer best known for her unofficial discovery of the [Branaugh system](gp:VJX9mlar4n) some time before 2877. Like many other explorers, she dreamed of discovering a new planetary system, a goal to which she dedicated all of her time. In order to fund her expeditions, she would regularly borrow from loan sharks, which sometimes led to her fleeing to other systems when repayment was due. Her friends reported her missing in 2873 after she failed to return from an expedition to the [Chronos system](gp:RvlQZKy95l). Her body was found four years later in a remote cave on [Branaugh II](gp:RL6524Kx6L) by explorer [Desmond Fell](gp:RX3dlQ5KON), near the wreckage of her spacecraft. Although the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) did not identify her killer, they were able to determine that her ship was shot down by someone who was using the area as a hideout. Fell named the system in her honor.","g":["branaugh system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5f957729-7161-4c57-acfd-95f2b20033c3"},
{"id":"thermal-shielding","gp":"R4ZG6lLak5","t":"Thermal Shielding","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Thermal shielding is a general term for manufactured technology capable of artificially sustaining life in extreme temperature environments. The term can refer to anything from enhanced spacesuit technology that allows EVA work, to the combination of electromagnetic shielding and hull plating necessary for spacecraft to operate near stars or other extreme sources of temperature. Thermal shielding is generally capable of blocking heat, radioactivity and light to varying degrees.","g":["thermal shielding "],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c081fd5a-2fe1-41b2-9739-b0bbad13e205"},
{"id":"thermyte-concern","gp":"bZwQ6pDza6","t":"Thermyte Concern","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Thermyte Concern is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) multidisciplinary manufacturer of mining equipment, personal and spacecraft-mounted weaponry, and munitions. Originally founded as a demolition and mining equipment company, Thermyte expanded its reach to weapons and missile warheads in the late 2800s. Its mining division produces some of the largest and most advanced mining heads currently available on the civilian market.","g":["mining equipment manufacturer","demolitions company","asura","ferron iii","weapons manufacturer","munitions manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3cb59741-3041-44e3-ab73-e755f4d72d61"},
{"id":"third-imperial-age","gp":"R4ZejoYNEY","t":"Third Imperial Age","k":"history","c":["Xi'an","History"],"x":"The Third [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) Age, ruled by [House Kr.ē](gp:R6v8OZOrP5), is the [Xi'an Empire's (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) current dynasty. It began in II.1824 (SEY 1457) with the selection of U.e'o se Kr.ē as the new Emperor, roughly a century after the Kr'thak's assassination of [House Xy.ō](gp:RXlXBrm5o1). During this era, the Xi'an formally ended hostilities with the [Kr'thak](gp:RxNxDYkqzz), made first contact with [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4), [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO), and [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), and established diplomatic relationships and opened channels of trade with Banu and Humans. The current Emperor, [T.uēng se Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo), was one of the signatories of the [Akari-Kr.ē Treaty](gp:bE3rKrl5z6) (III.1040 / SEY 2789), the first nonaggression pact between Humans and Xi'an, an instrumental step in the eventual end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (III.838 - III.1044 / SEY 2530 - 2793). Because he has no heirs, the Third Imperial Age will end upon his death or abdication, and the Fourth Imperial Age will begin with the selection of a new Imperial [House](gp:box9JmxvWL).","g":["house kr.ē","eras"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/155e6f6c-de0b-4bec-ba4d-af1a76c67773"},
{"id":"third-sister-kilian-iii","gp":"V8WWy3rgQx","t":"Third Sister (Kilian III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"The Third Sister (Kilian III) is a protoplanet in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that orbits the system's sun in the L5 Lagrange point of the hot Jupiter [First Sister (Kilian I)](gp:VlMMagKEzd). Glittering patches of ice can be found dotted across its surface. Because the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) utilizes the Third Sister as a testing ground for weapons, landing is prohibited without proper military clearance.","g":["third sister","kilian iii","kilian system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","three sisters"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/afc59834-d990-405a-ae91-72c59e2065a6"},
{"id":"thorshu-grey","gp":"R5poqwA6aX","t":"Thorshu Grey","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"# THORSHU GREY\nThe thorshu grey is an omnivorous, six-eyed crustacean indigenous to the cold southern oceans of Terra (Terra III) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Considered a delicacy for its tender, sweet meat, it is also a popular aquarium pet, and is one of the more commonly seen animals on shipboard aquatic enclosures.\n\n# DESCRIPTION\nThorshu have long, bright orange-red colored carapaces that cover their soft inner bodies, curved upwards into a narrow crescent. They have two dactyls and six walking legs, tipped in sky blue with mottled cream accents. The dark, barnacle-like lumps that grow on their carapaces and front claws may be eyespots, evolved to trick potential predators away from the thorshu's most vulnerable spots. Thorshu that have more eyespots than others have more success in mating. On average, they grow to between 10 and 20 cm long, and live for around 20 years.\n\n# BEHAVIOR AND ECOLOGY\nThough they are largely solitary, thorshu demonstrate complex social behavior in the wild. Upon meeting one another for the first time they engage in ritualized fighting, and ignore one another upon subsequent meetings. They are highly intelligent, able to recognize individual thorshu by scent and color, even if they have not re-encountered each other for several years. Captive thorshu have been known to escape their containers if not provided with stimulating enough environments.\n\nIn their lifetime, they can breed as many as 30 times. Eggs are laid in burrows dug under seabed rocks. The offspring spend the first few months of their life as microscopic organisms. They molt into their adult form at roughly four months, molting again multiple times until reaching their final size in their third year.\n\n# COMMERCIAL FOOD\nOn Terra (Terra III), thorshu are commercially bred and raised for their meat. Thousands of tons of whole flash-frozen thorshu are shipped across the UEE every year and sold to high-end restaurants. The leg meat is especially prized for its complex flavor, and is often served hot and dipped in a drawn butter and oza sauce. On Terra, where the thorshu is a conventional catch for local fishers, breaded and fried thorshu claws are a relatively common street food, especially in Quasi.\n\n# POPULAR CULTURE\nThanks to its color, size, and tendency to stay in the open, the thorshu is a favorite denizen of cold saltwater aquariums. It became a fashionable pet in the 27th century after being used as the model for the sidekick character Waka Grey in the children's show Clawsome. However, its tendency to break out of insecure enclosures and attack brightly colored objects such as decorative glassware put an end to the trend shortly after the show's final season. It is recommended only for experienced hobbyists.\n\nThe United Empire of Earth Navy 78th Bomb Squadron, known for its part in [Operation Unilateral Force](gp:bBp64B7G79), is nicknamed the \"Thundering Thorshu.\"","g":["terra iii","terra","pets","crustaceans"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/228226e9-a16b-4fdf-bc30-51a662901cff"},
{"id":"thrust","gp":"V3GP35zJQW","t":"Thrust","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Thrust is a nervous system stimulant that provides its user with a massive burst of energy, increased sociability, euphoria, and heightened tactile sensitivity. Rumored to have been developed as the base of an energy drink and then abandoned, its true makers are unknown, and it first became available on black markets as a party drug. It is taken via a small patch lined with nano-needles that puncture the skin over the spine to provide a quick pathway for the drug to enter the nervous system. Side effects include the risk of heart attack, deadly dehydration, seizures, rambling speech, flushed skin, and excessive perspiration.","g":["stimulant","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/77b740e2-c568-4114-bfc1-799c548ecc51"},
{"id":"tiber-belt-alpha","gp":"VDza9J272q","t":"Tiber Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Tiber belt alpha is the only asteroid belt of the [Tiber system](gp:RMNLm97EDj). Located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), the densely-packed belt is primarily used by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) for resource extraction. Before the [United Empire of Earth Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) withdrew from the system they strategically laid mine fields throughout the belt, increasing the danger of the already hazardous area.","g":["asteroid belt","tiber system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/95c22c12-3c0b-43dd-91d1-e04be76a0160"},
{"id":"tiber-i","gp":"VpMyzJM9DN","t":"Tiber I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tiber I is the first planet from the sun of the [Tiber system](gp:RMNLm97EDj) in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). A small, dense world, it has a naturally-occurring oxygen-nitrogen atmosphere with a high concentration of carbon dioxide. While the air is technically breathable, it is difficult to become accustomed to, and conditions are hot enough that few people elected to live there before the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) [overtook](gp:0OaBY5pGrq) the Tiber system in SEY 2736.","g":["tiber system","habitable","habitable planet","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/80cf84ae-45bc-4547-8573-3124db417b33"},
{"id":"tiber-system","gp":"RMNLm97EDj","t":"Tiber System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Tiber system is a planetary system in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), and was formerly a part of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE). Discovered in SEY 2474 during [Project Far Star](gp:0qnNAD6YKa), it was a sparsely populated mining system until 2681, when the [destruction](gp:RWwZDmxaXP) of [Dell Township](gp:RkZ9mGOpD4) in the neighboring system of [Orion](gp:VlMpwMky6d) sparked a period of rapid military buildup. In 2732, the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) launched a mass invasion on Tiber. A years-long [siege](gp:0OaBY5pGrq) followed that lasted until 2736 when UEE forces abandoned the system. It is now home to vast encampments of Vanduul.","g":["vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cf83a665-682d-483b-a127-6c3640b3ff64"},
{"id":"tide","gp":"RXlXOpwG6k","t":"Tide","k":"faction","c":["Organizations","Politics","Human"],"x":"Tide was an anti-Messer resistance movement responsible for airing footage of the [Massacre of Garron II](gp:01dWeqnMr1) to the people of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), thus catalyzing the events that led to the [anti-Messer Revolution](gp:bE3rKa32P7). Cells of Tide were distributed on most [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-inhabited planets in and around the UEE, especially [Rytif (Bremen II)](gp:R5pA7q691W), [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), and [Tohil III](gp:0OD1qEgJdN). Their command structure gave each cell individual autonomy while limiting their knowledge of other cells so the organization could not be compromised should a cell be lost. Over the years, the Tide claimed responsibility for staging protests, distributing anti-Messer information, and attempting to emancipate political prisoners. The full extent of their operations were made public after the fall of the Messers. They managed to recruit members of the UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) including [Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y), documented atrocities committed by the Messers and even coordinated with Xi'an sympathizers to smuggle political activists through [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) space. Tide's contacts within [SSN/CAtv](gp:0QxYwPK88l) helped them interrupt Spectrum broadcasts on 11 April 2792, sparking a direct coup against [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Linton Messer XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq).","g":["tide (activist group)","massacre of garron ii","anti-messer revolution"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9e9ea2e3-fdd2-441e-9088-0cb9dfeff0b9"},
{"id":"titan","gp":"V7gMyBEKv3","t":"Titan","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Titan is a variant of the [Avenger](gp:ReJanvr73r) patrol ship developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). Designers stripped much of the standard Avenger's rear cabin to create a dedicated cargo space. This additional capacity allows the variant to be used in a support role by the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN) and by independent operators who prefer to operate a freighter that carries a weapons and armor package by default. A limited edition, the Titan Renegade, was created by Aegis in conjunction with the makers of the flight-sim *[Arena Commander](gp:VyvY5LQXd6).*","g":["aegis dynamics","titan renegade","original systems","avenger series","light freight","freight","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bf6135d5-1779-46a9-987e-695dc26ecce8"},
{"id":"titan-sol-6a","gp":"bmGdx5EdaK","t":"Titan (Sol 6a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Titan (Sol 6a) is a moon of [Saturn (Sol VI)](gp:0jGpvn8AOW), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The largest of Saturn's moons, its nitrogen-methane atmosphere is denser than that of [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB). Titan is dotted with lakes and rivers of liquid hydrocarbons, and its climate has created surface features such as dunes, seas, and canyons, all shaped by a methane cycle rather than a water cycle.","g":["titan","sol 6a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f0d3c06a-0d6e-467d-8bca-0e7a720a3678"},
{"id":"titania-sol-7d","gp":"RX3oyQPamZ","t":"Titania (Sol 7d)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Titania (Sol 7d) is a moon of [Uranus (Sol VII)](gp:0rxOX3eKQ2), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The largest of Uranus' moons, its surface is scored with enormous canyons and scarps. Under its surface is a mantle of slushy ice that sits over a solid rocky core. It has a tenuous atmosphere of carbon dioxide.","g":["titania","sol 7d","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0ad6899a-b491-4e35-ae27-c99dadff5551"},
{"id":"titania-terraforming","gp":"RkGerKq6eN","t":"Titania Terraforming","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Titania Terraforming was a [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) company most notable for their failure to terraform [Uriel (Oberon II)](gp:RL673Gxjjv) in the unclaimed [Oberon system](gp:VYLdlgMqop). Founded in 2333, it was primarily contracted by larger conglomerates for piecework until it successfully placed the winning bid for the coordinates to the newly-discovered [Oberon](gp:VYLdlgMqop)-[Nul](gp:VgEnlpqyJ9) [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY). Since so much of their budget was spent on the contract, the company chose to offset future operating costs by selling low-price plots of land on the yet-to-be-terraformed Oberon II. Thousands of people signed on and headed to Oberon, not knowing that the neutron star at the heart of the system made terraforming unlikely at best. When Titania Terraforming failed to make the planet livable, they abandoned the people they had sold land to and immediately folded.","g":["terraforming company","human company","oberon system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5542c121-15e0-434e-bedc-4d7eaf111edc"},
{"id":"titus","gp":"0dXZG3ZBOw","t":"Titus","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Titus is the most populous city on Selene (Vega III), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and the seat of the planet's government. Titus was once a center of commerce, but it experienced a sharp economic and population drop after the [Fall of Virgil](gp:box5moyeoZ) in 2737. While the city center is developed, there are abandoned construction projects on the outskirts that pose a continuous hazard to the populace. Recently, outside interests have begun purchasing this land in hopes of redeveloping it.","g":["selene","vega iii","uee city","cities"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/08d97604-256c-4e36-8ffa-dc0dbb17f756"},
{"id":"titus-costigan","gp":"VDz7Be7E33","t":"Titus Costigan","k":"people","c":["Human","People"],"x":"Titus Costigan (2909 - present) is the CEO of Esrua Industries, director of the nonprofit Better Together Foundation, and eldest son of former [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Kelos Costigan](gp:VJOzBxdJ28) of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Running as a [Universalist](gp:VDo6qOgLx9), he was one of five final candidates for the office of Imperator in 2950. His platform included promises to increase economic activity by relaxing regulations on businesses, increase funding for the [Militia Mobilization Initiative](gp:RkZ96m89Jm), and improve transparency on how [Synthworld](gp:RLMmAnr4gj) funds are being spent. In the leadup to the final election, multiple attack ads were released by an unknown party tying Costigan to a multi-system drug syndicate. Costigan's campaign refused to respond.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/67024f9f-b8bb-44ea-8e90-b8dfb2be0071"},
{"id":"tohil-belt-alpha","gp":"Rw1r2Jx4qX","t":"Tohil Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Tohil belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the [Tohil system](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Dense with asteroids, travel conditions through it are dangerous enough that major mining companies in the UEE have declined to begin operations there. Smugglers and other outlaws who are especially skilled at piloting and navigation have been known to hide in the belt, but most choose not to risk their ships and lives and give it a wide berth.","g":["tohil system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3e6c318a-2bcd-432f-b1eb-edee0f6f755e"},
{"id":"tohil-i","gp":"RX35MEAmYq","t":"Tohil I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tohil I is the innermost planet of the [Tohil system](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is tidally locked to its sun. Close proximity to the star has turned the day side of Tohil I into an ocean of lava. Surveys indicate that the molten rock extends deep within the planet, nearly reaching its core. As it stretches near the solar terminator, the lava becomes increasingly sluggish until it eventually solidifies.","g":["tohil system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9887ef2d-d0e1-4c8f-818b-adc96c69904b"},
{"id":"tohil-ii","gp":"V3GBEA2mpj","t":"Tohil II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tohil II is a planet in the [Tohil system](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the second world from its sun. A mesoplanet, its mantle has been stripped away over many millennia due to intense solar winds. During the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792), smugglers would sometimes hide in the shadow of Tohil II if they came too close to being caught by government agents. It is rumored that there were at one point dozens of smuggler drops hidden away on the planet's surface, some of which still remain in active use.","g":["tohil system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c73578e4-1440-4a7d-8e97-e4dbeeb75e6e"},
{"id":"tohil-iii","gp":"0OD1qEgJdN","t":"Tohil III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tohil III is a planet in the [Tohil system](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and is the third world from its sun. Naturally habitable, it is an ocean world that supports massive botanical biomasses that sit atop the water and create floating islands. Smugglers frequently utilized Tohil III as a hideout and drop spot throughout the later years of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792). In 2789, Senator [Terrence Akari](gp:RL6ZQLwnko) of [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) and Emperor [T.uēng se Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo) of the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) chose Tohil III as their meeting spot to negotiate what would become the first peace treaty between [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj).","g":["tohil system","habitable planet","habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/195088cd-bb2c-4463-8697-c3f94454e1ec"},
{"id":"tohil-iv","gp":"0dX15LWpkp","t":"Tohil IV","k":"place","c":["People"],"x":"Tohil IV is a planet in the [Tohil system](gp:0Ql5X15Kr9), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is the fourth world from its sun. A massive super-Earth, Tohil IV exerts a strong gravitational pull that attracts frequent meteor and comet strikes. Deep craters pockmark its surface, some of which were utilized by anti-Messer revolutionaries during the final years of the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (2546 - 2792) as clandestine transfer spots for political refugees fleeing to safety.","g":["tohil system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bf4b8e44-1f2c-4a12-a46e-5c79ef1e54b9"},
{"id":"tohil-system","gp":"0Ql5X15Kr9","t":"Tohil System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"The Tohil system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that consists of a K-type main sequence star, two terrestrial planets, a mesoplanet, and a super-Earth. Discovered in SEY 2716 by smugglers Oisha Suen and Aadya Firmino, it was added to the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) in 2719 when the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) located a jump point to the system from [Oya](gp:0KxGow1ly4). Named Tohil after an ancient [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) war deity, it became a popular smuggling route after the UEE relocated its military forces to the [Castra system](gp:R4jxkAd8El). In 2789, Senator [Terrence Akari](gp:RL6ZQLwnko) of [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) and Emperor [T.uēng se Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo) met on [Tohil III](gp:0OD1qEgJdN) in secret and negotiated the first peace treaty between Humans and [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj). The [Akari-Kr.ē Treaty](gp:bE3rKrl5z6) contributed to the growing instability of the [Messer](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) government and helped bring an end to the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (2530 - 2793).","g":["uee system","perry line"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a4f828c1-3dbf-40ea-806d-1dd8145c9b9e"},
{"id":"toja-terra-2a","gp":"0Kx85no5JD","t":"Toja (Terra 2a)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Locations"],"x":"Toja is a natural satellite of [Pike (Terra II)](gp:Rvl7EggdAr) in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Tidally locked, its far side is heavily scarred with frequent meteor impacts from space debris. The near side of Toja is dotted with auxiliary service centers built to support the mining operations on Pike.","g":["toja","terra 2a","terra system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","pike moon","terra ii moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9c5c2f81-1e4e-4b7f-b0c1-7853e50d2b97"},
{"id":"tomb-tiber-ii","gp":"R5pxGYd9w7","t":"Tomb (Tiber II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tomb (Tiber II) is the second planet from the sun of the [Tiber system](gp:RMNLm97EDj) in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). An arid, desert world, it was once a sparsely-settled mining colony operated by settlers from the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE). In SEY 2734, halfway through the [Siege of Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq), the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) broke through UEE defenses, dropped [Harvester](gp:0n1MYzOkG7) on the planet's surface, and established encampments. The Navy responded by conducting countless bombing operations that ultimately failed to evict the Vanduul and left the surface of Tomb a cratered wreck.","g":["tomb","tiber ii","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","tiber system","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9f75d3e6-9ed5-49f1-bd86-6d39e1bc7883"},
{"id":"torpedo-burrito","gp":"0jGGy3zqle","t":"Torpedo Burrito","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Torpedo Burrito is a chain of vending machines and food stalls based in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that serves various fillings wrapped in large flour based tortillas. It debuted in 2878 as a part of the Bevic Group's push to expand their range of vending machines to include hot food. Now available in most populated areas of the UEE, Torpedo Burrito's line of flavors includes Carna-ritas, Shrimp Typhoon, Madras Asada, Strog-N-Off, PPC (Pollo, Peas, and Carrots), Cheddar Ham, and Locked-on Lentil.","g":["food retail","food company","bevic group"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5f06c05d-7a63-4fac-aa60-f5ba1bbb6fb3"},
{"id":"torral-aggregate","gp":"0j46Lzl8xm","t":"Torral Aggregate (Aoō'nu se T.or'al)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Military","Xi'an"],"x":"Torral Aggregate (Aoō'nu se T.or'al) is a [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) weapons manufacturer and [House](gp:box9JmxvWL) with a history of weapons production under auspice of the [Emperor](gp:VaZwmlmPQo) that dates back thousands of years. They produce a significant number of weapons and related systems for the Xi'an military. In recent years, they have begun to export products adapted for [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) use. Weapons available for sale directly to Humans include the Yeng'tu laser repeater (*ro'thli* Yeng'tu), which was first mounted on the [San'tok.yāi](gp:RWolyEwlxZ) fighter, and the Kahix missile launcher (*ro'noy.ithly'ehung* Kē'hith).","g":["torral aggregate","aoō'nu se t.or'al","ka'ua","hyoton iii","xi'an house","weapons manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bab9f221-ad4d-4943-bec1-0204288e7b01"},
{"id":"toshi-aaron","gp":"0NjkMMlGXD","t":"Toshi Aaron","k":"people","c":["People","Human","Exploration"],"x":"Toshi Aaron (SEY 2802 - SEY 2929) was a navjumper best known for discovering the [Stanton system](gp:RX3lKBA3dq) in SEY 2851. Born in the [Magnus system](gp:RWolrNa1Ge), she dreamed of discovering a new jump point since she was a small child. Lacking the funds to commit to her passion of exploring the stars full time, she would take high-risk, high-paying jobs fishing Magnus' oceans, then spend the off-season hunting for jump points. Her hard work paid off in 2851, when she detected an anomaly that would prove to be a jump point to a new system. Aaron reported her discovery to the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) government and requested that it be named Stanton in honor of her late brother.","g":["stanton system","human people"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cca8b39d-adff-4f4e-a217-a8d1e7104014"},
{"id":"touvoni-aiya-charon3a","gp":"01LL8pGq74","t":"Touvoni/Aiya (Charon 3a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Touvoni (Charon 3a) is the moon of [Charon III](gp:RkGGMvDpoz), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), known as Aiya in [Dellin](gp:0OaBKD9Kwk). After [Tarquin Klast](gp:0dQ4mGDJYd) was elected governor of Dellin in 2944, he passed a popular decree renaming the moon to differentiate the values of Dellin from the other states on Charon III. All other states on the planet still call the moon Touvoni.","g":["touvoni","aiya","charon 3a","charon iii moon","charon system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c85289fe-89fd-4b2c-a281-c4418ea871e5"},
{"id":"tradeway","gp":"R56n9MKzAX","t":"Tradeway","k":"faction","c":["Government","Commerce"],"x":"Tradeways are ports of entry maintained by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) for the purpose of exchanging goods with other civilizations such as the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) or the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). UEE tradeways are maintained by a combination of [Human](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) customs officials and representatives of the bordering nation. A major tradeway with the Banu Protectorate is located in the Corel System, the point through which the majority of legally processed goods transit between [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) and Humans.","g":["uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c40cd01f-66f4-4469-bdc3-e94863f212a2"},
{"id":"tram","gp":"bBzdDMvNEy","t":"Tram","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Human"],"x":"Tram is the largest city on Asura (Ferron III), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). It was the financial and cultural center of Asura's thriving economy until the mining crash in the early 2800s caused widespread economic collapse. Many of its buildings were abandoned as the majority of its population fled, and have been allowed to deteriorate. Today, drinking water shortages are common in some areas due to the failure of old infrastructure and source contamination issues. Pollution poses a continual hazard to those unwilling or unable to relocate. There has been a recent effort among some architecture historians to preserve some of the grand old buildings erected during the city's heyday.","g":["asura","ferron iii","cities","uee city"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4a06b7df-7aaf-4a51-8222-73576a00acba"},
{"id":"transitionalist-party","gp":"0OaylwDmvv","t":"Transitionalist Party","k":"faction","c":["Human","Politics"],"x":"The Transitionalist party is one of the three major political parties in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Formed on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa), the core ideologies of the Transitionalist party support measures that decentralize UEE governmental power, raise government spending towards education and the sciences, increase taxes on the wealthy, and fund exploration. Many Transitionalists support moving the capital of the UEE away from Earth (Sol III) to Terra.","g":["uee political party","universalist party"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b06e7d47-f65d-421a-8e83-ffdfc18909d1"},
{"id":"travelers-day","gp":"VYLa6BEL64","t":"Traveler's Day","k":"culture","c":["Culture","Human","Holidays"],"x":"Traveler's Day is an annual holiday observed by the [Church of the Journey](gp:V8WGP6zjXe) on January 1st. It originated in the Croshaw system in 2905 when a small gathering of Journeymen who had grown up together convened to exchange their experiences over the previous year. They repeated their actions the following year, and the next, wherever they were, thus spreading the practice until it became tradition. Traveler's Day activities include storytelling, a potluck feast, games, and a 20 km walk known as the Pilgrimage that begins at midnight local time. At the end of the walk, stories are swapped until sunrise. The largest Traveler's Day gathering in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) occurs in New Arden on Cestulus (Davien II), attracting thousands of visitors annually.","g":["travelers day","uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ba6547e9-2e9a-4e37-ab4a-61e25098f03c"},
{"id":"tribunal","gp":"bZwq5Nr5EL","t":"Tribunal","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The Tribunal is an executive governing body in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). It is made up of a High-Secretary, responsible for infrastructure; High-Command, a three-person position responsible for managing each of the military branches; and a High-Advocate, responsible for law enforcement. The Tribunal was initially formed alongside the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) but was eliminated when Ivar Messer I first took power. The Tribunal was reinstated by the UEE Senate and [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl)[Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y) in 2792.","g":["united empire of earth","human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8f870786-3f49-48b7-b3f9-a8f44cfeb629"},
{"id":"trident-attack-systems","gp":"RxNxl74OQM","t":"Trident Attack Systems","k":"company","c":["Weapons","Commerce","Human"],"x":"Trident Attack Systems is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) company that manufactures energy weapons. Founded in 2803, the company's original lineup of weapons was predominantly ballistic focused, but when they scaled up their operations in 2821 they pivoted to focus exclusively on energy weapons as a cost-saving measure. The Arame laser beam is considered the company's current flagship product.","g":["weapons manufacturer","weapon component manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/59c58d70-4589-473d-9aad-87eacd791733"},
{"id":"triggerfish","gp":"0rxrqgzgP6","t":"Triggerfish","k":"history","c":["Holidays","Human"],"x":"Triggerfish is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) holiday celebrated annually in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) on 01 April. Those who observe it play pranks and jokes on one another or participate in hoaxes, shouting \"Triggerfish!\" once a jape is complete. Though the holiday has origins stretching as far back as the 16th century, it first began to be called Triggerfish in the 2600s, when it became tradition for residents of Borea (Magnus II) to try and convince visitors that a secret fourth planet named \"Triggerfish\" existed in the Magnus system. Some outlaws would give victims coordinates to the planet, only to ambush them once they arrived. To put an end to this dangerous practice, the UEE launched an information campaign refuting the claim that Triggerfish existed. This spread the name outside its system of origin. Triggerfish became a nickname for a gullible person, and the name became the most common way to refer to the holiday.","g":["uee holiday"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dad44cb3-1b8b-4ec2-b270-ce71fa9c95c4"},
{"id":"trise-cordial","gp":"R9vGWkxw9x","t":"Trise Cordial","k":"culture","c":["Food and Beverages","Human"],"x":"# TRISE CORDIAL\n\nTrise Cordial is an herb liqueur 55% alcohol by volume (ABV) adapted from the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) drink *otisau falu* for safe [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) consumption. Introduced to the market in 2789, it has an herbal flavor profile with pungent notes of salammoniac. The original Banu version of the drink is distilled from both water and ammonia-based herbs grown on Trise I, and is poisonous to Humans.  \n\n# FLAVOR\n\nTrise Cordial has a strong, characteristic taste: bitter and herbal with a sweet undercurrent as it contacts the palate, followed by salammoniac with a hint of pine upon swallowing. It is often served at room temperature in a cordial glass as an aperitif. Trise Cordial is used as an ingredient in place of bitters in some cocktails, such as the whiskey-based Trise Sling, a drink first made popular at the G-Loc Bar in Area18 on ArcCorp (Stanton III). Clair Rios of Cafe Musain in the Nyx system takes credit for the recipe, claiming that bartenders working for G-Loc stole it when they passed through Delamar in 2911.   \n\n# HISTORY\n\nWhile the origin of *otisau falu* is not known, it has been consumed by Banu at least since Humans first made contact with them in the early 25th century. Although many safe Banu products entered the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) around this time, *otisau falu* was banned in 2445 after three Humans were accidentally poisoned from a [Slomaddon](gp:boxDDjWYJ7) containing the drink. It wasn't until 2789 that it became available, when a distillery [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron) on the Bacchus [flotilla](gp:0qnN5GrMAa) hit upon a Human-safe version of the cordial with little alteration to the flavor. It attracted a small but dedicated following among Humans who would visit the flotilla and bring bottles back with them to the UEE. Eventually the drink became popular enough that the Souli was able to take its profits and move to Trise I, where it could have more immediate and inexpensive access to the herbs. In 2802, it caught the attention of the Terran Liquor Group (TLG), a distributor based on Terra (Terra III).   \n \nSensing opportunity, the corporation sent representatives to the Souli that created the beverage to strike a distribution deal. Under the terms of the contract, TLG would handle marketing, bottling, and label design, and the Souli would handle distillation. To market the new drink, TLG embellished its origins with a story of ascetic Banu living spiritual lives on Trise I who produce the liqueur as a form of prayer. To further emphasize this connection, they named it Trise Cordial.\n\nSales went well for five years, until the [Essosouli](gp:R6v8kxEPBD) of the original Souli Divested and the Souli dissolved. New Soulis founded by former members of the old distillery Souli popped up, all making their own versions of Trise Cordial. After a long negotiation period, TLG extended its distribution deal to the newly founded Soulis; a practice that they continued until 2834, when inconsistencies among the various batches forced the company to distill the liqueur itself to maintain a consistent product. \n\nDespite TLG employing Banu distillers and using ingredients grown on Trise I, many connoisseurs of *otisau falu* claim that the current Trise Cordial recipe is a poor imitation of the authentic version. A small market for artisanal Souli-distilled versions of the drink has arisen. However, TLG's Trise Cordial remains the best-selling and most well-known version of the liqueur in the UEE.","g":["terran liquor group","alcohol","beverage","human beverage"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c888fae5-f19c-4a63-b1c3-53e95e5a2a8c"},
{"id":"trise-flotilla","gp":"bBzvp2683m","t":"Trise Flotilla","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Banu"],"x":"The Trise flotilla is an interconnected network of spacecraft and space stations located in the [Trise system](gp:VlMBN7QA6r), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Made up mostly of the ships belonging to trade-centered [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron), the Banu on the flotilla maintain contracts with the Religion [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) on [Trise I](gp:0GxYz6v43Q) to handle the export and import of goods to the planet.","g":["banu flotilla","trise system","space station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9be472e8-543e-40fc-a219-4e14462f7171"},
{"id":"trise-i","gp":"0GxYz6v43Q","t":"Trise I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Trise I is the first and only planet from the sun of the [Trise system](gp:VlMBN7QA6r), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). An inhabitable super-Earth near the inner edge of the system's green band, it has a warm climate and multiple oceans. For as long as the [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) have been in contact with other civilizations, Trise I has been a stronghold for Religion [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron), and is a major destination for Banu seeking to purchase divine guidance. It is said in the Protectorate that the Soulis on Trise I are able to influence daily life in the Protectorate by the weight of their dictums.","g":["trise system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b245100d-183c-4f23-a2c7-5667c6f96721"},
{"id":"trise-system","gp":"VlMBN7QA6r","t":"Trise System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Banu"],"x":"The Trise system is a planetary system in the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) that consists of a G-type main sequence star and one planet. A stronghold of religion [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron), the Trise system is the heart of spiritualism in the Banu Protectorate. It is connected to the rest of the Protectorate via a single jump point, and is somewhat isolated from the rest of [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) society. The Soulis that reside in Trise have utilized this isolation to build up a sense of mystique around the system, making it a compelling destination for the curious.","g":["banu system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fec06e0d-1089-447c-8121-37e0d0b2bf5e"},
{"id":"triton-sol-8a","gp":"0KxZ3KKDL4","t":"Triton (Sol 8a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Triton is a moon of [Neptune (Sol VIII)](gp:RX3wGrAoW1), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The largest of Neptune's moons, it the planet's only natural satellite massive enough to have achieved gravitational rounding. Additionally, even though it is a moon, it is larger than all other dwarf planets in the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), one of many factors that has led scientists to hypothesize that it was captured from the nearby [Kuiper belt](gp:0KxZ3KwZvY) (Sol belt beta) by Neptune's gravity.","g":["triton","sol 9a","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3d9797ba-9ab4-48f0-aa66-bc5d3d9d2083"},
{"id":"truth-and-reconciliation-commission","gp":"VJO4JGZQv7","t":"Truth and Reconciliation Commission","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"The Truth and Reconciliation Commission was a formal committee convened by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) to declassify unlawful acts committed by members of the government during and leading up to the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo) (SEY 2546 - 2792). Formed in 2806, the Commission made thousands of personal and official records available to the public. The Commission was disbanded in 2810.","g":["uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/294a022e-969e-45d5-9ad1-8130ac32f453"},
{"id":"tualu-eealuth-i","gp":"RkGDJ8yZ9n","t":"Tua'lu\" (Ē'aluth I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tua'lu\" (Ē'aluth I) is the first planet from the sun of the [Ē'aluth system](gp:Rw1xW1lzxN), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A gas dwarf-like puffy planet, Tua'lu\" has a diffuse, low-density atmosphere that is slowly eroding due to radiation from the star it closely orbits. The gas around Tua'lu\" is being gravitationally drawn to toward the star instead of away from it, creating an interesting sight for those who possess the correct viewing equipment. Astronomers predict that the planet will gradually become a super-Earth as its atmospheric gas continues to evaporate.","g":["tua'lu\"","ē'aluth i","ē'aluth system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an empire"]},
{"id":"tumbril-land-systems","gp":"VarkpZnxjd","t":"Tumbril Land Systems","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Ground Transportation","Military"],"x":"Tumbril Land Systems is a terrestrial vehicle manufacturer that reformed in 2941 after first closing in 2862. Originally founded on [Yar (Centauri II)](gp:R6dd5pyOZ5) in 2536, its first product was the DX20, a wheeled vehicle designed by founders Kavya Crosby and Aaron Douze. Due to the DX20's success, Tumbril became a military contractor during the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) (2541-2546) where it became a fixture of the military. After the [fall of the Messers](gp:bE3rKa32P7) in 2792, its military contracts were drastically reduced. The company declared bankruptcy in 2862. In 2941, DevCo Group purchased the Tumbril name and resurrected the brand and its designs, updating them for the 30th century. The new Tumbril Land Systems launch line up included the [Cyclone](gp:V3GdnGmmzZ) armored ground vehicle and [Nova](gp:01L8gLYXaY) battle tank.","g":["vehicle manufacturer","saisei","centauri iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e863bde6-5687-488f-8e2e-8356e878b7f2"},
{"id":"turiya-terraforming","gp":"VarGepjj5o","t":"Turiya Terraforming","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Turiya Terraforming was a [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) company most notable for winning the contract from the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) to spearhead development of the [Oretani system](gp:bo1eNYWqqN). Under CEO Adriana Bratanek, Turiya's policy was to house their employees and their families for free under the condition that they relocate to the newly-terraformed planet once work was complete. After an expansive advertising campaign, the company attracted thousands of workers to the Oretani system and began work in 2483. In 2485, amidst rumors of food shortages on the space stations and a sense of unrest among the workers at the lack of available land on [Oretani II](gp:VpMezplMwO), Bratanek invited reporters to tour operations in Oretani. Two days later, the [Ferron](gp:Vy2Qo1dB18)-Oretani jump point suddenly collapsed, cutting everyone inside the system off from the rest of the UNE. Turiya's remaining board members filed to dissolve the corporation in 2496.","g":["terraforming company","human company","oretani system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f9be739a-0496-4199-9c45-832a6e4e8c19"},
{"id":"tyrol-belt-alpha","gp":"bo1l7PkK3D","t":"Tyrol Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Tyrol belt alpha is an asteroid belt in the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N). Located between the third and fourth planets from its two suns, the belt was once situated within the temperate green band, which shifted outwards when the F-type star entered its subgiant phase. Some of the asteroids in the belt are sublimating, and display cometary dust trails when they reach perihelion.","g":["tyrol system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/533ee2c8-3fa6-4a87-8bc0-b2bd92ea5734"},
{"id":"tyrol-i","gp":"0GxQnP34YP","t":"Tyrol I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tyrol I is the first planet from the two suns of the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N). In close orbit around the barycenter of the binary stars, its proximity to them has led to a dangerously hot environment. Nevertheless, the surface is home to an ever-shifting group of squatters who drift on and off the planet. They mostly inhabit former research stations or mining facilities that were built to withstand the extreme heat. When the systems that keep these locations safe fail, people must flee to safer ground or risk death by hyperthermia.","g":["tyrol system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d60b425f-7c95-4a4e-91d7-72fc02333191"},
{"id":"tyrol-ii","gp":"0qal7PLpxa","t":"Tyrol II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tyrol II is a terrestrial planet in the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N), and is the second world from its two suns. An iron planet, it is composed mainly of heavy metals, and has only a scant silicate surface. Scientists believe that Tyrol I once had a thick crust and mantle that was stripped away due to an unknown event. Wide, dark plains on its surface suggest that it briefly had multiple lava oceans.","g":["tyrol system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ecf02f3e-f7be-41eb-ab6a-1b707813e059"},
{"id":"tyrol-iii","gp":"bBzk2xZLm5","t":"Tyrol III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tyrol III is a coreless terrestrial planet in the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N). Third from its suns, it is distant enough from them that it is overall cooler than [Tyrol I](gp:0GxQnP34YP) and [Tyrol II](gp:0qal7PLpxa), although still very hot. Thanks to the absence of a metallic core at the center, it lacks an electromagnetic field and has failed to maintain a protective atmosphere. In 2911, Tyrol III was the subject of a University of Rhetor research project on the formation of coreless planets.","g":["tyrol system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5e5284a9-1499-4744-8247-fb4d98c06cef"},
{"id":"tyrol-iv","gp":"0n1lNPm8nJ","t":"Tyrol IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tyrol IV is a chthonian planet in the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N), and is the fourth world from its two suns. Dense and rich in minerals, it is a popular destination for local miners seeking to strike it rich. However, its high gravity creates a working environment that takes a harsh toll on people's bodies over time. Local folklore supposes that some of the mines are haunted by the ghosts of those who became too exhausted by the strain to return to their ships.","g":["tyrol system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/57b968a5-644c-4831-9735-cb4057da9b93"},
{"id":"tyrol-system","gp":"0ODPpkqZ2N","t":"Tyrol System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Tyrol system is an unclaimed planetary system that consists of a binary star system, four terrestrial planets, a chthonian planet, a gas giant, and a protoplanet. Discovered by Damon Huerta in 2823, it was initially met with excitement until it became clear that the F-type star had just entered its subgiant phase and was slowly losing its outer atmosphere to its companion star, a white dwarf. At some point within the next few hundred years, the hydrogen accreted by the smaller star will undergo fusion into helium and cause a nova; a cataclysmic explosion that has the potential to wipe out the entire system. Tyrol has remained mostly unsettled beyond those interested in studying the building nova up close, those who wish to live outside the boundaries of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and those who have no other choice.","g":["unclaimed system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fa996c24-41ba-44e7-bac9-ba2d4ed9765c"},
{"id":"tyrol-v","gp":"0GxQ6EB3JE","t":"Tyrol V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tyrol V is a terrestrial planet in the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N). Fifth position from its two suns, it was once partially covered in a thick layer of water ice that melted when the F-type star entered its subgiant phase and forced the green band outward. This created thousands of large lakes and revealed vast chasms, canyons, and caverns generated by millennia of glaciers. The presence of water on the planet has led to the creation of the largest settlement in the system, [Haven](gp:V3G6l5aNLa).","g":["tyrol system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/23008e6a-df59-4f34-b1be-0b7417975be9"},
{"id":"tyrol-vi","gp":"R9vpKQ5OAd","t":"Tyrol VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tyrol VI is a gas giant in the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N). The sixth world from its two suns, it remained largely unaffected when the F-type star entered its subgiant phase. Rain inside the atmosphere of Tyrol VI is composed of helium. During precipitation, the helium droplets fall through the liquid hydrogen of the planet's interior, where they dissolve in the heat. Helium clouds contribute to the atmosphere's pale color.","g":["tyrol system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/deed9c62-be19-4c31-a616-a5d88e395edf"},
{"id":"tyrol-vii","gp":"R4jwKxQwdl","t":"Tyrol VII","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Tyrol VII is a protoplanet in the unclaimed [Tyrol system](gp:0ODPpkqZ2N), and is the outermost planet in the system. In 2943, a widely-reported academic article claimed that Tyrol VII was far enough from its two suns that it had a high chance of remaining out of danger in the event of a nova. Since then, multiple institutes of higher learning and private research organizations have expressed interest in constructing a permanent base on the planet from which to observe the nova's progress.","g":["tyrol system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/731c2ff0-8175-42e1-8aca-9474f0f1c592"},
{"id":"uee-army","gp":"RxnX5JOZ7Q","t":"UEE Army","k":"faction","c":["Military","Human"],"x":"The United Empire of Earth (UEE) Army is the branch of the [UEE](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military responsible for land-based military operations. Headquartered on [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB), It was founded alongside the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) in SEY 2380 as a part of the creation of the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE). The Army is represented by the [Legatus Exercitus](gp:0QlKMOJELo), one of three members of the [High Command](gp:RegxqX26ok) responsible for interpreting and facilitating the [Imperator's](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) orders.","g":["uee military"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7b2947e6-ec1a-4ee9-b169-88e10de9e285"},
{"id":"uee-calendar","gp":"RegMQYpAYw","t":"UEE Calendar","k":"culture","c":["Human","Culture"],"x":"The [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) calendar (Standard Earth Year, SEY) is a system of time measurement that is based on the celestial mechanics of the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) homeworld, [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB). The year is charted by how long it takes Earth to revolve around the system's sun, and each day (Standard Earth Day, or SED) lasts as long as it takes for Earth to complete a rotation on its axis. While most planets have local calendars, UEE calendar is the official dating system, allowing all its inhabitants to share a common chronology.","g":["uee time"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/67b75562-c834-4f60-a6fa-768bdee657a6"},
{"id":"uee-diplomatic-corps","gp":"0dXZGgNm1Z","t":"UEE Diplomatic Corps","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The United Empire of Earth Diplomatic Corps (UEEDC or more commonly DC) is an agency of the UEE government responsible for diplomatic efforts associated with other civilizations. It works with the [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl), [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ), and various agencies and departments to develop treaties, oversee trade agreements, and maintain embassies with the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) and the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). First contact protocols for meeting new civilizations are under the purview of the Diplomatic Corps. While the Diplomatic Corps is a civilian agency, it is closely supported by the military; in particular, the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) often assigns capital ships to serve as diplomatic flags for missions that require the transportation of diplomats outside UEE borders.","g":["uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9a1f0b79-09cf-4e96-b77e-75f48b2c1db9"},
{"id":"uee-marines","gp":"V7d5ZYEr1a","t":"UEE Marines","k":"faction","c":["Military","Human"],"x":"The [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) Marines are the infantry branch of the [UEE](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) armed forces. They specialize in planetary invasion and special operations, along with the support of land and space operations. Once a division of the UEE [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q), they were granted their own branch in SEY 2560. Their head, the [Legatus Marinuum](gp:RWolAvP7qp), is one of the three military representatives who make up the position of [High-Command](gp:RegxqX26ok). They are headquartered on [Corin (Kilian IX)](gp:V8WWyl5zGo). The Marines don't offer open recruitment; instead, they cherry-pick potential candidates from other branches of the military, and sometimes even the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk).","g":["uee military"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/72fe4ba6-7470-480c-93e5-e2560cf18714"},
{"id":"uee-naval-flight-academy","gp":"RxnPOmKPJE","t":"UEE Naval Flight Academy","k":"place","c":["Human","Education","Military","Locations"],"x":"The United Empire of Earth Naval Flight Academy (UNFA) is a coeducational service academy located on [MacArthur (Kilian V)](gp:Rz22dGBlnz). Established in SEY 2632, it is one of the oldest of the [United Empire of Earth's](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) service academies. It educates officers for commissioning into the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). Most graduates of the UNFA go on to the various combat squadrons in the Navy, but others may pilot capital or support vessels.","g":["higher education","uee navy","uee higher education","uee education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/42e4505b-62ec-4b0e-a25a-d6f1e5367c54"},
{"id":"uee-navy","gp":"RPDvKOpdP4","t":"UEE Navy","k":"faction","c":["Human","Military"],"x":"The [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) Navy is the largest branch of the UEE's armed forces. It is responsible for the operation of capital spacecraft, support ships, and fighters and the maintenance thereof. The UEE Navy is headed by the [Legatus Navium](gp:V7dPXLWYL3), who represents the branch in the military [High Command](gp:RegxqX26ok). It is headquartered at [MacArthur (Kilian V)](gp:Rz22dGBlnz) in the [Kilian system](gp:0ODD4mY9aP). The Navy is responsible for operations outside of UEE territory in times of war and for acting as an additional security presence to support law enforcement within the UEE's borders.","g":["uee military"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/aea272b5-a007-4e94-8d80-6d497c3ea543"},
{"id":"uees-flyssa","gp":"V3GqNQAAXA","t":"UEES Flyssa","k":"faction","c":["Spacecraft","Military","Human"],"x":"The UEES *Flyssa* was a [Javelin](gp:0OaBgMK9DO)-class [destroyer](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/destroyer) that crashed on the surface of [Daymar (Stanton 2b)](gp:VpMGDvX48N) in SEY 2862 and was last commanded by Captain Chin Ormiston of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4). \n\nLaunched in 2779 after a three year construction process, it was initially used as a patrol ship in systems near [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) territory under Captain Thembeka Muholi. It intercepted and destroyed three Vanduul [Blades](gp:RegdeBENkw) in the Odin system in 2801, and participated in a reconnaissance mission to Vanduul space in 2819. After Muholi's retirement in 2857, the *Flyssa* was assigned to the Stanton system under the command of Captain Chin Ormiston. The *Flyssa* was fatally damaged by the explosion of a fleeing spacecraft during an operation to remove illegal miners from Daymar. The resultant shower of debris and ore fragments shredded the thrusters, causing an overload when the Captain ordered a retreat. The *Flyssa* then careened onto the surface of the moon below. All 65 souls aboard perished.","g":["individual spacecraft","uee navy vessel","human vessel"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e0526720-abe5-4c41-a313-ee84d5dabe5d"},
{"id":"uees-olympus","gp":"0Gxk9rGkej","t":"UEES Olympus","k":"faction","c":["Human","Military"],"x":"The UEES *Olympus* was a [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) carrier that crash landed on the unclaimed planet Ashana (Nul V) in 2571 while pursuing a group of pirates. After the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) government decided against sending in a cleanup crew, a scavenger camp formed among the wreckage. Today, the remains of the Olympus are the heart of a town of the same name.","g":["uee navy vessel","human vessel","individual spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/51cd9cb3-46b1-4762-a3ce-a35cbe99ad1b"},
{"id":"uiraang-kaipua-i","gp":"bEzqmwGZ4J","t":"Ui'r.a'ang (Kai'pua I)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Ui'r.a'ang (Kai'pua I) is the first planet from the sun of the [Kai'pua system](gp:V3GBmlQoar), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Composed mainly of carbon, it is a terrestrial planet with black, brown, and red hued atmosphere. The temperatures and pressure in the planet's interior may have caused the formation of abundant diamonds beneath the surface. However, the Xi'an government prohibits mining, so this hypothesis remains unproven.","g":["ui'r.a'ang","kai'pua i","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet","kai'pua system"]},
{"id":"ultiflex","gp":"RWozkYmQLP","t":"UltiFlex","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Military","Human"],"x":"UltiFlex is a weapon manufacturer that specializes in creating military-grade combat knives. The UltiFlex name is synonymous with their flagship product, the FSK-8 Combat Knife. These combat knives are part of the standard field kit for UEE soldiers and are popular among civilian survivalists.\n\nFounded in SEY 2538, the company rose to prominence after the knives it was contracted to make for the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) were utilized during the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM). UltiFlex retained its contract after the government reorganized into the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) in 2546. After four decades of exclusive work for the government, UltiFlex expanded its operations to the public sector.","g":["weapons manufacturer","human company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/37d27f59-2070-4e08-a0d5-07067b8507ee"},
{"id":"ulysses-messer-x","gp":"bBp6YZPOGO","t":"Ulysses Messer X","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Ulysses Messer X (SEY 2702 - 2781) was [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) from 2751 - 2781. \n\nBefore becoming Imperator, he served as High-Secretary under his uncle [Galor IX](gp:VyvYAGKxAz) from 2722, overseeing the reconstruction of government buildings in the Meta-Baroque style of architecture. As Galor IX's health declined, Ulysses took on more and more of his day-to-day duties. \n\nAfter ascending as Imperator in 2751, Ulysses directed most of the UEE's resources into completing the reconstruction projects. Over the course of his reign, he stripped down environmental protections, raised taxes, lowered the minimum working age to 10, decreased government oversight of industry, suspended minimum wage, expanded police powers, rewrote treason laws, and enacted mass deregulations. His son, [Linton XI](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq), staged a coup in 2781. Ulysses X committed suicide before Linton XI's agents could reach him.","g":["uee imperator","messer dynasty","messer era","human people","uee high-secretary"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/eecc1083-7772-4bdd-9abe-0d4565fedd01"},
{"id":"umbriel-sol-7c","gp":"0qaj9AgLqq","t":"Umbriel (Sol 7c)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Umbriel (Sol 7c) is a moon of [Uranus (Sol VII)](gp:0rxOX3eKQ2), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). One of the darkest in color of the moons of Uranus, one of its larger craters has a ring of reflective material on its floor, making Umbriel appear as if it has a single small eye. Visual artist Tamsa Wheel utilized ice harvested from this ring as the centerpiece in her SEY 2949 sculpture \"The Anthropic Principle.\"","g":["umbriel","sol 7c","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","sol system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6df3c5a4-04ce-4d7f-b8c8-3aa415f106a6"},
{"id":"unclaimed-system","gp":"VgExMejDPx","t":"Unclaimed System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"An unclaimed system is a term used primarily in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) to describe a planetary system that has not been annexed or otherwise claimed by any type of formal government. Because these systems are not under the jurisdiction of any body of law, some unclaimed systems become havens for activity that would be seen as criminal elsewhere.","g":["uee legal definition"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9af8178b-c9f4-4f77-83a8-be721496898f"},
{"id":"unification-wars","gp":"RWolrAWw9m","t":"Unification Wars","k":"history","c":["History","Human","Military"],"x":"The Unification Wars were a series of wars that took place after the formation of the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) in 2380 until 2384. It was sparked on 20 October 2380 when the crew of the *Stanley*, a warship registered to the former country of Amecanio, mutinied and threatened to attack multiple cities on Earth (Sol III) unless the government reverted to its pre-unified form. The [UNE Council](gp:RegxPqm1N6) mobilized the military and successfully disabled and recaptured the *Stanley*; however, six more warships rebelled and fighting broke out in earnest. Although the first war ended with the defeat of anti-unificationists in early 2381, a second war erupted that same year when the UNE [Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) clashed with separatist rebels who had created fortifications in the Mars (Sol IV) frontier. The third and final war concluded on 29 July 2384 in the skies above New York City. Anti-unificationists who did not surrender fled the Sol system, and many went on to form outlaw gangs.","g":["wars"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/666a5b37-3475-455d-9c83-43f6a290cb48"},
{"id":"unified-currency-riot","gp":"0QlvpyjLvJ","t":"Unified Currency Riot","k":"history","c":["Human","Politics","History"],"x":"The Unified Currency Riot was a two-week period of political unrest and violence in [Jata](gp:Rz2PmWxpMM), [Cestulus (Davien II)](gp:0QlKaQ76a5) in SEY 2529 following the introduction of the United Earth Credit (UEC) to the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) market. The riot began when a private security officer discharged his weapon into a protesting crowd on the steps of the local [SSN/CAtv](gp:0QxYwPK88l) headquarters. Hundreds were injured in the subsequent riots and several died when the UPE military ultimately intervened, bringing two weeks of looting, vandalism, and property destruction to an end.","g":["human history","riot"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/bb5bd514-22bc-4db0-adc3-42ffe1cb9ce9"},
{"id":"united-empire-of-earth","gp":"VyvyKxy4v6","t":"United Empire of Earth","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The United Empire of Earth (UEE) is the name of the current [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) governmental body. It is led by a democratically elected [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) who serves for a single ten-year term; a [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) of [High-Advocate](gp:RWolAld13P), [High-Secretary](gp:RkG2n2MWYn), and [High Command](gp:RegxqX26ok); and the (UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ)), a legislative body composed of elected representatives from UEE planets. \n\nFormerly known as the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO), it transitioned to the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) (UPE) in SEY 2523 and was given its current name in 2546, after the conclusion of the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM). Then-High-General [Ivar Messer](gp:RXlXYPWk8q), who had been the face of the UPE's recruitment campaign during the war, claimed that the Tribunal system and Senate were rendered ineffective by bureaucracy. He thus introduced the concept of [Prime Citizen](gp:V7gM82vNmr), a singular figurehead of the government that would unclog the perceived governmental quagmire. As soon as he was elected to the office he created, Messer stripped the High-Secretary and High-Advocate of their positions and utilized the power of the military to declare himself Imperator for life. \n\nHis descendants reigned as dictators for centuries, modifying and corrupting the system to further ensconce their power. The [last Messer](gp:RwZBaD4Mdq) was deposed in SEY 2792 after a [popular uprising](gp:bE3rKa32P7). Under the leadership of the new Imperator, former Senator of Earth [Erin Toi](gp:R4ZG3NxM7Y), the government was re-organized into its current democratic form.","g":["human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/043a872e-d3f3-4e5e-9b5e-622a55c78347"},
{"id":"citizen","gp":"RLMmop8rkr","t":"United Empire of Earth Citizen","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"A Citizen is a resident of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) who has actively taken a role in making the UEE better. Often this can be achieved through military service, the performance of exemplary community service, or success in a government-proctored application. Citizens of the UEE are afforded some privileges that [civilians](gp:Vgg7rq5J73) are not afforded, including the ability to run for a seat on the UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ), apply to work for the UEE government, attain the office of [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl), and the reception of a special dispensation to pay lower tax rates.","g":["uee citizen","uee legal definition"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/91ffb54e-46b3-4545-b7aa-5199d652b208"},
{"id":"civilian","gp":"Vgg7rq5J73","t":"United Empire of Earth Civilian","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"A civilian is a resident of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) who has not taken the steps to become a [Citizen](gp:RLMmop8rkr). At the age of 17 SEY, a civilian can own property, can vote in local elections and legislation, and must start paying taxes. All civilians are eligible to hold planetary-level political office. Civilians cannot serve on the UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) seat or be elected to the office of [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl). Although not afforded some of the privileges of Citizens, civilians are still protected members of the UEE.","g":["uee civilian","uee legal definition"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8fca2696-7734-4752-b6bc-d68dae34d02a"},
{"id":"uee-governor","gp":"RkZ9A5KjBL","t":"United Empire of Earth Governor","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"A United Empire of Earth Governor is the elected executive leader of a [State](gp:RWwZ78lypa) or territory in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) planet. It can be filled by [Citizens](gp:RLMmop8rkr) or [Civilians](gp:Vgg7rq5J73), and is the highest-ranking government position a Civilian can attain. The position is limited to two six-year terms. A Governor oversees an area of land on a planet that is run by one hundred [Representatives](gp:0KnAzj9B1o) who are assigned to various committees and departments that oversee and regulate planetary infrastructure. A planet can have two or more Governors depending on the size of its population and number of states. Densely populated planets may have dozens of Governors.","g":["uee governor","uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/42227036-8c79-40ef-b550-219ce060d5bf"},
{"id":"uee-governors-council","gp":"0rqzA55WZ3","t":"United Empire of Earth Governors Council","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"The [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) Governors Council is the ruling body of a UEE planet. Each elected [Governor](gp:RkZ9A5KjBL) representing a [State](gp:RWwZ78lypa) or territory of the planet serves on the Governors Council to create planet-wide laws, settle disputes, and discuss worldwide issues that may affect their constituents. The Governors Council also has the ability to petition the UEE for official recognition.","g":["uee governors council","uee governor","uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/321540ac-dde4-4d0c-ba0d-f9836d5c96c4"},
{"id":"uee-imperator","gp":"0Gz5BoJ9wl","t":"United Empire of Earth Imperator","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"The Imperator is the democratically elected head of government in the United Empire of Earth (UEE). Bills and legislation that start in the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) and that have been approved by the [High-Secretary](gp:RkG2n2MWYn) move up to the Imperator for approval or veto. Imperators may serve single ten-year term limits. It is the highest office that a [Citizen](gp:RLMmop8rkr) of the UEE can obtain. The position was created by [Ivar Messer](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) in 2546 and was initially an inherited office in the [Messer Era](gp:V8gJ6ZwGqo).","g":["uee imperator","uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/41e6479b-c7d4-4955-b86d-a42c3e9a7ba3"},
{"id":"uee-representative","gp":"0KnAzj9B1o","t":"United Empire of Earth Representative","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"A Representative is an elected official that serves under a [Governor](gp:RkZ9A5KjBL) on a [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) planet. Their chief duties are overseeing departments and committees that regulate their state's infrastructure. The amount of Representatives assigned to each state is determined by the population of each state. Every ten years, the population census dictates whether the number of Representatives can rise or fall. Both [Civilians](gp:Vgg7rq5J73) and [Citizens](gp:RLMmop8rkr) are able to serve in this role.","g":["uee representative","uee government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9f7825d3-aa1d-4988-b9f1-0dc9e720fb7e"},
{"id":"united-nations-of-earth","gp":"R4ZQpY83oO","t":"United Nations of Earth","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The United Nations of Earth (UNE) was the first [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) unified government, founded in 2380, shortly after the [first planet](gp:0QlxqwG14Q) outside the Sol system was successfully [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). The world leaders of the time decided that Humanity's expansion into space would be better managed by a unified government. Existing countries formed the first [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) and supervised the first major terraforming boom in Human history and [the first diasporas](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm) from Earth. It was peacefully reformed as the [United Planets of Earth](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) in 2523.","g":["human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/655bf255-d83a-40ae-89cb-ce544d240a96"},
{"id":"une-council","gp":"RegxPqm1N6","t":"United Nations of Earth Council","k":"faction","c":["Government","Human"],"x":"The United Nations of Earth Council was the ruling body of the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) government from its inception in 2380 until the advent of the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) in 2523. It was made up of an elected representative from each of the states (then called nations) on Earth (Sol III). The Council's primary function was to exercise final approval of legislation that had passed through the Unified [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ), command the military, appoint diplomatic and judicial officers, and take the lead in policymaking. As the UNE expanded, [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) who resided on other worlds grew increasingly dissatisfied with their lack of representation on the Council. In response to this, the Council disbanded and was replaced with the [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) when the government transitioned into the UPE.","g":["une council","united nations of earth","human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/94e0d32e-4c91-47e4-99a4-8702f135d5fc"},
{"id":"united-planets-of-earth","gp":"0QxBjKP2PN","t":"United Planets of Earth","k":"faction","c":["Human","Government"],"x":"The United Planets of Earth was the name of the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) government from 2523 to 2546. It was led by a [Tribunal](gp:bZwq5Nr5EL) composed of a High-Advocate, a High-General, and a High-Secretary along with a [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) populated by elected representatives from all Human-controlled planetary systems. During this time, Humans introduced a unified currency, made first contact with the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X), and engaged in the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM)(2541-2546). [Ivar Messer I's](gp:RXlXYPWk8q) ascendancy to Prime Citizen in 2546 marked the end of the era as he transitioned the government into the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["human government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cc498803-7684-4fe5-bca9-7918d90a8882"},
{"id":"united-resource-workers","gp":"V7dPXPjeBn","t":"United Resource Workers","k":"faction","c":["Organizations","Human"],"x":"The United Resource Workers are an interplanetary guild of resource collectors such as asteroid miners and gas scoopers in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl). The guild was founded in 2112 to protect the rights of workers, from ensuring safer and better work practices to securing a living wage. Its motto is \"Solidarity Conquers Adversity.\"","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b519ee85-045d-4b23-bfa9-7b2568c735f3"},
{"id":"universal-body-armor","gp":"R4jvOo8qoq","t":"Universal Body Armor (UBA)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Universal Body Armor, commonly referred to as UBA, is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of personal armor. UBA was initially formed as a holding company. It gradually acquired small armor manufacturers until it had the capacity to offer a unified product across the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The company's focus on streamlined mass-production allows it to offer affordable armor intended to be easily worn, but typically does not have the protection of industrial or military-grade suits.","g":["armor manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4bbbabc9-422b-4cd3-a055-4e544aea23bc"},
{"id":"universalist-party","gp":"VDo6qOgLx9","t":"Universalist Party","k":"faction","c":["Human","Politics"],"x":"The Universalist party is one of the three major political parties in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The core ideologies of the Universalist party support measures for the expansion of government power, increasing government regulation, decreasing taxes on the wealthy, cutting government expenditures, and supporting free trade. The most recent Universalist [Imperator](gp:0Gz5BoJ9wl) of the UEE was [Kelos Costigan](gp:VJOzBxdJ28), who served from 2941 to 2951.","g":["uee political party"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/db3a6ce9-3ed9-4d5e-ade4-1b470d649078"},
{"id":"university-of-lo-new-junction-ulon","gp":"VgEngjy9y3","t":"University of Lo New Junction (ULON)","k":"place","c":["Education","Human","Locations"],"x":"The University of Lo, New Junction (ULON) is a small public university in [New Junction](gp:V3G53AXDgY), [Lo (Corel III)](gp:VarAoYEQYd), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). In SEY 2859, it was founded thanks to a large donation from [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA). \n\nULON offers a wide variety of two year and four year degrees, but is best known for its geotechnology program, which confers professional certifications in fields related to [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) and economics. The school is a member of a consortium of educational institutes dedicated to advancing the field of planetary technology. Nearly all applicants who reside on Lo are automatically accepted and given a discounted tuition rate in the interest of bettering the community.","g":["university of lo new junction","ulon","higher education","lo","corel iii","uee higher education","uee education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2273c22e-771a-4bd8-85e9-87f0d0f5262e"},
{"id":"university-of-mentor","gp":"RWozpy2kwa","t":"University of Mentor","k":"place","c":["Education","Human","Locations"],"x":"The University of Mentor (UM) is a public research university on [Mentor (Rhetor IV)](gp:RPDlZJeDLX), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). The school is one of several prestigious universities located in the Rhetor system. \n\nEstablished shortly after the planet was [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), it is the oldest and largest institute of higher learning on Mentor. Its physical sciences and history programs are highly competitive, with 5 to 10% admissions rates for new students. The school's reputation for rigorous, demanding study coupled with Mentor's frigid environment may factor into the school's relatively high dropout rate. \n\nThe University of Mentor is responsible for maintenance and research efforts connected with the UEE's universal seed vaults.","g":["higher education","mentor","rhetor iv","uee higher education","uee education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a60dac7a-ea4c-4ae8-80e6-3f14772adae5"},
{"id":"university-of-persei","gp":"Rz2XZkMrmN","t":"University of Persei","k":"place","c":["Education","Human","Locations"],"x":"The University of Persei is the oldest continually operating institute of higher education in the [Rhetor](gp:0ODlqMJXmP) system, [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). It is a collegiate research university made up of several semi-independent colleges and research institutes, including the University of Persei Analytical Research and Quantification ([UPARQ](gp:0n1Mz2WmD7)) center. \n\nAs a part of an agreement between the [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB) government and the discoverers of the system, land on [Persei (Rhetor II)](gp:0ODlqM6zKO) was explicitly reserved for public education, and the University of Persei was soon established. The school is best known for its programs in space technology, [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj), and psychology.","g":["higher education","persei","rhetor ii","uee higher education","uee education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4ee98ba1-55e2-4eb4-815d-cced722df122"},
{"id":"university-of-rhetor","gp":"bZkZGKGP8d","t":"University of Rhetor","k":"place","c":["Education","Human","Locations"],"x":"The University of Rhetor is a public institute of higher learning located on [Reisse (Rhetor III)](gp:0QljXw43Ev) in the [Rhetor system](gp:0ODlqMJXmP), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). A research university, it offers a wide range of subjects and invests heavily in research and development. Undergraduates at the school take four courses per semester and are required to engage in experiential education, which can include civic engagement, hands-on professional engagement, and one or more semesters studying abroad.\n\nIt was founded in SEY 2389 by a group of scholars who left the [University of Persei](gp:Rz2XZkMrmN) following a dispute over the low salaries of adjunct professors.","g":["higher education","reisse","rhetor iii","uee higher education","uee education"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7fbebd0b-6619-4751-8974-15b684cf9ea8"},
{"id":"untold-tales","gp":"bZkaoYnLEE","t":"Untold Tales","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"# UNTOLD TALES\n*Untold Tales* is a [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) show hosted by Saanvi Tejwani that recounts and explores a single real-world mystery to the audience. The format varies depending on the subject. An episode may present actual footage or re-enactments of incidents to examine a mystery, coupled with interviews with involved individuals or commentary from experts. Cold cases, supernatural phenomena, unexpected alien discoveries, missing persons, and unexplained historical events are the most common topics. The show's introductory monologue has become an element of popular culture, especially the final line, \"These are the universe's *Untold Tales*,\" or \"This is *Untold Tales*.\"  \n# FORMAT\nEach episode of *Untold Tales* opens with a montage composed of footage, images, and re-enactments that will be used in the episode, over which the host recites a monologue expounding on the unexplained happenings of the universe. Usually one mystery is covered, but sometimes up to three are explored in depth. At the end of each episode, the host wraps things up by asking unanswered questions raised by the mystery, inviting the viewers to solve it if they can. If a cold case was the main focus, the host asks the audience to contact the show if they have any information that will help bring the perpetrator to justice.\n# HISTORY\n*Untold Tales* began as a series of seven specials hosted by Ellroy Cass and Saanvi Tejwani beginning in 2945, covering famous paranormal phenomena throughout the UEE, such as the Hades cryptid and the lost civilization of [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). The specials earned high ratings, so much so that the producers ordered a full-fledged series. At first, the plan was to continue with two hosts, but Cass declined to sign the contract when they accepted a starring role in the then-upcoming film *Crimson Tower*. Production continued, and the first episode debuted in mid-2945 with Tejwani at the helm. It covered the 2711 unsolved robbery of the Greater Davien Bank and Trust, the mystery of the empty starliner *Gisele Tamar* discovered drifting near [Abyss (Orion IV)](gp:0KxK3vQk3Y) in 2903, and reported ghost sightings near the site of the long-since-collapsed Oretani jump point. \n\nTejwani's grave yet dramatic narration style quickly became synonymous with the show. Apparel featuring her signature line \"These are the universe's *Untold Tales*,\" sold out in its first run on Voyager Direct. When Tejwani took a leave of absence for personal reasons in 2947, ratings experienced a sharp drop, only to recover when Tejwani returned late that same year. \n# UPDATES\nViewers are occasionally given updates when a case is solved. Most famously, missing person and former child star Eliu Jalan Cervantes, abducted in 2940, was found living on [Delamar](gp:0GxoZnAGrg) in the [Nyx system](gp:0jGxP6kpG3) in 2948 under the assumed name Uriel Kane thanks to an anonymous tip from viewers. His manager Liberato Kane was arrested and convicted of the kidnapping, and Cervantes returned to his family.","g":["spectrum show","documentaries","saanvi tejwani"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5200eccf-d757-47c6-b468-66296292118b"},
{"id":"uparq","gp":"0n1Mz2WmD7","t":"UPARQ","k":"place","c":["Human","Military","Education"],"x":"University of Persei Analytical Research and Quantification (UPARQ) is a research center headquartered on [Persei (Rhetor II)](gp:0ODlqM6zKO), sponsored by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The researchers at UPARQ work largely on classified projects for the benefit of the UEE military. Due to its connections with the UEE government, public access to UPARQ is strictly controlled.","g":["persei","rhetor ii","higher education","university of persei"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2c4ee8aa-2ade-4315-88cf-b0b4ae3f46d8"},
{"id":"upsana-dixit","gp":"0Gx2n4G7na","t":"Upsana Dixit","k":"people","c":["People","Human"],"x":"Upsana Dixit (2491-2563) was a Human journalist, news anchor, showrunner, and [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q) show host. Born in 2491 in Quinton, Angeli (Croshaw II), she created [*Showdown!*](gp:RwZBw4Lrxz) in 2511 as a 30-minute long current events debate audio program. After amassing a significant following, it was purchased by [SSN/CAtv](gp:0QxYwPK88l) and converted to a Spectrum broadcast show in 2521. Dixit impartially moderated *Showdown!* until she retired in 2546 in protest of [Ivar Messer I](gp:RXlXYPWk8q)'s rise to power. She died at age 72 in an earthquake in her hometown [Quinton](gp:VY4Wg52JY1) in 2563.","g":["showdown!"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/05e5446a-8e14-4d00-b775-9cdf4cef5022"},
{"id":"uranus-sol-vii","gp":"0rxOX3eKQ2","t":"Uranus (Sol VII)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Uranus (Sol VII) is the seventh planet from the sun of the [Sol system](gp:Rz2zy6DGB5), [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Pale blue in color, it is an ice giant with an atmosphere that is made mostly of water, ammonia, and methane. The UEE government runs orbital research centers dedicated to the study of weather phenomena on Uranus, which remain some of the least understood in the known universe.","g":["uranus","sol vii","sol system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f2a1bd6a-2bd4-4ec6-8227-ea2130096e47"},
{"id":"uriel-oberon-ii","gp":"RL673Gxjjv","t":"Uriel (Oberon II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Uriel is the second planet from the neutron star in the unclaimed [Oberon system](gp:VYLdlgMqop). Before the formation of the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO), there were few regulations on the discovery of new systems. When [Titania Terraforming](gp:RkGerKq6eN) won the coordinates of Oberon in an auction, they sold plots of land on Uriel to offset the future costs of [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) the planet. However, the company failed to completely terraform the planet and stranded the newly-arrived colonists, who were forced to establish settlements underground in order to survive the cold and hostile world. Today, while there are some above-ground structures, the vast majority of people on Uriel live in a warren of interconnected, underground towns organized around familial lineages that can be traced back to the world's original settlers.","g":["uriel","oberon ii","oberon system","habitable planet","habitable","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/11822089-f899-42cf-9279-b6d8cf14544c"},
{"id":"ursa-rover","gp":"RAdjOOm67M","t":"Ursa Rover","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Human"],"x":"The Ursa Rover is an all-terrain exploration vehicle developed by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw), designed for ground-based scouting, mapping, and discovery applications. Though RSI is primarily a spacecraft manufacturer, they opted to tackle design and production of the Ursa internally in order to support their Constellation multi-crew spacecraft. [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) has also included the Ursa under license with their [Carrack](gp:R4ZGyLQaBl)-class explorer. The Ursa Rover Fortuna, a version of the Ursa with green livery, was available for a limited time.","g":["all-terrain vehicle (atv)","expedition","roberts space industries (rsi)","ursa rover fortuna","human vehicle"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c23e2443-0202-4a58-bf6e-65f8292da2b6"},
{"id":"vagabond-system","gp":"bBzvN8LL4m","t":"Vagabond System (VS-07)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Vagabond system (designated VS-07 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares no publicly-known jump points with any other systems. Included in UEE star charts as a part of [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), it has been confirmed that it has at least one planet, but all other details are classified. In the 2890s SEY, the name \"Vagabond\" inspired a popular folk song of the same name about the survivors of the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) and their struggle to find a permanent home.","g":["vagabond system","vs-07","vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c11f260d-194e-4437-873a-11fa5929129c"},
{"id":"valakkar","gp":"RMNKXwe51E","t":"Valakkar","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"# VALAKKAR\n\nThe valakkar is a colossal worm indigenous to the deserts of [Leir III](gp:RkGeZXw9pp). The largest animal on the planet, in rare cases they can grow over 300 meters long. Valakkar are born from clutches of eggs that are laid in shallow nests in the desert. When the young emerge, they burrow into the sand, where they spend the majority of their lives. They move with the aid of overlapping plates that grip the ground and push them along without the need for limbs. As omnivores, they subsist on a mixed diet of vegetation, detritus, and meat, and have evolved to need very little water to survive. They are known to attack settlements, which makes the construction of permanent habitation on Leir III very difficult. Valakkar that are removed from their home world and introduced to new environments often become invasive. \n\n# DESCRIPTION\nThe juvenile, adult, and apex stages of the valakkar differ from one another in multiple ways. Juveniles are earthy brown with semi-hard plates that are dotted with tooth-like protrusions, which help them push their way through the underground tunnels they make. Their beaks, not yet fully formed, are covered with a durable, jagged-edged shield that drops off when the juvenile approaches adulthood. Adults are sandy brown and have rough overlapping plates that are cracked in places due to everyday wear and tear, through which you can see the scales' reddish brown interior. Their mouths are ringed with three hard, curved, beak-like mandibles that are used to help the valakkar dig holes and grasp prey. Valakkars that have reached the apex stage are more than 150 meters long, and their plates are dark brown with ruddy scratches across their surfaces. Some apex valakkars that have lived an especially long time can reach over 300 meters in length. All stages of the valakkar have a throat thronged with rows of teeth that continually grow throughout the animal's life. \n\n# BEHAVIOR AND ECOLOGY\nAfter they hatch from their eggs, juveniles from the same clutch often travel together. Without the thick, tough plates they will develop as adults, juveniles are vulnerable to predation, especially on their original world Leir III. Juveniles in groups use strength in numbers to fend off potential threats or to take down prey below and above ground, which they are able to sense through vibrations in the earth. Adults also travel in groups for a time, but they tend to become more solitary as they age. Apex valakkars are fully solitary, and breed rarely. \n\nWhen a valakkar is ready to breed, it leaves its childhood brood and travels hundreds of kilometers to seek out a suitable mate. Adults are fiercely protective of their nests, only leaving them alone when they must eat. If an apex finds an active nest in its territory it will often claim it for itself, allowing the adults that laid the nest to leave, recover their strength, and lay another clutch elsewhere. Most nests contain between two and ten eggs, but when their population is under threat valakkars lay larger clutches, sometimes up to twenty at a time.\n\n# USE BY SENTIENTS\nValakkars are hunted for their fangs and pearls. The fangs are covered with enameloid, making them as hard as stone and very durable. Manufacturers and artisans use them to craft a wide variety of luxury items. The pearls, which form when a large piece of grit becomes embedded in a valakkar's hide, are valued for their beauty and for their use as an additive to ceramics, metals, and alloys.\n\n# INVASIVE SPECIES\nAlthough valakkars originally evolved to survive in a desert environment, they readily adapt to other biomes and have become invasive outside their homeworld. Locations that do not have large enough predators to hunt the juvenile and adult valakkars or eat their eggs are especially vulnerable to this. Due to this adaptability and their tendency to produce more eggs when their populations are low, valakkars are difficult to eradicate once they have established themselves. In the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N), for example, their numbers remain high despite countless extermination efforts from corporations, animal control organizations, and local gangs, among others. \n\n# IRRADIATED VALAKKAR\nOn [Pyro I](gp:RMNjxnZp3n), the invasive valakkars have undergone notable mutations after decades of surviving in an area that is constantly bombarded by high-energy radiation. Large, tumor-like growths emerge from their hides as they age, protruding from between their protective plates. These soft spots have made them more vulnerable to attacks from standard weapons. They have also gained the ability to expel radioactive saliva from their throats, making them even more dangerous to approach than a standard valakkar. Their pearls have developed unusual properties that may be applicable to regen technology. Various universities, research institutes, and private corporations are monitoring this population as they continue to survive in spite of the otherwise deadly environment.","g":["leir iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dbd1e01d-1b5f-4d7f-b794-2eb3e699d2f0"},
{"id":"valkyrie","gp":"0ODPYG1PdO","t":"Valkyrie","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human","Military"],"x":"The Valkyrie is a dropship spacecraft manufactured by [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD). Designed to carry personnel in and out of combat zones, it features twenty jump seats and gun racks, and is outfitted with manual turrets, remotely operated turrets, side-door guns, and front-mounted guns. Its vehicle bay is capable of carrying multiple ground-based transports that can be launched from its ramp as needed in battle. Used exclusively by the military after it was first made in SEY 2812, Anvil debuted a civilian version of the Valkyrie in 2948.","g":["anvil aerospace","dropship","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c25e641f-d9fa-42a2-960e-18fbe901fade"},
{"id":"vanduul","gp":"VpGPp92gdO","t":"Vanduul","k":"species","c":["Vanduul","Civilizations"],"x":"The Vanduul are hostile beings capable of space flight, quantum travel, and [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) navigation. [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) first made contact with the Vanduul after a Clan [raided Dell Township](gp:RWwZDmxaXP) on [Armitage (Orion III)](gp:RL6KLK4ylo) in SEY 2681, killing all the settlers but one. Every subsequent encounter with the Vanduul has resulted in mass deaths. The location of their homeworld is unknown. As a culture, the Vanduul seem to lack a central government or command structure; each Clan operates as a self-governing entity. All attempts at the establishment of diplomatic connections between Humans and Vanduul have failed.","g":["vanduul clans","extant civilizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/994bf19a-7672-4503-91dd-759b1c5d1e93"},
{"id":"vanduul-clans","gp":"R9vzjxmEBx","t":"Vanduul Clans","k":"culture","c":["Vanduul"],"x":"Vanduul Clans are groups of [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) who have banded together to form a single mutually-beneficial unit. Although observers have not yet fully defined the leadership structure, it is believed that Clans operate as a martial meritocracy that shares some similarities with a military unit. The primary goal for most Clans encountered in [Human-settled space](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) seems to be the collection of resources through raids on settlements and other Clans. Uncommonly powerful clans may possess a capital-class vessel such as the UEE designated \"[Kingship](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm).\"","g":["vanduul sociopolitics"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/366fc23a-986d-4963-b6e0-3c1058751d46"},
{"id":"vanduul-kingship","gp":"V3qWn9Dlvm","t":"Vanduul Kingship","k":"vehicle","c":["Vanduul","Spacecraft"],"x":"Kingship is a military designation for [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) capital ships that serve as the apparent flagships of some especially large [Vanduul Clans](gp:R9vzjxmEBx). The Kingship is the largest type of Vanduul capital asset encountered and is the most powerful class of known warship. Functionally, a Kingship is a dreadnought, fleet carrier, command and control ship and assault transport combined in a single hull. They are very rarely seen, and have only been observed during large-scale Vanduul raids. When present, they operate with a large number of other craft, including ships of the line, support vessels and screens of skirmishers. Xeno-anthropologists believe that the possession of a Kingship is a powerful symbol in Vanduul martial culture, signifying a Clan's power and strength.\n\n# CONSTRUCTION\n\nWhile the method of a Kingship's construction is unclear, based on scans of the ships and evidence collected from raid sites, they seem to have been built in zero gravity environments with the aid of advanced technology. Kingship silhouettes can differ from Clan to Clan, suggesting that the ships are either custom made or modified by the Clan in possession of it. Clans may add weapons, armor, modules, and other pieces to the base ship as they conduct raids and grow in martial prowess. \n\n# ENCOUNTERS\n\nKingships have likely been in service for centuries, though their discovery by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE) is relatively recent. The UEE first encountered a Kingship on 18 February 2712, during the [Vanduul invasion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K) of the [Orion system](gp:VlMpwMky6d). The Kingship in question surprised Orion's defenders and immediately turned the tide of the battle in favor of the Vanduul, forcing the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) to retreat to the Tiber system. The Vanduul did not continue their raid beyond Orion. Instead, the attacking clan kept the ship in question in orbit of the former [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) colony for over a year as it gathered resources. \n\nOn 7 July 2884, a Clan led by a Kingship slipped past the Caliban system's sensor beacons and sparked the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE), resulting in both the loss of the system and the [89th UEE Navy Logistic Support Squadron](gp:0Gz5BNmPqo). The Kingship reentered Vanduul space shortly after the end of the battle. \n\nIn 2940, the UEE Navy severely damaged a Kingship as part of [Operation Unilateral Force](gp:bBp64B7G79), a covert military operation that intended to weaken a single Vanduul clan and inspire infighting in the hope it would distract them from raiding Human colonies. Though the overall operation failed to have the expected impact, the 78th Squadron succeeded in inflicting heavy damage on the Kingship.\n\nA Kingship did not appear in Human space again until 5 October 2945, in the [Battle of Vega II](gp:0Gz5mkprmg). The Navy's 2nd Fleet led by Admiral [Ernst Bishop](gp:ReJaavPB3k) engaged the Kingship and remaining clan. After a fierce battle, the UEES *Gauntlet* charged the weakened Kingship at ramming speed. Both the *Gauntlet* and the Kingship were destroyed, marking the first time Human forces have successfully downed a Vanduul Kingship. \n\n# IMPACT\n\nThe sheer mass, firepower, and mystery surrounding Kingships has made them an object of extreme interest in the UEE. Due to their presence at key Vanduul invasions of Human space they have become symbolic of the extreme nature of the Vanduul threat. Human politicians frequently cite the threat of Kingships as justification for increased military spending.","g":["vanduul spacecraft","capital ship"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/138553b2-808f-456c-bad3-18721c1a9b9b"},
{"id":"vanduul-raids","gp":"Rw1gdnOKBp","t":"Vanduul Raids","k":"culture","c":["Vanduul"],"x":"Vanduul raids are attacks coordinated for the apparent purpose of harvesting or capturing resources. Raids vary in size; most are made up of a few [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) and employ quick hit and run tactics. Larger raids can sometimes include the deployment of \"[Harvesters](gp:0n1MYzOkG7),\" large vehicles used to pull resources from the surface of planets and moons. Frequent Vanduul raids in a planetary system are sometimes precursors to invasion.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0457af27-1579-4fc7-8145-76c125420483"},
{"id":"vanduul-territory","gp":"RPDAMLKP74","t":"Vanduul Territory","k":"culture","c":["Vanduul"],"x":"Known [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) territory consists of 16 planetary systems, with [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) connections to multiple points in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). The Caliban, Orion, Tiber, and Virgil systems were formerly controlled by the UEE, but were lost to the Vanduul after massed invasions. No permanent Vanduul settlements have been observed on any planet in Vanduul Territory. It is theorized that the Vanduul use celestial bodies purely for resource gathering. Newly discovered systems that have a significant Vanduul presence are given a military designation VS and a code name starting with the letter \"V\" such as the Vanguard system and the Voodoo system.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/98415261-50b6-40c0-b7e4-b2ddeed7a6f4"},
{"id":"vanduul-human-first-contact","gp":"RWwZDmxaXP","t":"Vanduul-Human First Contact","k":"history","c":["Exploration","Vanduul","Human"],"x":"On 9 August 2681 SEY, a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) raiding party invaded [Armitage (Orion III)](gp:RL6KLK4ylo), destroying the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) settlement of [Dell Township](gp:RkZ9mGOpD4). All 638 people were killed, save one. [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) authorities initially believed that outlaws were responsible for the attack. It wasn't until 15 September 2681 that the UEE military encountered their first [Vanduul Clan](gp:R9vzjxmEBx). Because the Vanduul do not operate under a unified government, the UEE was both unable to directly retaliate or seek to establish diplomatic relations. Relations between the UEE and the Vanduul remain hostile.","g":["vanduul clans","vanduul invasions","united empire of earth","armitage","orion iii","dell township","first contact"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d3c45900-5f7b-4b46-b0b3-01e5eddc1875"},
{"id":"vanguard-system-vs-02","gp":"Rz29PLnAqr","t":"Vanguard System (VS-02)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Vanguard system (designated VS-02 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares jump points with the [Leir](gp:0Ql7xwzmzL) and [Elysium](gp:RvlQrKZxPO) systems. Although no jump point connections to known Vanduul systems have been discovered, it is assumed that at least one must exist to facilitate easy travel between Vanguard and the rest of [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). It is known to have three planets. In SEY 2943, the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) explorer Christian Meyer entered Vanguard and observed a group of Vanduul living on the surface of Vanguard III. All other information on the system has been classified by the UEE military.","g":["vanguard system","vs-02","vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/154edaa4-f115-444d-ade8-fb2f6b4652a5"},
{"id":"vann-croshaw-iii","gp":"bZkk4l4j2D","t":"Vann (Croshaw III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human"],"x":"Vann (Croshaw III) is an inhabited planet in the [Croshaw system](gp:0qanKAEJwp)[terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) by the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is represented by two [Senators](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ). Located at the far outer edge of the [system's](gp:VaZwNWg372)[green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), its arctic environment supports a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) population along the planet's equator. Vann's economy, once dependent on mining, is now supported by tourism thanks to a thriving winter sports community and the spectacular nightly aurora, visible from all latitudes. Artists inspired by the aurora have begun to set up studios in the large, long-abandoned buildings once used by the mining industry.","g":["vann","croshaw iii","habitable","habitable planet","croshaw system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d0152493-034f-4f4d-b900-d1b778f16f56"},
{"id":"vasli-fragment-stone","gp":"0dQYZZzdno","t":"Vasli Fragment Stone","k":"culture","c":["Archaeology","Culture","Art"],"x":"# The Vasli Fragment Stone\nThe Vasli Fragment is the only known remnant of a stone stele theorized to have been created on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa) around 43,000 SEY ago. A script that has yet to be deciphered is engraved upon it on one side. It was most likely sculpted by the original inhabitants of Terra, who disappeared under unknown circumstances millennia before [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) colonization. In the years since it was discovered in 2832, the fragment has been the focus of debate among archaeologists, linguists, and the scientific community.\n \n# Description\nThe Vasli Fragment is a large granodiorite stone bearing an inscription on the face. The stone is dark grey in tint, with yellow crystalline streaks and swirls. The front surface is polished with an archaic script deeply incised upon it. A splash of silver and spots of polished yellow agate coat the left-side of the fragment, obscuring some of the text. The sides of the stone are smoothed from water erosion and show evidence of having been attached to a larger monument at some point, although no other fragments have ever been discovered.\n \n# Discovery\nIn the Summer of 2832, the University of Earth at Australia (UEA) conducted an archaeological expedition to Zaffre Bay near [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv) on Terra. The fragment was discovered around 150 km from the city, amid a haul of otherwise unremarkable debris. The leader of the expedition, Dr. Kleina Vasli, identified the markings on the stone as an inscription in an unknown language that she later named Terran A.\n \nThe fragment was taken to the Quasi Institute for Xenological Studies (QIXS) for analysis. Dr. Vasli and the linguists at QIXS connected the script to markers found at the Quasi ruins. This was the first time substantial writing samples had been discovered from the civilization that once inhabited Terra (nicknamed \"Atlanteans\" in popular culture). Over the next two years, linguists attempted to decipher the script but were unable to crack it.\n \n# From Earth to Terran Possession\nIn 2834, Dr. Vasli brought the fragment back with her to the UEA for further study. This decision was lambasted by the Terran academic community; many Terrans felt that the stone should remain where it was discovered. Upon Dr. Vasli's retirement in 2859, the UEA donated the stone to the Museum of Earth (MOE). It remained on display there for 75 years while the Terran government continually submitted requests for its repatriation.\n \nThe Vasli Fragment was finally returned in 2934. To commemorate this event, the Puglisi Collection commissioned Dr. Amelia Kesh, head chair of the Prime Linguistics Institute, and master sculptor Shinji Torusa to construct an exact copy of the Fragment. Replicas were made available for public sale in 2945.\n \n# In Popular Culture\nWhile the purpose of the Vasli Fragment is still unclear, it has been adopted by several movements in popular culture: Terran separatists use it as a symbol of their desire to break away from the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), while [Transitionalists](gp:0OaylwDmvv) tout the fragment as evidence that Humanity has many more things left to discover. Fringe groups also claim that the Vasli Fragment details the so-called Atlantean's conscious decision to leave Terra and influence the growth of all known civilizations. As the Fragment has yet to be translated, their claim is spurious at best.","g":["vasli fragment","terra","terra iii","zaffre bay","xenoarchaeology","xenolinguistics","puglisi collection"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0b292c60-908c-4bc5-a064-3bcad473ec5b"},
{"id":"vatra-pyro-5b","gp":"0dXpZm4xoL","t":"Vatra (Pyro 5b)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Vatra is the second moon from the gas giant [Pyro V](gp:RAXv9Yeqay), [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Its thick, high-pressure atmosphere of nitrogen and methane supports an ecosystem of plants that subsist on hydrocarbons instead of carbon dioxide. Some water is present on Vatra in the form of ice, but it is too cold on the surface for it to exist in a liquid state. Travelers who have harvested this ice in emergency situations report that, when melted, it is extremely bitter.","g":["vatra","pyro 5b","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","unclaimed moon","pyro system"]},
{"id":"vector-system-vs-01","gp":"VgEE5KQeWY","t":"Vector System (VS-01)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems"],"x":"The Vector system (designated VS-01 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares jump points with the [Tiber](gp:RMNLm97EDj) and [Kellog](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv) systems. In the final days of the [Siege of Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq), an enormous Vanduul clan in possession of a [Kingship](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm) entered the system through the Vector jump point and ultimately defeated the entrenched UEE forces, ending four years of fighting. While exact details of the system's makeup are classified, it is likely that it harbors one or more planets capable of supporting life.","g":["vector system","vs-01","vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/af4e1844-0e0e-4717-ba4e-615a6fb24399"},
{"id":"vega-2a","gp":"V8WWY9NAzM","t":"Vega 2a","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Vega 2a is a moon of [Aremis (Vega II)](gp:RkGGjdOwQz), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Its icy surface, remarkably smooth in some locations, is bright white and highly reflective. Jets of frozen water containing silica and salts that blast from the moon's many cryovolcanoes sometimes escape orbit and become part of Aremis' rings. The rest of the water turns into snow and falls to cover the surface.","g":["vega ii moon","aremis moon","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","vega system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b9037f30-ad9b-4533-a905-0ae7252e6a2d"},
{"id":"vega-2b","gp":"RPDDjEBYyE","t":"Vega 2b","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Vega 2b is the outermost moon of [Aremis (Vega II)](gp:RkGGjdOwQz), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A shepherd moon, it closely orbits the outer edge of Aremis' system of rings, clearing out stray debris in orbit around the planet which gives the rings a sharply defined edge. It is believed that the moon is a captured asteroid with possible origins in the [Vega belt alpha](gp:VarrQdgWBQ).","g":["aremis moon","vega ii moon","uninhabitable moon","not habitable","vega system","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/88393272-07f4-4b28-b3e4-cec9626a3ba0"},
{"id":"vega-belt-alpha","gp":"VarrQdgWBQ","t":"Vega Belt Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Vega belt alpha is a dense asteroid belt that orbits the star of the [Vega system](gp:0jGGODZ6O6), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Because of its location near the orbit of [Selene (Vega III)](gp:0qaa69qqNA), it is a popular location for aspiring miners to stake out their first claim and harvest resources. Permanent installations are less common, however, due to [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) raids.","g":["vega system","asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/eecd1eae-2b93-4638-a47d-654e77a2078d"},
{"id":"vega-i","gp":"VlMM6o1gPe","t":"Vega I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Vega I is a dwarf planet that orbits closely to the star of the [Vega system](gp:0jGGODZ6O6), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Small and very hot with temperatures that often exceed 200 C, Vega I is inhospitable to known forms of life. Its silicate crust covers a solid iron core, making the planet very dense in spite of its small size. Evidence suggests that a lava ocean once fully covered Vega I.","g":["vega system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0a47e073-f66e-4e6c-93e5-4ced9856818b"},
{"id":"vega-iv","gp":"RX33Yy62YJ","t":"Vega IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Vega IV is the fourth planet from the sun in the [Vega system](gp:0jGGODZ6O6), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). A gas giant, it has an reddish-brown outer atmosphere made up of hydrogen that is dotted with enormous clouds. Many independently-owned fuel refineries and refueling stations orbit Vega IV for easy access to its resources.","g":["vega system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/669272ab-e207-4c86-8e58-f0dc81bb80ff"},
{"id":"vega-system","gp":"0jGGODZ6O6","t":"Vega System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Human"],"x":"# VEGA SYSTEM\n\nThe Vega system is a planetary system in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). It consists of one mesoplanet, two terrestrial planets, one gas giant, one asteroid belt, and a G-type main sequence star. It was discovered in SEY 2402 and colonized only seven years later, owing to the presence of two planets that needed only minimal [terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) to be habitable. [Selene (Vega III)](gp:0qaa69qqNA) is recognized by the UEE, holding one seat in the [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ). [Aremis (Vega II)](gp:RkGGjdOwQz) was recognized by the UEE on 10 November 2945, in the aftermath of the [Battle of Vega II](gp:0Gz5mkprmg). \n\nAs one of the UEE systems bordering [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) territory, Vega is under heavy patrol by the UEE military. \n\n# PLANETARY SYSTEM\n\nThe system's star, Vega, is a G-Type main sequence star roughly 6.6 billion years old and about 80% the size of Sol. The closest planetary body to it is the mesoplanet Vega I, a hot and desolate rock with a silicate crust. Aremis (Vega II) and Selene (Vega III) are rocky planets terraformed to support [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) life. An asteroid belt with an active mining population sits between Selene and [Vega IV](gp:RX33Yy62YJ), a reddish-brown gas giant orbited by refineries. \n\n# DISCOVERY\n\nVega was discovered during the [Human Colonial Expansion Era](gp:0dQ4BjlQQm), thanks to the [United Nations of Earth](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) (UNE) Eastern Expansion Program. On 02 June 2402, surveyor Barbara Nagasaki found an anomaly in the Oberon system that suggested the presence of a [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY). After conferring with her son Marcus and her sister Vicki, who had accompanied her on this mission, the family decided to bring their ship closer to the anomaly to scan for its signature. Moments after they launched the scan, they accidentally triggered the jump, and the ship was pulled into interspace. Thanks to Marcus' experience in navigation and Vicki's quick piloting reflexes, they regained control of the ship and safely guided it to a new planetary system. Once the Nagasakis completed a survey of the new system, they safely traveled through the jump point a second time, journeyed to [Earth (Sol III)](gp:Rw1KpMJLZB), and reported their findings to the UNEEEP.\n\n# HISTORY\n\nLocated in the [green band](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), the planets Vega II and Vega III were lightly terraformed and opened for settlement in 2409. The population rapidly increased after 2412, when Alaine Viktus found the [Virgil](gp:RvlBgYrvEY)-Vega jump point in the Vega system. This discovery kicked off [Project Far Star](gp:0qnNAD6YKa), a program that provided funding to navjumpers and terraforming companies in an effort to expand the borders of the UNE outward from the Virgil system. \n\nAs expansion continued, Vega became a crossroads between such systems as [Orion](gp:VlMpwMky6d), [Tiber](gp:RMNLm97EDj), [Bremen](gp:02kd45eyxe), and [Terra](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4). Vega II was largely settled by the military, while Vega III rose as a center for commerce and culture, receiving its recognition from the UEE [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) as Selene in 2573. It seemed that the Vega system was well on its way to becoming one of the most influential in the UEE.\n\nIn 2712, however, its fortunes shifted. The Orion system, only three jumps away from Vega, was suddenly and unexpectedly [lost to the Vanduul](gp:RMXyYxqw8K). Population growth stalled. Sprawling construction projects built ahead of a projected population increase were abandoned, and the economy entered a recession. In 2736 and 2737, Selene's situation became even more dire when the Vanduul wrenched the [Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq) and [Virgil](gp:box5moyeoZ) systems from the grasp of the UEE, putting Vega directly on the border of [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). Refugees from Virgil chose to resettle on Vega II instead of Selene, due to its strong military presence. Experts believed that Vega would be the Vanduul's next target. Once one of the fastest-growing systems in the UEE, Vega's population growth entered the negatives.\n\nIn the mid 2800s, Vega II broke this pattern. Initially drawn by the cheap and available real estate, people from outside the system began to purchase homes and settle there. Then, in 2884, the Vanduul [invaded the Caliban system](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) instead of moving on Vega as had been predicted. The prevailing sense of danger in the system eased, especially on Vega II, under the direct protection of the military. By the early 2940s, it became more populous and prosperous than Selene, and the planet made a bid for Senate recognition. \n\nThe feared Vanduul invasion finally arrived in 2945, when a large [Clan](gp:R9vzjxmEBx) accompanied by a rarely-sighted [Kingship](gp:V3qWn9Dlvm) entered the system and launched a direct attack on Vega II. The [UEE Navy's](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) 2nd Fleet, commanded by Admiral [Ernst Bishop](gp:ReJaavPB3k), had been tracking scouts of this Clan and was in the area when the attack was launched. After a lengthy battle, the vastly outnumbered UEEN forces managed to destroy the Kingship and drive the Vanduul out of the system. The effects on Vega II were devastating; entire cities were wiped out and the death toll was in the millions. \n\nIn the aftermath of the attack, [Imperator Costigan](gp:VJOzBxdJ28) and the UEE Senate officially recognized Vega II as Aremis and Edward Aemile as its first senator. Buildings damaged in the Battle of Vega II have since been restored or replaced. \n\n# CULTURE\n\nVega is known throughout the UEE for its food. Selene's low cost of living and available land supports an urban farming movement in most of the planet's cities. In [Titus](gp:0dXZG3ZBOw), the planet's most populous city, there is a rising number of farm-to-table restaurants supported by city-grown fruits and vegetables. The nature of the food served changes depending on the time of year and what can be grown in each locale. On Aremis, the food culture is centered around molecular gastronomy. Elaborate meals based on experimental techniques are commonplace in [New Corvo](gp:RWwZqmP1w4). \n\nBecause it is located on the border of Vanduul territory, the threat of Vanduul invasion never fully leaves the consciousness of the people of Vega. Absurdist art, reflective of existential dread and the folly of war, is popular on Selene. There is also an artistic movement towards returning to nature. Bizarre pieces that express irrationality and degradation of form can be found in local galleries as easily as a sculpture made entirely from reclaimed or organic materials. Aremis, home to many descendants of refugees from Orion, Tiber, Caliban, and Virgil, offers a contrasting picture; the art there is decadent, sensuous, and experimental.","g":["uee system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/23f9d551-2407-47cd-80c4-2c0e950e0606"},
{"id":"vendetta-system-vs-04","gp":"V7dlg37mpA","t":"Vendetta System (VS-04)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Vendetta system (designated VS-04 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares no publicly known jump points with any other systems. The few intelligence reports that have been made public about this system suggest that it may be indirectly connected with [Orion](gp:VlMpwMky6d), but jump point connections and all other information on Vendetta is classified by the UEE military.","g":["vendetta system","vs-04","vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/89c92adf-38bf-49b2-8889-f58e95e7de8c"},
{"id":"venus-sol-ii","gp":"RL6kwDB9l3","t":"Venus (Sol II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Venus is the second planet from the sun of the Sol system, [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). A smog planet with a dense, high-pressure atmosphere, it has never been successfully [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) although [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) have made countless attempts since they first began terraforming other planets. Venus is orbited by multiple permanent space stations, some home to long-term colonies, and others used as terraforming research platforms by various corporate and scientific organizations.","g":["venus","sol ii","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","sol system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fc33b11b-e59c-41a4-8f1a-836cdbd31416"},
{"id":"verified-offworld-laser-technologies-volt","gp":"0qakL3YD1W","t":"Verified Offworld Laser Technologies (VOLT)","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Weapons","Human"],"x":"Verified Offworld Laser Technologies (VOLT) is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of energy weapons. The company specializes in producing handheld and ship weapons based on existing and proven technology rather than investing in an internal research department to innovate, like many of their competitors. This has allowed them to offer their products at below market rates and makes them a popular choice among purchasers who are cost conscious. These lower prices may also be indicative of lower quality manufacturing technique, as the company has frequently been plagued with reliability complaints. However, a formal investigation into their products in 2939 did not reveal a higher than average rate of failure. The VOLT lineup includes weapons such as the Zenith sniper rifle, Prism shotgun, Pulse energy pistol, and Stinger repeating laser.","g":["weapons manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/28ea838f-5db9-4474-a2e4-b56f47ac232d"},
{"id":"veritas-system-vs-05","gp":"Var5ZYB9wp","t":"Veritas System (VS-05)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Veritas system (designated VS-05 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares no known jump points with any other systems. It is included in UEE star charts as a part of [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), but little other information is known about it. In SEY 2945, an episode of the [Plain Truth](gp:bZwQ6lpJEd) explored a claim that the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) had met with Vanduul known to be based in Veritas.","g":["veritas system","vs-05","vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b1a6ac13-6344-43b1-99e2-602b60979d19"},
{"id":"vermilion-system","gp":"0ODWLrArDe","t":"Vermilion System (VS-11)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Vermilion system (designated VS-11 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares no publicly-known jump points with any other systems. Included in UEE star charts as a part of [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), all details on the system's makeup are classified. As a [Triggerfish](gp:0rxrqgzgP6) prank in SEY 2924, an anonymous jokester took out an ad in Mars Today advertising \"...fresh, sweet Vermilion apples, created by the Vanduul of the Vermilion system and hand delivered right to your door.\" This led to a flurry of inquiries and stirred up such fervor on spectrum that the UEE had to issue a statement assuring the public that Vermilion apples originated on Earth (Sol III).","g":["vermilion system","vs-11","vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0d5cfc4c-95a7-4743-a014-a8b36b06c2af"},
{"id":"vesper-system","gp":"R4jrNJZAr5","t":"Vesper System (VS-08)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Vesper system (designated VS-08 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares no publicly-known jump points with any other systems. It is included in UEE star charts as a part of [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), but little other information is known about it. In SEY 2919, the [University of Rhetor](gp:bZkZGKGP8d) released a paper describing signals in a strange language that they were unable to decode. They tentatively concluded that the communications originated from the Vesper system, but stated that further research was needed to prove or disprove this hypothesis.","g":["vesper system","vanduul system","vanduul territory","vs-08"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d0ca2eda-9db2-4632-a3b4-6262e09b916d"},
{"id":"vfg-industrial","gp":"01LQJodqPB","t":"VFG Industrial","k":"company","c":["Commerce"],"x":"VFG Industrial is a spacecraft hangar manufacturer that produces personal hangars designed for extreme environments. A wholly-owned subsidiary of [ArcCorp](gp:0dQ47zYd6O), VFG adapts asteroid mining techniques to hangar construction, allowing them to bury well-equipped hangars deep inside large asteroids and other planetoids. The VFG Industrial team maintains a unit of zero gravity workers and invests heavily in advanced excavation equipment.","g":["hangar manufacturer","arccorp (corporation)"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d26e631c-0675-4811-9dc3-8dabb627dc48"},
{"id":"vid","gp":"Vy2xAJ22zW","t":"Vid","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Vid is a term for any moving audiovisual media recorded via an electronic medium, such as content that is produced for and broadcast over [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q). Feature-length films, serial broadcasts, limited series, documentaries, and other types of audiovisual media all fall under the umbrella of vids. The term derives from the Latin video \"I see.\"","g":["vids","spectrum"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b7477111-2c93-47fc-933d-5a8df8bb71e1"},
{"id":"vidpro","gp":"bZkajJAEzD","t":"Vidpro","k":"culture","c":["Entertainment","Human"],"x":"Vidpro is a Spectrum site that presents the aggregate critical scores of [vids](gp:Vy2xAJ22zW) and other entertainment. Reviews from other outlets, cataloged and curated by the moderators of the site, are added together and averaged out to produce the final score. Non-critics are invited to submit their own scores, which are again added together with other submitted scores and averaged out to produce a final audience review. Vidpro also writes its own reviews.","g":["spectrum site"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/298e0950-f54f-45a6-b422-995104cc3b1f"},
{"id":"viking-system-vs-03","gp":"Vy2av35L6o","t":"Viking System (VS-03)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Viking system (designated VS-03 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares jump points with the [Caliban](gp:0jGyPQ1r5m) and [Orion](gp:VlMpwMky6d) systems. In the decades leading up to the [Fall of Caliban](gp:0Gz5DNryvE) in SEY 2884, it was one of the launch points for frequent Vanduul raids into the system. It is therefore believed that Viking likely has at least one planet that is being harvested by the Vanduul. All other information on the system is classified by the UEE military.","g":["viking system","vs-03","vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0b5773c0-b493-434b-8126-2091b6f00106"},
{"id":"vili-odin-2a","gp":"0dXE5Ny6Qd","t":"Vili (Odin 2a)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Vili (Odin 2a) is the moon of [Odin II](gp:0KxloXyPAM), [Odin system](gp:RX3jMavYGk), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Cold and snowy, the largest settlement on Vili is [Raleigh Station](gp:RkZ9rDD944), a former base of operations for a now-defunct weapons testing company. The station now serves as a waypoint for civilian contractors to bring in supplies and ferry out hazardous materials from Odin II.","g":["vili","odin 2a","odin system","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1b38c2cb-e33b-42d7-a42a-a4f9d7a376aa"},
{"id":"vindel","gp":"bEzz96Yxz2","t":"Vindel","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"# VINDEL\n\nThe vindel is a detritivorous fish indigenous to the shallow freshwater river and ponds of Locke (Idris IV), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Like other detritivorous animals, it feeds on the waste and dead material that collects at the bottom of bodies of water. The tentacles on its head aid the vindel in digging through the substrate to find food. Because of its small size and the voracity of its appetite, the vindel is favored by aquarium enthusiasts to control algae blooms and consume the waste of other fish. \n\n# DESCRIPTION\n\nA vindel can be identified by its distinctive mottled green scaleless skin and the six tentacles that sprout from the front of its flattened head. Instead of eyes, vindels have two false eye spots on their backs, which are used to deceive potential predators. The false eyes double as electroreceptors that alert the vindel if a potential predator gets too close. They have four triangular, blue-green pectoral fins, a long, thin dorsal fin, and blue-green tail fins. Over a 20 year life cycle, the vindel grows no more than 25 cm long. \n\n# BEHAVIOR AND ECOLOGY\n\nOn Locke, vindels exist in every climate except the arctic. They are highly adaptive, capable of breathing in very murky water, and have even been found in brackish water near the mouths of rivers. Water that has been purchased on or harvested from Locke must be thoroughly inspected for vindels before it is taken off world. Vindels that have made it into the water supply of spacecraft have been known to survive there for up to two standard weeks before starving. \n\nIn the wild, vindels spawn in the spring and summer, or when the water that they inhabit reaches a temperature of between 21 and 29 degrees Celsius. When they are ready to spawn, the male locates a nesting area such as between rocks, in the roots of plants, undercuts of banks, or other areas in which the eggs can be protected from strong currents. After the female lays her eggs, the male fertilizes them and drives the female from the nest. He then guards the eggs, chasing off predators and fanning them with his fins to keep them free of excessive sediment. The eggs hatch after roughly 12 standard Earth days. After all the eggs have hatched, the male leaves, and the fry disperse. Vindels can spawn every three standard weeks.\n\nThe fry that are not eaten by predators or otherwise killed reach maturity in about one Standard Earth Year. They generally do not breed until they have reached at least 15 cm in length.\n\n# INVASIVE SPECIES\n\nThanks to its hearty constitution and appetite for algae, the vindel has become a popular aquarium fish since its discovery in 2494 by [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO) surveyors. A vindel needs little supplementary feeding unless it is the only fish in its tank, and can survive in a wide range of temperatures. However, these attributes have also made it an invasive species in many parts of the UEE. It was so successful in taking root on Reisse (Rhetor III) that it caused the extinction of 11 other indigenous detritivores before the [Governors Council](gp:0rqzA55WZ3) was able to enact measures to get it under control. Fish enthusiasts who have released their vindels into the wild are subject to hefty fines.","g":["locke","idris iv","fish"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f5e6b974-4493-41ea-9162-b69c19d2c31f"},
{"id":"violet-curcuma","gp":"RX3o7Poknq","t":"Violet Curcuma","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The Violet Curcuma is a genetically modified plant created by [Rayari Inc.](gp:0jGnJnMwke) to grow on newly [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) worlds that orbit dim stars. Given a fractal structure to aid in the absorption of available light, the plant is dark in color, with deep purplish red and green leaves. The rhizomes the plant produces have medical applications and are edible, providing an easy-to-grow food resource to newly-formed settlements on colony worlds.","g":["rayari inc"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5335df43-e164-460b-91be-8d3fde6bd8ad"},
{"id":"virgil-iii","gp":"V8WagLl2Nx","t":"Virgil III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Virgil III is the third planet from the sun of the [Virgil system](gp:RvlBgYrvEY), located in [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74). An ice giant, it has a stormy atmosphere of hydrogen and helium that shrouds the significant amounts of volatiles such as water, ammonia, and methane that can be found in its depths. A rocky core lies under its volatile mantle.","g":["virgil system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","vanduul planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9866b29e-ba15-4463-96f2-7c2fb5d47238"},
{"id":"virgil-ltd","gp":"0qakL3DmJ5","t":"Virgil Ltd","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Virgil Limited is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) multidisciplinary manufacturer of combat armor, specialized industrial armor, and powered armor. Headquartered on [Aremis (Vega II)](gp:RkGGjdOwQz), the company has a reputation for creating durable, quality products. Their gear is frequently used as official uniforms by myriad organizations, including much of the armor worn by [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) agents. The Zeus System Titan armor and the TruDef-Pro combat armor are among its bestselling models.","g":["armor manufacturer"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f0f3e519-7b1e-4e09-9692-f5f3138451f5"},
{"id":"virgil-system","gp":"RvlBgYrvEY","t":"Virgil System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Virgil system is a planetary system within [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), formerly of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE). Discovered in SEY 2412, it was colonized by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) soon after as a part of [Project Far Star](gp:0qnNAD6YKa) and became a system renowned for its agriculture and lush vegetation. [Cyrene (Virgil I)](gp:VlMBNGnxK5) in particular was covered in tropical forests and densely populated cities. The system was ransacked by the [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) in 2737, immediately following the [Siege of Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq). Now occupied by the Vanduul, many of Virgil's celestial bodies are being strip-mined by [Clans](gp:R9vzjxmEBx) passing through the system, and Cyrene has been rendered nearly uninhabitable.","g":["vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/73692cf7-9830-474d-8b40-eb54811365a5"},
{"id":"virgo-system-vs-06","gp":"bZkewEGZrO","t":"Virgo System (VS-06)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Virgo system (designated VS-06 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)(UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares no known jump points with any other systems. Public information on Virgo is sparse. In the popular speculative novel *Beyond the Bounds of War* in SEY 2950, the author set the capital of his fictionalized Vanduul Empire in the Virgo system.","g":["virgo system","vs-06","vanduul territory","vanduul system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3cd7b2c2-55d6-454b-97c7-0efe8ba78703"},
{"id":"void","gp":"RWozkp8l82","t":"Void","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Vanduul"],"x":"The \"Void\" is the official [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6)[Navy (UEEN)](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) designation for a standard bomber operated by [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO) forces. Although UEE intelligence data on the Void bomber available to the public is extremely limited, it is known that the spacecraft is capable of carrying both explosive torpedoes and manned boarding craft. It was a pair of Void bombers believed to be responsible for the 2945 raid on Diamond Jim's Fuelporium in the Oberon system, which left no survivors.","g":["vanduul void","vanduul spacecraft","bomber","heavy bomber"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/470ba15b-2048-48eb-b519-86548b8254a3"},
{"id":"volt-system-vs-12","gp":"V7dlZA9ZJk","t":"Volt System (VS-12)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Volt system (designated VS-12 by [the United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares no publicly-known jump points with any other systems. Included in UEE star charts as a part of [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), it is confirmed to have at least one planet. UEE-based company [Verified Offworld Laser Technologies](gp:0qakL3YD1W) (VOLT) came under fire in SEY 2945 after the [Battle of Vega II](gp:0Gz5mkprmg) for having the same name as a Vanduul system. In response, the company made a substantial monetary donation to Vega relief efforts.","g":["volt system","vanduul system","vanduul territory","vs-12"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/02de37b3-06a2-47fe-a990-1858e784eead"},
{"id":"voodoo-system","gp":"V3GPNMrMdA","t":"Voodoo System (VS-10)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Voodoo system (designated VS-10 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares no publicly-known jump points with any other systems. It is included in UEE star charts as a part of [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), but little other information is known about it. A Vanduul ace that gained notoriety in SEY 2912 was named for this system. Notable for their habit of stalking patrols rather than engaging in face-to-face dogfights, Voodoo was primarily a distance killer, choosing to target the least threatening ships before moving onto the larger ones. They were reportedly killed in 2914 when attempting to target a small colony in the [Nul system](gp:VgEnlpqyJ9).","g":["voodoo system","vs-10","vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4575ef47-f5c8-4ec9-ae7e-5a552e0c69af"},
{"id":"vosca-elysium-iii","gp":"R9vQWkLNNM","t":"Vosca (Elysium III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Human","Tevarin"],"x":"Vosca is the third planet from the sun of the [Elysium system](gp:RvlQrKZxPO), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6), and is home to a small population of [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X). Largely covered with an arid desert, water is scarce on the surface of Vosca, except near the north and south poles. To cope with persistent drought conditions, water farms are common. Some mobile operations travel across the landscape just ahead of the solar terminator, staying on the planet's cooler nighttime side to increase their output. Many settlements, such as the arcology [Reza's Landing](gp:Vgg7jB2YE9), are constructed under protective domes due to persistent, violent sandstorms.","g":["vosca","elysium iii","habitable","habitable planet","elysium system","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ba4367bc-9252-4b80-8d05-3bf5d813a866"},
{"id":"voyager-direct","gp":"V7dgpKQ7rL","t":"Voyager Direct","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Voyager Direct is a general marketplace for goods that is widely utilized in the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE). Founded by former-hauler Cary Lindle in 2898, the company does not have its own line of products but rather acts as a third party storefront for sellers who wish to offer their goods to a wider range of people. In addition to having storefronts throughout the UEE, Voyager Direct offers its customers a popular [Spectrum](gp:VaZwen9E2Q)-based shopping service where they can remotely order various products. In 2936, the company was accused of illegal price-fixing by the Trade and Development Division of the UEE. The matter was settled out of court.","g":["general retail"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5fa69395-38d9-44d3-ae24-1203a5322a70"},
{"id":"vulcan","gp":"0qaJ8dOrgp","t":"Vulcan","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human","Military"],"x":"The Vulcan is a refuel, rearm and repair spacecraft manufactured by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) for the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military. First launched in SEY 2594, it was commissioned by the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) after they requested proposals for a medium-sized support spacecraft. After a successful trial period, the UEEN promoted the ship into active service as its standard front-line support ship during such conflicts as the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv) (2603 - 2610) and the [Siege of Tiber](gp:0OaBY5pGrq) (2732 - 2736). Since its introduction, it has been upgraded many times, and civilian models of the Vulcan have been offered to the public since the early 27th century.","g":["aegis dynamics","repair","medium repair","refuel","medium refuel","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ecb532d4-1dee-46ee-aa0a-16b4747ed2b9"},
{"id":"vulture","gp":"RPDAMBAOr4","t":"Vulture","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Vulture is a single-pilot salvage spacecraft manufactured by [Drake Interplanetary](gp:RLMm9KeZed) and first released in SEY 2938. It was designed for long-term solo operations in unclaimed or otherwise dangerous locations. Each Vulture is built with a cargo bay for the storage of harvested materials, along with scraper beams for efficient salvage and an industrial-grade tractor rig.","g":["drake interplanetary","salvage","light salvage","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cd09fb5a-9b91-4e28-b1cd-a1e2b26a9ab7"},
{"id":"vulture-system","gp":"01Lx6KLKO8","t":"Vulture System (VS-09)","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Vanduul"],"x":"The Vulture system (designated VS-09 by the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE)) is a [Vanduul](gp:VpGPp92gdO)-controlled planetary system that shares a jump point with the [Orion system](gp:VlMpwMky6d). In SEY 2712 on 16 February, thousands of Vanduul ships erupted from the previously-unknown jump point and initiated the [Battle of Orion](gp:RMXyYxqw8K). After two days of fighting, the UEE was forced to retreat and cede Orion to the Vanduul. It is included in UEE star charts as a part of [Vanduul territory](gp:RPDAMLKP74), but all other details on it are classified.","g":["vulture system","vs-09","vanduul system","vanduul territory"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2dbafbfa-af16-40fa-81f2-be0af0ecdfed"},
{"id":"vuur-pyro-5f","gp":"RWoOv9a47m","t":"Vuur (Pyro 5f)","k":"place","c":["Moons"],"x":"Vuur is the sixth moon from the gas giant [Pyro V](gp:RAXv9Yeqay), [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Thanks to an increased greenhouse effect in its dense carbon dioxide atmosphere, it is unusually warm for a moon so distant from its sun. Its carbon-rich soil supports forms of vegetation that utilize crystalline carbon in their base structures. Before the system was overtaken by outlaws in the early 27th century, these plants were a popular subject of research among botanists.","g":["vuur","pyro 5f","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","pyro system","unclaimed moon"]},
{"id":"wala-stanton-3b","gp":"V3GqNknrr2","t":"Wala (Stanton 3b)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"Wala is the second-closest moon of [ArcCorp (Stanton III)](gp:bBzpNY6ANd). Naturally-formed veins of blue-green crystal jutting from the moon's surface are visible from orbit. [ArcCorp](gp:0dQ47zYd6O) operates a number of surface mining facilities on Wala. Although the thin atmosphere and bitter cold make life on Wala challenging, organizations in search of lighter business restrictions than those on ArcCorp have established themselves there.","g":["wala","stanton 3b","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","arccorp moon","stanton iii moon","uee moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a67a6887-b2db-41a4-aba6-5fb19d45b3cb"},
{"id":"walleye-ellis-ix","gp":"0n1Ppn9Kr9","t":"Walleye (Ellis IX)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Walleye (Ellis IX) is a large gas giant in the [Ellis system](gp:RxnBEBWBjQ), [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Primarily used as a refueling world for passing freighters and warships, the skyline is dotted by refineries that keep fuel in steady supply. The planet's nickname comes from the strange storms that occur deep within the planet's atmosphere that cause white spots to appear. These spots are said to resemble the eyeshine of the walleye fish, an animal found on Earth (Sol III).","g":["walleye","ellis ix","ellis system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7a49a662-d711-4703-8d61-4a8fb544b667"},
{"id":"warden","gp":"0QxYDWPE7l","t":"Warden","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Vanguard Warden is a deep space fighter created by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv) for the United Empire of Earth Navy (UEEN). Its base model is a twin-engine, multi-crew ship designed to perform long duration missions that would otherwise be outside the reach of shorter-range fighters. Though it is less maneuverable than other Navy spacecraft like the Hornet, it is capable of taking more damage and carrying more munitions. Other variants of the Vanguard include the [Harbinger](gp:Vgg7Jj5Dge) fighter-bomber, the [Sentinel](gp:VY4Wog4K8e) electronic warfare platform and the [Hoplite](gp:VpGEjz6qL1) dropship.","g":["vanguard","aegis dynamics","fighter","human spacecraft","military spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1408770c-94e0-425f-84a4-0d8faa1a7248"},
{"id":"warlock","gp":"V3qgyY8AyW","t":"Warlock","k":"vehicle","c":["Military","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Warlock is a variant of the [Avenger](gp:ReJanvr73r) patrol ship developed by [Aegis Dynamics](gp:RAdk7jx5Kv). The Warlock replaces the rear living space of the standard model with an electro-magnetic pulse (EMP) generator. The [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) and [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) both use Avenger Warlocks for battlefield support and non-lethal apprehension missions; Aegis also makes a limited number of Warlocks available on the civilian market.","g":["aegis dynamics","interdiction","avenger series","military spacecraft","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5ac0a9b9-28ee-4987-b49d-acee779ec86b"},
{"id":"warlord-coraththal","gp":"RkGxWGQ2Qp","t":"Warlord Corath'Thal","k":"people","c":["Tevarin","People"],"x":"Corath'Thal was a [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X) Warlord who led an armed insurgency against the [United Empire of Earth](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) (UEE) during the [Second Tevarin War](gp:bE3rPrz3Pv). A brilliant and charismatic leader, he unified many Tevarin that had been scattered in the [First Tevarin War](gp:bZwQm3meJM) in order to reclaim their homeworld [Kaleeth](gp:VarAXY2zy2) (Jalan/Elysium IV) from the UEE. Corath'Thal utilized guerilla tactics to quietly move through systems and attack where the UEE military wasn't. This approach proved to be devastating against the UEE, who struggled to anticipate where Corath'Thal would attack next. However, as the war dragged on, the Tevarin forces fell in number and could not be replenished. When it became clear after the [Battle of Centauri](gp:VlM1yqjoNv) that the Tevarin would once again lose against the [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), Corath'Thal and his fleet engaged in a final push to Kaleeth, where they lowered their ships' shielding and burned up in the planet's atmosphere.","g":["second tevarin war"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ac376a2d-3957-4fcd-bacb-ad70c1df30f5"},
{"id":"weaver-palm","gp":"0QlnJaWkeN","t":"Weaver Palm","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The Weaver Palm is a genetically modified plant created by [Rayari Inc.](gp:0jGnJnMwke) to produce a renewable, strong, lightweight, and flexible fiber that could be utilized by colonists on newly [terraformed](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) worlds. The fiber can be processed into thread that can then be used to weave fabric. Low maintenance and able to withstand periods of drought, the plant can grow in a wide variety of climates.","g":["rayari inc","trees"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c98ce781-061c-4aa2-82ce-2a59de077902"},
{"id":"whammers","gp":"02k6zX3GLy","t":"Whammer's","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human","Food and Beverages"],"x":"Whammer's is a fast food chain in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) that serves burgers, sandwiches, and sides. Owned by Interstellar Restaurant Management, it was founded in SEY 2801 by brothers Sidney and Callahan Westmoreland on [Severus (Kiel III)](gp:V3GOdL9lYN). The low-cost sandwiches served at Whammer's found popularity amongst the remaining military personnel stationed on Severus, enabling the Westmoreland brothers to expand Whammer's across the planet. After catering the [Intergalactic Aerospace Expo](gp:R4jpEgezde) in 2916, the restaurant exploded in popularity and soon founded franchises on other worlds. Whammer's is known for its proprietary Crave Sauce, which is used on every sandwich on its menu, and its Skwash Stix, or zucchini fries.","g":["fast food","food company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f31b19ea-8751-4d32-a16e-a3768c556cd1"},
{"id":"whitleys-guide","gp":"V8WgdOP8px","t":"Whitley's Guide","k":"culture","c":["Publications","Entertainment","Human"],"x":"*Whitley's Guide* is a consumer-centric magazine released by Gallivan Publishing that features in-depth analysis and reviews of spacecraft, vehicles, and related items. Created by Sal Whitley and Darby Keilich, it was first published in 2856 and has been in continuous print since. Editors of *Whitley's Guide* require their reviewers to write as objectively as possible about the products that they test. In 2950, the magazine partnered with Terra Spectrum Broadcasting to launch a show by the same name, hosted by [Jax McCleary](gp:RL6MjgGJJ3). Although McCleary's enthusiastic style is a departure from the serious tone of the print magazine, his popularity with spacecraft enthusiasts made him the network's first and only choice as host.","g":["magazine","spectrum show","reviews"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9a5e07ce-e72c-4cac-968f-61e7aff923a6"},
{"id":"widow","gp":"RX3en1jpOK","t":"WiDoW","k":"culture","c":["Illegal Activity","Science and Technology"],"x":"WiDoW, also known as white diawirline or WDW, is a Class A narcotic that is known for its distinctive black color that can stain the veins and create web-like patterns in the skin of intensive users. When injected intravenously, it causes immediate pain relief, greatly lessens anxiety, and triggers a feeling of euphoria. However, repeated use can lead to collapsed veins, liver and kidney disease, heart conditions, and myriad other health issues.\n\n# ORIGIN\nIn SEY 2861, the discovery of the [Oso system](gp:bZkAMEarPd) brought government survey teams to [Oso II](gp:Rw19lYy9D7). Before the detection of the [Osoians](gp:0NwpEy2LNM) made travel to Oso II forbidden under the [Fair Chance Act](hhttps://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/RXlXmnaYGP-fair-chance-act), the teams collected a handful of unique native plant samples. One of these, named \"nightspiral\" for the multicolored swirls on its flowers, struggled to adapt to conditions outside of Oso II. Scientists crossbred the plant using grafting and genetic modification until they created a stable hybrid that produced seeds containing alkaloids. They conducted investigations into the seeds' potential medical applications and intoxicating effects, but their reports were classified. \n\nIt is unclear how the seeds made their way out of the lab, but in 2867 a new injectable drug called NightNight appeared on the market. Derived from the nightspiral seeds, it produced a calming and euphoric effect and was sold under the promise that it was not addictive. Demand skyrocketed, but the prohibitive cost of NightNight's manufacture due to the challenges associated with rearing the nightspiral plant kept supply low. Evidence collected by the [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk) suggests that underground chemists began to iterate on the drug's recipe, eventually reaching a low-cost, purely synthetic version in 2879. \n\n# SPREAD\n\nThis new formula, sold under the ironic name \"white diawirline\" or \"WDW,\" rapidly spread throughout the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Users who sought NightNight were offered WDW instead, or were sometimes sold WDW being passed off as genuine NightNight. This tactic hooked more users than might have otherwise fallen under the drug's thrall and guaranteed continual sales for the dealer.\n\nIn 2880, WDW made headlines when socialite Khali O'Brien went through sudden, extreme weight loss and black veins appeared on her neck. Friends of O'Brien leaked stories to the press about her plight, and paparazzi began to incessantly tail her. After layers of concealer failed to hide the web-like patterns on her neck and O'Brien took to wearing black turtlenecks and scarves, one gossip columnist nicknamed her the \"Black Widow.\" The name soon stuck to the drug itself, and government officials formally classified it as WiDoW. \n\n# MITIGATION \n\nThe UEE has declared WiDoW use as \"one of the most significant public health issues of the 30th century.\" Billions of UEC have been poured into information campaigns, rehab facilities, addiction counseling, and more, but overall fatality rates among its users have not dropped. The Advocacy runs frequent crackdowns on known makers of WiDoW and offers rewards for bringing dealers to justice. They also arrest users, which credentialed substance abuse counselors and social workers say only makes the lives of these users worse and often ensures that they will not seek help. Activists argue that legalization is the only way to mitigate the harm of the drug, help users who want to become sober, and stop the profitable blackmarket trade. Few politicians support this stance.","g":["wdw","controlled substance","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/4f4d8e73-2998-4bdf-bf30-e9cde1d96723"},
{"id":"wildstar-racing","gp":"bEzDK2z7W8","t":"Wildstar Racing","k":"company","c":["Organizations"],"x":"Wildstar Racing is a racing league known as an affordable proving ground for amateur racers. Founded in SEY 2811 as a vid-sharing spectrum channel, in its early days it was a community of hobbyists who utilized abandoned infrastructure and interesting planetary environments to construct race courses. By 2943, the organization had made enough money from advertisers that it began to work with professionals to improve their tracks. They became an officially recognized league in 2952.","g":["spacecraft racing"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8cfb7a11-fa50-41be-a78f-5d1dd3f06376"},
{"id":"willsop","gp":"bZkaBkrwKd","t":"WillsOp","k":"company","c":["Human","Commerce"],"x":"WillsOp is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) limited liability corporation that produces targeting system hardware and software used in spacecraft. Established in SEY 2902, they saw limited market success until a 2922 computer virus infected the firmware updates of many major ship manufacturers. This virus locked shipboard sensor suites to greyscale mode, making them nearly unusable. Due to a difference in coding systems, the virus failed to infect WillsOp-made sensor operating systems. Many security-minded companies opened contracts with WillsOp and increased the company's stake in the market. They currently have a contract with the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) military and [Anvil Aerospace](gp:0qnN6Od6YD) to manufacture the radar system installed in [F7A-R Hornets](gp:RXlXgwDlDk) and by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) to install a custom targeting system for the [325a](gp:0QxYAAwjGN).","g":["computer manufacturer","spacecraft component manufacturer","widow","software company"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0a2087eb-09ac-486f-8d65-809f083f24fa"},
{"id":"wintle-design-company","gp":"VgE3k1zeyn","t":"Wintle Design Company","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"The Wintle Design Company is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) manufacturer of luxury craft goods, located in [Prime](gp:RLMmA78vBv) on [Terra (Terra III)](gp:RL6ZrMrLNa). Since its founding in 2895, the company has remained committed to using only master craftspeople and their apprentices to create artisanal furniture, home goods, spacecraft interiors, and other high-end items. In 2941, [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) partnered with the Wintle Design Company to equip the master suite of the [Constellation Phoenix](gp:VyvYqezlqW).","g":["commercial goods manufacture","furniture manufacture","constellation phoenix","prime","terra","terra iii"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/82ce780c-6cde-4865-9815-ef2cfd406656"},
{"id":"worldmaker","gp":"VlMxQMw23Y","t":"Worldmaker","k":"company","c":["Commerce","Human"],"x":"Worldmaker was a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) company. Founded in the mid-22nd century during the first terraforming boom, the company initially focused on perfecting terraforming technologies and ultimately engaged in large-scale planetary development. By the start of the 25th century, Worldmaker had acquired much of its own competition and had become the third largest terraforming conglomerate in the [United Nations of Earth (UNE)](gp:R4ZQpY83oO). In 2480, [Shubin Interstellar](gp:V7gM8ZBodA) acquired a controlling interest in Worldmaker, until they eventually merged the company into itself.","g":["terraforming company","shubin interstellar"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/625f368d-880e-4bfa-9b07-5863f24d709b"},
{"id":"wuotan","gp":"RWoYD9xlae","t":"Wuotan","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The wuotan is a woody, bioluminescent plant indigenous to the [Pyro system](gp:0ODxJM917N). Able to thrive in stormy environments, it has evolved to withstand gale-force winds and weather lightning strikes. When hit, the wuotan redirects some of the energy and stores the rest, using it in place of photosynthesis to create nutrients. It produces a seed of the same name that can be harvested and used as a temporary light source.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/30e3a9bc-5dc4-4a93-a0ed-72e8108416f0"},
{"id":"x1","gp":"VDoPD9Ejz1","t":"X1","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The X1 is an open-canopy snub spacecraft manufactured by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) and designed by famed ship engineer Alberto Vara and his company Infinity Custom. Constructed with specialized polymers to keep it light, the X1 is a luxury single-seater built for speed and agility. It can be utilized for light combat on the ground and in space, but doesn't come with a quantum drive or jump engine. The joint vector thruster placement and integrated engine technology help achieve its sleek overall profile.","g":["x1 series","touring","origin jumpworks","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ed1a734f-6f1d-480b-8e2c-4d60c5cc51ca"},
{"id":"x1-force","gp":"box5vN1oDr","t":"X1 Force","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The X1 Force is a variant of the [X1](gp:VDoPD9Ejz1) ultralight spacecraft developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) and two-time Aron Award winner ship engineer Alberto Vara's design company, Infinity Custom. The redesign upgrades weaponry and armor in exchange for a slight reduction in speed and handling. The most significant changes are the addition of a second shield generator and the switch from an M3A Laser Cannon to a CF-117 Bulldog Laser Repeater. Produced in smaller numbers than the other X1 models, Origin has marketed it to anyone interested in fast combat, ground interception, and infiltration missions.","g":["x1 series","origin jumpworks","pathfinder","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cd09478c-c8bf-4dca-a140-44c540a4e3dc"},
{"id":"x1-velocity","gp":"bmNrP5oD4E","t":"X1 Velocity","k":"vehicle","c":["Ground Transportation","Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The X1 Velocity is a variant of the [X1](gp:VDoPD9Ejz1) ultralight spacecraft developed by [Origin Jumpworks](gp:VY4WOMoj2v) and two-time Aron Award-winning ship engineer Alberto Vara's design company, Infinity Custom. As the name implies, the Velocity focuses primarily on improved speed and handling over the base X1. To that end, Origin engineers abandoned all the attached weaponry and converted the majority of the standard hull material into [Syntek](gp:VJOzQ3L29P) composites. The process ultimately removed eight percent of the original model's total weight, creating a variant popular among open canopy racers.","g":["origin jumpworks","x1 series","racing","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/dd2dff07-27b8-49c8-abb0-978e956e0b8d"},
{"id":"xenia","gp":"0ODJ2DE6rZ","t":"Xenia","k":"place","c":["Locations","Human"],"x":"Xenia is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-constructed space station in the [Baker system](gp:Rz2KGkv13N) that serves as a shipping hub for the [Covalex](gp:V3qgXNEGQW) corporation. It was built to support trade between the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Its habitation facilities and pressurized hangar bays provide support for spacecraft crews making long haul cargo runs.","g":["space station"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/d55d1123-9868-49a7-9f03-75c82dd131f4"},
{"id":"xenoanthropology","gp":"RL68B6WLKZ","t":"Xenoanthropology","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology"],"x":"Xenoanthropology is the scientific study of alien behavior, cultures, and societies. There are many branches of xenoanthropology, including linguistic, biological, social, and cultural. There is an ongoing debate in the field over the value of observational versus total immersion studies. Degrees in the discipline began to be offered at [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) universities in the 2440s, after [Banu-Human First Contact](gp:VY4Wnv7ZgW) in 2438.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1920ceb8-76e9-4992-bebe-e6f253afc2c7"},
{"id":"xenoarchaeology","gp":"0QlOdMyvPo","t":"Xenoarchaeology","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Archaeology"],"x":"Xenoarchaeology is the study of alien culture and history through the excavation of ancient sites and the analysis of physical materials. A [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) xenoarchaeologist, for example, may specialize in [Hadesian](gp:RPPxMqdkpE) artifacts, whereas a [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) xenoarchaeologist may be an expert in excavating ancient Human pottery. Xenoarchaeology is mainly concerned with recovering knowledge of prehistory, especially of extinct alien civilizations. It draws upon multiple disciplines and requires years of study, mentorship, and practice.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1c2467e8-563c-4696-8589-d846907a8b0e"},
{"id":"xenothreat","gp":"VgExkEAB19","t":"XenoThreat","k":"faction","c":["Human","Illegal Activity","Organizations"],"x":"XenoThreat is a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) outlaw group based in the Pyro system that is known for a violently anti-alien and anti-corporate ideology. Law enforcement believes that the group is primarily formed by corrupt ex-members of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) military. \n\nMost of its criminal activity was concentrated in the Pyro system until SEY 2949, when systems connected to Pyro such as [Stanton](gp:RX3lKBA3dq) and [Terra](gp:VlMX7Mo9B4) began to report on raids led by members of XenoThreat. In 2951, XenoThreat launched an organized raid into the Stanton system that was eventually repelled by a combination of [Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4), [Advocacy](gp:VDoP5pmODk), and [CDF](gp:0QxYZvMl8o) forces.","g":["outlaw factions","human outlaw factions","pyro outlaw faction","pyro system"],"img":"https://static.robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/upload/b0690189-d136-420e-a314-ce873186f46f"},
{"id":"xi-rila-v","gp":"RkGDJnlB2p","t":"Xi (R.il'a V)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Xi (R.il'a V) is the fifth planet from the sun of the [R.il'a system](gp:Rw1xWXME1B), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Classified by the Xi'an government as a habitation world, it was extensively developed and meticulously organized in order to support a vast populace. Like neighboring planet [Xōl'uu (R.il'a IV)](gp:VYLzwxDrre), Xi is friendly to visitors, and has multiple areas designated for mixed populations of [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4), and [Tevarin](gp:V8gJv3nB3X). The largest of these, the small city Kōri'lya, has a unique culture made up of a mish-mash of customs from various civilizations.","g":["xi","r.il'a v","habitable","habitable planet","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"xian","gp":"ReJwN9KJEj","t":"Xi'an","k":"species","c":["Xi'an","Civilizations"],"x":"The Xi'an are a spacefaring civilization that originated on the planet RyiXy'an (Hyoton III). They are capable of space flight, quantum travel, [jump point](gp:0rqzJPaMpY) navigation, and [planetary terraformation](gp:V3qgj8vjnj). Their leader, [Emperor Kr.ē](gp:VaZwmlmPQo), has reigned over the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) since SEY 2643 (MXY III.926). \n\n[Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) first [made contact](gp:R4ZQpYEEvx) with the Xi'an in the Xi'an-controlled Th.us'ūng system in SEY 2530 (MXY III.838), when Human-owned Gaia Planet Services attempted to start terraforming operations on Th.us'ūng III, having done so without approval from the government and without having surveyed the planet to learn that it was already inhabited. After first contact, the Xi'an and Human governments entered into a period of sustained conflict known as the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ). Military buildup on both sides resulted in the creation of the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) in SEY 2542 (MXY III.847) as a buffer between the two factions. At its height, the Perry Line consisted of eight planetary systems with jump points connecting Xi'an and Human territories. At the end of the Cold War, the Perry Line systems were demilitarized, divided, and annexed into the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) and the Xi'an Empire. The end of the Cold War has brought warmer relations between the two governments.","g":["xi'an empire","extant civilizations"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/5c583682-2bed-41be-b8f4-c146377450d2"},
{"id":"xian-calendar","gp":"R4ZQ89gBQx","t":"Xi'an Calendar","k":"culture","c":["Xi'an","Culture"],"x":"The [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) calendar (Modern Xi'an Year, *r.aiXy'an*) is measured by the celestial mechanics of their former homeworld, RyiXy'an (Hyoton III). It differs from the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) calendar in a number of significant ways; for example, each Xi'an year is equivalent to 1.28 Human years, is assigned a number counting upwards from when the current Imperial House ascended to the throne, and is prepended with a number that represents the corresponding [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) Age. The [First Imperial Age](gp:VDoPeW55W4) began in the Human year 19668 BCE, and was recorded by the Xi'an as I.0 (or 1.0) The current [Third Imperial Age](gp:R4ZejoYNEY) began in the Human year 1457, and was recorded by the Xi'an as as III.0 (or 3.0).","g":["xi'an time"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/cf303dae-9d72-4841-bd8f-eb27472106d9"},
{"id":"xian-clothing","gp":"VJXkBwlKDn","t":"Xi'an Clothing","k":"culture","c":["Xi'an","Culture"],"x":"Xi'an clothing is typically made of long-lasting materials, and is passed down the [family line](gp:box9JmxvWL) for use by younger generations. Even mass-produced clothing is made to last for centuries. Wealthier Houses possess custom livery worn only by members of the family. However, those in the [Xi'an Youth Counterculture](gp:bEz5Bdal8Q) movement have embraced a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-inspired trend of disposable garments. The Xi'an clothing industry is managed by House Tuēl and its satellite Houses.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/e2922cca-3a61-4fa7-82eb-89e6224424be"},
{"id":"xian-criminal-professionals-nyayua","gp":"bZkaBD5alD","t":"Xi'an Criminal Professionals (Nyayu'a)","k":"culture","c":["Xi'an","Culture"],"x":"Xi'an criminal professionals (nyayu'a) are [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) who are granted license by the Xi'an government to practice certain forms of crime. Similar to Human crime syndicates, these Xi'an [Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) double as disciplined organizations whose business involves criminal activity. In return for sanction from the Imperial House, these Houses sometimes act as police forces for their locations, curtailing the activity of potentially dangerous criminals from non-crime Houses and keeping crime at levels considered acceptable by the Xi'an government. Many Xi'an will pay regular protection fees to criminal Houses in advance to limit the extent of their losses if they become victims of crime themselves.","g":["xi'an criminal professionals"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ad787fd5-1258-43e6-be8a-a89242bb7429"},
{"id":"xian-cuisine","gp":"V3qvm96LeA","t":"Xi'an Cuisine","k":"culture","c":["Xi'an","Food and Beverages"],"x":"# Xi'an Cuisine\nXi'an cuisine is the traditional method by which [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) prepare their food for consumption. Rather than using heat to alter the nutrient bioavailability of ingredients as is traditionally done by [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2), Xi'an utilize aging and fermentation. Xi'an cannot digest the majority of fresh fare and are intolerant of hot or cold meals. Level of aging, type of fermentation, strength of flavor, and texture are the most important aspects of Xi'an food preparation. Humans consider Xi'an food to be harshly flavored.\n \n# History\nThe first indications of cultivated Xi'an cuisine arose when Xi'an established permanent homesteads. Before this time, they traveled in nomadic family groups, scouring the landscape for sustenance while protecting one another from predators. The hot, humid environment of their homeworld was conducive to rapid decay of potential food sources. Food with rich microbiomes such as carrion and rotted leaves made up the bulk of the early Xi'an diet. Predators kept them on the move. It wasn't until agriculture and animal husbandry were discovered that families were able to create long-term settlements fortified against natural predators, allowing them time and space to experiment with meal preparation techniques.\n \nMajor characteristics of contemporary Xi'an cuisine soon emerged. Bacteria, molds, yeasts, and spices that enhanced food with intense textural sensations and robust flavors were sought after and cultivated. Aged eggs collected from abandoned *s.āoth* nests became so popular that the lizard was domesticated. Meat harvested from animals allowed to die of natural causes became famous among prosperous families for being more tender and flavorful than meat from slaughtered animals; this attitude persists among Xi'an chefs today. Meat that was heavily spiced, left to age in the sun until soft and pungent, and served alongside strips of the leafy vegetable* nga.u'ii'yēl* became a favorite dish.\n \nThe discovery of fermentation revolutionized the Xi'an diet. Plants they couldn't previously digest, such as grain *pai'pun* and legume *pai'lio*, became staples of their new diet. Vessels used for fermentation doubled as long-term food stores, allowing families to stockpile their resources and expand beyond homesteads into state-like powers called Houses. Demand for spice and other food additives opened trade routes between distant locations. As Houses continued to grow, so did the Xi'an palate.\n \n# Flavor and Texture\nEvery Xi'an dish is constructed to balance texture with intensity of flavor. 13 favorable tastes, 13 favorable textures, and 13 unfavorable qualities were identified by members of [House Uai'i](gp:RMXyBdkAQA) in their treatise *Three Leaves of Flavor*. These were compiled into a text and sold to traders en route to other Houses. The treatise was hugely influential to Xi'an cuisine as an art. Even today, the ideal *y.iy'atin'tang* (multitextured) meal described in the treatise remains the end goal for Xi'an chefs.\n \n# Fermentation and Aging\nFermentation is the foundation of the Xi'an diet. Ingredients are typically cut into large pieces, then seasoned and placed inside a *tyixa'yetui* (fermentation vessel). The vessel is then placed inside the *nyuntui* (fermentation chamber), a temperature-controlled room with deeply grooved walls inoculated with colonies of yeast, mold, and bacteria. These *tya e Yii'ua* (House strains), unique to each House and closely guarded, are cultivated over generations. At first, the vessels are left open to invite the strains into the process. The vessels are then sealed, usually for months, before being opened again, cut into bite-sized pieces, placed on large dishes, and served alongside other meals, most often at room temperature (30 C).\n \nFood that isn't fermented is aged via air-curing, sun-ripening, drying, controlled rot, the addition of micro-organisms, or other methods. If a dish has been prepared well, a Xi'an might say that it is \"properly rotted.\" A bland dish might be described as \"lacking rot.\" This applies to beverages as well. One popular drink, *chui.y'o'sui*, is made from the aged blood of various animals and mixed with complimentary vinegars. Even purified water would be considered unpalatable to Xi'an; on Xi'an worlds, drinking water is enhanced with minerals and various micro-organisms for health and flavor.\n \n# Condiments\nXi'an eat only a few times per week. Shared meals are considered a big family affair. Even Xi'an who are traveling alone will choose to share tables with strangers at restaurants. At the center of a communal table filled with various dishes one can always find a *thauil* (condiments platter) loaded with seasonings and dressings that will impart various favorable flavors on one's food, such as *ki.s'a* (ammoniac; chemical; bitter), *ngi'pi* (itching; buzzing; pain), or *p.ūnt.a* (alcoholic, warming). Xi'an do not experience intoxication from consuming alcohol, and some more forward-leaning Xi'an restaurateurs on Oya III have added Human-influenced alcoholic seasonings to their menus.\n \n# Modern Trends\nSince the thawing of tensions between the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9), Xi'an have begun to explore Human styles of cooking. Dishes such as shiokara, blue cheeses, and lutefisk have been unreservedly embraced by Xi'an chefs. Cold-brewed pu-erh tea has made waves due to its similarity to *hai'pe*, a beverage steeped in sunlight from the leaves of a tropical pine tree. The beverage rotik is similarly popular among adventurously-minded Xi'an. This is especially notable because *nginguichui* (milky; creamy; like animal milk) has been considered an unfavorable food quality for hundreds of *millennia*. However, hot and cold food, also ill-regarded in the Xi'an tradition, seems unlikely to catch on.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6f152073-264c-4a49-8df1-be72738b282b"},
{"id":"xian-empire","gp":"0n96JkwNo9","t":"Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)","k":"faction","c":["Xi'an","Government"],"x":"The Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an) is a multi-system government headed by the [Xi'an Emperor](gp:VaZwmlmPQo) and inhabited by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj). Its capital system, Hyoton, is the location of the former Xi'an homeworld [RyiXy'an (Hyoton III)](gp:bBz9mEDyqO) and [Ka'ua (Hyoton IV)](gp:0qa4Zow7pk), the current home of the [Emperor](gp:VYLyPxQnpp). It is made up of thirteen known planetary systems. Political experts believe that there might be more systems that the Xi'an haven't divulged to other civilizations. The Xi'an Empire borders the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE) along a series of planetary systems formerly known as the Perry Line. It also shares a border with [Kr'thak](gp:RxNxDYkqzz) territory, though the exact coordinates of this border are not known.","g":["xi'an empire","xi'an government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/02357028-aba4-4871-9947-bf23a32d7ad9"},
{"id":"xian-government","gp":"RxnPD9P9ay","t":"Xi'an Government","k":"faction","c":["Government","Xi'an"],"x":"The Xi'an government is an absolute monarchy, headed by an Emperor and supported by a High Council of three advisers. The advisors are responsible for maintaining the [Xi'an Service (Pō't.ōngp.ū)](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ), each branch of which is overseen by another Council of Three. Below the family of the Emperor are the Houses: state-corporations run by and made up of vast, interconnected families. Each House oversees a single aspect of society or production, approved of or dictated by the Emperor. The [current Emperor](gp:VaZwmlmPQo), the last heir of the House of Kr.ē, has reigned since 2643.","img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c44c489b-49df-4933-9360-0a697e20e31e"},
{"id":"xian-house","gp":"box9JmxvWL","t":"Xi'an House (Yii'ua)","k":"faction","c":["Xi'an","Government","Culture"],"x":"A Xi'an House (Yii'ua), or Line is a complex social and familial body in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) made up of members of a single family. Houses serve the functions of states and corporations within the framework of the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government. Each House is allowed by the Emperor to serve one function deemed vital to the mutual prosperity of the Xi'an Empire.","g":["xi'an house","xi'an government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f5d6036f-99e6-460a-aca6-af6bf221de8f"},
{"id":"xian-language","gp":"VY4k6m5DQm","t":"Xi'an Language (uo'aXy'an)","k":"culture","c":["Xi'an","Culture"],"x":"The Xi'an Language (uo'aXy'an) is a group of languages spoken by the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj). It refers to the standard dialect, the military dialect, and countless other dialects dispersed throughout the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Most Xi'an dialects are mutually intelligible due to the re-organization of Xi'an culture after the end of the [Great Divide](gp:VyvYA5qmqX) (20044 - 19770 BCE) and the requirement for all Xi'an to spend 30 years in the [Xi'an Service (Pō't.ōngp.ū)](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ). The same standardized writing system is used across all Xi'an dialects.","g":["xi'an language","language"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/75f6a606-313a-4a46-9af4-4cece585f1aa"},
{"id":"xian-service","gp":"0dQJ96mOeZ","t":"Xi'an Service (Pō't.ōngp.ū)","k":"faction","c":["Government","Xi'an"],"x":"The Xi'an Service (Pō't.ōngp.ū), or [Imperial](gp:VYLyPxQnpp) Bureaucracy is a bureaucratic and military body made up of [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) aged 40 to 70. The backbone of the reigning Imperial House (Yii'uaTao\"), the Service is compulsory for all Xi'an. It was created in the wake of the [Xi'an Civil War (20044 - 19770 BCE)](gp:VyvYA5qmqX) as a method to instill an overarching loyalty to the Imperial House and the Xi'an people rather than an individual Xi'an's personal [House](gp:box9JmxvWL) of origin. While most return to their own Houses after their Service period ends, some elect to stay in the Service permanently.","g":["xi'an service","xi'an government"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/3a666ac9-2a94-400b-96f3-1cbd2dcfaef7"},
{"id":"xian-terraforming","gp":"R6dWOrLEM4","t":"Xi'an Terraforming","k":"culture","c":["Xi'an","Science and Technology"],"x":"Xi'an terraforming practice is unique among known sentient civilizations. Rather than only creating a biome to sustain life, Xi'an [terraform](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) planets to fit functions seen as necessary to the well-being of Xi'an society. Some functions include manufacturing, nature preservation, and religious centers. \n\nThe Xi'an discovered terraforming roughly 6000 SEY before the beginning of the [First Imperial Age](gp:VDoPeW55W4) (about 25400 BCE), when a series of volcanic eruptions forced the then-divided [Houses](gp:box9JmxvWL) to pool their resources to push back against the rapid cooling of their home planet. Early [geohacking](gp:R9Bwj1BZAN) machines, the precursor to platform-based [terraformers](gp:bmNrZOQ2pQ), stopped the catastrophic global cooling cascade before it could end life on the planet. Today, the Xi'an use the Th.us'ūng system as a testbed for advanced terraforming technology.","g":["terraforming"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ae0dd18e-9d11-43d6-a2a6-b3babcddaeba"},
{"id":"xian-youth-counterculture-yiteekuiti","gp":"bEz5Bdal8Q","t":"Xi'an Youth Counterculture (Yitē'kuit.i)","k":"culture","c":["Xi'an","Culture"],"x":"Xi'an youth counterculture (yitē'kuit.i) is a movement made up of young [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj), mostly those who have not yet completed their compulsory time with the [Xi'an Service (Pō't.ōngp.ū)](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ), who experiment with practices not traditional to Xi'an society. [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) culture is particularly appealing to Xi'an youth. The main center of the counterculture movement is located in the former [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) system Kyuk'ya, on the Pue'nu (Kyuk'ya 1a) shipping hub thanks to its high level of interspecies trade.","g":["xi'an youth counterculture","yitē'kuit.i"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/300cab92-101a-4ebf-aab4-fa670a207982"},
{"id":"xian-human-cold-war","gp":"RXlLjDewkZ","t":"Xi'an-Human Cold War","k":"history","c":["History","Human","Xi'an","Military"],"x":"The Xi'an-Human Cold War (SEY 2530 - 2793) was a period of military and political tension between the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) and the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). It was sparked from [first contact](gp:R4ZQpYEEvx) between the two civilizations when in 2530 when a [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) terraforming company, acting illegally, attempted to set up operations in the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) system Th.us'ūng and were captured by the Xi'an who discovered them there. Though there was no large-scale combat between the sides, bordering planetary systems became militarized zones. The cold war formally ended with the signing of the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO) Pact in 2793.","g":["eras"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0a56756c-b8ad-4646-b33e-1a1a659787b6"},
{"id":"xian-human-first-contact","gp":"R4ZQpYEEvx","t":"Xi'an-Human First Contact","k":"history","c":["History","Xi'an","Human"],"x":"[Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and Xi'an first made contact in SEY 2530 when Gaia Planet Services (GPS), a Human [terraforming](gp:V3qgj8vjnj) corporation, attempted to set up operations on the Th.us'ūng system. Because GPS had illegally entered the system, they neglected to perform the necessary surveys required by law, and were thus unaware that the system was already occupied before they attempted to terraform one of the planets. This activity nearby attracted Xi'an military forces, who seized control of the facility and GPS personnel. For 57 days, the Xi'an held the Humans hostage while negotiating for information from the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN). Once the UPE capitulated to the [Xi'an Empire's](gp:0n96JkwNo9) terms, the hostages were released without harm. However, the distrust sown on both sides marked the beginning of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (2530 - 2793).","g":["first contact"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c98d9846-1854-4da5-a907-62c53c10e3b1"},
{"id":"xiphopod-blind-oni-crab","gp":"0rqMrr2YP3","t":"Xiphopod (Blind Oni Crab)","k":"life","c":["Animals"],"x":"# Xiphopod\nThe Xiphopod is a soft-shelled invertebrate omnivore indigenous to Leir I. Xiphopods, known colloquially as \"Blind Oni Crabs,\" are typically found on worlds with hot grassland environments, but have also been found to be highly adaptable to extreme conditions. They are considered an invasive species in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Their ability to float and propel themselves through the air has made them a favorite subject of xenobiologists.\n \nDiscovered during the initial planetary survey of Leir I, several specimens were captured and delivered to the University of Rhetor for study and classification. The scientists named the new species Xiphopod in honor of its resemblance to animals in the phylum Arthropoda and genus Xiphosura. The surveyors who discovered the animal, inspired by the \"face\" and \"nose\" that can be discerned in the animal's front carapace, were responsible for the more common name \"Blind Oni Crab.\"\n \n \n# Behavior and Ecology\nXiphopods are found naturally on Leir I, in hot to warm grassy climates at or near sea level. In their native environments, they spend their time hunting, scavenging for food, and resting. Xiphopods spend part of their year in groups, then split off and travel hundreds of kilometers to join other groups during mating season. Biologists theorize that this behavior developed in order to ensure genetic diversity among the species.\n \nTheir unique flight pattern occurs via biological process. The Xiphopod converts surrounding air into a hydrogen-helium mix and circulates it within a large, hollow cavity. This allows it to float. It then propels itself through the air by expelling gas from its body, which is incredibly light compared to its size. The most heavyweight adult Xiphopod ever found weighed only 300 g (10.58 oz).\n \n \n# Invasive Species\nThe Xiphopod is a common invasive species, thanks in large part to its opportunistic omnivorous diet, and its ability to adapt to a variety of conditions. Its reproductive habits also play a part: Xiphopods lay up to a thousand eggs at a time. Typically, the unattended eggs hatch in 13-17 Standard Earth Days. The UEE prohibits the trading of Xiphopods in order to discourage their spread throughout habitable space.\n \nThe hot, dry environment of [Hurston (Stanton I)](gp:0Qlx4dQnxL) has proven particularly hospitable to Xiphopods. Although it feeds on a variety of food types, it thrives off the biological waste generated from the settlements on Hurston, and has been able to breed in great numbers thanks to the lack of natural predators. While Xiphopod hunting is encouraged by the local government, for the poorest inhabitants of Hurston, the Xiphopod can be a food source. When roasted, the flesh of the Xiphopod becomes white and firm, and the meat has a musty, sweet flavor.","g":["xiphopod","invasive species","leir i","blind oni crab","hurston","stanton i"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7742355a-0042-4139-9c3e-24cd5aa881e9"},
{"id":"xis-kellog-ii","gp":"bmGJeMv2oK","t":"Xis (Kellog II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Xis (Kellog II) is the second planet from the sun of the [Fair Chance Act (FCA)](gp:RXlXmnaYGP)-protected [Kellog system](gp:Vy28ZQeYZv). A biologically diverse, lushly vegetated world, it is home to the developing [Orm](gp:RzPoqZXqZz) civilization and is protected by [UEE Army](gp:RxnX5JOZ7Q) patrols who enforce the FCA. Deep, multi-canopied rainforests and warm seas cover much of the planet's surface. The Orm largely reside in the temperate forests of the planet's polar regions. In the early 30th century, several freshwater slugs were smuggled off Xis and were sold to collectors under the name \"[Flo-Pets](gp:V8gJOo3ZGO),\" which led to a fad that ultimately turned the animals into an invasive species on multiple worlds throughout the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["xis","kellog ii","habitable planet","habitable","kellog system","unclaimed planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/90c7dd5b-e445-43b1-a7c4-94464539712a"},
{"id":"xyekyu-eealuth-iv","gp":"R5p2eq8y19","t":"Xyekyu (Ē'aluth IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Xyekyu (Ē'aluth IV) is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Ē'aluth system](gp:Rw1xW1lzxN), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A gas dwarf, its swirling blue and white atmosphere hides a rocky core and an icy ocean of ammonia and water. The platforms that serve as housing for the scientists, managers, and protectors of the nature preserve on the nearby planet [Ko'li (Ē'aluth III)](gp:Vy29gQ3x4Y) are mostly located in orbit around Xyekyu.","g":["xyekyu","ē'aluth iv","ē'aluth system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/11b8e4eb-3dd8-41cd-963e-c6f76f184a84"},
{"id":"xyeping-ailka-i","gp":"02kkXZpnDp","t":"Xyeping (Ail'ka I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Xyeping (Ail'ka I) is the innermost planet in the [Ail'ka system](gp:01LLZmEygJ), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A rocky protoplanet, it is likely to have originated from the nearby [Ail'ka belt alpha](gp:0dXXJ6Qano) that's located between it and the rest of the planetary system. Xyeping is bombarded with heat and radiation from the enormous B-type main sequence star that sits in the center of the Ail'ka system.","g":["xyeping","ail'ka i","ail'ka system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c3b3a610-8af2-46b2-a698-de16b9f1ddbc"},
{"id":"xooluu-rila-iv","gp":"VYLzwxDrre","t":"Xōl'uu (R.il'a IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Xōl'uu (R.il'a IV) is the fourth planet from the sun of the [R.il'a system](gp:Rw1xWXME1B), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Originally terraformed and developed as a planet to train military ground forces and build weapons, it was reclassified as an industrial world by the Xi'an government at the conclusion of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793 / MXY III.838 - III.1044). Its military factories have been decommissioned and replaced with commercial manufacturing centers, and its strategy centers have become office buildings. In the early 2900s, the Xi'an government established a policy of offering real estate discounts to [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-owned businesses that established branches on Xōl'uu in an effort to facilitate easy trading between the Xi'an Empire and the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["xōl'uu","r.il'a iv","habitable","habitable planet","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"yoome-taal-i","gp":"0Kxjm2nYOM","t":"Y.ōm'e (T.āl I)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Y.ōm'e (T.āl I) is the first planet from the sun of the [T.āl system](gp:R4j2mdjZE5), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A mesoplanet that closely orbits its star, it is pockmarked with craters from countless mining probes that were dispatched to survey the planet for potentially valuable resources. While little has been found so far, raw materials are in such high demand from T.āl's inhabited planets that missions to find heretofore undiscovered minerals are frequent.  The atmosphere of Y.ōm'e is dense enough that heat mirages can be observed rising from its surface during the day.","g":["y.ōm'e","t.āl i","t.āl system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","xi'an planet"]},
{"id":"yar-centauri-ii","gp":"R6dd5pyOZ5","t":"Yar (Centauri II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yar is the second planet from the sun in the [Centauri system], [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). Located close to the inner boundary of Centauri's [green zone](gp:ReJaAjgOwy), Yar's environment is hot and arid, and sparsely populated. The planet's most visible feature is a vast barren region known as the Red Desert. A variety of research and mining outposts were established on Yar after precious minerals were discovered there in the early 29th century; however, most were abandoned after the larger deposits were depleted in the early 2910s. A scattered population of [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) made up of remaining miners and their descendants remain on Yar.","g":["yar","centauri ii","centauri system","habitable","habitable planet","human planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8986edee-2c26-474f-b438-b6c694081b7b"},
{"id":"yeten-ailka-iii","gp":"R6ddGgQMPD","t":"Ye'ten (Ail'ka III)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Ye'ten (Ail'ka III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Ail'ka system](gp:01LLZmEygJ), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). [Terraformed](gp:R6dWOrLEM4) for the express purpose of agricultural production, Ye'ten is a world in which all available arable land is being used to grow food and other important organic staples, raise livestock, and ferment raw ingredients to supply the rest of the Xi'an Empire. It is estimated that decades of rations are stockpiled there in case of emergency. To reduce the chance of travelers bringing contaminants or invasive species to the planet, the only area open for landing is a sealed and tightly monitored enclosure.","g":["ye'ten","ail'ka iii","ail'ka system","habitable planet","habitable","xi'an asteroid belt"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6d24b45f-5ac5-4eb3-9b6d-fe5d9551d361"},
{"id":"yeton-ailka-v","gp":"bBz5npq95O","t":"Ye'ton (Ail'ka V)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Ye'ton (Ail'ka V) is the fifth planet from the sun of the [Ail'ka system](gp:01LLZmEygJ), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A gas dwarf that has a thick atmosphere of hydrogen and helium, the planet is dotted with several permanent storms. The harvesters and refineries that sit in stable orbit above Ye'ton keep the system's military fleets supplied with fuel.","g":["ye'ton","ail'ka v","uninhabitable planet","not habitable","ail'ka system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/2a6a142e-7355-4ba8-9db2-99777a2fa125"},
{"id":"yela-stanton-2c","gp":"bo1xJPgMNL","t":"Yela (Stanton 2c)","k":"place","c":["Moons","Human"],"x":"# YELA (STANTON 2C)\n\nYela is the outermost natural satellite of [Crusader (Stanton II)](gp:VarZxj1Qav), and is orbited by a ring of asteroids. A thin crust of water-ice on the moon's surface is said to represent the cool demeanor of Yela, the oldest sibling in the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) children's story [A Gift for Baba](gp:0KnMm3WX5P), after whom the moon was named. [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N) security came under fire during a [Senate](gp:VaZn8OqaNZ) hearing in SEY 2949 for failing to curtail criminal activity in the outpost colloquially known as Jumptown, located inside one of Yela's craters. \n\n# ENVIRONMENT\n\nDue to its thin oxygen atmosphere and distance from the system's sun, the surface of Yela is very cold, with average temperatures ranging between -55 °C and -10 °C. The large water ice sheets that sprawl across the plains and mountains feed the water cycle via sublimation. There are no bodies of liquid water on Yela's surface, nor is there any rainfall, but snow showers, fog, and windstorms can arise when the weather conditions are correct.\n\n# HISTORY\n\nDiscovered by navjumper Toshi Aaron alongside the rest of the Stanton system in 2851, Yela was briefly the sole property of the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6). During this time, the [UEE Navy](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) began to construct a base in the skies of Stanton II. It lightly mined the moons for resources, but largely left them alone. \n\nIn 2865, driven by a financial crisis, the UEE sold all the planets and moons in the system to various corporations, including [Crusader Industries](gp:0OaBkLLG1N), who purchased the parent planet along with Yela and its sister moons. After refitting the Navy's platforms on the newly-renamed planet Crusader for its own use, the company established multiple mining facilities and security outposts across Yela, [Cellin](gp:Rw1Z9yz1jJ) (Stanton 2a), and [Daymar](gp:VpMGDvX48N) (Stanton 2b), and offered some of the land for lease.\n\nIn spite of the inhospitable environment, some Humans have made Yela their home. Wilma Ivery built the first permanent homestead in 2907, where she lived until her death in 2935 from natural causes. In 2909, the first Human was born on Yela when Albert and Nora Triolo were forced to make an emergency landing to give birth to their daughter, Erma Triolo. Outlaw group Nine Tails began using abandoned Navy facilities as bases in 2946, leading to an increase in patrols from [Crusader Security](gp:bmNrmYB8MP).\n\n# CULTURE\n\nUnregulated ground-vehicle racing is a popular pastime among residents of and visitors to Yela. Lakedra Walsh organized and won the first recorded ground-vehicle race on the moon in 2912. The site of this race was made into a permanent racetrack, and was named Lakedra's Lap in her honor. Many of the racing sites take advantage of Yela's terrain, and include large boulders and rocks. In 2917, amateur racer Ethan Halton died in Nakamura Valley from injuries sustained during a crash while making a tight turn on one such track.","g":["yela","stanton 2c","not habitable","uninhabitable moon","crusader","stanton ii","crusader industries","uee moon","stanton ii moon"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7a220845-f74b-44ed-893d-94dea14b33f1"},
{"id":"yellow-puglath","gp":"V3GLN4EBNN","t":"Yellow Puglath","k":"life","c":["Plants"],"x":"The yellow puglath is a plant created by [Rayari Inc](gp:0jGnJnMwke). Derived from the ng.athxya, a plant indigenous the desert regions of Ka'ua (Hyoton IV), it was designed to capture as much water as possible from its surrounding environment. Specialized ridges along its trunk can capture early morning dew in arid climates, and its internal cells can collect up to a four liters of drinking water per day in ideal conditions.","g":["rayari inc","herbaceous plant"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ab7ba26c-60eb-4b88-a427-a4c2d134ebeb"},
{"id":"yengchuai-lauo-ii","gp":"R6demaZlkD","t":"Yengchuai (La'uo II)","k":"place","c":["Planets","Xi'an"],"x":"Yengchuai (La'uo II) is the second planet from the sun of the [La'uo system](gp:R6demJ8Xmq), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Partially covered with an ocean of lava, Yengchuai's surface is profoundly geologically active, and is thought to have survived a collision with a massive celestial body in the recent past. Between its lava flows, the Xi'an Empire has constructed heavy mining and construction facilities. Some of these are hard labor camps for Xi'an prisoners convicted of serious crimes. Sentient rights activists in the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) frequently petition the government to reproach the Xi'an Empire over this practice.","g":["yengchuai","la'uo ii","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","la'uo system","xi'an planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/93273da6-9444-4872-9287-cf1f95aed48d"},
{"id":"yethluul-seyeno-yaamon-iii","gp":"V8WPNjrEjW","t":"Yethlūl s.yen'o (Yā'mon III)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yethlūl s.yen'o (Yā'mon III) is the third planet from the sun of the [Yā'mon system](gp:VarxDJ5yLo), [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Along with the nearby planet [Yethlūl y.ath'o (Yā'mon II)](gp:bo1JQK12rr), it is being jointly terraformed by the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) corporation [ArcCorp](gp:0dQ47zYd6O) and the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government. This long-term collaboration is expected to benefit both sides as they share their technologies and methods with one another. In 2948, the planet was flooded with a violet-hued gas as a step in the atmospheric construction process. Part of the Koa e Ko'ia endurance race took place on Yethlūl s.yen'o in 2947.","g":["yethluul s.yen'o","yaamon iii","yaa'mon system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/a9c84efa-0b53-4e60-9fd3-fc6a91fc59aa"},
{"id":"yethluul-yatho-yaamon-ii","gp":"bo1JQK12rr","t":"Yethlūl y.ath'o (Yā'mon II)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yethlūl y.ath'o (Yā'mon II) is the second planet from the sun of the [Yā'mon system](gp:VarxDJ5yLo), [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9). Although it saw little use other than resource extraction during the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793), it is now a hub of activity as it is being terraformed under a joint project between the [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)  corporation [ArcCorp](gp:0dQ47zYd6O) and the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) government. The main ArcCorp station in orbit around Yethlūl y.ath'o is a popular destination for workers from either Empire to mingle. During the Koa e Ko'ia endurance race in 2947, the station reached maximum capacity as enthusiasts gathered there to watch the race.","g":["yethluul y.ath'o","yaamon ii","yaa'mon system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/897d08ba-85be-463d-99ca-7e4e49fd5612"},
{"id":"yulin-cluster-alpha","gp":"0jGyQZ9vmz","t":"Yulin Cluster Alpha","k":"place","c":["Space"],"x":"The Yulin cluster alpha is an asteroid cluster in the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Located in one of the Lagrange points in the orbit of [Yulin IV](gp:R9vEkmq2rM), it is a dense nest of irregularly-shaped asteroids that is often used as an obstacle course in starship races. Seeing an increase in popularity, some of the Racing [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) in the system have begun to look into expanding infrastructure in the cluster to accommodate more complex races and additional spectators.","g":["asteroid cluster","yulin system","spacecraft races of yulin"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/6e209fb8-cfa6-4eca-b9d3-6afbf378e947"},
{"id":"yulin-flotilla","gp":"RPDZ1JJpNZ","t":"Yulin Flotilla","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Banu"],"x":"The Yulin flotilla is a gathering of semi-permanent ships and space stations located in the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Situated in one of the Lagrange points of [Yulin II](gp:bo1yMW5Z5A), it is a nexus of commerce, entertainment, and vice. Various [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) that specialize in gambling, racing, recreational drugs, counterfeiting, and other such trades operate in the flotilla, making it a popular destination.","g":["yulin system","space station","banu flotilla"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/7b76ec6a-1969-462b-b9f3-a4187e2b2822"},
{"id":"yulin-i","gp":"Var6YNe9Ko","t":"Yulin I","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yulin I is the first planet from the sun of the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Orbiting very close to its sun, its lithosphere has been mostly worn away after eons of exposure to stellar wind and radiation. The surface of the planet is heavily cratered, resulting from countless meteor strikes. The largest of these craters are surrounded by long, thin streaks of particles that surround their impact sites like the spokes of a wheel.","g":["yulin system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/02380f3f-f376-43e9-8041-16d5d26e763d"},
{"id":"yulin-ii","gp":"bo1yMW5Z5A","t":"Yulin II","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yulin II is the second planet from the sun of the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A smog planet, it has a deadly but prismatic atmosphere that shimmers with many colors under the light of its star. It is a popular subject of photography among tourists. Postcards, wall-coverings, clothing, blankets, and other objects with images of the planet on it are sold at the nearby [Buloi Sataball Arena](gp:V3GEAj34wa) to its [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) and [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) visitors.","g":["yulin system","banu planet","not habitable","uninhabitable planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/0f1c9050-9727-49aa-9ed1-a410c5253eaf"},
{"id":"yulin-iii","gp":"RMNLEn6zmx","t":"Yulin III","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yulin III is the third planet from the sun of the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Located on the outer edge of the habitable zone, it is cold but temperate enough to be habitable for [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4). However, its ammonia oceans and high-pressure, methane-rich atmosphere make it inhospitable to those of other civilizations. To Banu, Yulin III is a relaxing resort world. Enterprising [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) have created a sealed arcology to encourage non-Banu vacationers to experience the planet's strange beauty.","g":["yulin system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ed2638f6-08d1-4fb6-b8bf-7d778140c359"},
{"id":"yulin-iv","gp":"R9vEkmq2rM","t":"Yulin IV","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yulin IV is the fourth planet from the sun of the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). Tectonic activity on this world has raised towering pillars of rock with natural windows caused by constantly-shifting wind patterns. The [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) in the system utilize these natural formations as obstacles in starship races. Geologists interested in observing these formations in person have been known to hire Smuggling [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) to get them to the planet's surface without catching the attention of any Racing Soulis, who believe that their presence will interfere with the races.","g":["yulin system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/ec60adc2-c766-448c-a900-d5b2639aa220"},
{"id":"yulin-system","gp":"R6dEoPKAZj","t":"Yulin System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Banu"],"x":"The Yulin system is a planetary system in the [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3) that consists of a G-type main sequence star, an iron planet, three terrestrial planets, an ice giant, a gas giant, and an asteroid cluster. A center of entertainment, it is home to the famed [Buloi Sataball Arena](gp:V3GEAj34wa), the ammonia-atmosphered resort planet [Yulin III](gp:RMNLEn6zmx), and the [Yulin flotilla](gp:RPDZ1JJpNZ), a hub of gambling and gaming.","g":["banu system"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/8349d839-a805-4128-9f03-cff3a1084efb"},
{"id":"yulin-v","gp":"VpMyJnx9yz","t":"Yulin V","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yulin V is the fifth planet from the sun of the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). An ice giant, its hydrogen and helium atmosphere contains water, ammonia, and methane ice that combine to give the planet a uniform pale blue color. Its strong equatorial winds feed storm systems that create dark spots.","g":["not habitable","uninhabitable planet","yulin system","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/b78a6f14-968c-4f10-bff1-ec27f4fc1781"},
{"id":"yulin-vi","gp":"RL63EJMkoZ","t":"Yulin VI","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yulin VI is the sixth planet from the sun of the [Yulin system](gp:R6dEoPKAZj), [Banu Protectorate](gp:Vgg795z2a3). A gas giant, its atmosphere is almost entirely composed of hydrogen, making it a popular hub for automated refineries and refueling stations. This has additionally attracted outlaws who have been known to ambush unwary travelers. Security [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) based in this area sell their protection for a steep fee.","g":["yulin system","not habitable","uninhabitable planet","banu planet"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/043997a4-ddec-47fe-9b8e-8aee9876902f"},
{"id":"yaamon-system","gp":"VarxDJ5yLo","t":"Yā'mon System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The Yā'mon system (also known as the Hadur System) is a planetary system in the [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that consists of an F-type main sequence star, three terrestrial planets, a dwarf planet, and an asteroid belt. Discovered in 2529 by navjumper Āi se Cho'an, it was designated as a supply system for the [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) military and placed under its protection. In 2531, it was re-discovered by [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) explorer Teesa Morrison when she traversed the [Baker](gp:Rz2KGkv13N)-Yā'mon jump point and encountered a Xi'an military escort team. This incident led the [United Planets of Earth (UPE)](gp:0QxBjKP2PN) High [Naval](gp:RPDvKOpdP4) Commander Jianna Perry to propose that Xi'an systems connected to the UPE be placed under control of the Navy in case of an attack. It became the first system to form the [Perry Line](gp:V8gJQMY9mO), and Humans renamed it Hadur after an ancient Human war deity. Under the terms of the 2789 [Akari-Kr.ē Treaty](gp:bE3rKrl5z6), it was ceded to the Xi'an Empire and reverted to its original name Yā'mon.","g":["yaa'mon system","xi'an system","perry line"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/40eca167-f894-4f55-a886-bf04ffd9b40b"},
{"id":"yaati","gp":"V8Wwm7GpgM","t":"Yā'ti","k":"place","c":["Settlements","Xi'an"],"x":"Yā'ti is a major city on [Xōl'uu (R.il'a IV)](gp:VYLzwxDrre), [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9). A center of commerce and industry, the city was once a military manufacturing center, but was redeveloped after the end of the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793 / MXY III.838 - III.1044). Multiple [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2)-owned corporations and [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) [Soulis](gp:RAdjm4mron) operate in Yā'ti to facilitate easy trade with the Xi'an Empire. To continue to encourage economic development, the Xi'an government offers tax breaks to any major House willing to establish operations in Yā'ti.","g":["xōl'uu","r.il'a iv","xi'an city","cities"]},
{"id":"yaamping-yaamon-iv","gp":"RWo6G4J82a","t":"Yām'ping (Yā'mon IV)","k":"place","c":["Planets"],"x":"Yām'ping (Yā'mon IV) is a dwarf planet in the [Yā'mon system](gp:VarxDJ5yLo), [Xi'an Empire](gp:0n96JkwNo9), and is the last planet from its sun. Once home to several military outposts during the [Xi'an-Human Cold War](gp:RXlLjDewkZ) (SEY 2530 - 2793), Yām'ping is now orbited by stations dedicated to entertainment, such as gambling halls, bars, hotels, and other services. [Xi'an](gp:ReJwN9KJEj) and [Human](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) workers from the [Yethlūl y.ath'o (Yā'mon II)](gp:bo1JQK12rr) and [Yethlūl s.yen'o (Yā'mon III)](gp:V8WPNjrEjW) terraforming projects often spend their time off here.","g":["yaam'ping","yaa'mon iv","yaa'mon system","uninhabitable planet","not habitable"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/c1a0ecca-f383-4338-967e-e7f2d24a4c37"},
{"id":"zeus","gp":"VYLd4WxODo","t":"Zeus","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft","Human"],"x":"The Zeus was a short-range spacecraft developed by [Roberts Space Industries (RSI)](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw), and was the first ship equipped with a quantum drive to be offered to civilians on the commercial market. After the first [quantum drive](gp:RX3DOkJdxJ) was developed by RSI for the military in 2075, demand for a civilian version grew until eventually the first commercial quantum-enabled spaceship prototype was produced during the 2130s. Known as the Zeus, the ship was not released until 2140 due to issues with hull integrity in its early test flights. After many project delays, RSI enlisted aid from Navy test pilot Michelle Saleno, the first Human to quantum travel beyond the orbit of Jupiter (Sol V). Saleno convinced the Amecanio Navy to form the 999th Test Squadron for the evaluation of cutting-edge spaceships, and the Navy agreed to use the 999th to help RSI refine the Zeus. After a complete overhaul of the Zeus's hull based on the advice of Saleno and the 999th, Saleno successfully piloted the Zeus in 2137. The availability of the Zeus was key in accelerating the early expansion of [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) beyond their home planet.","g":["roberts space industries (rsi)","expedition","human spacecraft"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/fc45323f-6d37-4112-a418-28b525a202f4"},
{"id":"zeus-mk-ii-cl","gp":"0Gx9adgK4P","t":"Zeus Mk II CL","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Zeus Mk II CL (Clipper) is a medium freight spacecraft manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) (RSI). One of three variants on the [Zeus Mk II series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/zeus-series), it includes a tractor beam to facilitate the easy loading and unloading of cargo, as well as a cargo bay four times larger than that of the [Zeus Mk II ES](gp:V7dDEeONjm). It is equipped with weaponry and shielding to defend the lives of its crew during missions, as well as living quarters to facilitate long-term travel.","g":["freight","medium freight","roberts space industries (rsi)","human spacecraft","zeus series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/f093dbf2-012f-4f00-8c5d-cda521ab5655"},
{"id":"zeus-mk-ii-es","gp":"V7dDEeONjm","t":"Zeus Mk II ES","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Zeus Mk II ES (Essential) is a medium exploration spacecraft manufactured by [Roberts Space Industries](gp:RWwZDn2Xrw) (RSI). An homage to the [Zeus](gp:VYLd4WxODo), the first commercially sold ship to come with a quantum drive, the Zeus Mk II retains the general shape of the original vessel but modernizes it for the 30th century SEY, introducing more width to allow for a larger living area. Each Zeus ES includes an advanced radar system to facilitate exploration alongside updated defensive capabilities to allow safer traversal along the frontier of the [United Empire of Earth](gp:VyvyKxy4v6) (UEE).","g":["expedition","roberts space industries (rsi)","human spacecraft","zeus series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9a75de9d-c134-48a3-82bf-8b46d1f602c2"},
{"id":"zeus-mk-ii-mr","gp":"Rz2zyEZpD5","t":"Zeus Mk II MR","k":"vehicle","c":["Spacecraft"],"x":"The Zeus Mk II MR (Marque) is a medium interdiction spacecraft manufactured by Roberts Space Industries. One of three variants in the [Zeus Mk II series](https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/tag/zeus-series), it swaps the radar scanner turret of the [ES](gp:V7dDEeONjm) model for a quantum dampener that can halt combatants from retreating into quantum travel, and adds an EMP device that can be used to scramble or disable the systems of other ships. The MR also includes [cryopods](gp:0GxY74adqg) that can be used for prisoner transport.","g":["interdiction","roberts space industries (rsi)","human spacecraft","zeus series"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/1390fc1e-fec9-41f5-b6a7-32cdced8f1c2"},
{"id":"zip","gp":"RPDWarxXOX","t":"Zip","k":"culture","c":["Science and Technology","Illegal Activity"],"x":"Zip is a stimulant and psychedelic drug that causes visual and auditory hallucinations in its users. Derived from the prescription drug evekemine, zip is a liquid drug that is typically taken by being administered directly into the eye. Longtime users of zip may have discoloration of the iris. While under the influence of zip, a user's senses are enhanced, allowing them to see vivid colors and to hear sounds that are not there.","g":["stimulant","psychedelic drug","illegal drug"],"img":"https://cig-galactapedia-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/upload/9b28e7e4-bfbf-4669-a0ba-ca10d993fad8"},
{"id":"aai-se-choan","gp":"Rw1r27OoJJ","t":"Āi se Cho'an","k":"people","c":["People","Xi'an","Exploration","History"],"x":"Āi se Cho'an (MXY III.726 - III.874? | SEY 2386 - 2577?) was a navjumper best known for her discovery of the [Yā'mon system](gp:VarxDJ5yLo). \n\nBorn into a [House](gp:box9JmxvWL) that specialized in jump point navigation, Āi was trained from a young age in navigational techniques and began her career hunting for potential jump points when she completed her [civil service](gp:0dQJ96mOeZ) in MXY III.796 (SEY 2477). Her discovery of the Yā'mon system in MXY III.837 (SEY 2529) earned her the status of Matriarch at the young age of 111. \n\nĀi disappeared in MXY III.874 (SEY 2577) while traveling in the T.āl system. Historians of House Cho'an maintain that she likely fell victim to an accident while navigating a yet-to-be-discovered jump point. House Cho'an has made it a rite of passage for their members to complete a year-long tour in T.āl, hoping to locate what Āi may have found.","g":["aai se cho'an","yaa'mon system","xi'an people","xi'an history"],"img":"https://static.robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/upload/a6e7aadb-4c14-4c0d-af04-90aab1e4624e"},
{"id":"eealuth-system","gp":"Rw1xW1lzxN","t":"Ē'aluth System","k":"place","c":["Planetary Systems","Xi'an"],"x":"The Ē'aluth system is a planetary system in the [Xi'an Empire (SaoXy'an)](gp:0n96JkwNo9) that consists of a K-type main sequence star, a puffy planet, a smog planet, a terrestrial planet, a gas dwarf, a gas giant, and an asteroid belt. Discovered in MXY I.14599 (SEY 981 BCE), it was immediately earmarked by the Xi'an government for development as a nature preserve. The third planet, [Ko'li (Ē'aluth III)](gp:Vy29gQ3x4Y), was terraformed and seeded with every single known plant and animal species that originated in Xi'an territory. Most food and resources needed to support the workers who maintain Ko'li are imported into Ē'aluth in order to preserve the sanctuary's carefully-crafted environments. Visitors to the system are permitted, but commercial development is strictly forbidden. [Humans](gp:0Nwpnr6wa2) first became aware of the system in MXY III.926 (SEY 2602), when a [Banu](gp:0NwpYPpNZ4) Information [Souli](gp:RAdjm4mron) sold the location of the [Oya](gp:0KxGow1ly4)-Ē'aluth jump point to the [United Empire of Earth (UEE)](gp:VyvyKxy4v6).","g":["xi'an system"]}
];
